{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition","id":818609,"title":"Genius: The Trangression 2th edition?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-28T11:42:13-08:00","id":818609,"title":"Genius: The Trangression 2th edition?","content":"Greetings fellow chroniclers. I recently stumbled on Genius: The Trangression and it absolutelly blew my mind. I had an orgasm reading it. It's my dream game come true, I mean, a game that centers around the idea of mad scientists? Bring it on!. I haven't finished reading it but I'm loving every moment of it.<br /> Now, after the fan meltdown, my question is as the title. Are the authors going to make a second edition? If so, is ther enay chance I could help in any way? Thank you so much for your hard work and for creating something so amazing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T12:33:36-08:00","id":818640,"title":"","content":"There was some discussion on this before, and I had some notes on it. I'll post a link when I have access to the flash drive they're one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T15:47:45-08:00","id":818798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=818640#post818640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was some discussion on this before, and I had some notes on it. I'll post a link when I have access to the flash drive they're one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you very much. I'm eager to see it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T19:34:39-08:00","id":818937,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1N0o3x3xDvsgU34sHQMUngSqoqTePt_mgFeK9PDj8jAo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Alright, these are my notes so far.</a><br /> <br /> Feel free to pick them apart and tell me what you think. The idea on the Wonders costing Experience was to make them more personal to the Genius, like an actual part of them and extension of their Inspiration than just a machine that you put Mania into and get stuff out of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T11:53:42-08:00","id":819400,"title":"","content":"Hum...the thing is I haven't had the chance to play genius, so I'm a bit hesitant to give you feedback. I need to study the system a bit more before saying anything. For now I will say this, the thematic changes that you are introducing are cool, I specially like the idea of the magnus opus and I would like to discuss with you a similar idea that I have, but as player I don't like the idea of wonders costing experience. I do understand the reasoning behind it, you want to make them more special, but my personal experience both playing and directing games is that players are very conservative with their experience points, and they don't like to expend them in things that are not related to their character progression. Also I don't see wonders as things that I just use and that's it, it's what makes my genius special. My personal recomendation if you want to make the player more invested in their wonders is give them options to personalize them even more, to add something truly unique that no other wonder has, and perhaps more nasty consequences in case they lose it or is destroyed. Again, for now, I can't really give more detailed feedback or advice till I have read the manual and your document some more. When I have more time I will tell you. Keep working on it, the game is fantastic, and let's hope more people join in, the mor eperspectives the better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T17:23:51-08:00","id":819601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=819400#post819400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...as player I don't like the idea of wonders costing experience. I do understand the reasoning behind it, you want to make them more special, but my personal experience both playing and directing games is that players are very conservative with their experience points, and they don't like to expend them in things that are not related to their character progression.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a valid point. The issue was more that I felt that Wonders should be considered a part of that character's development. That is, a mad scientist is determined, in part, by what he makes. Victor Frankenstein's character is built on the mad obsession he put into his Creature, as is Doctor Moreau, and even Doctor Forrester from MST3K.<br /> <br /> ...They really need to quit giving doctorates to people like these.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T17:25:19-08:00","id":819602,"title":"","content":"Here's my idea. Reading genius the transgression I came up with something to simultaneously regain obligation and serve humanity. One of the things that bummed me out the most reading genius was the fact that nothing I did really mattered, and that I was not a real scientist. I like to play highly altruistic characters that try to leave their mark in the world and make it a better place. Ok, here it goes.<br /> There's a moment in the life of a genius where he or she has to make a choice. It's very easy to get lost in the pure raw pleasure of creation. To dismiss the mundane and embark in the extraordinary, in the addictive power of mania. However, a genius remains a human, and she or he must decide just how human the are. If a genius chooses to follow his obligation to his or her fellow man then he or she can go through a process that it's equal parts sacred and painful: turning your wonder into mundane technology. <br /> It's not an easy endeavour by any means because the genius must go against his or her very nature, against the very spark of creativity that makes him or her a genius. In this process, the genius takes one of his or her wonders, and proceeds to turn it into something that regular people can use, but there is a catch and a very steep price for this.<br /> The catch is that the wonders power will be reduced to a fraction of what it can do. If it's a pill that can instantly repair tissue damage, then it becomes a supplement that aids in the healing process of injuries, if it's an engine that produces almost unlimited energy then it becomes a piece of tech that improves energy output in traditional generators, etc...<br /> The price is that the genius runs a very high risk of seeing his or her level of inspiration reduced and his sanity threatened. The process drains him or her of mania and willpower, not because it's used in the process, but because it evaporates away in an effort to maintain the concentration and the mental discipline necessary to do it, and if something goes wrong there's a very good chance that the genius will see his or her permanent rating of inspiration and/or willpower permanently reduced.<br /> The question is why? Why would the genius do such a thing? Why would he or she go through such a painful and soul draining process? Well, it's because if he or she cares and if she or he succeeds then she would have gone through a mundane technological and/or scientific breakthrough that will help humankind greatly in the long term.<br /> The pill he or she turned into a supplement may not end all illnesses in the world, but it will help in the healing process of many life-threatening injuries and it will open new lines of investigation among mundane scientists that will help them come up with new healing processes. When the genius sees years in the future how many lives he has helped then right there is when he or she knows that it has been worth it. <br /> It's a sacrifice, but a sacrifice that he or she does willingly, for a genius is always on the verge of madness by the power of mania, for it's only there that he or she can find the secrets of the universe that will help in the progress of humankind. The genius becomes a martyr that sacrifices his or her mind and sanity to help humanity. Because that is what real scientists do. Always seeking knowledge for the betterment of mankind, no one may ever recognise his or her effort, but she or he have very right to be alwasy proud of what they did.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T23:42:15-08:00","id":819713,"title":"","content":"I'm going to be frank. I don't like it.<br /> <br /> Genius isn't supposed to be about men of science changing the world. Step away from Johnny Quest, and toward the Venture Brothers. The point of Genius is that they <i>can't</i> really fix the world. Any attempts to do so would blow up in their faces, often literally. Their intemded communist utopia becomes a crushing dictatorship, their creations turn on them, and they're lucky to keep semi-sane at the end of the day. The Inspired aren't the men of science and hope, they're the mad and tortured geniuses that have to struggle every day just to keep their brilliance from killing us all. Those that embrace their genius always become insane, often incurably so. There's a reason Nicola Tesla was named a Lemurian in the book.<br /> <br /> Genius is not a hopeful game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T05:10:02-08:00","id":819767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=819713#post819713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to be frank. I don't like it.<br /> <br /> Genius isn't supposed to be about men of science changing the world. Step away from Johnny Quest, and toward the Venture Brothers. The point of Genius is that they <i>can't</i> really fix the world. Any attempts to do so would blow up in their faces, often literally. Their intemded communist utopia becomes a crushing dictatorship, their creations turn on them, and they're lucky to keep semi-sane at the end of the day. The Inspired aren't the men of science and hope, they're the mad and tortured geniuses that have to struggle every day just to keep their brilliance from killing us all. Those that embrace their genius always become insane, often incurably so. There's a reason Nicola Tesla was named a Lemurian in the book.<br /> <br /> Genius is not a hopeful game.</div> </div> </div> </div>The process is not supposed to fix the world. It's about accepting that you can't fix the world. It's about understanding that true science advances through hard work and patience, not sudden inspiration. It's about the genius acknowledging that he or she cannot solve everything, that there are no fast or easy solutions. It's about descending from the fantastic to the mundane so his or her fellow humans can have a tiny piece of the fantastic and have a better life. The tragedy of the genius is understanding that he or she will never be the saviour of the world, because that is not his or her job, it's an arrogant attitude that will lead to tragedy, but that doesn't mean that he or she can't try to leave his or her mark and make the world a better place, even if in the end he or she just makes a small difference.<br /> At least this is my point of view and how I want to play it. I understand that it's the world of darkness, but there has to be some light at the end. If there is no hope for transcendence, for bringing hope, then what is the point of being a genius? What is the point of me playing this game if no matter what it's going to end badly? All the other lines have ways of becoming better, of finding peace. It requires a lot of hard work and sacrifices but it's there. I understand that this is your game, and if you want it that way then ok. I just want you to understand that I'm not against bleakness or horror. I'm not against the genius living at the edge of madness and in constant frustration at the world. I just want to see that there is point to all that suffering, a reason for me to be a genius in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T08:56:22-08:00","id":819818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=819713#post819713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Genius is not a hopeful game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with everything else you said but not this.<br /> <br /> Genius is a game about <i>accepting</i> impotence. It's made almost explicit in the way the Peerage hammers home to it's members that they should give up on grand plans. Karl Marx is an example of the Genius who tries to save the world; but the iconic example of a Genius who Gets It would be The Doctor.<br /> <br /> A Genius can't build a perfect society, but being a tourist across all time and space, meeting poeple, helping them in little ways, they can do that. Once you accept that you can't build utopia you're freed from the responsibility to try and can focus on doing some little thing right. Your own life, that one person you think is special and sane. That's a very hopeful message, it's one that's very appropriate to our time*, and rather Buddhist now that I think about it.<br /> <br /> * I serously think that Genius is the best WoD game at <i>saying something</i> about life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 03-21-2016, 06:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T09:08:45-08:00","id":819826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=819818#post819818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with everything else you said but not this.<br /> <br /> Genius is a game about <i>accepting</i> impotence. It's made almost explicit in the way the Peerage hammers home to it's members that they should give up on grand plans. Karl Marx is an example of the Genius who tries to save the world; but the iconic example of a Genius who Gets It would be The Doctor.<br /> <br /> A Genius can't build a perfect society, but being a tourist across all time and space, meeting poeple, helping them in little ways, they can do that. Once you accept that you can't build utopia you're freed from the responsibility to try and can focus on doing some little thing right. Your own life, that one person you think is special and sane. That's a very hopeful message, it's one that's very appropriate to our time*, and rather Buddhist now that I think about it.<br /> <br /> * I serously think that Genius is the best game at <i>saying something</i> about life in the WoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with you, and I think is the right view. A genius is not there to fix the world, but that shouldn't mean that he or she couldn't help making things a little better, like every other person does everyday all around the world. A genius becomes wise when he or she realizes that a better tomorrow is in the hands of everyone, and not just one person. His connection with the extraordinary is there to inspire people with his vision, not to impose the vision on them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T14:41:57-08:00","id":820571,"title":"","content":"Can I ask you what was the inspiration and reasoning behind the paradigms and their exclusivity with the wonders? I think is an original idea but I'm not 100% convinced that it may work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T16:17:11-08:00","id":820634,"title":"","content":"I know that failure is one of the central themes in Genius, but perhaps it's possible to give more agency to the PCs over their chance of success with a re-phrasing. Instead of messing up and then feeling like your Inspiration doesn't matter, you can say it's a game about trial and error. After all, the scientific method can be described as trial + error + methodology.<br /> <br /> Geniuses don't suddenly forget all they knew about science because of their Breakthroughs. They approach science with an &quot;anything goes&quot; mindset. This is discussed in <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XZLN1PN3L4I\" target=\"_blank\"><b>this video</b></a> about Rick Sanchez from Rick And Morty, who could be interpreted as a Neid with low Obligation.<br /> <br /> I believe Genius would benefit from a tone shift towards &quot;you CAN get important things done, but don't expect things to go 100% the way you want&quot;. Just as the Initial Compromise questions in Demon reinforce the mindset of a spy, Genius could have its own starter questions. Besides the expected &quot;what was your biggest mistake?&quot; they would also have to answer &quot;what do you most want to do right?&quot;<br /> <br /> I have read multiple times that Genius has too much overlap with COD and OWOD Mage, especially the latter. The isolation for knowing truths people will not or cannot accept, among other themes. I don't believe it's feasible to remove this overlapping theme from Genius, but it needs to be explored distinctly.<br /> <br /> I, for one, would use the following comparison: if the Awakened are like Plato gesturing towards the Forms, the Inspired are like Aristotle gesturing toward the Empirical. I am no expert in philosophy, so take that as you will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T05:42:46-08:00","id":820908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=820571#post820571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can I ask you what was the inspiration and reasoning behind the paradigms and their exclusivity with the wonders? I think is an original idea but I'm not 100% convinced that it may work.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea is that a Genius can make just about any Wonder that any others can, but their specific world view makes them better at specific Wonders that align with it, at the cost of making it basically impossible to work with somebody who believes in something directly opposed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T07:21:42-08:00","id":820951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=820908#post820908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea is that a Genius can make just about any Wonder that any others can, but their specific world view makes them better at specific Wonders that align with it, at the cost of making it basically impossible to work with somebody who believes in something directly opposed.</div> </div> </div> </div> Isn't that an Unmada problem? Geniuses are stubborn, sure, but their worldviews can adapt. Any clashing aesthetics and beliefs could be handled with the Universalist Merit or something like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T10:59:03-08:00","id":821076,"title":"","content":"I agree with GottaGoFeast on that. By the way, have you considered what we have said so far? I insist, giving your characters the chance to create positive change does not negate the horror factor of the game, for the simple reason that the price and obstacles of that change can leave the character maimed both physically and mentally, if not death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T11:36:49-08:00","id":821095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=820951#post820951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Isn't that an Unmada problem? Geniuses are stubborn, sure, but their worldviews can adapt. Any clashing aesthetics and beliefs could be handled with the Universalist Merit or something like it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Maybe. I kind of that of it as Geniuses not being able to grasp opposing views, while an Unmada is virulently opposed to them. But the difficulties from a Paradigm only come up when they're assisting on a Wonder whose creator's Paradigm directly and completely opposes the Genius's own. So two theories that explain the same thing, differ, but don't necessarily exlclude each other. On top of that, the restriction only applies to Wonders that fall under that paradigm, so a Genius who believes in Spontaneous Generation could assist a Genius who worked in Lamarckian Evolution in creating a laser gun, or a teleporter, but the two would be unable to cooperate on a mutation ray because they have such wildly differing views on biology.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=821076#post821076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with GottaGoFeast on that. By the way, have you considered what we have said so far? I insist, giving your characters the chance to create positive change does not negate the horror factor of the game, for the simple reason that the price and obstacles of that change can leave the character maimed both physically and mentally, if not death.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not opposed to it, I just didn't feel it fit. I'm not an Unmada, and if you guys agree that it fits, it's not unreasonable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T11:51:20-08:00","id":821104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=821095#post821095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Maybe. I kind of that of it as Geniuses not being able to grasp opposing views, while an Unmada is virulently opposed to them. But the difficulties from a Paradigm only come up when they're assisting on a Wonder whose creator's Paradigm directly and completely opposes the Genius's own. So two theories that explain the same thing, differ, but don't necessarily exlclude each other. On top of that, the restriction only applies to Wonders that fall under that paradigm, so a Genius who believes in Spontaneous Generation could assist a Genius who worked in Lamarckian Evolution in creating a laser gun, or a teleporter, but the two would be unable to cooperate on a mutation ray because they have such wildly differing views on biology.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not opposed to it, I just didn't feel it fit. I'm not an Unmada, and if you guys agree that it fits, it's not unreasonable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perfect. Now, like real geniuses, here comes the hard part: finding common ground. I still think that my original idea could fit in the game. You can tinker with it as much as you like, as long as the core principle remains. The way I see it is that the magnus opus is the genius reaching his or her true potential: Understanding mania and inspiration, without succumbing to it. While my process could be a way for the genius to remind himself why he does what he does, to regain the connection lost with their fellow men, even as therapy for his alien mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T15:29:42-08:00","id":821248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=821104#post821104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perfect. Now, like real geniuses, here comes the hard part: finding common ground. I still think that my original idea could fit in the game. You can tinker with it as much as you like, as long as the core principle remains. The way I see it is that the magnus opus is the genius reaching his or her true potential: Understanding mania and inspiration, without succumbing to it. While my process could be a way for the genius to remind himself why he does what he does, to regain the connection lost with their fellow men, even as therapy for his alien mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think something like that could be best represented with reverse Breaking Points (that is, Breaking Points that raise Sympathy on success). That way, acting in ways that follow society's rules and benefit humanity will be something that's represented and encouraged in the rules.<br /> <br /> Presumably, Successes would provide the Inspired Condition, and Exceptional Successes might even give a burst of Mania.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T19:48:01-08:00","id":821386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=821248#post821248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think something like that could be best represented with reverse Breaking Points (that is, Breaking Points that raise Sympathy on success). That way, acting in ways that follow society's rules and benefit humanity will be something that's represented and encouraged in the rules.<br /> <br /> Presumably, Successes would provide the Inspired Condition, and Exceptional Successes might even give a burst of Mania.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like that approach. Do you have more notes? Are you the only one participating in the project?<br /> Apart from that. What was your reasoning for not being able to mix mundane technology with the wonders? I understand that you want to emphasize the alien aspect of geniuses and their creations, but I think that removing them completely from mainstream science and technology is not the answer. By doing that you're making them completely inhuman and difficult to relate too. If I'm being honest with you, right now geniuses feel more alien and inhuman to me that mages, and geniuses are supposed to at least pretend that what they are doing is science, not fancy magic with toys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2964,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","user":"Firanai","date":". 02-02-2016, 08:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T21:09:08-08:00","id":821425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=821386#post821386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like that approach. Do you have more notes? Are you the only one participating in the project?<br /> Apart from that. What was your reasoning for not being able to mix mundane technology with the wonders? I understand that you want to emphasize the alien aspect of geniuses and their creations, but I think that removing them completely from mainstream science and technology is not the answer. By doing that you're making them completely human and difficult to relate too. If I'm being honest with you, right now geniuses feel more alien and inhuman to me that mages, and geniuses are supposed to at least pretend that what they are doing is science, not fancy magic with toys.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never said anything about mixing mundane science and wonders. It's just when mundane <i>people</i> and Wonders mix that things are supposed to break down. It's sort of like when you have a program, and you've got it working, but then you have somebody else use it and it crashes for no discernible reason.<br /> <br /> As for being difficult to relate to, that's not surprising to me, since Genius always seemed on some levels to be kind of a satire of the academic community, being wrapped up in dense jargon and complicated ideas that don't make sense to outsiders, and being insanely bad at communicating their ideas to the public.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T01:01:05-08:00","id":821484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=821095#post821095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe. I kind of that of it as Geniuses not being able to grasp opposing views, while an Unmada is virulently opposed to them.</div> </div> </div> </div> You've got it backwards.<br /> <br /> An Unmada can't grasp opposing viewpoints, a regular Genius is virulently opposed to them* - along the lines of internet flamewars.<br /> <br /> Note though that Wonders are not always deeply tied to viewpoints. Take the artificers, they're a very political group considering themselves to be mostly underclass or working class and demanding a seat at the rich person's table. They're also Mad Engineers.<br /> <br /> For a working class Artificer with steam punk wonders, the &quot;opposing views&quot; isn't the working class artificer with pod people wonders, it's the wealthy ecconomist with scathingly views on marxist economics. An Artificer would dive right into a flamewar, an Unmada would look at you like you're a flat Earther and assume your either completely crazy or are deliberately lying because there's no possibility that's a genuine viewpoint.<br /> <br /> <br /> * Obviously it varies by Geniuses and catalysts. A Stunnan who's Breakthrough was &quot;isn't astronomy and LSD an awesome combination&quot; could be outright tolorent and interested in opposing viewpoints like &quot;nah, the fun stuff is underwater&quot; while a Neid will rarely show tollorence to people who disagree with core inspiration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 02-02-2016, 04:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T10:44:53-08:00","id":821725,"title":"","content":"Ok, let's start with something simple:<br /> What are the things that you think didn't work in the first edition and why?<br /> What new things do you want to include in the second edition and why?<br /> What's the new theme?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T17:42:25-08:00","id":822011,"title":"","content":"I've always thought the overall setting, and the bardos in particular, needed some work. Here's how I'd do it:<br /> <br /> Geniuses first appeared in 1895 in central Europe, although they quickly began to appear all over the world. History since then is more-or-less our history. The physical universe is exactly the same. Mars is the sterile Mars we're familiar with, and non-Genii will ever see anything different. However, some Wonders include the creation of unique pocket universes called bardos, which run on the conceits of the Wonder. Every bardo created by a particular Genius is distinct and isolated from that created by a different Genius, no matter how similar the Wonders are. Two Geniuses who travel to Mars by astral projection will find completely different alien civilisations, and will be unable to visit each other's Mars. Another Genius who builds a zero-point energy spacecraft could find yet another kind of alien, perhaps not native to Mars. It's also possible that either Wonder would transport the Genius to the actual, real-world Mars. Bringing concrete evidence of bardos into the real world encounters the same problems as Wonders interacting with the public.<br /> The same goes for time-travel, which can reach either real or fantastic history. The Lemurians have cobbled together an almost infinitely baroque &quot;secret history&quot; of the world from their time excursions, but this is just the historical version of their overarching &quot;scientific&quot; theories. One thing bardos have in common is that they lack Geniuses. The hypothetical Needle Grail, the Axiom of Inspiration itself, is rumoured to allow travel to bardos with Geniuses, or perhaps with nothing but Geniuses.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1430-gareth3","name":"Gareth3","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T18:52:34-08:00","id":822039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What are the things that you think didn't work in the first edition and why? </div> </div> </div>Everyone might disagree with me but... You don't feel like you're an inventor. I mean, the effects of axioms always seemed so specific. In D&amp;D I did things like gramarie to invent wondrous and horrific things, or used craft wondrous item to put together level one spell concepts and effects until I turned books into computers more advanced than the modern day. But with genius it always looked like you were tied to such specific effects. It's a side-effect of it just giving the result rather than the ingredients I think, so I'm not sure how it would be fixed as an issue. <br /> <br /> I mean, you can develop tonnes of stuff.... but you can't invent anything. Eh, pretty sure I'm wording this wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 02-02-2016, 10:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T20:18:06-08:00","id":822084,"title":"","content":"Part of the problem that I see here is that we all have very different perspectives on what a genius is. I think that the game is focusing too heavily in the genius as presented in Rick and Morty and the venture bros. If you keep telling your players that nothing of what they will do matters, then why play the game at all? you don't have to turn it into a Hanna-barbera cartoon, but let them be doc savage, tony stark, doctor doom, reed Richards, and lex Luthor if they want to. Also, let them create and invent, don't castrate them in the most interesting aspect of the game. Genius should be about him fighting to find acceptance in a world that rejects his vision, not about constantly struggling to create even a basic wonder. Let the genius invent, reality will take care of their inventions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T14:19:26-08:00","id":822750,"title":"","content":"Remember that Rick has significant and positive charachter development. He goes from not caring about anything and being borderline suicidal to loving his family and being willing to sacrifice himself for them. That's not saying that &quot;nothing of what they will do matters&quot;. It matters a huge deal, just on a personal level, rather than a cosmic level.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rick</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Take it from me Ice, you can't just float around space not caring about stuff forever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Btw Rick is a Klagen not a Neid. Though from what little hints we have he might have been closer to a Grimm or Hoffnung in his youth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T14:45:23-08:00","id":822785,"title":"","content":"I loved reading Genius The Transgression and I would love to play it but i can never find anyone to run it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T14:53:38-08:00","id":822794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=818937#post818937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1N0o3x3xDvsgU34sHQMUngSqoqTePt_mgFeK9PDj8jAo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Alright, these are my notes so far.</a><br /> <br /> Feel free to pick them apart and tell me what you think. The idea on the Wonders costing Experience was to make them more personal to the Genius, like an actual part of them and extension of their Inspiration than just a machine that you put Mania into and get stuff out of.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Question why did you make wonders cost XP. Wonders should cost Maina to make being that is the main thing Geniuses do is build wonders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T19:20:39-08:00","id":822966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=822794#post822794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Question why did you make wonders cost XP. Wonders should cost Maina to make being that is the main thing Geniuses do is build wonders.</div> </div> </div> </div>I explained it in literally the exact post you quoted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T17:25:00-08:00","id":823874,"title":"","content":"Malonkey1 how about if you point us to what kind of feedback do you want? is there any part that you want us to look at? an idea that you want to discuss? suggestions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":""