0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T16:37:22-08:00","id":825149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tambov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=824866#post824866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I checked Internet to see if there's a Lego Jurassic World (there is).<br /> <br /> Now, check out what Blue is doing (46:55):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JuHef5cnA1I&amp;t=46m55s\" data-code=\"JuHef5cnA1I\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/JuHef5cnA1I/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Kinda looks like kitbashing regular equipment, doesn't it?</div> </div> </div> </div>So it does.<br /> <br /> To be honest, I really only did the notes I did on a lark, I never really intended to do any sort of extended project to update the game.<br /> <br /> EDIT: That said, if people wanted to do that, I'd be more than willing to help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T20:01:43-08:00","id":825211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=825149#post825149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it does.<br /> <br /> To be honest, I really only did the notes I did on a lark, I never really intended to do any sort of extended project to update the game.<br /> <br /> EDIT: That said, if people wanted to do that, I'd be more than willing to help.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a pity, but I understand. It would be a massive project, and sadly I'm no good with systems, only with fiction. I hope that you get people to help, I really love the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T21:14:49-07:00","id":850411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=821725#post821725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, let's start with something simple:<br /> What are the things that you think didn't work in the first edition and why?<br /> What new things do you want to include in the second edition and why?<br /> What's the new theme?</div> </div> </div> </div>Things that I think didn't work: the Wonder Building system is a tad cumbersome and needs a lot of streamlining. Stupid Loserman said in the previous Genius thread that the tone focused on humor to the detriment of drama, and I agree. A balance between the two would be great. The Baramins' ideas about the correct future were a bit vague and confusing at times. Lemurians might work better as disorganized nutjobs who can't work as a team for too long. If they are yet another shadowy conspiracy, Geniuses of the Peerage will have an easier time telling themselves that they'll never stoop to such a level. But if Lemurians are more down to earth in scope and show the occasional glimmer of open-mindedness, they seem more nuanced and members of the Peerage can have more varied opinions on them. That's not to say that there can't be trends and alliances between Lemurians. I just imagine them as being similar to low Integrity Heroes: their thinking is dangerously black and white, which always leads to a lot of internal conflict, even if they have more resources than the Foundations.<br /> <br /> Things I wanna see in 2ED: <br /> <br /> 1) A more nuanced approach to the Peerage and Lemuria as mentioned above.<br /> <br /> 2) More details on factions for both of them, with special Merits and such to make each faction distinct. Aspects like hierarchies, recruitment, regional variants, resource distribution, internal conflict and so on deserve special attention.<br /> <br /> 3) A Wonder Building system that is simpler and more free-form. Milo has a point about the Axioms being rather restricted. There should be as much room for customization as possible to make the players feel more like inventors without memorizing loads of crunch. Borrowing bits and pieces from the other 2nd editions is OK, but should be kept to a minimum.<br /> <br /> 4) More Catalysts, Bardos and Manes.<br /> <br /> 5) An unique story catalyst, like the Strix, Idigam and Huntsmen. An updated version of the Illuminated was suggested in the previous thread, and I couldn't agree more. Lemurians and Unmada might be dangerous jerks, but at least they are still human. The Illuminated should either give a reason for Lemurians and Peers to team up, or cause an every-man-for-himself. They should have freaky advantages that go beyond Wonders, like perhaps some personalized Conditions and Tilts they inflict by just being in the scene, sort of like an Abyssal Verge pouring through a humanoid gateway.<br /> <br /> 6) More cross-over options, story seeds and signature cities. It'd be fun to see how the Inspired might interact with Beasts and Deviants.<br /> <br /> 7) Minimization of overlap with the themes of Mage, such as alienation and responsibility. This includes giving Obligation its own feel and impact on playing a Genius.<br /> <br /> The new theme should include &quot;trial and error&quot; and &quot;reconciliation of vision and reality&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 03-21-2016, 02:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T11:42:04-07:00","id":850718,"title":"","content":"Now that I think about it, if Nyarlathotep isn't an epic Unchained, he could easily be an Illuminated. His debut story vividly describes how much he upsets the lives of people wherever he goes, even though he was only making displays of technology that seemed fantastical to his audience. He is no human, and his full power is far more terrifying.<br /> <br /> I believe Sufficiently Advanced Aliens as a whole are a good place to start for developing the 2ED Illuminated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T20:41:45-07:00","id":850947,"title":"","content":"One more thing: I'd like more incentive for Beholden PCs. As it is, the only benefit they get from interacting with Geniuses is getting a worldview back, which Geniuses take away in the first place! And being a Beholden with no master is WAY too harsh. You can't recover willpower AT ALL and you die in less than a year. Even ghouls get better deals than these poor bastards. <br /> <br /> My suggestion is to treat this lack of a worldview as the <b>initial </b>stage of the Beholden. As they learn more about mad science and the rest of the strangeness in the CoD, they develop new identities and can even increase their chance of becoming Inspired. Having henchmen to do your dirty work is undeniably useful, but the lack of differing opinions can get boring and aggravating. In fact, I'd make the development of divergent Aspirations be the most common method of starting a Beholden's own Breakthrough. Geniuses who fear the growing independence of their Beholden can try to keep them mentally subservient in any way they can, but should the servant break free and Catalyze, there <b>will</b> be retribution. This is a game about Transgressions, after all, and limiting Beholden to NPCs takes away a source of good drama. It's similar to the enmity of ghouls and their vampire masters, sure, but what else can you really expect?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T22:28:48-07:00","id":850969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=822039#post822039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everyone might disagree with me but... You don't feel like you're an inventor. I mean, the effects of axioms always seemed so specific. In D&amp;D I did things like gramarie to invent wondrous and horrific things, or used craft wondrous item to put together level one spell concepts and effects until I turned books into computers more advanced than the modern day. But with genius it always looked like you were tied to such specific effects. It's a side-effect of it just giving the result rather than the ingredients I think, so I'm not sure how it would be fixed as an issue.<br /> <br /> I mean, you can develop tonnes of stuff.... but you can't invent anything. Eh, pretty sure I'm wording this wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually agree - given that the game has actual crafting rules now, I think that any Genius 2e should leverage them; maybe the Wonder Building rules could just tweak the Equipment Building rules <i>mercilessly</i> without actually supplanting them. If that's the case, then I'd say that a template ability <i>should</i> be expanding the Equipment Building rules to cover actual industry.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T22:45:08-07:00","id":850976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=850969#post850969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I actually agree - given that the game has actual crafting rules now, I think that any Genius 2e should leverage them; maybe the Wonder Building rules could just tweak the Equipment Building rules <i>mercilessly</i> without actually supplanting them. If that's the case, then I'd say that a template ability <i>should</i> be expanding the Equipment Building rules to cover actual industry.</div> </div> </div> </div> I had the same idea! But I forgot to write it down. Thanks for reminding me. I especially like your use of the word industry. You've given me some great inspiration (pun intended) for a draft of a new Wonder Building system.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T04:51:31-07:00","id":851071,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I'd like to see more of the Clockstoppers. They're quite fascinating, like the absolute inverse of an Illuminated. Hell, maybe that's what happens to a Genius at the other extreme - total rejection of the Spark as opposed to total surrender makes them anathema to not only the Spark itself, but to creativity in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4968-mrbreaksit","name":"MrBreaksIt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T22:25:54-07:00","id":862437,"title":"","content":"While I think Genius is an interesting concept, there is something that REALLY rubs me the wrong way (at least as of v1.1, which I have). Classifying Nikola Tesla as a Genius is not only way beyond lazy writing its completely ignoring the fact that we live in a modern world that was built using the technology that he engineered (Alternating Current, among other things). He most certainly was capable of expressing his ideas to others. To label him as a Mad Scientist (in essence) is an incredible disservice to a real-life genius whose life's work we now take for granted. Einstein didn't light the modern world anymore than Thomas Edison did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1801-craftmason-bob-s-cousin","name":"Craftmason Bob's Cousin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T01:14:25-07:00","id":862510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Craftmason Bob's Cousin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=862437#post862437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I think Genius is an interesting concept, there is something that REALLY rubs me the wrong way (at least as of v1.1, which I have). Classifying Nikola Tesla as a Genius is not only way beyond lazy writing its completely ignoring the fact that we live in a modern world that was built using the technology that he engineered (Alternating Current, among other things). He most certainly was capable of expressing his ideas to others. To label him as a Mad Scientist (in essence) is an incredible disservice to a real-life genius whose life's work we now take for granted. Einstein didn't light the modern world anymore than Thomas Edison did.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, I think it was more to tap into the mystique around him, and the stories of his more fanciful inventions (death rays and earthquake machines sound pretty crazy). Plus, he was a bit batty sometimes.<br /> <br /> And I think the presence of Tesla doesn't stomp on Tesla, so much as show that even people burdened by Inspiration can still do great things for humanity. He, despite being an Unmada (he was actually really angry about relativity in real life, mind), created the foundations for modern technology. He subverts the stereotype of the Doofenshmirtz Genius by not only making amazing, useful things that improve people's lives, but successfully conveys that knowledge to humanity.<br /> <br /> And looking back at Tesla's life, maybe there should be some representation of Mortals taking advantage of a Genius's, well, <i>Genius</i>, like Edison did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T09:34:35-07:00","id":862620,"title":"","content":"In terms of &quot;what doesn't work&quot;, we desperately need better reasons why Geniuses don't break the Masquerade. In 1e as its written, there's nothing stopping a Genius from, say, building a giant robot, having it smash a bunch of buildings, then filming it with his iPhone and throwing it on YouTube. I actually had the idea that Wonders interfere with mundane technology, meaning that they always look blurry and fake if you try to film them. And, fitting with the theme of futility and the struggle to actually change the world, I had the idea that people can see wonders just fine, but their memories cover them up. <br /> <br /> So, say a giant robot rampages through a city- people try to film it, but most cameras just glitch out. A few capture blurry images of a giant shape towering over the city. After it's over, most people swear that it was just an earthquake. The few people who do remember probably keep it to themselves, realizing they have no proof and no one would believe them. And that's how you can get away with giant robots rampaging through cities and still have a masquerade.<br /> <br /> On an earlier thread, I also mentioned having Manes be Twilight entities similar to Spirits, as another Masquerade measure, and I believe someone actually wrote out rules for this. To keep Mane Geniuses plausible, maybe we could say that Catalyzing gives a Mane the power to manifest?<br /> <br /> And, finally, I think Genius is rich and complete enough that it doesn't need to be a ChroD fangame. I would completely support creating an original set of mechanics and releasing it as an independent product.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 04-09-2016, 12:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T09:43:19-07:00","id":862625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=862510#post862510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, I think it was more to tap into the mystique around him, and the stories of his more fanciful inventions (death rays and earthquake machines sound pretty crazy). Plus, he was a bit batty sometimes.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair a lot of geniuses get &quot;batty&quot; as they age. Just look at Howard Hughes. A phenomenal business man and aeronautical engineer but he was totally batshit crazy by the end of his life.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=862510#post862510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I think the presence of Tesla doesn't stomp on Tesla, so much as show that even people burdened by Inspiration can still do great things for humanity. He, despite being an Unmada (he was actually really angry about relativity in real life, mind), created the foundations for modern technology. He subverts the stereotype of the Doofenshmirtz Genius by not only making amazing, useful things that improve people's lives, but successfully conveys that knowledge to humanity.<br /> <br /> And looking back at Tesla's life, maybe there should be some representation of Mortals taking advantage of a Genius's, well, <i>Genius</i>, like Edison did.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally agree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T09:52:41-07:00","id":862631,"title":"","content":"We already have a good reason. In the WoD the primary reason for the masquerade is mankind intentionally ignoring the clear evidence saying the supernatural exists.<br /> <br /> If they can ignore a Vampire throwing a truck, they can ignore a Genius in a large robot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T10:33:31-07:00","id":862644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=862620#post862620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In terms of &quot;what doesn't work&quot;, we desperately need better reasons why Geniuses don't break the Masquerade. In 1e as its written, there's nothing stopping a Genius from, say, building a giant robot, having it smash a bunch of buildings, then filming it with his iPhone and throwing it on YouTube. I actually had the idea that Wonders interfere with mundane technology, meaning that they always look blurry and fake if you try to film them. And, fitting with the theme of futility and the struggle to actually change the world, I had the idea that people can see wonders just fine, but their memories cover them up. <br /> <br /> So, say a giant robot rampages through a city- people try to film it, but most cameras just glitch out. A few capture blurry images of a giant shape towering over the city. After it's over, most people swear that it was just an earthquake. The few people who do remember probably keep it to themselves, realizing they have no proof and no one would believe them. And that's how you can get away with giant robots rampaging through cities and still have a masquerade.<br /> <br /> On an earlier thread, I also mentioned having Manes be Twilight entities similar to Spirits, as another Masquerade measure, and I believe someone actually wrote out rules for this. To keep Mane Geniuses plausible, maybe we could say that Catalyzing gives a Mane the power to manifest?<br /> <br /> And, finally, I think Genius is rich and complete enough that it doesn't need to be a ChroD fangame. I would completely support creating an original set of mechanics and releasing it as an independent product.</div> </div> </div> </div> I was the one who made those rules you mentioned, but I'm not satisfied with them. Giving normal Manifestations to Manes, even if tweaked and powered by Mania instead of Essence, makes them too close to spirits. Conceptually, they're closer to hobgoblins - a big aggregate of weirdness that is quite corporeal and shaped by ideas/stories. Perhaps they would be capable of shifting into the same frequency of Twilight as Goetia and Astral projections, but it would not be a universal ability. The more advanced or stranger Manes might have additional ways of interacting with the material world and the Mania within, but that would be rare.<br /> <br /> The Illuminated, however, are strong candidates for being modeled with an adapted ephemeral being template, like the Strix and Idigam. Remember how the Strix have Embodiments that alter their pseudo-ephemeral forms and allow different types of possession? And how the Idigam can mutilate and mutate spirits with their Essence-Shaping? The Illuminated should have something like that, but focused on the direct manipulation, generation and dissipation of Mania. Heck, they might not even need to build Wonders: their mastery of Mania would be such that they bring Wonders, Manes and even Bardos into existence simply by willing it. Like how Athena sprang fully formed and armed from Zeus' brow.<br /> <br /> In my new vision for the Illuminated, the notion that they are former Geniuses who had all Obligation burned away by Inspiration is a rumor and cautionary tale, rather than a fact. No one knows for sure how they come to be, or if they always were. Even figuring out what they want in most cases is very hard, as they are exceptionally alien. I need to think of ways to make them more distinct from True Fae as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 04-09-2016, 01:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T13:28:14-07:00","id":862733,"title":"","content":"Being the antagonist fanatic I am, may I suggest a little of both?<br /> <br /> <i>Some </i>Illuminated are almost definitely Geniuses who lost all Sympathy and no longer see the world as anything more than raw materials and a testing field for their dreams. These Illuminated often have a touch of tragedy about them, as their Magnum Opuses are often altruistic in nature; the overall theme (which I think should be something like Big Dreams, Little Dreamers-the passion and ambition is there, the capability is not, not without compromise and realistic expectations) is magnified and examined, showing exactly what happens when the dream makes no accommodations for anyone or anything else. Illumination is the light of pure knowledge and a higher truth, certainly, but the thing about light? It's <i>blinding, </i>and the Illuminated themselves are the most blind of all. I'm thinking something like Dr. Moreau; on some level, he wants desperately to perfect potentially revolutionary medical techniques, but he doesn't comprehend that turning a bunch of innocent animals into beings whose very existence is torture is causing more problems than it solves-and the sad part is, the very fact his beastmen live is proof he's on to something. On a less sympathetic note, Yohji Amada from Binary Domain creating a truly sentient AI-by, and I quote &quot;instilling the concept of suffering into [it].&quot; Grand dream, awful methods (Larvae on crack). Perhaps something more akin to super-Lemurians, but the possibility should be there, if only to show why Sympathy is needed.<br /> <br /> Others, though? Others seem to have come out of nowhere. They may be (hopefully) particularly unempathetic posthumans from a distant future, Mania elementals given a body, Manes embodying disproven <i>subconscious </i>theories (and thus not possessing a recognizable ego, only the urge to create), real no-shit extraterrestrials, all of these, none of these...Those Illuminated embody the mood (which is something like Endless Possibility, Endless Terror-a truly open world is also one truly open to things that can go wrong). Their past, what they are, is pointless-what they <i>do </i>is the entirety of what anybody should be concerned with. Much as how VII is the vampire's vampire story, these Illuminated are the mad scientist's mad scientist story-they appear from nowhere, set up shop, and unleash a tide of wonders and horrors into the world that no one is able to truly explain, only hypothesize.<br /> <br /> The difference from the True Fae? Gentry have obvious motives for alien actions. Illuminated? They can explain perfectly well what they're doing, and anybody who studies their black miracles can quickly grasp it. But their motives? Even madness seems too mundane for the experiments of the Awful Ones. Just as a complete lack of Sympathy prevents them from understanding you, so does it prevent you from being privy to their natural-disaster minds-only the aftershocks.<br /> <br /> (Don't think they should have ephemeral rules, though-not entirely. Perhaps they have full mental stats <i>but </i>P-F-R for everything else, like how Embodied Strix have physical and spirit stats. The core, soul, and heart of an Awful One is the nuclear engine she calls her brain. Everything else is but meaningless tools of it, and can be recycled and retrofitted as needed).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T13:54:23-07:00","id":862747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=862733#post862733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being the antagonist fanatic I am, may I suggest a little of both?<br /> <br /> <i>Some </i>Illuminated are almost definitely Geniuses who lost all Sympathy and no longer see the world as anything more than raw materials and a testing field for their dreams. These Illuminated often have a touch of tragedy about them, as their Magnum Opuses are often altruistic in nature; the overall theme (which I think should be something like Big Dreams, Little Dreamers-the passion and ambition is there, the capability is not, not without compromise and realistic expectations) is magnified and examined, showing exactly what happens when the dream makes no accommodations for anyone or anything else. Illumination is the light of pure knowledge and a higher truth, certainly, but the thing about light? It's <i>blinding, </i>and the Illuminated themselves are the most blind of all. I'm thinking something like Dr. Moreau; on some level, he wants desperately to perfect potentially revolutionary medical techniques, but he doesn't comprehend that turning a bunch of innocent animals into beings whose very existence is torture is causing more problems than it solves-and the sad part is, the very fact his beastmen live is proof he's on to something. On a less sympathetic note, Yohji Amada from Binary Domain creating a truly sentient AI-by, and I quote &quot;instilling the concept of suffering into [it].&quot; Grand dream, awful methods (Larvae on crack). Perhaps something more akin to super-Lemurians, but the possibility should be there, if only to show why Sympathy is needed.<br /> <br /> Others, though? Others seem to have come out of nowhere. They may be (hopefully) particularly unempathetic posthumans from a distant future, Mania elementals given a body, Manes embodying disproven <i>subconscious </i>theories (and thus not possessing a recognizable ego, only the urge to create), real no-shit extraterrestrials, all of these, none of these...Those Illuminated embody the mood (which is something like Endless Possibility, Endless Terror-a truly open world is also one truly open to things that can go wrong). Their past, what they are, is pointless-what they <i>do </i>is the entirety of what anybody should be concerned with. Much as how VII is the vampire's vampire story, these Illuminated are the mad scientist's mad scientist story-they appear from nowhere, set up shop, and unleash a tide of wonders and horrors into the world that no one is able to truly explain, only hypothesize.<br /> <br /> The difference from the True Fae? Gentry have obvious motives for alien actions. Illuminated? They can explain perfectly well what they're doing, and anybody who studies their black miracles can quickly grasp it. But their motives? Even madness seems too mundane for the experiments of the Awful Ones. Just as a complete lack of Sympathy prevents them from understanding you, so does it prevent you from being privy to their natural-disaster minds-only the aftershocks.<br /> <br /> (Don't think they should have ephemeral rules, though-not entirely. Perhaps they have full mental stats <i>but </i>P-F-R for everything else, like how Embodied Strix have physical and spirit stats. The core, soul, and heart of an Awful One is the nuclear engine she calls her brain. Everything else is but meaningless tools of it, and can be recycled and retrofitted as needed).</div> </div> </div> </div> Excellent suggestions! I agree that they would have Mental Attributes as their focus and Power/Finesse/Resistance for everything else. Would they have Rank and display respect or caution toward others of their &quot;kind&quot; who outRank them? I think it would be more fitting if they had a pseudo Rank like the Shadow Potency of the Strix. It could be called Conflagration, as a reference to an all-consuming Inspiration and outer space/other realms.<br /> <br /> How do you think the Illuminated would interact with the Principle, the God-Machine, and their associated beings and phenomena?<br /> <br /> Also, were you saying Sympathy instead of Obligation for any specific reason? Geniuses can be cautious and proactive without being all that fond of mere mortals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 04-09-2016, 05:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T15:56:57-07:00","id":862821,"title":"","content":"Sympathy was the new term for the Integrity meter in the document. I actually like Obligation a little better, so using that from now on.<br /> <br /> Love the Conflagration idea for pseudo-rank. We could also create a similar structure of Dread Powers for Illuminated, with each dot of Conflagration providing a different power related to the direct manipulation of Mania (we could call them Plasmas to keep the &quot;celestial fire&quot; theme, or it could be the different powers of the long-fabled Axiom of Pankosmoi, if we <i>really </i>want to drive in the &quot;alien knowledge&quot; thing-Lemuria's obsession would then be not so much discovering the Final Axiom but being somehow able to learn it while sane-by Lemurian standards), and different families of pure Dread Power to synergize with their Axioms. I figure that the groupings are based around the narrative qualities of Illuminated (with my working names based off of Greek philosophies-something the Lemurians came up with to try and quantify the unquantifiable): incomprehensible knowledge (Eleatic), the rapid reshaping of the world (Sophist), and the consumption of all things to fuel ambition (Pythagorean). Most are based more around buffing their Axioms and Wonders or messing with the abilities of others.<br /> <br /> As for the God-Machine, I'd say Illuminated are the closest thing you can get to actual reliable theorists on how occult physics work-they seem to have an instinctive understanding of a truth beyond paradigm that may be occult physics. Then again, could be something completely different, and in any case, the Awful Ones are, if anything, even stranger than the Machine (at least you can guess at the mindset and motives of angels). For its part, the Machine would love it if the Illuminated would leave, as it regards them as living natural disasters-at most, it can point them in the direction away from itself, but when one's dealing with the maddest of the mad, Infrastructure they find tends to be poked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T04:23:49-07:00","id":863564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=862631#post862631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We already have a good reason. In the WoD the primary reason for the masquerade is mankind intentionally ignoring the clear evidence saying the supernatural exists.<br /> <br /> If they can ignore a Vampire throwing a truck, they can ignore a Genius in a large robot.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is really all the explanation that is needed. What good is it that some - not even all - templates get some help with stealth, when they still very clearly leave an obvious trail about their activities? It is virtually impossible that their gimmicks and secrecy could be so effective that it would be enough to keep their existence a secret.<br /> For example, the fact that Vampires don't show up on film is more likely to create more problems than it is to solve others.<br /> The only reasonable answer is that the people of the WoD KNOW, but they prefer to keep their head down and not get involved in anything. It's a survival trait that develops in a society where the supernatural tends to cull hard anyone who is too nosy and sticks her head out.<br /> THe majority of WoD people are almost certainly very superstitious and paranoid, but try to only think of the good things to protect their necks and sanity.<br /> <br /> (I did once initiate a hypothetical fan template called &quot;Agent&quot;, which was essentially MIB mixed with Paranoia the RPG: people who aren't sure that their own memories are real or that they are even still human and who maintain a sense of paranoia and secrecy even with each other hunt down supernaturals who have broken the Masquerade and witnesses who got away, all in the service of an alleged worldwide conspiracy and world government.<br /> Morality stat was called Paranoia and compelled you to do things like never using your real name (Mr Brown and Mr Smith), never admitting everything you know about something, and so on.<br /> Renown stat was called Influence which you could swap for all kinds of social merits or equipment, to the level of having a hotline to the President to order a nuclear strike at the very top.)<br /> <br /> It could be easy to rework it for Genius, since Genius is good at modelling stuff like this anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2330-vree","name":"Vree","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T05:01:23-07:00","id":863572,"title":"","content":"Hello/welcome Firanai! Glad you like Genius.<br /> Do you maybe want to play-by-post it? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I might be willing to GM a forum game for a sufficiently MATUREbunch of players.<br /> <br /> Moochava isn't making a new version soon methinks - he said updating all the tangly details (starting with the bookmarks) was already too much of a bother in the 1.1 version.<br /> He does respond to fan letters and questions though! (via his email on his site)<br /> <br /> We've had discussions over at rpg.net as well as this board before - really too much to collect all of the good/bad ideas.<br /> <br /> Me, I'm against any so called &quot;new edition&quot; that starts to tinker with the parts that work. You do that, you fail as an amateur game developer.<br /> GMC version of Genius - I'm glad if some folks try to do that, (personally I don't give a sh#@, I think GMC is a crap system <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> What I'd want to do for a 2nd edition would be a minimalistic change list for things that just plain don't work.<br /> Here are the things I prepared hypothetical changes for:<br /> <br /> - Made Mania recovery more dynamic<br /> <br /> The current default method is &quot;research for X hours&quot;, which is a time investment that players skip anyway, and all it is good for is to holding up the game when PCs are on the clock or need to do stuff together. What I wanted to do was make players able to do &quot;research&quot; while on the move, and interact with the enviroment more - for example, disassembling technology to see how it works would net Mania but also destroy said equipment in the process (they'd net Mania based on their estimated Respurces value). So if you pick the TV apart and rebuild it as a death ray, you still have to answer to the landlord about where the TV had gone...Something like that, maybe. (remember this is all hypothetical)<br /> <br /> I also wanted to make the Resources requirement for Wonders more dynamic: you don't have to have the Resources MERIT to cover your expenses, you can just steal or otherwise acquire the materials for a one-time Resources bonus.<br /> <br /> <br /> - Switched up Metatropi rank order (and made minor adjustments to some other Axioms too)<br /> <br /> Metaptropi users currently gains the incredibly powerful Sorcerer's Stone effect (turning one material into another), which can do stuff like insta-kill enemies, at the early 2nd level.<br /> Yet changing size is somehow a Rank 3 effect. I switched all that up, so that now growing/shrinking stuff and attacking Size is a more basic effect (this is also in line with how the Collapsible variable works), so that there is a clearer progression from small cosmetic changes to more dramatic alterations<br /> <br /> <br /> - Limited what a single individual wonder can do<br /> <br /> Geniuses are incredibly powerful; each new Axiom rank gives them access to a host of new powers.<br /> What's MORE surprising though is that there is very little limit to how much of this they can exploit at once.<br /> Let me give you an example. If you want to make a Wonder that can do EVERYTHING at Apokalypsi 2 - you can!<br /> All you need is a successful skill roll. There is an attempt made to make the Genius' rank in science skills act as a limit on this, but it's not too difficult to bypass with a lucky roll. (Plus, any Genius can near-max out only 5 science skills easily, even if also need points for other things, say fighting and social skills.)<br /> There are variables that reward you for limited focus, but the tiny bonus from them is hardly worth the loss of flexibility they come with.<br /> <br /> I intended to make it so that there is a bigger incentive to create specialized Wonders, to cull down on Genius power a bit and encourage players to make more unique ones.<br /> <br /> (I recall when I was making a robot character and wondered <br /> <br /> - Made &quot;separate wonder&quot; rules clearer.<br /> <br /> This is really a formatting issue: some Wonders (like telephatic ones) are separated from others at the same rank in the same Axiom, but this is often unclear.<br /> You don't need a &quot;graph&quot; or something like Moochava suggested; you just need to make the borderline clear in the text.<br /> <br /> <br /> - Small updates to some variables<br /> eg: &quot;Assembly Line&quot; is now a variable, not a merit.<br /> (I could explain why/how it works but next time k?)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=862620#post862620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, finally, I think Genius is rich and complete enough that it doesn't need to be a ChroD fangame. I would completely support creating an original set of mechanics and releasing it as an independent product.</div> </div> </div> </div>I tinkered with my own &quot;WoD alternative&quot; systems before (to fuel all the fansplats that are being dreamed up if Onyx Path ever breaks off the permission - it is already impossible to storytell fansplat with GMC as you need THREE books (the core rules, the GMC update, and the fansplat book, very unpractical to the new player).<br /> I could work on one if there's interest.<br /> <br /> Though frankly, at the end of the day, you just want to play, and in most games 99% of the rules does not even actually matter.<br /> All I'd really want is a better die resolution mechanic. (Success/Fail options do not an interesting story make)<br /> Then there is the matter of years of skill mattering more, a better targeted shot system etc. ...actually, I may want a ot. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> But frankly you only need the basics for a good game. You can already take the best of oWoD/nWoD/GMC/other RPG system of preference to create a good not-so-original system that does just fine for a game, and playing is the whole point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2330-vree","name":"Vree","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T18:48:36-07:00","id":864027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Me, I'm against any so called &quot;new edition&quot; that starts to tinker with the parts that work. You do that, you fail as an amateur game developer.<br /> GMC version of Genius - I'm glad if some folks try to do that, (personally I don't give a sh#@, I think GMC is a crap system <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> What I'd want to do for a 2nd edition would be a minimalistic change list for things that just plain don't work. </div> </div> </div>1. What parts &quot;work&quot; is very subjective. I mean, I feel that &quot;how wonders are made in the system&quot; is an aspect of the system that doesn't work, since it doesn't make any sense for a game about super science.<br /> 2. If you're making a second edition, you'd be using GMC. Otherwise it's just &quot;1.etc&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T21:57:40-07:00","id":864119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=864027#post864027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1. What parts &quot;work&quot; is very subjective. I mean, I feel that &quot;how wonders are made in the system&quot; is an aspect of the system that doesn't work, since it doesn't make any sense for a game about super science.<br /> 2. If you're making a second edition, you'd be using GMC. Otherwise it's just &quot;1.etc&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I gotta agree on Wonders. They're more complex than they need to be, and it feels more like gadgeteering than mad science sometimes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T22:05:19-07:00","id":864123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=864119#post864119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I gotta agree on Wonders. They're more complex than they need to be, and it feels more like gadgeteering than mad science sometimes.</div> </div> </div> </div> I third this notion. However, what exactly makes mad science truly mad? The spontaneity, impulsiveness and even compulsion? The unintended effects and properties? Some abstract, vile part of your psyche subtly infecting the device? We need a consensus if we're gonna update the Wonder Building system.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T02:12:44-07:00","id":864182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=864119#post864119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I gotta agree on Wonders. They're more complex than they need to be, and it feels more like gadgeteering than mad science sometimes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Feels more like going on Ebay to me.... I mean, you just browse looking at the gadgets that already exist and buying them rather than making the gadgets yourself. The only &quot;inventiveness&quot; just comes from the equivalent to putting a sticker on the back of your laptop.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">I third this notion. However, what exactly makes mad science truly mad? The spontaneity, impulsiveness and even compulsion? The unintended effects and properties? Some abstract, vile part of your psyche subtly infecting the device? We need a consensus if we're gonna update the Wonder Building system.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Well, it just has to have cause =! effect I'd assume. Putting x + y + z components together equal b even though they should equal a. </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T09:30:41-07:00","id":864342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=863572#post863572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello/welcome Firanai! Glad you like Genius.<br /> Do you maybe want to play-by-post it? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I might be willing to GM a forum game for a sufficiently MATUREbunch of players.<br /> <br /> Moochava isn't making a new version soon methinks - he said updating all the tangly details (starting with the bookmarks) was already too much of a bother in the 1.1 version.<br /> He does respond to fan letters and questions though! (via his email on his site)<br /> <br /> We've had discussions over at rpg.net as well as this board before - really too much to collect all of the good/bad ideas.<br /> <br /> Me, I'm against any so called &quot;new edition&quot; that starts to tinker with the parts that work. You do that, you fail as an amateur game developer.<br /> GMC version of Genius - I'm glad if some folks try to do that, (personally I don't give a sh#@, I think GMC is a crap system <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> What I'd want to do for a 2nd edition would be a minimalistic change list for things that just plain don't work.<br /> Here are the things I prepared hypothetical changes for:<br /> <br /> - Made Mania recovery more dynamic<br /> <br /> The current default method is &quot;research for X hours&quot;, which is a time investment that players skip anyway, and all it is good for is to holding up the game when PCs are on the clock or need to do stuff together. What I wanted to do was make players able to do &quot;research&quot; while on the move, and interact with the enviroment more - for example, disassembling technology to see how it works would net Mania but also destroy said equipment in the process (they'd net Mania based on their estimated Respurces value). So if you pick the TV apart and rebuild it as a death ray, you still have to answer to the landlord about where the TV had gone...Something like that, maybe. (remember this is all hypothetical)<br /> <br /> I also wanted to make the Resources requirement for Wonders more dynamic: you don't have to have the Resources MERIT to cover your expenses, you can just steal or otherwise acquire the materials for a one-time Resources bonus.<br /> <br /> <br /> - Switched up Metatropi rank order (and made minor adjustments to some other Axioms too)<br /> <br /> Metaptropi users currently gains the incredibly powerful Sorcerer's Stone effect (turning one material into another), which can do stuff like insta-kill enemies, at the early 2nd level.<br /> Yet changing size is somehow a Rank 3 effect. I switched all that up, so that now growing/shrinking stuff and attacking Size is a more basic effect (this is also in line with how the Collapsible variable works), so that there is a clearer progression from small cosmetic changes to more dramatic alterations<br /> <br /> <br /> - Limited what a single individual wonder can do<br /> <br /> Geniuses are incredibly powerful; each new Axiom rank gives them access to a host of new powers.<br /> What's MORE surprising though is that there is very little limit to how much of this they can exploit at once.<br /> Let me give you an example. If you want to make a Wonder that can do EVERYTHING at Apokalypsi 2 - you can!<br /> All you need is a successful skill roll. There is an attempt made to make the Genius' rank in science skills act as a limit on this, but it's not too difficult to bypass with a lucky roll. (Plus, any Genius can near-max out only 5 science skills easily, even if also need points for other things, say fighting and social skills.)<br /> There are variables that reward you for limited focus, but the tiny bonus from them is hardly worth the loss of flexibility they come with.<br /> <br /> I intended to make it so that there is a bigger incentive to create specialized Wonders, to cull down on Genius power a bit and encourage players to make more unique ones.<br /> <br /> (I recall when I was making a robot character and wondered<br /> <br /> - Made &quot;separate wonder&quot; rules clearer.<br /> <br /> This is really a formatting issue: some Wonders (like telephatic ones) are separated from others at the same rank in the same Axiom, but this is often unclear.<br /> You don't need a &quot;graph&quot; or something like Moochava suggested; you just need to make the borderline clear in the text.<br /> <br /> <br /> - Small updates to some variables<br /> eg: &quot;Assembly Line&quot; is now a variable, not a merit.<br /> (I could explain why/how it works but next time k?)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I tinkered with my own &quot;WoD alternative&quot; systems before (to fuel all the fansplats that are being dreamed up if Onyx Path ever breaks off the permission - it is already impossible to storytell fansplat with GMC as you need THREE books (the core rules, the GMC update, and the fansplat book, very unpractical to the new player).<br /> I could work on one if there's interest.<br /> <br /> Though frankly, at the end of the day, you just want to play, and in most games 99% of the rules does not even actually matter.<br /> All I'd really want is a better die resolution mechanic. (Success/Fail options do not an interesting story make)<br /> Then there is the matter of years of skill mattering more, a better targeted shot system etc. ...actually, I may want a ot. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> But frankly you only need the basics for a good game. You can already take the best of oWoD/nWoD/GMC/other RPG system of preference to create a good not-so-original system that does just fine for a game, and playing is the whole point.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would really love to play. The mad genius trope is one of my favourtie ones from all time. It's such a tragic an amazing figure. The super intelligent scientist who can create amazing things capable of changin the world, but it's misunderstood and rejected by society. From the optimism of Tom strong to the pessimism of Rick Sanchez, both aspects of how well or bad can it go. <br /> By the way, I'm curious, what do you think about the proposals I posted? what do you think about them? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T15:32:48-07:00","id":864577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=864123#post864123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I third this notion. However, what exactly makes mad science truly mad? The spontaneity, impulsiveness and even compulsion? The unintended effects and properties? Some abstract, vile part of your psyche subtly infecting the device? We need a consensus if we're gonna update the Wonder Building system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you COULD randomize it.<br /> Instead of assembling the exact thing you want yourself, assign a number to the different variables (like it is done with Faults), roll 'em up, you'll get a different Wonder each time. And it's a lot trickier to replace a winning combination. Players will probably treasure that +2 raygun a lot more.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=864182#post864182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, you just browse looking at the gadgets that already exist and buying them rather than making the gadgets yourself. The only &quot;inventiveness&quot; just comes from the equivalent to putting a sticker on the back of your laptop.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is bull tho. (this and any other similar comments.)<br /> In fact it really makes me question if this answer even PLAYED Genius or just read the book properly. (since there are a lot of example custom Wonders in it, too)<br /> <br /> First of all, you could put what you say as a fault of ALL WoD books: you pick your abilities from a list, rather than creating your own.<br /> <br /> But 2nd, Genius is the EXCEPTION! Rather than giving you a list of powers, it actually gives you the tools to create your own powers!<br /> <br /> For example, where others book would say &quot;This is your Explosive attack (the only possible combination we give you), it costs this much and does this much damage, thxbye&quot; Genius says &quot;if you wanted to make a power Explosive, this is how much you'd adjust its cost by&quot;. That's what all of the variables are for, they are approximations of how much everything that exists in the WoD system is worth relative to each other and what the proper cost for ANY power you can dream up is.<br /> Where can you find more freedom than that? I really don't get what this answer is thinking, or if it even talks about this game.<br /> <br /> Heck, I can accept an argument that there is TOO MUCH freedom. Maybe if you're a mad scientists, building anything you want, AS you want it should not be THIS easy. But too LITTLE? Please. You better explain this.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2330-vree","name":"Vree","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T16:35:34-07:00","id":864606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=864577#post864577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, you COULD randomize it.<br /> Instead of assembling the exact thing you want yourself, assign a number to the different variables (like it is done with Faults), roll 'em up, you'll get a different Wonder each time. And it's a lot trickier to replace a winning combination. Players will probably treasure that +2 raygun a lot more.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This is bull tho. (this and any other similar comments.)<br /> In fact it really makes me question if this answer even PLAYED Genius or just read the book properly. (since there are a lot of example custom Wonders in it, too)<br /> <br /> First of all, you could put what you say as a fault of ALL WoD books: you pick your abilities from a list, rather than creating your own.<br /> <br /> But 2nd, Genius is the EXCEPTION! Rather than giving you a list of powers, it actually gives you the tools to create your own powers!<br /> <br /> For example, where others book would say &quot;This is your Explosive attack (the only possible combination we give you), it costs this much and does this much damage, thxbye&quot; Genius says &quot;if you wanted to make a power Explosive, this is how much you'd adjust its cost by&quot;. That's what all of the variables are for, they are approximations of how much everything that exists in the WoD system is worth relative to each other and what the proper cost for ANY power you can dream up is.<br /> Where can you find more freedom than that? I really don't get what this answer is thinking, or if it even talks about this game.<br /> <br /> Heck, I can accept an argument that there is TOO MUCH freedom. Maybe if you're a mad scientists, building anything you want, AS you want it should not be THIS easy. But too LITTLE? Please. You better explain this.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I think what he means is this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=822039#post822039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everyone might disagree with me but... You don't feel like you're an inventor. I mean, the effects of axioms always seemed so specific. In D&amp;D I did things like gramarie to invent wondrous and horrific things, or used craft wondrous item to put together level one spell concepts and effects until I turned books into computers more advanced than the modern day. But with genius it always looked like you were tied to such specific effects. It's a side-effect of it just giving the result rather than the ingredients I think, so I'm not sure how it would be fixed as an issue.<br /> <br /> I mean, you can develop tonnes of stuff.... but you can't invent anything. Eh, pretty sure I'm wording this wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I feel much the same way.<br /> <br /> Skafoi is always every mode of transport no matter how unrelated they are.<br /> Apocalypsi is scanning and computers<br /> Katastrophi is always hurting, weaponry, or ray guns for the other things.<br /> Protasia is for all your defense needs.<br /> And Eprikato just irked me for it's theme of &quot;control&quot; being so wide spread that it felt like a leftovers grabbag.<br /> <br /> <br /> I get that many other splats don't have the option of customization as Genius does, but Genius also very... bound in a way to the Axioms. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 04-12-2016, 07:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T17:15:35-07:00","id":864622,"title":"","content":"Well, that's just what you get in a system that's starting with the result and not the source. You can take either path when you're writing an an rpg, it's largely a matter of preference. One can have a preference for one or the other, but I don't know what can be done if the only problem is simply that it isn't your thing.<br /> <br /> I personally prefer result-based systems, for example, since they are easier to handle on the mechanical side. Why'd I use a separate skill for a Force Lightning and a Bloodletting if they both result in the same 2 damage effect? I might as well start with the 2 damage and add the source and related fine detail 2nd, or even let the player define where and how it came from.<br /> In the systems you mention that start with the source you get all kinds of overlaps, two categories able to do similar things or things that are normally outside their scope and so on.<br /> <br /> This is hardly unique to Genius in the Wod tho, oMage and nMage was the same way too.<br /> (Genius took a ton of inspiration (lowercase I) from oMage, as everybody knows.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2330-vree","name":"Vree","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T17:35:01-07:00","id":864627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=864342#post864342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would really love to play. The mad genius trope is one of my favourtie ones from all time. It's such a tragic an amazing figure. The super intelligent scientist who can create amazing things capable of changin the world, but it's misunderstood and rejected by society. From the optimism of Tom strong to the pessimism of Rick Sanchez, both aspects of how well or bad can it go.<br /> By the way, I'm curious, what do you think about the proposals I posted? what do you think about them? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Which comment would that be, is it #7 on the first page?<br /> <br /> I think that a Genius who is trying to cure herself of her Inspired condition can be a fascinating character. Certainly a good story in that.<br /> <br /> That said I'm not sure if I agree with the way you went about it.<br /> (Now, you can do in your own campaigns what you want, of course, you don't need to follow the book. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Still, these are some pretty crucial elements.)<br /> <br /> When you say:<br /> <br /> &quot;In this process, the genius takes one of his or her wonders, and proceeds to turn it into something that regular people can use&quot;<br /> <br /> This isn't possible and this is why.<br /> <br /> Behind real technological advances there is research. Ie. an attempt to understand how natural processes work, then trying to see if any of what that allows for that could be beneficial for humans.<br /> How the real laws work is not up to the researcher. Sometimes you get unexpected or unwanted results. Sometimes it turns nature simply does not allow for something, or that the cost is too high to afford.<br /> <br /> Wonders definitely DO give you what you wish for. But, although the laws that hold them together may SEEM real, they are really a product of the Genius' imagination plus the mystical mumbo-jumbo wecall Mania and Inspiration.<br /> Remove Mania and the laws the Genius made up also disappear.<br /> (Of course some Genii may argue that these laws are also true and real on some meta-level of a &quot;higher&quot; reality, but it does not make much difference from the POV of science in our &quot;mundane&quot; reality.)<br /> <br /> Making a true, mass reproducable scientific equivalent of a Wondernot as simple as taking a Wonder and substituting the &quot;real&quot; laws. There may not even be an equivalent real law, or the same result may only be achievable through a completely different process.<br /> You can't force the laws you need on reality, you can only learn more about its set laws. (And that's what Mania is all about, forcing the laws you want on nature.)<br /> <br /> A genius who gets it into her head that she can make a Wonder &quot;real&quot;, what she's actually doing is replacing make-believe laws with other make-believe laws, still all held together by Mania.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying Wonders can never be turned into &quot;real&quot; machines. All Wonders by their very nature have at least a little real science in them. Replace the Aether Mechanism in a clock with a regular mechanism, you've got a clock. It may not be able to show you the Universal Countdown anymore, but it will still tell the time. For a Genius who's trying to reconnect with the munande scientist she used to be, rebuilding her Wonders in this manner can certainly offer some solace and clarity.<br /> <br /> But this is very different from actual scientific advances, which can only be achieved by regular, mudane research, research and research.<br /> If a Genius can somehow make a recovery from her Maniac state she may be able to resume doing this. She may spend decades trying to remake the Quantum Mechanical Butterfly she once could create from just fantasy and air, but for real this time. She may find that natural laws do not allow it, or allow only for a much weaker version<br /> She may find that even if it is possible in theory, research will still need decades or even centuries to get there. That is the lot of a mundane scientist.<br /> <br /> (On the bright side, she may realize once again that reality can be more creative than human imagination and that there are unexpected, unexplored possibilities in this type of world too.<br /> Maybe she'll even end up preferring things being like this to what humans (her included) can dream up for themselves.)<br /> <br /> IF SHE CAN ACCEPT ALL THAT, then she may be able to make a recovery.<br /> If she is still trying to make Wonders turn real though, still chasing dreams, then actual recovery can't even begin yet.<br /> <br /> What a Genius who wants to be a real researcher has to do is this:<br /> <br /> First, she has to try to become a non-Genius. At least temporarily. To overcome a madness that clouds her eyes and think critically once more.<br /> The obvious problem is that any laws that a Genius can dream up BECOME real. It's not so easy to find criteria by which one can separate fact from fantasy.<br /> Of course, many of them ARE real too. Many Genii have a good theory which has ONE critical flaw. Sometimes it is a real flaw - the numbers don't add up, the logical process followed misses some required step. And sometimes the flaw is simply not being backed up by evidence.<br /> But the Genius can convince herself quite easily that thing ARE being backed up by evidence. How will she know it's not? People have accepted various scientific theories for centuries because they mostly fit and anything that didn't was not confirmed to be (un)true.<br /> But even if the Genius did try to confirm everything: Mania conspires to pull the wool over her eyes.<br /> Whole BARDOS spring up to seemingly support one theory or another.<br /> <br /> So here's what I think a Genius could do.<br /> <br /> 1. force herself to become aware of the flaws in her own theory.<br /> <br /> It's really a self-seeking process.<br /> Do any results seem to come to her too fast, too easily? Those MAY well be a product of her madness. (A bigger problem is if they aren't, yet the Genius still can't trust them. See how this is not easy?)<br /> <br /> What happened during her Catalysation? When she thought she discovered something, it probably FELT real. Like she stumbled upon actual <br /> Yes, there probably all sorts of small bits that did NOT fit but she could not see them.<br /> Was there any time when she was going too fast, was too obsessed to pay attention?<br /> Is there anything that would have seemed surprising or unbelievable, before she became a Genius?<br /> <br /> The more successful she is at finding the tangly bits in her own theories, the better chances she has.<br /> <br /> 2. seek therapy<br /> <br /> Madness is often routed in some sort of trauma for the Genius, often related to her Catalyst.<br /> If she realizes what ulterior desires keep her in the madness place and solve them, that could &quot;cure&quot; her too.<br /> It may actually be more sensible to take this approach.<br /> <br /> Many Geniuses have the desire to prove themselves feel wronged by their peers and society, and so on.<br /> So this COULD be where Inspiration comes from, too.<br /> <br /> 3. surgery<br /> Well, not neccessarily real surgery. The idea here is that you identify the physical or mystical source of Inspiration and remove it by force.<br /> Of course, one problem is, nobody's really sure what the source of Inspiration IS.<br /> One option is to simply destroy random parts of oneself one by one until one is no longer a Genius..<br /> Another option is to try this on somebody else first. Number 3 is definitely the preferred option of many mad scientists. Genii who study Inspiration are dangerous and feared for this reason - they need OTHER Genii to be their test subjects.)<br /> <br /> IF the Genius completed the process (and nobody says any of these even really work), then he/she has to deal with the after-effects.<br /> Like an addiction, Inspiration tends to leave behind a void.<br /> <br /> Some Genii relapse or become Beholden, no longer able to believe in their own ideas but desiring the comforting feeling of there being a higher meaning, or organizedness, or a sense of morality, to nature. They need that certainty with which somebody declares the laws of nature to be so, and the only one they can get this from is another Genius.<br /> <br /> A rare unlucky few turn Clockstopper, or a similar creature. Having lost faith in ALL science, Inspiration takes a 180 turn and what previously warped the world to contain MORE science now forces it to hold LESS science, STILL proving the former Genius right.<br /> <br /> All of this is they make it in the first place. But here is a better question:<br /> If somebody believed in REAL science and was content with it this much, how did they become an Inspired in the first place?<br /> <br /> Every Genius transgresses at some point, venturing into the unknown driven by...something. They all sacrifice something, physically or inside themselves.<br /> Faust sold his soul to the devil. Frankenstein stole corpses. Pretorius was excommunicated by his peers.<br /> Inspiration is really a sort of madness. Not something you get out of the blue and definitely not something you get against your will.<br /> If that spark is not lit, if the Genius can not put his knowledge and work before what other humans hold dear in order of importance, then he will not Catalyze.<br /> Every genius once throws away conventions - including scientific conventions - in exchange for the secrets of the universe.<br /> <br /> I don't think it's impossible to try to go back on this choice - a Genius' path is fraught with disappointment and dissatisfaction.<br /> <br /> (Though this also has to do with their unsatiable hunger - a Genius may not neccessarily think his condition is WRONG or not better than the mundane method, they just still don't feel like it's ENOUGH.)<br /> <br /> But if you go by how mad scientists normally operate, would they drop a tear for their colleagues or the public, for the cowards who were too WEAK to see the truth?<br /> No way! You, alone, a human superior than the rest of humankind, can truly understand its meaning, truly appreciate its beauty.<br /> Without madness there is no &quot;mad&quot; science. If you are a scientist, but you're not mad. If you're not mad, how could you ever catalyze?<br /> <br /> ------------<br /> Now you don't have to actually answer any of that, your character, your game, your story.<br /> But I THINK I'd probably ask if I was GMing, how did this character become a Genius and what caused him to turn his back on it?<br /> Just to round out the character a bit. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> -----------<br /> <br /> If you want to do something for the world:<br /> onders may not be able to help scientific progress, but they can still do a lot of good. If you can cure a man's cancer with a pill, who cares that the pill was a one-of-a-kind? If you crush an evildoer with a giant robot, even if the robot will only exist as long as the Genius does, they are still crushed.<br /> <br /> Plus, the Inspired are a world to themselves. What they can do as a tiny society and how you can help that tiny society are also noble goals.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2330-vree","name":"Vree","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T19:44:47-07:00","id":864675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-ge