preciate its beauty.<br /> Without madness there is no &quot;mad&quot; science. If you are a scientist, but you're not mad. If you're not mad, how could you ever catalyze?<br /> <br /> ------------<br /> Now you don't have to actually answer any of that, your character, your game, your story.<br /> But I THINK I'd probably ask if I was GMing, how did this character become a Genius and what caused him to turn his back on it?<br /> Just to round out the character a bit. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> -----------<br /> <br /> If you want to do something for the world:<br /> onders may not be able to help scientific progress, but they can still do a lot of good. If you can cure a man's cancer with a pill, who cares that the pill was a one-of-a-kind? If you crush an evildoer with a giant robot, even if the robot will only exist as long as the Genius does, they are still crushed.<br /> <br /> Plus, the Inspired are a world to themselves. What they can do as a tiny society and how you can help that tiny society are also noble goals.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You make excellent points and your arguments are fantastic, if &quot;healing&quot; the genius were my objective which is not.<br /> I don't know why people read my comments that way, because it's not my intention.<br /> For me, the ultimate &quot;victory&quot; for my genius is to act as a bridge between the world of pure raw inspiration and the mundane world. To be the light that inspires humanity to ever greater achievements. To give people the courage to try and make the impossible possible, because even if they fail they will obtain valuable experience and knowledge.<br /> When the genius tries to fix all the worlds ploblems by himself he's falling in the trap of pride. No person can fix the world alone, we're all in this toguether. Forcing the world to work according to your vision only makes things worst, because your vision is not perfect. It's as flawed as the rest of us, even if it's more wide and ambituous.<br /> The process that I described is for the genius to learn humility, compassion, and that all their fantastic inventions and creations are worthless if they cannot share them with humanity. Because at the end of the day knowldege is meant to help all of us to move forward. Going through the process of mundane research helps the genius understand the difficulties and efforts of real research, and with that appreciate the victories of mundane scientists.<br /> Making a mundane version of a wonder creates a watered down device that has only a tenth of the power and convenience of the original wonder, but it can be replicated and understood by the rest of the scientific community. Maybe you're not capable of offering everyone your awesome vita ray device that can heal all wounds, but you just created an electromagnetic scanner than can improve the diagnostics of certain illnesses.<br /> That discovery will help countless sick people, and will open new lines of research. You haven't saved the world, but you have given people the means to imporve the world, even if it's only a little bit. That in my book is a victory.<br /> The Genius commits a trangression when he dares to go into the world of unlimited possibilities that is inspiration, but he does it to bring back some of that fire to our dark world, because even if the fire dies and only a small spark remains, it will ignite a fire inside the hearts of men that will lighten our world. A genius risks his life, his sanity, and his happiness for this, and I say that is a transgression worth makin. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2964,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","user":"Firanai","date":". 08-18-2016, 12:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T04:05:47-07:00","id":864811,"title":"","content":"I'd clarify/append that such &quot;Mundane research&quot; require non-Genius, non-Beholden fellow researchers (extended teamwork roll?), thematically to represent community and the group effort of real science, and mechanically to add some risk (affecting others or them laughing at your madness). Plus, while Genii are capable of great deductive leaps, you need some sane mind to spot the crazy elements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T17:08:13-07:00","id":869761,"title":"","content":"I agree that Epikrato has too many functions, but I'm not sure how to fix that. My first idea is to divide it into two Axioms: one for controlling physics, and the other for controlling minds. Nine Axioms sounds a little weird, though. Also, the Neid would have to pick one between these sub-Epikrato, while the other Catalysts wouldn't have to make such a choice. That's very asymmetrical.<br /> <br /> What if affecting minds was an inherent advantage of the Genius template, like using Mania to affect mundane technology? You would probably need to spend Mania for it, and the results would not be easily predictable or repeatable, as is normally the case with mad science. And I'm talking about more than turning people into Beholden.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T18:45:44-07:00","id":869800,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the Axiom of Control is pretty broad, but I'm not sure what else can be done with it either. I don't think I'd restrict it (or another Axiom) to just minds, though. That makes it too much like the Mind Arcana and Axioms are effect-based as opposed to mechanism-based (as opposite as that sounds).<br /> <br /> Revisiting an old idea, but what about restructuring Axioms to be more like W:tF 2E Shadow Gifts, in that there is a Core, and a number of Facets. If kept at Rank 1-5 for the Axiom itself, each level would have different Facets (or equivalent term) that could be purchased separately (with the first one being free with the dot) representing the various effects. In this model, Epikrato would have more Facets, but you'd still have to buy them all to do everything (rather than get the effects for free).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T19:26:23-07:00","id":869821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=869800#post869800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the Axiom of Control is pretty broad, but I'm not sure what else can be done with it either. I don't think I'd restrict it (or another Axiom) to just minds, though. That makes it too much like the Mind Arcana and Axioms are effect-based as opposed to mechanism-based (as opposite as that sounds).<br /> <br /> Revisiting an old idea, but what about restructuring Axioms to be more like W:tF 2E Shadow Gifts, in that there is a Core, and a number of Facets. If kept at Rank 1-5 for the Axiom itself, each level would have different Facets (or equivalent term) that could be purchased separately (with the first one being free with the dot) representing the various effects. In this model, Epikrato would have more Facets, but you'd still have to buy them all to do everything (rather than get the effects for free).</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm not sure what that would look like, but I'll read my W:tF 2ED more closely to see if I can come up with some examples, however sparse.<br /> <br /> That being said, your suggestion does solve the issue of powers that must be bought sequentially. In this version, a Neid can focus on probability control without having to buy telekinesis and mind control first. That's already a huge improvement.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T20:05:41-07:00","id":869843,"title":"","content":"Honestly, if I were feeling like fixing things, it might be more effective (albeit also more extreme) to throw out the current Axiomata and replace them with ones based on scientific disciplines. This would make them behave a little more like Mage Arcana, but it would mean that you would be able to build the Wonders you need without needing to invest in half the Axiomata.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T20:40:32-07:00","id":869878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=869843#post869843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, if I were feeling like fixing things, it might be more effective (albeit also more extreme) to throw out the current Axiomata and replace them with ones based on scientific disciplines. This would make them behave a little more like Mage Arcana, but it would mean that you would be able to build the Wonders you need without needing to invest in half the Axiomata.</div> </div> </div> </div> Isn't the weirdness of Axioms when compared to normal science pretty much on purpose? You do have a point about the need to invest in a lot of them to be an effective Genius, though.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T09:57:04-07:00","id":883865,"title":"","content":"The Wisdom of Mages in 2ED is more about carefulness and subtlety than ethics, right? Obligation could go the other way and be more about pro-activity and adaptability on-the-fly.<br /> <br /> A Genius with high Obligation would have a stronger filter and leash for their Inspiration. That is, they would keep from theatrical displays of frustration and gadgeteering for the heck of it. Besides the advantages like the Science Hero Merit, they could have bonuses for Unmada and Havoc checks (using Prostasia to protect against Havoc felt like cheating to me). Above all, they would not give up on their dreams, be they wonderful or horrifying, and they would freaking <u><i>learn</i></u> from their failures.<br /> <br /> A Genius with low Obligation is capricious in how they use their gifts, going from project to project without a coherent vision and leaving half-finished devices behind that can cause a lot of harm. They are obsessive to the point of not thinking straight, often using the same basic approach to problems and expecting different results because &quot;it's my way or the highway&quot;. They are not well adjusted, not even by mad scientist standards, and fail to grasp what the Peerage was named after: peer review. <br /> <br /> I admit that this will need better phrasing to not end up too similar to Wisdom in actual gameplay regardless. What does everyone else think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T10:43:28-07:00","id":883893,"title":"","content":"DR; If there is going to be any Genius 2.0 I would suggest a bit extra on the interaction between things Fae and Maniacal (Changelings and Genii respectively). When I first read Genius, I noticed that there is almost a synergy between the two splats what with the whole thematic undercurrent of Madness, both Beautiful and Wondrous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7106-extant-reality","name":"Extant Reality","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7106_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T11:14:56-07:00","id":883913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=883865#post883865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Wisdom of Mages in 2ED is more about carefulness and subtlety than ethics, right? Obligation could go the other way and be more about pro-activity and adaptability on-the-fly.<br /> <br /> A Genius with high Obligation would have a stronger filter and leash for their Inspiration. That is, they would keep from theatrical displays of frustration and gadgeteering for the heck of it. Besides the advantages like the Science Hero Merit, they could have bonuses for Unmada and Havoc checks (using Prostasia to protect against Havoc felt like cheating to me). Above all, they would not give up on their dreams, be they wonderful or horrifying, and they would freaking <u><i>learn</i></u> from their failures.<br /> <br /> A Genius with low Obligation is capricious in how they use their gifts, going from project to project without a coherent vision and leaving half-finished devices behind that can cause a lot of harm. They are obsessive to the point of not thinking straight, often using the same basic approach to problems and expecting different results because &quot;it's my way or the highway&quot;. They are not well adjusted, not even by mad scientist standards, and fail to grasp what the Peerage was named after: peer review.<br /> <br /> I admit that this will need better phrasing to not end up too similar to Wisdom in actual gameplay regardless. What does everyone else think?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds fair. Genii definately need to subvert the Mad-Scientist cliche at higher Obligation, why embracing it at lower levels, I feel. Maybe a higher end Obligation also might let a Genus shake off the Unmada (Condition?)?<br /> <br /> Tying Havoc to Obligation has some merit too - low Obligation Genii likely don't care who gets harmed by their experiments, and may be a little sloppier with their work, in contrast to high Obligation Inspired, who probably double check their calculations and look for leaks.<br /> <br /> Might also synergize well with the Illuminated - they don't even <i>have</i> Obligation anymore, which has the side effect of meaning they wouldn't be affected by low Obligation penalties to Havoc rolls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T11:33:20-07:00","id":883931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=883913#post883913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sounds fair. Genii definately need to subvert the Mad-Scientist cliche at higher Obligation, why embracing it at lower levels, I feel. Maybe a higher end Obligation also might let a Genus shake off the Unmada (Condition?)?<br /> <br /> Tying Havoc to Obligation has some merit too - low Obligation Genii likely don't care who gets harmed by their experiments, and may be a little sloppier with their work, in contrast to high Obligation Inspired, who probably double check their calculations and look for leaks.<br /> <br /> Might also synergize well with the Illuminated - they don't even <i>have</i> Obligation anymore, which has the side effect of meaning they wouldn't be affected by low Obligation penalties to Havoc rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div> Exactly. Good catch about the Illuminated.<br /> <br /> I'd like to add that there could be Merits that work better for low Obligation Geniuses. For example:<br /> <br /> 1) Weaponizing Jabir to disrupt mundane research that you don't approve.<br /> <br /> 2) Directed &quot;blasts&quot; of an Unmada Field in the form of an Environmental Tilt that induces Havoc in stable Wonders and Manes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T12:03:26-07:00","id":883951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=883931#post883931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Exactly. Good catch about the Illuminated.<br /> <br /> I'd like to add that there could be Merits that work better for low Obligation Geniuses. For example:<br /> <br /> 1) Weaponizing Jabir to disrupt mundane research that you don't approve.<br /> <br /> 2) Directed &quot;blasts&quot; of an Unmada Field in the form of an Environmental Tilt that induces Havoc in stable Wonders and Manes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe. I'd need more codified rules surrounding Wonders and such, before I could comment more. I'm skeptical about self-directed use of the Unmada field, though - it seems like a byproduct of the madness, and as such, would be &quot;hidden&quot; from the source. Unmada are crazy, but don't think they are crazy. If they know they have an Unmada field, then they'd know they are crazy. Right?<br /> <hr /><br /> Mechanically, how about a few Conditions surrounding the Inspired?<br /> <br /> <u><b>Unmada</b></u> (Persistent)<br /> There is insane, and then there is the truly <i>mad</i> - those who not only don't see reality as others do, but are <i>certain</i> that <i>their</i> perceptions are the only correct ones. Unmada are Inspired whose mad certainty has broken the bounds of their mere thoughts and theories and reach out to bend their surroundings towards their mad vision. [Add Unmada mechanics, such as Mania loss, Unmada field, etc.]<br /> <b>Possible Sources</b>: Dramatically Failing a Transgression check. Resolving an Aspiration in a manner conductive with their [Vice]. Failing an Unmada check (such as after performing Deep Inspiration).<br /> <b>Beat</b>: Whenever your madness impairs your Aspirations.<br /> <b>Resolution</b>: Dramatically Failing a Transgression check (in which case the Genius becomes Illuminated). Being confronted with their failures and accepting they are at fault. Exceptional Success on a Transgression check.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Temporary Sanity</b></u><br /> Sometimes even the mad get a breath of clarity, however fleeting. During these times, a Genius feels the manic drive of their Inspiration, if not disappear, at least fade. The Inspired find their thoughts more ordered, less clouded by Mania, and themselves able to engage in rational scientific research once more. [Add actual mechanical impact here] This Condition fades after one day per dot of Obligation. If it fades, it does not grant a Beat.<br /> <b>Possible Sources</b>: Exceptional Success on a Transgression check. Resolving an Aspiration in a manner conductive with their [Virtue].<br /> <b>Resolution</b>: Making a Transgression check (regardless of success or failure).<br /> <br /> <u><b>Beholden</b></u> (Persistent)<br /> There are those who lead, and those who follow - and you are firmly in column B. Your mind has brushed up against the light of Inspiration and had your own will burned by its source. Those who've become Beholden substitute their worldview (and one of their Aspirations) for those of the Genius they serve. Their Integrity is treated as the Genius's Obligation (mad Genii tend toward mad followers, while more restrained Inspired cultivate the same in their assistants). The Genius they serve is treated as having a Perfect Impression for Social interaction - even if circumstances would lower this impression, it returns to Perfect the next day. Beholden no longer provoke Havoc when interacting with Wonders from the Genius they serve, and have a +5 bonus to avoid causing Havoc with any other Wonder.<br /> <b>Possible Sources</b>: Dramatic Failure on a Breaking Point when exposed to Wonders or other Mad Science.<br /> <b>Beat</b>: When suffering serious harm or setback in pursuit of their Genius's goals.<br /> <b>Resolution</b>: Undergoing their own Breakthrough (in which case, they Catalyze as a Genuis). Losing their Genius, be it through death, abandonment, or personality conflict (in which case, trade this Condition for Broken and [Aimless]). Spend 10 points of consecutive Willpower toward your own Aspirations, and none of the Genius's (in which case, they resolve this Condition and regain their previous Integrity).<br /> <br /> <u><b>[Aimless]</b></u> (Persistent)<br /> It is a terrible thing to be without purpose. Bereft of a Genius to serve and emulate, and no way of choosing a path for themselves, a former Beholden succumbs to despair and listlessness. The character suffer a -2 penalty to all social rolls and cannot gain Willpower. They are also treated as if they had Integrity 0, as their minds offer little resistance to trauma.<br /> <b>Possible Sources</b>: Being Beholden and losing their Genius. Having one's mind broken by Epikrato.<br /> <b>Beat</b>: Whenever you would gain Willpower, except through sleeping.<br /> <b>Resolution</b>: Find a Genius to serve (replace this Condition with Beholden, tied to that Genius). Complete a Long Term Aspiration (in which case, they resolve this Condition and regain their previous Integrity).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T12:18:29-07:00","id":883968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=869843#post869843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, if I were feeling like fixing things, it might be more effective (albeit also more extreme) to throw out the current Axiomata and replace them with ones based on scientific disciplines. This would make them behave a little more like Mage Arcana, but it would mean that you would be able to build the Wonders you need without needing to invest in half the Axiomata.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=869878#post869878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Isn't the weirdness of Axioms when compared to normal science pretty much on purpose? You do have a point about the need to invest in a lot of them to be an effective Genius, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I think that's not a bug, but a <u>feature</u>.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, it slows you down from getting the 5th dot in the Axioms - and those were <i>crazy powerful</i>. Now, a Genius can either shoot for fantastic, but narrow, power, or diversify, but take longer to reach the heights.<br /> <br /> Narratively, encouraging diversification is also truer to the source material. These are Mad Scientists we are talking about. There is a reason <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/OmnidisciplinaryScientist\" target=\"_blank\">Omnidisciplinary Scientist</a> is a trope, after all.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T13:35:51-07:00","id":884031,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a>: You have a point about Unmada-ness being an instinctive thing. And to be honest, the Unmada Field is dangerous enough as it is. If these madmen want to do some Editing, they can just use Katastrofi and Beholden.<br /> <br /> I would allow Beholden to use Wonders if they received Mania from a Genius, Mane or some other source. I'd say that they can store up to their [Intelligence + Resolve] in Mania, like unInspired Manes. However, I would not make the Beholden's Integrity = Genius' Obligation idea a hard rule, just a tendency. A well-intentioned Genius can have a lackey with a hidden agenda if the latter has a strong enough will, and an evil Genius can have a good-natured but conflicted and/or blackmailed assistant.<br /> <br /> I think giving Beholden without masters both the Broken and Aimless Conditions is way too much. Instead, I'd only give them Aimless, but written like this:<br /> <br /> <u><b>[Aimless]</b></u> (Persistent)<br /> <br /> It is a terrible thing to be without purpose. Bereft of a Genius to serve and emulate, a former Beholden has immense difficulty leading their own lives. The character only gains 1 willpower point from acting out Virtues and Vices, as nothing is quite as fulfilling as following a Genius to them (but the limits on how often they can act out these traits still apply). Spending Willpower points only gives +2 to normal rolls and +1 when applying a Resistance trait as a penalty, and they can only spend 1 willpower point per scene. Halve their Willpower dots, round down, but do not change their Resolve or Composure. Their Integrity is capped at [highest between Resolve or Composure + 1], as their minds offer less resistance to trauma.<br /> <br /> <b>Possible Sources</b>: Being Beholden and losing their Genius. Having one's mind broken by Epikrato.<br /> <b>Beat</b>: Whenever you face considerable risks and difficulties in the pursuit of a Long Term Aspiration<br /> <b>Resolution</b>: Find a Genius to serve (replace this Condition with Beholden, tied to that Genius). Complete a Long Term Aspiration (in which case, they resolve this Condition and regain their previous Integrity).<br /> <br /> EDIT: I like Temporary Sanity too. It gives something for Geniuses to strive for if they still feel like interacting with mortal scientists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 05-06-2016, 04:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T14:00:41-07:00","id":884050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=884031#post884031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would allow Beholden to use Wonders if they received Mania from a Genius, Mane or some other source. I'd say that they can store up to their [Intelligence + Resolve] in Mania, like unInspired Manes.</div> </div> </div> </div>&lt;shrug&gt; It depends upon how Wonders will work. If they can be &quot;charged&quot; with Mania, or don't require Mania to operate, this isn't as needed. Though I could see a Merit that give a Mania Store, certainly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=884031#post884031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, I would not make the Beholden's Integrity = Genius' Obligation idea a hard rule, just a tendency. A well-intentioned Genius can have a lackey with a hidden agenda if the latter has a strong enough will, and an evil Genius can have a good-natured but conflicted and/or blackmailed assistant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Integrity doesn't map to morals or ethics anymore - you can be good-natured but low Integrity, or a scumbag but high Integrity. This was more to 1) Tie the Beholden intrinsically to their Genius 2) Serve to &quot;freeze&quot; Integrity vs effects. 1 means a high Obligation Genius's Beholden are more effective and resistant on their own, while a low Obligation Genius needs to &quot;augment&quot; their Beholden to reach the same levels in those categories. 2 essential immunizes Beholden to Breaking Points (though not their Genius boss from Transgressions, depending) as well as Soul Loss (which makes &quot;becoming Beholden&quot; beneficial, kinda, in certain rare cases) and any other Integrity manipulating effect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=884031#post884031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think giving Beholden without masters both the Broken and Aimless Conditions is way too much. Instead, I'd only give them Aimless, but written like this:<br /> <br /> <u><b>[Aimless]</b></u> (Persistent)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Broken was due to the old Fluff about how, well, broken &quot;unemployed&quot; Beholden are/were. Aimless can easily factor some of those features, though. The idea behind &quot;can't gain Willpower&quot; was to represent the downward spiral without <i>completely</i> screwing the ex-Beholden. Since they aren't <i>losing</i> Willpower, they can technically exist in that funk indefinitely (a gain over 1E's &quot;starve to death if left too long&quot; fate).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=884031#post884031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: I like Temporary Sanity too. It gives something for Geniuses to strive for if they still feel like interacting with mortal scientists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. Any ideas on mechanical effects? Eliminates Jabir penalty, maybe?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T14:07:20-07:00","id":884056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=884050#post884050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks. Any ideas on mechanical effects? Eliminates Jabir penalty, maybe?</div> </div> </div> </div><b><u>Momentarily Sane</u></b><br /> You have managed to put your...peculiarities out of view for a while. While you're alright for now, stress could easily snap you back into your usual state.<br /> <b>Effect:</b> Your Jabir penalties are reduced by 3, and any penalties from Persistent Mental conditions are likewise reduced by 3.<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> You lose this Condition if you are placed in a situation that causes you to suffer a Breaking Point or perform an action involving increased mental strain (e.g. Kitbashing, spending Willpower).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T14:12:36-07:00","id":884062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=884056#post884056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><u>Momentarily Sane</u></b><br /> You have managed to put your...peculiarities out of view for a while. While you're alright for now, stress could easily snap you back into your usual state.<br /> <b>Effect:</b> Your Jabir penalties are reduced by 3, and any penalties from Persistent Mental conditions are likewise reduced by 3.<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> You lose this Condition if you are placed in a situation that causes you to suffer a Breaking Point or perform an action involving increased mental strain (e.g. Kitbashing, spending Willpower).</div> </div> </div> </div>Even generic expenditure of Willpower? Seems kinda harsh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T14:21:02-07:00","id":884071,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a>: Ah, right. I was accidentally describing Morality for a second there. You are very right, and I missed those implicit plot hooks you mentioned. Being the Beholden of an Unmada is suffering, I bet.<br /> <br /> I changed the Aimless Condition so the Beholden has a lot of incentive to Resolve it, but can still function in a basic way. Willpower expenditure is very important in 2ED, even more so than 1ED.<br /> <br /> For Temporary Sanity, I would reduce the Genius' Inspiration for the purposes of determining their Jabir (not sure about the quantity). If they have Science Hero or something like that, they can take that reduced Jabir and turn it into a bonus for all Mental and Social rolls meant for Teamwork and co-operation in general. They worked hard for that Condition, which only lasts for about a week anyway. Let them have a boost. <br /> <br /> EDIT: Ninja'd by Malonkey1. I agree that ending the Condition with any Willpower expenditure at all seems harsh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 05-06-2016, 05:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T14:48:14-07:00","id":884092,"title":"","content":"One issue I just thought of with the Beholden Condition and its tie to a Genius - what happens if they &quot;imprint&quot; upon an Illuminated (other than <i><u>bad things</u></i>)? As stated, Illuminated have &quot;transcended&quot; mere Obligation and morality. Not sure if that should be their Beholden become equally inhuman monsters (mentally) or what, due to the effective &quot;lack&quot; of Integrity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T15:04:31-07:00","id":884102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=884092#post884092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One issue I just thought of with the Beholden Condition and its tie to a Genius - what happens if they &quot;imprint&quot; upon an Illuminated (other than <i><u>bad things</u></i>)? As stated, Illuminated have &quot;transcended&quot; mere Obligation and morality. Not sure if that should be their Beholden become equally inhuman monsters (mentally) or what, due to the effective &quot;lack&quot; of Integrity.</div> </div> </div> </div> Depends on the Illuminated. I think it would be more insidious if the Beholden of a human-shaped Illuminated worked like the Beholden of a Genius with unremarkable Obligation, maybe even a high one.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T05:10:59-07:00","id":885300,"title":"","content":"Some thoughts on Wonders and Costs:<ul><li>Requires Bound Mania: Old system.<ul><li>Pros:<ul><li>Already built out.</li> <li>Makes the Wonders tied to the Genius who created it. It is <i>theirs</i>.</li> <li>Creates cost/value decisions - More Wonders, but less fluid Mania, or fewer Wonders, but more Mania to work with.</li> </ul></li> <li>Cons:<ul><li>Dramatically limits the number of Wonders a Genius can possess.</li> <li>Restricts Mania economy.</li> <li>Makes Wonders either owned or Orphaned, no in between.</li> </ul></li> <li>Hacks:<ul><li>Inspiration or Axioms can grant &quot;freebies&quot; on the Bound Mania costs - going over your &quot;allotment&quot; still requires Bound Mania, but this allows for more Wonders per Genius.</li> <li>Standby or Hibernation mode - Mania is only bound to Wonders that are actively being used, with the rest just &quot;resting&quot; in storage or on a shelf somewhere. Bound Wonders are the Genius's, but anyone else can pickup and Bind a Wonder just sitting around.</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> <li>Requires XP: Proposed system<ul><li>Pros:<ul><li>Maps to newer &quot;Magic item&quot; creation a bit better (though removing the middle-man of Willpower Dots and converting it to straight XP).</li> <li>Opens up theoretically more Wonders in play.</li> <li><i>May</i> allow for more nuanced costing structures.</li> <li>Opens up Mania for active abilities.</li> </ul></li> <li>Cons<ul><li>New system - needs to be designed and balanced.</li> <li>Makes Wonders a bit less tied to the Genius that created them.</li> <li>XP Sink - Geniuses would find more XP going towards individual Wonders, rather than self-improvement.</li> <li>XP Economy confusion - Is the XP refunded if the Genius looses a Wonder? Under what conditions? If the Genius wishes to cannibalize a Wonder - can <i>that</i> XP be spent on non-Wonders? Does this restrict Wonder creation to XP-level?</li> </ul></li> <li>Hacks:<ul><li>Wondrous XP - Separate XP track solely used for Wonder creation. Normal XP can be spent in addition (optional?), but this offers a separate mechanism for the Wonder creation economy.</li> <li>Hybrid - Mania binding might still exist, giving either bonuses, or reducing/obviating the XP costs for those Genii without the XP to spare at the moment.</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> <li>Requires Minimum Resources Merit: Old System<ul><li>Pros:<ul><li>Already built out.</li> <li>Restricts the heights and extremes of mad science - all those toys have to come from <i>somewhere</i>.</li> <li>Adds story hooks - Why would a Genius rob a bank? Because funding is <i>hard</i>.</li> </ul></li> <li>Cons:<ul><li>Restricts upper Wonder creation to the Wealthy.</li> <li>Adds a hidden &quot;requirement&quot; stat to Wonder creation.</li> <li>Budgets suck up enjoyment for those not interested in accounting (in which case, it might be moved to Pros?).</li> </ul></li> <li>Hacks:<ul><li>Make it a Roll - Having enough Resources for your Wonder is nearly assured to work, but those short on funds and material can always cut corners and use sub-standard parts. Failure might lead to simple Wonder creation failure, or add more Faults, but there is always the chance the impoverished Genius can succeed. Having <i>more</i> money than necessary might allow for bonuses or Fault reduction, even (so billionaire Genii can still rub it in their peers' faces).</li> <li>Allow for substitute Merits - though subject to justification and ST permission, allow for Merits like Allies, or Fame, or even Barfly and Striking Looks to substitute for Resource dots. You'd be trading on said Merits rather than directly funding the creation yourself.</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> </ul><b>Sidebar: But Where's The Science?</b><br /> Much has been stated how Genius operates more as Mad Engineering (with the focus on Wonder creation) rather than any actual science. Some potential solutions to that could be:<ul><li>Wondrous/Inspired XP: Conducting insane research, uncovering enigmas in the world, and reverse engineering Wonders might give special XP, encouraging actual research.</li> <li>Wondrous Plans - The new Equipment creation system allows for Plans now - and who would be better at making crazy, yet astonishingly successful Plans that the Inspired? The more they know (about <i>anything</i>, really, considering their inherent cross-specialization), the better and more durable their Plans are.</li> <li>Wondrous Facts/Knowledge - Uncover something previous unknown to the Genius? Get a Fact. These could be used in Plan creation, cashed in for Beats, be used to &quot;pay&quot; for Wonder costs (XP or Bound Mania), or some new thing analogous to Clues in the Investigation System.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 05-09-2016, 08:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T05:20:44-07:00","id":885304,"title":"","content":"&lt;grumble&gt; Stupid Forum ate my post.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Looks like it didn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":".  ...The Forum didn't eat my post, just took longer to digest than normal. 05-08-2016, 08:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T13:40:35-07:00","id":885655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=884092#post884092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One issue I just thought of with the Beholden Condition and its tie to a Genius - what happens if they &quot;imprint&quot; upon an Illuminated (other than <i><u>bad things</u></i>)? As stated, Illuminated have &quot;transcended&quot; mere Obligation and morality. Not sure if that should be their Beholden become equally inhuman monsters (mentally) or what, due to the effective &quot;lack&quot; of Integrity.</div> </div> </div> </div>?Why do you think anything is supposed to happen? Beholden morality isn't tied to their Genius' morality in any shape or form, except as far as Dirty Jobs and other participation in questionable tasks, like building with Larvae, reduces it the normal way, IF they oblige.<br /> <br /> It's perfectly normal (mechanically speaking) to have a wicked genius with a saintly Beholden, or vica versa.<br /> <br /> Beholden and intelligent Automata DO have their own free will and may not decide to serve a master they don't like (though not just because of Obligation but due to any personal pet peeve they have with the Genius - maltreating your Beholden/Automata for example is usually universally a cause for loss of loyalty).<br /> And a Genius has the choose to not entertain a Beholden whose methods they find questionable, though they don't always get a big range of choices.<br /> (Heck, an obedient if immoral Beholden may cause less harm serving the Genius than he would otherwise, especially now that they have the condition.)<br /> <br /> There really isn't anything unusual about how this works for Illuminated.<br /> Illuminated can have Beholden the same as anyone else.<br /> Many Beholden would stick with the Master even after they start going off the deep end out of loyalty - related literature has plenty of precedents.<br /> Certainly you need to be a special kind of person to swear loyalty to an Illuminated AFTER they gained the condition, but Beholden status is a kind of addiction - the admiration for the Inspired's infinitely valuable genius mind and the need to see it in action takes priority over other matters. You can make up any reason to justify it afterwards.<br /> <br /> Beholden always have the choice to rebel and either try to deal with their condition through therapy, or go off in search of another Genius. Beholden status does not make you a slave. It IS a sort of addiction (the excitement and thrill of seeing a Genius' theories in action is uncomparable to anything else), but they can deal with their problem in other ways or get their &quot;fix&quot; elsewhere if they want to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=885300#post885300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]Requires Bound Mania: Old system.[*]Dramatically limits the number of Wonders a Genius can possess.</div> </div> </div> </div>sigh <br /> In fact the opposite is true.<br /> The primary reason of Wonder XP (should someone choose it) would be to REDUCE the number of Wonders and make them feel more &quot;special&quot;, to make the game more about the invention and less about the inventor effectively.<br /> (Again, a matter of taste - yes a lot of scifi movies are about ONE invention (Back to the Future, Frankenstein etc. etc.) but steampunk or inventor-type characters (Agatha Heterodyne, Gyro Gearloose, MacGuyver etc.) have no problem churning out new inventions at a moment's notice as they need them, either.)<br /> <br /> I think you may have been mislead by the fact that there is a limit on Wonders due to bound Mania.<br /> <br /> What you should consider instead is how easy it is to &quot;rotate&quot; them.<br /> <br /> The majority of Wonders can be built in a few hours or days, and if you only need them for a scene, there's always Kitbashing.<br /> The number of Wonders you can build is quite generous even with the lowest starting number (max Mania 10) and scales up pretty well with more Inspiration.<br /> There really isn't much reason for you to carry more than 4-5 Wonders at any given time.<br /> (And if speed is your goal, you can always further improve it if you join the Y-splat that specializes in it (Artificers).)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2330-vree","name":"Vree","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T21:47:59-07:00","id":885958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=884071#post884071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a>:I agree that ending the Condition with any Willpower expenditure at all seems harsh.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? The condition is called &quot;Momentarily Sane&quot; not &quot;Permanently Sane,&quot; it should be something you can lose in a moment. It looks like it represents getting your faculties back for just a moment, long enough to communicate some great discovery, or be taken seriously enough that people will heed your warning, before drifting back off into madness again.<br /> Think Renfield or the comic version of Lewis Prothero.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4968,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4968-mrbreaksit","user":"MrBreaksIt","date":". 05-09-2016, 12:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4968-mrbreaksit","name":"MrBreaksIt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T22:16:41-07:00","id":885964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrBreaksIt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=885958#post885958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why? The condition is called &quot;Momentarily Sane&quot; not &quot;Permanently Sane,&quot; it should be something you can lose in a moment. It looks like it represents getting your faculties back for just a moment, long enough to communicate some great discovery, or be taken seriously enough that people will heed your warning, before drifting back off into madness again.<br /> Think Renfield or the comic version of Lewis Prothero.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was the general idea, yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T23:24:32-07:00","id":885981,"title":"","content":"So, in a flash, I was blessed with a collection of jumbled, disjointed thoughts which I will attempt to push through Jabir.<br /> <br /> The first point was that the horrific tone of the game is very well represented by the songs of the Clockwork Quartet, that mad drive to accomplish tasks entirely divorced from sense but still seeming perfectly logical within the head of those attempting to accomplish them - devising a complicated contraption to kill a random bystander as an act of revenge on a former employer, turning your wife into a wasted wretch on a thousand different life support machines that only keep her alive through the fact that she's technically not dead, burning through all your money, your resources, your worldly possessions, because you need a microscope that can see just a little closer...<br /> That's the tone that fits into the Chronicles of Darkness proper, but that's not the tone that's projected by the mechanics - the mechanics project a wacky, hammy science adventure that people seem to enjoy.<br /> The question is, how do we resolve these clashing tones, and perhaps it could be done through simply changing the rules according to the tone you wish to play ala Paranoia's Zap/Classic/Straight options. More work, certainly, but the changes don't have to be terribly drastic and can, indeed, be slotted neatly into an appendix explaining the small alterations that must be made to fit a certain tone<br /> <br /> <br /> Now that that odd little rant is out of the way, I can move on to what I actually wanted to discuss here, namely that the Genius powerset is, paradoxically, both too broad and too narrow, that Mania being used to create and power Wonders is an important construct of the setting (and that removing it would make Mania useless) and that Mad Science is about more than just building cool things.<br /> All of these problems, I propose, can be solved through a single measure - we can add an additional sort of power that a Genius can possess which we can call... uh... Courses? Fountains? Alignments? Realignments?<br /> The name doesn't really matter. What matters is that these Alignments (I'll just call them that for now, it's simpler) represent the Genius tapping into Inspiration to alter his mindset to better accomplish a particular sort of task, and take the place of the more generic powers of other splats.<br /> Let's throw create and examine an incredibly crude prototype for the purpose of examining this idea.<br /> We'll say that &quot;The Workings of the Human Machine&quot; is a Wits+Inspiration roll to manifest, although other Alignments might use either Intelligence or Resolve, and sets the Genius on the path of thinking of the human body as a machine. It costs 1 Mania a turn/scene to maintain (whichever is more relevant) and, in addition to giving the &quot;Anatomy&quot; interdisciplinary specialty for the duration of its effect if the Genius does not already possess it, adds Inspiration to the dicepool of any Crafts or Medicine rolls while active, as well as any attack roll that seeks to cause a specific physical impairment (for example, a leg rack), with some sort of additional bonus on an exceptional success.<br /> There are a couple of catches, however.<br /> One is that this ability requires continued Mania expenditure to maintain, and the other is that it can't simply be turned off - the Genius must make a roll of, say, the amount of Mania spent to maintain any currently active Alignment + Inspiration, - Obligation?<br /> On an exceptional success, the Genius becomes caught in the Alignment mindset, losing a point of Obligation, gain a negative mental condition appropriate to the Alignment and cannot manifest the Alignment again until this condition is resolved.<br /> On a success, the Genius must make an Obligation check and gains a condition unique to the Alignment (for example, this one might provide a malus to empathy rolls?). They <u>can</u> attempt to manifest this Alignment again before the condition is resolved, but gain a cumulative -1 to activate and +1 to deactivate for as many times as this effect is rolled before the condition is resolved.<br /> On a failure, the Genius successfully reverts to a more stable mindframe<br /> On a dramatic failure, the Genius is refunded a portion of the mania spent and gains a +1 to activate and -1 to deactivate next time this Alignment is used.<br /> <br /> There is also the possibility of using these &quot;Alignments&quot; as prerequisites for building certain kinds of Wonder, or Wonders that provide certain effects, or at least providing bonuses to manufacturing those sort of Wonder.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: I think this might be what Inspiration feels like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4968-mrbreaksit","name":"MrBreaksIt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T06:13:54-07:00","id":886150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=885655#post885655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">?Why do you think anything is supposed to happen? Beholden morality isn't tied to their Genius' morality in any shape or form, except as far as Dirty Jobs and other participation in questionable tasks, like building with Larvae, reduces it the normal way, IF they oblige.<br /> <br /> It's perfectly normal (mechanically speaking) to have a wicked genius with a saintly Beholden, or vica versa.<br /> <br /> Beholden and intelligent Automata DO have their own free will and may not decide to serve a master they don't like (though not just because of Obligation but due to any personal pet peeve they have with the Genius - maltreating your Beholden/Automata for example is usually universally a cause for loss of loyalty).<br /> And a Genius has the choose to not entertain a Beholden whose methods they find questionable, though they don't always get a big range of choices.<br /> (Heck, an obedient if immoral Beholden may cause less harm serving the Genius than he would otherwise, especially now that they have the condition.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Mortals (and thus Beholden) don't track Morality anymore, but Integrity, which means different things. A resolution condition of dramatic personality conflict does need to be listed, but I'm not sure how to do so &quot;efficiently&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=885655#post885655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">sigh<br /> In fact the opposite is true.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except: hard cap due to Mania capacity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=885655#post885655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The primary reason of Wonder XP (should someone choose it) would be to REDUCE the number of Wonders and make them feel more &quot;special&quot;, to make the game more about the invention and less about the inventor effectively.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is one potential Pro of such XP if desired. Even using Bound Mania, Wondrous XP could be treated like Larvae.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=885655#post885655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Again, a matter of taste - yes a lot of scifi movies are about ONE invention (Back to the Future, Frankenstein etc. etc.) but steampunk or inventor-type characters (Agatha Heterodyne, Gyro Gearloose, MacGuyver etc.) have no problem churning out new inventions at a moment's notice as they need them, either.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Kitbashing pretty much serves this role.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=885655#post885655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you may have been mislead by the fact that there is a limit on Wonders due to bound Mania.</div> </div> </div> </div>There <i>is</i> a limit. I'm pointing that out.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=885655#post885655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What you should consider instead is how easy it is to &quot;rotate&quot; them.<br /> <br /> The majority of Wonders can be built in a few hours or days, and if you only need them for a scene, there's always Kitbashing.<br /> The number of Wonders you can build is quite generous even with the lowest starting number (max Mania 10) and scales up pretty well with more Inspiration.<br /> There really isn't much reason for you to carry more than 4-5 Wonders at any given time.<br /> (And if speed is your goal, you can always further improve it if you join the Y-splat that specializes in it (Artificers).)</div> </div> </div> </div>The limitation on Wonders remains: you either have it Bound or it goes Orphan. If you no longer need the Terramorphoric Traversal Pod, your options are:<br /> 1) Let it eat up you Bound Mania and serve no purpose<br /> 2) Deconstruct it for the Mania<br /> 3) Let it become an Orphan.<br /> If you need it in the future? You have to rebuild it again. That's not really rotation. (For something that eliminates this, see the Standby or Hibernation Hack option)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T06:28:28-07:00","id":886162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrBreaksIt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=885981#post885981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's throw create and examine an incredibly crude prototype for the purpose of examining this idea.<br /> We'll say that &quot;The Workings of the Human Machine&quot; is a Wits+Inspiration roll to manifest, although other Alignments might use either Intelligence or Resolve, and sets the Genius on the path of thinking of the human body as a machine. It costs 1 Mania a turn/scene to maintain (whichever is more relevant) and, in addition to giving the &quot;Anatomy&quot; interdisciplinary specialty for the duration of its effect if the Genius does not already possess it, adds Inspiration to the dicepool of any Crafts or Medicine rolls while active, as well as any attack roll that seeks to cause a specific physical impairment (for example, a leg rack), with some sort of additional bonus on an exceptional success.<br /> There are a couple of catches, however.<br /> One is that this ability requires continued Mania expenditure to maintain, and the other is that it can't simply be turned off - the Genius must make a roll of, say, the amount of Mania spent to maintain any currently active Alignment + Inspiration, - Obligation?<br /> On an exceptional success, the Genius becomes caught in the Alignment mindset, losing a point of Obligation, gain a negative mental condition appropriate to the Alignment and cannot manifest the Alignment again until this condition is resolved.<br /> On a success, the Genius must make an Obligation check and gains a condition unique to the Alignment (for example, this one might provide a malus to empathy rolls?). They <u>can</u> attempt to manifest this Alignment again before the condition is resolved, but gain a cumulative -1 to activate and +1 to deactivate for as many times as this effect is rolled before the condition is resolved.<br /> On a failure, the Genius successfully reverts to a more stable mindframe<br /> On a dramatic failure, the Genius is refunded a portion of the mania spent and gains a +1 to activate and -1 to deactivate next time this Alignment is used.<br /> <br /> There is also the possibility of using these &quot;Alignments&quot; as prerequisites for building certain kinds of Wonder, or Wonders that provide certain effects, or at least providing bonuses to manufacturing those sort of Wonder.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: I think this might be what Inspiration feels like.</div> </div> </div> </div>That... looks like merely an Integral Wonder itself. I mean, the rules already (broadly) support exactly what you listed - &quot;Build&quot; a Wonder that is Size 0, call it &quot;The Workings of the Human Machine&quot;, set the dice pool, effects, and talk to the ST about the &quot;problems turning it off&quot; Fault.<br /> <br /> Wonders are <i>extremely</i> broad - they are no more bound to the Gizmo model than Demon is to the Bio-Mechanical aesthetic.<br /> <br /> Want your super-intelligent &quot;hero&quot;/crazy using their carefully pre-plotted and analyzed knowledge of probability and human systems to change things via superior understanding/memetic manipulation/kung-fu? Make their Wonders Integral. BAM! It's not a Hypno-Ray doing it, it's Dr. Insano's Advanced Mesmerism Technique. They didn't &quot;build&quot; it, they &quot;devised&quot; it through extensive study and experimentation.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I'm sorry if my explanation seems like the cruel reductionism of &quot;the Consensus&quot; in response to truly Inspired ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T06:51:13-07:00","id":886178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=886162#post886162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That... looks like merely an Integral Wonder itself. I mean, the rules already (broadly) support exactly what you listed - &quot;Build&quot; a Wonder that is Size 0, call it &quot;The Workings of the Human Machine&quot;, set the dice pool, effects, and talk to the ST about the &quot;problems turning it off&quot; Fault.<br /> <br /> Wonders are <i>extremely</i> broad - they are no more bound to the Gizmo model than Demon is to the Bio-Mechanical aesthetic.<br /> <br /> Want your super-intelligent &quot;hero&quot;/crazy using their carefully pre-plotted and analyzed knowledge of probability and human systems to change things via superior understanding/memetic manipulation/kung-fu? Make their Wonders Integral. BAM! It's not a Hypno-Ray doing it, it's Dr. Insano's Advanced Mesmerism Technique. They didn't &quot;build&quot; it, they &quot;devised&quot; it through extensive study and experimentation.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I'm sorry if my explanation seems like the cruel reductionism of &quot;the Consensus&quot; in response to truly Inspired ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>You fools are yet to recognise the true extent of my genius! But I'll show you! I'LL SHOW THEM ALL!<br /> <br /> Really, I just came up with that because I wanted A) a power for the Inspired that wasn't directly Wonder related and B) to add a little more complexity to the Wonder creation system, increasing the amount of Wonders designed to do one specific thing rather than all the things you can get away with making do. I was also pleasantly surprised with how the idea could represent the mind-shaping aspect of the Spark when not channeled directly into Wonder making.<br /> <br /> <br /> Still, the fact that an actual Wonder could do this much more simply makes the whole thing fall flat on its face a bit, doesn't it?<br /> I still think the core idea is sound enough - that selections of powers representing a specific Inspired state of mind that can be used as Wonder prerequisites could be useful to the game - even if my execution was, admittedly, amateurish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4968,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4968-mrbreaksit","user":"MrBreaksIt","date":". 05-09-2016, 10:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4968-mrbreaksit","name":"MrBreaksIt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T09:45:34-07:00","id":886353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrBreaksIt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=886178#post886178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You fools are yet to recognise the true extent of my genius! But I'll show you! I'LL SHOW THEM ALL!<br /> <br /> Really, I just came up with that because I wanted A) a power for the Inspired that wasn't directly Wonder related and B) to add a little more complexity to the Wonder creation system, increasing the amount of Wonders designed to do one specific thing rather than all the things you can get away with making do. I was also pleasantly surprised with how the idea could represent the mind-shaping aspect of the Spark when not channeled directly into Wonder making.<br /> <br /> <br /> Still, the fact that an actual Wonder could do this much more simply makes the whole thing fall flat on its face a bit, doesn't it?<br /> I still think the core idea is sound enough - that selections of powers representing a specific Inspired state of mind that can be used as Wonder prerequisites could be useful to the game - even if my execution was, admittedly, amateurish.</div> </div> </div> </div>There, there. That's what revision and improvement are for, after all.<br /> <br /> I think there <i>does</i> need to be some incentive to narrow vs everything Wonders. What are your thoughts on the &quot;Facet&quot; (needs a better Genius-flavored term) method? Axioms are still ranked 1-5, but you no longer get access to all of their powers at once, but must &quot;buy&quot; them separately instead?<br /> <br /> As for non-Wonder things, what about leveraging the new Plan typed Equipment, or doing something with the new Investigation sub-system?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T11:39:55-07:00","id":892655,"title":"","content":"No one has any opinions on the Hacks proposed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T12:45:14-07:00","id":892714,"title":"","content":"Taking a glance at Alignments:<br /> <br /> I'd like to see Genius' powers moved <i>away</i> from &quot;make a Wonder for everything&quot; - the lack of <i>spontaneity</i> with Wonder creation kinda takes away from them in my mind.<br /> <br /> I kinda want to see Geniuses as being to investigation/crafting stuff what Werewolves are to combat or what Vampires are to social interaction.<br /> <br /> What'd be <i>hilarious</i> would be if their powers are predicated on them being <i>failures</i>. They get a big ol' penalty to building equipment and researching things, but can salvage &quot;failed&quot; experiments with a little Mania.<br /> <br /> A normal guy screws up at fixing his car's engine, gives up, and calls a mechanic.<br /> A Genius screws up at fixing his engine, keeps going, and ends up with a car that gets 80 miles to the gallon. Of blood, but <i>still</i>.<br /> <br /> And your powers get <i>stronger</i> if you dramatically failed the roll.<br /> <br /> (And a big discount if you incorporate a Lemure. Sure, a <i>normal</i> person would think twice about sticking a human heart in their fuel tank, but <i>normal</i> people aren't saving SO MUCH MONEY on gas.)<br /> <hr /><br /> Maybe (incidental thought after looking at the Beholden condition) world-view could be a <i>mechanical</i> thing?<br /> <br /> Like building new Wonders by failing rolls adds a new &quot;hook&quot; to your world-view. Making stuff that falls within your world-view is flipped (so you can make Wonders by actually <i>succeeding</i> at something), doesn't take the penalties, and all that other fun stuff...<br /> <br /> The one thing is that you need to have <i>consistency</i> in your world-view. If you, say, have figured out that machinery works better when fuelled by blood and that brass works better for wiring than copper... you'd <i>better</i> have some way to link those. You've got your Grand Unified Theory about how the world <i>really</i> works... it'd be a shame if it all turns out to be as much of a sham as the scientific consensus.<br /> <br /> One way to do this mechanically is come up with a list, a la Touchstones or the different archetype-type replacements that a few of the splats get instead of Virtue/Vice. Then you could do stuff like letting Geniuses that share Fragments (sounds like a good term) of their world-view work better together, mad-science-wise.<br /> <br /> (Joke-y idea: there's a social penalty for not sharing world-views. It's biggest when the world-view is not shared at all <i>and</i> when it is mostly (but not completely) shared.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T13:05:25-07:00","id":892723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=892714#post892714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Taking a glance at Alignments:<br /> <br /> I'd like to see Genius' powers moved <i>away</i> from &quot;make a Wonder for everything&quot; - the lack of <i>spontaneity</i> with Wonder creation kinda takes away from them in my mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kitbashing isn't enough, then?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=892714#post892714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kinda want to see Geniuses as being to investigation/crafting stuff what Werewolves are to combat or what Vampires are to social interaction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mages kind of have the lock-down on Investigation. And didn't you just say you <i>didn't</i> like the crafting focus?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=892714#post892714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What'd be <i>hilarious</i> would be if their powers are predicated on them being <i>failures</i>. They get a big ol' penalty to building equipment and researching things, but can salvage &quot;failed&quot; experiments with a little Mania.<br /> <br /> A normal guy screws up at fixing his car's engine, gives up, and calls a mechanic.<br /> A Genius screws up at fixing his engine, keeps going, and ends up with a car that gets 80 miles to the gallon. Of blood, but <i>still</i>.<br /> <br /> And your powers get <i>stronger</i> if you dramatically failed the roll.<br /> <br /> (And a big discount if you incorporate a Lemure. Sure, a <i>normal</i> person would think twice about sticking a human heart in their fuel tank, but <i>normal</i> people aren't saving SO MUCH MONEY on gas.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny, but I'm not sure how well it would work with the rules system. Generally speaking, you are trying to get <i>better</i> at things as time goes on, whereas with the &quot;Failure Model&quot;, Players would have no incentive to actually improve their characters. Also, you can take a Dramatic Failure instead of a normal Failure for a Beat.<br /> <br /> Now, you might swing &quot;accidental&quot; Wonder creation as a potential outcome of Failures/Dramatic Failures on certain rolls (Crafts, Science, Medicine, etc.). Then the Genius gets a &quot;free&quot; Wonder that is more akin to a Cursed Item than something they want (but is still useful).<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> Maybe (incidental thought after looking at the Beholden condition) world-view could be a <i>mechanical</i> thing?<br /> <br /> Like building new Wonders by failing rolls adds a new &quot;hook&quot; to your world-view. Making stuff that falls within your world-view is flipped (so you can make Wonders by actually <i>succeeding</i> at something), doesn't take the penalties, and all that other fun stuff...<br /> <br /> The one thing is that you need to have <i>consistency</i> in your world-view. If you, say, have figured out that machinery works better when fuelled by blood and that brass works better for wiring than copper... you'd <i>better</i> have some way to link those. You've got your Grand Unified Theory about how the world <i>really</i> works... it'd be a shame if it all turns out to be as much of a sham as the scientific consensus.<br /> <br /> One way to do this mechanically is come up with a list, a la Touchstones or the different archetype-type replacements that a few of the splats get instead of Virtue/Vice. Then you could do stuff like letting Geniuses that share Fragments (sounds like a good term) of their world-view work better together, mad-science-wise.<br /> <br /> (Joke-y idea: there's a social penalty for not sharing world-views. It's biggest when the world-view is not shared at all <i>and</i> when it is mostly (but not completely) shared.)[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> Worldview could certainly be codified. Obviously, <i>sane</i> scientists wouldn't share it (thus, Jabir penalty). The Unmada Condition might double the penalty (because they are <i>very</i> focused on their Worldview).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T13:46:07-07:00","id":892754,"title":"","content":"No, kitbashing isn't enough.It's not &quot;it takes too long to build Wonders&quot;, its that &quot;I can build anything <i>as long as I know how to build it</i>&quot; thing. It's too static as a thing for mad scientists for my tastes - there's a reason most games that go with the whole &quot;inventor&quot; thing just let them build whatever with maybe a theme holding stuff together, rather than going &quot;I'm sorry, you can only build rayguns because you only picked the raygun power.&quot;<br /> <br /> Yeah, Mages do investigation - no one ever said that there should never be overlap. The crafting isn't a problem - it's the &quot;all they've got is crafting&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> I mean, <i>seriously</i>. Mad geniuses <i>only</i> being able to create new gizmos and being useless outside of that is an <i>NPC</i> thing. Sure, give them a focus on building stuff, but don't make it their <i>only</i> thing.<br /> <hr /><br /> The idea I was suggesting would go something like:<br /> <br /> Fail to build something \u2192 Mania it into a Wonder \u2192 Incorporate it into your world-view \u2192 You can now do it <i>intentionally</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T14:18:29-07:00","id":892771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=892754#post892754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, kitbashing isn't enough.It's not &quot;it takes too long to build Wonders&quot;, its that &quot;I can build anything <i>as long as I know how to build it</i>&quot; thing. It's too static as a thing for mad scientists for my tastes - there's a reason most games that go with the whole &quot;inventor&quot; thing just let them build whatever with maybe a theme holding stuff together, rather than going &quot;I'm sorry, you can only build rayguns because you only picked the raygun power.&quot;<br /> <br /> Yeah, Mages do investigation - no one ever said that there should never be overlap. The crafting isn't a problem - it's the &quot;all they've got is crafting&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> I mean, <i>seriously</i>. Mad geniuses <i>only</i> being able to create new gizmos and being useless outside of that is an <i>NPC</i> thing. Sure, give them a focus on building stuff, but don't make it their <i>only</i> thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about the ability to temporarily add Axioms/&quot;Facets&quot; when Kitbashing for a cost (Mania? Willpower? Extra Fault?)? Knowing more means you don't have to take this step/risk, but you <i>can</i> if you need to. Since Wonders are more permanent, you can't just slap crap together and hope it works - you actually need to have some idea of what you are doing.<br /> <br /> What about the proposals for Inspired/Wonderous Plans (as in, the &quot;Equipment&quot; from Chronicles of Darkness Corebook)? Whipping up an overly complex, yet somehow useful plan on the spot seems like it would fit a Genius. And gives even more excuse to shout &quot;Just As I Planned&quot; during scenes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=892754#post892754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea I was suggesting would go something like:<br /> <br /> Fail to build something \u2192 Mania it into a Wonder \u2192 Incorporate it into your world-view \u2192 You can now do it <i>intentionally</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Intent is as a side benefit, not the primary Wonder creation mechanic, correct?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 05-17-2016, 05:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T14:24:03-07:00","id":892775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=892754#post892754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, <i>seriously</i>. Mad geniuses <i>only</i> being able to create new gizmos and being useless outside of that is an <i>NPC</i> thing. Sure, give them a focus on building stuff, but don't make it their <i>only</i> thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also it's more engineer than scientist. Without a knowledge-gaining angle it'd be abit weird to call them (mad) scientists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T14:36:50-07:00","id":892783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=892775#post892775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also it's more engineer than scientist. Without a knowledge-gaining angle it'd be abit weird to call them (mad) scientists.</div> </div> </div> </div>To which one could ask:<br /> <br /> An <i>how</i> are they gaining this knowledge? They can't &quot;magick&quot; the knowledge into their heads - they need tools and experimentation.<br /> <br /> Also, so you have knowledge. Great! Now what are you doing with it? Because without some way to express said knowledge, it is just notes. <hr /><br /> So... would adding something inherent to the Genius Template, that ties into Plans and/or the Clues/Investigation sub-systems help? Such as being able to generate or need fewer Clues? Because <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/BatDeduction\" target=\"_blank\">Bat Deduction</a> seems right at home here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 05-17-2016, 05:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T00:05:31-07:00","id":893090,"title":"","content":"The Clue mechanics are uniquely bad for bat deduction like powers, as the Uncovering the Truth rules provides things like plausible-deniability if you're short on clues.<br /> <br /> Given that bat deductions cannot stand up in any reasonable Court, it doesn't make sense to remove plausible deniability and you can't make it a power to use fewer Clues when that option is already there for everyone.<br /> <br /> The best solution would be to just say that Geniuses tend to Uncover the Truth early, which is why Genius related criminal investigations are full of Batmobile chases, rescuing hostages from bond-villian death traps, and the university dean complaining that there's no place in a respectable university for tenured professors having fisticuffs with captains of industry while dressed up in animal costumes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 05-18-2016, 03:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T14:03:33-07:00","id":893582,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a>: I am not 100% sure, but a Mania + Wondrous Experiences rule set sounds like the best option. Perhaps you make a Wonder permanent with the Wondrous Experiences, and as you grow in Inspiration, you can update your Wonders with Advanced Functions that require Mania to be activated. Sort of like how Mages get more free Reach for their initial spells as they increase their Arcana ratings.<br /> <br /> I don't have any ideas on how to modify Plans and Building Equipment at the moment, sorry.<br /> <br /> As a side note, how does everyone feel about the Catalysts? They are broad enough to cover most types of mad scientists, sure, and writing a Thesis as you grow in Inspiration can help you role play with more nuance if you do it right. However, I have a feeling that there aren't enough ways to approach each Catalyst.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T14:44:53-07:00","id":893625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=893090#post893090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Clue mechanics are uniquely bad for bat deduction like powers, as the Uncovering the Truth rules provides things like plausible-deniability if you're short on clues.<br /> <br /> Given that bat deductions cannot stand up in any reasonable Court, it doesn't make sense to remove plausible deniability and you can't make it a power to use fewer Clues when that option is already there for everyone.<br /> <br /> The best solution would be to just say that Geniuses tend to Uncover the Truth early, which is why Genius related criminal investigations are full of Batmobile chases, rescuing hostages from bond-villian death traps, and the university dean complaining that there's no place in a respectable university for tenured professors having fisticuffs with captains of industry while dressed up in animal costumes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, <i>why</i> can't you have something like &quot;Mania totally says that my Bat Deductions hold up in court&quot;? It's an in-genre thing for mad scientists to make <i>absolutely</i> crazy things sound reasonable, at least for a little bit.<br /> <br /> Or something where you can spend Mania to restrict what the ST can impose as a result for skipping Clues - make it safer/more tempting to do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T18:07:23-07:00","id":893760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=893625#post893625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait, <i>why</i> can't you have something like &quot;Mania totally says that my Bat Deductions hold up in court&quot;? It's an in-genre thing for mad scientists to make <i>absolutely</i> crazy things sound reasonable, at least for a little bit.<br /> <br /> Or something where you can spend Mania to restrict what the ST can impose as a result for skipping Clues - make it safer/more tempting to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>That could be an interesting mechanic, actually. I think the issue might be in preventing it from short-circuiting stories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T19:09:53-07:00","id":893788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=893760#post893760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That could be an interesting mechanic, actually. I think the issue might be in preventing it from short-circuiting stories.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hm... so what if in certain situations, the &quot;Jabir penalty&quot; works as an advantage, maybe once per story, but only things that are hopelessly insane? Maybe a specific benefit of a specific sub splat","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T20:07:01-07:00","id":893827,"title":"","content":"Say what you want about 1st ed, but a few of those subsplats were jolly interesting.<br /> I'm particularly fond of the one dedicated to seeing just how unscientific they can make Wonders before they stop working.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4968-mrbreaksit","name":"MrBreaksIt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T21:36:23-07:00","id":893850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrBreaksIt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=893827#post893827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Say what you want about 1st ed, but a few of those subsplats were jolly interesting.<br /> I'm particularly fond of the one dedicated to seeing just how unscientific they can make Wonders before they stop working.</div> </div> </div> </div>AKA Troll Science (specifically, trolling those who take mad science too seriously). &quot;LOL, this cube is firing a laser, despite having no actual light source. Suck it, plausibility!&quot;<br /> <br /> I wouldn't necessarily say Mania makes Clues acceptable in court, so much as the Mania forces/enables you to uncover &quot;real&quot; Clues, despite being next to no way to do so. As far a normals and the rules are concerned, you are getting them ex nihilo (or, &quot;pulling them out of your ass&quot;, if you prefer that phrase), but from there on, they are real Clues, handled the same way as other Clues. You aren't Uncovering the Truth early (missing data), you just got there with info to spare in record time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T00:42:16-07:00","id":893886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=893625#post893625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait, <i>why</i> can't you have something like &quot;Mania totally says that my Bat Deductions hold up in court&quot;? It's an in-genre thing for mad scientists to make <i>absolutely</i> crazy things sound reasonable, at least for a little bit.</div> </div> </div> </div> It's not so much in-genre so much as it's a per story difference. The Ghostbusters got arrested, and they weren't even insane.<br /> <br /> Jabir implies that this particular mad science story is one where they can't sound reasonable.<br /> <br /> <br /> Though I did have a better idea. Spend a point of Mania and roll Intelligence + Investigation vs Wits + Suberfuge + Clues you haven't discovered yet. Win the roll and there's no penalty for unfound clues and the players get all the info through bat-logic, otherwise there's the usual penalty. Thus incentivising Geniuses to rush investigations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 05-19-2016, 04:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T05:47:11-07:00","id":893962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=893886#post893886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It's not so much in-genre so much as it's a per story difference. The Ghostbusters got arrested, and they weren't even insane.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then perhaps they weren't insane <i>enough</i>?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=893886#post893886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though I did have a better idea. Spend a point of Mania and roll Intelligence + Investigation vs Wits + Suberfuge + Clues you haven't discovered yet. Win the roll and there's no penalty for unfound clues and the players get all the info through bat-logic, otherwise there's the usual penalty. Thus incentivising Geniuses to rush investigations.</div> </div> </div> </div>That could work too. Probably better than free Clues, since that can be easily abused to the point Investigations almost make no sense as a speed bump. Why not add Inspiration into the roll, though, since it seems relevant here?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T14:24:00-07:00","id":894318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=893582#post893582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a>: I am not 100% sure, but a Mania + Wondrous Experiences rule set sounds like the best option. Perhaps you make a Wonder permanent with the Wondrous Experiences, and as you grow in Inspiration, you can update your Wonders with Advanced Functions that require Mania to be activated. Sort of like how Mages get more free Reach for their initial spells as they increase their Arcana ratings.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was seeing it as: There are two ways to &quot;stabilize&quot; a Wonder - you can either incorporate detailed knowledge of your discoveries and &quot;correct&quot; physics (Wondrous XP), or you can keep readjusting and tinkering with it (Bound Mania). Starting Genii will likely need to use Bound Mania (lacking the Wondrous XP reserves), but they can later incorporate those discoveries into &quot;refining&quot; their old designs (paying for them with Wondrous XP, which frees up the Bound Mania). Of course, there might be benefits to doing both (like maybe bonuses against Havoc wrecking the Wonder, or penalizing others' use of <i>your</i> Wonder).<br /> <br /> With Wondrous XP, I'd have deconstructing and reverse engineering other Wonders give you the Wondrous XP spent on them. Provided they were already &quot;stable&quot;. Unstable, non-supported Wonders fall apart or go Orphan.<br /> <br /> What about the Resources requirement(s)? <hr /><br /> I'm also hoping for/thinking about less... hazardous &quot;installation&quot; for Integral/Internalized Wonders. Dropping the damage (though perhaps remaining as an option), but probably sticking the recipient with a Condition.<br /> <br /> One of the things I'd like to enable is: Dr Eureka is trapped in a not-so-abandoned factory and about to meet some hemophages. The Dr needs to open the barred door, but currently lack the strength to do so. They decide to Kitbash a Wondrous Formulation to give them the might necessary to burst through. They have a few minutes, so they use Exelixi to Kitbash their &quot;Applied Force Theorem&quot; in a minute or so (if going with the &quot;improvisation&quot; option, they might spend Mania to temporarily &quot;give&quot; themselves enough Exelixi to do so). Now they have the Theorem, they rush Internalize it in a minute (or a few). Using their newly devised strength technique, Dr Eureka busts down the door, and escapes before they acquire an acute case of anemia. Of course, modifying their own physio-mental makeup like that has consequences, and they find themselves suffering from the Murderous Anger Condition (penalty to Social, and makes them Go For Blood at the slightest provocation) for a time.<br /> <br /> Thoughts, people? Does something like this fit your needs better <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1170_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1170\" data-vbnamecard=\"1170\">amechra</a>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 05-19-2016, 05:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T14:45:24-07:00","id":894335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=894318#post894318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was seeing it as: There are two ways to &quot;stabilize&quot; a Wonder - you can either incorporate detailed knowledge of your discoveries and &quot;correct&quot; physics (Wondrous XP), or you can keep readjusting and tinkering with it (Bound Mania). Starting Genii will likely need to use Bound Mania (lacking the Wondrous XP reserves), but they can later incorporate those discoveries into &quot;refining&quot; their old designs (paying for them with Wondrous XP, which frees up the Bound Mania). Of course, there might be benefits to doing both (like maybe bonuses against Havoc wrecking the Wonder, or penalizing others' use of <i>your</i> Wonder).<br /> <br /> With Wondrous XP, I'd have deconstructing and reverse engineering other Wonders give you the Wondrous XP spent on them. Provided they were already &quot;stable&quot;. Unstable, non-supported Wonders fall apart or go Orphan.<br /> <br /> What about the Resources requirement(s)?</div> </div> </div> </div> These uses for Wondrous XP and Bound Mania sound appropriate. We could brainstorm a few benefits for Binding Mania into a stabilized Wonder, preferably without specifying Axioms. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/443280-making-genius-fit-the-wider-world-of-darkness?p=483698#post483698\"><b>Malonkey1 had a great idea for a change to the Resources requirements.</b></a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=894318#post894318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm also hoping for/thinking about less... hazardous &quot;installation&quot; for Integral/Internalized Wonders. Dropping the damage (though perhaps remaining as an option), but probably sticking the recipient with a Condition.<br /> <br /> One of the things I'd like to enable is: Dr Eureka is trapped in a not-so-abandoned factory and about to meet some hemophages. The Dr needs to open the barred door, but currently lack the strength to do so. They decide to Kitbash a Wondrous Formulation to give them the might necessary to burst through. They have a few minutes, so they use Exelixi to Kitbash their &quot;Applied Force Theorem&quot; in a minute or so (if going with the &quot;improvisation&quot; option, they might spend Mania to temporarily &quot;give&quot; themselves enough Exelixi to do so). Now they have the Theorem, they rush Internalize it in a minute (or a few). Using their newly devised strength technique, Dr Eureka busts down the door, and escapes before they acquire an acute case of anemia. Of course, modifying their own physio-mental makeup like that has consequences, and they find themselves suffering from the Murderous Anger Condition (penalty to Social, and makes them Go For Blood at the slightest provocation) for a time.<br /> <br /> Thoughts, people? Does something like this fit your needs better <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1170_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1170\" data-vbnamecard=\"1170\">amechra</a>?</div> </div> </div> </div> I know that Geniuses are often addicted to coming up with convoluted solutions, but this Dr. Eureka would have a better chance of escaping if he Kitbashed a device rips apart the walls to let sunlight in. If it's nighttime, he could improve his chances by Kitbashing something that allows him to move faster and fit through small spaces. What I'm trying to say is that Kitbashing should be straight to the point. The use of Internalization in that scenario sounds like a suicidal complication.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T15:28:35-07:00","id":894362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=894335#post894335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> These uses for Wondrous XP and Bound Mania sound appropriate. We could brainstorm a few benefits for Binding Mania into a stabilized Wonder, preferably without specifying Axioms. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/443280-making-genius-fit-the-wider-world-of-darkness?p=483698#post483698\"><b>Malonkey1 had a great idea for a change to the Resources requirements.</b></a></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the new Resource/Availability rules cover Wonders pretty well in my opinion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> I know that Geniuses are often addicted to coming up with convoluted solutions, but this Dr. Eureka would have a better chance of escaping if he Kitbashed a device rips apart the walls to let sunlight in. If it's nighttime, he could improve his chances by Kitbashing something that allows him to move faster and fit through small spaces. What I'm trying to say is that Kitbashing should be straight to the point. The use of Internalization in that scenario sounds like a suicidal complication.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>I could see it being done in rare circumstances (for example, an emergency prosthetic in case of unexpected mid-chase amputation), and while it's niche, it should be considered in the rules.<br /> <br /> Maybe inflict the Arm/Leg Wrack tilt for limb-related Wonders, Drugged, Insensate or Poisoned for chemical Wonders, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":4488,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","user":"malonkey1","date":". 05-19-2016, 06:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T16:44:33-07:00","id":894418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=894335#post894335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> These uses for Wondrous XP and Bound Mania sound appropriate. We could brainstorm a few benefits for Binding Mania into a stabilized Wonder, preferably without specifying Axioms. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/443280-making-genius-fit-the-wider-world-of-darkness?p=483698#post483698\"><b>Malonkey1 had a great idea for a change to the Resources requirements.</b></a></div> </div> </div> </div>...Convergent thought, I see. &lt;shrug&gt; Well, I didn't <i>entirely</i> retread ground...<br /> <br /> I like the Resource/Availability rules there for simplicity, but a Roll might also be nice for a degree of variability. Or just penalizing the Wonder creation roll? For using substandard parts?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=894335#post894335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[COLOR=#252C2F][FONT=Helvetica][SIZE=13px] I know that Geniuses are often addicted to coming up with convoluted solutions, but this Dr. Eureka would have a better chance of escaping if he Kitbashed a device rips apart the walls to let sunlight in. If it's nighttime, he could improve his chances by Kitbashing something that allows him to move faster and fit through small spaces. What I'm trying to say is that Kitbashing should be straight to the point. The use of Internalization in that scenario sounds like a suicidal complication.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe the factory wasn't the best setting, but I meant if you don't have <i>any</i> usable materials in easy access - then you need to make the Wonder out of nothing more than thought and Mania. Yeah, Doing Science to a nearby wrench or something <i>would</i> have been far more efficient.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 05-19-2016, 07:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T12:32:33-07:00","id":894895,"title":"","content":"Opinions on the &quot;Facet&quot; acquisition model for Axioms? Thoughts on pricing? Ideas for a more Genius name?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T16:24:34-07:00","id":895103,"title":"","content":"I like Facets as a way of making Axiomata more approachable and flexible. We could call the facets &quot;Postulates&quot;. I'd probably price it similarly to Werewolf Gifts/Facets, and maybe have some &quot;Advanced Postulates&quot; that reuire another Postulate to learn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T00:33:51-07:00","id":899820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition#post818609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, after the fan meltdown, my question is as the title. Are the authors going to make a second edition? If so, is ther enay chance I could help in any way? Thank you so much for your hard work and for creating something so amazing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Moochava OKed a 2nd ed. project on RPG.net. I was ill at the time, and it fell through as the RPG.net Genius community drifted away, but I assume he's still OK with it.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=884031#post884031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would allow Beholden to use Wonders if they received Mania from a Genius, Mane or some other source. I'd say that they can store up to their [Intelligence + Resolve] in Mania, like unInspired Manes.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're in luck, then:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beholden (\u25cf to \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf; special)</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A genius can transfer Mania into beholden. This works just like transferring Mania into a capacitor. He can also draw it out, and beholden can transfer Mania they hold or draw Mania from a capacitor. Storing Mania in a beholden lets them use wonders. Beholden can hold a maximum number of Mania points equal to their Intelligence + Resolve.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=894318#post894318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm also hoping for/thinking about less... hazardous &quot;installation&quot; for Integral/Internalized Wonders. Dropping the damage (though perhaps remaining as an option), but probably sticking the recipient with a Condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I used a houserule in one of my games, paying Willpower to install personal Wonders instead of taking damage.<br /> <br /> Could be that it's painful, anaesthetic techniques involved sapped your willpower, or it required immense mental discipline (in the case of purely mental Wonders.) Regardless, it cost Willpower, rather than stretching to justify damage. (It was originally just one point, but I upped it to half-Rank when that seemed too low.)<br /> <br /> I also had an idea that you could spend permanent Willpower dots to buy the Mane merit in the moment, and then install it as an Integral Wonder - so Internalized Wonders were impossible for non-Manes - but I never got to test that and I'm not sure if it would work.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=862620#post862620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In terms of &quot;what doesn't work&quot;, we desperately need better reasons why Geniuses don't break the Masquerade. In 1e as its written, there's nothing stopping a Genius from, say, building a giant robot, having it smash a bunch of buildings, then filming it with his iPhone and throwing it on YouTube.<br /> <br /> [snip]<br /> On an earlier thread, I also mentioned having Manes be Twilight entities similar to Spirits, as another Masquerade measure, and I believe someone actually wrote out rules for this. To keep Mane Geniuses plausible, maybe we could say that Catalyzing gives a Mane the power to manifest?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why don't Spirits break the masquerade? They can manifest visibly just fine. Mortals can interact with them and even control them. They can't erase memories.<br /> <br /> The spirit-masquerade is far more tenuous than the genius-masquerade, which I guess is why they're in core.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=885300#post885300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ul><li>Standby or Hibernation mode - Mania is only bound to Wonders that are actively being used, with the rest just &quot;resting&quot; in storage or on a shelf somewhere. Bound Wonders are the Genius's, but anyone else can pickup and Bind a Wonder just sitting around.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>This is kind of already the case:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stasis:</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">An orphan wonder that wants to prolong its existence can enter a state of stasis. The wonder spends one point of Mania to enter this state. In this state, the wonder spends one point of Mania per year. It awakens automatically if touched by someone or something that contains Mania or if it suffers damage. Most orphans in ancient techo-ruins spend their time in this state.</div> </div> </div> </div>Orphans are weird, though. I really, really think that acquiring self-motivation should be a possible Orphan Mutation (they gained dots in Automata!), not the default.<br /> <br /> So yeah, what you're saying; it should be possible to leave your Wonder on a shelf without either maintaining some weird psychic connection that drains you of power or having it grow teeth and eat you.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=850947#post850947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One more thing: I'd like more incentive for Beholden PCs. As it is, the only benefit they get from interacting with Geniuses is getting a worldview back, which Geniuses take away in the first place!</div> </div> </div> </div>Beholden can use Wonders. They're certainly a zillion times better than playing a vanilla mortal in a Genius game ... but a good bit worse than a humanoid Mane. Of course, that makes sense, since being a Mane costs Merit points.<br /> <br /> Still, it would make way more sense for them to gain Beats for aiding their master, especially compared to replacing their Virtue and Vice with &quot;aid master&quot; the way 1st ed does it; a positive benefit, not an exchange. Beholden lack worldviews, not personalities.<br /> <br /> I think the &quot;you can't keep Beholden with a vastly different Morality to you&quot; rule is important enough that Beholden should use Sympathy now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":877,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","user":"MugaSofer","date":". 05-26-2016, 03:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T06:43:48-07:00","id":899986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=899820#post899820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also had an idea that you could spend permanent Willpower dots to buy the Mane merit in the moment, and then install it as an Integral Wonder - so Internalized Wonders were impossible for non-Manes - but I never got to test that and I'm not sure if it would work.</div> </div> </div> </div>So they just transform themselves into a Mane? Seems kinda cumbersome, personally, though it would have to be play-tested. I'm fond of &quot;Wondrous Knowledge&quot; (Internalized, thought-based Wonder) as an option, especially for Kitbashing in an emergency.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=899820#post899820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why don't Spirits break the masquerade? They can manifest visibly just fine. Mortals can interact with them and even control them. They can't erase memories.<br /> <br /> The spirit-masquerade is far more tenuous than the genius-masquerade, which I guess is why they're in core.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always seen it as Genii self-regulate the more egregious displays. The pure informational stuff gets explained away and ridiculed as Time-Cube stuff.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=899820#post899820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is kind of already the case:<br /> <br /> Orphans are weird, though. I really, really think that acquiring self-motivation should be a possible Orphan Mutation (they gained dots in Automata!), not the default.<br /> <br /> So yeah, what you're saying; it should be possible to leave your Wonder on a shelf without either maintaining some weird psychic connection that drains you of power or having it grow teeth and eat you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Basically for there to be an intermediate step between &quot;active use&quot; and &quot;actively trying to eat people or exploding&quot;. Dr. Insano can have a vault full of Wonders that they've created, sitting inactive. In fact, that actually <i>creates</i> story hooks - finding a famous/infamous Genius's Vault/Workshop to steal their Wonders. Even with the Hybrid Model (Spend XP or Bind Mania), it works - Stabilized Wonders can be used as is, while Unstable Wonders, your just Bind the Mania to and then use.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=899820#post899820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beholden can use Wonders. They're certainly a zillion times better than playing a vanilla mortal in a Genius game ... but a good bit worse than a humanoid Mane. Of course, that makes sense, since being a Mane costs Merit points.<br /> <br /> Still, it would make way more sense for them to gain Beats for aiding their master, especially compared to replacing their Virtue and Vice with &quot;aid master&quot; the way 1st ed does it; a positive benefit, not an exchange. Beholden lack worldviews, not personalities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why making it a Condition is great now - just include a Beat line and its done. I've seen it as more replacing Aspirations (now that they exist) than Virtue/Vice, since it changes a person's goals, but not who they are.<br /> <br /> And a Beholden PC is every bit as eligible as a Ghoul PC. Both are semi-dependent upon a main splat. Ghouls need Vitae and can use Disciplines, and Beholden get a worldview (Aspiration) and can use the Genius's Wonders. If the Beholden PC's goals already are close enough to the Genius's... what are they really losing (in the short term)?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=899820#post899820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the &quot;you can't keep Beholden with a vastly different Morality to you&quot; rule is important enough that Beholden should use Sympathy now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sympathy? Was that a proposed Obligation replacement?<br /> <br /> I wouldn't give Beholden Obligation/Sympathy, as that reflects something core to the Inspired condition (also has potentially unforeseen interactions, such as making them immune to Lunacy). I'd make it more narrative where a Beholden can leave you if you force them to violate their Virtue or other Aspirations. Integrity doesn't map to Morality anymore, and there's no reason I can see why an Evil Genius can't manipulate good (or high Integrity) Beholden, so long as they are more careful in their manipulations. And even when the Beholden leave a Genius, they are still Beholden, so it can't really Resolve the Condition either...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T04:43:08-07:00","id":900827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=899986#post899986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sympathy? Was that a proposed Obligation replacement?<br /> <br /> I wouldn't give Beholden Obligation/Sympathy, as that reflects something core to the Inspired condition (also has potentially unforeseen interactions, such as making them immune to Lunacy). I'd make it more narrative where a Beholden can leave you if you force them to violate their Virtue or other Aspirations. Integrity doesn't map to Morality anymore, and there's no reason I can see why an Evil Genius can't manipulate good (or high Integrity) Beholden, so long as they are more careful in their manipulations. And even when the Beholden leave a Genius, they are still Beholden, so it can't really Resolve the Condition either...</div> </div> </div> </div>Sympathy was a proposed Obligation replacement, yeah (from the Google doc malonkey1 posted.) I just love the name; &quot;Obligation&quot; as a term never sat right with me, given the focus on remaining &quot;in tune&quot; with Mortal perceptions of morality. An Illuminated still feels &quot;obligated&quot; to research, after all, but we don't call that Obligation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T19:24:25-07:00","id":904648,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\">Very very very lazy quick-fix for 2e mad-scientists who make gadgets using physics only they understand.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T21:25:27-07:00","id":904703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=904648#post904648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\">Very very very lazy quick-fix for 2e mad-scientists who make gadgets using physics only they understand.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>It's certainly pretty quick and elegant for Genius-type characters, provided you have access to Demon stuff.<br /> <br /> I actually have my Genius metaphysics work off of Infrastructure principles in my own little world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T22:00:50-07:00","id":904720,"title":"","content":"I'd much prefer for the Inspired to be their own, self-contained thing rather than relying on God-Machine cosmology or attached to an existing gameline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4968-mrbreaksit","name":"MrBreaksIt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T07:25:29-07:00","id":904947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrBreaksIt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=904720#post904720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd much prefer for the Inspired to be their own, self-contained thing rather than relying on God-Machine cosmology or attached to an existing gameline.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, I'm just saying in my personal cosmology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T07:31:06-07:00","id":904950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrBreaksIt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=904720#post904720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd much prefer for the Inspired to be their own, self-contained thing rather than relying on God-Machine cosmology or attached to an existing gameline.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, definitely. They have such rich potential for their own stories. But quick and dirty hacks always have their place, especially for those who only want a taste of Mad Science in addition to a different game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T19:10:54-07:00","id":907382,"title":"","content":"Well, I'm not so sure what 2ED Obligation should be about. However, I found an <a href=\"http://thoughtcatalog.com/ryan-holiday/2014/10/passion-is-the-problem-not-the-solution/\" target=\"_blank\"><b>article about the dangers of thoughtless passion</b></a> that might give us some ideas. The Integrity traits of supernaturals should be markedly different from conventional modes of behavior. Should Obligation be about balance, like 2ED Harmony? Or should it be a scale where one extreme is preferable to the other? What could it affect besides Havoc and Jabir?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T07:02:33-07:00","id":907613,"title":"","content":"Someone had an idea where Obligation cycles from top to bottom so that having too much resets you down to 1. That could be interesting to explore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4968-mrbreaksit","name":"MrBreaksIt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T19:55:23-07:00","id":908058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrBreaksIt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=907613#post907613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Someone had an idea where Obligation cycles from top to bottom so that having too much resets you down to 1. That could be interesting to explore.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> How would that work mechanically?<br /> <hr /><br /> So, what is solidified regarding Changes for 2E?<br /> <br /> Expanding upon the Axiom/Postulate idea: Axioms are still ranked 1-5 as in 1E. Rather than allowing all options and variables, each dots grants you a &quot;free&quot; Postulate in that Axiom. Other abilities (Postulates) and Variables cost extra. Some (like more advanced abilities) require higher ranks in the Axiom or prior Postulates. Maybe total ranks in the Axiom also affect the Dice Pool?<br /> <br /> \u200bResources are more flexible, as described by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4488_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4488\" data-vbnamecard=\"4488\">malonkey1</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/443280-making-genius-fit-the-wider-world-of-darkness?p=483698#post483698\">here</a>.<br /> <br /> Wonders can be made &quot;stable&quot; (not blowing up, falling apart, or going Orphan) through either applying Wondrous XP, or Binding Mania (as in 1E). Wondrous XP cost need to be devised, ideally mapping to the equivalent Bound Mania. (Each W!XP reduces the required Bound Mania by 1?)<br /> <br /> Should Wonders (not just Orphans) be able to be put into Hibernation Mode as well?<br /> <br /> Should &quot;internalization&quot; be more forgiving for certain Wonders? I'm not seeing how a Size 0 nano-infusion, or purely mental Wonder would cause implantation damage. Afflict you with its Fault as a Tilt or Condition, yeah.<br /> <br /> Changes to Obligation?<br /> <br /> Changes to Theme or Setting?<br /> <br /> Template changes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T06:47:40-07:00","id":908301,"title":"","content":"I don't think anything is solidified yet. We're really at the brainstorming stage.<br /> <br /> (Well, some things are obvious - Prostasia shouldn't be in a separate document, f'rinstance.)<br /> <br /> I liked the idea that was tossed around on the old thread, that the Axioms remained much the same, but you could purchase a Merit that let you swap out &quot;Postulates&quot; (I believe they were called Applications.) I think I have a partial writeup of it somewhere on my hard drive, I'll have to see if I can dig it up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrBreaksIt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=907613#post907613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Someone had an idea where Obligation cycles from top to bottom so that having too much resets you down to 1. That could be interesting to explore.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've noticed that several alternate Obligation schemes seem to use this idea of &quot;Breaking upwards&quot; - moments of redemption that act as anti-Breaking Points and increase Obligation. The idea that both high and low Obligation are a bad thing is an interesting one.<br /> <br /> I think we should start with the themes and build up from there. What are the themes of Genius?<br /> <br /> Struggling with mental illness, the possibility and potential in the world, feeling alienated from one's peers... that &quot;technology&quot; encompasses almost everything humans do, and abandoning that is terrible. Probably a couple I'm forgetting? We should isolate the key themes and try to tie everyting back to that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T09:34:00-07:00","id":908388,"title":"","content":"Hm, has there been any work on minor-template Geniuses? There's a lot in ChroD about otherwise normal people managing to create supernatural inventions- Alchemists, the people making Deviants, assorted odd artifacts like the Rizetti Apparatus- that I think it's an option worth pursuing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T19:54:12-07:00","id":908826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=908301#post908301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think we should start with the themes and build up from there. What are the themes of Genius?<br /> <br /> Struggling with mental illness, the possibility and potential in the world, feeling alienated from one's peers... that &quot;technology&quot; encompasses almost everything humans do, and abandoning that is terrible. Probably a couple I'm forgetting? We should isolate the key themes and try to tie everyting back to that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Obsession is another big one.The Inspired pursue their goals beyond all reason, as do the Clockstoppers, and Bardos are just like fragments of the universe that refuse to give up on an idea.<br /> <br /> That last bit also fits in really well with the academic aesthetic, as the &quot;old guard&quot; tend to be rather untrusting of new paradigms (quoth SMBC &quot;Maybe we can redefine the whole of mathematics so its wrong!&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4968-mrbreaksit","name":"MrBreaksIt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T20:23:41-07:00","id":908843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=908301#post908301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we should start with the themes and build up from there. What are the themes of Genius?<br /> <br /> Struggling with mental illness, the possibility and potential in the world, feeling alienated from one's peers... that &quot;technology&quot; encompasses almost everything humans do, and abandoning that is terrible. Probably a couple I'm forgetting? We should isolate the key themes and try to tie everything back to that.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think the central theme is &quot;Grandiose Designs, Flawed Executions&quot;. I don't like to boil it down to just &quot;Failure&quot;, though. As I've said before, while the characters might stumble upon obstacles and tragedies that make their Inspiration feel worthless, the players should not feel that way. There should be a focus on what can wrong AND what can go right.<br /> <br /> We also have to delve deeper into the subtitle. Do you know any mad scientists that conform to the rules and expectations of their societies just fine? I certainly don't. Much more than just psychiatric labels, being a Genius is about not fitting in, for one reason or another. But isolation is not a sure sign of talent or insight. The Inspired are torn between the desire for acceptance or at least recognition, and the desire to say and create whatever they wish. Perhaps this can be incorporated into the new Obligation (or whatever we might choose to name it) in the following ways. Feedback is greatly appreciated, especially on how to streamline the good parts.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">1) Geniuses MUST create. This is no mere compulsion, it is a psycho-spiritual necessity. Going for too long without exposure and interaction with Wondrous phenomena moves you upwards in the scale. Your capacity to build Wonders may be lessened somehow, but there may be benefits such as reduction of Jabir. Allowing your Inspiration to flow more freely may allow you to access more Postulates simultaneously (and perhaps give you temporary Postulates, to address the lack of spontaneity pointed out by Amechra), but Havoc and Jabir will become more dangerous for yourself and others.<br /> <br /> 2) Approaching the extremes of the Obligation scale does not necessarily mean going off the deep end and becoming unplayable. I believe Obligation should be like Satiety (i.e. it can very wildly in a single session, with each extreme being a valid play style). <br /> <br /> 3) As an alternative to the traditional 1 to 10 scale, we can innovate by not assigning a number to Obligation. Instead, Geniuses could start out with one of two Conditions, with one favoring carefulness and the other spontaneity (not sure on the precise bonuses/penalties). Geniuses would be capable of switching between the two Conditions more or less at will, with a cost of time and/or Mania being included to &quot;switch gears&quot;. Each Genius would have a third Condition that is unique to them, which they get in a moment of equilibrium between passion and planning. This Condition would be acquired mostly through roleplaying, but there would be one dice roll involved (with a flexible dice pool). There should be a limit on how often you can try to get this Condition, with a few suggested modifiers. Results on the roll would look more or less like this:<br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The Genius feels their Inspiration flare intensely with a supernova of ideas, but does not realize they are flawed or corrupted. Whatever Wondrous thing they want to create or Inspired conflict they wish to solve, the result will be a Dramatic Failure. They will receive an entire Wondrous Experience, but also a serious Persistent Condition such as Broken, Notoriety or Fugue. You may also consider Persistent Condition based on critical malfunction of a Wonder, such as Amnesia for Epikrato and Deformed for Metaptropi/Exelixi.<br /> <br /> <b>Failure:</b> The Genius' ideas flash briefly but do not take flight. Apply a Condition of your choice to represent the circumstances behind this (e.g. Obsession if they can't let it go, Embarrassing Secret if they made a rookie mistake, Starved/Exhausted if they ignored their physical needs).<br /> <br /> <b>Success:</b> The Genius gains the Informed Condition, which must be applied to a roll pertaining to Wondrous/Inspired phenomena (it need to be Wonder creation, it can also be a way to resolve conflicts between Foundations/Baramins).<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> Besides the benefit of Success, a full refill of Mania OR a number of the Inspired Condition equal to [Inspiration/2 round up], which can be applied to any roll.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T20:34:09-07:00","id":908850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=908388#post908388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm, has there been any work on minor-template Geniuses? There's a lot in ChroD about otherwise normal people managing to create supernatural inventions- Alchemists, the people making Deviants, assorted odd artifacts like the Rizetti Apparatus- that I think it's an option worth pursuing.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think that being Beholden is more like being a Sleepwalker than a proper minor template. Perhaps Beholden can evolve into Tinkerers. The latter would have 1 dot of Inspiration and would spend Mania to use a more limited version of Kitbashing (i.e. quick and probably unstable Equipment but not true Wonders). They would still have Integrity, but would not be capable of generating Mania on their own, which would motivate them to seek out Geniuses and run the risk of devolving to Beholden or evolving to Inspired.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T22:53:37-07:00","id":908910,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4443_5.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4443\" data-vbnamecard=\"4443\">GibberingEloquence</a> I do like most of what you just said there. Not creating screwing with your Obligation, Obligation like Satiety, but this:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=908843#post908843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 3) As an alternative to the traditional 1 to 10 scale, we can innovate by not assigning a number to Obligation. Instead, Geniuses could start out with one of two Conditions, with one favoring carefulness and the other spontaneity (not sure on the precise bonuses/penalties). Geniuses would be capable of switching between the two Conditions more or less at will, with a cost of time and/or Mania being included to &quot;switch gears&quot;. Each Genius would have a third Condition that is unique to them, which they get in a moment of equilibrium between passion and planning. This Condition would be acquired mostly through roleplaying, but there would be one dice roll involved (with a flexible dice pool). There should be a limit on how often you can try to get this Condition, with a few suggested modifiers. Results on the roll would look more or less like this:<br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The Genius feels their Inspiration flare intensely with a supernova of ideas, but does not realize they are flawed or corrupted. Whatever Wondrous thing they want to create or Inspired conflict they wish to solve, the result will be a Dramatic Failure. They will receive an entire Wondrous Experience, but also a serious Persistent Condition such as Broken, Notoriety or Fugue. You may also consider Persistent Condition based on critical malfunction of a Wonder, such as Amnesia for Epikrato and Deformed for Metaptropi/Exelixi.<br /> <br /> <b>Failure:</b> The Genius' ideas flash briefly but do not take flight. Apply a Condition of your choice to represent the circumstances behind this (e.g. Obsession if they can't let it go, Embarrassing Secret if they made a rookie mistake, Starved/Exhausted if they ignored their physical needs).<br /> <br /> <b>Success:</b> The Genius gains the Informed Condition, which must be applied to a roll pertaining to Wondrous/Inspired phenomena (it need to be Wonder creation, it can also be a way to resolve conflicts between Foundations/Baramins).<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> Besides the benefit of Success, a full refill of Mania OR a number of the Inspired Condition equal to [Inspiration/2 round up], which can be applied to any roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems too binary to me, but that's just me - you're either Will Magnus on his meds or Sander Cohen off of them with no middle ground.<br /> Maybe we could do something like the Virtuous/Sinister skill rows in better angels, where we have 2 smaller scales (probably capping out at 5) that &quot;overlap&quot; so that being high in one necessarily means being low in the other? Obligation countered by Creativity, perhaps? Or maybe even the Inspiration stat itself? Things to think about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4968-mrbreaksit","name":"MrBreaksIt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T23:28:55-07:00","id":908925,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4968-mrbreaksit\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4968\" data-vbnamecard=\"4968\">MrBreaksIt</a> I agree that it is too binary. There should be more room for customization. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1170_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1170\" data-vbnamecard=\"1170\">amechra</a> What do you think the main themes should be in 2ED? Is there too much overlap with Mage?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 06-07-2016, 02:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T12:41:48-07:00","id":909378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=908925#post908925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1170_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1170\" data-vbnamecard=\"1170\">amechra</a> What do you think the main themes should be in 2ED? Is there too much overlap with Mage?</div> </div> </div> </div>[Caveat: not <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1170_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1170\" data-vbnamecard=\"1170\">amechra</a>]<br /> Well, both &quot;investigate&quot; and delight in &quot;mysteries&quot;. I think the subtle distinction is that Geniuses pursue &quot;real&quot; (or to Mage, Fallen) mysteries on their own merits, or for their insight into the rest of the world (not just the Symbols behind them).<br /> <br /> I think Genii might also be a bit more pro-active: rather than looking for pre-existing Mysteries, Genii often seem more willing to conduct their own experiments (for SCIENCE!!!). There is overlap, of course, but I can see more Genius Chronicles being about events that the players originate, rather than events they encounter.<br /> <br /> I think some of the themes might be slightly different: in Mage, an external force (Exarchs, the Fallen World) are holding you back, while in Genius, I think more <i>personal</i> obstructions should be focused on (Havoc is incidental and avoidable, but it's your personal failings should doom your grand vision).<br /> <br /> Maybe some Themes could also be <b>Dangerous Knowledge</b> (be it in it acquisition, or what the knowledge reveals itself) and <b>Uncontrollable Change</b> (in the manner of once some technology or insight is let out of the bottle, it can't be stopped)?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Actually, I think a theme of <b>You are the cause of your own misfortune</b> might be a strong one for Genius overall. Both personal causes, and other Genii at large, are the reason for much of the conflict, especially if the X Chronicle is/remains focused upon the Illuminated.<br /> <br /> EDIT SECUNDUS: But this isn't to be confused with &quot;Failure&quot;. Yes, you (and other Inspired) are the reason for your life's difficulties, but that doesn't mean you can't achieve something wonderful as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 06-07-2016, 03:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T16:34:26-07:00","id":909581,"title":"","content":"I think &quot;<b>Your Own Worst Enemy</b>&quot; (to paraphrase Vent's edit) is probably the best theme for Genius. Maybe downplay the Foundations and make it less about Peerage vs. Lemuria to help differentiate from Mage better, and maybe even add some ambiguity to exactly how &quot;wrong&quot; Geniuses are?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T16:43:32-07:00","id":909586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=909581#post909581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think &quot;<b>Your Own Worst Enemy</b>&quot; (to paraphrase Vent's edit) is probably the best theme for Genius. Maybe downplay the Foundations and make it less about Peerage vs. Lemuria to help differentiate from Mage better, and maybe even add some ambiguity to exactly how &quot;wrong&quot; Geniuses are?</div> </div> </div> </div> That's a good theme. I just didn't understand what you were referring to with &quot;add ambiguity&quot;. Is it in relation to the source and true nature of Inspiration, or the worldview of each Foundation?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T18:13:06-07:00","id":909664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=909586#post909586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That's a good theme. I just didn't understand what you were referring to with &quot;add ambiguity&quot;. Is it in relation to the source and true nature of Inspiration, or the worldview of each Foundation?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Why not both?<br /> <br /> I've always seen the Foundations as not &quot;our good guys&quot; but rather &quot;these people that partially share my worldview, even as we occasionally smile and backstab each other over trivial reasons&quot;. I think that one of the motivations behind letting Lemuria exist, that it unites the Peerage against a common foe, is telling. Even the Protagonist organization is a hair's breadth from self destruction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T18:14:12-07:00","id":909666,"title":"","content":"The way Genius is written, the rules of Inspiration are that everything the Genius does is powered purely by crazy and Mania, and trying to prove your worldview right is regarded as craziness. I think it might be more interesting if it's not quite as clear that that's the case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T18:25:58-07:00","id":909675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=909666#post909666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way Genius is written, the rules of Inspiration are that everything the Genius does is powered purely by crazy and Mania, and trying to prove your worldview right is regarded as craziness. I think it might be more interesting if it's not quite as clear that that's the case.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Like rumors of Wonder, or the foundational ideas behind a Wonder, actually <i>working</i> and being discovered and adopted by mainstream science?<br /> <br /> With the Peerage's whole &quot;no, Wonders work only do to Mania and Inspiration/acknowledge you are Crazy&quot; line being itself incorrect (or only partly true)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T18:26:37-07:00","id":909676,"title":"","content":"If you're going to be borrowing a Greg Stolze sliding stat mechanic, I think you could check out Unknown Armies 3e's version of Madness Meters.<br /> <br /> At least, when it comes out.<br /> <br /> As for themes...<br /> <br /> <b>Perfectionism And Guilt Waltzed Into A Bar</b>, and <b>The Eyes Are Longer Than The Arms</b>, of course. <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hrUzGGaMYcQ&amp;list=PLYK-WgDbjAlZtrIGZ0xL6JlfLXX45IC-e&amp;index=5\" target=\"_blank\">We tried to reach for the stars and we destroyed them - what does that mean to you?</a><br /> <br /> Then again, for me, Mad Scientists are more like <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ppwowTJg0mI\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> or <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VHEJrXPvU5s\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>. Or maybe <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1jfPRa7kD-Y\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>.<br /> <br /> Or...<br /> <br /> There's a short story I read years ago where a guy sits down next to a man crying into his booze at a bar. They chat for a little bit, and get on the topic of FTL travel, which the man <i>flinches</i> at. It turns out that FTL travel drastically shortens your lifespan and messes up your health pretty badly.<br /> <br /> After he leaves, the bartender confides that he's confused about why the man comes in to drown his sorrows every evening - shouldn't he be proud? He <i>was</i> the scientist that invented the FTL drive that made interstellar trade possible, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T07:54:49-07:00","id":910082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=909676#post909676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a short story I read years ago where a guy sits down next to a man crying into his booze at a bar. They chat for a little bit, and get on the topic of FTL travel, which the man <i>flinches</i> at. It turns out that FTL travel drastically shortens your lifespan and messes up your health pretty badly.<br /> <br /> After he leaves, the bartender confides that he's confused about why the man comes in to drown his sorrows every evening - shouldn't he be proud? He <i>was</i> the scientist that invented the FTL drive that made interstellar trade possible, after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems to read to me <b>It's not a good as you thought it would be</b>. Basically, despite your perfect, utopian (or apocalyptic) visions, the actual resultant reality is every bit as flawed as before, just with a new coat of paint and the furniture moved around. (And this goes for Vengeance, I'll-show-them, and other motivations besides Utopia)<br /> <br /> Which, if you think the improved Feng Shui is enough, is fine. It's okay to accept less than perfection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T08:02:58-07:00","id":910087,"title":"","content":"I really hope we keep &quot;no one is in charge&quot; as a core theme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T20:03:55-07:00","id":910505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=910082#post910082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That seems to read to me <b>It's not a good as you thought it would be</b>. Basically, despite your perfect, utopian (or apocalyptic) visions, the actual resultant reality is every bit as flawed as before, just with a new coat of paint and the furniture moved around. (And this goes for Vengeance, I'll-show-them, and other motivations besides Utopia)<br /> <br /> Which, if you think the improved Feng Shui is enough, is fine. It's okay to accept less than perfection.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reminds me of that Klagen quote from 1E. What was it again? Something about putting down the syringe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4968-mrbreaksit","name":"MrBreaksIt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T20:21:25-07:00","id":910513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrBreaksIt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=910505#post910505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reminds me of that Klagen quote from 1E. What was it again? Something about putting down the syringe?</div> </div> </div> </div> That quote appears just before the stereotypical opinions that Klagen have on the other Catalysts (page 54).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When I was in high school my teacher told me that there are more people alive today than have ever lived. Don't worry: she lied, then got cancer. (Not my fault.) We live atop a mountain of corpses. The Earth is swimming in humans, above and below the ground, so when I see you trying to raise the dead, I'm torn. On the one hand, I recognize your despair. On the other hand, do you really want to spend the rest of the week fending off a zombie apocalypse as the Earth vomits up her dead? AGAIN? Come on, man, think this through: every time you try this, we end up fighting zombies. I hate zombies. Just put the syringe down. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T20:23:47-07:00","id":910515,"title":"","content":"Quick observation: is it just me, or is <a href=\"http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-049\" target=\"_blank\"><b>SCP-049</b></a> an excellent example of an Illuminated who thinks they're doing the right thing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T01:56:57-07:00","id":915468,"title":"","content":"I'm actually working on a remake of Awakening that's heavily based on Transgression, combined with a lot of Ascension. It's designed to be make it possible to play sorcerors, mad scientists, and the rest of the incredible variety of character types from Ascension, but crossover friendly and with the idea of &quot;mage as monster&quot; emphasized.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T09:07:09-07:00","id":915643,"title":"","content":"So, given the general &quot;power-up&quot; 2E has given to the main splats, are there any ideas for modifications to the Genius Template itself?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T12:54:33-07:00","id":915777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=915643#post915643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, given the general &quot;power-up&quot; 2E has given to the main splats, are there any ideas for modifications to the Genius Template itself?</div> </div> </div> </div>Geniuses can get pretty wicked powerful to begin with, even giving Magi a run for their money under the right circumstances.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T13:13:55-07:00","id":915794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=915777#post915777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Geniuses can get pretty wicked powerful to begin with, even giving Magi a run for their money under the right circumstances.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. Though that is more a function of Axioms and Wonders. Mages now get Mage Sight as a core part of their template, for instance of a 2E upgrade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T13:25:21-07:00","id":915805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=915794#post915794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True. Though that is more a function of Axioms and Wonders. Mages now get Mage Sight as a core part of their template, for instance of a 2E upgrade.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but it's hard to think of an innate ability that doesn't stretch the theme. I could see them having inhuman analytical and technical skills (maybe drop a point of Mania to get a free Specialty for a scene?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T13:36:50-07:00","id":915810,"title":"","content":"At the least, they should probably go the way of most of the other 2e splats and develop some sort of Condition/Tilt inflicting &quot;aura&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T13:40:48-07:00","id":915816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=915805#post915805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but it's hard to think of an innate ability that doesn't stretch the theme. I could see them having inhuman analytical and technical skills (maybe drop a point of Mania to get a free Specialty for a scene?)</div> </div> </div> </div> You know how they can spend Mania to power, improve and sabotage mundane techology in a broad sense? We could expand that. We could also allow kitbashing to create temporary gadgets that are useful but mundane.<br /> <br /> As for enhanced analytical and technical skills...maybe they bonuses to creating Plans that further their goals related to mad science (which could take away from the excessive focus on engineering that's been mentioned multiple times).<br /> <br /> They could have their own equivalent of Going Loud, which would give temporary Axioms/Postulates, speed up their Wonder creation and give huge bonuses to all Mental rolls, like 8 Again or Rote Quality. The risk would be an Unmada check, with results ranging from attracting Manes and Illuminated to generating a temporary Unmada field.<br /> <br /> That might make Unmadaness closer to Embracing The Wyrd than being a Mad Mage, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T14:09:25-07:00","id":915833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=915816#post915816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for enhanced analytical and technical skills...maybe they bonuses to creating Plans that further their goals related to mad science (which could take away from the excessive focus on engineering that's been mentioned multiple times).</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds familiar... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T14:45:34-07:00","id":915852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=915833#post915833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sounds familiar... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> Ah, yes, you mentioned that as well. Convergent thought at work again.<br /> <br /> What sorts of Conditions/Tilts could the Genius Aura inflict besides Beholden? I don't think the worldview of every Genius sounds like Time Cube after Jabir is applied. You know how <b><a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Music/DoctorSteel\" target=\"_blank\">Doctor Steel</a></b> has a massive in-universe fanclub/personal army despite the <b><a href=\"https://youtu.be/JCE7hOgXVEM\" target=\"_blank\">extensive documentation of his insanity?</a></b> I want that to be possible for Geniuses as a whole, though not necessarily with the same amount of effort for each one of them. An Aura mechanic sounds perfect for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 06-16-2016, 06:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T14:53:17-07:00","id":915859,"title":"","content":"Also, I think it should not be easy to dismantle or take control of a Genius' mind or Wonders with powers like Dominate and Matter Arcanum. Geniuses would benefit from a general awareness of the state of their Wonders, and a way to remotely protect and control them to some degree. This could be represented with a Clash Of Wills, which could be improved by certain internalized augmentations, security bonuses of your laboratory, hidden countermeasures in the Wonders themselves and so on. It would be very anti-climatic if you could easily kneecap the main supernatural advantage of the entire splat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T16:50:30-07:00","id":915920,"title":"","content":"I'm gonna be following this, but I think mostly I'll be sticking to development of Mage: The Transgression. If I see anything here I want to use, I'll ask whoever posted it if I can use it/how to give credit, I don't want to steal anyone's ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T17:13:13-07:00","id":915933,"title":"","content":"Perhaps we could introduce an &quot;experiment&quot; mechanic, to once again remove the focus from engineering? I've no idea what it would be, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4968-mrbreaksit","name":"MrBreaksIt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T19:40:32-07:00","id":915979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=915859#post915859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I think it should not be easy to dismantle or take control of a Genius' mind or Wonders with powers like Dominate and Matter Arcanum. Geniuses would benefit from a general awareness of the state of their Wonders, and a way to remotely protect and control them to some degree. This could be represented with a Clash Of Wills, which could be improved by certain internalized augmentations, security bonuses of your laboratory, hidden countermeasures in the Wonders themselves and so on. It would be very anti-climatic if you could easily kneecap the main supernatural advantage of the entire splat.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Maybe make that an advantage of Binding Mania to a Wonder you already paid XP for? Because there is also the niche of turning a Genius's own Wonders against them. This way, there is room for both in the rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrBreaksIt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=915933#post915933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps we could introduce an &quot;experiment&quot; mechanic, to once again remove the focus from engineering? I've no idea what it would be, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe make that a side system or something? Or integrate it with Plans? Maybe make it like an odd form of the Investigation sub-system? Honestly, I see Genii coming up with their own &quot;plots&quot; via attempting to conduct their insane experiments. Rather than a Prince handing you some task, or a Spirit rolling into town, your own character(s) want to see what would happen if you get a Spirit to try and Claim a Hobgoblin, or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 06-16-2016, 10:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T03:24:42-07:00","id":916105,"title":"","content":"The problem is that it's really hard to GM for that, and a lot of players aren't that self-motivated anyway. <br /> You have to make your players do the experiments, then work them in to the existing world you've created, then figure out everyone's reactions to the experiment (shock and horror, probably), then wrangle a plot motivator out of all of that. <br /> <br /> Not to mention that it doesn't work with super-high Obligation characters, or the sort who are more interested in just observing things, or are aware that any observations they make would be tainted by Mania.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4968-mrbreaksit","name":"MrBreaksIt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T07:17:33-07:00","id":916174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrBreaksIt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=916105#post916105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is that it's really hard to GM for that, and a lot of players aren't that self-motivated anyway.<br /> You have to make your players do the experiments, then work them in to the existing world you've created, then figure out everyone's reactions to the experiment (shock and horror, probably), then wrangle a plot motivator out of all of that.<br /> <br /> Not to mention that it doesn't work with super-high Obligation characters, or the sort who are more interested in just observing things, or are aware that any observations they make would be tainted by Mania.</div> </div> </div> </div>So make NPCs conduct the experiments. While similar to the previous external plots, it is different in that those external actors are different from the PCs by status or nature, while the fellow Genius is <i>just like</i> the PCs. <i>Nothing</i> stops them from doing the same thing (other than their own self-imposed limitations or sloth).<br /> <br /> Or run an &quot;experiment&quot; like an Investigation. At the end, compile the Clues towards a flat score or a roll to gain Wondrous Beats/Experiences. Knowledge is Power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T07:34:16-07:00","id":916185,"title":"","content":"There's really nothing stopping you from getting plot stuff from people who aren't heads of state, anyway. When I was in Azahul's Mummy game, we ended up getting quests from rival Arisen, the Hierophants of our Cults, a group of pirates, LDI, ghosts, Fate itself and plenty of other things. Still, this isn't an argument we need to be having, so I'll quiet down about it after this.<br /> I like the idea of experiment-as-investigation, maybe with a couple of tweaks.<br /> <br /> I also really appreciate the effort and thought you put into all of your posts. Who knows, with you around we may actually get something out of this discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4968-mrbreaksit","name":"MrBreaksIt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T19:53:15-07:00","id":916571,"title":"","content":"More thoughts:<br /> <br /> <b>Havoc</b><br /> <br /> So when an un-Inspired mortal directly interacts with or analyzes a Wonder, it provokes Havoc. I'm thinking a Wonder only Fails, Explodes, suffers/causes an Accident, or goes Orphan on Dramatic Failure, Failure applies a Fault, Success does nothing (but applies a -1 Penalty to the next roll, for the same Scene), and Exceptional Success is nothing (and maybe prevents the next roll). Modifiers: -1 per Fault (so Failures increase the risk of Dramatic Failure). -1 Per applicable skill the mortal has (Science for most Wonders, though biological ones might be Medicine, etc.). +1 or -1 per Rank? [Either more advanced Wonder are more robust, or more fragile]. Base Pool: Obligation (or replacement name), or based on it (5 dice at the highest levels, 1 die at lowest)? Or make that a feature of Bound Wonders, and track Stable Wonders differently (such as a flat 4 dice as a base, similar to the bonus for permanent effects in a Clash of Wills)? Unmada Fields might offer a dice bonus scaled to Inspiration (a high Inspiration and Obligation Genius - rare as they are - rarely has their Wonders suffer from Havoc)?<br /> <br /> <b>Interstellar and Time Travel</b><br /> <br /> Have super-luminal and temporal transit risk/cause a &quot;Bardo incident&quot;, a dimensional shift that throws the travelers into the alternate universe of a Bardo. Outsiders are treated as Manes inside such alien realities (and natives from such realities are treated as Manes in the &quot;real&quot; world)? This can explain the various &quot;Mane-like&quot; behavior and effects from Time Travellers and &quot;Aliens&quot;. It can also serve as justification for stories of why the Genii visitors are different/exceptional, and they solve some problem that was plaguing the natives for some time (they literally have an edge... sometimes). Havoc in such cases might be &quot;alien sickness&quot; or &quot;temporal ejection&quot; or spawning &quot;time/space wraith to deal with the violators&quot; (a Genius version of Abyssal Manifestations).<br /> <br /> <b>Specialist Wonders</b><br /> <br /> I'm thinking &quot;specialized&quot; Wonders (guns that only harm Ghosts, fields that only block one kind of creature, scanners that only detect a certain form of radiation) should just have a dice bonus, maybe +1 (or higher, if justified). They are kind of like the equivalent of Skill Specialties, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 06-17-2016, 10:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T10:38:07-07:00","id":917420,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a>: I like the sound of those Havoc rules, but I think Specialized Wonders should get more than a +1. Maybe they could cost less Bound Mania (which can give bonuses to Clash Of Wills, like you mentioned in your reply to my previous post). <br /> <br /> I don't know if Genius should have a universal system for Time Travel. Instead, it could have a few very broad methods with different outcomes if successful. I personally like Mage's idea of an objective present.<br /> <br /> Has anyone thought of suggestions for how Geniuses might interact with the 2ED versions of the gamelines? I think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4488_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4488\" data-vbnamecard=\"4488\">malonkey1</a> wrote something in the previous thread about Angels of the G-M being incapable of handling Mania. However, Demons could have a Technology installed into them by a Genius which allows the Demon to use their Aether as Mania.<br /> <br /> I think changelings and certain hobgoblins should be capable of using Wonders, but not True Fae or Huntsmen. Mania is a burning energy of creativity, after all, which is something that does not come naturally to the latter two. I'd go as far as to say that Wonders can't even be used ON the True Fae or Huntsmen, but that is better left to ST fiat.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T10:39:48-07:00","id":917422,"title":"","content":"Also, what sort of Beasts would develop Kinship with Geniuses? If that is possible, I'm pretty sure the latter would count as Fundamentally Human, just like Mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T10:52:04-07:00","id":917434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=917420#post917420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a>: I like the sound of those Havoc rules, but I think Specialized Wonders should get more than a +1. Maybe they could cost less Bound Mania (which can give bonuses to Clash Of Wills, like you mentioned in your reply to my previous post).<br /> <br /> I don't know if Genius should have a universal system for Time Travel. Instead, it could have a few very broad methods with different outcomes if successful. I personally like Mage's idea of an objective present.<br /> <br /> Has anyone thought of suggestions for how Geniuses might interact with the 2ED versions of the gamelines? I think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4488_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4488\" data-vbnamecard=\"4488\">malonkey1</a> wrote something in the previous thread about Angels of the G-M being incapable of handling Mania. However, Demons could have a Technology installed into them by a Genius which allows the Demon to use their Aether as Mania.<br /> <br /> I think changelings and certain hobgoblins should be capable of using Wonders, but not True Fae or Huntsmen. Mania is a burning energy of creativity, after all, which is something that does not come naturally to the latter two. I'd go as far as to say that Wonders can't even be used ON the True Fae or Huntsmen, but that is better left to ST fiat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, my thinking was that Changelings don't cause Havoc, and I kind of like the idea of narrative laws being a valid paradigm for Genii. As for Geniuses and the Hedge, they would probably pretty much break it. Geniuses would twist the Hedge around their Paradigm hard enough that an Unmada basically overwrites the Hedge nearby, and the Genius would probably be able to toy with Hedgespinning pretty easily, at the cost of more rapid descent into self-delusion.<br /> <br /> True Fae and Wonders would behave unpredictably, especially when the Narrative Law paradigm comes into play.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=917422#post917422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, what sort of Beasts would develop Kinship with Geniuses? If that is possible, I'm pretty sure the latter would count as Fundamentally Human, just like Mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably going to be Tyrants or Collectors more than anything else. They might be in for a surprise when a stolen Wonder goes Orphan, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T11:03:21-07:00","id":917440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=917434#post917434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, my thinking was that Changelings don't cause Havoc, and I kind of like the idea of narrative laws being a valid paradigm for Genii. As for Geniuses and the Hedge, they would probably pretty much break it. Geniuses would twist the Hedge around their Paradigm hard enough that an Unmada basically overwrites the Hedge nearby, and the Genius would probably be able to toy with Hedgespinning pretty easily, at the cost of more rapid descent into self-delusion.<br /> <br /> True Fae and Wonders would behave unpredictably, especially when the Narrative Law paradigm comes into play.</div> </div> </div> </div> Sounds pretty close to canon. I like it. Could a Hedgespun item serve as a Larva if the Changeling and/or Genius lost Clarity/Obligation while building it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=917434#post917434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably going to be Tyrants or Collectors more than anything else. They might be in for a surprise when a stolen Wonder goes Orphan, though.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well said. Beasts can accumulate immunity to many types of harm, which can be put to good use if they're a Tyrant/Collector willing to enter Bardos, Invisible Realms and dangerous mundane locations to get materials for Wonders.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T11:18:56-07:00","id":917458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=917440#post917440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Sounds pretty close to canon. I like it. Could a Hedgespun item serve as a Larva if the Changeling and/or Genius lost Clarity/Obligation while building it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, yeah.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Well, I got that screaming eye you needed. I had to rip it out of a fairy wolf and infuse it with the essence of terror, though.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Sweet. Now I can finish this laser.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well said. Beasts can accumulate immunity to many types of harm, which can be put to good use if they're a Tyrant/Collector willing to enter Bardos, Invisible Realms and dangerous mundane locations to get materials for Wonders. </div> </div> </div>Yep. A Genius who manages to befriend has a powerful source of exotic materials. Also, a tempting test subject for especially crazy Genii.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T12:27:13-07:00","id":917493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=917420#post917420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a>: I like the sound of those Havoc rules, but I think Specialized Wonders should get more than a +1. Maybe they could cost less Bound Mania (which can give bonuses to Clash Of Wills, like you mentioned in your reply to my previous post).</div> </div> </div> </div>Bound Mania/Wondrous XP discount seems like a good idea.<br /> <br /> Any ideas on &quot;reconfiguring&quot; a specialized Wonder to target different phenomena? Reversing the polarity (or similar technobabble BS) to temporarily allow your ghost finder to detect spirits? Cost Mania, lasts a Scene, I'm thinking?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=917420#post917420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if Genius should have a universal system for Time Travel. Instead, it could have a few very broad methods with different outcomes if successful. I personally like Mage's idea of an objective present.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there was Time Travel in I think the appendix. I was just thinking &quot;anything that lets a Genius travel beyond conventional detect risks them just entering a Bardo&quot;. Future timelines? Likely Universe sized Bardos. Alien star systems? Likely Bardos. Travelers from those place? Treated as Manes to prevent easy &quot;contamination&quot; of the current World (of Darkness).<br /> <br /> Allows Storytellers to dodge the question of whether such things are &quot;true&quot; or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 06-19-2016, 03:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T12:44:11-07:00","id":917504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=917493#post917493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bound Mania/Wondrous XP discount seems like a good idea.<br /> <br /> Any ideas on &quot;reconfiguring&quot; a specialized Wonder to target different phenomena? Reversing the polarity (or similar technobabble BS) to temporarily allow your ghost finder to detect spirits? Cost Mania, lasts a Scene, I'm thinking?</div> </div> </div> </div> That's a property (or Postulate) of Metaptropi 4, page 237. I believe it should be lowered to Metaptropi 3.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=917493#post917493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, there was Time Travel in I think the appendix. I was just thinking &quot;anything that lets a Genius travel beyond conventional detect risks them just entering a Bardo&quot;. Future timelines? Likely Universe sized Bardos. Alien star systems? Likely Bardos. Travelers from those place? Treated as Manes to prevent easy &quot;contamination&quot; of the current World (of Darkness).<br /> <br /> Allows Storytellers to dodge the question of whether such things are &quot;true&quot; or not.</div> </div> </div> </div> The rules for Time Travel begin on page 300. And beginning on page 349 there is a list of possible futures that work somewhat like what you described:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The future isn't what it used to be. Once a linear progression of events leading eventually to the Terminals, the timeline is now a mess of pocket chrono-fiefdoms and unstable causality. This increasing disorder, coupled with the fact that time-traveling into the future necessarily removes the genius from the timeline, means that rarely will two trips into, say, the year 3,000, produce the same result. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T13:11:13-07:00","id":917518,"title":"","content":"I just wanna check something: how does everyone feel about the progress we made so far? I think we're getting close to a pretty solid base. I especially liked the idea of Postulates, as it solves the issue of non-thematic powers being bundled in with the ones you want. Who came up with the Postulates, again?<br /> <br /> I'd like to add some comments about Larvae:<br /> <br /> They're far too costly for a mere +1 to Wonder building. For a loss of Obligation and the associated negative Condition, you should get a similarly dramatic benefit, like an automatic Exceptional Success on the Wonder building (or at least an Exceptional Success with 3 Successes).<br /> <br /> I'd place a limit on how many times you can use Larvae per Story, so Lemurians won't have tons of ultra-sophisticated Wonders no member of the Peerage can surpass on their own.<br /> <br /> I'd give the Illuminated special uses for Larvae, so as to encourage the horrific experiments they're known for.<br /> <br /> Lastly, I'd allow Geniuses with the Technomancer Merit to incorporate materials from other splats as Larvae, as long as the building process involved the other supernaturals doing something they're personally against. The splats that do not suffer normal Breaking Points might be exempt from providing Larvae at ST discretion, but they can compensate in other ways (e.g. Demons can compare notes about Infrastructure with Geniuses and lend/sell Gadgets).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T13:15:45-07:00","id":917521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=917504#post917504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That's a property (or Postulate) of Metaptropi 4, page 237. I believe it should be lowered to Metaptropi 3.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe we should have freeform, on-the-fly reconfiguration be a universal thing (maybe using Kitbashing).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The rules for Time Travel begin on page 300. And beginning on page 349 there is a list of possible futures that work somewhat like what you described: </div> </div> </div>The time travel rules have always been kind of arcane to me. I'll reread and add something after I refresh myself.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Okay, now I remember why I don't remember Genius's time travel rules very well: I kind of hate them.<br /> <br /> For starters, the timeline's way too ordered and simplistic, and enacting changes is far too difficult. It makes it too hard to really toy around with the &quot;unintended consequences of time travel.&quot; The <s>Time Masters</s> Guardians of Forever kind of feels like a cheap way to penalize your time-travelling shenanigans when they should just come organically from the results of your stupid, arrogant chicanery.<br /> <br /> Second, it also doesn't make a huge amount of sense. If they exist in all points in time, then by definition, they have already experienced the future, which means that the future is already set for them, which means that they would have no need to police time, because the timeline for them has already been set. Any policing just prevents other, alternate timelines from existing that have basically no effect on them.<br /> <br /> I would completely discard the time travel rules as they are. Time travel is unregulated (and basically impossible to regulate without constant, extratemporal murder), and changing the timeline requires no more than a time machine, a raygun and a bottle of tequila. Your existence in a given point in time doesn't affect the stability of that timeline when you visit it. You can return to your time, but you still need to deal with your alternate self where applicable. If you prevent your existence, you don't blink out, you're just orphaned from time (and incur a serious Transgression roll). You don't get to just let things snap back, and you deal with the consequences of your actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":4488,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","user":"malonkey1","date":". 06-19-2016, 04:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T15:44:52-07:00","id":917588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=917518#post917518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just wanna check something: how does everyone feel about the progress we made so far? I think we're getting close to a pretty solid base. I especially liked the idea of Postulates, as it solves the issue of non-thematic powers being bundled in with the ones you want. Who came up with the Postulates, again?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I posted it here, but I can't verify for certain I didn't see it posted elsewhere in some shape or form.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=917518#post917518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to add some comments about Larvae:<br /> <br /> They're far too costly for a mere +1 to Wonder building. For a loss of Obligation and the associated negative Condition, you should get a similarly dramatic benefit, like an automatic Exceptional Success on the Wonder building (or at least an Exceptional Success with 3 Successes).<br /> <br /> I'd place a limit on how many times you can use Larvae per Story, so Lemurians won't have tons of ultra-sophisticated Wonders no member of the Peerage can surpass on their own.<br /> <br /> I'd give the Illuminated special uses for Larvae, so as to encourage the horrific experiments they're known for.<br /> <br /> Lastly, I'd allow Geniuses with the Technomancer Merit to incorporate materials from other splats as Larvae, as long as the building process involved the other supernaturals doing something they're personally against. The splats that do not suffer normal Breaking Points might be exempt from providing Larvae at ST discretion, but they can compensate in other ways (e.g. Demons can compare notes about Infrastructure with Geniuses and lend/sell Gadgets).</div> </div> </div> </div>Rather than just improving Wonder creation, what about Larvae permanently modifying the Wonder? Like the lower Exceptional Success threshold, or some list of benefit (like Mummy's Talismans, or Demon's Overclocking).<br /> <br /> What about Larvae comprised <i>of</i> the other Splats?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I was rereading some of the first few pages. I thinking incorporating the Equipment and Investigation rules would help. I'm for making purely &quot;mental&quot; Wonders more accessible, to represent Inspired Knowledge (and decrease the Mad Engineer feel). Yes, the rules are basically the same, but that's because the rules are very flexible. As for why it requires &quot;building&quot; a Wonder to begin with - knowledge is nice and all, but it needs to be Applied before it has an effect upon the world. Lacking inherent magical powers, Genii need to Apply that Knowledge with something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 06-20-2016, 09:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T17:07:00-07:00","id":917641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=917521#post917521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe we should have freeform, on-the-fly reconfiguration be a universal thing (maybe using Kitbashing).</div> </div> </div> </div>Seconded.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=917521#post917521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The time travel rules have always been kind of arcane to me. I'll reread and add something after I refresh myself.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Okay, now I remember why I don't remember Genius's time travel rules very well: I kind of hate them.<br /> <br /> For starters, the timeline's way too ordered and simplistic, and enacting changes is far too difficult. It makes it too hard to really toy around with the &quot;unintended consequences of time travel.&quot; The <s>Time Masters</s> Guardians of Forever kind of feels like a cheap way to penalize your time-travelling shenanigans when they should just come organically from the results of your stupid, arrogant chicanery.<br /> <br /> Second, it also doesn't make a huge amount of sense. If they exist in all points in time, then by definition, they have already experienced the future, which means that the future is already set for them, which means that they would have no need to police time, because the timeline for them has already been set. Any policing just prevents other, alternate timelines from existing that have basically no effect on them.<br /> <br /> I would completely discard the time travel rules as they are. Time travel is unregulated (and basically impossible to regulate without constant, extratemporal murder), and changing the timeline requires no more than a time machine, a raygun and a bottle of tequila. Your existence in a given point in time doesn't affect the stability of that timeline when you visit it. You can return to your time, but you still need to deal with your alternate self where applicable. If you prevent your existence, you don't blink out, you're just orphaned from time (and incur a serious Transgression roll). You don't get to just let things snap back, and you deal with the consequences of your actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, the Guardian of Forever certainly have their role in <i>some</i> stories. I think it might be best of Genius' Time Travel rules were more Timey Wimey. Some Genii have rules that explain how time travel works, and, irritatingly, they are correct <i>some times</i>. Exception invariably occur which invalidate those models. Sometimes, pan-temporal Time Cops are putting their boot on your neck to &quot;protect the timeline&quot;. Other times, they don't exist and <i>never existed</i>. Kinda like the time waves in Achron - things keep changing.<br /> <br /> I do like as one commonly accepted outcome of &quot;Paradoxing&quot; yourself from the timeline is that it renders you a Mane, and further Havoc can completely erase you from the timeline, or turn you into some goatee wearing doppleganger.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T17:40:48-07:00","id":917658,"title":"","content":"I just realized something. The sorts of Experiments-as-Investigations that a Genius will be likely perform are going to be directed by their Catalysts, Aspirations <i>and</i> their Aesthetic. I believe the third should be expanded into a Worldview, which would be unique to each Genius and would provide them with a starter set of Experiments to perform and Plans to put into motion.<br /> <br /> For example, let's take a Worldview off the top of my head: Eco-friendliness. Experiments might include &quot;how do I fix the town's factories&quot;. The Clues (or Data) you get by following this could be applied to a relevant roll such as Intelligence + Science, with additional modifiers based on the current list for Investigations. What I'd like to see is that the more penalties you inflict upon the Experiment (accidentally or not), the more Wondrous Beats you get should you Succeed. A Dramatic Failure should yield a similar quantity of Wondrous Beats, perhaps slightly larger to make up for narrative conflicts like alerting the police or becoming indebted to a shady Genius or Mane. These multiple Wondrous Beats could be granted via thematically appropriate Persistent Conditions (we will probably need new ones to cover situations outside of Notoriety, Obsessed and such). This is meant to represent how Geniuses tend to pursue knowledge even when it would likely result in catastrophe.<br /> <br /> Another important aspect of Experiments would be how they differ from normal science. The latter is more preoccupied with the whys of nature, refutability, reproducibility and practicality. The former are more concerned with &quot;why nots&quot;, novelty, passion and creativity. For example: why not find a way to hybridize positive servile spirits and plants to revolutionize the food industry? The Data you receive as you follow your Plan and perform the Experiments (even if they are not strictly true according to other splats' metaphysics or mundane physics) can be incorporated into Wonders that match your Worldview.<br /> <br /> Does this sound like viable gameplay? How would we represent changes in Worldview?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 06-19-2016, 08:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T00:13:10-07:00","id":917843,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Hey, just wanted to note that we're pretty interested in the Genius project over at the <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Dragon Rekindled</span></a></b> project. Whoever's rebooting this one should feel free to contact us if they want advice on what we're doing and how we're doing it, or if they'd liked to collaborate on crossovers and stuff...<br /> <br /> We're full of advice and ideas, us... I guess that's to be expected of people trying to make a game about living fantasies with the quality of the main-line books...</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T04:37:06-07:00","id":917947,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10120_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10120\" data-vbnamecard=\"10120\">RockstarRaccoon</a> I'll keep that in mind.<br /> <br /> I think I saw a comment about the Peerage vs Lemuria conflict being too similar to Pentacle vs Seers. I agree somewhat, but how do we address that? How about making each city with a lot of Geniuses have a different distribution of Foundations/Baramins/Fellowships, resulting in distinct power plays with no standard good/bad guy factions? Or would that be too much like Vampire?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T04:42:40-07:00","id":917951,"title":"","content":"I do like having the Peerage as a unified group that squabbles, but still prefers each-other to an alternative group. It puts me in mind of a bunch of university departments squabbling over funding, but occasionally getting together to bitch about those bastards at the Sunshine Coast University in the next town over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4968-mrbreaksit","name":"MrBreaksIt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T06:39:58-07:00","id":917993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=917947#post917947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10120_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10120\" data-vbnamecard=\"10120\">RockstarRaccoon</a> I'll keep that in mind.<br /> <br /> I think I saw a comment about the Peerage vs Lemuria conflict being too similar to Pentacle vs Seers. I agree somewhat, but how do we address that? How about making each city with a lot of Geniuses have a different distribution of Foundations/Baramins/Fellowships, resulting in distinct power plays with no standard good/bad guy factions? Or would that be too much like Vampire?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, one distinction is that the Peerage &quot;won&quot;, in so much as they <i>could</i> have destroyed Lemuria. They didn't because they know Lemuria was ultimately essential to their own survival. I can also see a more &quot;cordial&quot; set of relations between the two groups, afterwards. They may not like each other, but they can tolerate each other. At least, to the extent most Genii can tolerate others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T07:03:15-07:00","id":918012,"title":"","content":"It is, after all, hard to make friends when no-one appreciates the full extent of your genius.<br /> I do like the idea of a truce between Lemuria and the Peerage, or rather, the organised surrender of Lemuria to the Peerage, treaty of Versailles style.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4968-mrbreaksit","name":"MrBreaksIt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T08:12:50-07:00","id":918049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=917521#post917521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Maybe we should have freeform, on-the-fly reconfiguration be a universal thing (maybe using Kitbashing).</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Maybe Kitbashing can allow you to temporarily swap around Postulates for less rigid and recipe-like Wonder creation? It should still be an improvisational technique, so the less mechanics for it, the better.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">As for your observations on time travel, I agree. It should be easier to change the timeline(s), but still very dangerous. The lack of regulation would help with that, and it would force each time traveler to deal with the consequences on their own. While I do like the idea of becoming a Mane after erasing yourself from time, I prefer that as a Persistent Condition, rather a permanent change written down on the character sheet. This Condition would be Resolved by fixing your mistakes the hard way: going back and undoing all that work, while paying attention so you don't mess up again.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=917993#post917993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, one distinction is that the Peerage &quot;won&quot;, in so much as they <i>could</i> have destroyed Lemuria. They didn't because they know Lemuria was ultimately essential to their own survival. I can also see a more &quot;cordial&quot; set of relations between the two groups, afterwards. They may not like each other, but they can tolerate each other. At least, to the extent most Genii can tolerate others.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the idea of conflicts between the Peerage and Lemuria being more cordial and resource-based, rather than philosophical and cosmic like Diamond vs Seers. The tone of 1ED implies a more or less uniform anger towards Lemuria on part of the Peerage, which seemed unnecessarily restrictive to me. I would also like to see both factions co-operating more often than the Diamond and Seers, who apparently only put their differences aside when one of the Bound is escaping. I personally imagine the Peers and Lemurians going so far as to keep score boards and lotteries about their Wondrous achievements. In other words, I see them more as rivals and <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/FriendlyEnemy\" target=\"_blank\"><b>friendly enemies</b></a>. They still become flat-out enemies on occasion, though.<br /> <br /> Something I want to see about rivalries between Genii is more focus on groups outside academia. Street gangs, techno-religious leaders, indie artists, wanna-be political revolutionaries and such. Maybe even a few pointers on how to incorporate the history and science of a city into a cool setting, kinda like how Freeholds in 2ED use fables and folklore to create the Courts and their Bulwark.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T20:14:18-07:00","id":918924,"title":"","content":"So, I don't really know much about this game, though I do hope a 2nd edition version gets pulled off,but I was curious; how much monkeying around with the rules would I have to do if I wanted to make a Mad Botanist who creates an array of sapient killer plant minions to serve him, as a shout out to Plants vs. Zombies?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T20:58:07-07:00","id":918930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=918924#post918924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I don't really know much about this game, though I do hope a 2nd edition version gets pulled off,but I was curious; how much monkeying around with the rules would I have to do if I wanted to make a Mad Botanist who creates an array of sapient killer plant minions to serve him, as a shout out to Plants vs. Zombies?</div> </div> </div> </div>Almost none at all. It can be covered pretty easily with a few dots in Exilixi and Automata.<br /> <br /> Like for reals, Genii give Mages a run for their money as far as versatility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T06:34:47-07:00","id":919066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=918930#post918930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Almost none at all. It can be covered pretty easily with a few dots in Exilixi and Automata.<br /> <br /> Like for reals, Genii give Mages a run for their money as far as versatility.</div> </div> </div> </div>And projectile or more dedicated weaponry can be added with Katastrofi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T13:38:15-07:00","id":919296,"title":"","content":"Huh, really? I figured at the very least the karma meter would probably get in the way of doing something like that. Thank you for correcting my false assumptions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T14:46:22-07:00","id":919325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=919296#post919296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh, really? I figured at the very least the karma meter would probably get in the way of doing something like that. Thank you for correcting my false assumptions.</div> </div> </div> </div> Maybe the new Progenitors can give a benefit to members that allows them to ignore Obligation checks for simply creating sapient Wonders (which is a &quot;sin&quot; against Obligation at 6 dots)?<br /> <br /> You know what, 1ED Obligation seriously restrains possibilities for any Genius that wants to experiment more while keeping sane. I think we should throw out the concept of &quot;sin&quot;, like the other Integrity analogues did in 2ED.<br /> <br /> Another thing that I'd change is Favored/Non-Favored Axioms. They work more like speed bumps than anything else, and do not emphasize your proficiency with an Axiom very well. How about we scratch out the speed bump of Non-Favored, and add these benefits to the Favored:<br /> <br /> 1) Every time you buy a dot in this Axiom, you gain an additional Postulate and a free Wonder (whose Rank can be lower than the one you currently have*).<br /> <br /> 2) Instead of +1 <i><u>only</u></i> to the Wonder creation roll, you gain an Interdisciplinary Specialty with Area Of Expertise regarding the Axiom, which can be applied to rolls such as repairing, modifying, creating, sabotaging, aiming, etc. You may ignore the prerequisites these Merits normally have.<br /> <br /> *By picking a more basic but versatile Wonder, you would get a bonus of +1 to +3 on activation rolls, which would stack with benefit number 2 mentioned above for a cool maximum of +5. For maximum effect, you may allow the 9 Again and Rote Quality of Professional Training on rolls to utilize Wonders and any other relevant actions, <u><i>except</i></u> creating them. For bonuses on the creation roll, you need resources like Laboratory Equipment, Blueprints, Beholden/Inspired assistants and Larvae.<br /> <br /> This way, Geniuses can create advanced Wonders earlier, or experiment more with less advanced ones and other combinations of Postulates before moving on to the bigger projects. Come to think of it, that would be a cool name for mad science related Plans: Projects.<br /> <br /> I would also change Jabir. As it is, the penalty is not that harsh and increases very slowly with Inspiration. Rather than just changing it to a fixed -[Inspiration/2 round up], I think it should be a Persistent Condition that interacts with Social Maneuvering fast and loose. It could add Doors and worsen Impressions, but if you keep your Obligation in check (not necessarily high), get the right Merits/Equipment and plan ahead, Jabir should be possible to temporarily cancel out or at least mitigate (the Temporarily Sane Condition posted eariler would represent this well). However, Jabir should always be looming over the Genius' head, tempting him with outrage, self-isolation and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T14:47:21-07:00","id":919326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=919296#post919296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh, really? I figured at the very least the karma meter would probably get in the way of doing something like that. Thank you for correcting my false assumptions.</div> </div> </div> </div>As long as you aren't making them sentient (in which case, you get dinged for Slavery), it's only a minor hit, if any.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T15:48:29-07:00","id":919352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=919325#post919325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Maybe the new Progenitors can give a benefit to members that allows them to ignore Obligation checks for simply creating sapient Wonders (which is a &quot;sin&quot; against Obligation at 6 dots)?<br /> <br /> You know what, 1ED Obligation seriously restrains possibilities for any Genius that wants to experiment more while keeping sane. I think we should throw out the concept of &quot;sin&quot;, like the other Integrity analogues did in 2ED.</div> </div> </div> </div>I cannot give my support to this idea strongly enough. All too often, karma meters in NWoD are just... bad. 2e has made some stellar leaps with the idea, particularly Cover, baseline Integrity and especially Harmony, but all too often the idea is ultimately a punishment system. It's like the very worst aspects of AD&amp;D's alignment system mixed with the Powers Checks of Ravenloft.<br /> <br /> I've argued before that Obligation shouldn't &quot;work&quot; as a conventional morality system, and particularly that it shouldn't force Genii to interact with mortals when all that really does is hurt them both. At the very least, losing the idea of &quot;sins&quot; is a good place to start.<br /> <br /> You have no idea how <i>sick</i> I got of seeing each 1e karma meter be &quot;Morality, oh, but with some extra special sins tacked on&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T16:23:53-07:00","id":919367,"title":"","content":"\u200b<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4488_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4488\" data-vbnamecard=\"4488\">malonkey1</a>: can you two please offer your thoughts on my previous post? I wanted to address how Geniuses could become more powerful/effective so as to compete with the other splats in 2ED. I have a feeling my grasp of crunch is not helping a lot, however.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, do you two like the idea of Kitbashing allowing the temporary swapping around of Postulates for more spontaneous and free form Wonder creation?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 06-22-2016, 07:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T17:05:29-07:00","id":919384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=919367#post919367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4488_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4488\" data-vbnamecard=\"4488\">malonkey1</a>: can you two please offer your thoughts on my previous post? I wanted to address how Geniuses could become more powerful/effective so as to compete with the other splats in 2ED. I have a feeling my grasp of crunch is not helping a lot, however.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, do you two like the idea of Kitbashing allowing the temporary swapping around of Postulates for more spontaneous and free form Wonder creation?</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems like a good idea. It makes Wonders more immediately versatile without rendering them too overpowered. Maybe have them suffer Havoc after the scene ends?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T17:22:07-07:00","id":919392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=919384#post919384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems like a good idea. It makes Wonders more immediately versatile without rendering them too overpowered. Maybe have them suffer Havoc after the scene ends?</div> </div> </div> </div> I like that idea. Do you think there should be a limit on how often Kitbashing is possible? I'd go for a limit based on Mania expenditure.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T17:29:10-07:00","id":919397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=919392#post919392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I like that idea. Do you think there should be a limit on how often Kitbashing is possible? I'd go for a limit based on Mania expenditure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Mania already puts a limit on Kitbashing. You're only going to be doing so much before you need to go into Deep Inspiration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T19:30:49-07:00","id":919451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=919325#post919325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Maybe the new Progenitors can give a benefit to members that allows them to ignore Obligation checks for simply creating sapient Wonders (which is a &quot;sin&quot; against Obligation at 6 dots)?<br /> <br /> You know what, 1ED Obligation seriously restrains possibilities for any Genius that wants to experiment more while keeping sane. I think we should throw out the concept of &quot;sin&quot;, like the other Integrity analogues did in 2ED.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, in general. Though I do feel it should track &quot;crimes against science/humanity&quot; at least <i>somewhat</i>. Would it be all that much of a change to recast it into a &quot;fucks given&quot; meter? Low Obligation doesn't mean you are a serial killer, it just means you <i>don't care</i>. Or is that not really different enough?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=919325#post919325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another thing that I'd change is Favored/Non-Favored Axioms. They work more like speed bumps than anything else, and do not emphasize your proficiency with an Axiom very well. How about we scratch out the speed bump of Non-Favored, and add these benefits to the Favored:<br /> <br /> 1) Every time you buy a dot in this Axiom, you gain an additional Postulate and a free Wonder (whose Rank can be lower than the one you currently have*).<br /> <br /> 2) Instead of +1 <i><u>only</u></i> to the Wonder creation roll, you gain an Interdisciplinary Specialty with Area Of Expertise regarding the Axiom, which can be applied to rolls such as repairing, modifying, creating, sabotaging, aiming, etc. You may ignore the prerequisites these Merits normally have.<br /> <br /> *By picking a more basic but versatile Wonder, you would get a bonus of +1 to +3 on activation rolls, which would stack with benefit number 2 mentioned above for a cool maximum of +5. For maximum effect, you may allow the 9 Again and Rote Quality of Professional Training on rolls to utilize Wonders and any other relevant actions, <u><i>except</i></u> creating them. For bonuses on the creation roll, you need resources like Laboratory Equipment, Blueprints, Beholden/Inspired assistants and Larvae.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm in favor of this in general (if still uncertain about the specific). I've always liked a bit more specific &quot;oomph&quot; to splats than just a boring XP discount.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=919325#post919325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would also change Jabir. As it is, the penalty is not that harsh and increases very slowly with Inspiration. Rather than just changing it to a fixed -[Inspiration/2 round up], I think it should be a Persistent Condition that interacts with Social Maneuvering fast and loose. It could add Doors and worsen Impressions, but if you keep your Obligation in check (not necessarily high), get the right Merits/Equipment and plan ahead, Jabir should be possible to temporarily cancel out or at least mitigate (the Temporarily Sane Condition posted eariler would represent this well). However, Jabir should always be looming over the Genius' head, tempting him with outrage, self-isolation and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds good. Need more details to really comment, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T19:33:45-07:00","id":919452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=919451#post919451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agreed, in general. Though I do feel it should track &quot;crimes against science/humanity&quot; at least <i>somewhat</i>. Would it be all that much of a change to recast it into a &quot;fucks given&quot; meter? Low Obligation doesn't mean you are a serial killer, it just means you <i>don't care</i>. Or is that not really different enough?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds good to me. High Obligation makes you Reed Richards, low Obligation makes you Rick Sanchez.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T20:02:18-07:00","id":919468,"title":"","content":"Okay, so, I wanted to try and be useful, but here's my own random ideas on the matter. I'm not caught up in all the nuances of the game or in what's happened in the past few pages of the topic, so apologies if I'm reinventing the wheel with any of this stuff.<br /> <br /> <br /> I really would move away from the whole &quot;consensual (un)reality&quot; explanation for Mania. It really feels, as other posters have noted, like a hamfisted MtAscen fanboyism/anti-MtAwak effort. I think that &quot;why does Mad Science work for us, and not for anyone else&quot; should be one of the big mysteries of the game. Maybe Geniuses are somehow acting as nodes for the occultic infrastructure of the God Machine. Maybe their gadgets are nothing but shells for some kind of metaphysical energy. Maybe Geniuses are walking rifts in reality, their brains attuned to alien otherworlds where the laws of physics work differently, and they can shove aside our reality to let their own come through. Whatever they really are, they shouldn't know, and they should try to explain that with many different theories.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Sanity Meter desperately needs an overhaul. I've always been a fan of the more alien morality meters in 1e - Harmony and Synergy - and a huge supporter of how 2e has drastically changed the klaptrap &quot;Alignment and yet not&quot; system that was Morality. And to me, at least, it makes a ton of sense that Mad Scientists should be truly alien in nature.<br /> <br /> When I think of a Mad Scientist splat, I think of Blue and Orange Morality. To be a Genius means that you inherently <i><i>don't <b><b>think</b></b> like everyone else does</i></i>. That's why you're a MAD scientist. Even the sanest and most stable Genius is still viewing the world from a mental paradigm that mundies would find unnaturally askew. This really builds on that trope about intelligence causing social isolation, and that's what the Genius Sanity Meter should play to.<br /> <br /> I picture a &quot;High Sanity&quot; Genius as being like the New Series Doctor, or certain incarnations of the Classic Doctor; friendly enough, wanting to do good, and usually tries to remember that other people don't think the way he does, but still tending to be... quirky at best. There's always that barrier between the Doctor and whoever he interacts with; his way of looking at the world isn't their way. Think of that episode for the...10th Doctor, I think it was, where Torchwood is founded because Queen Victoria, after seeing the Doctor's attitude towards the werewolf he saved her from, declares he's insane and as dangerous as any monster.<br /> <br /> &quot;Obligation&quot;, then, should cover just how well a Genius can bring themselves to remember that their minds are broken in comparison to human minds... and, more importantly, how well they can bring themselves to <b><b>care</b></b>. As Obligation goes down, Geniuses should becoming increasingly dismissive of humans as actually meaning anything; human opinions, human morals, human <b><b>lives</b></b> are increasingly devoid of consideration as a Genius spirals into the all-consuming light of Mania.<br /> <br /> Essentially, I think is close to what was literally posted as I was writing this; &quot;Obligation measures your Fucks Given About Human Views/Problems&quot;. Which is actually a pretty good &quot;Obligation basis&quot;, in my eyes. The Harmony style, where your karma/sanity meter tends to flux wildly over the course of even a given game, feels much more mad scientist to me than the &quot;hanging onto your soul for grim death&quot; style of, say, Humanity - you can still try to play your Genius clinging to high Obligation, you're just not screwed over if the Storyteller decides that you shouldn't have yelled at that kid for not running out of the way of your Mobile Fortress even when you told him to.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not a huge fan of the &quot;force Geniuses to get out with mundies&quot; parts of the 1e Obligation meter, either. It just doesn't make a lot of sense for Mad Scientists. In all honesty, I think it makes more sense that Geniuses actually have a Torment esque mechanic, where interacting with mundies too much or on too high a level is <i>bad for them</i>, in that it forces them to try and mesh their broken worldview against the human worldview, until the clash drives them into destructive outbursts of frustration. This is where you get your &quot;They called me mad! I'll show them!&quot; berserk tantrums from.<br /> <br /> Doing it this way also enforces the masquerade; not only do Wonders break down from human contact, but Geniuses themselves actively <i>avoid</i> mass human contact, for the sake of their own definition of sanity.<br /> <br /> Besides which, mad scientists usually hang around with only a small handful of &quot;normals&quot; in such works, anyway; look at the Doctor and his small but ever-changing number of companions, or Girl Genius where this is a grand total of ONE major occurring character who isn't either a Spark or touched by SCIENCE in some way - I'm talking about Moloch, specifically.<br /> <br /> <br /> I vaguely recall that at one point, it was mentioned that the current need to put dots into various levels of Axioms rather hinders players. Perhaps we can examine a new way of handling that?<br /> <br /> For example, rather than sufficient dots in Axiom = specific building options unlocked, what if we go for the idea of a more &quot;universal&quot; power level? Omnidisciplinary Scientist is a trope applied to mad scientists for a reason, after all. With this, your general &quot;IQ Rank&quot; determines what kinds of stuff you can build, and you can freely access all of the Axioms. In this case, specific affinities based on X/Y Splats translate as a boost to &quot;IQ&quot; when you're working with a specific Axiom.<br /> <br /> So, essentially, all Genii can make use of Wonders that use the Katastrofi Axiom, but Grimm are far more capable of unlocking its full potential.<br /> <br /> Sound like it could work? Or is this too out there, even compared to Beasts and their Satiety/Avatisms/Nightmares methodology?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T00:47:23-07:00","id":919574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=919468#post919468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, rather than sufficient dots in Axiom = specific building options unlocked, what if we go for the idea of a more &quot;universal&quot; power level? Omnidisciplinary Scientist is a trope applied to mad scientists for a reason, after all. With this, your general &quot;IQ Rank&quot; determines what kinds of stuff you can build, and you can freely access all of the Axioms. In this case, specific affinities based on X/Y Splats translate as a boost to &quot;IQ&quot; when you're working with a specific Axiom.<br /> <br /> So, essentially, all Genii can make use of Wonders that use the Katastrofi Axiom, but Grimm are far more capable of unlocking its full potential.<br /> <br /> Sound like it could work? Or is this too out there, even compared to Beasts and their Satiety/Avatisms/Nightmares methodology?</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't this more or less exactly what we decided on doing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4968-mrbreaksit","name":"MrBreaksIt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T13:15:21-07:00","id":919897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrBreaksIt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=919574#post919574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't this more or less exactly what we decided on doing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Less? Current trend of thought is to still have ranked Axioms, it's just each dot gives you a free Postulate, and you need to purchase the others separately. Some Postulates might require the Axiom at a certain rank/dot to pick up.<br /> <br /> Should we start coming up with actual lists of Postulates so we have a better idea of how it would look?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T14:45:31-07:00","id":924108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=919897#post919897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Less? Current trend of thought is to still have ranked Axioms, it's just each dot gives you a free Postulate, and you need to purchase the others separately. Some Postulates might require the Axiom at a certain rank/dot to pick up.<br /> <br /> Should we start coming up with actual lists of Postulates so we have a better idea of how it would look?</div> </div> </div> </div> Let me try to come up with a quick list of possible Postulates for one Axiom:<br /> <br /> <br /> <i><b>Apokalypsi:</b></i><ul><li>1 dot: Data Retrieval, Data Analysis</li> <li>2 dots: The Five Types Of Scanning Mentioned In The Book, Revealing Telepathy, Projective Telepathy, Computer Telepathy, Universal Translation, Binoculars/Microphones/Night Vision</li> <li>3 dots: Pinpoint The Location Of Objects/Subjects/Phenomena, Forming Maps And Models, Scrying</li> <li>4 dots: Probability Calculation, Messages Through Disconnected Mediums, Extradimensional Scanning</li> <li>5 dots: Reveal Any Information And Detect Anything Within Range</li> </ul>The distribution of Postulates is quite assymetrical between the dots. I am doubting if it's feasible to really mimic the symmetry of Gifts &amp; Facets, unless we fold a lot of Postulates together, which would be very complicated. The fifth dot is way too broad as well, but I don't know what could replace it. The Binoculars/Microphones/Night Vision style Wonders should go into the first dot.<br /> <br /> We also need to streamline the list of Core Modifiers and Axiom Modifiers.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T14:56:21-07:00","id":924114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=924108#post924108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Let me try to come up with a quick list of possible Postulates for one Axiom:<br /> <br /> <br /> <i><b>Apokalypsi:</b></i><ul><li>1 dot: Data Retrieval, Data Analysis</li> <li>2 dots: The Five Types Of Scanning Mentioned In The Book, Revealing Telepathy, Projective Telepathy, Computer Telepathy, Universal Translation, Binoculars/Microphones/Night Vision</li> <li>3 dots: Pinpoint The Location Of Objects/Subjects/Phenomena, Forming Maps And Models, Scrying</li> <li>4 dots: Probability Calculation, Messages Through Disconnected Mediums, Extradimensional Scanning</li> <li>5 dots: Reveal Any Information And Detect Anything Within Range</li> </ul><br /> The distribution of Postulates is quite assymetrical between the dots. I am doubting if it's feasible to really mimic the symmetry of Gifts &amp; Facets, unless we fold a lot of Postulates together, which would be very complicated. The fifth dot is way too broad as well, but I don't know what could replace it. The Binoculars/Microphones/Night Vision style Wonders should go into the first dot.<br /> <br /> We also need to streamline the list of Core Modifiers and Axiom Modifiers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd generalize &quot;Night Vision/etc.&quot; to Sensory Amplification. I'd also add Observable Criteria Trigger to the fist dot. That would be used for Retinal Scans, Motion Detection, etc. when combined with Automata.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking Apokalypsi 1 would basically be anything detection related with modern science. 2 might include more esoteric (but still essentially basic) scanning, with 3, 4 and 5 being abstract and extreme distance scanning.<br /> <br /> Regarding Postulates, I was thinking something like:<br /> <br /> Improved Vision \u2022<br /> <br /> Twilight Vision \u2022\u2022<br /> Prerequisites: Improved Vision \u2022, Occult 1+<br /> <br /> Shadow Detection \u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> Prerequisites: Twilight Vision \u2022\u2022, Occult 2+<br /> <br /> The \u2022s after the name are the minimum Apokalypsi required. Some may have other dependencies, though, unrelated to Axiom dots. This theoretically could support multiple \u2022 Postulates that nevertheless require other Postulates of the same dot level. The Genius wouldn't need to increase the Axiom rating, but still need to fulfill the pre-reqs (if progression needed to be slowed).<br /> <br /> You could also restrict Postulate effects to their potential pre-reqs, so the 5 dot &quot;Omniscience&quot; of Apokalypsi might only be able to detect observable phenomena and Twilight, but not the Shadow or other supernaturals, if you lacked those Postulates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 06-30-2016, 06:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T15:01:35-07:00","id":924119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=924114#post924114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd generalize &quot;Night Vision/etc.&quot; to Sensory Amplification. I'd also add Observable Criteria Trigger to the fist dot. That would be used for Retinal Scans, Motion Detection, etc. when combined with Automata.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking Apokalypsi 1 would basically be anything detection related with modern science. 2 might include more esoteric (but still essentially basic) scanning, with 3, 4 and 5 being abstract and extreme distance scanning.</div> </div> </div> </div> So, how many Postulates are we aiming for with each Axiom dot? I do like the idea of Apokalypsi 5 letting you scan vast areas and distances. Maybe the fifth dot lets you combine the Postulates of the third and fourth dots?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T15:47:12-07:00","id":924143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=924119#post924119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So, how many Postulates are we aiming for with each Axiom dot? I do like the idea of Apokalypsi 5 letting you scan vast areas and distances. Maybe the fifth dot lets you combine the Postulates of the third and fourth dots?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I can see it as a kind of &quot;upgrade&quot; of prior Postulates - it doesn't do much on its own, but expands prior capabilities to epic levels.<br /> <br /> Oh. I edited the prevoius post. Did you see the suggestions there yet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T16:03:02-07:00","id":924155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=924143#post924143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, I can see it as a kind of &quot;upgrade&quot; of prior Postulates - it doesn't do much on its own, but expands prior capabilities to epic levels.<br /> <br /> Oh. I edited the prevoius post. Did you see the suggestions there yet?</div> </div> </div> </div> I love that idea! It falls in line with the other systems for powers in 2ED: later dots give new abilities and improve the previous ones.<br /> <br /> I believe we should move away from strictly mimicking Gifts &amp; Facets and focus on your suggestions instead. So, would Postulates cost 1 Wondrous Experience per dot? How do we justify the acquisition of new Axioms and Postulates in-universe?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T16:51:19-07:00","id":924171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=924155#post924155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I love that idea! It falls in line with the other systems for powers in 2ED: later dots give new abilities and improve the previous ones.<br /> <br /> I believe we should move away from strictly mimicking Gifts &amp; Facets and focus on your suggestions instead. So, would Postulates cost 1 Wondrous Experience per dot? How do we justify the acquisition of new Axioms and Postulates in-universe?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think maybe we have the Postualtes each be a flat 2 XP each (So, on par with skill Specialties, which seems fair), with the Axiomata themselves having a cost per each dot. Acquiring new Postulates and raising Axiomata can be justified as connecting of your paradigm with to that field of study. So a Grimm obsessed with Gestalt Consciousness would be able to add postcognition to his Apokalypsi repertoire under the idea of shared memory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T19:42:18-07:00","id":924242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=924171#post924171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think maybe we have the Postualtes each be a flat 2 XP each (So, on par with skill Specialties, which seems fair), with the Axiomata themselves having a cost per each dot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that sounds fair. Higher Axiom Ranks probably increases some modifier, and unlocks access to higher tier Postulates, but there is still plenty of room at the bottom for Genius to invest in. And it'll have payoffs further up the Axiom-Postulate tree.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=924171#post924171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Acquiring new Postulates and raising Axiomata can be justified as connecting of your paradigm with to that field of study. So a Grimm obsessed with Gestalt Consciousness would be able to add postcognition to his Apokalypsi repertoire under the idea of shared memory.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds good. However a Genius chooses to justify their crazy theories is up to them (and part of the fun).<br /> <hr /><br /> Thoughts regarding Postulate structure?<br /> <br /> <b>Name \u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: [if any]<br /> <b>Effect</b>: <br /> <b>Notes</b>: [if any]<br /> <br /> What about adding a [] type to Postulates, where the [] signifies that the Postulate has a kind of fill-in-the-blank designator? So <b>Incident Detection [Vampires] \u2022\u2022</b> would be an Apokalypsi Postulate that lets you detect the supernatural powers of vampires (like a Vampire-only Peripheral Mage Sight). <b>Energy Projectile [Electricity] \u2022</b> would be a Katastrofi Postulate that enables electrical energy to be projected at a distance. By using the [] designator, you let individual players and storytellers opt into whatever phenomena or sub classifications they wish, without them having to be spelled out in the rule-book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T07:54:41-07:00","id":924453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=924155#post924155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe we should move away from strictly mimicking Gifts &amp; Facets and focus on your suggestions instead. So, would Postulates cost 1 Wondrous Experience per dot? How do we justify the acquisition of new Axioms and Postulates in-universe?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mostly meant &quot;Gifts &amp; Facets&quot; In that there is a core thing (Gift or Axiom dot) that has other things tied to it (Facets or Postulates), and acquiring the first thing gets you one of the second things for free. Other than that, the similarity ends. Axioms are Ranked 1-5, and Postulates aren't restricted to only 5 per (due to there being no Renown). I suppose they are also close to 1E Promethean's Transmutations.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, tying Postulates to Axiom rank, restricts certain higher tier or more powerful effects to those who've invested heavily into it. Other prerequisites help to tie things together logically, and allow a Genius who hasn't heavily invested in an Axiom to still have things they can investigate/advance in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T07:42:52-07:00","id":924880,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Hey, Dragon Rekindled team leader here again.<br /> <br /> Does anyone who's on this project want to organize a Skype call sometime? We want to include Genius in our crossover rules (when we get to them), and we'd like to talk Genius 2nd Edition with you guys....</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T09:19:30-07:00","id":924904,"title":"","content":"About &quot;Postulates&quot; - why is it desirable to put hard limits on what a Genius can do? Mad scientists, as a trope, are all about overreaching - they go beyond the limits of morality and sanity, and are destroyed by the dangers they in their hubris dismissed. The Genius powerset should not, therefore, have predictable ladders of techniques to be mastered in order; instead it should be wide open from the start, but be balanced by risk to the Genius. Building Wonders you don't really understand should be not just possible, but basically routine - with a very real possibility of blowing yourself up every time you do it. Progress in studying Axioms shouldn't expand what you can do, but reduce the risks involved in doing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T11:16:30-07:00","id":924957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=924904#post924904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About &amp;quot;Postulates&amp;quot; - why is it desirable to put hard limits on what a Genius can do? Mad scientists, as a trope, are all about overreaching - they go beyond the limits of morality and sanity, and are destroyed by the dangers they in their hubris dismissed. The Genius powerset should not, therefore, have predictable ladders of techniques to be mastered in order; instead it should be wide open from the start, but be balanced by risk to the Genius. Building Wonders you don't really understand should be not just possible, but basically routine - with a very real possibility of blowing yourself up every time you do it. Progress in studying Axioms shouldn't expand what you can do, but reduce the risks involved in doing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>How would be represented mechanically? Because there still needs to be guidelines. Even mage has guidelines. <br /> <br /> I could see something like with the &quot;fated&quot; Affinity option for Mummy, maybe. You spend less XP or Bound Mania and let the Storyteller decide (or randomly roll from a list) - even if the Genius doesn't actually possess the knowhow at the moment. A story might then entail researching the principle behind just what they made.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T11:18:32-07:00","id":924958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=924880#post924880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Hey, Dragon Rekindled team leader here again.<br /> <br /> Does anyone who's on this project want to organize a Skype call sometime? We want to include Genius in our crossover rules (when we get to them), and we'd like to talk Genius 2nd Edition with you guys....</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>And if there were a dev team as opposed to people just posting things to a thread, that might help...<br /> <br /> I don't even know who, if anyone, *is* the Genius team.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T11:51:16-07:00","id":924970,"title":"","content":"Ok, I haven't been following this thread but... Someone's actually compiling a ruleset, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T16:30:57-07:00","id":925094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=924957#post924957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would be represented mechanically? Because there still needs to be guidelines. Even mage has guidelines.</div> </div> </div> </div>As it happens I was thinking of Mage's Paradox/Reach system. Adding Reach to a spell makes it more potent, but it also increases a pool of Paradox dice that has to be rolled before the spell is cast. Every success on that roll changes the spell's effect in ways contrary to the mage's intent. This fits for Genii even better than for mages - the question when a Genius builds a Wonder isn't whether the Wonder does anything, but whether it does what the Genius wants it to. But it doesn't fit well with mechanics that split up the possible effects into hundreds of fine categories, each of which has to be acquired independently. Ideally I'd want a Storyteller to listen to a short description of a Wonder, compare it to the Axioms, give it ratings and set a dice pool for Havoc and a cost in Resources or weird materials in just a few minutes; the more finely graded the Axiom schema is, the harder it gets to do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T17:36:29-07:00","id":925129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=925094#post925094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As it happens I was thinking of Mage's Paradox/Reach system. Adding Reach to a spell makes it more potent, but it also increases a pool of Paradox dice that has to be rolled before the spell is cast. Every success on that roll changes the spell's effect in ways contrary to the mage's intent. This fits for Genii even better than for mages - the question when a Genius builds a Wonder isn't whether the Wonder does anything, but whether it does what the Genius wants it to. But it doesn't fit well with mechanics that split up the possible effects into hundreds of fine categories, each of which has to be acquired independently. Ideally I'd want a Storyteller to listen to a short description of a Wonder, compare it to the Axioms, give it ratings and set a dice pool for Havoc and a cost in Resources or weird materials in just a few minutes; the more finely graded the Axiom schema is, the harder it gets to do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>But how do you even arbitrate that? When a spell goes haywire, there are still guidelines given for that level of Arcana.<br /> <br /> With a random/haywire Wonder, even with Postulates, a Storyteller can just select *other* Postulates (or Faults).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T18:56:01-07:00","id":925162,"title":"","content":"So... is there anyone actually compiling this ruleset as you guys talk? I suggest someone at least start taking organized notes on what's being decided into a google doc, share editing of that with active members like GibberingEloquence and Malonkey1, and put it in the first post of the thread...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":10120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","user":"RockstarRaccoon","date":". 07-02-2016, 10:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T07:43:52-07:00","id":925333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=925129#post925129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But how do you even arbitrate that? When a spell goes haywire, there are still guidelines given for that level of Arcana.<br /> <br /> With a random/haywire Wonder, even with Postulates, a Storyteller can just select *other* Postulates (or Faults).</div> </div> </div> </div> We could add a mechanic to Deep Inspiration that lets you acquire Postulates for which you do not yet meet the Axiom prerequisites, with the risk of greater Havoc and an Unmada check. Kitbashing, on the other hand, would be comparatively safer, as it would swap around the Postulates you already purchased, allowing you to improvise a Wonder.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T07:50:54-07:00","id":925339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=925333#post925333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> We could add a mechanic to Deep Inspiration that lets you acquire Postulates for which you do not yet meet the Axiom prerequisites, with the risk of greater Havoc and an Unmada check. Kitbashing, on the other hand, would be comparatively safer, as it would swap around the Postulates you already purchased, allowing you to improvise a Wonder.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've got some mechanical ideas. Might need to wait until Monday, when I'm back at a computer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T14:53:36-07:00","id":925505,"title":"","content":"Here's a thought (from someone who really hasn't been following this project or even read Genius in the past few years), Geniuses are about making things, right? What if they can overstep the bounds of their Axiom by making, say, 2 3rd level things that make it possible for another 3rd level thing to do something that should normally only work at the 4th level? OR what if they can go use mundane science to supplement their mad science by building more normal stuff into their design? That's how I would try to get around the limitations of my level if I were playing a Genius.<br /> <br /> I'll note that when I play stuff like Genius, Mage, and similar things in other games, and my characters build things, I try and get the details in to make them as realistic as possible before resorting to it just working because &quot;Advanced Technology&quot; / &quot;Magic&quot;, so any design I'd make would probably do something like that. You guys might want to make sure your rules are taking that into consideration while you're thinking about that stuff...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T15:28:33-07:00","id":925530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=925505#post925505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a thought (from someone who really hasn't been following this project or even read Genius in the past few years), Geniuses are about making things, right? What if they can overstep the bounds of their Axiom by making, say, 2 3rd level things that make it possible for another 3rd level thing to do something that should normally only work at the 4th level? OR what if they can go use mundane science to supplement their mad science by building more normal stuff into their design? That's how I would try to get around the limitations of my level if I were playing a Genius.<br /> <br /> I'll note that when I play stuff like Genius, Mage, and similar things in other games, and my characters build things, I try and get the details in to make them as realistic as possible before resorting to it just working because &amp;quot;Advanced Technology&amp;quot; / &amp;quot;Magic&amp;quot;, so any design I'd make would probably do something like that. You guys might want to make sure your rules are taking that into consideration while you're thinking about that stuff...</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally, Wonders do stuff better, but mundane tech is more reliable and easier to come by. <br /> <br /> If you don't absolutely *need* a disintegrator, just use a gun. But some Genii still have problems with that. Cause of the the insanity and all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T16:37:07-07:00","id":925553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=925505#post925505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a thought (from someone who really hasn't been following this project or even read Genius in the past few years), Geniuses are about making things, right? What if they can overstep the bounds of their Axiom by making, say, 2 3rd level things that make it possible for another 3rd level thing to do something that should normally only work at the 4th level? OR what if they can go use mundane science to supplement their mad science by building more normal stuff into their design? That's how I would try to get around the limitations of my level if I were playing a Genius.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we mentioned something like that upthread. Deep Inspiration exists already in the rules, and with the Postulate system, I could see it being used to access Postulates you don't yet have at the cost of increased risk to life and limb.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'll note that when I play stuff like Genius, Mage, and similar things in other games, and my characters build things, I try and get the details in to make them as realistic as possible before resorting to it just working because &quot;Advanced Technology&quot; / &quot;Magic&quot;, so any design I'd make would probably do something like that. You guys might want to make sure your rules are taking that into consideration while you're thinking about that stuff... </div> </div> </div>I think that's something that can be easily abstracted out of the ruleset, honestly. The issue is that Geniuses explicitly work outside real science much of the time, so bending over backward to make it fit our understanding of reality is kind of at odds. I think it's more important in Genius to make sure a Genius's work is consistent with itself. So, for example, you couldn't have a Genius obsessed with luminiferous aether couldn't create a hologram that relied on light's wave/particle nature, since it would be going against his (incorrect but internally useful) understanding of how light worked.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T23:33:25-07:00","id":925757,"title":"","content":"Oh, I should clarify what I meant...<br /> <br /> I'm a technology consultant, so I like to draw detailed schematics for whatever contraptions my characters have/make. Because I don't have time to research the internal designs of most of the hardware I work with, I'm used to drawing in black boxes. With a Genius, I'd just draw things based on how I know they work, not worrying about reality or physics. I'm asking because I've had characters in sci-fi campaigns where I've given detailed explanations for the layouts and functioning of ships and energy-rifles and power-suits and all that, and I'd probably do that with this...<br /> <br /> Like I said though, don't take it as criticism or anything, just a note of how I'd play: I haven't had time to dig into Genius in the past few years, and may not for a while at this point...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T16:29:01-07:00","id":926142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=925757#post925757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I should clarify what I meant...<br /> <br /> I'm a technology consultant, so I like to draw detailed schematics for whatever contraptions my characters have/make. Because I don't have time to research the internal designs of most of the hardware I work with, I'm used to drawing in black boxes. With a Genius, I'd just draw things based on how I know they work, not worrying about reality or physics. I'm asking because I've had characters in sci-fi campaigns where I've given detailed explanations for the layouts and functioning of ships and energy-rifles and power-suits and all that, and I'd probably do that with this...<br /> <br /> Like I said though, don't take it as criticism or anything, just a note of how I'd play: I haven't had time to dig into Genius in the past few years, and may not for a while at this point...</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I get it. So what you meant wasn't &quot;realism&quot; so much as detail and consistency?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T17:01:20-07:00","id":926168,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I like to be able to draw out schematics for what my characters have. Most of my sheets have pictures of the characters in whatever sort of loadout they have, whether it be a description of a Knight's armor, or an explanation of a space-suit, or just the various places my detective has things hidden on her. Some of the more tinkery ones have actual designs for their gadgets, even if they don't make perfect sense. I've used this in the past to make odd contraptions like Samus's beam-cannon and a magical shield, and Genius sounds like a game I'd go crazy with.<br /> <br /> I'm not asking you to put in detailed schematic rules just yet, but I think you should keep in mind that some players / storytellers will use that sort of design methodology for exploiting fictional physics and making cool effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T17:59:44-07:00","id":926184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=926168#post926168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I like to be able to draw out schematics for what my characters have. Most of my sheets have pictures of the characters in whatever sort of loadout they have, whether it be a description of a Knight's armor, or an explanation of a space-suit, or just the various places my detective has things hidden on her. Some of the more tinkery ones have actual designs for their gadgets, even if they don't make perfect sense. I've used this in the past to make odd contraptions like Samus's beam-cannon and a magical shield, and Genius sounds like a game I'd go crazy with.<br /> <br /> I'm not asking you to put in detailed schematic rules just yet, but I think you should keep in mind that some players / storytellers will use that sort of design methodology for exploiting fictional physics and making cool effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, what's the level of detail you'd like to see?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T02:39:25-07:00","id":926335,"title":"","content":"I dunno man, I'm just saying how I'd use the book. Just make sure to be clear about how it works and I'm sure it'll be fine.<br /> <br /> What I'm REALLY here for is to try and build some collaboration between the books, that's all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T07:40:09-07:00","id":926398,"title":"","content":"@All: Is there anyone here assembling Genius 2E into a doc in an official capacity? If not, is there some Inspiration signal somewhere we can light, to summon the forum's craziest homebrewers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T14:43:25-07:00","id":926649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=926398#post926398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@All: Is there anyone here assembling Genius 2E into a doc in an official capacity?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I'm saying. You guys need to write this down before it becomes like what's happening with the last Embers thread: it's too hard to track and reference the discussions they were having there, because there aren't alot of notes in one spot, so there's a lack of information for whoever wasn't there for those talks. Someone should make a doc and start building a transitional ruleset.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T16:55:21-07:00","id":926721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=926398#post926398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@All: Is there anyone here assembling Genius 2E into a doc in an official capacity? If not, is there some Inspiration signal somewhere we can light, to summon the forum's craziest homebrewers?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll put together more formalized documents today and tomorrow if nobody more qualified wants to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T18:49:52-07:00","id":926764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=926721#post926721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll put together more formalized documents today and tomorrow if nobody more qualified wants to.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sounds good. I'd do it, but my time isn't reliable lately.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T01:11:39-07:00","id":926914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=926721#post926721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll put together more formalized documents today and tomorrow if nobody more qualified wants to.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll PM you my Google account, you can share me on it. I don't have alot of experience with Genius, nor do I have time outside of Dragon, but I'd be more than happy to offer some advice and some structural / editing help for you. The Dragon team is going to need to know what's up with Genius and the other books by the time we write our Crossover chapter, and I'd like to get the fan projects to talk to each other more in general, maybe get some coordinated effort down for our next releases...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T06:44:54-07:00","id":927022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=926398#post926398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">is there some Inspiration signal somewhere we can light, to summon the forum's craziest homebrewers?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, to send the signal you simply put <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar134_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"134\" data-vbnamecard=\"134\">The Kings Raven</a> in a post <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (going by total output either myself or LostLight holds the crown of craziest homebrewer).<br /> <br /> Anyway, congrats on getting to this point everyone and best of luck going forward. Also, for my curiosity, do you have a summery of what updates you're planning and your core direction for the themes and for wonders? (By wonders I mean, are you aiming geniuses with dozens of wonders or a few signature devices? Do you want general wonders like omni-sensors or specialized wonders like bio-scanners to be the default? - and what mechanics are you using to promote your choice)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 07-06-2016, 10:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T10:36:11-07:00","id":927159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=927022#post927022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, for my curiosity, do you have a summery of what updates you're planning and your core direction for the themes and for wonders? (By wonders I mean, are you aiming geniuses with dozens of wonders or a few signature devices?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm amenable to having either or both be workable, really.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do you want general wonders like omni-sensors or specialized wonders like bio-scanners to be the default? - and what mechanics are you using to promote your choice) </div> </div> </div>I think specialization is going to be more the default, considering the switch from the old Axiom system to the new Axiom-and-Postulates system making specialization within an Axiom easier. Plus, I think it'd be a good idea to make a lot of the Axiom-specific factors (e.g. Skafoi Ray) into Postulates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T11:08:46-07:00","id":927177,"title":"","content":"I have to say I feel honored. I never thought my post would become THE post for the new edition for Genius. I wish you the best guys. I love the game. Good luck. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T11:16:17-07:00","id":927182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=927159#post927159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think specialization is going to be more the default, considering the switch from the old Axiom system to the new Axiom-and-Postulates system making specialization within an Axiom easier. Plus, I think it'd be a good idea to make a lot of the Axiom-specific factors (e.g. Skafoi Ray) into Postulates.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, more specific in general is the ideal - <i>but</i> there being options to Kitbash or reconfigure existing Wonders at a cost let's you have the best of both worlds.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking there will more options for &quot;Genius pulls crazy out of their... hat&quot;. Kitbashing letting you switch around Postulates, Deep Inspiration for accessing Postulates (and Axiom ranks?) you don't possess (yet), etc. Wonders can be nice and safe(-ish), but when you need to, you can spin stuff up on the fly.<br /> <br /> Regarding Wonder numbers, I think the hybrid Wondrous XP and Bound Mania supports either style. You can either use a mix to support an arsenal, or sink a bunch of effort into a few signature devices/formulae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T11:45:19-07:00","id":927199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=927022#post927022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, for my curiosity, do you have a summery of what updates you're planning and your core direction for the themes and for wonders?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the kind of thing I'm asking them to build. Right now it feels like this is in the &quot;just an idea&quot; phase, and the people here have yet to commit to whether or not they're actually going to do this. A set of notes for things like this would really help with that...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T14:59:48-07:00","id":927290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=927159#post927159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think specialization is going to be more the default, considering the switch from the old Axiom system to the new Axiom-and-Postulates system making specialization within an Axiom easier. Plus, I think it'd be a good idea to make a lot of the Axiom-specific factors (e.g. Skafoi Ray) into Postulates.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=927182#post927182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, more specific in general is the ideal - <i>but</i> there being options to Kitbash or reconfigure existing Wonders at a cost let's you have the best of both worlds.</div> </div> </div> </div> A best of both worlds is a good idea.<br /> <br /> I've been reading up on your Postulates and I have a suggestion. Rather than making them cost exp, why not do them like Mage's Reach, each Axiom Dot automatically unlocks a long list of Postulates but each has a reach cost and one or more associated mental skills. Your Reach is based on those Mental Skills rather than for Dots in Axioms. That would be a very mechanically easy way to create a clear distinction between the biologist, the physicist, the mechanic, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=927182#post927182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm thinking there will more options for &quot;Genius pulls crazy out of their... hat&quot;. Kitbashing letting you switch around Postulates,</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm... more options for pulling crazy out the hat is a must. But from memory in fiction there's mad scientists who rarely kitbash (e.g. The Doctor) and mad scientists that kitbash new wonders fall the time (most Sparks). But I can't think of many kitbashing by changing the core function of wonders on the fly.<br /> <br /> What was the reason for changing kitbashing from making new wonders to reworking old wonders?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=927182#post927182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Deep Inspiration for accessing Postulates (and Axiom ranks?) you don't possess (yet), etc. Wonders can be nice and safe(-ish), but when you need to, you can spin stuff up on the fly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds good. Mad Scientist has a new idea for an invention and cannot stop themselves building it is a common trope (Agetha's coffee machine for example). If the Obsession or the Magnum Opus provided a key advantage to Deep Inspiration (maybe dialing it down from really dangerous to just dangerous) you'd perfectly replicate the trope.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=927159#post927159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm amenable to having either or both be workable, really.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=927182#post927182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding Wonder numbers, I think the hybrid Wondrous XP and Bound Mania supports either style. You can either use a mix to support an arsenal, or sink a bunch of effort into a few signature devices/formulae.</div> </div> </div> </div>A quick search reveals that you don't have a pricing system for Wondrous XP yet, so I can't really comment.<br /> <br /> My suggestion is to start by identifying key mad scientists in fiction; and when they aquire new wonders and when they loose old wonders. Once you've done that then you can design a system and make sure it supports all of them, without any of the playsyles being mechanically sub-optimal (a little sub-optimility is fine, but too much is a bad thing).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 07-06-2016, 06:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T17:32:29-07:00","id":927367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=927290#post927290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A best of both worlds is a good idea.<br /> <br /> I've been reading up on your Postulates and I have a suggestion. Rather than making them cost exp, why not do them like Mage's Reach, each Axiom Dot automatically unlocks a long list of Postulates but each has a reach cost and one or more associated mental skills. Your Reach is based on those Mental Skills rather than for Dots in Axioms. That would be a very mechanically easy way to create a clear distinction between the biologist, the physicist, the mechanic, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. Maybe. Would cut down on the XP sink. Could also make those skills requirements. Hmmm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=927290#post927290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm... more options for pulling crazy out the hat is a must. But from memory in fiction there's mad scientists who rarely kitbash (e.g. The Doctor) and mad scientists that kitbash new wonders fall the time (most Sparks). But I can't think of many kitbashing by changing the core function of wonders on the fly.<br /> <br /> What was the reason for changing kitbashing from making new wonders to reworking old wonders?</div> </div> </div> </div>Kitbashing is still &quot;create a one Scene Wonder on the fly&quot;. I meant you might be able to switch around which Postulates you &quot;have&quot; to build it with (if the above Reach method isn't used). And being able to change an existing Wonder thing would be another ability. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=927290#post927290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds good. Mad Scientist has a new idea for an invention and cannot stop themselves building it is a common trope (Agetha's coffee machine for example). If the Obsession or the Magnum Opus provided a key advantage to Deep Inspiration (maybe dialing it down from really dangerous to just dangerous) you'd perfectly replicate the trope.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reducing risk if it aligns with your Obsession/Magnum Opus is a good idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=927290#post927290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A quick search reveals that you don't have a pricing system for Wondrous XP yet, so I can't really comment.<br /> <br /> My suggestion is to start by identifying key mad scientists in fiction; and when they aquire new wonders and when they loose old wonders. Once you've done that then you can design a system and make sure it supports all of them, without any of the playsyles being mechanically sub-optimal (a little sub-optimility is fine, but too much is a bad thing).</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking maybe 1 Wondrous XP = 1 Bound Mania to keep things simple. You could phase in Wondrous XP to stabilize Wonders so you don't need to bind Mania to them (or keep it bound for additional effect, like the 1E 2x Mania for no Fault).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T02:01:51-07:00","id":927503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=927367#post927367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking maybe 1 Wondrous XP = 1 Bound Mania to keep things simple. You could phase in Wondrous XP to stabilize Wonders so you don't need to bind Mania to them (or keep it bound for additional effect, like the 1E 2x Mania for no Fault).</div> </div> </div> </div>If you work out the XP -&gt; Mania ratio from 1E using Assembly Line and Foundations as a guideline that's actually a really bad ratio.<br /> <br /> Like I said, the question is which iconic mad scientists have a whole arsenal of gadgets. With a name or two you could examine them properly and create mechanics to model them.<br /> <br /> The reason I bring this up is because I'm worried that extra bound mania would just become an exp sink where even Geniuses with a few signature Wonders feel the need to buy it because more Mania is always a good thing. If we had specific mad scientists to work with then the mechanic could be narrowed down from just throwing extra Mania at Geniuses into replicating a specific trope.<br /> <br /> For example the iconic name for an arsenel of gadget is Batman*, but aside from a few core Wonders (Batsuit, Batmobile, Batplane, batarangs and Batgrappling hook) most of his gadgets appear only occasionally and quite often only once. If I was to represent Batman I wouldn't give him a ton of extra bound mania, I'd give him a Merit called Crazy Prepared that says once per session he can turn out to already have taken a Wonder he needs out of storage and has it on his person. (Assuming that Geniuses have a way of storing Wonders where they don't Bind Mania)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *My knowledge of Batman is mostly the Justice League cartoon and the Batman: the Brave and the Bold cartoon","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 07-07-2016, 05:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T02:45:39-07:00","id":927514,"title":"","content":"Here's a tip about deciding on which mechanic or element to go with: figure out some internal systems of how it's supposed to work 1) narratively, 2) mechanically, and 3) lore-wise, so that you can you can make your decisions based on internal consistency. Sometimes you'll have parts where it's like &quot;which of the 2 proposed mechanics should we use?&quot; and the answer is &quot;What fits with the existing idea of what's going on?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T07:32:29-07:00","id":927608,"title":"","content":"Hello everyone! I am pretty new to the Genius but I've been reading development on this thread with star eyed excitement and wanted to share some of my own ideas and insight with the group. Unfortunately I have no first hand experience on the mechanics of the actual gameplay, because I haven't had a chance to play World or Chronicles of Darkness, but let's just see if any of my ideas might work?<br /> <br /> <br /> Firstly, Obligation. The mysterious Code of behavior encouraged by the Peerage and ignored by Lemuria... feels slightly out of place in a game about Weird Science and whimsical slightly amoral scientists messing with reality for fun and profit. Obligation seems to be sort of &quot;don't be a weirdo&quot; -morality system in a game where being a weirdo should be part of the appeal. This is on the top that the game of psychological horror and mad science seems to be completely missing an iconic Sanity system.<br /> Here is my idea how to &quot;fix&quot; this: Let's instead measure how much &quot;in touch&quot; Genius is with humanity. How much they can relate to other humans and humans can relate to them, and how much Genius cares about this ability. After mulling over the different terms that could represent it I finally had an epiphany. What if we flip the Sanity scale into Insanity scale and call it... Alienation, signifying Genius's unwanted journey from your average geek into a walking element of destructive potential of Mad Science. At Alienation 0 Genius can easily adapt to people they are trying to sympathize and empathize with (maybe even too easily?) while the higher they climb the ladder of Alienation the less they can understand them, and slowly consider them more and more just cattle. Alienation would represent how isolated Genius has become from the Consensus, how fast they make their mortal allies turn on them and how quick does it take mundane to bore them.<br /> Alienation would also make another stepping stone in &quot;redeeming&quot; Lemuria, as some people in this thread have suggested. While Peers were busy promoting their principles of Obligation and the Law, they might have Alienated themselves from humanity just as much as Lemuria. It takes both halves of Inspired community to realize how distant they have grown in their endless grudges and flame wars.<br /> Examples of Alienation: Bruce Wane, Alienation 2; The Doctor, Alienation 1; Doc Brown, Alienation 4, Rick Sanchez (season 1), Alienation 8; Stanford Pines, Alienation 5; True Fea, the God-Machine and Illuminated, Alienation 10.<br /> <br /> Second: This thread has brought up several times the matters of Unmada and the broken worldview of Geniuses. I recall some suggestions and some rebuttals, but my biggest complain is about how out of place &quot;worldview&quot; sounds in a game filled with techno babble and science-y lingo. My suggestion: In addition to Aesthetic (and possible Opus) each Genius should have a Theory. Theory is an explanation, narrative, a flawed model a genius has constructed around themselves and their wonders. Geniuses Wonders, even the ones they built on dismissed scientific theories, often fit into the larger system Genius is subconsciously iterating. For Unmada Theory and Aesthetic become distinguishable from truth as their field warps reality to confirm them. How flawed the Theory is, and how much does Genius really believe in it, should be up to the player and Storyteller. Theory could play more important role in certain foundations, baraminds, and fellowships.<br /> Examples of Theories: Dr. Vienna, Theory of Aesthetic Function; the Doctor, Timey Wimey -Theory; average Phenomenologist, Archweltanschaaung -Theory; Stanford Pines, Theory of Weird Magnetism.<br /> <br /> At the moment I haven't been able to come up with any mechanical importance for Theory, beside similar one to Aesthetic. The key difference between Obsession, Theory, and Aesthetic is that the First one is what Inspiration wants Genius to do, Second is narrative Genius spins around their Inspiration and Wonders, and Aesthetic is how they make it look.<br /> So did any of this make any sense?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12082,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","user":"Weird","date":". 07-07-2016, 10:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T11:30:37-07:00","id":927704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=927608#post927608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello everyone! I am pretty new to the Genius but I've been reading development on this thread with star eyed excitement and wanted to share some of my own ideas and insight with the group. Unfortunately I have no first hand experience on the mechanics of the actual gameplay, because I haven't had a chance to play World or Chronicles of Darkness, but let's just see if any of my ideas might work?<br /> <br /> <br /> Firstly, Obligation.<br /> <br /> Second: This thread has brought up several times the matters of Unmada and the broken worldview of Geniuses.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, we've had some similar ideas to what you've mentioned. I think we were going with &quot;Paradigm&quot; for what you call &quot;Theory&quot;.<br /> <br /> As for Obligation, You're right in that it doesn't really measure something that makes sense for Mad Scientists to worry about. I've played with the idea of an upside-down Integrity replacement before, and &quot;Alienation&quot; certainly seems like something that a Genius would need to keep in check.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":4488,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","user":"malonkey1","date":". 07-07-2016, 02:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T07:17:56-07:00","id":928099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=927704#post927704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, we've had some similar ideas to what you've mentioned. I think we were going with &quot;Paradigm&quot; for what you call &quot;Theory&quot;.<br /> <br /> As for Obligation, You're right in that it doesn't really measure something that makes sense for Mad Scientists to worry about. I've played with the idea of an upside-down Integrity replacement before, and &quot;Alienation&quot; certainly seems like something that a Genius would need to keep in check.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd keep it 10-to-0 instead of reversing it, though. Make conversion easier and the math leads to the same result.<br /> <br /> I thought the current interpretation of Obligation was how much the Genius actually cares about the consequences of their actions. Which, I would think, applies to all Mad Scientists.<br /> <hr /><br /> Thoughts on Axioms and Postulates:<br /> <br /> What about for Postulates that define an incremental effect (dice bonus, damage, etc.), it uses the Axiom rating? So a Katastrofic weapon has a damage rating of [Katastrofi] as a default, Apokalypsi scanners gives a sensory bonus of [Apokalypsi] as a default, etc. Keeps things to a 1-5 scale, mostly, limits bonus/dice growth somewhat, and keeps things simple. Postulates affect <i>what</i> you know, while the Axiom rating is how <i>well</i> you know it.<br /> <br /> Specific example for a Apokalypsi Data Scanner<br /> <b>Data Breech \u2022\u2022</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Computers 2+, Data Reader<br /> <b>Effect:</b> The Wonder can automatically bypass mundane security and encryption (the equipment modifier used to help protect content) rated at Apokalypsi or less. Against Wonderous or metanormal data protection measures, the Wonder gains a bonus to Clash of Wills to breech the security equal to Apokalypsi.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T07:46:57-07:00","id":928121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=927503#post927503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you work out the XP -&gt; Mania ratio from 1E using Assembly Line and Foundations as a guideline that's actually a really bad ratio.<br /> <br /> Like I said, the question is which iconic mad scientists have a whole arsenal of gadgets. With a name or two you could examine them properly and create mechanics to model them.<br /> <br /> The reason I bring this up is because I'm worried that extra bound mania would just become an exp sink where even Geniuses with a few signature Wonders feel the need to buy it because more Mania is always a good thing. If we had specific mad scientists to work with then the mechanic could be narrowed down from just throwing extra Mania at Geniuses into replicating a specific trope.<br /> <br /> For example the iconic name for an arsenel of gadget is Batman*, but aside from a few core Wonders (Batsuit, Batmobile, Batplane, batarangs and Batgrappling hook) most of his gadgets appear only occasionally and quite often only once. If I was to represent Batman I wouldn't give him a ton of extra bound mania, I'd give him a Merit called Crazy Prepared that says once per session he can turn out to already have taken a Wonder he needs out of storage and has it on his person. (Assuming that Geniuses have a way of storing Wonders where they don't Bind Mania)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *My knowledge of Batman is mostly the Justice League cartoon and the Batman: the Brave and the Bold cartoon</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, robot armies, super-tech arsenals, and stealing another Genius's inventions are all staples of the Genre.<br /> <br /> The idea behind Wondrous XP and Gadgets is that the Wondrous XP is separate, so it doesn't inhibit normal XP growth (you can't spend it on normal Attributes and Merits), and to prevent hard caps on Wonder amounts. Inspiration only give you so much Mania that could be used to Bind, for instance - this is a way around those limits. Of course, a Genius needs to acquire Wondrous XP, so a starting Genius will likely Bind their first couple of Gadgets. Another thing Wondrous XP conferred stability allows is for Wonders to be given to non-Genii to use - Beholden and metanormal allies can be given ray guns and teleporters without the Genius needing to stay home because all their Mania is Bound enabling their friends/allies/minions.<br /> <br /> I'm for allowing Gadgets to also be &quot;archived&quot; (or put into sleep mode), where they don't take up Bound Mania, but also don't Orphan either. In that case, Batman might have a cave full of Wonders that are just sitting around, only taking a few with him (Binding Mania to stabilize them) at a time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T10:16:43-07:00","id":928231,"title":"","content":"I still really think Obligation needs a name change. The word itself reeks of instituionalization, unwanted responsibility and guilt tripping which only amplifies feeling that it's a Morality meter.<br /> Alienation and flip of scale seemed to me like simplest and most natural solution to terminology problem (I mean it's &quot;with great power comes great insanity&quot; and not &quot;with great power comes great loss of sanity&quot;), but if that doesn't work I think we should keep digging in thesaurus.<br /> Quick alternatives from the top of my head: Objectivity (important quality of legitimiate scientific research), Acceptance (how accepted genius is by others and how well do they accept mundane and contradictions), Empathy (empathy, empathy, put yourself in place of me), Humility (fitting in a game of scientific hubris)...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T10:19:43-07:00","id":928234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=928121#post928121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea behind Wondrous XP and Gadgets is that the Wondrous XP is separate, so it doesn't inhibit normal XP growth (you can't spend it on normal Attributes and Merits), and to prevent hard caps on Wonder amounts. Inspiration only give you so much Mania that could be used to Bind, for instance - this is a way around those limits. Of course, a Genius needs to acquire Wondrous XP, so a starting Genius will likely Bind their first couple of Gadgets. Another thing Wondrous XP conferred stability allows is for Wonders to be given to non-Genii to use - Beholden and metanormal allies can be given ray guns and teleporters without the Genius needing to stay home because all their Mania is Bound enabling their friends/allies/minions.</div> </div> </div> </div>So what happens if you want to play The Doctor (who has only two Wonders - TARDIS and sonic screwdriver) or Doctor Octopus (pretty much only his arms). Do you just leave your Wondrous XP sitting there unused?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=928099#post928099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about for Postulates that define an incremental effect (dice bonus, damage, etc.), it uses the Axiom rating? So a Katastrofic weapon has a damage rating of [Katastrofi] as a default</div> </div> </div> </div> That would mean you have to be a top tier mad scientist to make rayguns more powerful than a civilian issue mundane shotgun. What's the point of that? Moochava had a very good reason for saying Katastrofi has a base damage of 5.<br /> <br /> I'd say go out of your way to make as little as possible depend upon dots in Axioms. If you want to build a super car at Skafoi 1 but flight or teleportation doesn't fit your charachter you shouldn't be buying Skafoi just to make your car better. Buy Inspiration or mundane skills for that.<br /> <br /> (Clash of Wills could Inspiration + Core Modifier)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 07-08-2016, 01:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T10:27:20-07:00","id":928240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=928234#post928234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what happens if you want to play The Doctor (who has only two Wonders - TARDIS and sonic screwdriver) or Doctor Octopus (pretty much only his arms). Do you just leave your Wondrous XP sitting there unused?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure you can add it to existing wonders...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T10:39:27-07:00","id":928250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=928231#post928231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still really think Obligation needs a name change. The word itself reeks of instituionalization, unwanted responsibility and guilt tripping which only amplifies feeling that it's a Morality meter.<br /> Alienation and flip of scale seemed to me like simplest and most natural solution to terminology problem (I mean it's &quot;with great power comes great insanity&quot; and not &quot;with great power comes great loss of sanity&quot;), but if that doesn't work I think we should keep digging in thesaurus.<br /> Quick alternatives from the top of my head: Objectivity (important quality of legitimiate scientific research), Acceptance (how accepted genius is by others and how well do they accept mundane and contradictions), Empathy (empathy, empathy, put yourself in place of me), Humility (fitting in a game of scientific hubris)...</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm still using Obligation because I'd rather change as little as necessary, but I'm open to better terminology. I'd still like to keep to a 10-to-1 rather than an inverse scale, though, for conversion (and character sheet) reasons.<br /> <br /> As to the suggestions:<br /> Objectivity - this seems like it might get a bit vague. I can see the word meaning multiple, somewhat contradictory things in regards to an Integrity analog.<br /> Acceptance - Of their condition, or by others? I'm leery of basing it upon outside views, since those can vary by group easily.<br /> Empathy - Already a Skill, sadly, but in concept, this probably fits the best.<br /> Humility - Might work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":"necessary 07-08-2016, 01:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T10:49:54-07:00","id":928259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=928234#post928234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what happens if you want to play The Doctor (who has only two Wonders - TARDIS and sonic screwdriver) or Doctor Octopus (pretty much only his arms). Do you just leave your Wondrous XP sitting there unused?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you might be able to spend it on other Genius related things. More Axioms or Postulates, maybe. Or add more to their existing Wonders - after all, more modifications are likely to increase the Mania requirements, and there may be other options to sink it into for single Wonders.<br /> <br /> What does a Mage (or other character type) do when they don't really change their ability set much?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=928234#post928234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would mean you have to be a top tier mad scientist to make rayguns more powerful than a civilian issue mundane shotgun. What's the point of that? Moochava had a very good reason for saying Katastrofi has a base damage of 5.<br /> <br /> I'd say go out of your way to make as little as possible depend upon dots in Axioms. If you want to build a super car at Skafoi 1 but flight or teleportation doesn't fit your charachter you shouldn't be buying Skafoi just to make your car better. Buy Inspiration or mundane skills for that.<br /> <br /> (Clash of Wills could Inspiration + Core Modifier)</div> </div> </div> </div>Point. Though your super-car's speed (and other abilities) might only factor in Skafoi as a part of its calculations (like the free Reach or Primary Factor for Arcana).<br /> <br /> And Buying Inspiration requires a Thesis (unless that is changed).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T10:59:36-07:00","id":928275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=928250#post928250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.<br /> Humility - Might work.</div> </div> </div> </div>The more I think about it the more it seems like Humility is most fitting word for 10-to-1 Genius Integrity scale. In stories where Genius's greatest enemy is Genius themself, their problems stream from their unchecked arrogance. While Humility is a in-game Virtue, it would be extraordinary for a mad scientist to posses it. While Obligation centered stories seem to focus on neglect of responsibility, stories about Humility would naturally focus on the theme of the game: Self-inflicted hubris as result of Inspired arrogance. It also makes it so much easier to explain what generally constitutes as a Transgression for a Genius; Act of unchecked (and often harmful) arrogance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T12:33:54-07:00","id":928342,"title":"","content":"Something kind of hit me today (well, last night, but that wouldn't be a song quote, now would it?)<br /> <br /> More specifically, I realized why Axioms feel <i>off</i> to me. They have no guidelines.<br /> <br /> Consider:<br /> \u2022 Mage Arcana? Guidelines on what each level should be able to do, and how much it should cost.<br /> \u2022 Vampire Disciplines? Guidelines on what each level should be able to do, and how much it should cost.<br /> \u2022 Werewolf Gifts? Guidelines on costs and general purview of effects for each facet.<br /> <br /> Note that these are <i>system wide</i>. Genius' Axioms currently don't have that.<br /> <br /> So...<br /> <br /> What should Geniuses be able to do with basic competency (1-2 levels in an Axiom)?<br /> What should that cost them?<br /> How should they progress?<br /> How should they be structured? Mad science isn't linear, so it makes no sense that the Axioms are.<br /> <br /> One idea I had: Axioms <i>build off each-other</i>. Each Axiom has a list of related Axioms - you get a price cut if you buy Axioms that are related to the ones you already have.<br /> <br /> Something like 3xp/4xp/5xp - Unfavored, unrelated Axioms cost 5xp per dot/unit, related or favored Axioms cost 4xp per, and any Axiom that's related AND favored costs 3xp per.<br /> <br /> So let's say you have Katastrophi favored and you just learned the principles behind gravity guns. Sure, you could learn how to create artificial life for 5xp... but learning to upscale that to a gravity <i>cannon</i> only costs you 3xp...<br /> <hr /><br /> Also, I want to crib notes off of <a href=\"http://www.giantitp.com/forums/showthread.php?291019-By-the-Inferior-Science-of-our-Enemies-Gramarie-Mark-II\" target=\"_blank\">Gramarie</a> (which I believe has been mentioned). Not for the precise effects (which are too tied to D&amp;D's cosmology for them to work), but for that similar pseudo-science vibe and <i>openness</i>.<br /> <br /> Take a look around - that's the kind of &quot;holy crap, I can do <i>so much</i>&quot; that I want to see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T12:37:27-07:00","id":928345,"title":"","content":"I don't think Humility is right. The Doctor's ego is far bigger than, say, Tarvek Sturmvoraus but the latter should have a far lower Integrity-trait score.<br /> <br /> The key thing about Genius' karma meter is that it represents a conscious effort on the part of the Genius. To quote the Doctor &quot;good people don't need rules, today isn't the day to find out why I have so many.&quot; A word like Humility implies an innate trait rather than conscious effort, so it doesn't fit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=928259#post928259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, you might be able to spend it on other Genius related things. More Axioms or Postulates, maybe. Or add more to their existing Wonders - after all, more modifications are likely to increase the Mania requirements, and there may be other options to sink it into for single Wonders.</div> </div> </div> </div>That won't help. Unless you add <i>tons</i> of additional Mania requirements players it will still hit the point where players have piles of Wonderous XP lying around and nothing to spend it on. If you do add tons of additional Mania requirements then the Genius with an arsenal of wonders won't be able to afford good wonders.<br /> <br /> If you expand Wonderous XP to include other things, then you'll be getting a far worse deal on your XP for buying Bound Mania than you would if you brought Inspiration or Aximos and freed up regular exp to join a Fellowship.<br /> <br /> Adding a core trait to a charachter template isn't something you do lightly. It's not enough to just think of charachter's who'd make good use of it, you have to ask yourself if they're charachters where it doesn't make sense for them to use it - and in this case the answer is quite probably yes. This is why I keep saying you need to come up with the iconic mad scientists you're trying to represent with Wonderous XP. Once you have clear examples to examine you can start working on a more narrowly focused mechanic that works for them (like the Crazy Prepared Merit I proposed for Batman) that won't alienating people trying to play The Doctor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=928259#post928259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Point. Though your super-car's speed (and other abilities) might only factor in Skafoi as a part of its calculations (like the free Reach or Primary Factor for Arcana).</div> </div> </div> </div>It should be easy to avoid making much scale with Axiom dots, and unlike Mage it probably should be avoided in favour of Inspiration and mental skills.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 07-08-2016, 03:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T13:28:15-07:00","id":928382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=928342#post928342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something kind of hit me today (well, last night, but that wouldn't be a song quote, now would it?)<br /> <br /> More specifically, I realized why Axioms feel <i>off</i> to me. They have no guidelines.<br /> <br /> Consider:<br /> \u2022 Mage Arcana? Guidelines on what each level should be able to do, and how much it should cost.<br /> \u2022 Vampire Disciplines? Guidelines on what each level should be able to do, and how much it should cost.<br /> \u2022 Werewolf Gifts? Guidelines on costs and general purview of effects for each facet.<br /> <br /> Note that these are <i>system wide</i>. Genius' Axioms currently don't have that.<br /> <br /> So...<br /> <br /> What should Geniuses be able to do with basic competency (1-2 levels in an Axiom)?<br /> What should that cost them?<br /> How should they progress?<br /> How should they be structured? Mad science isn't linear, so it makes no sense that the Axioms are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe we should dispense with the 1-5 dot structure entirely. Each Axiom is a set of Postulates, independent of any dot rating (see Demonic Embeds and Exploits, Werewolf Facets). You might need ranks in certain skills, or specific other Postulates, but you don't need to but dots into some nebulous Axiom.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One idea I had: Axioms <i>build off each-other</i>. Each Axiom has a list of related Axioms - you get a price cut if you buy Axioms that are related to the ones you already have.<br /> <br /> Something like 3xp/4xp/5xp - Unfavored, unrelated Axioms cost 5xp per dot/unit, related or favored Axioms cost 4xp per, and any Axiom that's related AND favored costs 3xp per.<br /> <br /> So let's say you have Katastrophi favored and you just learned the principles behind gravity guns. Sure, you could learn how to create artificial life for 5xp... but learning to upscale that to a gravity <i>cannon</i> only costs you 3xp... </div> </div> </div>I like the idea of building on existing knowledge, though. Maybe arrange Axiomata on a wheel, Axiomata get a cost break if you know Postulates from the others?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, I want to crib notes off of <a href=\"http://www.giantitp.com/forums/showthread.php?291019-By-the-Inferior-Science-of-our-Enemies-Gramarie-Mark-II\" target=\"_blank\">Gramarie</a> (which I believe has been mentioned). Not for the precise effects (which are too tied to D&amp;D's cosmology for them to work), but for that similar pseudo-science vibe and <i>openness</i>.<br /> <br /> Take a look around - that's the kind of &quot;holy crap, I can do <i>so much</i>&quot; that I want to see. </div> </div> </div>Damn, it's been forever since I've been on GiTP.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=928345#post928345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That won't help. Unless you add <i>tons</i> of additional Mania requirements players it will still hit the point where players have piles of Wonderous XP lying around and nothing to spend it on. If you do add tons of additional Mania requirements then the Genius with an arsenal of wonders won't be able to afford good wonders.<br /> <br /> If you expand Wonderous XP to include other things, then you'll be getting a far worse deal on your XP for buying Bound Mania than you would if you brought Inspiration or Aximos and freed up regular exp to join a Fellowship.<br /> <br /> Adding a core trait to a charachter template isn't something you do lightly. It's not enough to just think of charachter's who'd make good use of it, you have to ask yourself if they're charachters where it doesn't make sense for them to use it - and in this case the answer is quite probably yes. This is why I keep saying you need to come up with the iconic mad scientists you're trying to represent with Wonderous XP. Once you have clear examples to examine you can start working on a more narrowly focused mechanic that works for them (like the Crazy Prepared Merit I proposed for Batman) that won't alienating people trying to play The Doctor.<br /> <br /> It should be easy to avoid making much scale with Axiom dots, and unlike Mage it probably should be avoided in favour of Inspiration and mental skills.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're probably right on that. I'm becoming less and less sure that Wondrous XP is a good idea, except maybe as a hack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":4488,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","user":"malonkey1","date":". 07-08-2016, 04:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T13:43:00-07:00","id":928395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=928382#post928382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe we should dispense with the 1-5 dot structure entirely. Each Axiom is a set of Postulates, independent of any dot rating (see Demonic Embeds and Exploits, Werewolf Facets). You might need ranks in certain skills, or specific other Postulates, but you don't need to but dots into some nebulous Axiom.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't feel right to me. It lacks one thing - flexibility. I think Geniuses' need to but powers as a set rather than individually. Much like mage, being able to improvise is core to both the theme and the fun of the game. But you can't improvise if you have to buy every sub-power individually.<br /> <br /> My suggestion is that, like in 1E, the only &quot;power&quot; you spend exp on is Axioms. However we introduce a Reach like mechanic to make wonders more fine-grained, so a mad doctor with a bioscanner and a ghostbuster with a ghost scanner have two different wonders - rather than both having an everything scanner.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=928382#post928382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea of building on existing knowledge, though. Maybe arrange Axiomata on a wheel, Axiomata get a cost break if you know Postulates from the others?</div> </div> </div> </div> Do be careful about stuff like this. You want to avoid cases where buying the same things in a different order has a different exp cost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T13:47:50-07:00","id":928398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=928345#post928345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think Humility is right. The Doctor's ego is far bigger than, say, Tarvek Sturmvoraus but the latter should have a far lower Integrity-trait score.<br /> <br /> The key thing about Genius' karma meter is that it represents a conscious effort on the part of the Genius. To quote the Doctor &quot;good people don't need rules, today isn't the day to find out why I have so many.&quot; A word like Humility implies an innate trait rather than conscious effort, so it doesn't fit.</div> </div> </div> </div>But we are trying to throw a karma meter out of a window where it belongs and replace it with sanity meter, are we not? I do agree that Humility sounds bit too much like an innate trait, but I can't think of better word at the moment to represent conscious effort to not give in into one's self-reliant arrogance.<br /> In addition I must say that Tarvek as a typical example of a Huffnung has a well inflated ego, it's just that he and Doctor channel it differently. Doctor turns it into eccentric theatrics while Tarvek turns it into sneaky scheming.<br /> <br /> I think we should try to think of Transgression more as an act of Hubris rather than as a moral misstep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12082,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","user":"Weird","date":". 07-08-2016, 04:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T14:35:12-07:00","id":928434,"title":"","content":"I don't think Tarvek's scheming is related to an inflated ego. He's just a schemer. <br /> <br /> As for Hubris. Mad Science has been moving away from hubris as a core theme for a while now. There's a lot of hubristic mad scientists, sometimes it's a symptom of science related memetic disorder, sometimes they're just arrogant people. But it's very rare for a mad science story to have the moral that hubris is bad these days. Besides that's Mage's thing and it would be unfair on Klagen.<br /> <br /> As Hubris became less core to the idea of a mad scientist it was replaced by the idea of loss of control. A mad scientist is literally compelled by insanity to act in certain ways, and this theme is everywhere: A Miracle of Science, Girl Genius, Wicked Science, Narbonic, Soon I will be Invincible. Heck, the only time the film version of Tony Stark went through the traditional mad scientist plot in Age of Ultron, he did it because someone was messing with his head.<br /> <br /> That's the theme Genius' Integrity should tie into. Both the willingness and ability to force yourself to think like a normal sane person for a while. It would probably look a LOT like Vampire's humanity - though you'd need to have an option for codes of condcut and morality along side touchstones. Batman has Alfred, he also has his &quot;one rule&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T15:14:18-07:00","id":928461,"title":"","content":"*snaps fingers*<br /> How about Discipline? (or synonym of such?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T17:11:09-07:00","id":928515,"title":"","content":"One idea for the price break:<br /> <br /> You get it &quot;for free&quot; in one direction... and then can turn around and get a refund somehow.<br /> <br /> Like one guy learns how to make anitgrav scooters for 5xp and then gets the discount on gravity guns; if he then does [blank] to integrate his research, he gets back the one extra point of XP he spent on it.<br /> <br /> So it goes Full Cost -&gt; Discount -&gt; Refund.<br /> <br /> =---=<br /> <br /> One reason I pointed out Gramarie is that it's an example of picking up one power with <i>really</i> wide applicability. Like Yggdratecture's base ability lets you make extradimensional pockets - a later upgrade lets you build portals and such as a side effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T22:40:08-07:00","id":928598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=928461#post928461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*snaps fingers*<br /> How about Discipline? (or synonym of such?)</div> </div> </div> </div>What about <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ubuntu_(philosophy)\" target=\"_blank\">Ubuntu?</a> The term didn't really enter the English language until recently, but that kind of seems appropriate to me, having Geniuses only really worry about social consciousness (that is, society as a collection of people, not just as a system) with our highly-connected internet world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":4488,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","user":"malonkey1","date":". 07-09-2016, 01:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T01:15:43-07:00","id":928636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=928250#post928250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Empathy - Already a Skill, sadly, but in concept, this probably fits the best.</div> </div> </div> </div>The word that might work is &quot;Conscience&quot;. What did the last edition use though? Do you really need to change it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=928598#post928598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ubuntu_(operating_system)\" target=\"_blank\">Ubuntu?</a></div> </div> </div> </div>That's the Operating System I use.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T03:30:55-07:00","id":928669,"title":"","content":"What about Perspective? A high Perspective Genius knows what they are doing (or has a good idea of the ramifications of it anyways) while a low Perspective Genius gets lost in their own little concerns and goals, uncaring of wider implications.<br /> <br /> Still trying to think of a good word that encapsulates &quot;ability to care about repercussions to others, or the consequence of one's actions&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T04:07:07-07:00","id":928678,"title":"","content":"While an inability to care about wider implications fits fine for characters like The Doctor and Rick Sanchez it can't model Girl Genius that well, it would actually imply that Baron Wolfenbach is the highest Integirty-Stat member of the cast. And a Hoffnung Atomist is all about the consequences of technology, they just have a warped definition of what's a good consequence.<br /> <br /> I'd keep the focus on the Genius' ability to recognise and care about what other people think and feel.<ul><li>Paragon: I understand why you find the idea of uploading into a robotic body icky, but it will free humanity from our violent and savage natures.</li> <li>Mid Range: Hold on a second, you're not chearing? Igor, why aren't people leaping at the chance for robotiziation?</li> <li>Bottoming out: I have scientifically proven that robotic bodies are the best solution. Minions, start abducting people and throw them into the robotiziation chambers!</li> </ul><br /> <br /> That models The Doctor perfectly. It does well for Girl Genius, where Agatha's heroism is portrayed as superior to the Baron's cold pragmatism, and the Castle Heterodyne inmates (and the castle itself actually) who're awfully casual about atrocities as though they just don't see the problem with what they're doing. I can't think of any real counter examples where a more crazy charachter has more empathy for regular people than a less crazy mad scientist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=928636#post928636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What did the last edition use though? Do you really need to change it?</div> </div> </div> </div> Obligation, I'm fine with the word actually, but I feel the description needs to change from being about a Mad Scientist's duty to their fellow man to being able to force themsevles to think like their fellow man.<br /> <br /> The scene where Clara hands The Doctor flash cards telling him what to say to reassure the people who's lives were in danger is an example of a mid Integrity-stat Genius (still tries, no longer that good at it) using a Touchstone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=928636#post928636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the Operating System I use.</div> </div> </div> </div> My sympathies. You should go to Debian Testing.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 07-09-2016, 07:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T04:30:44-07:00","id":928686,"title":"","content":"My biggest beef is still the word though. Obligation is a fancy word for responsibility which ties strongly into Morality. Again games about Mad Science would (and should) leap into questions of scientifical ethics, but I strongly believe we need a word that would tie it better into sanity.<br /> I also feel like I should bring up Humility again, since as I see it, the act of humility for Mad Scientist is not turning into doormat, but understanding that non-Geniuses are not worth less than them despite not being able to engage in Mad Science. This interpritation of system would actually put Agatha higher on the scale than Baron, but also shows the flaws of most heroic characters; Sometimes it's just hard to not consider yourself better than anyone else. The moment of Transgression is the instant when Genius sees spark of disgust and confusion and fear in the eyes of the mundane-folks and snarls &quot;Whatever! I didn't need you anyway, sheeple!!&quot;<br /> Also if one likes to think of Illuminated as what Inspiration wants Inspired to turn into, one of the possible ways to blind them to their transformation and isolate them from their support network would be stoking their arrogance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12082,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","user":"Weird","date":". 07-09-2016, 07:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T05:37:26-07:00","id":928699,"title":"","content":"While Agatha is more humble than Baron Wulfenbach, neither of them have arrogance or hubris as a charachter trait. Most mad scientist protagonist since Girl Genius started have been the same. Hubris just doesn't fit as a core trait.<br /> <br /> Hubris would probably work best as a Persistent Condition given to Hoffnungs. They already got Narcacism as their core Derangement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T12:42:06-07:00","id":928867,"title":"","content":"If we redefine Obligation into &quot;capacity to will oneself into thinking like a mortal&quot;, it could be renamed to Comprehension.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I'm in favor of eliminating the linearity of Axioms like Amechra suggested.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T13:48:35-07:00","id":928899,"title":"","content":"How would you preserve the ability to kitbash a solution to a problem if every effect has to be brought individually? You're not playing mad scientists if you don't get to invent on the fly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T16:34:24-07:00","id":928948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=928899#post928899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would you preserve the ability to kitbash a solution to a problem if every effect has to be brought individually? You're not playing mad scientists if you don't get to invent on the fly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there's the idea of &quot;Reaching&quot; for extra effects when kitbashing.<br /> <br /> On another note, Who's going to be actually working on this project, so I can send you Drive links and keep in more focused contact?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T16:35:18-07:00","id":928949,"title":"","content":"I'll contribute (something, some time).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T16:37:11-07:00","id":928951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=928899#post928899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would you preserve the ability to kitbash a solution to a problem if every effect has to be brought individually? You're not playing mad scientists if you don't get to invent on the fly.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hence the &quot;can reconfigure or just grab a few new ones temporarily&quot;.<br /> <br /> If Axiom ratings are eliminated, how is progression handled? Omniscience, Disintegrators, and Mind Control right out of the gate?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T16:41:23-07:00","id":928955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=928951#post928951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Hence the &quot;can reconfigure or just grab a few new ones temporarily&quot;.<br /> <br /> If Axiom ratings are eliminated, how is progression handled? Omniscience, Disintegrators, and Mind Control right out of the gate?</div> </div> </div> </div>Weaker Postulates are available off the bat, more adanced ones might require X number of Postulates or a specific previous postulate. I mean, we can't give the characters omnipotence off the bat, but there are some examples of characters with really narrow, really advanced creations (Frankenstein creating a full human from the word &quot;jump&quot; out of bits and pieces, for example).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T17:00:31-07:00","id":928959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=928867#post928867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we redefine Obligation into &quot;capacity to will oneself into thinking like a mortal&quot;, it could be renamed to Comprehension.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like that one! Do we have a bingo?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T18:19:39-07:00","id":928998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=928959#post928959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like that one! Do we have a bingo?</div> </div> </div> </div>Comprehension just doesn't feel right. I suggested Sympathy a while back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T02:51:55-07:00","id":929138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=928678#post928678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">, I'm fine with the word actually, but I feel the description needs to change from being about a Mad Scientist's duty to their fellow man to being able to force themsevles to think like their fellow man.</div> </div> </div> </div>But why is this name change so important? I mean, I've always understood the morality of a Genius as being a descent into hubris and madness (which are one in the same here), and that a Genius lower on the scale starts becoming like Lex Luthor in the Superman movie, where he doesn't get that his henchwoman is going to turn on him when his scheme is going to kill her mother. The idea of a Mad Scientist'sr is pretty much tied into the idea of them getting into unethical behavior because they're too engrossed in their undertaking to even consider the collateral damage: everyone else just becomes an ignorant obstacle to progress, am expendable test-subject, or someone to leave in awe of their work.<br /> <br /> ...Actually, saying that makes me see what you mean...<br /> <br /> The term in actual science is called &quot;Compliance to Ethical Standards&quot;, or perhaps just &quot;Ethics&quot;, and I can see the downfall of the low end being that they become impulsive when people are stopping them from achieving their goals...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":10120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","user":"RockstarRaccoon","date":". 07-10-2016, 05:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T04:03:37-07:00","id":929162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=929138#post929138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But why is this name change so important?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're asking the wrong person <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'm fine with &quot;Obligation&quot;, Comprehension could work too. Ethics as a word would imply that a low Ethics person is willing to do nasty stuff, but it wouldn't imply that they're unable to understand why someone else considers it nasty.<br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Save</span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T12:23:17-07:00","id":929323,"title":"","content":"I am most geared towards Comprehension since the word gives a mental imagine of mad scientist simply not understanding people, though Ethics too has its charm.<br /> My seething dissatisfaction with Obligation is that for many Geniuses it's end up being literally responsibility they didn't ask for. By measuring instead how much they &quot;can focus on thinking like a normal person&quot;, &quot;respect normal people&quot;, &quot;can understand why it's bad to force a person into transcendence humanity&quot;, we make a story were there is still space for redeemable low meter characters, it's just that they are less likely to understand that there is something wrong with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T16:23:57-07:00","id":929443,"title":"","content":"Well, I'd go with &quot;Ethics&quot;, because it 1) seems like a good parallel to Mage's &quot;Wisdom&quot; and 2) actually describes how much consideration someone is giving to others. (also, Dragon isn't using it anymore, so there's that) It also leaves room to keep talking about the Obligation stuff, which was kind of supposed to measure how close they are to humanity.<br /> <br /> Of course, you COULD go with a more nuanced system of having them have something other than a single vertical scale, but once again, I don't feel like you need to spend this much time on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T03:42:21-07:00","id":929642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=929443#post929443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I'd go with &quot;Ethics&quot;, because it 1) seems like a good parallel to Mage's &quot;Wisdom&quot; and 2) actually describes how much consideration someone is giving to others. (also, Dragon isn't using it anymore, so there's that) It also leaves room to keep talking about the Obligation stuff, which was kind of supposed to measure how close they are to humanity.<br /> <br /> Of course, you COULD go with a more nuanced system of having them have something other than a single vertical scale, but once again, I don't feel like you need to spend this much time on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Once again, I'd like to remind people of my &quot;crossing scales&quot; idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4968-mrbreaksit","name":"MrBreaksIt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T06:07:31-07:00","id":931953,"title":"","content":"Quick idea for new Integrity system for Geniuses: I'd like to contrast Lemurians and Peers a bit. Yes, both organizations are stuffed with mad scientists, some more lucid or more in denial than others, but the way they look at their creations, mania, and other supernaturals are polar opposite. Peers are constantly in a state of cynical disbelief, they must disbelief their own paradigm to avoid becoming unmada slip-slopping into Illumination. When they confront a new unknown phenomena they must keep their cool and approach it firstly as a fraud, either by mania or mortal charlatan. This makes the Law of living without lies partially enforced in gameplay. Peers risk Transgression when they believe false information.<br /> <br /> Lemuria couldn't careless about Peers and their dumb laws. They have Archweltanschaaung! Every theory is correct! Every paradigm is true! The world is beautiful cacophony of contradictions of realities and Lemurians know it to be so. &quot;Look at Bardos and manes! Aren't they proof enough that reality and truth are multifaceted?&quot; If Peers rather disbelief truth than believe lies, Lemuria are the opposite. To Lemurians the slippery slope into Illumination isn't belief in lies, it's disbelief of truth. When Lemurian claims something as impossible especially if someone believes it, they assert themselves as someone &quot;more&quot; than that person which may quickly lead to isolation, destabilization, and Illumination. Lemurian's risk Transgression when they disbelieve in something (especially if that something is real.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12082,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","user":"Weird","date":". 07-15-2016, 09:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T14:14:48-07:00","id":932202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=915805#post915805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but it's hard to think of an innate ability that doesn't stretch the theme.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, can Geniuses understand how each other's creations work? Being able to see them working would be a good ability...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T17:13:27-07:00","id":932259,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry, but this is what you are writing about now.<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hFGDu4i04eI\" data-code=\"hFGDu4i04eI\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-