ook to work, especially since the Genius is also a talking dinosaur. I forgot to mention that. Moving on...<br /> <br /> Now, see, what if said train was used to travel through time to the future, where they discovered the after effects of an apocalyptic event which destroyed their dinosaur utopia. unable to ascertain at event was, let alone stop it, this Genius, with only a pair of precocious children (a pterodactyl and her adopted brother) for assistance, must now scour the time stream to find a way to save his people, either by stopping the event or ferrying them through time to a place where they will be safe to start anew...<br /> <br /> Let's just say.... <span style=\"color:#DAA520\"><i>I ha</i></span><span style=\"color:#008000\"><i>v</i></span><span style=\"color:#DAA520\"><i>e a hy</i></span><span style=\"color:#008000\"><i>p</i></span><span style=\"color:#DAA520\"><i>ot</i></span><span style=\"color:#008000\"><i>h</i></span><span style=\"color:#DAA520\"><i>es</i></span><span style=\"color:#008000\"><i>i</i></span><span style=\"color:#DAA520\"><i>s.</i></span><br /> <img src=\"http://statici.behindthevoiceactors.com/behindthevoiceactors/_img/chars/mr-conductor-dinosaur-train-9.56.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Why did you just plot out Dinosaur Train?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T16:46:52-07:00","id":933150,"title":"","content":"It's a story hook! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T18:38:07-07:00","id":933189,"title":"","content":"Are... are we being sarcastic about something? I'm a little lost here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T03:18:03-07:00","id":933332,"title":"","content":"I'm joking, obviously. These are just dumb ideas that go through my head. Don't worry about it. I'll stop being silly, because it's derailing discussion more than I intended, so sorry about that.<br /> <br /> Though, to be serious, that video from Static Shock <i>is</i> how I imagine a genius awakening, and that Dinosaur Train idea <i>would</i> be a very good hook for a time-travel campaign...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T04:25:23-07:00","id":933357,"title":"","content":"Gear's awakening is far too easy to be a Genius. Maybe an exceptionally lucky Hoffnung or Stunnen with the Science Hero merit could get away with it, but not your average Genius.<br /> <br /> I'd say a good example of a Genius' Breakthrough would be in Stranger Things. <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Specifically Joyce in episodes 1-3 where nobody believes her that Will is alive, she's sounding progressively crazier and crazier, alienating people, and finally ends up building a device out of Christmass Tree lights to communicate with the other side.<br /> <br /> After that though, other charachters start to figure out that she's right. She becomes less crazy, so I guess you could call it an almost Breakthrough.<br /> <br /> (I'm not sure if she fits any of the Catalysts though. Perhaps a Catalyst of Fear is needed.)</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 07-18-2016, 08:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T12:19:42-07:00","id":934014,"title":"","content":"I got board and decided to write up a morality trait. I went with Ethics for the name, since I looked at it from a different angle and it clicked nicely. Ethics always was my favourite word since it's nice and sciencey. And when I realised you could describe ethics as the product of &quot;comprehension&quot; it all fit - the Genius knows his morality is mad, thus he replaces his morals with a code of ethics from the consensus .<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ethics</b><br /> From Up Here They Look Like Ants<br /> <br /> A genius' Breakthrough, once she has mastered his first Axioms and created her first wonders, is often accompanied by a godlike feeling of invincibility and of escape from the fetters of the mundane world. But a genius cannot escape humanity, at least while keeping his humanity intact.<br /> <br /> Instead, a genius is bound to humanity by ties of Ethics. The genius can never again trust his own sense of morality, of right and wrong. Instead he must rely upon the consensus to provide a code of Ethics. To the Inspired following the rules and dogmas of small minded mortals is as much a chain as an anchor, and Inspiration cannot be truly chained. A Genius will break free, he can only choose when and how: Not too often, and only after carefully thinking through the morality, consequences, and potential benefits of his actions.<br /> <br /> That's the ideal, and few Inspired live up to it. Even peers are willing to use their own moral intuition, while Lemuria sees it's philosophies as superior to the consensus. Those Paragons who retain their sense of Ethics are rare, especially as the pressure of finding test subjects, grant money, and a place to work grows more fierce as a genius grows in ability and Inspiration. Powerful geniuses often see themselves more as conduits for the raw stuff of Inspiration than as people who happen to be Inspired, and behave accordingly. Those acts that violate a genius' sense of Ethics are called transgressions. Too many, too often, with too little regard for their consequences, can drive a genius into true madness<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Modified Advantage: Ethics (Integrity)</b><br /> <br /> Good men don't need rules. Today is not the day to find out why I have so many of them.<br /> - The Doctor<br /> <br /> The Inspired are extreme creatures, capable of great and terrible transgressions. To fight the corrosive influence of those crimes against the natural order, geniuses focus on the rules and taboos of mundane humanity: Which they quantify in a code of Ethics.<br /> <br /> Ethics measures a Genius' wiliness and ability to to ignore their Inspiration, and how far they are from becoming a true mad scientist, one of the Illuminated who has lost all concern for the well-being and dignity of others, and who sees humans as we might see laboratory mice. As Ethics falls, the genius becomes less and less able to understand the rules of normal sane behaviour and less interested in doing so for any decent reason.<br /> <br /> Geniuses quickly learn that Ethics is more than morality: it is tied to the standards of sane and normal behaviour that humans apply to their fellows. Many acts that a genius can rationalize as for the greater good\u2015or even demonstrate to be beneficial and useful\u2015are transgressions, since they violate the standards of regular human behavior and erode a genius' ability to mimic sanity.<br /> <br /> Transgression:<br /> <br /> When a genius acts in a way that violates his Ethical standards, he commits a transgression. The genius must make a degeneration roll to see if he loses a dot of Ethics. If an act can be described by two different levels of transgression, use the lower one on the chart.<br /> <br /> ROLL RESULTS GO HERE<br /> <br /> Transgressions include, from least to most heinous:<br /> <br /> Actions that imply a lack of respect for the dangerous power of Inspiration,<br /> Actions that regular humans find gross, improper, or &quot;cold&quot; (whether or not they're actually immoral),<br /> Actions that physically or psychologically distance the genius from humanity,<br /> Actions that display a cold or reckless disregard for civilization and/or the rule of law, and<br /> Actions that stem from a genius' willingness to see humans as disposable, replaceable, or beneath consideration.<br /> <br /> The list below is not complete or all-inclusive; the Storyteller is expected to examine questionable actions from a genius to see if they fit with the general pattern of transgressions listed below, and to warn the genius' player of a transgression that the mad scientist is poised to commit.<br /> <br /> ETHICS CHART GOES HERE (The Obligation chart will probably work as is)<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;The more we do to you, the less you seem to believe we are doing it.&quot;<br /> -Dr. Joseph Mengele<br /> <br /> Ethics and Integrity:<br /> <br /> Beholden and unInspired manes possess Integrity. Geniuses, Inspired manes, and intelligent automata possess Ethics.<br /> <br /> Benefits of Ethics:<br /> <br /> Paragon Status:<br /> <br /> A genius with an Ethics of 7 or higher qualifies as a Paragon. People have difficulty imagining that the genius is up to no good. Even the most maladjusted genius, if he possesses high Ethics, is automatically seen as a trustworthy authority figure by regular mortals, someone to be admired for his intelligence and contributions to humanity. Anyone trying to tar the genius' reputation suffers a -3 penalty to the attempt, his indiscretions and gaffs are written off as a brilliant eccentricity.<br /> <br /> Drawbacks of Ethics:<br /> The Dampness of the Sea<br /> <br /> Iracus was warned not too fly too low or else the water would clog his wings. Exceptional Geniuses who maintain an Ethics of 8 more more find that living with so many rules cramps and limits their Inspiration. Some find it a welcome relief from the mania of Inspired life, most pace their cell and struggle against their chains, and all of them find it harder to draw on their Inspiration.<br /> <br /> A Genius who maintains an Ethics of 8 or more treats their Inspiration as two dots lower (minimum of 1) when using Deep Inspiration.<br /> <br /> The Heat of the Sun:<br /> <br /> TODO: Basically it works like Werewolf 2E's death rage triggers. The lower Ethics is, the easier Jabir is to trigger. When Jabir happens either your enemy gains a positive Condition (oops! You told Mr Bond your evil plan) or you take a negative condition (everyone on the Tenure Committee thinks you're crazy).<br /> <br /> The Broken Chains:<br /> <br /> Should a genius reach zero Ethics, she becomes one of the Illuminated. Freed from all ethical constraints, she becomes an abomination of science and forbidden secrets, able to see humans only as victims and objects.<br /> <br /> <br /> Science Hero (OOO, OOOOO)<br /> <br /> The Genius gains a Virtue, it need not be the same one they had before their Breakthrough but it must represent an altruistic drive to act for the good of others or for mankind as a whole.<br /> <br /> Whenever she is acting in accordance with her Virtue she treats her Ethics as 2 dots higher, to a maximum of 10. In addition if their Ethics is 6 or more (not counting this Merit) they may attempt to take charge of Mortals who are facing a chaotic and dangerous situation in which the Genius has unique insight by spending a point of Willpower and rolling Ethics.<br /> <br /> ROLL RESULTS GO HERE \u2013 if you've seen Doctor Who you know what's going on here.<br /> <br /> The five dot varient of this Merit allows the Genius to regain Willpower from her Virtue, as though she were a regular mortal.<br /> <br /> Drawback<br /> <br /> Whenever the Genius is acting in an immoral, selfish or low manner they treat their Ethics as two dots lower, to a minimum of 1. As a rule of thumb if the average mortal would consider it to be immoral or a moral obligation then a Science Hero must behave appropriately or else suffer the drawback.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 07-20-2016, 07:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T12:53:49-07:00","id":934033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Beholden and unInspired manes possess Morality. Geniuses, Inspired manes, and intelligent automata possess Ethics. </div> </div> </div>What is this \u201cMorality\u201d of which you speak?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Should a genius reach zero Obligation, she becomes one of the Illuminated. Freed from all ethical constraints, she becomes an abomination of science and forbidden secrets, able to see humans only as victims and objects. </div> </div> </div>Likewise, what is \u201cObligation\u201d?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T13:12:54-07:00","id":934046,"title":"","content":"I think you've gone Unmada Dataweaver. Those quotes aren't in my post <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T14:55:13-07:00","id":934113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Drawbacks of Obligation:<br /> The Dampness of the Sea </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Modified Advantage: Ethics (Morality) </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Geniuses quickly learn that Ethics is more than Morality: it is tied to the standards of sane and normal behavior that humans apply to their fellows. Many acts that a genius can rationalize as for the greater good\u2015or even demonstrate to be beneficial and useful\u2015are transgressions, since they violate the standards of regular human behavior and erode a genius' ability to mimic sanity. </div> </div> </div>It seems that a few have survived the attempt to rewrite history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T15:22:56-07:00","id":934129,"title":"","content":"That last one was changed to a small m morality rather than Integrity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T15:36:58-07:00","id":934136,"title":"","content":"On the Axioms: could we maybe keep the levels, but recast as some sort of success thresholds rather than dot ratings? For instance: instead of requiring five dots of Automata, require an additional eight successes. <br /> <br /> I also wouldn't mind if Axioms became \u201cSkill unlocks\u201d rather than stand-alone traits: that is, you wouldn't take \u201cApokalypsi\u201d and then apply it to Computer, Academics, and/or Medical; you'd start with dots in (say) Computer, and then spend an Inspired Experience on it to be able to use Computer-based Apokalypti capabilities. Put another way, treat the purchasing of Axioms in a manner similar to how Specialties are acquired. Play up the notion that the skills are at the heart of what Geniuses do, and that Axioms are enhancements to the skills and let them push beyond their normal limits to achieve seemingly impossible results.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T16:38:03-07:00","id":934168,"title":"","content":"I do enjoy the write up on Ethics, but I think chart needs to be adjusted here and there to really reflect the new ideals of Geniuses' Integrity.<br /> Also I really think we should try tying Catalysts into it, since they are supposed to be what connects Geniuses to rest of humanity. Maybe they could grand some way to gain Ethics when mortals have mutual understanding with Genius over it (Straunen and mortal share a moment of awe in front of something impossible but breathtakingly beautiful) or whe Genius breaks out of a stereotype (&quot;In retrospect it does seem like I got overly defensive over that one stupid miscalculation,&quot; Neid admits in front of their ex-colleagues)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12082,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","user":"Weird","date":". 07-20-2016, 05:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T18:35:26-07:00","id":934229,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar134_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"134\" data-vbnamecard=\"134\">The Kings Raven</a>, you've basically struck on nearly everything I wanted out of 2e Genius's Integrity replacement.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=934168#post934168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do enjoy the write up on Ethics, but I think chart needs to be adjusted here and there to really reflect the new ideals of Geniuses' Integrity.<br /> Also I really think we should try tying Axioms into it, since they are supposed to be what connects Geniuses to rest of humanity. Maybe they could grand some way to gain Ethics when mortals have mutual understanding with Genius over it (Straunen and mortal share a moment of awe in front of something impossible but breathtakingly beautiful) or whe Genius breaks out of a stereotype (&quot;In retrospect it does seem like I got overly defensive over that one stupid miscalculation,&quot; Neid admits in front of their ex-colleagues)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Axioms aren't what connects a Genius to humanity. If anything, they serve to set them <i>apart</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T21:31:13-07:00","id":934279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=934136#post934136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the Axioms: could we maybe keep the levels, but recast as some sort of success thresholds rather than dot ratings? For instance: instead of requiring five dots of Automata, require an additional eight successes.<br /> <br /> I also wouldn't mind if Axioms became \u201cSkill unlocks\u201d rather than stand-alone traits: that is, you wouldn't take \u201cApokalypsi\u201d and then apply it to Computer, Academics, and/or Medical; you'd start with dots in (say) Computer, and then spend an Inspired Experience on it to be able to use Computer-based Apokalypti capabilities. Put another way, treat the purchasing of Axioms in a manner similar to how Specialties are acquired. Play up the notion that the skills are at the heart of what Geniuses do, and that Axioms are enhancements to the skills and let them push beyond their normal limits to achieve seemingly impossible results.</div> </div> </div> </div>That has a few flaws. Namely that most of what a Genius wants to use Axioms for falls under the umbrella of &quot;Science.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4968-mrbreaksit","name":"MrBreaksIt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T21:53:35-07:00","id":934290,"title":"","content":"Then why do I see so many references to Computers, Academics, Medicine, and Crafts among the existing Axiom write-ups? In fact, Science shows up only slightly more often than Occult does. And that's just when I restrict myself to the skills referenced under Construction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T23:48:33-07:00","id":934321,"title":"","content":"Personally I'm warming up to the idea making a &quot;tech-tree&quot; like system. You split the Axioms up into chunks each the size of a Mage Spell. Each chunk or &quot;Inference&quot; (I never liked the word Postulate) has links to others, so Apokolipsi bio-scanner would have links to various other scanners, but it might also have a link to Exelixi healing.<br /> <br /> A Genius can buy an Inference adjacent to any Inference they already know, and Axioms serve as a starting point.<br /> <br /> Multiple Inferences can be used in a wonder, based on <i>Reach</i> (a scientific sounding name would be nice). Each Inference has a Reach cost and a Construction Skill and a Genius' Reach is equal to the <u>lowest</u> Skill of the Inferences they plan to include. E.G. if they want to build a scanner that can do Biological, Physical and Metanormal scans they must have at least 3 dots in Science, Medicine and Occult. More powerful Inferences might cost additional reach, and even some Variables might cost Reach. (E.G. Apokolypsi Alerts might work better as a Variable that costs Reach and requires an AI based Inference than as an Inference)<br /> <br /> In addition there must be links between all the Inferences used. You could create a biological scanner that's also an Exelixi healer, but you couldn't make a physical scanner + healing unless you also included a biological scanner to bridge the gap. How they work togeather is left to common sense. An omni scanner could scan with every Infrance at once, but a scanner + healer would probably require you to choose scanning or healing at the point of use. It's best to think of it as two separate Wonders in one physical object and with a reduced mania cost.<br /> <br /> When a Genius builds a Wonder they need to know all the Inferences included in that Wonder. However when they Kitbash they do not. When a Genius does Deep Inspiration they Kitbash and gain an additional Inspiration dots of Reach. However unless their Magnum Opus or Obsession applies to the situation this is very dangerous.<br /> <br /> Of course this being me, that system could be ridiculously over-engineered and I'd be fine with it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=934229#post934229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar134_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"134\" data-vbnamecard=\"134\">The Kings Raven</a>, you've basically struck on nearly everything I wanted out of 2e Genius's Integrity replacement.</div> </div> </div> </div> The secret is years of experience homebrewing <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Save</span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 07-20-2016, 07:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T02:06:32-07:00","id":934355,"title":"","content":"Typed Axioms instead of Catalysts. How embarassing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T02:16:28-07:00","id":934357,"title":"","content":"I'd just say that Catalyst appropriate Transgressions give you an extra die on your degeneration roll. No need for it to be more complex than that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T11:12:59-07:00","id":938961,"title":"","content":"Regarding Ethics: I'm iffy on it as the Integrity equivalent. The way it is described, it brings the discussion back to Hubris/Humility. At high Ethics, you're choosing to submit to the consensus (the repeated references to the consensus brings M:tA to mind), at low Ethics you're saying &quot;Screw that, I know what's right&quot;. That does align with a lot of mad scientist characters (The Doctor, Morbius, Moreau, Laurience, etc), but I thought that wasn't what you were going for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=928678#post928678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd keep the focus on the Genius' ability to recognise and care about what other people think and feel.<ul><li>Paragon: I understand why you find the idea of uploading into a robotic body icky, but it will free humanity from our violent and savage natures.</li> <li>Mid Range: Hold on a second, you're not chearing? Igor, why aren't people leaping at the chance for robotiziation?</li> <li>Bottoming out: I have scientifically proven that robotic bodies are the best solution. Minions, start abducting people and throw them into the robotiziation chambers!</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Ethics covers the bottoming out on that, but not the paragon or mid range.<br /> <br /> On different subject: Reworking Havoc+Jabir<br /> <br /> There's been something that's been bugging me since I saw someone dismiss G:tT as just a M:tA clone for nWoD. It's not an entirely invalid criticism, one that I think could be addressed by reworking Jabir and Havoc.<br /> <br /> The &quot;Mad Scientists' inventions only work for them&quot; is a superhero trope, not a mad science trope. It's an explanation for why Reed Richards is Useless, and one that is rarely used well. It shows up in DC, Marvel, Worm and the Whately Universe. It treats Mad Science as magic, which is where the M:tA comparisons come in.<br /> <br /> Looking at works where the focus is Mad Science (ex: The Forbidden Planet, The Man Who Changed His Mind, The Island of Doctor Moreau, Narbonic/Skin Horse, Girl Genius, Miracle of Science, Doctor Who (sometimes)) that trope isn't in effect.<br /> To my mind, Narbonic/Skin Horse acts as a very good example of what G:tT is aiming for. You have a population of Mad Scientists (Genii), their Henchmen (Beholden) and the travesties against nature and decency they have created (Orphans/Manes), all being willfully ignored by the general population. That setting also has a character whose job is reverse engineering Mad Science devices. In Doctor Who/Torchwood, there are mere mortal scientists who are making progress on copying the sonic screwdriver. Agatha Heterodyne can pass off a death ray to anyone.<br /> <br /> Based on that, I'd say that Wonders are not intrinsically linked to their creators. However, it's also true that their use is not without risk, and that risk can outweigh the reward as perceived by a mere mortal.<br /> For example: hand a random person off the street a normal screwdriver and the Sonic Screwdriver without any instructions. In the hands of a skilled operator, the Sonic Screwdriver is a monstrously more effective tool. In the hands of the untrained mere mortal, the normal screwdriver will be more useful.<br /> In another example: take a caveman, shove them in the cab of a big rig, tell them the gas pedal makes it go, the brake pedal makes it stop and that the steering wheel tells it which way to go. See how well they handle changing gears while taking a corner.<br /> <br /> My suggestion: make it so that Wonders experience Havoc due to misuse, not because they intrinsically break down for mere mortals. Make it so that the Jabir penalty leads to misuse.<br /> <br /> All Wonders require a roll for mere mortals to use, and that roll suffers from the Geniuses Jabir penalty.<br /> Ex: Intelligence + Athletics to put on the armor correctly. Intelligence + Science to align the forcefield emitters correctly. Wits + Firearms to properly calibrate and operate the death ray.<br /> <br /> Difficulty of this roll is based on power of Wonder, let's say 1 + rating of highest Axiom used to make the Wonder (or whatever would be appropriate going with a Tech Tree/Inference system)<br /> <br /> Dramatic failure causes Havoc: The gun explodes in your hands because you didn't set up the heatsink correctly. You try to shift gears without using the clutch while making too sharp a turn, damaging the vehicle. You keep cycling the power button and fry the computer.<br /> Failure causes the Wonder to not work properly, suffering the Genius's Jabir penalty to all rolls or benefits. You fail to properly link the death ray's IFF, rangefinder and recoil dampeners, resulting in inaccurate shots that don't do the damage they should (Jabir penalty to attack and damage rolls). You put on the armor, but you're wearing it wrong so it doesn't defend you as well (Jabir penalty to armor values). You've got no idea how to properly shift gears, so you're stuck in first for a transcontinental drive (Jabir penalty to drive rolls). Suffering a dramatic failure on a roll suffering from Jabir causes Havoc.<br /> Success allows you to get the full benefit of the Wonder. Yay!<br /> Dramatic Success allows you to use the Wonder to its fullest extent, the activation for that type of Wonder becomes a Rote Action and you get a bonus to activation rolls with Wonders made by that Genius in the future.<br /> <br /> For a Genius, witnessing a Dramatic Failure on a roll influenced by Jabir suffers a breaking point. On the other hand, witnessing a Dramatic Success allows you regain Ethics/Obligation/Connection.<br /> <br /> There is also a chance for mere mortals to reverse engineer a Wonder. Doing so would be an extended roll, suffering from Jabir penalty with difficulty determined similar to activation rolls, requiring a lot of threshold successes. Dramatic failures would risk turning Beholden or Catalysing.<br /> Success allows the mere mortal to recreate the Wonder with a much lower difficulty activation roll and no Jabir penalty (activation failure inflicts a -1).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7874-thamuzz","user":"Thamuzz","date":". 07-28-2016, 02:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7874-thamuzz","name":"Thamuzz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T11:40:01-07:00","id":938978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thamuzz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=938961#post938961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding Ethics: I'm iffy on it as the Integrity equivalent. The way it is described, it brings the discussion back to Hubris/Humility. At high Ethics, you're choosing to submit to the consensus (the repeated references to the consensus brings M:tA to mind), at low Ethics you're saying &quot;Screw that, I know what's right&quot;. That does align with a lot of mad scientist characters (The Doctor, Morbius, Moreau, Laurience, etc), but I thought that wasn't what you were going for.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Ethics covers the bottoming out on that, but not the paragon or mid range.<br /> <br /> On different subject: Reworking Havoc+Jabir<br /> <br /> There's been something that's been bugging me since I saw someone dismiss G:tT as just a M:tA clone for nWoD. It's not an entirely invalid criticism, one that I think could be addressed by reworking Jabir and Havoc.<br /> <br /> The &quot;Mad Scientists' inventions only work for them&quot; is a superhero trope, not a mad science trope. It's an explanation for why Reed Richards is Useless, and one that is rarely used well. It shows up in DC, Marvel, Worm and the Whately Universe. It treats Mad Science as magic, which is where the M:tA comparisons come in.<br /> <br /> Looking at works where the focus is Mad Science (ex: The Forbidden Planet, The Man Who Changed His Mind, The Island of Doctor Moreau, Narbonic/Skin Horse, Girl Genius, Miracle of Science, Doctor Who (sometimes)) that trope isn't in effect.<br /> To my mind, Narbonic/Skin Horse acts as a very good example of what G:tT is aiming for. You have a population of Mad Scientists (Genii), their Henchmen (Beholden) and the travesties against nature and decency they have created (Orphans/Manes), all being willfully ignored by the general population. That setting also has a character whose job is reverse engineering Mad Science devices. In Doctor Who/Torchwood, there are mere mortal scientists who are making progress on copying the sonic screwdriver. Agatha Heterodyne can pass off a death ray to anyone.<br /> <br /> Based on that, I'd say that Wonders are not intrinsically linked to their creators. However, it's also true that their use is not without risk, and that risk can outweigh the reward as perceived by a mere mortal.<br /> For example: hand a random person off the street a normal screwdriver and the Sonic Screwdriver without any instructions. In the hands of a skilled operator, the Sonic Screwdriver is a monstrously more effective tool. In the hands of the untrained mere mortal, the normal screwdriver will be more useful.<br /> In another example: take a caveman, shove them in the cab of a big rig, tell them the gas pedal makes it go, the brake pedal makes it stop and that the steering wheel tells it which way to go. See how well they handle changing gears while taking a corner.<br /> <br /> My suggestion: make it so that Wonders experience Havoc due to misuse, not because they intrinsically break down for mere mortals. Make it so that the Jabir penalty leads to misuse.<br /> <br /> All Wonders require a roll for mere mortals to use, and that roll suffers from the Geniuses Jabir penalty.<br /> Ex: Intelligence + Athletics to put on the armor correctly. Intelligence + Science to align the forcefield emitters correctly. Wits + Firearms to properly calibrate and operate the death ray.<br /> <br /> Difficulty of this roll is based on power of Wonder, let's say 1 + rating of highest Axiom used to make the Wonder (or whatever would be appropriate going with a Tech Tree/Inference system)<br /> <br /> Dramatic failure causes Havoc: The gun explodes in your hands because you didn't set up the heatsink correctly. You try to shift gears without using the clutch while making too sharp a turn, damaging the vehicle. You keep cycling the power button and fry the computer.<br /> Failure causes the Wonder to not work properly, suffering the Genius's Jabir penalty to all rolls or benefits. You fail to properly link the death ray's IFF, rangefinder and recoil dampeners, resulting in inaccurate shots that don't do the damage they should (Jabir penalty to attack and damage rolls). You put on the armor, but you're wearing it wrong so it doesn't defend you as well (Jabir penalty to armor values). You've got no idea how to properly shift gears, so you're stuck in first for a transcontinental drive (Jabir penalty to drive rolls). Suffering a dramatic failure on a roll suffering from Jabir causes Havoc.<br /> Success allows you to get the full benefit of the Wonder. Yay!<br /> Dramatic Success allows you to use the Wonder to its fullest extent, the activation for that type of Wonder becomes a Rote Action and you get a bonus to activation rolls with Wonders made by that Genius in the future.<br /> <br /> For a Genius, witnessing a Dramatic Failure on a roll influenced by Jabir suffers a breaking point. On the other hand, witnessing a Dramatic Success allows you regain Ethics/Obligation/Connection.<br /> <br /> There is also a chance for mere mortals to reverse engineer a Wonder. Doing so would be an extended roll, suffering from Jabir penalty with difficulty determined similar to activation rolls, requiring a lot of threshold successes. Dramatic failures would risk turning Beholden or Catalysing.<br /> Success allows the mere mortal to recreate the Wonder with a much lower difficulty activation roll and no Jabir penalty (activation failure inflicts a -1).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, a lot of the &quot;Wonders only work safely for Genii&quot; was more to enforce a Masquerade.<br /> <br /> Hmm. I too was planning on proposing moving Havoc to &quot;use or analysis&quot; instead of merely touching. I'd decouple that from Jabir, though. Jabir is the phenomena of &quot;no one&quot; being able to understand your Genius (mostly because to non-inspired, you sound like a crackpot).<br /> <br /> Actually, on that note: How about Jabir is more related to the listener's understanding (read: Skill Rating), with more severe Jabir just aggravating the effect? Like, talk to a pleb about your Wonder involving Science, and you've got a -1 penalty, if that. Talk to an actual scientist (or worse, one with a Specialty in that field) and it's <i>far worse</i>. End result is your impression goes down, no one takes you seriously, and you might even get Conditions like Notorious Quack, Denigrated, or Pariah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T13:02:46-07:00","id":939063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=938978#post938978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, a lot of the &quot;Wonders only work safely for Genii&quot; was more to enforce a Masquerade.<br /> <br /> Hmm. I too was planning on proposing moving Havoc to &quot;use or analysis&quot; instead of merely touching. I'd decouple that from Jabir, though. Jabir is the phenomena of &quot;no one&quot; being able to understand your Genius (mostly because to non-inspired, you sound like a crackpot).<br /> <br /> Actually, on that note: How about Jabir is more related to the listener's understanding (read: Skill Rating), with more severe Jabir just aggravating the effect? Like, talk to a pleb about your Wonder involving Science, and you've got a -1 penalty, if that. Talk to an actual scientist (or worse, one with a Specialty in that field) and it's <i>far worse</i>. End result is your impression goes down, no one takes you seriously, and you might even get Conditions like Notorious Quack, Denigrated, or Pariah.</div> </div> </div> </div>My idea is that Jabir penalizes the activation roll due to a disconnect in design philosophy. Basically physical technobabble. To the Genius, swiping your finger along the purple strip from front to back then pressing the green button is a perfectly reasonable way to discharge the capacitors, while swiping from front to back then pressing the orange button is a perfectly intuitive way to prime the self destruct.<br /> <br /> From a gameplay standpoint, there isn't a lot to incentivize a player to pursue situations where Jabir might come up. A ST can craft scenarios where it comes up, sure, but I'd like to add some reward to the risk-reward analysis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7874-thamuzz","name":"Thamuzz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T14:09:47-07:00","id":939126,"title":"","content":"FYI, computer is dead. Posting from phone. Unable to continue work for time being.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T08:17:23-07:00","id":939544,"title":"","content":"Are we still considering redeeming Lemuria as Peerage's frenzied &quot;roommate&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T08:30:45-07:00","id":939552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=939544#post939544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are we still considering redeeming Lemuria as Peerage's frenzied &quot;roommate&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the Invisible War still happened. I see them more as bitter rivals who now sometimes wonder why they hated each other <i>quite</i> so much. They still don't like each other, but it's not &quot;kill on sight&quot; anymore, and they can appreciate some of the others' strengths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T09:11:30-07:00","id":939576,"title":"","content":"How I would approach &quot;redeeming Lemuria&quot;<br /> <br /> \u2022Diversify Lemurians: not all Unmada, but mostly unmada creating contrast to Peerage's non-unmada majority (could be made a positive feature, since Peerage basically encourages their Unmadas to hide their true nature); Anchronism may remain but shouldn't be the core of their existence. As matter of fact even the first edition Baramins didn't really fit! What era did Phenomenologist weep over? Why are so many Machinist more exicted about market than fatalism? Didn't Atomist weep over the zeerusted future rather than actual past?<br /> \u2022Make Lemurian's do right things when Peers do wrong: the Peerage was foil of Lemurian Empire, it's logical that beat up Lemuria would try to be foil of Invisible Empire. Lemurians could recognize difference between medically recognized mental disorders and disorders caused by Inspiration, making them think that Peerage's constant &quot;You are Mad!&quot; sounds like gaslighting tactic? Lemurians could be the guys who scavange up experiments and equipment from supernatural accidents (for their mercantuses and personal projects) to stop it from falling into mortals' hands and result in havoc? Maybe Lemurian's are The Face of Genius when interacting with other Supernaturals since Peerage's often sceptical and bitter mindset is rather unfriendly?<br /> \u2022Exploring hypocricities of Peerage: We already had mentions of older Peers acting sometimes as bad as Lemurians, Peer Illumiated, mentions of Peers manipulating recruits for personal profit and Peerage's fanatical Extermination Squads? This could create just as interesting and terrifying enemies as Lemuria. <br /> \u2022Creating examples of exciting cooperations and childishness of mutual pettiness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12082,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","user":"Weird","date":". 07-29-2016, 03:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T12:15:27-07:00","id":939698,"title":"","content":"In addition: Lemurian Baramin descriptions may need to be extended to lenght of Foundation descriptions, and they might need their own version fo The Law.<br /> <br /> I suggest Lemurian equivalent of Peers' &quot;Fuck Lemuria&quot; is &quot;No Refunds!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T13:00:29-07:00","id":940203,"title":"","content":"Hmph, still bothered by how moralizing words Ethics and Obligation are. These are supposed to represent Geniuses slippery slope away from mundane into the horrifying mindset of Illuminated, but Illuminated aren't less than humans. Obviously they aren't much more than human either, they are just something plain alien (why I felt Alienation would have been correct inverse Integrity stat)...<br /> So how about trying something more blatant? Relation \u2014 how well does Genius relate to humans?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T20:15:05-07:00","id":940410,"title":"","content":"Guys, I want to note something: integrity isn't about how you're going to act, it's about how past events have scarred you.<br /> <br /> Notice how, with Dragon's Conviction, we've got Breaking Points which push towards Hubris whenever an event reinforces megalomania, and ones which push towards Guilt whenever they fail to live up to being a goddamn super-powerful Dragon. As Hubris encroaches, self-image becomes more powerful, but selfish whims and instincts become less manageable. As Guilt encroaches, self image becomes weaker while self-loathing begins to drive them to self-destruction, but determination to do just one thing right pushes them forward. The scale shows how well they're managing their newfound sense of power as it teeters between the two unhealthy extremes.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, with Vampire (which I think might be the closest to this), you have Humanity. Vampires are clinging to the last shreds of their humanity, and every time it's reinforced that they are no longer human, they slip. They can have human touchstones around to keep them from losing it faster, but as the years wear on, simply outliving eras without aging is a constant reminder that they are apart from humanity. As they slip, it shows, because the supernatural afflictions which separate them from humanity get worse.<br /> <br /> Try and think of a system based on a series of mental-scars and psychological-reinforcements, and the benefits and consequences of those experiences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T00:48:56-07:00","id":940522,"title":"","content":"Finally somebody gets it!!<br /> Exactly what I was talking about with my rage against Obligation and attempt to explain Alienation! The obvious breaking points for Genius are easy to define. Geniuses don't take heel-realization well. For example wittnessing mundane take a breaking point caused by Genius or mania will cause Genius to question their existence. The good option in this situation is for Genius to realize that yes, this is pretty fucked up, while the big T Transgression is Genius deciding that mortal is wrong and Genius is right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12082,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","user":"Weird","date":". 07-31-2016, 04:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T05:42:14-07:00","id":942652,"title":"","content":"Should we maybe include examples of Illuminated in media? First few to come to mind are Bill Cipher (Illuminated Unmada Mane with complete mastery of Metatropi), Kilgrave (Illuminated with tons of extremely strong internalized Epikatro wonder), Evil Rick Sanchez, Dr. Brenner may qualify too.<br /> <br /> Also I think we should make Geniuses' fear of unwilling exposure more mechanically justified and more terrifying. Nothing should throw Genius in greater panic than possibility of their unfinished or unstable Wonder being exposed to their friends and relatives, and thought of their grabby ignorant hands reaching towards it sends shivers down any Genius's spine. Of course any competent Storyteller is likely to inflict countless mundane humans with fatal case of grabby hands, but it moves blame away from Genius who made a super-intelligent deathdispenser onto another mortal who was just too stupid to realize that maybe touching something that looks like it might kill you a bad idea.<br /> Perhaps mortals exposed to mania suffer from sapped sense of self-preservation and critical thinking? This would once again move responsibility onto Genius, to make sure that mundanes won't be exposed to maniacal activity in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12082,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","user":"Weird","date":"Than. Basic grammar, Weird. Keep your jabir in check damnit! 08-03-2016, 09:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T06:40:26-07:00","id":942675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=942652#post942652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also I think we should make Geniuses' fear of unwilling exposure more mechanically justified and more terrifying. Nothing should throw Genius in greater panic that possibility of their unfinished or unstable Wonder being exposed to their friends and relatives, and thought of their grabby ignorant hands reaching towards it sends shivers down any Genius's spine. Of course any competent Storyteller is like to inflict countless mundane humans with fatal case of grabby hands, but it moves blame away from Genius who made a super-intelligent deathdispenser onto another mortal who was just too stupid to realize that maybe touching something that looks like it might kill you a bad idea.<br /> Perhaps mortals exposed to mania suffer from sapped sense of self-preservation and critical thinking? This would once again move responsibility onto Genius, to make sure that mundanes won't be exposed to maniacal activity in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, other than the public mockery and loss of all respect for being exposed as a quack, someone fiddling with a Wonder is a sure-fire ticket to &quot;unfortunate circumstances&quot;. Sure, the <i>Genius</i> thinks the Wonder's operation makes perfect sense, and there is <i>no reason</i> to push the &quot;Kill Everything&quot; or &quot;Self Destruct Lair&quot; buttons, but somehow most people don't just automatically know what those large, unlabelled red buttons do.<br /> <br /> Though if you want, you could always make Mania generate a subtle, passive aura of fascination. Genius's are <i>very</i> fascinated by a number of things, after all, it makes sense that the energies of insight and rare distilled Eureka might affect even unInspired minds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T14:38:01-07:00","id":943006,"title":"","content":"I have returned from vacation. Is anyone starting a document to keep track of things.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thamuzz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=938961#post938961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding Ethics: I'm iffy on it as the Integrity equivalent. The way it is described, it brings the discussion back to Hubris/Humility. At high Ethics, you're choosing to submit to the consensus (the repeated references to the consensus brings M:tA to mind), at low Ethics you're saying &quot;Screw that, I know what's right&quot;. That does align with a lot of mad scientist characters (The Doctor, Morbius, Moreau, Laurience, etc), but I thought that wasn't what you were going for.<br /> <br /> Ethics covers the bottoming out on that, but not the paragon or mid range.</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually that stuff is still there. Note this line &quot;As Ethics falls, the genius becomes less and less able to understand the rules of normal sane behaviour and less interested in doing so for any decent reason.&quot; If it looks a little barebones that's because the meat of the concept was to go in the Jabir rules, and I didn't write up any of those.<br /> <br /> Also it's important to note that while Hubris can lead to lower Ethics. Hubris is <b>not</b> the same thing as Ethics. You could be a humble, unassuming clockmaker who's only goal is to make a perfectly accurate clock, and who simply doesn't understand that chopping up orphans for parts is wrong. That's a charachter with low Ethics and low Hubris.<br /> <br /> This means that Ethics can model iconic works like Girl Genius where Baron Wulfenbach isn't noticeably more Hubristic than Agather Hetrodyne despite one being the hero and the other being at best an anti-villain.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thamuzz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=938961#post938961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My suggestion: make it so that Wonders experience Havoc due to misuse, not because they intrinsically break down for mere mortals.</div> </div> </div> </div> I agree with this.<br /> <br /> Also, your roll results are too generous.<br /> <br /> Dramatic failure: The wonder blows up or turns into an Orphan.<br /> Failure should create an additional Fault until the Genius has a chance to recalibrate it.<br /> Success: You can use the wonder.<br /> Exceptional Success: You gain manical insight. Take a Condition, until that Condition is resolved you can use this wonder without having to roll to calibrate it. <b>Drawback: </b>The condition is some form of madness; and you're only a short step away from becoming a Beholden or starting the path to a Breakthrough.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=938978#post938978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, on that note: How about Jabir is more related to the listener's understanding (read: Skill Rating), with more severe Jabir just aggravating the effect? Like, talk to a pleb about your Wonder involving Science, and you've got a -1 penalty, if that. Talk to an actual scientist (or worse, one with a Specialty in that field) and it's <i>far worse</i>. End result is your impression goes down, no one takes you seriously, and you might even get Conditions like Notorious Quack, Denigrated, or Pariah.</div> </div> </div> </div>That could work. I want to completely rework Jabir so that rather than being just a dice pool modifier it's more like Werewolf's Death Rage. You get certain triggers and if one is pressed you have to roll. If you rant or make an epic faux pass and get Conditions like your Igor/Beautiful Daughter is poised to betray you, or you've revealed your plans to James Bond.<br /> <br /> Low Ethics would either make the triggers broader (a Grimm's hatred of the Mafia broadens to all criminals, or worse, all Italians!), worse (the tenure committee don't just deny your application. They grab torches and pitchforks and smash up your laboratory), or both.<br /> <br /> But making the roll at a penalty if you're talking to actual scientists - sure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=939576#post939576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How I would approach &quot;redeeming Lemuria&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> Lemuria don't need &quot;redeeming&quot;. They're already redeemed. Though you're right that &quot;fuck Lemuria&quot; doesn't really work, and they obviously should get full sized write ups.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=939576#post939576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What era did Phenomenologist weep over? Why are so many Machinist more exicted about market than fatalism? Didn't Atomist weep over the zeerusted future rather than actual past?</div> </div> </div> </div> This is a fundamental misunderstanding of the Baramins. They don't weep over eras. They weep over <u>ideas</u> that were proven false.<br /> <br /> Take the Atomists. They weep over the idea that &quot;Technology will save us!&quot;. An idea that died when the power of the atom turned out to create the atom bomb instead of jetpacks, atomic powered cars and The American Dream. The zeerusted future is just the decoration, and you'll get plenty of exceptions: Nanotech Atomists who belive in post scarcity futures. Economists ranting about 2008 happening because banks didn't understand their perfect formulas. Old school hackers complaining that the internet was supposed to end racism because no one could tell your race online. Etc.<br /> <br /> (That said the Mechanists are actually a bit of a mess - I spoke with Moochava about them a while back and he said they don't really have a core idea, he just liked Clockpunk. I also discussed alternatives and we both liked the idea that they're upset that mass production replaced skilled craftsmen.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=939576#post939576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022Exploring hypocricities of Peerage</div> </div> </div> </div> No need. That's already done.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=942652#post942652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should we maybe include examples of Illuminated in media?</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing about Illuminated is that you have to answer a very tough question. &quot;What's the difference between Ethics 1 and Illumination?&quot;. An Ethics 1 Genius is cutting up orphan boys and for all intents and purposes unable to understand any sane thought. You can't just make an Illuminated slightly worse, they need to feel unique and different.<br /> <br /> My suggestion for the Illuminated: Base them on Adolf Hitler. Not wacky mad science Nazis, the real Hitler.<br /> <br /> <br /> Hitler / Nazi anti semitism is essentially insane. It requires you to believe things that are factually untrue, and yet Hitler was able to convince an entire country to believe it with absolutely horrific results.<br /> <br /> That's what an Illuminated should be like. An Ethics 1 Genius is utterly alienated from normal sane people. They might do terrible things to normal sane people, but their ability to interact is mostly limited to blasting them with Katastrofi or Epikrato.<br /> <br /> An Illuminated looks like they have gone through madness and come out the other side. But they haven't. They walk and talk like regular people, but what they're saying is just ever so slightly out of sync with reality. And their Mania is infectious.<br /> <br /> Essentially their Unmada field affects normal people, Havoc proofing their Wonders and convincing everyone they make sense. They still need to see the wonder or speak to the Genius, but they're pre-deposed to believe. In the best case Geniuses have to work around the clock to round up and dispose of all the Jetpacks, find ways to convince people that they never owned a jetpack before they leave the Unmada field and go crazy, and censor social media to stop people outside the Unmada field going crazy.<br /> <br /> In the worst case the Illuminated convinces people to commit genocide.<br /> <br /> <br /> Oh. And Geniuses cannot tell an Ethics 4-6 Unmada Genius from an Illuminated. Sometimes it's obvious - if mortals are building and buying devices based on a publicly disporved scientific theory like the luminiferous aether someone's obviously Illumianted. But there's plenty of cases where some legitimate new mortal invention (lets say Graphine) catches the imaginiation of an Unmada and other Geniuses who think that Graphine is actually mad nonsense kill the &quot;Illuminated&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-03-2016, 05:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T15:41:29-07:00","id":943057,"title":"","content":"I'd like Illuminated to push the Alien hyper-scientific danger rather than make them an example of the worst human charisma can offer.<br /> <br /> Something like...<br /> Illuminated's original personality has entirely burned away. Sure they still have memories and can perfectly mimic the fragile humanity of their former egg shell, but the mind behind those glowing eyes is much more like True Fea than something that human could possibly recognize. Illuminated become oblivious to their bodily needs and functions, easily starving or overworking themselves if they can't remember their daily routine, but when they show up the world around them becomes exactly like what their past personality was trying to fathom on their spread sheets: Sky becomes divided into neat star map grid with constellations marked out and named, or human skin has a pre-set cutting line. Or New York gets overflown with ghosts! Or sky tears apart and giant pyramid of All Seeing Eye springs out of the ground! <br /> Each Illuminated believes themself to be completely alone in the universe, after all one can only with 100% confidence say that one is the free thinking individual, however it's common courtesy to assume that so is everyone else; Illuminated haven't heard of common courtesy and threat everything and anything, everyone and anyone, with same respect and understanding as bug collector respects the insects they preserve on the needles in their collection. They know others might kill them if they ever get a chance to realize that Illuminated is a threat, but Illuminated doesn't, no, <i>cannot </i>comprehend that there are minds beside their own in the universe.<br /> <br /> In a way I'd want Illuminated to be the exact opposite of strongest Clockstoppers like Walking Man. The elemental destructive force of potential of science and culture, but without any restrain or humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T16:25:23-07:00","id":943089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=943057#post943057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like Illuminated to push the Alien hyper-scientific danger rather than make them an example of the worst human charisma can offer.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was more an exmaple of the worst a bad idea can do... but I just don't feel your idea is horrific.<br /> <br /> The True Fae are relatable because they're relatable, not all Changeling players have personally suffered abuse, but we can all understand the fear of being completely in someone else's power and them abusing that power.<br /> <br /> Illuminated as reality warpers aren't relatable. Their very alienness makes them less horrific. In contrast Lovecraft's creations, the gold standard for alien horror, was a metaphor for a cold uncaring unverse which is a very relatable concept. The Illuminated (like most things in Genius) need to be the same, they can't just be weird, powerful and dangerous, they have to have a deeper message that the players can relate to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=943057#post943057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a way I'd want Illuminated to be the exact opposite of strongest Clockstoppers like Walking Man. The elemental destructive force of potential of science and culture, but without any restrain or humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I want the same thing. But flooding New York with ghosts is not the way to do it. Sometimes less is more.<br /> <br /> Having mortals build factories that create robots, that in turn put people out of work until they starve on the streets is more horrific than having an army of robots appear out of mid air. The first is Thatcherism or the American rust belt. The second is an episode of Doctor Who which will be resolved in 45 to 90 minuets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T16:43:22-07:00","id":943099,"title":"","content":"This might be shooting off the hip, but trying to think in things that have already been done... How about Illuminated as Phyrexians for Magic the Gathering (if you are familiar with them). The lot of their recent inspiration is taking the good of progress too far and turning it into terrifying and sickening, in their cold calculative search for the Compleated state of all. They even talk in terms of &quot;us&quot; and &quot;not-us&quot;, from which the incompleate &quot;not-us&quot; should and must be cut apart and reassembled into their idea of perfection?<br /> <br /> Ultimately how I'd separate Ethics 1 from Illuminated:<br /> <b>Ethics 1:</b> <i>Only I know the truth!</i><br /> <b>Illuminated: </b><i>Only I am true.</i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12082,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","user":"Weird","date":". 08-03-2016, 07:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T08:21:14-07:00","id":946178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=943006#post943006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have returned from vacation. Is anyone starting a document to keep track of things.<br /> <br /> <br /> Actually that stuff is still there. Note this line &quot;As Ethics falls, the genius becomes less and less able to understand the rules of normal sane behaviour and less interested in doing so for any decent reason.&quot; If it looks a little barebones that's because the meat of the concept was to go in the Jabir rules, and I didn't write up any of those.<br /> <br /> Also it's important to note that while Hubris can lead to lower Ethics. Hubris is <b>not</b> the same thing as Ethics. You could be a humble, unassuming clockmaker who's only goal is to make a perfectly accurate clock, and who simply doesn't understand that chopping up orphans for parts is wrong. That's a charachter with low Ethics and low Hubris.<br /> <br /> This means that Ethics can model iconic works like Girl Genius where Baron Wulfenbach isn't noticeably more Hubristic than Agather Hetrodyne despite one being the hero and the other being at best an anti-villain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmmmm... I'd suggest re-wording it to deemphasis the idea that the genius is submitting to the judgement of the masses.<br /> &quot;At high Ethics, a Genius is capable of reverse engineering their ethical framework based on the mores and values of society&quot;<br /> Something like that, emphasizing connection/comprehension of mere mortals rather than a willingness place society's rules over their own judgement.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=943006#post943006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with this.<br /> <br /> Also, your roll results are too generous.<br /> <br /> Dramatic failure: The wonder blows up or turns into an Orphan.<br /> Failure should create an additional Fault until the Genius has a chance to recalibrate it.<br /> Success: You can use the wonder.<br /> Exceptional Success: You gain manical insight. Take a Condition, until that Condition is resolved you can use this wonder without having to roll to calibrate it. <b>Drawback: </b>The condition is some form of madness; and you're only a short step away from becoming a Beholden or starting the path to a Breakthrough.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the things I want is for a Wonder to under-perform a mundane equivalent in mere mortal hands, and I'm not sure* that layering on the Faults is the right way to go.<br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">I'd suggest that creating an Orphan should be the result of mere mortals trying to actually reverse engineer a Wonder.</span><br /> Edit: Disregard, I was mixing up Orphans and Pandorans in my mind.<br /> <br /> Maybe:<br /> <br /> Dramatic failure: The Wonder is unusuable and suffers Havoc.<br /> Failure: The wonder simply does not work.<br /> Success: Wonder does not work properly, suffering the Genius's Jabir penalty to all rolls or benefits. You fail to properly link the death ray's IFF, rangefinder and recoil dampeners, resulting in inaccurate shots that don't do the damage they should (Jabir penalty to attack and damage rolls). You put on the armor, but you're wearing it wrong so it doesn't defend you as well (Jabir penalty to armor values). You've got no idea how to properly shift gears, so you're stuck in first for a transcontinental drive (Jabir penalty to drive rolls). Suffering a dramatic failure on a roll suffering from Jabir causes Havoc.<br /> Exceptional Success: You gain manical insight. Take a Condition, until that Condition is resolved you can use this wonder without penalty or having to roll to calibrate it. <b>Drawback: </b>The condition is some form of madness; and you're only a short step away from becoming a Beholden or starting the path to a Breakthrough.<br /> <br /> *Genuinely uncertain. I can see it working, depending on revisions to the Fault system, but I really like using the Jabir penalty for this, since I feel it helps justify Genius isolation. Its not that their devices are actually magic, its just that their HMI prevents mere mortals from adopting their tech.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7874-thamuzz","user":"Thamuzz","date":". 08-08-2016, 11:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7874-thamuzz","name":"Thamuzz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T06:34:47-07:00","id":946912,"title":"","content":"I'm in favor of Havoc being the result of Mere Mortals &quot;using it wrong&quot;, generally speaking, at least for operated Wonders. I'd probably want some sort of Mania induced compulsion for Mortals to use the Wonder, however (a subtle Pandora's Box temptation). That would &quot;encourage&quot; such incidents from occurring even from people without the compulsive &quot;touch anything&quot; vice.<br /> <br /> Hmm. Possibly the &quot;Mortal Analysis&quot; Havoc Trigger might be more confronting the Genius with evidence/explanation on why Wonder XYZ is impossible. There, it is the doubt, however subconscious, that afflicts the Genius's mind that sabotages their own Wonder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T08:55:11-07:00","id":946974,"title":"","content":"Giving the mortal a Beat when they trigger Havoc would do Pandora's Box nicely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=946912#post946912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. Possibly the &quot;Mortal Analysis&quot; Havoc Trigger might be more confronting the Genius with evidence/explanation on why Wonder XYZ is impossible. There, it is the doubt, however subconscious, that afflicts the Genius's mind that sabotages their own Wonder.</div> </div> </div> </div>Geniuses know their wonder's run on nonsense so this doesn't make sense.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T09:31:50-07:00","id":947008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=946974#post946974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Giving the mortal a Beat when they trigger Havoc would do Pandora's Box nicely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Storyteller character's don't really track Beats much, though. &lt;shrug&gt;<br /> <br /> Maybe roll Willpower vs the Wonder's Rank or Jabir penalty at the end of each scene and/or if the Wonder would be useful? Give someone an energy shield, and they'll be tempted to use it, warnings be damned, if it could be useful?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=946974#post946974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Geniuses know their wonder's run on nonsense so this doesn't make sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>But sincerely held nonsense? Unmada don't think it is nonsense. I'm reaching for some justification here. Immaterial, passive, and internalized Wonders need some way to trigger Havoc, I think.<br /> <hr /><br /> As far as the effects of Havoc rolls, I think it should probably be a flexible as Mage's Paradox results. Faults in the Wonder are an option, as are &quot;mistargeting&quot;, power surges (and loss), inverted use (using a Healing Wonder may inflict harm), etc., with Orphan being the equivalent of &quot;calls an Abyssal entity into being&quot; as the <i>really bad</i> thing that could happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 08-09-2016, 12:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T09:34:53-07:00","id":947010,"title":"","content":"Passive wonders still need to be turned on - a suit of armour needs to be buckled up. Internalized wonders can inflict Faults on the genius themself and are limited to Size 0. Immaterial wonders don't really exist, they have to be contained within something physical even if only the Genius' brain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T09:41:38-07:00","id":947021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=947010#post947010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Passive wonders still need to be turned on - a suit of armour needs to be buckled up. Internalized wonders can inflict Faults on the genius themself and are limited to Size 0. Immaterial wonders don't really exist, they have to be contained within something physical even if only the Genius' brain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are Internalized Wonders safe from Havoc, then? Definitely a major advantage, if so. Of course, you also are saddled with a Fault you can't just turn off either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T14:41:04-07:00","id":947233,"title":"","content":"Ultimately it seems like Illuminated otherness and inhumanity is left to be portrayed by each Storyteller, but I fee like guidelines that might help capturing their Illuminated-ness:<br /> <br /> -No Endgame. Illuminated's grand plan is all they have. There is no next step. Their achievement is as far as they have planned (usually because there is nothing left to plan after you extinguish the sun or engineer a plague that will kill all life on Earth.)<br /> <br /> -Utterly driven and obsessive to the point beyond human limits. Illuminated never stop to wonder if what's they are doing is right or good. It doesn't matter. They have put their minds to it, and there is no turning back.<br /> <br /> -Inconvenient fragile shell. It's quite clear that Illuminated are not human despite having a human body and human memories, but despite of this very few of them seems to be actually familiar with its need and basic functions which results with them often straining themselves too hard or are taken completely by surprise when they feel pain.<br /> <br /> -Murder is best option. First and foremost solution Illuminated seem to find when dealing with any inconvenient form of life is to end it. Each Illuminated believes in a way that they are the only thinking sentient being in the universe and that eventually anything that might kill them will try to kill them, so each Illuminated saves themselves a lot of trouble by killing anything that comes across their way at slightest opportunity unless they have a better use for mostly live thing.<br /> <br /> -Distractions. Illuminated no longer feel need to even bother with their virtues and vices (honestly they'd need less human willpower regaining mechanic upgrade). To them there is only They, The Goal, and Distractions. Some distractions are particularly pleasant to Illuminated and require additional effort to hold back (resolve + compulsion), such distractions are often their past people of interest (extremely bad news to those people since Illuminated usually seek to eliminate them to stop worrying about them) or addictions or phobias. <br /> For example Glutonious Genius will still need to resist gorging themselves after they lost interest for food in general in favor of building a blackhole in their basement, and Genius who used to be particularly afraid of germs ends up upon becoming Illuminated being unable to work in enviroment that isn't perfectly sanitary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12082,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","user":"Weird","date":". 08-09-2016, 07:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T07:01:56-07:00","id":947736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=947233#post947233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ultimately it seems like Illuminated otherness and inhumanity is left to be portrayed by each Storyteller, but I fee like guidelines that might help capturing their Illuminated-ness:<br /> <br /> -No Endgame. Illuminated's grand plan is all they have. There is no next step. Their achievement is as far as they have planned (usually because there is nothing left to plan after you extinguish the sun or engineer a plague that will kill all life on Earth.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I'd add some commentary alone the lines of not all Goals are omnicidal (such as mass AI transcendence, individual opinion on the matter irrelevant). And that the individual steps/phases of a goal can be sufficiently complex as to each seem like their own overriding plot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=947233#post947233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Utterly driven and obsessive to the point beyond human limits. Illuminated never stop to wonder if what's they are doing is right or good. It doesn't matter. They have put their minds to it, and there is no turning back.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly fine with this. There Is Only The Goal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=947233#post947233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Inconvenient fragile shell. It's quite clear that Illuminated are not human despite having a human body and human memories, but despite of this very few of them seems to be actually familiar with its need and basic functions which results with them often straining themselves too hard or are taken completely by surprise when they feel pain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, this could be common, if not absolute. It would also serve to explain why so few Illuminated <i>stay</i> human (transforming themselves into cybernetic dragons, self-propagating memetic viruses, merging with energy fields larger than their head, etc.).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=947233#post947233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Murder is best option. First and foremost solution Illuminated seem to find when dealing with any inconvenient form of life is to end it. Each Illuminated believes in a way that they are the only thinking sentient being in the universe and that eventually anything that might kill them will try to kill them, so each Illuminated saves themselves a lot of trouble by killing anything that comes across their way at slightest opportunity unless they have a better use for mostly live thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I say no to &quot;Murder is best option&quot;. I'd rephrase it as &quot;brutally efficient&quot;. If killing someone prevents them from causing further problems, sure that's the optimum choice (as morality, ethics, and such things are irrelevant to the Illuminated). But if it would cause further problems, then the least intensive effort is then chosen (lying, sending minions to distract them, etc.). Does it further the Goal? Yes = do it. No = don't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=947233#post947233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Distractions. Illuminated no longer feel need to even bother with their virtues and vices (honestly they'd need less human willpower regaining mechanic upgrade). To them there is only They, The Goal, and Distractions. Some distractions are particularly pleasant to Illuminated and require additional effort to hold back (resolve + compulsion), such distractions are often their past people of interest (extremely bad news to those people since Illuminated usually seek to eliminate them to stop worrying about them) or addictions or phobias.<br /> For example Glutonious Genius will still need to resist gorging themselves after they lost interest for food in general in favor of building a blackhole in their basement, and Genius who used to be particularly afraid of germs ends up upon becoming Illuminated being unable to work in enviroment that isn't perfectly sanitary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Their peculiar insanities should inform their actions more, yeah. To the point of superseding any of the above points.<br /> <br /> At least, until they &quot;edit&quot; out such flaws in their psyche.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T09:28:54-07:00","id":947819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=947736#post947736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I say no to &quot;Murder is best option&quot;. I'd rephrase it as &quot;brutally efficient&quot;. If killing someone prevents them from causing further problems, sure that's the optimum choice (as morality, ethics, and such things are irrelevant to the Illuminated). But if it would cause further problems, then the least intensive effort is then chosen (lying, sending minions to distract them, etc.). Does it further the Goal? Yes = do it. No = don't.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like Illuminated defaulting to murder would serve to contrast them to low Integrity Geniuses. Crooked Genius is unlikely to see problem with murdering someone if it gets them what they want but might find idea of casual pointless murder waste of time. Illuminated as beings that usually see all life as a thing opposing to them, have inclination to think &quot;Will continuation of this life benefit the Goal? Yes, keep it alive./No, better kill it now and ask questions later.&quot;<br /> <br /> Genius: Spare when can, murder when need to.<br /> Illuminated: Murder when can, spare when need to.<br /> <br /> Note that in this case however murder and overwriting individual's identity are synonymous, if Illuminated wants all life to &quot;join&quot; them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12082,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","user":"Weird","date":". 08-10-2016, 12:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T23:23:02-07:00","id":948399,"title":"","content":"No. That would be extreemly boring and the opposite of horrific. It would make Illuminated into something like Warhammer 40K's Khorne. With cute memes about blood for the blood god.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T02:29:19-07:00","id":948460,"title":"","content":"I mean if players who couldn't take Illuminated seriously would get to play as them that would inevitably be the result, but they are by their very nature NPC. As such the default to murder would mean that when confronting the Illuminated PCs either need to be able to flight or fight or in worst case scenario convince Illuminated that they are vital to their plot alive. Which in the peaceful situation when done right by thr Storyteller should create tension in the player when they are dealing with seemingly normal Genius whose behaviour starts to give out subtle hints about being Illuminated; Can we convince them not to kill us? Where is closest exit? Can I draw my raygun before they draw theirs?<br /> Or do you have better way to sell that Illuminated are completely inhumane beings without any morals that posses direct threat to everyone they come across without limiting Storyteller options and variety?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T10:10:51-07:00","id":948663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=946974#post946974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Giving the mortal a Beat when they trigger Havoc would do Pandora's Box nicely.<br /> <br /> Geniuses know their wonder's run on nonsense so this doesn't make sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd really like to move away from that interpretation, (see Superhero vs Mad Scientist tropes). Maybe make the whole &quot;we're working with madness, not real science&quot; thing be a Peerage coping mechanism; an easy out from shoving your arm into the pit of rusting iron and broken glass (Jabir/Havoc/failure and the ridicule that comes with it) in search of that one pure nugget of gold (public acceptance/adoption of a Wonder).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7874-thamuzz","name":"Thamuzz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T10:38:33-07:00","id":948677,"title":"","content":"That would break the fundamental themes of the Peerage and either destroy the player's flexibility in choosing how their Wonders work or destroy any hope of a coherent setting.<br /> <br /> In other words: Either<br /> <br /> 1) Every cool-but-wrong scientific theory in history is actually true all at once. Which leads to an incoherent setting.<br /> 2) Geniuses can only use the theories that are actually true. Which removes player flexibility.<br /> 3) Geniuses can use theories which are false. Which is what we have now.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway. There's nothing wrong with including superhero tropes in Genius. Even Girl Genius uses the runs-on-nonsense trope (it's mentioned in the novelizations) and we'll never stop players from building powered armour and fighting crime if we wanted to (which I don't, the Irridum Sentinels are cool). It's far better to accept the superheroic tropes and tie them into Transgression and Bitter Disapointment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T21:58:55-07:00","id":949115,"title":"","content":"I've been doing a lot of work that could be useful for this, but I've been doing it as part of a remake of Mage. For example, I'm working out a new system for creating magical effects which is also meant to be a simpler way to create Wonders. <br /> <br /> Reading the Illuminated ideas was interesting, since I'm keeping them as antagonists. They're sort of the equivalent of Archmasters now, and I'm having them mostly reside in the Astral inside their personal unreality bubbles, but they can intrude on the world.<br /> <br /> Another idea that could be used for Genius is that Mages now develop Bans and Banes as they lose Wisdom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T06:39:08-07:00","id":949280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=949115#post949115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been doing a lot of work that could be useful for this, but I've been doing it as part of a remake of Mage. For example, I'm working out a new system for creating magical effects which is also meant to be a simpler way to create Wonders.<br /> <br /> Reading the Illuminated ideas was interesting, since I'm keeping them as antagonists. They're sort of the equivalent of Archmasters now, and I'm having them mostly reside in the Astral inside their personal unreality bubbles, but they can intrude on the world.<br /> <br /> Another idea that could be used for Genius is that Mages now develop Bans and Banes as they lose Wisdom.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really seeing how Bans and Banes makes sense for Mad Scientists. &quot;Bans&quot;, <i>maybe</i> as particular forms of insanity. Banes, no, unless it is due to a Fault on a Wonder (which, if grafted/Internalized would be permanently on the Genius). But tying it to Obligation/Ethics seems like more of the old Low-Morality Punishment that 2E is moving away from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T11:04:38-07:00","id":949425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=949280#post949280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not really seeing how Bans and Banes makes sense for Mad Scientists. &amp;quot;Bans&amp;quot;, <i>maybe</i> as particular forms of insanity. Banes, no, unless it is due to a Fault on a Wonder (which, if grafted/Internalized would be permanently on the Genius). But tying it to Obligation/Ethics seems like more of the old Low-Morality Punishment that 2E is moving away from.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, since Mage incorporates sorcerers and mad scientists, it might make more sense there. But for Banes, I was thinking more like &quot;universal weaknesses that apply to all Wonders created by that scientist&quot;.<br /> <br /> And MtT uses Wisdom, which isn't so much morality as prudence. The explanation for Workings needing Frailties is that putting limits on them provides protection from the destruction inferno of infinite potential that fuels them, and dropping Wisdom means giving in more and more to that, which also draws you closer to Paradox and the Abyss. So your soul develops restrictions as a subconscious way to protect itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T17:22:09-07:00","id":949649,"title":"","content":"Still bothered that Ethics sounds more like something you'd rename Morality as rather than Integrity. Have been thinking bit more and maybe being blunt with understanding might help? Reflection (as in reflecting how ones behavior affects others), Compassion (self-explanatory), Sensibility (how well Genius can adapt their thinking to normal and use it to explain their point of view), Rationality (self-explantory), Sanity (or would this be too blunt?), or Objectivity (Not saying that high Integrity Geniuses are always objective, but this scale sort of ties into how low integrity Geniuses are willing to sacrifice scientific objectivity in name of subjective wants and needs).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T06:57:21-07:00","id":951083,"title":"","content":"I think we should take another look at how the book defines Obligation so we can identify how it is tied to Morality, and then identify how it could be more like the Integrity traits of 2ED.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Inspired are extreme creatures, capable of great and terrible transgressions. To fight the corrosive influence of those crimes against the natural order, most geniuses focus on the one thing that still ties them to mundane humanity: their Obligation to it. <u><i>Their Obligation may be to improve, to protect, or even to punish, but it ultimately ties them to their unInspired brethren.</i></u> Obligation monitors how close a genius is to losing all ties with humanity and becoming a true mad scientist, one of the Illuminated who has lost all concern for the well-being and dignity of others, and who sees humans as we might see laboratory mice. As Obligation falls, the genius becomes less and less able to interact with normal humans, and less and less interested in doing so for any decent reason.<br /> <br /> Geniuses quickly learn that Obligation is more than Morality: <u><i>it is tied to the standards of sane and normal behavior that humans apply to their fellows.</i></u> Many acts that a genius can rationalize as for the greater good\u2015or even demonstrate to be beneficial and useful\u2015are transgressions, since they violate the standards of regular human behavior and distance a genius from the mortals in his charge. </div> </div> </div> Emphasis mine.<br /> <br /> So what can we gather from this?<br /> <br /> 1) Obligation is about making an effort to think like a regular mortal, in other words, distance yourself somehow from your Inspired worldview.<br /> 2) Obligation can mean different things between one Genius and another. This is similar to the questions of what constitute Breaking Points for Integrity. That is to say, Obligation is not objective.<br /> 3) Obligation cannot be used to rationalize acts which would provoke a Breaking Point in the vast majority of human beings.<br /> <br /> So, here's what I'm thinking. We can stick to the 1 to 10 scale, but make it easier to go from one extreme to the other, to reflect the instability of Inspiration. One day, the Genius might have a firm grasp on how mortals think through effort, but care less the next day.<br /> <br /> We could associate a Condition to each of the extremes.<br /> <br /> Near 10, you would have a Condition that represents your Paragon status, which would allow you to negate some of the penalties of Jabir. However, keeping up this level of Obligation should be taxing and tempt Geniuses to move away from mortal ways of thinking. Perhaps Social rolls to interact with mortals could deplete your Mania reserves, or your Obligation naturally depletes over time.<br /> <br /> Near 1, your Condition of Rogue marks you as dangerous and increases Jabir, but since you are closer to the Inspired worldview, you should gain a bonus to interacting with other Geniuses, Manes, Wonders and other supernaturals relevant to your worldview.<br /> <br /> What I don't know is what Conditions could be associated to the middle of the scale. A Genius with average Obligation should be caught between a rock and a hard place, similar to Beasts at mid Satiety.<br /> <br /> What I would like to is an Obligation that is not bought with Experiences, but handled through scenes that either bring you closer to or further away from mortals. We could something like the Satiety Potential chart, with certain actions granting dice that you roll to increase or decrease your Obligation.<br /> <br /> How does that sound?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 08-15-2016, 10:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T07:51:48-07:00","id":951109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=951083#post951083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we should take another look at how the book defines Obligation so we can identify how it is tied to Morality, and then identify how it could be more like the Integrity traits of 2ED.<br /> <br /> Emphasis mine.<br /> <br /> So what can we gather from this?<br /> <br /> 1) Obligation is about making an effort to think like a regular mortal, in other words, distance yourself somehow from your Inspired worldview.<br /> 2) Obligation can mean different things between one Genius and another. This is similar to the questions of what constitute Breaking Points for Integrity. That is to say, Obligation is not objective.<br /> 3) Obligation cannot be used to rationalize acts which would provoke a Breaking Point in the vast majority of human beings.<br /> <br /> So, here's what I'm thinking. We can stick to the 1 to 10 scale, but make it easier to go from one extreme to the other, to reflect the instability of Inspiration. One day, the Genius might have a firm grasp on how mortals think through effort, but care less the next day.<br /> <br /> We could associate a Condition to each of the extremes.<br /> <br /> Near 10, you would have a Condition that represents your Paragon status, which would allow you to negate some of the penalties of Jabir. However, keeping up this level of Obligation should be taxing and tempt Geniuses to move away from mortal ways of thinking. Perhaps Social rolls to interact with mortals could deplete your Mania reserves, or your Obligation naturally depletes over time.<br /> <br /> Near 1, your Condition of Rogue marks you as dangerous and increases Jabir, but since you are closer to the Inspired worldview, you should gain a bonus to interacting with other Geniuses, Manes, Wonders and other supernaturals relevant to your worldview.<br /> <br /> What I don't know is what Conditions could be associated to the middle of the scale. A Genius with average Obligation should be caught between a rock and a hard place, similar to Beasts at mid Satiety.<br /> <br /> What I would like to is an Obligation that is not bought with Experiences, but handled through scenes that either bring you closer to or further away from mortals. We could something like the Satiety Potential chart, with certain actions granting dice that you roll to increase or decrease your Obligation.<br /> <br /> How does that sound?</div> </div> </div> </div>I like it, in a general sense. I'm more for not requiring XP for something that almost seems to be intended to be lost.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I think it should strongly interact with Touchstones. There are many tales of a mad scientist who has reconsidered when something/someone improtant to them was affected. Or damned themselves completely when they sacrificed even that. I think Touchstones (like Vampire has), would be a good idea to reflect all the ways a Genius has to stay/become &quot;Restrained&quot;.<br /> <br /> I think we all generally agree that High Obligation Genii are: Empathic (even if only in an understanding/abstract sense) of unInspired, Restrained in their pursuit and application of Science.<br /> Low Obligation: Could care less about (most) Mere Mortals, Unrestrained in their pursuit and application of SCIENCE!<br /> <br /> Middle Obligation then seems like they are the Genii that are seen as risky or dangerous, but still mostly mean well. They have lines they don't cross, even if those lines may be odd or still beyond some people's.<br /> <br /> Low Obligation Genii are still distinct from Illuminated in that they still have a <i>few</i> lines left, or they at least know what lines <i>are</i>. (A low-Obligation Genius might know chopping up orphans for parts is wrong, but do so anyways, while an Illuminated wonders why someone left some free material unguarded) <hr /><br /> <u>Elaboration upon Touchstones</u><br /> <br /> You could even have one (at least) be Catalyst inspired/based/dependent:<ul><li>Klagen: The source of their sorrow. It reminds them of why they bother, and repeating it themselves can be lead them to cast off all care.</li> <li>Hoffnung: Their vision of a new/better world (for all, or just someone). Seeing their actions threaten it might shock them back into Obligation, or efforts to &quot;force it&quot; might decay their ethics further.</li> <li>Grimm: Their target of anger. It might drive them to be better, or right wrongs, or drive them to commit the very same wrongs in pursuit of revenge.</li> <li>Neid: Their need for acknowledgement. They might keep on the &quot;straight and narrow&quot; for continued high regard, or descend into the depth in search of it.</li> <li>Staunen: Their sense of wonder. They might ensure they can share their insights and vistas with others, or they might sacrifice other to delve into things only they <i>can</i> see.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> The idea being, the Touchstone(s) are the reason why a Genius bothers... and their loss leads them to question why they should bother.<br /> <br /> Idea: Touchstone &quot;evolution&quot; based on Obligation? Low Obligation has very specific focus, while High Obligation has broader focus? Rather than simply becoming &quot;detached&quot; like in Vampire, that is.<br /> <br /> EDIT: May even be able to link Larvae to Touchstones instead of Transgressions. Or more specifically, a Transgression that costs one a Touchstone. Like the brains of the ethics board that mocked the Neid, or the heart of the Hoffnung's beloved daughter.<br /> <br /> Will elaborate further if someone has questions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 08-15-2016, 04:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T11:22:19-07:00","id":951215,"title":"","content":"For Staunen, maybe something that reminds them of the beauty and wonder in the world, reminding them that things have value in and of themselves?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T13:17:38-07:00","id":951268,"title":"","content":"I'd say for Straunen the thing they can't stand is seeing mortal shocked, horrified, or disgusted by something Straunen saw as beautiful. In that moment Straunen feel intense loathing, either for themselves or the mundane. &quot;What's wrong with me?! Why can't I think and see like other people do!&quot; or &quot;What's wrong with you?! Why can't you see that it's beautiful!&quot;<br /> <br /> The touchstone is sharing a moment of mutual wonder or awe with somebody else. Looking at the stars with loved one, showing of one's latest invention to one's friends and seeing one's excitement reflect in them, or bringing somebody to alien worlds so they see what Straunen has seen. Curiosity, wonder, amazement, and awe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12082,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","user":"Weird","date":". 08-15-2016, 04:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T13:53:35-07:00","id":951295,"title":"","content":"Edited Staunen to reflect Wonder as their key Touchstone. I'm still kinda uncertain on the wording or exact implementations of it, but there it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T14:54:30-07:00","id":951321,"title":"","content":"I think that all the Touchstones should tie into mortals somehow.<br /> <br /> A Grimm's touchstone is a mortal who can restrain and/or direct their anger, teaching them how a sane person handles anger.<br /> A Klagen's touchstone is a mortal they can save from a similar mistake to that which Catalyzed them, teaching them how far they can go before <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-U3jrS-uhuo\" target=\"_blank\">a sane person is more scared of you than of being saved.</a><br /> <br /> And so forth.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T15:05:08-07:00","id":951334,"title":"","content":"That would mean that Neids need someone who's opinions they value over their pride and who they feel loyal to?<br /> Trying to make sure it would be something akin to development of Rick's relationship with his family.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T18:32:56-07:00","id":951421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=951321#post951321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that all the Touchstones should tie into mortals somehow.<br /> <br /> A Grimm's touchstone is a mortal who can restrain and/or direct their anger, teaching them how a sane person handles anger.<br /> A Klagen's touchstone is a mortal they can save from a similar mistake to that which Catalyzed them, teaching them how far they can go before <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-U3jrS-uhuo\" target=\"_blank\">a sane person is more scared of you than of being saved.</a><br /> <br /> And so forth.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can also see it being about people who you have a less positive relationship with:<br /> The Grimm's Touchstone is the crime family that started them on their path. They exemplify themselves by being <i>not</i> like them, and working against their depradations. They fall off the wagon when they stoop to being just like them or commit worse crimes.<br /> The Neid's touchstone is whoever mocked their work. The Genius exemplify themselves when they work to <i>earn</i> respect (on the giver's terms). They dive deeper into madness/callousness when they settle for fear, or outright eliminate them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T23:13:11-07:00","id":951517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=951334#post951334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would mean that Neids need someone who's opinions they value over their pride and who they feel loyal to?<br /> Trying to make sure it would be something akin to development of Rick's relationship with his family.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep.<br /> <br /> (Even though Rick is probably a Klagen his touchstone relationship is pure Neid. If you ignore the fact he was probably a very different person when he was younger)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T12:08:59-07:00","id":953944,"title":"","content":"TBH it never made sence to me that Hoffnungs recieved Narcissism.<br /> <br /> If your Utopia revolves around making the world a better place for other (who you may no longer belong to (any more???)), you shouldn't value yourself more than others.<br /> <br /> You should value your Utopia.<br /> <br /> A penalty to Unmada checks fits much better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T12:41:43-07:00","id":953963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tambov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=953944#post953944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">TBH it never made sence to me that Hoffnungs recieved Narcissism.<br /> <br /> If your Utopia revolves around making the world a better place for other (who you may no longer belong to (any more???)), you shouldn't value yourself more than others.<br /> <br /> You should value your Utopia.<br /> <br /> A penalty to Unmada checks fits much better.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's more &quot;you think <u>your own</u> ideas of Utopia are best&quot;, as opposed to &quot;<u>you</u> are the best&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T12:56:25-07:00","id":953970,"title":"","content":"One of the things I think Moochava did wrong was that he stuck to the origonal corebook Derangements. And Derangements weren't even the best idea since they're purely a stick, you want carrots to reward roleplaying your Catalyst.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't give any Catalyst bonuses or penalties to Unmada checks.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T14:29:37-07:00","id":954043,"title":"","content":"Hello everyone. My main PC is still dead, but I've finally managed to find a laptop that doesn't try to murder me when I use Drive.<br /> <br /> So, what we're talking about now is Anchors and Touchstones, yeah?<br /> <br /> Right, so, are Genii mentally different enough to justify replacing Vice and Virtue? Because I like Magnum Opus and Delusion, but I'm not actually sure if they're inhuman enough to warrant replacing those Anchors, since they're not terribly much more inhuman than Magi. I guess it depends on whether we think Inspiration makes Virtue and Vice irrelevant.<br /> <br /> As for Touchstones, I like the idea of Catalyst-specific ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":4488,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","user":"malonkey1","date":". 08-19-2016, 05:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T15:03:38-07:00","id":954056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=954043#post954043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, so, are Genii mentally different enough to justify replacing Vice and Virtue? Because I like Magnum Opus and Delusion, but I'm not actually sure if they're inhuman enough to warrant replacing those Anchors, since they're not terribly much more inhuman than Magi. I guess it depends on whether we think Inspiration makes Virtue and Vice irrelevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>I vote no, <b>but</b> giving them extra Aspirations (like Mage's Obsessions) and/or Conditions (like Demon's Agendas) to represent Magnum Opus and/or Delusion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=954043#post954043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Touchstones, I like the idea of Catalyst-specific ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, as a starting point. But I do think Genii should be able to pick up all kinds of additional Touchstones to ground them. People who matter to them. Specific principles they won't violate. Etc.<br /> <br /> It also gives one more to use as &quot;fuel&quot; if they become critical to generating Larvae.<br /> <br /> (Rather than just a &quot;I mind controlled someone&quot; Transgression, we are talking about ruining the Orphanage the Genius grew up in just because it is the best site for their Thaum Reactor. It's the sacrifice of something Important upon the altar of Ambition that fuels the Larvae.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 08-19-2016, 06:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T01:01:44-07:00","id":954264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=954056#post954056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I vote no, <b>but</b> giving them extra Aspirations (like Mage's Obsessions) and/or Conditions (like Demon's Agendas) to represent Magnum Opus and/or Delusion.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Yeah, as a starting point. But I do think Genii should be able to pick up all kinds of additional Touchstones to ground them. People who matter to them. Specific principles they won't violate. Etc.<br /> <br /> It also gives one more to use as &quot;fuel&quot; if they become critical to generating Larvae.<br /> <br /> (Rather than just a &quot;I mind controlled someone&quot; Transgression, we are talking about ruining the Orphanage the Genius grew up in just because it is the best site for their Thaum Reactor. It's the sacrifice of something Important upon the altar of Ambition that fuels the Larvae.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I concur completely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T02:29:32-07:00","id":954284,"title":"","content":"I could go either way.<br /> <br /> If not Virtue/Vice I would make Magnum Opus a Long Term Aspiration (one where it's acceptable to choose something that is essentially impossible) and fold just fold Delusion into Jabir*.<br /> <br /> <br /> * For those who missed the first time I see Jabir as workign a bit like Werewolf's Death Rage. You get triggers, say: 1 from Magnum Opus, one from circumstances of your catalyst and one free choice. These get broader as Ethics falls. So a Neid who Canalised from jealousy about not getting tennure might start with the topic of the experiment that failed and &quot;cost him tenure&quot;, then broaden to the field of science, then to all sane science.<br /> <br /> The Jabir roll would probably be Composure with a penalty based on Inspiration, with the results inflicting a Condition. Even a success would have mild conditions like fail a social roll because the other guy thinks you weird. Failure or dramatic failure would result in Igor or your beautiful daughter betraying you or a torch wielding mob.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T08:37:32-07:00","id":954409,"title":"","content":"Okay, so I remembered somebody invoked bans and banes, and while bans make perfect sense as compulsive behavior or irrational fobias, banes don't make sense since they are usually magical and enforce weakness that Geniuses don't generally have.<br /> <br /> But tongue in cheek here are banes I would imagine Mad Scientists to have that could be included as an optional rule: <br /> \u2022Angry Mobs: Genius with this bane looses will to fight back from cheer terror when faced against crowd of adversaries<br /> \u2022Pitchforks: Lethal damage from punctures done with pitchforks upgrades automatically to agravated. 'Menial Labor Allergy'<br /> \u2022Simplicity: Genius with this bane received bashing damage headache from dealing with stuff that isn't at least a little bit complex.<br /> \u2022Own Petard: Genius's wonders tend to be far more effective when turned against them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12082,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","user":"Weird","date":". 08-20-2016, 11:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T09:07:43-07:00","id":954427,"title":"","content":"I was actually thinking that Bans could be more like Batman's One Rule. Which is to say, you can actually break them any time you want but you really shouldn't.<br /> <br /> Lets stick to Batman as an example. Batman decides that it's too complicated trying to figure out when and when beating someone up is appropriate. So he decides he'll keep it simple, killing is never ok (even though mortals know it sometimes is) and beating people up is always acceptable (even though mortals know it rarely is).<br /> <br /> From that moment on Batman can beat people up any time he wants without rolling for an Ethics Violation, but he also gets some Persistent Condition because he's letting his worldview drift further from mortals and sanity. And if he ever <u>intentionally</u> kills someone his Ethics drops all the way down to whatever point killing someone no longer becomes a Transgression.<br /> <br /> To paraphrase batman &quot;Because I'd never stop at one!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T09:10:57-07:00","id":954428,"title":"","content":"I just realized that these banes could be categorized by Catalysts.<br /> Neid: Angry Mobs (Makes them wary of being outnumbered)<br /> Grim: Pitchforks (Violenece begets more violence)<br /> Straunen: Simplicity (Slowly drives them away from mundane)<br /> Hoffnung: Own Petard (Most likely to desire world domination)<br /> Klagen: They are tormented enough by themselves, no banes required.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T22:25:19-07:00","id":954821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=954284#post954284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could go either way.<br /> <br /> If not Virtue/Vice I would make Magnum Opus a Long Term Aspiration (one where it's acceptable to choose something that is essentially impossible) and fold just fold Delusion into Jabir*.<br /> <br /> <br /> * For those who missed the first time I see Jabir as workign a bit like Werewolf's Death Rage. You get triggers, say: 1 from Magnum Opus, one from circumstances of your catalyst and one free choice. These get broader as Ethics falls. So a Neid who Canalised from jealousy about not getting tennure might start with the topic of the experiment that failed and &quot;cost him tenure&quot;, then broaden to the field of science, then to all sane science.<br /> <br /> The Jabir roll would probably be Composure with a penalty based on Inspiration, with the results inflicting a Condition. Even a success would have mild conditions like fail a social roll because the other guy thinks you weird. Failure or dramatic failure would result in Igor or your beautiful daughter betraying you or a torch wielding mob.</div> </div> </div> </div>That works for me. Maybe certain Triggers inflict different conditions, so losing your shit when somebody mocks you would saddle you with an &quot;Enraged&quot; Condition, while being reminded of your traumatic Breakthrough might leave you Shaken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T15:13:14-07:00","id":955219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=954284#post954284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* For those who missed the first time I see Jabir as workign a bit like Werewolf's Death Rage. You get triggers, say: 1 from Magnum Opus, one from circumstances of your catalyst and one free choice. These get broader as Ethics falls. So a Neid who Canalised from jealousy about not getting tennure might start with the topic of the experiment that failed and &quot;cost him tenure&quot;, then broaden to the field of science, then to all sane science.<br /> <br /> The Jabir roll would probably be Composure with a penalty based on Inspiration, with the results inflicting a Condition. Even a success would have mild conditions like fail a social roll because the other guy thinks you weird. Failure or dramatic failure would result in Igor or your beautiful daughter betraying you or a torch wielding mob.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some further thoughts.<br /> <br /> We should have advice that says that if neither your Magnum Opus or your catalyst creates a trigger related to your field of science/alchemy/etc you should probably use your free choice for that.<br /> <br /> We could tie Unmada into this system to give some crunch to the psychological side of it (the Unmada field can stay as is). Unmada simply treat their Ethics as X lower when calculating how broad their triggers are and they suffer Jabir when dealing with other mad scientists. We'd probably need Conditions appropriate for antagonists, things that make them vow revenge on the player. etc.<br /> <br /> The Dharmists' grant could include the ability to not trigger Jabir on other mad scientists- hence how they led Lemuria.<br /> <br /> The Phenomenologists' Grant could be replaced with the ability to change their Jabir triggers if they focus for a few minutes. They shouldn't be able to ignore Jabir with a point of Mania, but they should be able to plan ahead and make sure their triggers match the Genius they're talking to - hence how they maintain the Archweltanschaaung.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-22-2016, 10:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T05:50:54-07:00","id":958173,"title":"","content":"Since I began a crossover game filled with both official and fan content I've had many thoughts about updating Genius to a 2E standard. For starters I wanted to put down my draft of a 'new' Catalyst as expanded from a short paragraph on pg 61 of the 1.1 Genius pdf.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">There are rumors of other catalysts based on other kinds of societies. One catalyst, said to have existed in China before Lemuria's eradication of their Inspired society, focused on a sort of enlightened embracing of the universe-as-it-is. Another concentrated on an Inspired mastery of one's place and position in the complicated social strata of those societies. The catalyst of &quot;Enthusiasm,&quot; triggered by a genius touching the Godhead during his Breakthrough, shows up in rumors and legends. Nonetheless, almost all known geniuses belong to one of the five catalysts listed above.</span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">From finding common themes I came up with this Catalyst.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Eifer: The Catalyst of Enthusiasm</u></b><br /> Nickname: Spocks<br /> Planet: Pluto<br /> Axiom: Prostasia<br /> <i>&quot;Fascinating...&quot;</i><br /> <br /> At first 'Enthusiasm' sounds like an odd title for a Catalyst, as if it would be a better fit under Staunen. This interpretation of Enthusiasm is 'one that becomes one with their work.' Even compared to their fellow Catalysts the Eifers define themselves by their art, science and careers most of all. They constantly reevaluate themselves compared to their societies, their worlds and their (unfortunately skewed) perspective of events around them. Maintaining such a balance means that the Eifer tend towards muted emotions. Even in the most harrowing of events these Geniuses radiate an unusual calm, much like the beloved Vulcan character portrayed by Leonard Nimoy that serves as a persisting nickname for this Catalyst. Given this calmness, from which an Eifer tries to find a harmonious whole out of Mad Science, the common stereotype is that this is the quietest Catalyst. A fitting descriptor, as many Eifers of the past were eradicated by Lemuria. Survivors and new members of this Catalyst tend to not cause as many waves as their more emotive fellows, although the adage about the quietest person in the room being the most dangerous can hold true for some Eifers.<br /> <br /> Some of this Catalyst may break the mask of stoicism occasionally for a raw, cathartic expression. At their worst the Eifer become completely alien to emotional states. They are predisposed towards <b>dissociation</b> and <b>detachment</b>. An Eifer can become so focused and invested in their projects that the idea of a sole self, the Genius that attempts to bring Inspired thought into reality, does not exist. Some may have shown signs of low self esteem, avoidance or lack of fostering acclaim before their Breakthrough. Others were once humble with a great sense of humility. Others were on a spiritual path towards enlightenment. Whatever the case, the mark of this Catalyst was that the Genius entered such a concentrated state of focus, freed from the distraction of emotions that their early Wonders came into being. Trying to apply rationality towards the inherent Mania of Inspiration is a daunting and often an impossible task. For some of this Catalyst the realization of their state can bring self-justification to the most horrific of transgressions, distancing themselves from their humanity towards a definition of logic and reason built from uncertainty and false truths. Next to Grimms or Hoffnung this can trigger delusions of godhood, only the Eifer sees themselves as a vital force in the underpinnings of reality.<br /> <br /> Eifer can be good teammates in any collaborative if they can find harmony with the other Geniuses. Often they provide support in much needed areas to help restore balance to the group. Their trend towards suppressing (if not outright <i>removing</i>) their emotions can make them appear cold and heartless. An Eifer can also be prone to becoming unfocused from the task at hand as they get lost in thinking about bigger concepts or the bigger picture. Just as easily they may fail to pick up on the subtleties or emotional needs of their colleagues. It would require other Geniuses, Beholden or Manes to bring the Eifer back to the present and in touch with their companions.<br /> <br /> <br /> Examples: Mr. Spock (Star Trek), Egon Spengler (Ghostbusters), Sherlock Holmes (as portrayed by Robert Downey Jr and Benedict Cumberbatch)</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12284,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","user":"-metablender","date":". 08-26-2016, 05:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T06:21:35-07:00","id":958184,"title":"","content":"Speaking of other Catalysts. I tried to do a Catalyst of Fear based on Joyce from Stranger things. I hit a writers block, but I'm sure it's a good concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T15:28:50-07:00","id":958455,"title":"","content":"I don't think we need a fear catalyst... It could be perfectly illustrated by another brand of Mad Scientists we've been missing: &quot;Dabblers&quot;, Geniuses who had only opened their minds to Inspiration out of despair for options to save somebody very close to them from beyond (Joyce, Stanley Pines, and I am sure there are other examples). Dabblers likely have series of limitations to their abilities, but have one strength in eyes of other Geniuses, they can actually turn back. Dabblers should have an additional aspiration of saving somebody that has under some extraordinary circumstances can only be saved by supernatural means. Until aspiration is fullfilled or all hope is lost Dabblers would have access to most things regular Geniuses have.<br /> <br /> Additional idea I've been brewing on: Braineater merit for Orphans, feral manes and Illuminated. Merit serves as an additional and much more visceral access to mania by literal devouring of brains of thinking individuals. Brains of Geniuses obviously provide more nutrion to these more dangerous pretas which is second reason (after Havoc) why semi-annual zombie apocalypses haven't ended the world just yet; Zombies head first for those who are most well equiped for dealing with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T00:08:28-07:00","id":958625,"title":"","content":"The main question is how much further the theme of Fear could be taken in regards to a single Catalyst (or pseudo-Catalyst). When looking at the original Catalysts each of them can cause fear in others with their own ways. The only Catalysts that speak to be as regularly being motived by fear are the Klagen, when driven by a sense of doom or impending disaster; or the Neid, whose personal fears are magnified into their paranoia. Perhaps Hoffnung as well if fearful of their visions not coming to pass.<br /> <br /> I think it's important that a Catalyst allows for a spectrum of portrayals with its signature emotion. A Grimm can be always wrathful, blowing up at the slightest drawback, or have low-key but continuous seething anger or appear grounded but ready to fly off the handle if wronged and everyone can glimpse that. Staunen could be forever curious and chipper, childish with a dash of naivet\u00e9, eccentric to a fault or fixated by a single utter fascination that no one understands.<br /> <br /> As I tried to convey in my draft of Eifer/Enthusiasm, you can play around with how limited their emotions come to be. Are emotional experiences just rare for them or nonexistent? In keeping to a intense focus do they become disinclined towards or look down upon lesser minds? Or are they just not <i>there</i>, human in everything but behavior and motive? In distilling the concepts of each Catalyst from the Genius guide I found the descriptions to do the same thing, expanding the concept of each through highs and lows, stereotypes and extreme instances.<br /> <br /> I kinda agree with Weird as my initial thought of a Fear catalyst is that of a reluctant Mad Scientist to the nth degree, suggesting that they would turn away from Inspiration if they could. That rejection of Inspiration only to be consumed by it also occurs with heavily melancholy Klagen. And the aforementioned overlap with Neid and Klagen. A 'Fear' Catalyst would need to cover at least another facet of personality or more to make it interesting, help it stand out.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Calculus Vampire merit (<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u25cf\u25cf</span></span>) is already known by orphaned wonders, manes and such when they're going renegade. Braineater would have to provide even more Mania gain or some other option, and it sounds a little niche. Perhaps the feral creation/entity can make improvements to themselves by committing a Larvae-harvesting type of action? Brain-eating would definitely fit that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T16:02:23-07:00","id":958934,"title":"","content":"The Catalyst of Fear casing fear in it's own way is easy. Fear can make you irrational, and an irrational person with a ray gun is bad news. Even if they're rational you really don't want to be between a Catalyst of Fear and the person they fear loosing. Alternatively a Genius of fear could inflict that fear on the people they're trying to protect. Smothering them, or trapping them behind layers of Prostasia for their own protection.<br /> <br /> The reason Fear needs to be a catalyst is simple. Joyce was definately part way through a Breakthrough but she didn't fit any of the existing catalysts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=958455#post958455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think we need a fear catalyst... It could be perfectly illustrated by another brand of Mad Scientists we've been missing: &quot;Dabblers&quot;, Geniuses who had only opened their minds to Inspiration out of despair for options to save somebody very close to them from beyond (Joyce, Stanley Pines, and I am sure there are other examples). Dabblers likely have series of limitations to their abilities, but have one strength in eyes of other Geniuses, they can actually turn back. Dabblers should have an additional aspiration of saving somebody that has under some extraordinary circumstances can only be saved by supernatural means. Until aspiration is fullfilled or all hope is lost Dabblers would have access to most things regular Geniuses have.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's every Catalyst.<br /> <br /> Not every Breakthrough is completed. Take Dr Ibanez from the Genius opening, she says that this was her second Breakthrough, and she resisted the first Breakthrough and considers resisting it again.<br /> <br /> Joyce never completed her Breakthrough, when Jim Hopper said he believed her she was pulled back. However if she continued further on she would have Catalysed through fear.<br /> <br /> Stanley Pines (you mean Grunkle Stan, not his fully Inspired brother right?) wouldn't even qualify as a dabbler. He'd be a Hunter with <i>something</i> that made him immune to Havoc who managed to repair a damaged wonder using a Genius' notes. His immunity is possibly a Companion template; because Genius needs something for the Rory Williams and Donna Nobles that's distinct from the Igors and Rose Tylers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T06:19:54-07:00","id":959199,"title":"","content":"Well going by the rules Joyce would be Straunen on account that her first Wonder was Apalypsi based and she wants to <u>know</u> where her son went and how she could save him. If Joyce hadn't truly brokenthrough during the series other catalysts she seemed to be heading for would have been Neid and Klagen. She was already kind of a social outcast with people spreading tales about her and her family, with ultimate breaking point coming for when people just wouldn't listen to her while she was speaking the truth (her wonder in that case could have been ruled off as a proto-wonder that served as a part of her catalyzing). Had her son been actually lost to the Underside the despair caused by such realization would surely drive her into becoming Cassandra.<br /> <br /> Also if taking a look at &quot;five core emotions&quot; and five catalysts parallels could be drawn as following: Joy (Straunen), Sadness (Klagen), Anger (Grim), Disgust (Hoffnung, as &quot;in we can do better&quot;), and Fear being Neid, since they are effectively ruled by their fear of loosing one's face, being manipulated, or outdone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T11:07:39-07:00","id":959908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=959199#post959199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well going by the rules Joyce would be Straunen on account that her first Wonder was Apalypsi based</div> </div> </div> </div>There's aboslutely no rule saying your first wonders come from your Catalyst's axiom. You start with 3 favoured axioms remember. And if you're assigning a fictional charachter to a Catalyst by wonder rather than Axiom you're doing it wrong. Simple as that.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T07:57:55-07:00","id":963226,"title":"","content":"This thread has frozen again so someone needs to add more fuel into fire. Here is my idea for Integrity we have been brainstorming over: Comprehension, Genius's ability understand ideas, emotions, and concepts that aren't their own. High Comprehension Genius is natural universalists and could easily realize how to express themselves in a way that would help others understand them. Low Comprehension Geniuses meanwhile tend to wrap more and more into themselves, with their Wonders becoming more and more personalized to be only usable by them and their Beholden, as they start to struggle to use technology they didn't build, and find any ideas as not as their own inferior.<br /> Rather than being journey below or away from humnanity, Comprehension would be Genius spiralling into oneself, extremes building on extremes until Genius's fragile ego snaps and leads way to Illumination.<br /> The list of &quot;scientific sins&quot; might be unsuitable for this, which does unfortunately complicate larvea collection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T15:14:02-07:00","id":963411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=963226#post963226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This thread has frozen again so someone needs to add more fuel into fire. Here is my idea for Integrity we have been brainstorming over: Comprehension, Genius's ability understand ideas, emotions, and concepts that aren't their own. High Comprehension Genius is natural universalists and could easily realize how to express themselves in a way that would help others understand them. Low Comprehension Geniuses meanwhile tend to wrap more and more into themselves, with their Wonders becoming more and more personalized to be only usable by them and their Beholden, as they start to struggle to use technology they didn't build, and find any ideas as not as their own inferior.<br /> Rather than being journey below or away from humnanity, Comprehension would be Genius spiralling into oneself, extremes building on extremes until Genius's fragile ego snaps and leads way to Illumination.<br /> The list of &quot;scientific sins&quot; might be unsuitable for this, which does unfortunately complicate larvea collection.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What about tying Larvae into personal Touchstones? In this model, you are sacrificing external benchmarks (things close to your Genius as a human being) in pursuit of personal goals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T23:04:27-07:00","id":966076,"title":"","content":"<br /> When it comes to the 2E version of Obligation (or whatever the common consensus of Integrity variant is) I believe it shouldn't just sit there as a karma score. Other games have used those meters for certain benefits. Demon and Beast are quite different for how the levels are used in the game.<br /> <br /> Reading the 1.1v of Genius brought me my own thoughts similar to what ArcaneArts brought up in his massive review. Obligation doesn't hold any meat or penalty, causing the common stereotype of Geniuses quickly plummeting down the meter to isolate themselves from the world. What do they need from the rest of humanity?<br /> <br /> Quite a lot, actually. For another use of Obligation I've called it to an idea called Funding. A system separate from the multi-variations of the resources Merit outlined on pg 88 G:tT. I'm of the belief that you should't have to heavily modify or restrict core merits when introducing another game line.<br /> <br /> Funding is purchased at 2 Experiences per dot and new players distribute 3 dots of Funding at character creation. Whenever new Wonder(s) is made or 'discovered' in the Genius's research its rating is compared to the dots of available Funding, bringing penalties to the creation roll if the complexity of the Wonder exceeds the Funding.<br /> <br /> Each Funding has certain upkeep and thus inherent Obligations for the Genius to fulfill. Ignoring these particulars will cause the Genius to lower their Obligation and lose out on the Funding. Ideally some sort of perk with each as well. This modifies some of the Genius Merits as well; Resources can be sacrificed to get missing components quickly although it can't patch Funding. The Tenure merit is now paired with a sole source of Funding that can only be diminished to 1 dot, along with its other functions. Dumpster Diver is treated as a Funding rating for Kitbashing only.<br /> <br /> Current types of Funding I've gathered:<ul><li>Entrepreneur - the Genius works a business, for all the time and involvement such a business entails</li> <li>Loan - requires payment back of rating +1</li> <li>Family - any wealth is budgeted along others likely non-Inspired ((like Rick with his family))</li> <li>Inheritance - monthly deposits overseen by a trustee or advisor scrutinizing the Genius (use Social Maneuvering)</li> <li>Research Grant - quite lucrative but intensive both for results and the scrutiny of others</li> <li>Commission - an advance of pay for a job less scrutinizing than Research Grant, although the commissioned job must be completed</li> <li>Crime - risky as the planned heists bring not only legal trouble but both devalued fundings and increased spoils</li> <li>Salvage - daunting and physically exhausting work fraught with peril</li> <li>Appeal - crowdsourcing and such donations, acting a little like the Fame merit both for dealing with their audience and the Genius attracting more attention</li> </ul>Obligation also determines Paragon status, the mantle of authority for a Genius. Perhaps Obligation could play into Havoc some way as well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T02:17:49-07:00","id":966116,"title":"","content":"I agree with &quot;shouldn't sit there as a karma score&quot;. I think it should be somekind of sanity/insanity meter, since the game is about Mad scientists. <br /> The funding idea seems interesting, but my main issue with it is that doesn't Funding kind of undermine the classical Mad Science dynamic where villains are rich and well equiped (think Bond Villains, Villainous Sparks, folks from CUBE) and heroes are middle class when they are extremely lucky and likely scavenging spare parts from geek shops and scrapyards?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12082,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","user":"Weird","date":".  Me, it's pronounced Sanity not Sanoty! 09-09-2016, 05:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T16:14:27-07:00","id":966469,"title":"","content":"Maybe make it rise and fall easily?<br /> <br /> My thought, is that there could be &quot;Permanent Sanity&quot; and &quot;Momentary Sanity.&quot; (Sanity is just a name being used for this example) Momentary Sanity rises and falls pretty easily, and you can even voluntarily drop it to protect against Havoc or dodge an Unmada check (giving in to harmful coping mechanisms or self-destructive traits in order to relieve stress), and you suffer Breaking Points against Permanent Sanity only with extreme breaches or when Temporary Sanity hits zero? Maybe even have this replace Mania point costs?<br /> <br /> What do you folks think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T17:43:45-07:00","id":966498,"title":"","content":"The term 'Funding' is hampered by trying to match the pseudo-academic classifications used in the guide. Much like the Resources merit it doesn't pertain to an exact monetary value, and the 'wealth' of Resources can vary from one location to the next from where your chronicle is set.<br /> <br /> To look at your examples, Weird, the middle class or scrounger Genius starting out would have at most 2 or 3 Funding under certain kind of fields. Like work at a personal or locale business (Entrepreneur) or foraging/junking their needs for their Wonders (Salvage). Your Bond-level super villains likely have multiple sources of Funding at high values in the 4 to 5 range each.<br /> <br /> The reason to separate Funding into its own system is to allow for easy changes, as ideally sources of Funding will change over the chronicle in lieu with a collaborative's development, progression and travel. Although a single source of Funding (the various tag words) is rated from 1-5 dots, there is no theoretical cap to what the Genius could sustain if they can upkeep the Funding. For one Genius, <b>Chuck</b>, he may have 3 dots of Inheritance representing royalty checks from a prior family member's patent. Another (<b>Roxelle</b>) may have 3 total split amongst a part time job (Entrepreneur 1), tapping the abandoned mine for veins (Salvage 1) and stealing anything else she's missing (Crime 1).<br /> <br /> What each source of Funding is and how it works can be customized by players and Storytellers. Ideally each Funding should require a means of upkeep, a slight bonus and criteria that will hamper the Genius. Thus the pull into Obligation; does the Genius stick to their lifestyle means if they feel it a shackle, or do they abandon the Funding in search of other ventures? How the Genius interacts with their Funding brings a modifier to their Obligation checks.<br /> <br /> Using my placeholder names, Chuck only has his ancestor's royalty checks that lets him raise mycological colonies and template new diseases in the back shed. Provided he upholds the family legacy (which is a household cleaning product and here he is growing more voliate strains of mold) he has a potent bonus to his Obligation, +3 from the rating, to meet the family's financial planner's approval. However if Chucks 'fungal freaks' cause too many incidents that Chuck doesn't bother to reign in, the rating becomes -3 to the Obligation check. Not only does Chuck's Obligation lower he loses access to the Inheritance when he cuts ties with the family's estate.<br /> <br /> Roxelle may have lesser ratings to support or hamper her Obligation (+/-1) but she has more versatility than Chuck if she loses access to one Funding over the other. She might find her work hours, however little, to be personally offensive and quits her job. She's out that Funding dot but she has the two others from Salvage and Crime. She does much better as a budding super villain that later in the chronicle her rating of Crime increases. Conversely, anything to scrap at the abandoned mine runs out as the city collapses the entrance to prevent youngsters from harming themselves within. How Roxelle felt about this (either helping the city do the right thing or sabotaging their efforts to no avail) determines if the rating becomes a bonus or penalty to Obligation before the Funding is lost. If Roxelle buckles down to accept more work hours her Entrepreneur raises later in the story.<br /> <br /> <br /> In the grand scheme of things a Genius may have no Funding, which doesn't bar them from Wonder creation although their efforts are constantly plagued by improper materials, housing or energy representing continued penalties. The total sum of a Genius's available Funding serves as a budget for what they can work on simultaneously, along only a single variety of Funding can modify an Obligation check at a time. If Roxelle wanted to build two Skafoi 5 vehicles in time for beach season she hopefully would have secured 10 ratings of Funding from various sources. Whether its the major heists (Crime 5), overtime at work (Entrepreneur 3) or managing her new GoFundMe page (Appeal 2) that prevents her from attending her sister's wedding determines which rating becomes the modifier to the Obligation check.<br /> <br /> Perhaps more lucrative or themed Fundings could be allowed from select Foundations (and Baramins on the flip side). Whether this is an Experience discount, role-play rewards or a rating cap removal I'm not sure which is better. Funding types should change as much as Obligation would, although losing it should hurt. Not like Sanctity of Merits, where lost Merit dots can be turned into something else, although I know that having Funding be too expensive would cause Experience waste when it is gone. Although there would be nothing baring a Genius from tweaking their current Funding slightly between stories, to represent the change in setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T11:44:18-07:00","id":966848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=966469#post966469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe make it rise and fall easily?<br /> <br /> My thought, is that there could be &quot;Permanent Sanity&quot; and &quot;Momentary Sanity.&quot; (Sanity is just a name being used for this example) Momentary Sanity rises and falls pretty easily, and you can even voluntarily drop it to protect against Havoc or dodge an Unmada check (giving in to harmful coping mechanisms or self-destructive traits in order to relieve stress), and you suffer Breaking Points against Permanent Sanity only with extreme breaches or when Temporary Sanity hits zero? Maybe even have this replace Mania point costs?<br /> <br /> What do you folks think?</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems easier to use Conditions than a &quot;Momentary Sanity&quot; track.<br /> <br /> BTW One idea I had was letting a Genius spend a point of Mania to reduce the interval of a purely mental and mundane extended action (solving an equation, thinking up a plan, solving a puzzle) down to a single reflexive action (they can limit it a bit if they want to slow it down to something like &quot;as fast as I can write on this chalkboard&quot;).<br /> <br /> Not only is it a fitting power extended actions require you to take Conditions on a failure, meaning it's a great way to have a flash of brilliant insanity. You get your plan, but you also get Conditions like ethically callous, need to show off, and won't explain anything (looking at you The Doctor).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T08:27:28-07:00","id":967328,"title":"","content":"So I've been thinking of crossover troubles, in particular the Scolastic/Libertine alliance and the reasons for it:<br /> <br /> Peerage-trained Mage:<br /> Won't contain Paradox;<br /> Won't Pattern Scour;<br /> Will require tools/sacrifices (best represented as an Addiction Condition?);<br /> Prone to self-doubt (which is conductive to turning Banisher according to M2e core)<br /> <br /> Diamond-trained Genius:<br /> Will perform Deep Inspiration;<br /> Is obsessed (as in, Condition (or Thesis?!)) with avoiding &quot;Paradox&quot; (Havoc);<br /> Prone to Hybris<br /> <br /> Anything to add?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T13:30:56-07:00","id":967499,"title":"","content":"Thing is, do we really need to continue 1e's tradition of &quot;Mages and Geniuses have no interaction with each other whatsoever&quot;? I think that's the element most people like to point out to when the claim Genius was made by one Ascension-immigrant Sons of Ether/Technocracy fanboy with a particular enmity for Awakening. Maybe we should consider redesigning Mage/Genius interaction from the ground up.<br /> <br /> Let's face it, Mages are basically living embodiments of the idea that &quot;There IS A Higher Truth Out There!&quot; - or else proof that reality is all subjective, depending on which angle you want to take. I know for a fact that The King's Raven is uncomfortable with crossovers, but even so, I hope he would agree that there's still more potential for the two then &quot;they try to pretend the other doesn't exist outside of making sure they don't mix up their recruits&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T14:01:24-07:00","id":967519,"title":"","content":"Mage and Genius, both in terms of the themes of the game and culture of the characters, are fundamentally opposed. That has to be respected, but that said there's definitely room to improve over 1E's &quot;Mage's think Geniuses are Abysal&quot; but fundamentally Mage's idea that they alone see the Truth will look uncomfortably like an Unmada - even Peers who know Mages can't go Unmada will find it uncomfortable.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile one thing the Diamond (and the Seers) agree on is that Mages should be responsible with power, Mage society is structured to ensure that there's plenty of checks and balances on the Awakened. Geniuses are nothing but irresponsible, and they just finished taking all those checks and balances apart and replaced them with a support group. I mean, wouldn't you be horrified if you discovered someone with the personality of a Grimm or Neid had enough weaponry to level a city block in their basement?<br /> <br /> <br /> But we don't need to do more than that. We can let the Geniuses be uncomfortable that Mages think they have a unique access to the Truth and leave it at that. We can let Mages be horrified that when the leaders of the peerage see nothing wrong with letting kids build giant death robots so long as they regularly get peer review. We don't need to go beyond that to Mages thinking that Geniuses are Abyssal.<br /> <br /> <br /> BTW I actually did have a Mage in a Genius game (it wasn't really crossover, it was a Genius game, we just had a Mage PC in it). The general contrast we came to was:<br /> <br /> Mages are the bad kind of academics. They have claim to work together for the good of humanity but in practice they're a seething mass of politics.<br /> Geniuses are tech start-ups. They're officially rivals and don't work together (without being paid for it) but they socialise more and actually like each other.<br /> <br /> The game also included the relevation that there's a perpetual mania storm caused by children leaning there is no Santa Clause so the Peerage have to shoot down his sleigh every year before he leaves enough Havoc vulnerable presents to destroy large parts of the world. (I would have thought Lemuria handled stuff like that, but ah well)<br /> <br /> Also Santa can make his deliveries because he is a quantum wave form, simultaneously under every tree unless somebody observes his location.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T15:51:57-07:00","id":967576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=967519#post967519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also Santa can make his deliveries because he is a quantum wave form, simultaneously under every tree unless somebody observes his location.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nonsense. He uses a Space Patterning spell to make himself omnilocational.<br /> <br /> Or maybe he has a Contract with Christmas?<br /> <br /> Or perhaps he uses a Frozen in Time-based Lambda?<br /> <br /> Or maybe he has a specially upgraded Up in Smoke charm?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T17:15:26-07:00","id":967618,"title":"","content":"Obviously there is a worldwide conspiracy network of Santa Clauses working together in unison, and their powersets and metaphysical nature vary from member to member.<br /> What comes to Mage/Genius interactions I quite enjoy the quiet, spiteful and mutual &quot;keep your bullshit to yourself&quot;, taking in account how much anger mere mention of Genius raises among Awakening -fans.<br /> If I would try to rewrite something it would be Genius/Vampire interaction. Idea of Geniuses being stronger members of the heard is amusing, but taking in account themes and moods it would be more fun to see Vampires try to use their &quot;mind draining cousins&quot; in their power games, and Maniacal society's rapid phase clashing with Kindreds' stagnant Danse Macabre.<br /> For example: &quot;Some Vampires may be aware of existence of Dementes, psychic draining individuals of reckless nature and gift for creation of scientific marvels. They are known for their despair for economical support and validation which ambitios or desparate enough Kindred could easily exploit.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12082,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","user":"Weird","date":".  Added an example of what Vampires might think of Genii 09-11-2016, 08:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T12:37:34-07:00","id":968078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=967576#post967576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nonsense. He uses a Space Patterning spell to make himself omnilocational.<br /> <br /> Or maybe he has a Contract with Christmas?<br /> <br /> Or perhaps he uses a Frozen in Time-based Lambda?<br /> <br /> Or maybe he has a specially upgraded Up in Smoke charm?</div> </div> </div> </div>Or he's a True Fae. And he and Krampus aren't different people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T16:31:46-07:00","id":970302,"title":"","content":"After some reconsideration, I have come to the conclusion that a game about mad scientists where my master plan for the world is doomed to fail just isn't fun. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4488_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4488\" data-vbnamecard=\"4488\">malonkey1</a>, I remember that you proposed a trait called Magnum Opus, which works like a sort of Obsession for Geniuses. Do you have any other ideas for it?<br /> <br /> I believe that trait should be explored further, perhaps as a source of Wondrous Experiences. I also believe we should move away from the defeatism of 1ED and focus on a new theme more closely tied to the subtitle of Transgression. I suggest &quot;The Price Of Victory&quot; as this new theme. I want a game where I am incentivated to change the status quo, not wallow in Jabir and lack of funding.<br /> <br /> I mean, in Demon, your characters can overcome the God-Machine itself to achieve their vision of Hell. Why wouldn't Geniuses be able to overcome their own obstacles to fulfill their dreams?<br /> <br /> What I'm trying to say is that we need to get back to the basics of theme and such before moving ahead in any meaningful way. What do you all think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T16:56:27-07:00","id":970312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=970302#post970302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After some reconsideration, I have come to the conclusion that a game about mad scientists where my master plan for the world is doomed to fail just isn't fun. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4488_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4488\" data-vbnamecard=\"4488\">malonkey1</a>, I remember that you proposed a trait called Magnum Opus, which works like a sort of Obsession for Geniuses. Do you have any other ideas for it?<br /> <br /> I believe that trait should be explored further, perhaps as a source of Wondrous Experiences. I also believe we should move away from the defeatism of 1ED and focus on a new theme more closely tied to the subtitle of Transgression. I suggest &quot;The Price Of Victory&quot; as this new theme. I want a game where I am incentivated to change the status quo, not wallow in Jabir and lack of funding.<br /> <br /> I mean, in Demon, your characters can overcome the God-Machine itself to achieve their vision of Hell. Why wouldn't Geniuses be able to overcome their own obstacles to fulfill their dreams?<br /> <br /> What I'm trying to say is that we need to get back to the basics of theme and such before moving ahead in any meaningful way. What do you all think?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've kind of been thinking that we need to move away from mad scientists a little. Obviously, they should remain an important part, but I think we should move to a more general sense of &quot;geniuses&quot;. On top of mad scientists, there are plenty of Mad Politicians, Mad Artists and all sorts of other Mad professions that feel really left out.<br /> <br /> I mean, there's already plenty of conceptual space for mad political science, but why not open some space for supernatural Van Goghs and Warhols?<br /> <br /> EDIT: As for Genii succeeding, I'm pretty much all for that being a possibility. But I think a core theme should be dealing with success as much as failure. To use a historic example, Alfred Nobel, who founded the Nobel Foundation out of guilt over the destructive nature of his previous invention, TNT.<br /> <br /> A lot of good stuff could be mined from seeing the full consequences of your works turning out to be horrifying or even just disappointing. Yeah, you managed to convert all humanity to digital consciousness, but now we don't care about being able to breathe the air and pollution has run rampant. You've cured death, but now the world is starting to overcrowd and become increasingly decrepit, demographically. You cured the common cold, but the rare plant that the cure is extracted from has started to choke out local plant life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":4488,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","user":"malonkey1","date":". 09-15-2016, 08:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T17:30:42-07:00","id":970332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=970312#post970312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've kind of been thinking that we need to move away from mad scientists a little. Obviously, they should remain an important part, but I think we should move to a more general sense of &quot;geniuses&quot;. On top of mad scientists, there are plenty of Mad Politicians, Mad Artists and all sorts of other Mad professions that feel really left out.<br /> <br /> I mean, there's already plenty of conceptual space for mad political science, but why not open some space for supernatural Van Goghs and Warhols?</div> </div> </div> </div> I agree wholeheartedly. There should be many ways to play a Genius besides engineers. We could adjust the mechanics so that tangible Wonders aren't the sole means of expressing Inspiration. We could also come up with some Fellowships for these less typical Geniuses.<br /> <br /> But seriously now. What are going to be the themes of 2ED? We need to get that written down before progressing. How exactly is this going to be a game about Transgressions?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T17:37:33-07:00","id":970336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=970332#post970332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How exactly is this going to be a game about Transgressions?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can do anything... as long as you accept the price?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T17:45:15-07:00","id":970344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=970332#post970332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I agree wholeheartedly. There should be many ways to play a Genius besides engineers. We could adjust the mechanics so that tangible Wonders aren't the sole means of expressing Inspiration. We could also come up with some Fellowships for these less typical Geniuses.<br /> <br /> But seriously now. What are going to be the themes of 2ED? We need to get that written down before progressing. How exactly is this going to be a game about Transgressions?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, we could start with what the characters do.<br /> <br /> Clearly, the Wonders &quot;transgress&quot; the laws of mortal science, but that's not enough. I think an act of transgression and rule-breaking needs to be built into the Wonders. Wonders shouldn't work because they're <i>wrong</i>. They should work despite <i>society saying they're wrong</i>. A Genius might work their Wonders on perfectly valid theoretical principles, but they need to defy the limits of what we accept. An Inspired Warp drive should work in ways that a person might be able to &quot;grok&quot; but should be utterly unprovable with what we know now.<br /> <br /> An economist creates a perfect economy, based on principles of perfectly-balanced supply and demand. it shouldn't work because of a number of reasons, but somehow, it does for as long as he's in control.<br /> <br /> An artist creates paintings so real-looking, you swear you could step into them if you tried. When you ask him about his technique, he gets irrationally angry and demands you leave.<br /> <br /> A philosopher has claimed to have &quot;solved&quot; morality, and can justify almost any crime he commits. His reasoning is flawless when he says it, but it loses something when you try to repeat it later.<br /> <br /> A programmer has created a sentient, self-improving anti-virus that can perfectly protect any system. When you decompile the code and pick it apart, it makes no sense and uses a bunch of libraries you've never heard of, and when you try to recompile it, it all bluescreens.<br /> <br /> I hope I'm being coherent, I'm kind of slightly messed up on cough syrup right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T18:32:38-07:00","id":970373,"title":"","content":"I understand you. But those are really all permutations on &quot;doing the impossible&quot;.<br /> <br /> For instance, the idea behind <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/865489-crossover-concept-detective-agency?p=893472#post893472\">Landon Black</a>, was a Mad Politician (or Political Science), on the reasoning that Politics and Government was mere a social construct humans built or repurposed to their own benefit (technology of a more abstract sort). If he could just infuse Mania directly into his political apparatus, that would be great.<br /> <br /> My personal pet theory for Genii and Inspiration is that it taps into alternate realities, where such things just work. Havoc is the fact that such imported physics/logic is alien and inherently unstable. It's right for the Genius (and any theoretical native of such place), but wrong for everyone else.<br /> <br /> But I'm rambling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 09-15-2016, 10:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T19:24:50-07:00","id":970409,"title":"","content":"I'm all for the expansion of Genius into alternate professions. The Mad <i>Sciences</i> and academia tends to dominate from the nomenclature used in the original document.<br /> <br /> I like to equate Geniuses with the Wizened of Changeling. They both perform their occupations, talents and professions to a superhuman degree. Genii perhaps have it easier to be well rounded or try new things, if it fits their aesthetic and paradigm, than the Wizened's Clarity being based on their special talent. In my Sunday crossover game for every Genius NPC of Mad Science/Academia I also have a Genius of very different means. For the college provost and theatre producer there's also a graffiti 'correcting' artist that dabbles as an arms dealer and a Genius that runs a sandwich shop.<br /> <br /> I also lean towards the alternate realities, as that is how Bardos are said to work. A Genius deals in Un-Realities and Untruths, if you will. It works, hell it even may make sense after its explained, but the sheer otherness of what a Genius does transgresses against common conception and understanding, from the fundamental truths humanity has developed to this given day. The challenge comes from bridging the impossible-possible with the rest of the world in a way where it will not cause Havoc and other issues.<br /> <br /> The emphasis on Untruth, for my purposes, is a quite freeing concept that still allows for the wide wide range Mania can be purposed. If you're into crossover it also allows for good contrast with Mage, the empowered who believe to know the Truths as learned from the realms of magic that the Earth of today has fallen from. Inspiration does not have a grand unified theory behind it, it is the raw force that persists hundreds of unstable, incorrect and disproven ideas for everything that does work. It's not like Demons tapping into the occult subroutines used by the God-Machine to impact reality, a Demon would be quite confused for Genii being able enact grand devices and schemes without having an known source of this Light of Inspiration. The Principle behind Prometheans, Azoth and Alchemy may be inscrutable at times but it is consistent. Inspiration as a force in the world is constantly redefined by those that wield it.<br /> <br /> In short, beyond Mad Science I suggest Genius should focus on Untruth, Instability and Uncertainty. The Genius can draw on their understanding of the Axioms for how their Wonder works, yet they should always have the worry about the when and how their Wonder/theory will be disproven. That a new reality has yet to be formed, its still the Transgressions incurred from a reality that doesn't exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T23:52:52-07:00","id":970537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=970332#post970332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I agree wholeheartedly. There should be many ways to play a Genius besides engineers. We could adjust the mechanics so that tangible Wonders aren't the sole means of expressing Inspiration. We could also come up with some Fellowships for these less typical Geniuses.</div> </div> </div> </div> Intangible Wonders are already in 1E and are not particularly untypical.<br /> <br /> Just use the Internalised Your secret psychological manipulation techniques are just an internalised wonder.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=970344#post970344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They should work despite <i>society saying they're wrong</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think that's missing the point.<br /> <br /> Take a light saber. It's not transgressive because scientists can't understand how you're getting a shaped magnetic bottle strong enough to hold plasma out of a few AA batteries and a large crystal.<br /> <br /> It's transgressive because your lightsaber is symbolic of a larger idea. A society and a world where by laser swords are superior to laser guns. A society where individual warriors matter more to warfare than a mass of uniform soldiers. Or for a more horrifying concept: your lightsaber is symbolic of a world where only exceptional people matter, and everyone else is just part of the disposable faceless masses. We don't feel bad when Luke Skywalker kills Stormtrooper #30. Heck, Obi Wan's death had more emotional impact than the Death Star blowing up Alderaan.<br /> <br /> <br /> An even better example would be Batman. In most adaptions his suit is just body armour. There's nothing &quot;beyond the understanding of science&quot; in a suit of body armour that looks a bit like a bat.<br /> <br /> But Batman outright tells us what his suit symbolises. He dresses up as a bat because he was scared of bats, and he wanted criminals to share his fear. Replacing a world where crime is prevented by law and due process with one where crime is prevented through fear and superstition. That's a pretty transgressive idea.<br /> <br /> <br /> Wonders allow Geniuses to bring products of the world they wish to create into reality; to expose them to humanity's harsh judgement and see what happens.<br /> <br /> <br /> However I don't think you can, and I definitely don't think you can force, players to embrace transgression as a theme. You will always get people playing the WoD as &quot;trenchcoats and katanas&quot;, trying to stop them is both futile and wrong.<br /> <br /> Having the Magnum Opus as a charachter trait will help as it forces players to think about their charachter's ultimate goal. However you'll always get someone who just puts down something like &quot;destroy the local vampires&quot;.<br /> <br /> If there are any mechanics that support Transgression it should be rewards rather than restrictions or punishments. Things like Larvae. I have some ideas for how Larvae could be significantly more tempting in 2E.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 09-16-2016, 03:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T03:47:46-07:00","id":970611,"title":"","content":"I think people might struggle with remembering existence of intenglable Wonders because either their purpose is something intanglible in game mechanics like &quot;poetry so pretty it instantly brigthens the day of the listener&quot; or because rules of creation don't always make sense with them. For example how does one make Larval intenglable wonder? Why is internalization mainly treated as a surgery, if it would be completely in genre to apply some of the new wonders via pills, syringes, memetic screens, or for example by thinking about it very very hard?<br /> <br /> To be quite honest I love the idea of Mad Artists/Cooks/Bards, but most of their Wonders could be very easily be translated in-game mechanics as 1-2 dot Epikatro, Metatropi, or Exlexi Wonders. Beautiful painting? Memetic Epikatro that gives subject positive effects. Delicious pie? Might be a Wondrous Metatropi recipie that turns any ingredients into pie, or it might be pie-shaped Exlexi pill. Axioms are perculiar in a way that their effects are heavily game effect based. <br /> <br /> Unrelated, did I understand correctly that Geniuses can't build cybernetic limbs until Exlexi 4?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T07:00:21-07:00","id":970660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=970611#post970611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Larval intenglable wonder? Why is internalization mainly treated as a surgery</div> </div> </div> </div> Probably because the surgery rules were written first. But there is a rule saying you replace medicine with accademics when it's not a physical implant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=970611#post970611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">pills, syringes, memetic screens, or for example by thinking about it very very hard</div> </div> </div> </div> All those work fine with the rules as written.<br /> <br /> The rules say you can rush the job down to a turn at (a dice penalty), and you don't have to go unconcious if you're willing to take damage. So if you want to think hard or just swallow a pill to instantly internalise a Wonder you can.<br /> <br /> Or you can say that the pills requires you to sleep for a few hours while your system integrates the contents while Igor or Automata monitor your vitals and make adjustments. Lying strapped to the operating table is pretty similar to being strapped in front of memetic screens and again, you need someone to make constant adjustments to the screen otherwise you might end up scrambling your brain.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=970611#post970611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unrelated, did I understand correctly that Geniuses can't build cybernetic limbs until Exlexi 4?</div> </div> </div> </div>Limbs are Automata 1. Exlexi 4 lets you heal the origonal limb, with the nice advantage that it doesn't bind Mania or suffer from Havoc.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T20:32:10-07:00","id":976322,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar134_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"134\" data-vbnamecard=\"134\">The Kings Raven</a>: Didn't you mention something about making Jabir work kinda like Lunacy? Could you tell us more about that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T02:28:32-07:00","id":977669,"title":"","content":"Meanwhile as part of &quot;redeem Lemuria&quot; innitiative: each Baramin needs a longer three part name to go with the Foundation and Fellowship naming conventions (this is basically a meme in Inspired society by now, isn't it?). I recall Moochava's original campaign nameddropped official names of Machinists and Atomists but I can't remember them at the moment. However here are my suggestions for reminding Baramins: Oraclic Committee of Ethics, Advocates of Ether United and Bureau of Phenomenal Inspection.<br /> <br /> Also I have an idea of Lemurian movement: New Lemuria, who seek to reform the entire global organization to stand as a foil to cynism and pessimism of the Peerage. Movements nobility and idealogy could of course wary from Storyteller to Storyteller, but they could serve as one of justifications for non-unmada Lemurians. Movement is symbolized by rose tinted goggles (or other eyewear) which are meant to represent their opposition to Peerage's jaded worldview (and serve as not so subtle metaphor for movement's greatest flaw: they look at Lemuria, Inspiration, and mania through rose-tinted glasses).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T14:38:49-07:00","id":977975,"title":"","content":"Lemuria doesn't need redmining. It's great the way it is.<br /> <br /> As for longer names: The Children of the Atom, The Institute for Etheric Sciences, The International Guild of Master Mechanists, The Post-Empirical School of Phenomenological Theory, The Hallowed Order of Oracles<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=976322#post976322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar134_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"134\" data-vbnamecard=\"134\">The Kings Raven</a>: Didn't you mention something about making Jabir work kinda like Lunacy? Could you tell us more about that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not Lunacy. Death Rage.<br /> <br /> Each Genius would get three triggers. Typically one relating to their Catalyst, one to their Magnum Opus and one to their Asthetic. Triggers would always be designed so they only come up within the context of social interaction with mortals. The lower your Ethics score is the broader they get. So for example a steampunk Genius might have:<br /> <br /> Specific (Ethics 6+): A mortal critcises the works of Isambard Kingdom Brunel.<br /> <br /> Standard (Ethics 4+): A mortal argues that mass production is superior to individually crafted items.<br /> <br /> Broad (Ethics 1+): A mortal says something good about a mass produced item.<br /> <br /> <br /> When your trigger is pressed (and assuming you're not in the middle of combat) you a flat dicepool based on Inspiration and take a Beat. If you fail you get a negative condition, e.g., you start ranting to James Bond and reveal your diabolical plot. If you get a Dramatic Failure you take a worse condition. Perhaps your ranting horrifies Igor / your beautiful daughter and leads to your betrayal.<br /> <br /> <br /> If you're Unmada you remove the requirement mortals only restriction and are more likely to take conditions like &quot;vowing revenge&quot; than &quot;betrayed&quot; but otherwise Jabir works the same for Unmada.<br /> <br /> The Dharmasists had a Grant that lets them not trigger Jabir in Unmada which they used to hold Lemuria togeather. The Phenomenologists have the grant to change their triggers if they spend an hour or so and a point of mania. They use this to hold Lemuria togeather, with significantly less competence than the Dharmasists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 09-28-2016, 05:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T16:27:50-07:00","id":978030,"title":"","content":"Ah, thank you for longer names. I didn't talk about renaming Lemuria, but extended baramin write-ups would have required the full name of each of them.<br /> New Lemuria isn't intended to be the literally whole new Lemuria, but rather a chism within the faction. I feel like creating and including them in second edition may be required because Lemuria seems awfully stagnant for a global organization made entirely out of mad scientists... And as I mentioned before having entire faction consist of unmada doesn't generate as much different stories as faction that consists mostly of unmada. New Lemuria would be yet another reason Peers could feel tempted to jump sides, since they could join the reformists who'd let them enjoy boons of Lemuria without subscribing to their destructive idealogies (though I'd like New Lemuria's idealogies to remain vague and self-contradictionary, making movement's legitimacy questionable).<br /> Speaking of boons of Lemuria... as part of &quot;redeeming Lemuria&quot; -initiative (aka making them feel like a legitimate playable faction and not designed evil npc faction) would we require rules for maintaining Mercantus and using Bureaus? (In addition I propose we create an umbrella term for global mad scientist conspiracies like Peerage and Lemuria, because I am sick and tired of writing &quot;faction&quot; ...and there will inevitable exist Genius fansettings where neither faction would exist and we might as well spare them time and give them faction creation rules.)<br /> As for Jabir revamp idea... That's interesting and even exciting but why would we need this? This feels like another vague and hard to define gauge to keep in mind for thing that's would be most fun when done by players' volition (Maybe we should add Willpower point rewards for certain Mad Scientist behaviors ala Archetypes?) and in process removes Technobabble which is actually one of best staples of the genre.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12082,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","user":"Weird","date":".  In a perfect world I wouldn't be writing this at 2 am... 09-28-2016, 07:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T16:34:22-07:00","id":978033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=977975#post977975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lemuria doesn't need redmining. It's great the way it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kind of disagree. It doesn't make a lot of sense for them to keep any sort of unified front considering the Baramins are, by definition, violently opposed to all other worldviews to the point of being willing to destroy their opponents and any evidence for their opponents' ideas. Obviously working within a Baramin makes sense, but I don't get why Baramins would ever cooperate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T16:41:17-07:00","id":978039,"title":"","content":"Because Lemurians agree on one thing: Inspired should lead the mankind! ...to their DOOM!<br /> No, but for real Baramins are supposed to function somewhat identical to Foundations of Peerage. You could have all Atomist zoetec, but sometimes you need a ray gun, a psychic, an alchemist, and a giant clockwork manticore. And after all... Disagreement is where new ideas are forged and conflicts are vital to stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T19:04:20-07:00","id":978128,"title":"","content":"I'm beginning to wonder if Genius shouldn't just have Foundation / Baramin creation rules much like the upcoming Changeling 2E Freehold Court creation system, allowing for many varieties of community. Although this would blur the lines that separate Foundation and Fellowship, potentially.<br /> <br /> Baramins, of which the grouping collectively known as Lemuria are most well known, are associated around a sole 'unifying' theory based on where mankind's development went wrong. Atomists wanted a world of nuclear proliferation without the drawbacks, Etherites found the Luminous Ether to be the most elegant theory for the transmission of light, shame it was incorrect. A Baramin becomes antagonistic when they work to try and 'correct' the world around them to fit within their world view. Deviation from that theory necessitates the Genius changing groups entirely.<br /> <br /> Foundations, in contrast, welcome as many contradictory theories as you can shake a stick at, as they have a baseline of understanding that the paradigms of a Genius work primarily due to their nuance with Mania, the theory isn't quite false as much as a secondary need. If you strip away the backstory and collegiate nomenclature of the Foundations they more commonly share a methodology, outlook or approach to Mad Science rather than an academic department or central theory.<br /> <br /> <u>Artificers</u> constantly build, design and rethink. They are encouraged to have many ideas and try out each of their ideas.<br /> <u>Directors</u> are project coordinators. They seek assistance in their esoteric science wherever they can, creating an organization or collaborative devoted to their causes.<br /> <u>Navigators</u> embody a traveler's ideal of action. They leap before they act, save testing for the field and can be the most driven in their projects.<br /> <u>Progenitors</u> are concerned with legacy, rebuilding in new directions given the particulars of past generations of Wonders.<br /> <u>Scholastics</u> try to bring a semblance of reason (however bizarre the logic) to the trappings of Mad Science as its researchers and chroniclers.<br /> <br /> <br /> The main differences when developing a Foundation vs a Baramin, then, is whether the group is built around an approach or a theory. This helps sets the group's Grant and favored Axioms, allowing for different fluff and history as fitting the chronicles they are designed for.<br /> <br /> Fellowships, as pulled from the 1.1 guide, aim a little closer to the current mechanics of a Freehold Court, in terms of being based on the Mystery Cult Initiation merit. Each Fellowship is highly specialized in their Wonders by both method and theory (as Foundations and Baramins are broad along different strata). Each Fellowship has Scholarships or a Syllabus that builds from 1 to 5 dots, arranged around the particulars of their signature Wonders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T02:01:09-07:00","id":978273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=978030#post978030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Jabir revamp idea... That's interesting and even exciting but why would we need this?</div> </div> </div> </div>To reward players with beats when they act in in an appropriate mad science fashion. Secondarally to provide geniuses with a weakness that could be exploited by mortal antagonists. The Vorstellen Police should be viable antagonists in a game of Genius. (If you don't know them shame upon you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> they're from A Miracle of Science, the trope namer for science related memetic disorder)<br /> <br /> So basically the same reasons Werewolf has rules for Death Rage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=978033#post978033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obviously working within a Baramin makes sense, but I don't get why Baramins would ever cooperate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, most of the time they don't cooperate.<br /> <br /> They <i>used to</i> cooperate because<br /> <br /> 1) The secret masters would reward them if they did (and see my proposed Dharmasist grant for bypassing Unmada)<br /> 2) The secret masters would punish them if they didn't.<br /> <br /> That has left them enough of a legacy to cooperate. But only in exceptional circumstances when they have a common enemy in the peerage or some Chuthlu like Mane; or when everyone involved thinks that they're leading the alliance (probably because of a <i>very</i> convincing Phenomenologist)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=978128#post978128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm beginning to wonder if Genius shouldn't just have Foundation / Baramin creation rules much like the upcoming Changeling 2E Freehold Court creation system</div> </div> </div> </div> It shouldn't.<br /> <br /> The Foundations are designed to represent archetypical mad scientists and they do that job well. In addition Genius has a rich in-setting history (especially important for a game with time travel). A build your own group would loose both of those advantages and since we already have build your own for Fellowships it wouldn't even add much.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=978128#post978128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Baramins, of which the grouping collectively known as Lemuria are most well known, are associated around a sole 'unifying' theory based on where mankind's development went wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's actually a deeper level to them. Baramins are each based on a style of thinking that is, in of itself, dangerous. I don't mean they're automatically bad and if you think that way you should stop. I just mean dangerous, they have inherent risks that must be protected against.<br /> <br /> Atomists reduce everything to numbers on a spreadsheet.<br /> Etherites are fundamentalists, valuing ideological purity above life itself.<br /> Mechanics take no responsibility for their actions.*<br /> Oracles cannot see subtly or shades of grey.<br /> Phenomenologists believe that a convincing argument trumps empirical reality.<br /> <br /> That's another thing I think is awesome and would be lost with a build your own system.<br /> <br /> * I actually think Mechanist's are weakest and would rework them to be people who think people only have worth if they earn it. Think Randian Objectivism through the lens of renaissance craftsmen guilds rather than modern American corporations.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 09-29-2016, 05:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T05:23:24-07:00","id":978322,"title":"","content":"Actually Foundation/Baramin/Faculty creation rules were given to us by Moochava in first edition: Each require Mania a day investment, has two prefered axioms, grands a grant, and requires character to aquire dot in a mental skill if player seeks to switch faculties. Fill this up, create the fluff behind your Faculty and you are done. <br /> This rules are pretty useless for games set in World of Darkness, since it would muddle up original themes and moods by trying to force an additional puzzle piece in complete picture, but are extremely useful if you want to try to make your own setting (in which for example Peerage and Lemuria wouldn't exist).<br /> <br /> As for Jabir revamp rules. I don't think this is a good idea. The mechanic is genuinely interesting but it's weird mix of involuntary reward/punishment. In addition it meddles with pretty subjective concepts of what is and isn't broad/narrow enough category for each tier of Integrity. And in addition it doesn't contibute enough to the game, because Mad Scientists going into rants is already encouraged by &quot;And now I will tell you my plan&quot; (and by being just plain fun thing to do for some). In addition as I had said above by using this ability to substitute already existing Jabir you remove mechnics for technobabble which is actually a classic trope of Sci-Fi.<br /> Ultimately, I think this is just a clunky way to do something already suggested in other edition: Archetypes.<br /> Lector:<br /> Once per scene gains one willpower by putting one self in danger or significant disadventage by ranting about something only they care about.<br /> Once per session gain all will power by ranting for 10 or more turns and revealing information that had to remain secret.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12082,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","user":"Weird","date":". 09-29-2016, 08:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T06:26:18-07:00","id":978340,"title":"","content":"The mechanic has already been proven to work in Werewolf.<br /> <br /> It doesn't have to replace And Now I Will Tell You My Plan. Just make that rule say you regain Mania but have to make an automatic Jabair check when you do. It makes the rule work even better because you can now actually have a Condition called &quot;I told you my plan&quot;.<br /> <br /> As for technobabble, if I'm honest, the Jabir mechanic has it backwards. Most technobabble makes perfect sense to the charachter who says it and the charachter who doesn't. Scotty or Spock technobabbling to Kirk is more likely to get a &quot;great idea&quot; than a &quot;speak English man&quot;. Besides, a flat dice penalty is not sufficent to handle core themes of a splat.<br /> <br /> For that reason I'd limit technobabble to talking about Wonders. If you try to explain how a Wonder works you reduce your successes by their dots in a relevant mental skill. Any competent scientist will cut you off the moment you mention phlogiston. (Unless they know you're a mad scientist, in which case they'll just nod and smile).<br /> <br /> Doing this has the advantage in that it makes it much easier to justify charachter concepts like university professor (who really should be easy to have). Instead having Jabir every time you lecture on, say, biology, you only have a problem when you talk about mitosis (and normally your lectures are on a different part of biology anyway). Rare but big events make better story seeds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T06:51:10-07:00","id":978352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=978340#post978340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The mechanic has already been proven to work in Werewolf.<br /> <br /> It doesn't have to replace And Now I Will Tell You My Plan. Just make that rule say you regain Mania but have to make an automatic Jabair check when you do. It makes the rule work even better because you can now actually have a Condition called &quot;I told you my plan&quot;.<br /> <br /> As for technobabble, if I'm honest, the Jabir mechanic has it backwards. Most technobabble makes perfect sense to the charachter who says it and the charachter who doesn't. Scotty or Spock technobabbling to Kirk is more likely to get a &quot;great idea&quot; than a &quot;speak English man&quot;. Besides, a flat dice penalty is not sufficent to handle core themes of a splat.<br /> <br /> For that reason I'd limit technobabble to talking about Wonders. If you try to explain how a Wonder works you reduce your successes by their dots in a relevant mental skill. Any competent scientist will cut you off the moment you mention phlogiston. (Unless they know you're a mad scientist, in which case they'll just nod and smile).<br /> <br /> Doing this has the advantage in that it makes it much easier to justify charachter concepts like university professor (who really should be easy to have). Instead having Jabir every time you lecture on, say, biology, you only have a problem when you talk about mitosis (and normally your lectures are on a different part of biology anyway). Rare but big events make better story seeds.</div> </div> </div> </div>I approve. Both because it makes &quot;triggering&quot; a strategic option (for others), and a consideration (at least for the self-aware) towards keeping one's Obligation/Ethics/etc. high.<br /> <br /> I also am in favor of restricting Jabir to Wonders (and/or just generally Genius things), as that allows for Genii not to be total pariahs. And because a few of my character concepts do have them in actually academic or technical fields. They should still be competent (just don't ask them about their pet projects).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T08:04:42-07:00","id":978407,"title":"","content":"Has there been any consensus reached on Wonders regarding Mania Investment? Bound Mania, but cost-less Hibernation mode (enabling a vault of Gadgets, but you can only &quot;use&quot; those you Bind), or the ability to &quot;pay&quot; for Wonders (meaning XP can expand how many Wonders you have)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T01:21:59-07:00","id":978917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=978407#post978407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bound Mania, but cost-less Hibernation mode</div> </div> </div> </div>This is my preference.<br /> <br /> I was also thinking that there should be a many-in-one wonder that reduces bound mania costs. If you have enough skill dots to traverse on the tech web.<br /> <br /> To take that concept from the top.<br /> <br /> Axioms are split into individual abilities called Infrances. So Apokolypsi 2 would be split into one Infrance for each type of scanner, etc. Each Infrance has a cost (lets call it Sparks (of Inspiration)) and an associated Mental Skill. A biological scanner would cost 1 Spark and require Medicine. A mad science scanner would cost 1 Spark and require Science. When creating a Wonder a Genius has one Spark per dot in the <i>lowest</i> of all associated skills.<br /> <br /> Because biological scanners are connected to mad science scanners on the tech web a Genius could create one wonder that scans both biology and mad science at the same time. Just so long as they have at least two dots in both Science and Medicine. It would only require one Bound Mania<br /> <br /> Wonders like this either do both at once (you point the scanner at something and gain both science and biological information) are target sensitive (your ice beam does damage and applies Immobilized if you point it at a person, it applies the Icy environmental tilt if you point it at the ground) or have a switch between modes (you biological scanner and healer has different buttons for scanning and healing).<br /> <br /> -------------<br /> <br /> All of those would only Bind the Mania of the most expensive Infrance they include. However all Wonders would have an additional flat cost of 2-3 bound Mania to make the default a few powerful signature wonders plus lots of kitbashing. (Kitbashing also allows you to use Infrances you haven't spent exp on. But you have to start on the web at one of your favoured Axioms or an Infrance you brought).<br /> <br /> And to provide exceptions to the above they'll be Merits like:<ul><li>Crazy Prepared: Once per session you can transfer a Wonder from hibernation in your Laboratory to your pocket by spending it's Bound Mania cost (and binding the spent points). The player retroactively declares that their charachter predicted they'll need the Wonder and brought it with them. The Wonder must be size 3 or less, but a Crazy Prepared Genius can declare that their self-piloting airship has been hovering nearby or that their Beholden is watching the clock and ready to teleport a wonder to a predetermined location.</li> <li>Signiture Wonder: The Genius has a single primary wonder, usually a vechicle, suit, or robot. Any Wonders Integral to their primary wonder reduce the Bound Mania requirement by X (where X is flat cost). However other wonders (except the prime wonder itself) increase their bound mania cost by Y (probably 1)</li> <li>Posthuman: Like signature Wonder but for grafted or interlaized wonders in your own body.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> Larvae could also be more available too. With basic Larvae (e.g. graverobbing) only requiring that you take a Condition and only more powerful Larvae requiring serious Ethical breaches. Larvae could also provide bonus Sparks; with some powerful Wonders like doomsday cannons costing 6+ sparks all by themselves meaning that only the most powerful Geniuses can build them without questing for a McGuffin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T07:04:03-07:00","id":978993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=978917#post978917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is my preference.<br /> <br /> I was also thinking that there should be a many-in-one wonder that reduces bound mania costs. If you have enough skill dots to traverse on the tech web.<br /> <br /> To take that concept from the top.<br /> <br /> Axioms are split into individual abilities called Infrances. So Apokolypsi 2 would be split into one Infrance for each type of scanner, etc. Each Infrance has a cost (lets call it Sparks (of Inspiration)) and an associated Mental Skill. A biological scanner would cost 1 Spark and require Medicine. A mad science scanner would cost 1 Spark and require Science. When creating a Wonder a Genius has one Spark per dot in the <i>lowest</i> of all associated skills.<br /> <br /> Because biological scanners are connected to mad science scanners on the tech web a Genius could create one wonder that scans both biology and mad science at the same time. Just so long as they have at least two dots in both Science and Medicine. It would only require one Bound Mania<br /> <br /> Wonders like this either do both at once (you point the scanner at something and gain both science and biological information) are target sensitive (your ice beam does damage and applies Immobilized if you point it at a person, it applies the Icy environmental tilt if you point it at the ground) or have a switch between modes (you biological scanner and healer has different buttons for scanning and healing).<br /> <br /> -------------<br /> <br /> All of those would only Bind the Mania of the most expensive Infrance they include. However all Wonders would have an additional flat cost of 2-3 bound Mania to make the default a few powerful signature wonders plus lots of kitbashing. (Kitbashing also allows you to use Infrances you haven't spent exp on. But you have to start on the web at one of your favoured Axioms or an Infrance you brought).<br /> <br /> And to provide exceptions to the above they'll be Merits like:<ul><li>Crazy Prepared: Once per session you can transfer a Wonder from hibernation in your Laboratory to your pocket by spending it's Bound Mania cost (and binding the spent points). The player retroactively declares that their charachter predicted they'll need the Wonder and brought it with them. The Wonder must be size 3 or less, but a Crazy Prepared Genius can declare that their self-piloting airship has been hovering nearby or that their Beholden is watching the clock and ready to teleport a wonder to a predetermined location.</li> <li>Signiture Wonder: The Genius has a single primary wonder, usually a vechicle, suit, or robot. Any Wonders Integral to their primary wonder reduce the Bound Mania requirement by X (where X is flat cost). However other wonders (except the prime wonder itself) increase their bound mania cost by Y (probably 1)</li> <li>Posthuman: Like signature Wonder but for grafted or interlaized wonders in your own body.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br /> Larvae could also be more available too. With basic Larvae (e.g. graverobbing) only requiring that you take a Condition and only more powerful Larvae requiring serious Ethical breaches. Larvae could also provide bonus Sparks; with some powerful Wonders like doomsday cannons costing 6+ sparks all by themselves meaning that only the most powerful Geniuses can build them without questing for a McGuffin.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. That system seems kind of dense and complex. Charts might help. I'll think about it and the ramifications a bit more before commenting further on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T15:47:36-07:00","id":979295,"title":"","content":"In regards to character groups, of course the present Foundations and Baramins are good for default use for pick up and play. I wouldn't say they're exhaustive of all Mad Scientist archetypes but it would likely be better to have extra specialization via the Fellowships for those that want home brewing tools.<br /> <br /> -------------------------<br /> <br /> Bound Mania sounds better for general Wonder creation, as more stable Wonders that are Experience based could come from Fellowships (perhaps a Fellowship could become a shared project that stays consistent compared to other creations of Inspiration).<br /> <br /> I've been wanting to make Wonder creation more robust as well, in doing so how each Axiom can be differed by pairing with other skills. Primarily, we need more than the 5 mental skills used within the 1.1 guide for wonder creation. At minimum, all of the Mental skills plus <i>applied</i> Physical and Social skills. Axioms, in terms of what they do, are grouped by verb. They are more like the Practices that define Spells in Mage (per Arcana) or the Manifestations of Geist: the Sin-Eaters (paired with Keys).<br /> <br /> In these systems powers are created by pairing fundamental and thematic aspects into a supernatural ability. Axioms provide the foundation of what a Wonder or Inspired creation does. But does the <i>thematic</i> strata to pair with Axioms really need to be something new? When Skills are already provided to be plenty robust, as an Axiom and Skill are already used within the Wonder creation dice pool.<br /> <br /> Infrance and Sparks sound novel enough, but if the Infrances divvy up an Axiom by skill and the Sparks are derived from skills, why not cut out the middle man and just use the character's own Skill ratings? The Axiom is the only supernatural stat for Genius to define the scope of a Genius's capabilities, ideally scaled from minute every specific kinds of Wonders at low rating to broad and groundbreaking at high Axiom rating. A Genius could still attempt to make a greater Wonder beyond their current rating of the Axiom if they have a penalty (the remaining difference) and more Faults or other drawbacks.<br /> <br /> <br /> In my notes I've been thinking of every applied use of a Skill a Genius would use for their projects and occupations. Note that after creation a Wonder will likely be operated with a different skill pool.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Mental</b></u><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Academics</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">For history, research, social sciences (microspective) and psychology</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Crafts</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">For mechanical construction and engineering, robotics, design and artwork</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Computer</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">For programs, data analysis, hi-tech electronics, algorithms and AI</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Investigation</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Forensics, analysis, understanding wonders and tracking</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Medicine</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Health and disease, biological components, surgery, organic chemistry</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Occult</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dead, paranormal and other supernatural involvement</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Politics</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Macrospective social applications, civil service, behavior on societal level</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Science</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Energy, subatomic particles, \u2018normative\u2019 and miscellaneous science</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b>Physical</b></u><br /> <br /> Firearms<br /> For artillery, projectiles, maintenance, scoping<br /> <br /> Weaponry<br /> For melee, maintenance, smithing<br /> <br /> Survival<br /> For landscaping, terraforming, ecosystems and natural architecture<br /> <br /> <u><b>Social</b></u><br /> <br /> Animal Ken<br /> For training, (crypto) zoology<br /> <br /> Expression<br /> For artistry, artwork, music, and literature","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T01:15:37-07:00","id":979550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=979295#post979295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Infrance and Sparks sound novel enough, but if the Infrances divvy up an Axiom by skill and the Sparks are derived from skills, why not cut out the middle man and just use the character's own Skill ratings?</div> </div> </div> </div> Simple. Because there is no 1-5 rating for Axioms under that system. You buy Infrances individually and you can buy them in any order.<br /> <br /> (I have not yet put thought into what the actual Infrances will be or how they link. This is just an example)<br /> <br /> A Genius might favour Exelixi. That means they can buy Mechanical Repair or Healing Devices. If they buy Healing Devices they unlock the ability to buy Organic Weapons or Biological Imrpovements. Buying Biological Improvements unlocks Mechanical Improvements or Biological Automata.<br /> <br /> <br /> Another Genius might favour Automata and buy Organic Triggered Devices --&gt; Oragnic Automata --&gt; Organic Improvement --&gt; Healing Devices. Because they didn't favour Exelixi they had to take this long detour to get healing.<br /> <br /> Basically imagine something like the tech web from Beyond Earth<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://www.cosmosgaming.com/wp-content/uploads/2014/11/Beyond-Earth-2-1024x559.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The Axioms are in the middle and each technology is an Infrance. If you buy one Infrance you can buy any other Infrance it's connected too. Or you can use that Infrance as a starting point when Kitbashing, include Infrances you don't know in your Wonder so long as you have enough Sparks to travel to them.<br /> <br /> For artistry, artwork, music, and literature[/QUOTE]<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=978993#post978993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. That system seems kind of dense and complex. Charts might help. I'll think about it and the ramifications a bit more before commenting further on it.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well I am a computer programmer so don't ask me to judge what's dense and complex. But I do like that system a lot.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T07:32:45-07:00","id":979647,"title":"","content":"Hmm, my first gut reaction is to say that having the Wonder creation system use a tech tree would be another step towards diminishing the Genius experience. The player wouldn\u2019t think they are creating anything new, just unlocking options on a tech tree and thereby making Wonders more predictable, boring, and less creative.<br /> <br /> I also don\u2019t see why Axioms are no longer rated with dots, as regardless of tiers or effects your Axiom <i><b>adds dice</b></i> to the Wonder creation pool.<br /> <br /> -------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> That being said, when taking another look at the Infrance and tech tree system it sounds like a much more elegant way to present Variables, the first \u2018subset\u2019 properties for Wonders in the 1.1 guide. In the first guide you kind of just \u2018knew\u2019 Variables upon being a Genius, some with a few Axiom prerequisites, either split between an individual Axiom or general use. I always felt that was unrefined, although Variables were also seen as rigid to some from only connecting expected properties together.<br /> <br /> I also like the idea of if you can\u2019t meet the prerequisite normally, by not having the proper Axiom or whatever, you could cheat the effect from chained knowledge bringing you about to the Infrance/Variable by a number of linked types instead of the normal prerequisite rating.<br /> <br /> Instead of there being a universial tech tree (as Mania and Inspiration are not presented as being that predictable) what if each Genius has their own personal \u2018tech-tree\u2019 that they develop over the course of play? It is not predetermined, like you said about chaining the properties in any order, as beyond the starting general or simple Axiom granted Infrances/Variables the Genius may link up each specialized application only if thematic, categorical, Wonder type or Axiom is shared. <br /> <br /> A Genius who has dabbled with organic beings has a sudden change of passion, they add \u2018Mechanical Scanner\u2019 to branch from their previous \u2018Organic Scanner\u2019 that previously represented meat-tech quasi-living components that derived biometric information. Further dabbling with heavy mechanics bring the Genius along a new flourishing branch of their tech tree but they of course still have their starting organics branch to fall back on.<br /> <br /> <br /> A personalized tech web would also benefit mechanics for Variable/Infrance creation and customization I wanted to introduce at a future time. The basics are that to add more of a researcher and experimenter feel to the game, the Genius is able to give their hypothesises validity in the form of new Variables and theorems if successful. To add to their tech web the Genius requires it to link with at least one other property, more would be better. Another Genius could then \u2018reverse-engineer\u2019 that custom Variable by finding a way it would stick into their tech tree, likely because of a very different linkup.<br /> <br /> There could also be rules to suggest (if the web of a Geniuses Infrance/Variables is capped by Inspiration stat in some way) that the Genius could invalidate old applications for new ones if they lacked the space to add more desirable options. Its effectively a self contained Sanctity of Merits kind of scenario within this system, as no new costs are needed to trade Infrances for others. However, the Infrance\u2019s position along the branch can cause problems if it forms the only bridge with a web of options the Genius still wishes to possess. Reflexively, the Genius will have to spend a point of Mania for each Variable they wish to redefine (read, connect it back to the tech tree). Broken off options are either lost for no refund or add increased, potent Faults when used or other drawbacks. When the Genius is able to find a way to bridge broken Infrances back into their web these drawbacks are removed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T12:39:56-07:00","id":980383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=979647#post979647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, my first gut reaction is to say that having the Wonder creation system use a tech tree would be another step towards diminishing the Genius experience. The player wouldn\u2019t think they are creating anything new, just unlocking options on a tech tree and thereby making Wonders more predictable, boring, and less creative.</div> </div> </div> </div> I feel the opposite this adds more options.<br /> <br /> Infrances already exist in the current system. The difference is that you buy them as a group. So while you might have slight differences based on variables a radiation beam and a laser gun are basically the same mechanically. With Infrances you can combine various effects together to create something truly unique. The radiation beam might also be used to mutate animals, while the laser gun could be used for welding.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=979647#post979647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also don\u2019t see why Axioms are no longer rated with dots, as regardless of tiers or effects your Axiom <i><b>adds dice</b></i> to the Wonder creation pool.</div> </div> </div> </div> Removes dice actually. You could do something similar with a penalty equal to sparks spent<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=979647#post979647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Instead of there being a universial tech tree (as Mania and Inspiration are not presented as being that predictable) what if each Genius has their own personal \u2018tech-tree\u2019 that they develop over the course of play? It is not predetermined, like you said about chaining the properties in any order, as beyond the starting general or simple Axiom granted Infrances/Variables the Genius may link up each specialized application only if thematic, categorical, Wonder type or Axiom is shared.</div> </div> </div> </div> A while back I had the thought that alternative webs for the same infrances would make a great way to create unique technology to make exploring Bardos or ruins of ancient laboratories but I hadn't considered individual webs.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't want it to go so far as every Genius having a 100% customised tech web. But the idea of individual additions could work. The standard web is based on &quot;real science&quot;, or rather cultural ideas that in the modern world are based on real science. <br /> <br /> So healing is linked to biological scanners because obviously identifying the problem is directly linked to healing the problem. But in a culture which believed healing, regardless of the disease, is done through prayer healing might be linked to the Infrance used to control Spirits. Meanwhile an Oracle raised as a modern secular atheist American might start to believe that al healing is done through prayer and add that link as a personal addition to the tech web.<br /> <br /> I'd probably say you have to have brought both Infrances with exp before you can link them. Just to avoid people getting top level powers like time travel or resserection straight out the gate.<br /> <br /> <br /> BTW Any tech web we write will probably not be comprehensive. So a player who finds a cool new idea could either invent a new Infrance in charachter or they could declare it's publically known and add it to the standard web.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T21:55:44-07:00","id":980580,"title":"","content":"This is the Wonder Creation roll outlined on pg. 143 in the Genius 1.1 document:<br /> <span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">Inspiration + Attribute + Skill + Laboratory Equipment + Beholden Ability - Wonder Rank <br /> Add an additional die if the wonder is of the genius' favored Axiom.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Let's break this down as to what is going on at each step.<br /> <br /> Inspiration, Attribute and Skill is going to be the base dicepool.<br /> <br /> Laboratory, Equipment, Beholden and Teamwork are occasional modifiers that will only contribute if you have beneficial merits reflecting these elements.<br /> <br /> Wonder Rank is derived from the combined Axioms in the desired Wonder, so I was incorrect in saying that you add dice from your Axioms but the rating of Axiom is still important as it acts in penalty. Creation of a Wonder with Skafoi 1 and Metatropi 2 will be -3 altogether.<br /> <br /> You get a bonus die from a favored Axiom being used, determined by Catalyst and Foundation.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now here's where other factors NOT listed on this page come into play. From pg. 136 further penalties are mentioned but where not included in the formulae above.<br /> <br /> If the Genius doesn't have a Resources rating matching or greater than Wonder Rank, the difference of higher Rank and Resources becomes another penalty. This brings up the 'Where your Resources comes from' discussion again. If it's considered that important I've felt a new system should be put into place to tie into this, call it Funding or the Budget a Genius has to have the materials, space and energy necessary for their projects. If you don't have the Budget for it, Creation also gets another penalty. It would also cover the long list of potential deprived, environmental and similar drawbacks mentioned on pg. 136.<br /> <br /> Then the particulars for Kit-bashing get mentioned, but this plays into how long it takes to create a Wonder based on its Size. Which doesn't factor microscopic or intangible Wonders, nor things like literature or coding by word/page count. Default is said to be 1 day on the pg. 138 Time Taken chart, but this really means six hours per day, and everything goes screwy from there. Basically penalties start doubling as you reduce total creation time, or you get further +1 die for taking longer time to 'perfect' the Wonder.<br /> <br /> There's far too many sticking points on what can't be done, in a game about Geniuses that can regularly screw with the laws of nature and science as powered by Inspiration which has few consistencies. For one thing, I don't believe the Attributes should be limited to two Mental (Intelligence or Wits) or 5 Mental skills to create a Wonder. It should be determined if Physical, Mental or Social attributes are more important to the kind of Wonder being made. And see my earlier thoughts on applied Skills, although you would still use the lesser of multiple Skills that would cover the Wonder in question.<br /> <br /> You can also enhance creation with Mania and Willpower. Willpower can be used once, usual +3, and Mania adds 1 for 1.<br /> <br /> ----------------------------<br /> <br /> The idea of a personalized web is that for every group of Geniuses that do all do 'common' kinds of mad science tech, you have the other Geniuses that fly in the face of that with baffling inventions that don't follow any previous convention. It's implied throughout the book that other Geniuses can't make the projects, wonders and theorems of their peers work for themselves. (Unless they take the Universalist merit). Consistent, nigh 'perfected' Wonders that work for multiple Geniuses only come from the members being in the same Fellowship.<br /> <br /> If the Genius is governed by their Aesthetic and their Paradigm (am I missing any traits?) whose to say they'll always draw from previous sets of Variables?<br /> <br /> With an Infrance as a cluster of Variables, if I gather it correctly, and knowing that no great web/list will be exhaustive, how do you plan to categorize these Infrances? And how they bridge to each other. Keywords, categories, archetypes.<br /> <br /> This may be as snarled of any nest to smooth out as any, since the freeform system still needs some easy to comprehend guidelines. The most elegant freeform system I've seen in awhile is the <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Br5u6ylBDdzNDG6Q_r09pohkyGvgq3hSWVuJPDPrRXA/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Verse</a> powers introduced in Siren: the Drowning. Each Verse has Introduction, Opus and Conclusion. Intro sets the target and duration, Opus is the thematic and Conclusion is the effect. Conclusion and Axiom are the most alike, being tiers of effects. Presumably Infrances are the thematic packages?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T14:39:50-07:00","id":985685,"title":"","content":"So I've recently had a thought for how to outline an Inspired Web/Tech Tree to bring some organization into the kinds of pseudoscience a Genius could be involved in. It brings additional definition to several terms suggested throughout this thread.<br /> <br /> <b>Magnum Opus</b><br /> <u>What:</u> A modified Aspiration and Virtue<ul><li>Steps towards completing the Magnum Opus grant Willpower and/or Mania</li> <li>Allows for gain of Inspired Beats (Supernatural Experience)</li> <li>Rigid, difficult or impossible to change until completed or setback</li> <li>A Characters starting Paradigm(s) reflect their Magnum Opus</li> <li>No Experience cost of its own but laborious to achieve</li> </ul>The Magnum Opus, initially, forms the root of the budding tech tree. The main categories or branches of the tree are Paradigms (alternative: Facets, Infrances)<br /> <br /> <b>Paradigm</b><br /> <u>What:</u> the theory, outlook or worldview the Genius labors under; an approach towards achieving the Magnum Opus<ul><li>provides the Pesudoscience law behind their Wonders and experiments</li> <li>amplified, codified or penalized by Unmada fields and Bardos</li> <li>combines with Axioms when creating Wonders and such phenomena (the thematic)</li> <li>requires systematic upkeep/'proof' or loss of application</li> </ul><br /> Paradigms are further fragmented into Postulates (Variables, Sparks)<br /> <br /> <b>Postulate</b><br /> <u>What:</u> what the applied Paradigm does, the desired effect or output of a Wonder<ul><li>Does at most one thing, highly specialized (like a merit or ability)</li> <li>Scaled along Axiom dots as governed by Paradigm</li> <li>Created and modified from an Experimental process</li> <li>Wonders operate via Postulates, and the max Postulates in any Wonder is the Genius's Axiom dots + half Inspiration at time of creation</li> </ul><br /> Secondary to the Paradigm is the Aesthetic, first introduced in the original Genius document<br /> <br /> <b>Aesthetic</b><br /> <u>What:</u> how the Wonders, experiments and efforts of a Genius are styled by materials, process and cosmetics<ul><li>Secondary overlaping criteria with many Paradigms, Unmada fields, Bardos and similar</li> <li>Easy for the Genius to collect and change out, fad based</li> <li>Amount likely scaled with Inspiration</li> </ul><br /> Now, what is the tech web actually formed from?<br /> <br /> <b>Rationale</b><br /> <u>What:</u> the bridging element along the Genii's tech tree from conceptual or abstract association.<ul><li>Requires 1 bound Mania to form the link</li> <li>The pairing must make sense for the linked concepts, even if it is adjectively false or untrue</li> <li>Postulates branch off from Paradigms</li> <li>If a Postulate is also valid for another Paradigm the Genius can link to that cluster</li> <li>Alternatively, if there is an overlap of Aesthetic the Genius can temporary connect to obscure Postulates/Paradigms, adding them to the tree with bound Mania as normal</li> <li>More links means more consistency (increased bonus or lessened Faults or some benefit)</li> </ul><br /> So in effect, the Genius develops a web of personalized technology and theorems that operate for themselves. This is merely the organization of such a system, mechanics and limits to be determined. Paradigms, the main aspect of the tech tree/web (Needs a better name) can be gotten different ways. The Genius could perform an experiment to validate a Paradigm or Postulate (modeled after Investigative Clues, to be posted in future), adapt or adopt a Paradigm from another Genius. A Collaborative could draw from each other's Paradigms for an increased cost/some sort of minor penalty. And Paradigms form the basis of Fellowships and Baramins, or could be gleaned from Bardo travel.<br /> <br /> How this would interact with Inspiration, Obligation, Havoc, Faults and other systems is to be determined. The future second edition of Genius would provide many examples of Paradigms, Postulates and Aesthetics but also show that these are not exhaustive examples, encouraging creativity from those that want to home-brew but providing enough ideas and suggested links for pick up and play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T11:11:08-07:00","id":986231,"title":"","content":"Staying out of Tech Tree talk because it seems way too complex for a &quot;simple&quot; one sheet Roleplaying game to me at the moment, and because I am fairly inexperienced with how player have operated with Axiom dot system.<br /> <br /> Instead I have several propositions towards general theme and mood shift. Some players suggested shifting radically from Bitter Disappointment and towards Success at Any Costs. I honestly don't think either is quite a perfect option for a game of mad science. First tends to result with Venture Bros. styled pop-culture deconstruction with added layer of cynicism and unecessary angst, while other is... literally how Illuminated operate. <br /> Suggested new theme: Was/Is it Worth it? Inspired with their twisted reasoning and radicalized worldviews have to vigilantly evaluate themselves and ask if what they are doing is really worth it. Utopias are built at great costs, but how many lives have been lost for utopias that never came or became tyrannies before fullfilling their promise. Is a potential masterpiece always worth distancing oneself from one's family and friends? <br /> <br /> Also, not to be rude, but Batman and his code of a Vigilante sounds pretty at home in Hunter; Wasn't Genius supposed to be the game about those sitting in Arkham, obsessing over fear, plants, Alice, and Nora?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T12:28:19-07:00","id":991483,"title":"","content":"For a 2e Genius I'd like a way to obtain more Mania without having to suck it out of other people or kidnapping them. As is you're stuck with 7 Mania per day, which is only enough if you don't use things that require a daily allotment of Mania (IE: Automata).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T17:15:09-07:00","id":993791,"title":"","content":"Batman has one of the most recognizable rogues galleries for a reason. As DC's flagship franchise both the Caped Crusader and his villains are drawn from pulp adventures, mystery and horror in different ways that one could use as inspiration for Genius. I'm of the opinion you can use other media to inspire your CoD game's for different venues. Both Hunter and Genius and other supernatural lines could draw different ideas from Batman.<br /> <br /> Batman himself is a gadget based hero, something the more active Foundations like the Navigators would become. Iron Man is another example of a tech heavy 'superhero.' From the villains you have those shaped by their science (Mr. Freeze, Poison Ivy) their brand of insanity (Joker) or a mix of both (Harley Quinn, being a former psychiatrist). The use of bizarre science in nearly all superhero media means you can easily play such characters in Genius.<br /> <br /> <br /> Not that I mean to bring up the Mage and Genius comparisons again but it serves as the easiest explanation for determining Genius characteristics. For Mage they scale each Arcana they know, or a purview of influences they have. The Thematic quality of their powers. At each dot of Arcana they can do more with it, with 13 Practices or 'Actions' they can do with Arcana at their given level. It's makes a very straightforward and predictable setup. If you can learn a character's ratings of Arcana you can predict what they are capable of. Geist has a similar system with Manifestations (actions) and Keys (thematic). For home-brew, the system for Siren: the Drowning's <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Br5u6ylBDdzNDG6Q_r09pohkyGvgq3hSWVuJPDPrRXA/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Verses</a> does the action and thematic pairing very brilliantly, along with a changeable 'target' for the powers.<br /> <br /> Genius approaches the supernatural abilities differently. You scale the <i><b>Actions</b></i> from 1 to 5 dots. Each Axiom is a verb. It is a category of what Wonders can do, with each increasing rating getting more groundbreaking/gamebreaking. The trouble of this is that it's harder to determine what perquisites you need for a certain Wonder. The 1.1 version of Genius used common super science tropes and had write-ups/Variables in the axioms that suggested certain kind of Thematic parallels to each Axiom, although this was never concrete. Siren's Conclusions, the verbs, are very similar.<br /> <br /> I'm fine with sticking to Axioms as the only set of Supernatural traits. To me, it would be more of a disservice to Genius if there was an overarching 'thematic' system to pair with the Axioms. For one, it tells the player you can only player certain kinds of Mad Scientists, certain occupations and niches. Others aren't allowed. Second, as presented Inspiration and Mania are not consistent or predictable. This is the biggest contrast from Mage; in Mage the character becomes awakened to the Supernal Truths of the world, the existence of magic. The magic is still magic, with Mages all studying the same Truths.<br /> <br /> For Genius there is no 'Truth' behind everything. Even the Principle of Promethean has more consistency behind it. All theories are valid until disproven. Even when disproven by others a Genius can keep their Wonders ongoing from sheer belief and insanity. The inherent Un-Truth and Uncertainty of Genius is something to be embraced, these a qualities that help it stand out from other game lines.<br /> <br /> The obvious drawback, I realize, is that this type of freeform is hard to balance from a game mechanics perspective. For players without the DIY attitude persisting in Genius they will need some sort of reference to draw from when determining what their characters can do. To that end yes, have lists of various kinds of effects you can get from Wonders and example builds completed. There should be the emphasis that these are only examples with more room for customization, not the be-all-end-all.<br /> <br /> I've tried outlining the scope of each Axiom dot by dot but even that gets very circumspect with my first drafts. At basic, I suggest that Axiom 1 be very specific to Axiom 5's very broad application. And at Axiom 3 it can interact with other kinds of supernatural subjects and powers (like Numen or other venues).<br /> <br /> <br /> I also have a thought for other Mania gain, although that is saved for a future post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T11:42:29-07:00","id":995724,"title":"","content":"I'll insist that Batman shouldn't be primary &quot;superhero&quot; inspiration on account how &quot;tame&quot; is equipment is and how his motives and actions are of a vigilante rather than of a mad visionary. Iron Man does serve as a better example of a wealthy Irradium Sentinel. Stark also serves as a classical example of Genius usually being their own worst enemy. <br /> <br /> Trying to compare other Integrity systems and how they relate to the gamelines and their themes made me wonder if Genius's Itegrity trait should be Reason, which would be lost over crimes that yeld no significent social, economical and/or intellectual benefit. Geniuses sound like they would be flexibly utilitarian in things they consider acceptable. Of course consequences are everything and when facing with unexpected by-products of their actions Geniuses are likely to have second thoughts whether or not their actions were necessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T07:49:50-07:00","id":997689,"title":"","content":"So, what are the current thoughts on the Axioms?<br /> <br /> Ranked, with rank affecting:<ul><li>Allowed abilities (as in 1E, basically)</li> <li>Wonder modifier (Axiom dots/ranks/level affects calculations or effects)</li> <li>Depth in field (if using a &quot;Tech-web&quot;, perhaps Axiom rating allows how much you can pile on in any one category - you want a heal-anything multi-tool, better have high dots in Exelixi)</li> <li>A modifier to rolls with the Wonder, either activation (superior knowledge of field lets you use the devices better), or construction (if Wonder creation is like Mage 2E's spell casting - base pool, with factors lowering the dice pool - then high rank may allow more reliable creation, like adding an extra Skill to the dice pool)</li> <li>Free variables per rank (like the Free Reach/Grasp Mage Arcana grants)</li> </ul><br /> Unranked<ul><li>Defines categories of abilities (like Demon's Embed categories)<ul><li>Category could affect options available</li> <li>Groups sub-options that have to be purchased separately (Postulates/Inferences)</li> <li>Allows for broadly applicable effects (like +1 to Epikrato rolls, or undoes Metatropi effects, etc.)</li> </ul></li> <li>Allowed abilities (like with 1E, except all options become available with an Axiom unlocked)</li> </ul><br /> Ditched","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 11-03-2016, 10:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T11:16:24-07:00","id":997782,"title":"","content":"I don't really see why the Axioms would require such heavy reworking. Some finetuning perhaps, and have Prostasia do something more, and you're pretty much set.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T11:47:16-07:00","id":997800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=997782#post997782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really see why the Axioms would require such heavy reworking. Some finetuning perhaps, and have Prostasia do something more, and you're pretty much set.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, basically a vote for &quot;as in 1E&quot;?<br /> <br /> Yeah, some of the specific effects are going to need reworking for the 2E update, and just tweaks in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T15:27:04-07:00","id":997910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=997782#post997782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really see why the Axioms would require such heavy reworking. Some finetuning perhaps, and have Prostasia do something more, and you're pretty much set.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it might be good to have it structured more like Werewolf 2E gifts: You have your Axiomata, rated 1-5, and then you can choose Facets from various Fields for things your Wonders can do. Every time you rank up in an Axiom, you get a new Application from one of your Fields for that Axiom for free, and you can buy access to new Fields as you wish.<br /> <br /> For example, you could have a Field of Biology (call it life-weaving or something if you want it to be more paradigm-neutral) that has the following Applications:<ul><li>Mutation (Metaptropi)</li> <li>Necrosis (Katastrofi)</li> <li>Revivification (Exilixi)</li> <li>Immunity (Prostasia)</li> <li>Uplift (Automata)</li> <li>etc.</li> </ul><br /> That way, we can have a lot of flexibility in how a Genius develops as a Genius and cut out the clutter of options for any single character, but it doesn't totally close you off from being an Omnidisciplinary Expert if you want to put in the Experiences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T22:09:05-07:00","id":998616,"title":"","content":"The old Axioms are basically OK (although I agree Infrances should be made explicit rather than implicit.) But they <i>can </i>be limiting.<br /> <br /> Why not make alternate tech-trees a merit? Like Raven's idea with bardos having their own weird science, or metablener's idea with some geniuses just Not Following The Rules.<i> In general</i> people use Axioms, but some characters buy a Biology Scanner to match their Healing Ray or only buy half of the next rank in Metatropi.<br /> <br /> Something like one Merit dot per rank, allows you to buy an Infrance of that rank without purchasing or qualifying for the associated Axiom, and it counts as having that Axiom rank for the purpose of unlocking things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T15:59:23-07:00","id":998927,"title":"","content":"I don't think Axiom's need to be nerfed or overcomplicated (which is what I am understanding from the Facet talk). <br /> <br /> If you need to balance Geniuses I propose adding bans and banes, and I have figured out suitable story explanation that in fact could make banes enchance story structure. <br /> Most banes are result of flaw of supernatural source of power of supernatural beings. For Geniuses that source is Inspiration and their mania. Mania seeks to adjust reality in accord with Genius's vision, and as results starts to alter their bodies to physically reject things Genius rejects mentally (be it disgust, subconcious repulsion, phobia or something alike). <br /> For example Peer who never liked milk might find it burning their skin like acid. Or urbanite Lemurian who hates rural is more vulnerable to injuries by farming equipment. Rogue who thinks printed press should be history might loose concious from single swat with a rolled up newspaper. <br /> Possibilities are endless.<br /> <br /> This enchances the sense of each Genius being harbinger of their own doom, however unconcious and unintentional that might be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12082,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","user":"Weird","date":". 11-05-2016, 07:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T16:40:30-07:00","id":998942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=998927#post998927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think Axiom's need to be nerfed or overcomplicated (which is what I am understanding from the Facet talk).<br /> <br /> If you need to balance Geniuses I propose adding bans and banes, and I have figured out suitable story explanation that in fact could make banes enchance story structure.<br /> Most banes are result of flaw of supernatural source of power of supernatural beings. For Geniuses that source is Inspiration and their mania. Mania seeks to adjust reality in accord with Genius's vision, and as results starts to alter their bodies to physically reject things Genius rejects mentally (be it disgust, subconcious repulsion, phobia or something alike).<br /> For example Peer who never liked milk might find it burning their skin like acid. Or urbanite Lemurian who hates rural is more vulnerable to injuries by farming equipment. Rogue who thinks printed press should be history might loose concious from single swat with a rolled up newspaper.<br /> Possibilities are endless.<br /> <br /> This enchances the sense of each Genius being harbinger of their own doom, however unconcious and unintentional that might be.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't really make much sense to me. I can see psychological quirks getting developed or magnified, but physiological reactions seem like they should only come from when a Genius starts tinkering with his own actual biology.<br /> <br /> And the idea with the Facets isn't to nerf or complicate Genii, so much as make them more focused, free-form and a la carte. Right now, Axiomata are structured like Mage Arcana, except sideways (Mage Arcana have a subject and more dots unlocks more actions, Axiomata have an action and unlock subjects), and while that kind of thing makes sense for philosopher-magi who are controlling the underlying symbols of reality, it makes less sense for visionaries trying to advance a very specific vision of the world they want to create with a very specific set of ideals and discoveries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T17:16:53-07:00","id":998954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=998942#post998942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That doesn't really make much sense to me. I can see psychological quirks getting developed or magnified, but physiological reactions seem like they should only come from when a Genius starts tinkering with his own actual biology.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd agree. <br /> <br /> Though I do think Persistent Mental Conditions (Derangements in 1E) should see far more use and detailing in 2E. Part of what defines and works against a Genius is the flaws in their own views and thinking - and I think Conditions that reward you into playing into your own failings (and sabotaging, or accepting ST suggested sabotage, of your actions/goals) would be an excellent way to do that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T17:26:45-07:00","id":998955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=998954#post998954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd agree.<br /> <br /> Though I do think Persistent Mental Conditions (Derangements in 1E) should see far more use and detailing in 2E. Part of what defines and works against a Genius is the flaws in their own views and thinking - and I think Conditions that reward you into playing into your own failings (and sabotaging, or accepting ST suggested sabotage, of your actions/goals) would be an excellent way to do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually had some notes for Catalyst Conditions. <s>Once I can get to a Drive-friendly device, I'll copy-paste them in here.</s> Here they are:<br /> <b>Grimm: Wrath of a Genius</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Grimms are defined by their fury, which comes through in their use of Katastrofi Wonders.<br /> <b>Beat: </b>Your temper causes you to lose sight of your goals or put yourself or friends in danger.<br /> <b>Resolution: </b>You can push yourself past normal anger into a white-hot rage. Resolve this Condition to gain a +3 bonus to attack and Intimidation rolls for the scene, but you may not use All-Out Defense.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <b>Hoffnung: Give Me the Wheel</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Visionaries are fueled by a need for control and power, sometimes as a desire to \u201cimprove\u201d the world, otherwise just as plain power-lust.<br /> <b>Beat: </b>You attempt to take control to the detriment of yourself or others.<br /> <b>Resolution: </b>You stay strong when lesser people buckle. Resolve this Condition to gain a +3 bonus a Breaking Point roll, or on a roll to resist coercion or control, be it mundane, supernatural, or super-science.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <b>Klagen: Cassandra Truth</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Klagen are keenly aware of the destruction they attract, and most are devoted to desperately and pointlessly trying to warn others away.<br /> <b>Beat: </b>You fail to prevent harm to others when you saw it coming.<br /> <b>Resolution: </b>It's happening again, but you know what to do to defuse the situation. You can Resolve this Condition to gain a +3 on a roll to prevent violence or disaster (e.g. talking down an enemy, defusing a bomb, etc.)</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <b>Neid: I'll Show You All!</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Neids are the classic bitter mad scientist with a bone to pick, and a need for approval that can drive them to extremes.<br /> <b>Beat: </b>Your need to prove yourself drives you to harm yourself or those close to you.<br /> <b>Resolution: </b>You will have the recognition you deserve! Resolve this Condition to gain a +3 bonus to any roll to intimidate, coerce or convince others that you're right.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <b>Staunen: Neophilia</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Your affinity for new things can easily distract you from the dangers they carry. This makes you amazing at braving the unknown, but you easily forget how bad an idea that is.<br /> <b>Beat: </b>You endanger yourself or those close to you by pursuing a new phenomenon or obsession<br /> <b>Resolution: </b>You can look into the Abyss longer than others, and learn more when doing so. When studying a metanormal phenomenon or advanced scientific creation, you can Resolve this condition to gain a +3 bonus on a roll to analyze or contain it.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":4488,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","user":"malonkey1","date":". 11-05-2016, 08:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T18:26:28-07:00","id":998975,"title":"","content":"Reminds me I have to think of a Condition for the Eifer Catalyst I wrote.<br /> <br /> How do Facets splinter off the Werewolf Gifts? Is it similar to 2E Promethean, where each Transmutation had four sub-branches of the ability that each did different things. On one hand that would help with the organization but I don't think the Axioms should be complicated with further subdivisions. Having the 'field' in Genius be something like the Key in Geist would be ideal to minimize or eliminate Experience costs. Once you know a field it works in all your Axioms. Or maybe the Genius limits their fields based on Inspiration, and thus could advance in new fields at the cost of having their latter fields of work no longer work for them.<br /> <br /> That being said, I propose another way of doing it (as to play devil's advocate):<br /> <br /> Why not just pair a Skill with an Axiom?<br /> <br /> When it comes to Axiom creation (at default Attribute + Skill + Axiom) expanding how Skills are applied would already create a bunch of options. The 1.1 version used five mental skills and Medicine often fit the weird biology category. Expanding the Skills used with Axioms to all categories (Physical and Social included) will also help branch Genius out of the predominate academia themes.<br /> <br /> With this model your tech tree nodes/variables/infrances/what have you are collected like Skill Specialties, somewhat, only when it comes to matters of Inspiration the Genius can apply them to any other fitting Wonder, experiment or some such.<br /> <br /> -----------------------------------<br /> <br /> What may be best is bridging both systems for use in play. Using Skill + Axiom is the most off the cuff, useful for the innovative Geniuses to create freeform Wonders, etc. Having a grand field of work (like weird biology) could be modeled like the Fellowships. As written they focused more on individual kinds of Wonders but it would be a suitable way to map a field of the Mad Arts &amp; Sciences. I'd wager more Geniuses working on the same stuff might bring the barest trappings of consistency, such as more easily mitigated Faults and Havoc.<br /> <br /> That way several Fields/Fellowships could be written up, an overview of recent Inspired trends with favoritism amongst the Foundations. And you'd still have Skill + Axiom for more radical or alternative applications, and the options for a Genius collaborative to set up their own Field.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T19:51:03-07:00","id":999009,"title":"","content":"You know, I've been thinking about what ArcaneArts said. &quot;The horror of the mad scientist is not that they might fail, but that they might suceed&quot;.<br /> <br /> I agree, and I think Genius would benefit from an endgame option using the Magnum Opus as a guideline. Perhaps a way to overcome Havoc and Jabir so that your Wonders become an accepted part of the world's physical laws?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T19:53:40-07:00","id":999011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=998975#post998975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reminds me I have to think of a Condition for the Eifer Catalyst I wrote.<br /> <br /> How do Facets splinter off the Werewolf Gifts? Is it similar to 2E Promethean, where each Transmutation had four sub-branches of the ability that each did different things. On one hand that would help with the organization but I don't think the Axioms should be complicated with further subdivisions. Having the 'field' in Genius be something like the Key in Geist would be ideal to minimize or eliminate Experience costs. Once you know a field it works in all your Axioms. Or maybe the Genius limits their fields based on Inspiration, and thus could advance in new fields at the cost of having their latter fields of work no longer work for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Each Gift has five Facets, one for each Renown. When you get a new Gift, you get a free Facet from that Gift. When you get a new dot of Renown, you get a new Facet from one of your Gifts, keyed to that Renown. You can't get a Facet unless you have at least one dot in the proper Renown.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That being said, I propose another way of doing it (as to play devil's advocate):<br /> <br /> Why not just pair a Skill with an Axiom?<br /> <br /> When it comes to Axiom creation (at default Attribute + Skill + Axiom) expanding how Skills are applied would already create a bunch of options. The 1.1 version used five mental skills and Medicine often fit the weird biology category. Expanding the Skills used with Axioms to all categories (Physical and Social included) will also help branch Genius out of the predominate academia themes.<br /> <br /> With this model your tech tree nodes/variables/infrances/what have you are collected like Skill Specialties, somewhat, only when it comes to matters of Inspiration the Genius can apply them to any other fitting Wonder, experiment or some such. </div> </div> </div>That's an interesting idea, actually. I'll toy around with the idea a little and come back to it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What may be best is bridging both systems for use in play. Using Skill + Axiom is the most off the cuff, useful for the innovative Geniuses to create freeform Wonders, etc. Having a grand field of work (like weird biology) could be modeled like the Fellowships. As written they focused more on individual kinds of Wonders but it would be a suitable way to map a field of the Mad Arts &amp; Sciences. I'd wager more Geniuses working on the same stuff might bring the barest trappings of consistency, such as more easily mitigated Faults and Havoc. </div> </div> </div>Alright, so you have the popular Fields that everybody has some access to, but you can go establish or discover your own like Mage Legacies or (again) Werewolf Gifts? That's actually a really interesting idea. Keep off-the-cuff Kitbashed Wonders as just Axiom + Skill for a simple, quick effect, but have complicated and powerful Wonders be constrained to Fields you've explored.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That way several Fields/Fellowships could be written up, an overview of recent Inspired trends with favoritism amongst the Foundations. And you'd still have Skill + Axiom for more radical or alternative applications, and the options for a Genius collaborative to set up their own Field. </div> </div> </div>So, for example, you could have some basic Fields like Metabiology, Fringe Physics and Extrasensory Perception that are just kind of generally-accepted and well-established pseudosciences among the Peerage, but then you might have a Fellowship of Ghostbusters that offer tutelage in the field of Spectral Science, or a society of time travellers that jealously guard the secrets of Paratemporal Physics?<br /> <br /> I like that idea a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T20:24:40-07:00","id":999033,"title":"","content":"Okay, so I've been reading some discussion in other thread, and a lot have been saying that Genius doesn't have a clear identity, and I'm inclined to agree.<br /> <br /> So we need to take a step away from the Axiomata for a second, and think about that before we do anything else.<br /> <br /> So, let's start with the theme.<br /> <br /> In the introduction, the Genius book says the theme is &quot;<b>Transgression</b>&quot;. But there's not actually a lot of transgression happening. In fact, in a lot of ways, players are rewarded for <i>not</i> transgressing. Keeping Obligation high offers nothing but benefits, low Obligation offers nothing but problems, showing the world your creations is doomed to blow up before anything significant can even happen, and the player-aimed faction has a stated goal of &quot;make sure we don't fuck up society.&quot; It feels like Genius is that #edgy kid that tries to say shocking stuff, but never really registers as anything but cute.<br /> <br /> So what can we do to try and make <b>Transgression</b> the center of Genius?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T20:30:46-07:00","id":999036,"title":"","content":"Rewards for going &quot;bad&quot;. Make low Obligation and Unmada attractive. Encourge character flaw driven self sabotage.<br /> <br /> I'm all for Larvae being stronger and more tied to personal sacrifice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T20:46:47-07:00","id":999047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=999033#post999033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what can we do to try and make <b>Transgression</b> the center of Genius?</div> </div> </div> </div>Easiest way would be more horrific the means required to create/maintain/fuel a wonder = the more likely it works when muggles touch and tinker with it rather than it exploding. Though it's rather hamfisted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T21:22:23-07:00","id":999054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=999036#post999036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rewards for going &quot;bad&quot;. Make low Obligation and Unmada attractive. Encourge character flaw driven self sabotage.<br /> <br /> I'm all for Larvae being stronger and more tied to personal sacrifice.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=999047#post999047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Easiest way would be more horrific the means required to create/maintain/fuel a wonder = the more likely it works when muggles touch and tinker with it rather than it exploding. Though it's rather hamfisted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely places to start. But I think we can also look at the world, too. Something that's supposed to be a big part of Genius is how &quot;nobody's in charge,&quot; but what if we make it more explicit?<br /> <br /> What if we cut out the Foundations and Lemuria? Or, at least cut them down to being just big Fellowships? The Peerage are just the blustery remnants of a dying academic hierarchy, Lemuria is a few groups of disgruntled lunatics, and nobody has a handle on anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T21:46:43-07:00","id":999063,"title":"","content":"Or we could retain them as they were in 1E... but historically. In the aftermath of the Invisible Wars, both groups slowly disintegrated. The Lemurians to members questioning why they are still part of a decaying system (especially one filled with contradictory worldviews). The Peerage to members wondering why they should participate in an alliance against a vanquished enemy. Each departing to persue *their own* research and goals without interference. <br /> <br /> There are still remnants that try to pretend the old setup remains, but the truth of it is lonesomes, independent collaboratives, and new organizations are far more numerous. Academies of Inspired learning and fellowship have fewer seats filled each year, and more colleagues drop out of communication. <br /> <br /> All those Genii, operating without check or oversight... No one who knows who goes Illuminated or when...<br /> <br /> No one is in charge. Which is a problem when talking about people who can build death-rays and have decaying senses of what is reasonable or right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 11-06-2016, 01:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T03:07:02-08:00","id":999136,"title":"","content":"*potral opens &amp; sticks head out*<br /> <br /> Hey guys, I think I might have something positive to contribute to this Project. (Unless this has already been brought up already. There are a lot of posts between here and the start.) But first I really think focusing on the whole &quot;No one is in charge&quot; thing is another step backwards. Especially since the way things are now the real theme of Genius actually is: Bitter Dissapointment. But enough of that, I'm here to actually contribute in a positive way.<br /> <br /> Genius sorta has the same problem that Requiem 1st Edition had when it first came out. It has no real mysteries to explore. Requiem 2nd Edition remedied that with both the Strix Chronicle and the magnificent World We Die In section that's just chalked full of unique ideas and setting. I think Genius need something like that, a jumping off point for players and STs to showcase what's possible and what interesting stories can be told. <br /> <br /> For instance, you know all those Splintered Timelines that Mage, Hunter, and Demon introduced? Well, what if we tied those more directly into the Genius gameline as a whole? They already function similarly to Bardos already, why not just use those instead and give them an intimate link to being Inspired. Imagine what the game would be like if when a Genius Catalyses they cognitively perceive and comprehend an infinitude of possible realities. Each one either a divergence from how the world formed (different timelines, life forms, physics) or a possibility of how the world could be (hyper technology, Utopias, Hellscapes.) From that infinitude does the Inspired comprehend physical laws and scientify properties reality has either rejected or isn't ready for, and that is how they build their wonders. But those laws and properties are not of the current reality, so the Genius' inventions are prone to Havok as reality tries to eliminate the anachronism that taints it. But more than that, the Genii are able to comprehend how to make reality like the possible Utopias of the Infinitude. They know how they can make the world better, kinder, safer. But in Infinitude they also see all of realities indifference and mankind's folly, equally able to see how things can go wrong and fall apart. The game then becomes about the Genii gauging how much they're willing to transgress in order to bring about their vision of the future against what costs they're willing to make to get there. I call it: The Hollow Earths Chronicle, using the term Hollow Earths to refer to the Infinitude of Splintered Timelines.<br /> <br /> Aaaaand that's all I've got for now. It's been on my mind for the past couple of days or so, so I hope it helps. <br /> <br /> *pokes head back through portal*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Polish 11-06-2016, 06:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T03:55:21-08:00","id":999147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=999136#post999136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*potral opens &amp; sticks head out*<br /> <br /> Hey guys, I think I might have something positive to contribute to this Project. (Unless this has already been brought up already. There are a lot of posts between here and the start.) But first I really think focusing on the whole &quot;No one is in charge&quot; thing is another step backwards. Especially since the way things are now the real theme of Genius actually is: Bitter Dissapointment. But enough of that, I'm here to actually contribute in a positive way.<br /> <br /> Genius sorta has the same problem that Requiem 1st Edition had when it first came out. It has no real mysteries to explore. Requiem 2nd Edition remedied that with both the Strix Chronicle and the magnificent World We Die In section that's just chalked full of unique ideas and setting. I think Genius need something like that, a jumping off point for players and STs to showcase what's possible and what interesting stories can be told.<br /> <br /> For instance, you know all those Splintered Timelines that Mage, Hunter, and Demon introduced? Well, what if we tied those more directly into the Genius gameline as a whole? They already function similarly to Bardos already, why not just use those instead and give them an intimate link to being Inspired. Imagine what the game would be like if when a Genius Catalyses they cognitively perceive and comprehend an infinitude of possible realities. Each one either a divergence from how the world formed (different timelines, life forms, physics) or a possibility of how the world could be (hyper technology, Utopias, Hellscapes.) From that infinitude does the Inspired comprehend physical laws and scientify properties reality has either rejected or isn't ready for, and that is how they build their wonders. But those laws and properties are not of the current reality, so the Genius' inventions are prone to Havok as reality tries to eliminate the anachronism that taints it. But more than that, the Genii are able to comprehend how to make reality like the possible Utopias of the Infinitude. They know how they can make the world better, kinder, safer. But in Infinitude they also see all of realities indifference and mankind's folly, equally able to see how things can go wrong and fall apart. The game then becomes about the Genii gauging how much they're willing to transgress in order to bring about their vision of the future against what costs they're willing to make to get there. I call it: The Hollow Earths Chronicle, using the term Hollow Earths to refer to the Infinitude of Splintered Timelines.<br /> <br /> Aaaaand that's all I've got for now. It's been on my mind for the past couple of days or so, so I hope it helps.<br /> <br /> *pokes head back through portal*</div> </div> </div> </div>I love your idea. It makes it possible for a genius to change things but it maintains the idea of terrible consquences for such trangression. I would expand and say that part of the journey is learning humility and wisdom, because an excess of trangression can undo all the good your trying to bring to the world, or even make it worse. Finding a careful balance between pragmatism and idealism. Understanding that you cannot force your idea of paradise on people unless they accept it on their own free will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T04:41:24-08:00","id":999160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=999136#post999136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*potral opens &amp; sticks head out*<br /> <br /> Hey guys, I think I might have something positive to contribute to this Project. (Unless this has already been brought up already. There are a lot of posts between here and the start.) But first I really think focusing on the whole &quot;No one is in charge&quot; thing is another step backwards. Especially since the way things are now the real theme of Genius actually is: Bitter Dissapointment. But enough of that, I'm here to actually contribute in a positive way.<br /> <br /> Genius sorta has the same problem that Requiem 1st Edition had when it first came out. It has no real mysteries to explore. Requiem 2nd Edition remedied that with both the Strix Chronicle and the magnificent World We Die In section that's just chalked full of unique ideas and setting. I think Genius need something like that, a jumping off point for players and STs to showcase what's possible and what interesting stories can be told.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that part is still pending, once some of the mechanical details are ironed out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=999136#post999136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>For instance, you know all those Splintered Timelines...</i>&lt;snip&gt;<b>Unknowningly posts Vent0's personal headcannon</b>&lt;/snip&gt; ...are prone to Havok as reality tries to eliminate the anachronism that taints it.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=999136#post999136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But more than that, the Genii are able to comprehend how to make reality like the possible Utopias of the Infinitude. They know how they can make the world better, kinder, safer. But in Infinitude they also see all of realities indifference and mankind's folly, equally able to see how things can go wrong and fall apart. The game then becomes about the Genii gauging how much they're willing to transgress in order to bring about their vision of the future against what costs they're willing to make to get there. I call it: The Hollow Earths Chronicle, using the term Hollow Earths to refer to the Infinitude of Splintered Timelines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they technically already need to decide how much they want to Transgress to achieve their vision. That <i>could</i> be better clarified, though.<br /> <br /> I think (unless this changed when I wasn't looking) that the planned &quot;Chronicle&quot; idea was The Illuminated Chronicles, highlighting just what can happen when a Genius lets themselves go.<br /> <br /> As for &quot;No one is in charge&quot; not lending itself to stories on its own, I'd disagree. In fact, what with Bardos and Timetravellers (potential future, or splintered past), you could even highlight that now without any unified group &quot;in charge&quot; of maintaining interactions with these, they are now becoming a more immediate problem. With the Peerage still in power, the Martian Invasion was repelled. Now that the Peerage is crumbling, who will stop any other invasions? Will that be you? How might your own grasp at power and authority go, and what could possibly go wrong?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T06:17:11-08:00","id":999184,"title":"","content":"If we're gonna remove the Foundations and Baramins to emphasize &quot;No One Is In Charge&quot;, what will the new Y splats be? Perhaps a philosophical &quot;Approach To Magnum Opus&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T06:26:30-08:00","id":999187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=999160#post999160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for &quot;No one is in charge&quot; not lending itself to stories on its own, I'd disagree. In fact, what with Bardos and Timetravellers (potential future, or splintered past), you could even highlight that now without any unified group &quot;in charge&quot; of maintaining interactions with these, they are now becoming a more immediate problem. With the Peerage still in power, the Martian Invasion was repelled. Now that the Peerage is crumbling, who will stop any other invasions? Will that be you? How might your own grasp at power and authority go, and what could possibly go wrong?</div> </div> </div> </div>That was the idea.<br /> <br /> Increasing the importance of Bardos and Time Fractures is definitely something I want to do, as well as changing how time travel works.<ul><li>For starters, the Guardians of Forever as they exist in 1E can burn in Hell.</li> <li>Screwing with time will be easier. No need to spend Mania, you can just do it.</li> <li>Timeline changes are unpredictable. You might change the &quot;real&quot; timeline, you might get dumped in a Time Splinter, you might <i>create</i> a Time Splinter, or something crazy.</li> </ul><br /> But Genii definitely do need more mysteries and a few clear adversaries. We do have the Illuminated, who are neat because they are totally amoral, but can blend in with more scrupulous Genii. On top of that, there are plenty of Bardos that might have an interest in forcing themselves to be real or straight-up invading reality (and a few Inspired might think that's a <i>good</i> thing). I think we also should make Inspiration a more active force in the universe as well. Inspiration is supposed to be a force of creation, chaos and, well, <i>inspiration</i>, but except for the Genii and Mania storms, we don't see a lot of Inspiration directly acting upon people.<br /> <br /> What if places of creativity and innovation acted like natural Mania generators? And what if you could occasionally find a &quot;naturally-occuring&quot; Wonder, like how Mummies can sometimes find unintentionally created Relics? Maybe even a Wonder that has rare or valuable capabilities that other Genii may want to study and adapt for themselves? Making Inspiration part of the world, and worth studying directly, would help give Genii things to do, and help make the Genii themselves look less like the enlightened holders of divine inspiration, and more like people who were lucky enough to figure out more than the rest of the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T07:31:07-08:00","id":999205,"title":"","content":"Genius already <i>has</i> an old order that disintegrated and now we're dealing with the results. Two, if you count what happened to time travel.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=999187#post999187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Increasing the importance of Bardos and Time Fractures is definitely something I want to do, as well as changing how time travel works.<ul><li>For starters, the Guardians of Forever as they exist in 1E can burn in Hell.</li> <li>Screwing with time will be easier. No need to spend Mania, you can just do it.</li> <li>Timeline changes are unpredictable. You might change the &quot;real&quot; timeline, you might get dumped in a Time Splinter, you might <i>create</i> a Time Splinter, or something crazy.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>The time travel system from 1e needs fixing, yeah.<br /> <br /> I wrote a system once that might work here, actually. I'll have to go find it, but it worked basically like this:<ul><li>The future is constantly changing, to the point different jumps almost never encounter the same one.</li> <li>How far you go determines the rough &quot;genre&quot; of futures you encounter. Travel a week into the future, you see all sorts of disasters that are constantly being averted by time travellers. Travel a billion years, you see some other lifeform has arisen to replace humans.</li> <li>The past is <i>not</i> constantly changing.</li> <li>If you <i>do </i>change the past, when you try to travel forward, it acts as if you travelled from the present - i.e. if you travel back a billion years and mess with stuff, you'll find humanity has been replaced by some other lifeform when you come back. The only way to return to your present is to fix what you altered.</li> <li>Whether these alternate presents are actually overwriting reality or they're just alternate universes is left ambiguous.</li> </ul><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=999187#post999187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Genii definitely do need more mysteries and a few clear adversaries. We do have the Illuminated, who are neat because they are totally amoral, but can blend in with more scrupulous Genii. On top of that, there are plenty of Bardos that might have an interest in forcing themselves to be real or straight-up invading reality (and a few Inspired might think that's a <i>good</i> thing). I think we also should make Inspiration a more active force in the universe as well. Inspiration is supposed to be a force of creation, chaos and, well, <i>inspiration</i>, but except for the Genii and Mania storms, we don't see a lot of Inspiration directly acting upon people.<br /> <br /> What if places of creativity and innovation acted like natural Mania generators? And what if you could occasionally find a &quot;naturally-occuring&quot; Wonder, like how Mummies can sometimes find unintentionally created Relics? Maybe even a Wonder that has rare or valuable capabilities that other Genii may want to study and adapt for themselves? Making Inspiration part of the world, and worth studying directly, would help give Genii things to do, and help make the Genii themselves look less like the enlightened holders of divine inspiration, and more like people who were lucky enough to figure out more than the rest of the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>There were elements of this in previous editions - large numbers of normal people being inspired naturally generated Mania. The whole &quot;calculus vampire&quot; thing is a remnant of that IIRC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":877,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","user":"MugaSofer","date":". 11-06-2016, 10:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T08:10:38-08:00","id":999220,"title":"","content":"Wow, busy night that I missed.<br /> <br /> In regards to the Peerage and Lemuria, we don't have to do away with their Foundations and Baramins, just downplay the results of the Invisible war and who 'controls' the world. The trend in 2E is having less overall backstory to allow Storytellers and players to craft their own histories. When it comes to what each splat defines a Genius have as the Y-splat options they are still useful. Each Foundation offers a <b>How</b> for the Genius with its grants and outlook, as approaches towards the Mad Arts &amp; Sciences exist within them. The Catalyst determines the <b>Who</b> as common foibles, quirks, and personality types for the Genius. As for Fellowship/Field expansion that is the <b>What</b> of what branch the Genius is more actively engaged in.<br /> <br /> ------------------<br /> <br /> When it comes to themes for Genius I've felt there should be a shift towards <b>Untruth</b> and <b>Uncertainty</b>. An attempt to embrace past criticisms of 'amounts to nothing' and 'bitter disappointment' and 'no one is in charge.' Mage has it easy for a game where their Truth is the existence of Supernal magic. And compared to other game lines one with no straight answers up front is refreshing in my eyes.<br /> <br /> Do we actually know what the next scientific breakthrough or the next big invention is going to be? Sure you can following current trends, development blogs and cutting edge science but even within the last few decades there were plenty of surprises. Who would have predicted the iPod, Youtube, Pokemon Go and a variety of other platforms? Further back in history, when the proponents to Alternating and Direct current were duking it out who knew, at the time, what the future harnessing of electricity would look like?<br /> <br /> For a Genius, the are posed between the world as it is and the world that isn't. Untruths, false realities, splintered timelines and stranger dimensions all vying for existence. Why should reality have all the fun? Why should what is currently known of science be absolutely true? After all Science is a process, a methodology of learning about the world that has shifted radically as understanding has increased. But still, you have the disproven theories, the technology far ahead of its time, and the countless alternatives to 'Truth' vying for attention. Inspiration and Mania is less about guiding humanity towards greater eras of enlightenment and more the chaotic stream of all ideas, good and bad and weird and ludicrous and failed ideas, all pushing for existence. In the mind of a Genius, with the inspired as their conduit.<br /> <br /> Uncertainty comes from the questions the Genius has when they have a chance to stop and think. Sure, your advancements in Metaphysics may have earned you a flying telepathically controlled entropy flipping car, but unforeseen Faults can creep in without your awareness. The next stroke of Havoc could destroy it completely, or the next Umada Field or Bardo goes against it enough to destroy it. If your Fellowship has gathered much consistency, why are their still holes in your theory that can rip it apart? What if you pegged your opponent herbologist as to how her Wonders work, yet her paradigm comes blindside?<br /> <br /> Isn't it a common roleplaying experience where you're put on the spot with an unfinished plan, unexpected arrivals, and underfunded equipment? The Peerage warns that for all the parts where Mania starts making sense, it doesn't, to remind Genii that they may not be able to plan for everything. This encourages lateral thinking, something that Genii are masters of (for how crazy their logic sounds on the outside). Lemuria and similar Inspired antagonists have rejected the warning of there being no hard answers, taking to their theory of everything at the cost of being unable to divert from it strongly, of preventing variety amongst their Wonders.<br /> <br /> The question from an Uncertain future isn't what is right or wrong, the question is who will act.<br /> <br /> ------------------<br /> <br /> Building from the Untruths idea, since Bardos do require Mania to survive you can draft up as many antagonistic invaders as you do more neutral Bardos.<br /> <br /> The other set of adversies are the Clockstoppers, or Hollow Men. The people who can cause works of Mania to not exist, predisposed towards Geniuses but if left unchecked can undo technological advancement as we know it. This is only my taste but their name never impressed me, and their span of Voids seemed arbitrary. But it is useful to have adversaries that are as anti-Genius as the Fetch's abilities are anti-Changeling. Definitely could use some expansion and more prominence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T08:20:44-08:00","id":999224,"title":"","content":"Also, props to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/997612-a-critical-look-at-genius-the-transgression?p=999168#post999168\">Vent0</a> for the reply on the critical discussion thread. I really dig the notion that failure is not guaranteed from the outset of everything a Genius does. An individual can succeed or fail at so much. Lasting, consistent and broad scope successes come from being able to get more Geniuses focused on the same topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T10:17:16-08:00","id":999288,"title":"","content":"Not so much ignorance as <i>rationalization</i>, I think.<br /> <br /> Just as brilliant people can end up constructing brilliant reasons why their biases and prejudices are right, a Genius' superhuman pattern-matching ability can turn inward on itself and create spurious reasons why X is true just as easily as ways to make rocket boots.<br /> <br /> That instinct to justify ourselves ... who hasn't seen some news story or argument and <i>wanted</i> it to be true, even if we suspected it was false, because it would make us look better? One of those jerks did something that perfectly conforms to our idea of them; someone tried out our pet Thing and it worked brilliantly; there's some brilliant argument why an idea we hate is self-contradictory/illegal/ruining everything.<br /> <br /> And then it turns out to be wrong.<br /> <br /> It's where urban legends come from. Who really <i>wants </i>to check if Winston Churchill said &quot;the fascists of the future will be called anti-fascists&quot;, or a Societ nail factory once filled a quota for &quot;12 tonnes of nails&quot; by making a single 12-tonne nail, or Christians are up in arms over Starbucks' red coffee cup? Wow, 8 spiders a year? Really? That'll really gross out my friends ...<br /> <br /> Skepticism can turn inwards too. Conspiracy theorists have <i>piles</i> of evidence, detailed debunkings of the truth, all of it subtly wrong. <a href=\"http://slatestarcodex.com/2014/04/15/the-cowpox-of-doubt/\" target=\"_blank\">Homeopaths have peer-reviewed studies &quot;proving&quot; homeopathy works</a>. <a href=\"https://www.insidehighered.com/news/2014/08/06/how-rumors-spread-sloppy-citation-practices\" target=\"_blank\">Academics cite papers that they haven't read</a> that supposedly debunk myths.<br /> <br /> It's that impulse to be &quot;right&quot; even when you aren't right that creates cranks, and that's what Geniuses are - weaponized cranks, ones whose Time Cube-esque delusions produce useful results.<br /> <br /> That's what Unmada represent, I think. That temptation to <i>rationalize</i>.<br /> <br /> Or at least that's what I think they <i>should </i>represent. Right now they're more generalized mental-illness-derived delusions, since they're basically just the Mad nicked from Awakening.<br /> <br /> Not &quot;we don't know what's going on, we need to figure it out&quot; - &quot;you don't know what's going on, you need to stop pretending you do&quot;. But at the same time, you <i>can't </i>abandon everything you believe; that way lies solipsism and madness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":877,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","user":"MugaSofer","date":". 11-06-2016, 01:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T10:24:13-08:00","id":999295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=999220#post999220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, busy night that I missed.<br /> <br /> In regards to the Peerage and Lemuria, we don't have to do away with their Foundations and Baramins, just downplay the results of the Invisible war and who 'controls' the world. The trend in 2E is having less overall backstory to allow Storytellers and players to craft their own histories. When it comes to what each splat defines a Genius have as the Y-splat options they are still useful. Each Foundation offers a <b>How</b> for the Genius with its grants and outlook, as approaches towards the Mad Arts &amp; Sciences exist within them. The Catalyst determines the <b>Who</b> as common foibles, quirks, and personality types for the Genius. As for Fellowship/Field expansion that is the <b>What</b> of what branch the Genius is more actively engaged in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, that makes some sense to me. I've been thinking that Inspired society isn't as open to non-scientists as I think it could be. Perhaps we could expand what the Foundations' members <i>do</i>?<ul><li><b>Artificers:</b> Instead of being Mad Engineers, they're makers and crafters of all stripes, who believe their Magnum Opus is best served by making concrete physical things. They're Engineers, Artisans, and Industrialists.</li> <li><b>Directors:</b> Instead of Mad Psychologists, the Directors are the Genii that believe that in order to effect their dreams, they need to control the underlying systems of society. They're the Sociologists, Economists and Politicians.</li> <li><b>Navigators:</b> Instead of Mad Physicists, the Navigators are people of action, who follow the old adage of &quot;Want a job done right, do it yourself.&quot; They're the Explorers, Experimentalists and Warriors. Tony Stark (Marvel Comics) and the Joker fit in here.</li> <li><b>Progenitors:</b> Instead of Mad Biologists, Progenitors are Genii who want to change the world by changing the <i>people</i>. They are the Doctors, Educators and Transhumanists.</li> <li><b>Scholastics:</b> Instead of being Mad Philosophers, they're the ones who believe that they can achieve their vision by perfecting an idea. They're the Philosophers, Poets, and Occultists.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When it comes to themes for Genius I've felt there should be a shift towards <b>Untruth</b> and <b>Uncertainty</b>. An attempt to embrace past criticisms of 'amounts to nothing' and 'bitter disappointment' and 'no one is in charge.' Mage has it easy for a game where their Truth is the existence of Supernal magic. And compared to other game lines one with no straight answers up front is refreshing in my eyes.<br /> <br /> Do we actually know what the next scientific breakthrough or the next big invention is going to be? Sure you can following current trends, development blogs and cutting edge science but even within the last few decades there were plenty of surprises. Who would have predicted the iPod, Youtube, Pokemon Go and a variety of other platforms? Further back in history, when the proponents to Alternating and Direct current were duking it out who knew, at the time, what the future harnessing of electricity would look like? </div> </div> </div>That does feel pretty in-theme for Transgressive Visionaries. Plus, Thomas Edison publicly electrocuting an elephant to death with his opponent's technology does sound like something a particularly petty and cruel Genius would do to try and discredit another.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For a Genius, the are posed between the world as it is and the world that isn't. Untruths, false realities, splintered timelines and stranger dimensions all vying for existence. Why should reality have all the fun? Why should what is currently known of science be absolutely true? After all Science is a process, a methodology of learning about the world that has shifted radically as understanding has increased. But still, you have the disproven theories, the technology far ahead of its time, and the countless alternatives to 'Truth' vying for attention. Inspiration and Mania is less about guiding humanity towards greater eras of enlightenment and more the chaotic stream of all ideas, good and bad and weird and ludicrous and failed ideas, all pushing for existence. In the mind of a Genius, with the inspired as their conduit. </div> </div> </div>So the Genii are fighting for their own visions of the future, some of which are mutually exclusive. That does seem like a good source of conflict, and the idea of all these differing beliefs in constant collision does also help drive the &quot;nobody's in charge&quot; theme. Even within your own Foundation or Fellowship, you might find people who hate what you believe and want nothing more than to watch your plans fall to ashes.<br /> <br /> To use an example from fiction, there's Marvel Comics' Civil War event. Iron Man wants to make a safer world by controlling superhumans and arguably destroying some of their freedoms, and Captain America wants to preserve liberty at the possible risk of further superhero-related disasters. Tony and Steve are not only colleagues, but close friends, but they still got torn apart by this one difference in ideals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Uncertainty comes from the questions the Genius has when they have a chance to stop and think. Sure, your advancements in Metaphysics may have earned you a flying telepathically controlled entropy flipping car, but unforeseen Faults can creep in without your awareness. The next stroke of Havoc could destroy it completely, or the next Umada Field or Bardo goes against it enough to destroy it. If your Fellowship has gathered much consistency, why are their still holes in your theory that can rip it apart? What if you pegged your opponent herbologist as to how her Wonders work, yet her paradigm comes blindside?<br /> <br /> Isn't it a common roleplaying experience where you're put on the spot with an unfinished plan, unexpected arrivals, and underfunded equipment? The Peerage warns that for all the parts where Mania starts making sense, it doesn't, to remind Genii that they may not be able to plan for everything. This encourages lateral thinking, something that Genii are masters of (for how crazy their logic sounds on the outside). Lemuria and similar Inspired antagonists have rejected the warning of there being no hard answers, taking to their theory of everything at the cost of being unable to divert from it strongly, of preventing variety amongst their Wonders.<br /> <br /> The question from an Uncertain future isn't what is right or wrong, the question is who will act. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, these are definitely questions that should confront players.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Building from the Untruths idea, since Bardos do require Mania to survive you can draft up as many antagonistic invaders as you do more neutral Bardos.<br /> <br /> The other set of adversies are the Clockstoppers, or Hollow Men. The people who can cause works of Mania to not exist, predisposed towards Geniuses but if left unchecked can undo technological advancement as we know it. This is only my taste but their name never impressed me, and their span of Voids seemed arbitrary. But it is useful to have adversaries that are as anti-Genius as the Fetch's abilities are anti-Changeling. Definitely could use some expansion and more prominence. </div> </div> </div>With Clockstoppers, I think they fall kind of flat because all they are is a literally empty-headed luddite. To me, I think it'd be more interesting if they had something like Inspiration, but instead of wanting to make a future, they want to bring back a lost past. If the Genii are futurists and innnovators, then the Clockstoppers are Romantics and nostalgic. They may not even be malicious to Genii by default, but they want a time that's been lost and may never have really existed, and the constant march of change and progress scares them and pushes them to fight back.<br /> <br /> For example, you may have a man who wants society to go back to the &quot;white picket fence&quot; ideal 50's he remembers, where everything was simpler, family mattered, and people still worked for a living, ignorant of how terrible that time was for many groups of people. He's normally a sweet old grandpa, but when he sees society move away from the values he remembers, he starts to get spiteful, without being able to control or really notice it. He starts posting hateful memes on Facebook, and then he starts berating and yelling at young people for not living how he lived, and as time goes on, that anger at the world changing around him twists in on itself until he snaps and &quot;un-Catalyzes&quot; into a Clockstopper. He's not empty, he's <i>scared and angry</i> and lashing out at what he thinks needs to be destroyed. He just wants to make America great again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T11:04:36-08:00","id":999323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=999187#post999187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if places of creativity and innovation acted like natural Mania generators? And what if you could occasionally find a &quot;naturally-occuring&quot; Wonder, like how Mummies can sometimes find unintentionally created Relics? Maybe even a Wonder that has rare or valuable capabilities that other Genii may want to study and adapt for themselves? Making Inspiration part of the world, and worth studying directly, would help give Genii things to do, and help make the Genii themselves look less like the enlightened holders of divine inspiration, and more like people who were lucky enough to figure out more than the rest of the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>All of these are kind of done already with Bardos.<br /> <br /> Lots of people change their minds, it causes a Mania Storm (why?), and a bunch of naturally-occurring Wonders and Manes show up and start spilling all over the place.<br /> <br /> Bardos are awkward because they exist in tension with the idea that Wonders are <i>real</i>, not just magical reality warping. They're just kind of ... there, living examples of false beliefs, only they run on Mania. So I'm reluctant to risk pressing such a fragile piece of worldbuilding too hard.<br /> <br /> But if you want to tie Inspiration into the world more clearly, I suspect you'd want to tie in or rework Bardos.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=999295#post999295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been thinking that Inspired society isn't as open to non-scientists as I think it could be. Perhaps we could expand what the Foundations' members <i>do</i>?<ul><li><b>Artificers:</b> Instead of being Mad Engineers, they're makers and crafters of all stripes, who believe their Magnum Opus is best served by making concrete physical things. They're Engineers, Artisans, and Industrialists.</li> <li><b>Directors:</b> Instead of Mad Psychologists, the Directors are the Genii that believe that in order to effect their dreams, they need to control the underlying systems of society. They're the Sociologists, Economists and Politicians.</li> <li><b>Navigators:</b> Instead of Mad Physicists, the Navigators are people of action, who follow the old adage of &quot;Want a job done right, do it yourself.&quot; They're the Explorers, Experimentalists and Warriors. Tony Stark (Marvel Comics) and the Joker fit in here.</li> <li><b>Progenitors:</b> Instead of Mad Biologists, Progenitors are Genii who want to change the world by changing the <i>people</i>. They are the Doctors, Educators and Transhumanists.</li> <li><b>Scholastics:</b> Instead of being Mad Philosophers, they're the ones who believe that they can achieve their vision by perfecting an idea. They're the Philosophers, Poets, and Occultists.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>I like this. Diversity should definitely be emphasized.<br /> <br /> The change to Progenitors is interesting. If Internalized Wonders are changed to emphasize Inspired <i>ideas</i> more clearly, not just surgical implants, it's a natural fit for them to be Educators with their Grant.<br /> <br /> \u200bAlthough I do worry it brings them a little close to the Directors' conceptual space.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=999295#post999295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With Clockstoppers, I think they fall kind of flat because all they are is a literally empty-headed luddite. To me, I think it'd be more interesting if they had something like Inspiration, but instead of wanting to make a future, they want to bring back a lost past. If the Genii are futurists and innnovators, then the Clockstoppers are Romantics and nostalgic. They may not even be malicious to Genii by default, but they want a time that's been lost and may never have really existed, and the constant march of change and progress scares them and pushes them to fight back.<br /> <br /> For example, you may have a man who wants society to go back to the &quot;white picket fence&quot; ideal 50's he remembers, where everything was simpler, family mattered, and people still worked for a living, ignorant of how terrible that time was for many groups of people. He's normally a sweet old grandpa, but when he sees society move away from the values he remembers, he starts to get spiteful, without being able to control or really notice it. He starts posting hateful memes on Facebook, and then he starts berating and yelling at young people for not living how he lived, and as time goes on, that anger at the world changing around him twists in on itself until he snaps and &quot;un-Catalyzes&quot; into a Clockstopper. He's not empty, he's <i>scared and angry</i> and lashing out at what he thinks needs to be destroyed. He just wants to make America great again.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've said this before, but Clockstoppers have always worked for me because &quot;luddite&quot; is such a classic type of <i>protagonist</i>. And really, can you blame them? Technology <i>is</i> scary, Inspired technology doubly so. If progress went awry, <i>has</i> gone awry, how do we stop it? Are we even capable of stopping it?<br /> <br /> It's not about being politically conservative. It's about a very specific <i>fear </i>that mad scientists represent, of a person who manages to impose some flawed idea on the world and <i>break</i> <i>the world</i>.<br /> <br /> The demagog whose ideas overrun the globe in a 1984-esque nightmare. The weapon of mass destruction that kills billions. The faceless new technology that lets the rich lay off workers ... hell, R.U.R was about vat-grown slaves becoming an oppressed underclass.<br /> <br /> But also stuff like Jurassic Park, Terminator, Alien. The scientist may be well-meaning, but the <i>hero </i>knows deep down it'll go awry and kill everyone. And so it does. So it <i>always </i>does. <span style=\"font-size:9px\">(Because science is evil.)</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":877,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","user":"MugaSofer","date":". 11-06-2016, 02:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T11:48:33-08:00","id":999355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=999323#post999323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All of these are kind of done already with Bardos.<br /> <br /> Lots of people change their minds, it causes a Mania Storm (why?), and a bunch of naturally-occurring Wonders and Manes show up and start spilling all over the place.<br /> <br /> Bardos are awkward because they exist in tension with the idea that Wonders are <i>real</i>, not just magical reality warping. They're just kind of ... there, living examples of false beliefs, only they run on Mania. So I'm reluctant to risk pressing such a fragile piece of worldbuilding too hard.<br /> <br /> But if you want to tie Inspiration into the world more clearly, I suspect you'd want to tie in or rework Bardos.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Bardos may need a rework as far as how they work cosmologically, but we'll figure that out later on down.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I've said this before, but Clockstoppers have always worked for me because &quot;luddite&quot; is such a classic type of <i>protagonist</i>. And really, can you blame them? Technology <i>is</i> scary, Inspired technology doubly so. If progress went awry, <i>has</i> gone awry, how do we stop it? Are we even capable of stopping it?<br /> <br /> It's not about being politically conservative. It's about a very specific <i>fear </i>that mad scientists represent, of a person who manages to impose some flawed idea on the world and <i>break</i> <i>the world</i>.<br /> <br /> The demagog whose ideas overrun the globe in a 1984-esque nightmare. The weapon of mass destruction that kills billions. The faceless new technology that lets the rich lay off workers ... hell, R.U.R was about vat-grown slaves becoming an oppressed underclass.<br /> <br /> But also stuff like Jurassic Park, Terminator, Alien. The scientist may be well-meaning, but the <i>hero </i>knows deep down it'll go awry and kill everyone. And so it does. So it <i>always </i>does. <span style=\"font-size:9px\">(Because science is evil.)</span> </div> </div> </div>That's a fair point. I guess my deal is more that Clockstoppers feel really flat to me because the book presents them as <i>only</i> luddites (unless I'm misreading). It literally calls them empty voids that lack any spark of Inspiration, and suck up creativity without giving <i>anything</i> back. Clockstoppers seem to be presented less like Ian Malcolm, and more like <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/EvilLuddite\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;Evil Luddites&quot;</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T15:37:19-08:00","id":999465,"title":"","content":"I was wondering if we could come up with a quick list of what we think are the game's flaws, and which solutions have been proposed so far.<br /> <br /> From what I've gathered, the flaws are:<br /> <br /> 1) The structure of the Axioms<br /> 2) The mechanic of Binding Mania<br /> 3) Not enough incentive to lose Obligation/Transgress<br /> 4) Not enough diversity in the professions that Geniuses have<br /> 5) Bad rules for time travel<br /> 6) Insufficient representation of Inspiration as a force of change<br /> 7) Failure and Bitter Disappointment receive too much focus as themes<br /> 8) No One Is In Charge isn't really what's going on<br /> 9) No aura mechanic for Geniuses<br /> 10) Few reasons to play as a Beholden<br /> 11) Jabir is too minor of a problem<br /> 12) No distinctive mysteries to explore<br /> <br /> The proposed solutions are:<br /> <br /> 1) Postulates/Inferences<br /> 2) Freebie Wonders, Wondrous Experiences, Hibernation Mode for unused Wonders<br /> 3) More uses for and neccessity of Larvae, more benefits for low Obligation and going Unmada<br /> 4) Broadening the scope of the Foundations<br /> 5) Make it more free form and easy<br /> 6) Magnum Opus and Foundations as sources of visions for the World Of Tomorrow<br /> 7) Shift the emphasis onto smaller victories and teamwork<br /> 8) Make both Foundations and Baramins less centralized and more about loose alliances<br /> 9) ???<br /> 10) Make the Beholden into a Condition, and come up with a proper lesser template<br /> 11) Turn Jabir into a Death Rage style mechanic, with triggers connected to your level of Obligation<br /> 12) Redefine the nature of Inspiration, Bardos and other Wondrous phenomena<br /> <br /> Did I miss anything?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T17:46:32-08:00","id":999503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=999465#post999465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">9) No aura mechanic for Geniuses</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm really not sure this is actually a flaw. Not every splat really needs an &quot;aura&quot;. I suppose if we <i>must</i> have one, it's probably be a low-level Mania field that gets magnified during Obligation Breaks, at Low Obligation, or when Unmada and applies a Tilt based on Paradigm, but I really don't see why Genii would have an aura.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T20:09:12-08:00","id":999545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=999355#post999355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a fair point. I guess my deal is more that Clockstoppers feel really flat to me because the book presents them as <i>only</i> luddites (unless I'm misreading). It literally calls them empty voids that lack any spark of Inspiration, and suck up creativity without giving <i>anything</i> back. Clockstoppers seem to be presented less like Ian Malcolm, and more like <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/EvilLuddite\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;Evil Luddites&quot;</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I think your idea of making them not so much Luddites so much as anti-Geniuses doesn't actually negate the Luddism angle at all while making them more complex. As mentioned, your idea about them is that they look to the past as they imagine it, and that invariably involves reversing social and/or technical progress of some kind. Rather than making them universal tech haters, it makes them <i>specific </i>tech haters. An environmentalist Clockstopper may want to undo industrial farming and factories but leave the internet and ecologic engineering intact and possibly even more advanced. A neoreactionary (modern-day monarchist) is no fan of democracy, but capitalism and civil rights are a-ok (although she actually voicing that maybe black people are as smart as whites isn't going to make any friends on the alt-right; perhaps her frustration with her peers over their refusal to acknowledge that seeing people as easily classified dots on a poll sheet is exactly what the problem with democracy is what provoked the counter-Catalyst).<br /> <br /> In other words, they become more varied while not losing the torches and pitchforks. And it opens the possibility they may even work with a Genius whose Wonders they tolerate...<br /> <br /> If we're still terming this the Illuminated Chronicles, that also ties in with the fact that Illumination is still the outside-context problem. Clockstoppers are something the Inspired actually understand, and understand <i>well</i>. Every Genius has felt the frustration of the Magnum Opus being delayed or made difficult. To them, a Clockstopper is someone who has a Magnum Opus that never has the possibility of ever <i>lasting. </i>Time waits for no one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T04:01:37-08:00","id":999657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=999187#post999187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That was the idea.<br /> <br /> Increasing the importance of Bardos and Time Fractures is definitely something I want to do, as well as changing how time travel works.<ul><li>For starters, the Guardians of Forever as they exist in 1E can burn in Hell.</li> <li>Screwing with time will be easier. No need to spend Mania, you can just do it.</li> <li>Timeline changes are unpredictable. You might change the &quot;real&quot; timeline, you might get dumped in a Time Splinter, you might <i>create</i> a Time Splinter, or something crazy.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I think the Guardians could still exist. Sometimes, as the ST needs. With their existence varying even inside the same game. Time Travel being funny like that. Need Time Police? They exist! Need there to not be Time Police? They never existed (yes, even when they did before)!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=999187#post999187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Genii definitely do need more mysteries and a few clear adversaries. We do have the Illuminated, who are neat because they are totally amoral, but can blend in with more scrupulous Genii. On top of that, there are plenty of Bardos that might have an interest in forcing themselves to be real or straight-up invading reality (and a few Inspired might think that's a <i>good</i> thing). I think we also should make Inspiration a more active force in the universe as well. Inspiration is supposed to be a force of creation, chaos and, well, <i>inspiration</i>, but except for the Genii and Mania storms, we don't see a lot of Inspiration directly acting upon people.<br /> <br /> What if places of creativity and innovation acted like natural Mania generators? And what if you could occasionally find a &quot;naturally-occuring&quot; Wonder, like how Mummies can sometimes find unintentionally created Relics? Maybe even a Wonder that has rare or valuable capabilities that other Genii may want to study and adapt for themselves? Making Inspiration part of the world, and worth studying directly, would help give Genii things to do, and help make the Genii themselves look less like the enlightened holders of divine inspiration, and more like people who were lucky enough to figure out more than the rest of the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, places where the fast flow of thoughts and possible ideas generate Mania? Or moments in time and space that empower an individual into a temporary Genius (able to build one Wonder and then Inspiration fades)? Or a Wonder than <i>wants to be</i> - anyone working on it gains the ability to do so, losing Inspired abilities once they are no longer focused (obsessed) with that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T04:04:06-08:00","id":999659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=999545#post999545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, I think your idea of making them not so much Luddites so much as anti-Geniuses doesn't actually negate the Luddism angle at all while making them more complex. As mentioned, your idea about them is that they look to the past as they imagine it, and that invariably involves reversing social and/or technical progress of some kind. Rather than making them universal tech haters, it makes them <i>specific </i>tech haters. An environmentalist Clockstopper may want to undo industrial farming and factories but leave the internet and ecologic engineering intact and possibly even more advanced. A neoreactionary (modern-day monarchist) is no fan of democracy, but capitalism and civil rights are a-ok (although she actually voicing that maybe black people are as smart as whites isn't going to make any friends on the alt-right; perhaps her frustration with her peers over their refusal to acknowledge that seeing people as easily classified dots on a poll sheet is exactly what the problem with democracy is what provoked the counter-Catalyst).<br /> <br /> In other words, they become more varied while not losing the torches and pitchforks. And it opens the possibility they may even work with a Genius whose Wonders they tolerate...<br /> <br /> If we're still terming this the Illuminated Chronicles, that also ties in with the fact that Illumination is still the outside-context problem. Clockstoppers are something the Inspired actually understand, and understand <i>well</i>. Every Genius has felt the frustration of the Magnum Opus being delayed or made difficult. To them, a Clockstopper is someone who has a Magnum Opus that never has the possibility of ever <i>lasting. </i>Time waits for no one.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't know... This makes them sound more like Lemurians. Actually, what separates them, other than mechanics at this point?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T04:12:32-08:00","id":999660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=999659#post999659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I don't know... This makes them sound more like Lemurians. Actually, what separates them, other than mechanics at this point?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's kind of the empathy basis. They're similar to Lemurians, with the rather critical exception that they're working towards something that is invariably the destruction of something they despise about modernity, while Lemurians want to build something that doesn't acknowledge modern science; truth is, Lemurians are less bitter. They're angry and frustrated, sure, but they're still working towards progress (even if their idea of progress is circa 1884).<br /> <br /> Yes, Clockstoppers generally are more bitter than <i>Lemurians. </i>This is one of the reasons why they aren't generally playable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T06:20:40-08:00","id":999701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=999657#post999657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I think the Guardians could still exist. Sometimes, as the ST needs. With their existence varying even inside the same game. Time Travel being funny like that. Need Time Police? They exist! Need there to not be Time Police? They never existed (yes, even when they did before)!</div> </div> </div> </div>In 1st ed they were around, but the loss of their masters left them scattered and stretched thin.<br /> <br /> That seems like the best approach to me - they can exist in the background, ready to show up if the plot demands it but not appearing every time someone tries to time-travel. Maybe we should emphasize just how broken they are even more heavily, so it feels less like a restriction and more like a plot hook. More thematic.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=999545#post999545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I think your idea of making them not so much Luddites so much as anti-Geniuses doesn't actually negate the Luddism angle at all while making them more complex. As mentioned, your idea about them is that they look to the past as they imagine it, and that invariably involves reversing social and/or technical progress of some kind. Rather than making them universal tech haters, it makes them <i>specific </i>tech haters. An environmentalist Clockstopper may want to undo industrial farming and factories but leave the internet and ecologic engineering intact and possibly even more advanced. A neoreactionary (modern-day monarchist) is no fan of democracy, but capitalism and civil rights are a-ok (although she actually voicing that maybe black people are as smart as whites isn't going to make any friends on the alt-right; perhaps her frustration with her peers over their refusal to acknowledge that seeing people as easily classified dots on a poll sheet is exactly what the problem with democracy is what provoked the counter-Catalyst).<br /> <br /> [...]<br /> <br /> Clockstoppers are something the Inspired actually understand, and understand <i>well</i>. Every Genius has felt the frustration of the Magnum Opus being delayed or made difficult. To them, a Clockstopper is someone who has a Magnum Opus that never has the possibility of ever <i>lasting. </i>Time waits for no one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I worry that this makes them <i>too much</i> like Geniuses.<br /> <br /> Those are valid Catalysts for a Genius. If a Clockstopper is just a Genius who gets eeevil powers instead of Inspiration ... they're just Banishers.<br /> <br /> I could see them more as anti-<i>Beholden</i>. They both have a kind of &quot;empty inside&quot; vibe, after all. Another reason to be cautious about showing people Wonders - rather than weakening their sense of morality, people might recoil from the Transgression so hard they permanently hate progress (and try to kill you, of course.)<br /> <br /> This would tie in nicely to the idea of Inspiration as a force in the world - Clockstoppers can form when normal change and progress gets too intense too.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, that reminds me - I think we should play up the idea of Inspiration as <i>natural</i>. There's an idea in 1st ed that Wonders really do run on natural laws, and you can get genuine insights from studying them, but they're too fragile and complex for mortal eyes to grasp. Ancient Wonders resemble modern technology; future technology resembles modern Wonders, only mundane. Inspiration creates mundane insight, and mundane insight creates Inspiration; they're two sides of the same coin.<br /> <br /> This stuff has limited mechanical representation in 1st ed, but I really like the idea of &quot;genius&quot; as ambiguously supernatural, a kind of God-Machine maybe-magic-maybe-mundane vibe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":877,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","user":"MugaSofer","date":". 11-07-2016, 09:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T06:45:44-08:00","id":999716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=999701#post999701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 1st ed they were around, but the loss of their masters left them scattered and stretched thin.<br /> <br /> That seems like the best approach to me - they can exist in the background, ready to show up if the plot demands it but not appearing every time someone tries to time-travel. Maybe we should emphasize just how broken they are even more heavily, so it feels less like a restriction and more like a plot hook. More thematic.<br /> <br /> I worry that this makes them <i>too much</i> like Geniuses.<br /> <br /> Those are valid Catalysts for a Genius. If a Clockstopper is just a Genius who gets eeevil powers instead of Inspiration ... they're just Banishers.<br /> <br /> I could see them more as anti-<i>Beholden</i>. They both have a kind of &quot;empty inside&quot; vibe, after all. Another reason to be cautious about showing people Wonders - rather than weakening their sense of morality, people might recoil from the Transgression so hard they permanently hate progress (and try to kill you, of course.)<br /> <br /> This would tie in nicely to the idea of Inspiration as a force in the world - Clockstoppers can form when normal change and progress gets too intense too.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually an interesting thought. So, in this interpretation, they're not Luddites or anti-progress loonies, but a normal person's reaction to transgressive things, but amplified by Mania?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Incidentally, that reminds me - I think we should play up the idea of Inspiration as <i>natural</i>. There's an idea in 1st ed that Wonders really do run on natural laws, and you can get genuine insights from studying them, but they're too fragile and complex for mortal eyes to grasp. Ancient Wonders resemble modern technology; future technology resembles modern Wonders, only mundane. Inspiration creates mundane insight, and mundane insight creates Inspiration; they're two sides of the same coin.<br /> <br /> This stuff has limited mechanical representation in 1st ed, but I really like the idea of &quot;genius&quot; as ambiguously supernatural, a kind of God-Machine maybe-magic-maybe-mundane vibe. </div> </div> </div>In other words, it works, it has rules, just nobody knows what the rules <i>are</i> yet. (My headcanon for a while has been that Wonders run on G-M metaphysics, and that could certainly be an option in a Demon crossover).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T07:27:05-08:00","id":999730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=999716#post999716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's actually an interesting thought. So, in this interpretation, they're not Luddites or anti-progress loonies, but a normal person's reaction to transgressive things, but amplified by Mania?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> In other words, it works, it has rules, just nobody knows what the rules <i>are</i> yet. (My headcanon for a while has been that Wonders run on G-M metaphysics, and that could certainly be an option in a Demon crossover).</div> </div> </div> </div>Still, there is the question of Havoc: what it is, why it works the way it does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T07:58:47-08:00","id":999743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=999730#post999730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Still, there is the question of Havoc: what it is, why it works the way it does.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that might be something that's up to the Storyteller. Though, if a Wonder works on poorly-understood, unconscious rules with the cracks filled in with Mania and chewing gum, Havoc isn't that surprising.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T08:37:33-08:00","id":999769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=999743#post999743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, that might be something that's up to the Storyteller. Though, if a Wonder works on poorly-understood, unconscious rules with the cracks filled in with Mania and chewing gum, Havoc isn't that surprising.</div> </div> </div> </div>If Wonders are based on valid, though poorly understood laws, Havoc can work when non-Inspired try to use them (pressing the unlabelled self-destruct or core-dump button, &quot;because of course it is there and why would anyone press it unless they wanted to&quot; Inspired logic). It doesn't work under analysis. Which is, perhaps, fine, but it does mean Havoc can only occur with direct interaction (as opposed to casual).<br /> <br /> If Wonders are based upon splicing alternate timelines and/or dimensions, interaction and observation could trigger some sort of quantum-state collapse. That would allow for indirect interaction to trigger Havoc.<br /> <br /> I supposed we just need to settle on something and deal with the consequences.<br /> <hr /><br /> Or maybe both? I supposed 1 allows 2 with certain sufficiently advanced tech...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T12:20:28-08:00","id":999860,"title":"","content":"I think I am person who complains most about Obligation/Integrity. Not because there is no reason to break it, but because it's outright moralizing a story about &quot;monsters&quot; when said &quot;monsters&quot; just beg for a sanity meter. How about another paradigm switch? Forget morals and obligation, be a selfish petty prick who uses mad science for self-indulgence, just don't get caught. Mad Scientist is often synonymous with Evil Scientist, and while majority agress we want it to be shades of gray, Obligation makes it Gray-White morality. <br /> <br /> My idea, briefly: high Integrity Genius is a eccentric loon who toys around with mad science, confuses curious mortals and bothers supernaturals (be it just manes or other splats), while the lower their Integrity the more global they get. They will start building lairs, show up on talkshows to scream about everyone being wrong, and/or caught by mortals dissecting aliens. Both extremes could be seens as wrong, but Geniuses &quot;fall&quot; by flying too close to the sun. They can still imposse change and make the difference, they just must do they darnest to avoid getting caught. Think it this way: as long as there is no good reason for mortals to bust in your lab to &quot;stop your evil plan&quot;, you are good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T12:37:10-08:00","id":999886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=999860#post999860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I am person who complains most about Obligation/Integrity. Not because there is no reason to break it, but because it's outright moralizing a story about &quot;monsters&quot; when said &quot;monsters&quot; just beg for a sanity meter. How about another paradigm switch? Forget morals and obligation, be a selfish petty prick who uses mad science for self-indulgence, just don't get caught. Mad Scientist is often synonymous with Evil Scientist, and while majority agress we want it to be shades of gray, Obligation makes it Gray-White morality.<br /> <br /> My idea, briefly: high Integrity Genius is a eccentric loon who toys around with mad science, confuses curious mortals and bothers supernaturals (be it just manes or other splats), while the lower their Integrity the more global they get. They will start building lairs, show up on talkshows to scream about everyone being wrong, and/or caught by mortals dissecting aliens. Both extremes could be seens as wrong, but Geniuses &quot;fall&quot; by flying too close to the sun. They can still imposse change and make the difference, they just must do they darnest to avoid getting caught. Think it this way: as long as there is no good reason for mortals to bust in your lab to &quot;stop your evil plan&quot;, you are good.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel the degree of control and restraint is a better barometer. It serves well to distinguish disciplined inventors, from the more unhinged monologuers, and the outright unfettered Illuminated. No Genii fits within the bounds of conventional sanity, but some are working with that, some ignore that, and some don't even know what &quot;sane&quot; means.<br /> <br /> And you can be perfectly composed, collected, and in control, with a detail plan for all outcomes, and still have an heinous or &quot;illogical&quot; end goal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 11-07-2016, 04:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T12:41:04-08:00","id":999890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=999886#post999886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel the degree of control and restraint is a better barometer. It serves well to distinguish disciplined inventors, from the more unhinged monologuers, and the outright unfettered Illuminated. No Genii fits without the bounds of conventional sanity, but some are working with that, some ignore that, and some don't even know what &quot;sane&quot; means.<br /> <br /> And you can be perfectly composed, collected, and in control, with a detail plan for all outcomes, and still have an heinous or &quot;illogical&quot; end goal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like an excellent measurement scale for new Morality-free Integrity meter! So, now we need to define &quot;sins&quot; and give it a flashy name?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T14:13:16-08:00","id":999940,"title":"","content":"You guys may be onto something. The more I think it the more I like it. &quot;Good&quot; Geniuses practice restraint, patience, and humility because they know that, regardless how much smarter they are and how quickly they could change the world, they understand that forcing your vision on the world will have all kinds of unforseen consequences. &quot;Bad&quot; Geniuses will have none of that. They know they're right and wasting time so inferior minds could grasp his vision is not an option. After all, everyone will agree with him once he has conquered the world and turned it into a paradise, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T14:31:12-08:00","id":999951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=999940#post999940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You guys may be onto something. The more I think it the more I like it. &quot;Good&quot; Geniuses practice restraint, patience, and humility because they know that, regardless how much smarter they are and how quickly they could change the world, they understand that forcing your vision on the world will have all kinds of unforseen consequences. &quot;Bad&quot; Geniuses will have none of that. They know they're right and wasting time so inferior minds could grasp his vision is not an option. After all, everyone will agree with him once he has conquered the world and turned it into a paradise, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally, yeah. Typically, the &quot;Good&quot; Genius will practice restraint, knowing their plans and inventions could have unforeseen consequences, while a &quot;Bad&quot; Genius will employ their devices and plans casually, knowing &quot;they're right&quot;.<br /> <br /> Of course, nothing prevents you from having a High [Restraint/Self-Control/Whatever] Genius from being a cautious monster, while a Low [Whatever] Genius might be genuinely well meaning, but a bit too quick with the ray-guns and indy ploys. Moriarty vs Doc Brown, perhaps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T15:13:42-08:00","id":999969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=999951#post999951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Generally, yeah. Typically, the &quot;Good&quot; Genius will practice restraint, knowing their plans and inventions could have unforeseen consequences, while a &quot;Bad&quot; Genius will employ their devices and plans casually, knowing &quot;they're right&quot;.<br /> <br /> Of course, nothing prevents you from having a High [Restraint/Self-Control/Whatever] Genius from being a cautious monster, while a Low [Whatever] Genius might be genuinely well meaning, but a bit too quick with the ray-guns and indy ploys. Moriarty vs Doc Brown, perhaps.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. For example, Lex Luthor is a pretty well-restrained Genius, in that he can keep a good public image, avoid obvious moments of villainy, and doesn't take too many unnecessary risks (depending on the writer)<br /> <br /> That said, I'm worried that making Obligation more about Restraint might cause it to step on Mage in regards to Wisdom.<br /> <br /> Though, Low Wisdom is pretty universally bad, and Low and High Restraint can both have their advantages and disadvantages, which might be one way to help separate them.<br /> <br /> A Restrained Genius gets along better with normal folk, certainly, but they're hamstringing themselves when it comes to dealing with sudden problems since they have to keep in mind things like laws and normal folks' Integrity when they deal with whatever threat du jour appears.<br /> <br /> An Unhinged Genius is probably going to be a pariah at best, possibly actively hunted by law enforcement and Hunters, but they can get shit <i>done.</i> A few normies might lose their shit, but hey, at least they weren't eaten by psychic tandem war elephants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T15:20:39-08:00","id":999975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">An Unhinged Genius is probably going to be a pariah at best, possibly actively hunted by law enforcement and Hunters, but they can get shit done.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is Hingedness a word? It might be just be zanny enough to work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12082,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","user":"Weird","date":". 11-07-2016, 06:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T15:28:39-08:00","id":999981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=999975#post999975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is Hingedness a word? It might be just be zanny enough to work.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not really a word. I was thinking Restraint would be what we would go with, since it is pretty indicative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T15:29:34-08:00","id":999982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=999975#post999975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might be just be zanny enough to work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, we can tell who here is already on the low end of the scale. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T15:49:51-08:00","id":999996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=999982#post999982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, we can tell who here is already on the low end of the scale. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Have I failed exposing myself as a rotten twisted Lemurian Phenomenologist?! Darn it, I might need to consider changing my baraminns!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T18:14:22-08:00","id":1000067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=999701#post999701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\\<br /> <br /> I worry that this makes them <i>too much</i> like Geniuses.<br /> <br /> Those are valid Catalysts for a Genius. If a Clockstopper is just a Genius who gets eeevil powers instead of Inspiration ... they're just Banishers.<br /> <br /> I could see them more as anti-<i>Beholden</i>. They both have a kind of &quot;empty inside&quot; vibe, after all. Another reason to be cautious about showing people Wonders - rather than weakening their sense of morality, people might recoil from the Transgression so hard they permanently hate progress (and try to kill you, of course.)<br /> <br /> This would tie in nicely to the idea of Inspiration as a force in the world - Clockstoppers can form when normal change and progress gets too intense too.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, that reminds me - I think we should play up the idea of Inspiration as <i>natural</i>. There's an idea in 1st ed that Wonders really do run on natural laws, and you can get genuine insights from studying them, but they're too fragile and complex for mortal eyes to grasp. Ancient Wonders resemble modern technology; future technology resembles modern Wonders, only mundane. Inspiration creates mundane insight, and mundane insight creates Inspiration; they're two sides of the same coin.<br /> <br /> This stuff has limited mechanical representation in 1st ed, but I really like the idea of &quot;genius&quot; as ambiguously supernatural, a kind of God-Machine maybe-magic-maybe-mundane vibe.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the way you think. <br /> <br /> Changing my mind to your idea: A Clockstopper is more anti-Beholden than anti-Genius. They see terrifying wonder, and rather than come to worship its maker as divine, they are repulsed so much they want to tear something of it down. Whether it be an actual Wonder or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T15:38:32-08:00","id":1001034,"title":"","content":"(emerges from a Detective Conan marathon)<br /> <br /> <b>Expanding Foundations</b><br /> I like the additions brought to each Foundation. Another option that fits the Progenitors is that they are most mindful of legacy. Be it the next generation of their refined Wonders or what the next generation of humanity will inherit.<br /> <br /> <b>Clockstoppers</b><br /> I had a similar thought recently about linking Beholden and Clockstoppers. In cases where a Genius tries to bend a companion and assistant to their worldview they might wind up with a person that is now a null void to their Wonders. From another angle, if a Genius that has given into Inspiration is Illuminated then a person devoid of any, the mundane and maniacal versions, becomes the figure of entropy that is a Clockstopper.<br /> <br /> If Clockstoppers are more like Beholden, however, there should be a distinction of how they are made. While the Beholden template is something that can be gained or lost, a Clockstopper template would be permanent.<br /> <br /> <b>Obligation</b><br /> Degree of restraint, I've felt, was something inferred from 1E Obligation although it wasn't well defined. It's good to bring that to the forefront. In terms of making Obligation more like an Integrity styled meter it should involve criteria more than just how Geniuses interact with the non-inspired.<br /> <br /> A Genius is obliged to humanity, because to disregard others is to disregard theirs. It is shunning the place they live. A Genius is also obliged to their Wonders, to take care of them and use them, to keep them stable in the onslaught of Havoc. A Genius is obliged to other Genii, for while the Inspired can vary field, occupation, paradigm and aesthetic greatly they have common ground in how they try to comprehend Inspiration. Collaboratives not only work on Wondrous projects but assist each other in various matters. And a Genius is also obliged to themselves, to manage their needs as a person along with the mania of Inspiration.<br /> <br /> The highs and lows of Obligation 2.0 are looking good. Are there hard numbers in mind, or what a Genius would be like in the middle ground of Obligation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T15:55:42-08:00","id":1001042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1001034#post1001034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Obligation</b><br /> Degree of restraint, I've felt, was something inferred from 1E Obligation although it wasn't well defined. It's good to bring that to the forefront. In terms of making Obligation more like an Integrity styled meter it should involve criteria more than just how Geniuses interact with the non-inspired.<br /> <br /> A Genius is obliged to humanity, because to disregard others is to disregard theirs. It is shunning the place they live. A Genius is also obliged to their Wonders, to take care of them and use them, to keep them stable in the onslaught of Havoc. A Genius is obliged to other Genii, for while the Inspired can vary field, occupation, paradigm and aesthetic greatly they have common ground in how they try to comprehend Inspiration. Collaboratives not only work on Wondrous projects but assist each other in various matters. And a Genius is also obliged to themselves, to manage their needs as a person along with the mania of Inspiration.<br /> <br /> The highs and lows of Obligation 2.0 are looking good. Are there hard numbers in mind, or what a Genius would be like in the middle ground of Obligation?</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually think that being at either end (or keeping in the middle) each has its own risks and rewards. High Restraint (I'm calling it &quot;Restraint&quot; for now) could make interacting with normals easier, at the cost of making Wonders more expensive and making acting inappropriately more difficult, Low Restraint would make it easier to act outside what society deems &quot;acceptable&quot; and makes Wonders easier to use, but makes you more prone to Jabir and make Havoc worse. Keeping it in the middle lets you have a balance of control and proactivity, but one end of the bar might be useful to you than the other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T19:57:13-08:00","id":1001162,"title":"","content":"High: reduced Jabir, reduced Havoc, increased Mania cost (to make sure their Wonders are stable), initiative penalty (or some other thing representing the double checking they must do constantly), maybe add more Mental Conditions (Syndromes?) like obsessive compulsive?<br /> Low: opposite of high, except also more Syndromes (but &quot;chaotic&quot; ones).<br /> Middle: &quot;Baseline&quot;, manageable Jabir, Havoc, Mania binding, Syndromes, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T13:07:26-08:00","id":1001895,"title":"","content":"I really like Restraint, but just to make sure that we have options I decided to look up some synonyms. Unfortunately most of appropriate ones are already in use for Virtues or Attributes (Temperance and Composure, and what a shame that Discipline means something entirely different in another gamline) but there is one that still might be suitable: Patience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T13:15:29-08:00","id":1001902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1001895#post1001895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like Restraint, but just to make sure that we have options I decided to look up some synonyms. Unfortunately most of appropriate ones are already in use for Virtues or Attributes (Temperance and Composure, and what a shame that Discipline means something entirely different in another gamline) but there is one that still might be suitable: Patience.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about, ironically, Control? Mostly as in Self-Control, but also as a dig against the line &quot;No one is in Control&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T13:56:18-08:00","id":1001921,"title":"","content":"Caution?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=999769#post999769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If Wonders are based on valid, though poorly understood laws, Havoc can work when non-Inspired try to use them (pressing the unlabelled self-destruct or core-dump button, &quot;because of course it is there and why would anyone press it unless they wanted to&quot; Inspired logic). It doesn't work under analysis. Which is, perhaps, fine, but it does mean Havoc can only occur with direct interaction (as opposed to casual).<br /> <br /> If Wonders are based upon splicing alternate timelines and/or dimensions, interaction and observation could trigger some sort of quantum-state collapse. That would allow for indirect interaction to trigger Havoc.<br /> <br /> I supposed we just need to settle on something and deal with the consequences.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, that's a good point.<br /> <br /> I'd lean towards direct interaction. As you say, making it based on observation pins us down to more mystical/supernatural interpretations.<br /> <br /> Direct interaction could as easily be split timelines as hypertech, but the opposite isn't as true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":877,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","user":"MugaSofer","date":". 11-11-2016, 05:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T15:29:04-08:00","id":1001952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1001921#post1001921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Caution?<br /> <br /> <br /> Hmm, that's a good point.<br /> <br /> I'd lean towards direct interaction. As you say, making it based on observation pins us down to more mystical/supernatural interpretations.<br /> <br /> Direct interaction could as easily be split timelines as hypertech, but the opposite isn't as true.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure? I mean, depending on what is possible, after a certain point it doesn't matter. Clark's Third Law and all. If Hypertech is capable of folding divergent timelines/universes into the current one in an unstable field subject to disruption from observation and calculation, &quot;People seeing it makes it break, so it must be magic&quot; is an uninformed but functional assessment. That you are doing so with highly advanced technology instead of pure will and mystical knowledge doesn't change the details for most folks.<br /> <br /> Maybe lower end Wonders, being less divergent from currently understood principles, are more resistant to Havoc, and only trigger it with significant tampering. Moderately ranked Wonders draw upon little understood forces and innovations, and thus are subject to Havoc at even casual use. The highest ranked Wonders need to &quot;cheat&quot; by folding other realities and timelines over this one, and are extremely fragile - where someone nearby observing it and running the numbers in their head generates enough unaccounted for distortion, and triggers Havoc.<br /> <br /> Better-than-normal scanner or cutting-end gun? Hard to break. Bullshit quantum-material teleporter or omniscience super-computer? Try not to think about it too hard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T15:59:15-08:00","id":1001964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1001952#post1001952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure? I mean, depending on what is possible, after a certain point it doesn't matter. Clark's Third Law and all. If Hypertech is capable of folding divergent timelines/universes into the current one in an unstable field subject to disruption from observation and calculation, &quot;People seeing it makes it break, so it must be magic&quot; is an uninformed but functional assessment. That you are doing so with highly advanced technology instead of pure will and mystical knowledge doesn't change the details for most folks.<br /> <br /> Maybe lower end Wonders, being less divergent from currently understood principles, are more resistant to Havoc, and only trigger it with significant tampering. Moderately ranked Wonders draw upon little understood forces and innovations, and thus are subject to Havoc at even casual use. The highest ranked Wonders need to &quot;cheat&quot; by folding other realities and timelines over this one, and are extremely fragile - where someone nearby observing it and running the numbers in their head generates enough unaccounted for distortion, and triggers Havoc.<br /> <br /> Better-than-normal scanner or cutting-end gun? Hard to break. Bullshit quantum-material teleporter or omniscience super-computer? Try not to think about it too hard.</div> </div> </div> </div>So something along the lines of Vulgar vs. Covert magic?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T07:54:28-08:00","id":1003390,"title":"","content":"Restraint, Patience, Caution, Discipline, Control all sound wonderful although each has slightly different bend on what they would intuitively track. Important detail here. I don't think Genii should get crazier as their Restraint goes down. Restraint helps them from acting out in a way that alerts other of their issues (for example lower to moderate Restraint requires Willpower to avoid acting like a looney). Genius go crazier with higher Inspiration (Go Mad with Inspiration/Great Power Comes with Great Insanity), or does craziness perhaps empower Inspiration?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T08:59:09-08:00","id":1003426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1003390#post1003390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Restraint, Patience, Caution, Discipline, Control all sound wonderful although each has slightly different bend on what they would intuitively track. Important detail here. I don't think Genii should get crazier as their Restraint goes down. Restraint helps them from acting out in a way that alerts other of their issues (for example lower to moderate Restraint requires Willpower to avoid acting like a looney).</div> </div> </div> </div>It might not just be as it goes down - I could see certain Conditions applying at high [Obligation], reflecting the effort at consideration and self-control. Low [Obligation], they'd reflect the lack of self-control.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1003390#post1003390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Genius go crazier with higher Inspiration (Go Mad with Inspiration/Great Power Comes with Great Insanity), or does craziness perhaps empower Inspiration?</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely the former, if anything. Genii aren't empowered by &quot;crazy&quot; - Inspiration just has the effect (side or not) of knocking one's worldview/perception off skew.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T16:25:47-08:00","id":1003661,"title":"","content":"Put another way: Inspiration attunes you to the Mania in the world. In that regard, it's a bit like <b>Mage: the Awakening</b>'s Mage Sight, in that the higher your Inspiration goes the stranger the world looks to you. <br /> <br /> I like Restraint; that said, it reminds me a lot of <b>Mage: the Awakening</b>'s Wisdom. Both games share a theme that you have phenomenal power your fingertips and that you need to exercise prudence to avoid being destructive with that power. Restraint and Wisdom are essentially synonyms for prudence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T17:27:18-08:00","id":1003694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1003661#post1003661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Put another way: Inspiration attunes you to the Mania in the world. In that regard, it's a bit like <b>Mage: the Awakening</b>'s Mage Sight, in that the higher your Inspiration goes the stranger the world looks to you.<br /> <br /> I like Restraint; that said, it reminds me a lot of <b>Mage: the Awakening</b>'s Wisdom. Both games share a theme that you have phenomenal power your fingertips and that you need to exercise prudence to avoid being destructive with that power. Restraint and Wisdom are essentially synonyms for prudence.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a valid point. Hopefully, it'll be different in practice, though. You won't get many Magi who intentionally play Low Wisdom, since there's not much good and a lot bad; conversely A Genius might have incentive to play Low Restraint.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T17:30:55-08:00","id":1003700,"title":"","content":"Mage 2e's author has pointed to Harry Dresdon as an example of a low-Wisdom mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T17:44:43-08:00","id":1003706,"title":"","content":"I am gonna level with you, I got no idea who that is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T21:21:17-08:00","id":1003771,"title":"","content":"The main character of an extensive urban fantasy series of novels called \u201cThe Dresdon Files\u201d. It's gotten its own role-playing game and a TV series adaptation. I'd recommend googling it, if only to get a sense of what it's like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T06:32:45-08:00","id":1003900,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4488_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4488\" data-vbnamecard=\"4488\">malonkey1</a> <b>I'd</b> recommend reading them. Perhaps twice (as there is a lot of foreshadowing that only really becomes clear when you know what eventually happens).<br /> <br /> But back to Genius...<br /> <br /> I'm seeing Obligation or its replacement as a measure indicating how &quot;together&quot; a Genius has it. High, and they are basically functional, Low and they are the stereotypical Mad Scientist or Evil Genius. Low, I'm seeing as having demonstrable effects and social impact, so that when a Genius goes Illuminated and <i>drops</i> [Obligation], they superficially seem like a Mid-to-High [Obligation] Genius.<br /> <br /> Hm. Another way to look at it might be how much the Genius thinks the outside world perceives them. High, and they are confident in public perception, Low and they <i>know</i> they are rejected and they scramble for recognition. Illuminated, and they just don't care anymore (provided their mindset even includes the notion of outside sentient actors).<br /> <br /> [NOTE: I'm just spinning ideas here to see what sticks]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 11-16-2016, 09:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T09:44:29-08:00","id":1003989,"title":"","content":"I think I suggested Alienation to track how Genius is received by others, but we could call it Publicity. After all Demon and Beast gamelines already stopped caring about sanity and karma. Villain with Good Publicity, anyone?<br /> If I recall that idea was shot down back then because it was &quot;unfair&quot; that Genius's meter was affected by other people, but I think that could fit perfectly with narative of Genii being relucant to interact with mortals outside of necessrity. And after all, isn't Storyteller required to craft situations where characters have to compromise their stats anyway?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12082,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","user":"Weird","date":". 11-16-2016, 12:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T11:29:44-08:00","id":1004027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1003989#post1003989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I suggested Alienation to track how Genius is received by others, but we could call it Publicity. After all Demon and Beast gamelines already stopped caring about sanity and karma. Villain with Good Publicity, anyone?<br /> If I recall that idea was shot down back then because it was &quot;unfair&quot; that Genius's meter was affected by other people, but I think that could fit perfectly with narative of Genii being relucant to interact with mortals outside of necessrity. And after all, isn't Storyteller required to craft situations where characters have to compromise their stats anyway?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thing is, I don't think Publicity really fits all cases. The word seems to be a synonym for Fame, but there are plenty of reclusive and hidden Mad Scientists. When I referenced &quot;how the outside world perceives them&quot;, I meant <i>in the mind of the Genius</i>. Should somehow the world (however big) respects them, but <i>the Genius</i> thinks they are being laughed at and needs to earn recognition? Low meter. Usually, the outside world will impact how the Genius sees themselves and their work, and the two will be in sync... but it might not have to be.<br /> <br /> Does that make any sense?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T13:38:30-08:00","id":1004096,"title":"","content":"I think it does. How in touch Genius is with themselves and how they perceive others to perceive themselves?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T12:12:40-08:00","id":1007794,"title":"","content":"I don't think I'm the most qualified to comment on this, but from what I get from Genius: the Transgression is that they have trouble connecting with people, right? So why not have Association as an Integrity replacement? High Association means that you're more connected to society around you, and you tend towards the more respectable type of Scientist. A low Association would go with the Mad Scientist Trope that doesn't care about people at all and is willing to do more experiments that could harm others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T12:01:37-08:00","id":1010291,"title":"","content":"Obligation 2.0 (until a new name is settled) serves as the basis of how well a Genius interacts with humanity. High, although eccentric they are respected or at least heard out. Low, they are a pariah and stereotypical evil genius to the nth degree. Transgressions now extend to what end the Genius will disturb previous perceptions of themselves. The quirky if strange old man refitting a DeLorean in his garage is not the guy who would kill people for their body parts. Although he is willing to burn down his house for insurance money and trick terrorists into giving him plutonium, events his [Obligation 2.0] rating may not survive.<br /> <br /> Alongside Obligation 2.0 is a set of inverted boons and penalties. Geniuses high on the scale are Paragons (like the Science Hero merit and Paragon terms from 1.1e) better able to manage their reputation and trust, respect or believability. What they say makes sense. However, their Wonders are at a disadvantage as Havoc is all the more forthcoming as Inspired and actual science clash. On the flip side those low on Obligation 2.0 can have their Wonders bettered at the cost of distance from humanity, Jabir plaguing their interactions and performance around the non-Inspired.<br /> <br /> I like Vent0's alternate way of looking at it, as Obligation 2.0 is fundamentally how the Genius perceives their connection to society around them. A Genius stuck at one end of the scale could be surprised for how others' perspective changes from their own, like the Paragon finding horrified reactions from something that was 'perfectly safe' or the MAD scientist finding begrudging respect from someone he didn't think he had helped.<br /> <br /> As for bonuses and penalties, it would look much like having two flipped sets of Kenning that Changelings have from Clarity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T03:40:57-08:00","id":1010995,"title":"","content":"Just thought a word that couldn't be used anywhere else but would be perfect for Genii: Credibility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T14:11:15-08:00","id":1012166,"title":"","content":"I don't have any ideas for Obligation 2.0 at the moment, but I do like the sound of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12436_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12436\" data-vbnamecard=\"12436\">Ever Professional</a>'s Association.<br /> <br /> However, I'd like to share some ideas to make Geniuses more powerful.<br /> <br /> 1) Spending Mania to boost Mental Attributes grants +2 per point. The same goes for the Grants of the Directors and Navigators.<br /> <br /> 2) By spending a point of Mania when they get 3 Successes on a Mental roll, they may turn it into an Exceptional Success. They may do this a number of times per scene equal to Inspiration.<br /> <br /> 3) Add Inspiration to all Build Equipment rolls, including Plans. This stacks with number 2.<br /> <br /> 4) By spending 1 Mania, you may decrease the normal time taken by a Mental extended action into singular turns. This includes Meditation, creating Plans and Investigations. The cost must be paid every turn.<br /> <br /> 5) Do not bind Mania to create Wonders. Instead, Binding Mania unlocks additional features once you have surpassed the minimal Axiom requirements for a given Wonder. It also adds dice to Clashes Of Wills involving the Wonders. Certain high Inspiration Merits may allow the Binding of Mania to add extra functions even to 5 dot Wonders, and dice tricks to Clashes Of Wills involving the Wonders.<br /> <br /> 6) Contesting a power meant to turn a Genius away from their Magnum Opus receives the Rote Quality.<br /> <br /> 7) The extra Mental Attribute dot given at character creation may take that Attribute above the normal limits imposed by Inspiration.<br /> <br /> 8) Geniuses now have access to a trio of aura mechanics similar to those of vampires, but meant to represent Inspiration as a force of change, progress and transgression. Here is the draft:<br /> <br /> Roll a Mental Attribute + Inspiration. This may not benefit from Mania expenditure. Each Attribute causes a different Condition (see the spoiler below) and represents a certain archetypal aspect of the Genius.<br /> <br /> <b>Action:</b> I am unsure. Vampires use simple actions that take up a turn at most, but these might take multiple turns.<br /> <br /> <b>Intelligence:</b> The Professor. It invokes the Genius as a figure of wisdom and guidance, or authority and dominance. Success on the roll inflicts the <i>Instructed</i> Condition.<br /> <br /> <b>Wits:</b> The Visionary. It invokes the Genius as someone filled with intuition and big plans, or a methodical and analytical machine. Success on the roll inflicts the <i>Shared Vision</i> Condition.<br /> <br /> <b>Resolve: </b>The Adventurer. It invokes the Genius as the brave soul who fears no danger. They can risk themselves for the greater good of humanity, or use their gifts for personal gain at the expense of others. Success on the roll inflicts the Condition.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><u><b>Instructed</b></u><br /> Your character has been taught to act in a certain way by an expert or authority, or at least someone who acts the part. They find that following this advice feels natural. When following the instructions to the letter, they gain +2 and an Exceptional Success on 3 Successes. Attempts to turn them away from this course of action suffer a -2 penalty and lose 10 Again. This Condition fades after a number of days equal to the Inspiration of the Genius who inflicted. After resolving Instructed, your character cannot be subject to it again for a full month.<br /> <br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Follow the instructions to the end. Make considerable effort to openly challenge them.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Shared Vision</b></u><br /> Your skills have been carefully inspected to make you an efficient part of a plan, and you are properly motivated to see it carried out. All revelant rolls you make as a secondary actor in a Teamwork action receive the Rote Quality. If you are the primary actor, all rolls which benefit from the bonus dice given from secondary actors are considered an Exceptional Success with 3 Succcesses. This Condition fades after a number of days equal to the Inspiration of the Genius who inflicted. After resolving Instructed, your character cannot be subject to it again for a full month.<br /> <br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Carry out the plan to the end, significantly change its outcome with personal alterations, or sabotage it for your own gain.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Impressed</b></u><br /> You have been awed by the achievements and stories of a larger than life figure, and you find it difficult to get in their way or do them harm. All rolls meant to do so suffer a -2 penalty and lose 10 Again, including supernatural powers. Their Impression level with you is one step higher than it would normally be, up to a maximum of Excellent. Their rolls in Social Maneuvering against you gain Exceptional Successes with 3 Successes. This Condition fades after a number of days equal to the Inspiration of the Genius who inflicted. After resolving Instructed, your character cannot be subject to it again for a full month.<br /> <br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Ask to join them in an adventure, challenge them to a competition.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T17:08:16-08:00","id":1012271,"title":"","content":"I don't think we <i>need</i> Geniuses to be more powerful, though. They are on even or near-even footing with Mages as it stands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T05:30:23-08:00","id":1012512,"title":"","content":"There's one aspect of Genius I wanted to discuss: Funding. Being a genius is expensive since they rely completely on technology to do their thing. I like how the game acknwoledges this, but as some people have pointed out in here a player shouldn't be worrying about balancing numbers and businesses. As such I have come with a system that I hope will balance both aspects. Please, feel free to share your opinions and suggestions on it.<br /> <br /> <b><u>-Funding.</u></b><br /> <br /> In game terms, funding refers exclusively to the characteristics and origin of the resources (Money, personel, tools, materials, buildings, etc...) that the genius needs to create and maintain the infrastructure that allows him to build wonders. Each type of funding will have advantages and disadvantages that the player will have to deal with at the discretion of the storyteller.<br /> In game mechanics Funding is a way for the storyteller to create drama and adventures for the player character by introducing complications. It's not intended to be a hassle or another thing to worry about. It's just another way to add fun to the game. The storyteller, with the help of the player, is the one that decides when the complicatons enter the game and always with the intention to enrich the adventure.<br /> During character creation a player character must chose between one of the following fundings, or come up with a new one with the approval of the storyteller. (These are just some examples. If you have another one, or think one shouldn't be here, please feel free to say it)<br /> <br /> - Trust fund.<br /> <br /> Someone in your family or close to you was very rich, liked you a lot, and recently died. As a result, you have inherited a vast amount of wealth that you're using to fund your research and wonders. However, there's an obvious catch: it's limited. Sooner or later your funds will run out, and many young geniuses underestimate just how expensive the live of a genius can get. This type of funding is great for players who don't want to worry about funding, at least in the begining. As the campaign advances, and depending on the character's actions, the storyteller can tell the player their funding is running low and they need to find an alternative source of income or risk running out of cash at a very inconvenient moment.<br /> <br /> -Freelancer.<br /> <br /> The genius offers his skills and inventions in order to fund itself. The genius is already a stablished freelancer with a list of regular clients. It's important to specify what type of client and jobs they take since it will affect their reputation and the kind of clients and jobs they will get in the future. This type of funding offers the most independence. The big catch is that, even with regular clients, it's a very unstable source of income. Also, taking into account how chaotic the life of a genius can get (and let's be honest, their creations are not famous for being very safe or stable) planning becomes nightmare, with projects often delayed or destroyed, and there's the risk of angry clients coming back for the genius.<br /> <br /> - Business.<br /> <br /> You own a business that provides you with a stable source of funding. The player has to specify what type of business it is. It's large and succesful enough that it runs itself, so the player doesn't need to worry about management. The main advantage is that it allows the genius to be independent and gives access to the resources of the business. However, apart from the regular problems that may assault any businesses, the genius has to deal with the simple fact that his or her business is ill prepared to deal with what enemy geniuses may throw at it, which makes it a very vulnerable point of attack. Here's an example, batman and iron man are used to battle supervillains, but the people that work at wayne enterprises and stark tech are not. A genius must be prepared to defend their business.<br /> <br /> -Organization.<br /> <br /> A big and powerful organization is the one providing the funding. The player has to specify which one (Government, corporation, etc...). Working for an organization has the advantage of not having to worry about anything except the research and building of wonders, the organization provides anything they may need. The main catch is that the genius has to justify their expenses, answer to the organizations demands and help it reach their goals, whatever those may be, or face the wrath of their superiors. In conclusion, it's a secure source of income and security in exchange for independence.<br /> <br /> Well, that's it for now. If you have more ideas feel free to share them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T06:43:55-08:00","id":1012551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1012166#post1012166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have any ideas for Obligation 2.0 at the moment, but I do like the sound of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12436_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12436\" data-vbnamecard=\"12436\">Ever Professional</a>'s Association.<br /> <br /> However, I'd like to share some ideas to make Geniuses more powerful.<br /> <br /> 1) Spending Mania to boost Mental Attributes grants +2 per point. The same goes for the Grants of the Directors and Navigators.<br /> <br /> 2) By spending a point of Mania when they get 3 Successes on a Mental roll, they may turn it into an Exceptional Success. They may do this a number of times per scene equal to Inspiration.<br /> <br /> 3) Add Inspiration to all Build Equipment rolls, including Plans. This stacks with number 2.<br /> <br /> 4) By spending 1 Mania, you may decrease the normal time taken by a Mental extended action into singular turns. This includes Meditation, creating Plans and Investigations. The cost must be paid every turn.<br /> <br /> 5) Do not bind Mania to create Wonders. Instead, Binding Mania unlocks additional features once you have surpassed the minimal Axiom requirements for a given Wonder. It also adds dice to Clashes Of Wills involving the Wonders. Certain high Inspiration Merits may allow the Binding of Mania to add extra functions even to 5 dot Wonders, and dice tricks to Clashes Of Wills involving the Wonders.<br /> <br /> 6) Contesting a power meant to turn a Genius away from their Magnum Opus receives the Rote Quality.<br /> <br /> 7) The extra Mental Attribute dot given at character creation may take that Attribute above the normal limits imposed by Inspiration.<br /> <br /> 8) Geniuses now have access to a trio of aura mechanics similar to those of vampires, but meant to represent Inspiration as a force of change, progress and transgression. Here is the draft:<br /> <br /> Roll a Mental Attribute + Inspiration. This may not benefit from Mania expenditure. Each Attribute causes a different Condition (see the spoiler below) and represents a certain archetypal aspect of the Genius.<br /> <br /> <b>Action:</b> I am unsure. Vampires use simple actions that take up a turn at most, but these might take multiple turns.<br /> <br /> <b>Intelligence:</b> The Professor. It invokes the Genius as a figure of wisdom and guidance, or authority and dominance. Success on the roll inflicts the <i>Instructed</i> Condition.<br /> <br /> <b>Wits:</b> The Visionary. It invokes the Genius as someone filled with intuition and big plans, or a methodical and analytical machine. Success on the roll inflicts the <i>Shared Vision</i> Condition.<br /> <br /> <b>Resolve: </b>The Adventurer. It invokes the Genius as the brave soul who fears no danger. They can risk themselves for the greater good of humanity, or use their gifts for personal gain at the expense of others. Success on the roll inflicts the Condition.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><u><b>Instructed</b></u><br /> Your character has been taught to act in a certain way by an expert or authority, or at least someone who acts the part. They find that following this advice feels natural. When following the instructions to the letter, they gain +2 and an Exceptional Success on 3 Successes. Attempts to turn them away from this course of action suffer a -2 penalty and lose 10 Again. This Condition fades after a number of days equal to the Inspiration of the Genius who inflicted. After resolving Instructed, your character cannot be subject to it again for a full month.<br /> <br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Follow the instructions to the end. Make considerable effort to openly challenge them.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Shared Vision</b></u><br /> Your skills have been carefully inspected to make you an efficient part of a plan, and you are properly motivated to see it carried out. All revelant rolls you make as a secondary actor in a Teamwork action receive the Rote Quality. If you are the primary actor, all rolls which benefit from the bonus dice given from secondary actors are considered an Exceptional Success with 3 Succcesses. This Condition fades after a number of days equal to the Inspiration of the Genius who inflicted. After resolving Instructed, your character cannot be subject to it again for a full month.<br /> <br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Carry out the plan to the end, significantly change its outcome with personal alterations, or sabotage it for your own gain.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Impressed</b></u><br /> You have been awed by the achievements and stories of a larger than life figure, and you find it difficult to get in their way or do them harm. All rolls meant to do so suffer a -2 penalty and lose 10 Again, including supernatural powers. Their Impression level with you is one step higher than it would normally be, up to a maximum of Excellent. Their rolls in Social Maneuvering against you gain Exceptional Successes with 3 Successes. This Condition fades after a number of days equal to the Inspiration of the Genius who inflicted. After resolving Instructed, your character cannot be subject to it again for a full month.<br /> <br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Ask to join them in an adventure, challenge them to a competition.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>1 and 2 seem a little too strong. I like 3 and 4. Not sure exactly how 5 would work out - do Wonders cost XP, Willpower Dots (basically XP), or are free? Hmm. Maybe Havoc is treated like a Clash of Wills, so Binding Mania makes it more resistant... 6 seems okay, but I think you mean the Genius gains the Rote Quality to their contested roll. 7 seems extremely edge-case. 8 I'm uncertain on - the Conditions seem a bit strong, and I don't really get why and where Genii need an Aura mechanic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1012271#post1012271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think we <i>need</i> Geniuses to be more powerful, though. They are on even or near-even footing with Mages as it stands.</div> </div> </div> </div>Provided they have tools. A Mage is dangerous as long as they are conscious. Trap a Genius in a room without tools, and there is very little they can do immediately (sure they can Deconstruct Technology to get out, probably, then grab whatever is nearby to Kitbash something, but a Mage can go from &quot;in a box&quot; to &quot;shredding space and time, etc.&quot; in 3 seconds.).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","cus