t is. It's large and succesful enough that it runs itself, so the player doesn't need to worry about management. The main advantage is that it allows the genius to be independent and gives access to the resources of the business. However, apart from the regular problems that may assault any businesses, the genius has to deal with the simple fact that his or her business is ill prepared to deal with what enemy geniuses may throw at it, which makes it a very vulnerable point of attack. Here's an example, batman and iron man are used to battle supervillains, but the people that work at wayne enterprises and stark tech are not. A genius must be prepared to defend their business.<br /> <br /> -Organization.<br /> <br /> A big and powerful organization is the one providing the funding. The player has to specify which one (Government, corporation, etc...). Working for an organization has the advantage of not having to worry about anything except the research and building of wonders, the organization provides anything they may need. The main catch is that the genius has to justify their expenses, answer to the organizations demands and help it reach their goals, whatever those may be, or face the wrath of their superiors. In conclusion, it's a secure source of income and security in exchange for independence.<br /> <br /> Well, that's it for now. If you have more ideas feel free to share them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hmm. Would you see Funding as something that might be worth tracking, almost like Beast tracks Satiety? It goes up and down as you get new income streams, or spend vast resources on Wonders and research?<br /> <br /> Or just keep it to a more elaborated (and separate) Resources?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T07:06:06-08:00","id":1012560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1012553#post1012553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Hmm. Would you see Funding as something that might be worth tracking, almost like Beast tracks Satiety? It goes up and down as you get new income streams, or spend vast resources on Wonders and research?<br /> <br /> Or just keep it to a more elaborated (and separate) Resources?</div> </div> </div> </div>The main reason I avoided tracking or any mechanics is because I have absolutely no idea how to design game mechanics, in fact, I'm pretty bad about it. I wanted to leave it as a storyteller resource and a way for players to add more dept to their characters. However, if you have any idea of how to do it then by all means go ahead. Beasts satiety is a good example, but I think funding is a bit more complex.<br /> <br /> Now, the way I see funding is that it's a way to explain where the backgrounds and merits, like resources, of the genius come from. The best example I can come with is that it's similar to the paradigms, practice and instruments from mage 20th anniversary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2964,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","user":"Firanai","date":". 12-05-2016, 02:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T14:50:12-08:00","id":1012794,"title":"","content":"My thought was to keep funding and supplies as RP-based as possible. Basically, the idea was to have Wonders require specific components instead of needing abstract Resource requirements. So instead of worrying about funding for your death ray, you just need to worry about the giant diamond itself, and how you get it (purchase with the normal Resource/Availability, theft, finding it in some Bardo, etc.) is up to you and the Storyteller. That reduces the number of new systems we need and still keeps Wonder contstruction as a character action rather than just rolling in downtime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T07:16:13-08:00","id":1014749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1012551#post1012551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1 and 2 seem a little too strong. I like 3 and 4. Not sure exactly how 5 would work out - do Wonders cost XP, Willpower Dots (basically XP), or are free? Hmm. Maybe Havoc is treated like a Clash of Wills, so Binding Mania makes it more resistant... 6 seems okay, but I think you mean the Genius gains the Rote Quality to their contested roll. 7 seems extremely edge-case. 8 I'm uncertain on - the Conditions seem a bit strong, and I don't really get why and where Genii need an Aura mechanic.</div> </div> </div> </div> What I meant with number 5 is that Wonders would cost Wondrous Experiences. Binding Mania would unlock additional effects much like spending Reach does in Mage. Havoc could indeed be treated as a Clash Of Wills, which would probably pit the Genius' Inspiration + Resolve + Bound Mania vs Dexterity or Wits + Skill. But Binding Mania could also help with other types of Clashes Of Wills. For example: a Genius wants to use an Epikrato raygun to mind control someone, but a vampire wants to do use Dominate on the same person, and their orders are mutually exclusive.<br /> <br /> For number 6, it is indeed the Genius who gains the Rote Quality.<br /> <br /> For number 8, I want to have an Aura mechanic for Geniuses for exactly the reason you said: they are mostly defenseless without tools. I also think it would be cool if Geniuses could respond to the Auras of other supernaturals. How would you do this Aura? If you don't like the idea, what alternative do you suggest?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 12-09-2016, 10:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T07:45:08-08:00","id":1014766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1014749#post1014749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> What I meant with number 5 is that Wonders would cost Wondrous Experiences. Binding Mania would unlock additional effects much like spending Reach does in Mage. Havoc could indeed be treated as a Clash Of Wills, which would probably pit the Genius' Inspiration + Resolve + Bound Mania vs Dexterity or Wits + Skill.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now that you've spelled it out, I like Havoc as an opposing Dice Pool that includes Skill. Attribute might include a few more Attributes, depending on what is done, I'd think (operation: Dex, Notice: Wits, Deconstruction/Analysis: Intelligence). But for the Genius's end, what about [Obligation] instead of Inspiration or Resolve (just for Havoc rolls, mind you)?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1014749#post1014749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> For number 8, I want to have an Aura mechanic for Geniuses for exactly the reason you said: they are mostly defenseless without tools. I also think it would be cool if Geniuses could respond to the Auras of other supernaturals. How would you do this Aura? If you don't like the idea, what alternative do you suggest?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, off hand. I didn't really think every splat needed an Aura, so I haven't put much thought into it. I'd guess Unmada Field would be similar, but that is restricted to a subset of Genii.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T19:25:12-08:00","id":1015097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1014749#post1014749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Havoc could indeed be treated as a Clash Of Wills, which would probably pit the Genius' Inspiration + Resolve + Bound Mania vs Dexterity or Wits + Skill</div> </div> </div> </div>I was actually thinking that individual Wonders would have Havoc dicepools, so a Genius who wanted to cut corners and ignore safeguards (basically, skipping Components) could do so, but their Wonder would be permanently more unstable.<br /> <br /> But that's not necessarily mutually exclusive with your idea, either. It could easily be Base Havoc + Inspiration + Modifiers vs. Attribute + Skill.<br /> <br /> I've been working on preliminary Wonder/Axiom/Postulate rules, but I'm not ready to share yet. I'll try for tomorrow, though!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":4488,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","user":"malonkey1","date":". 12-09-2016, 11:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T14:41:44-08:00","id":1015855,"title":"","content":"Alright, I've got the start of Wonder Construction. It's pretty close to Mage spell construction at the moment, as I thought it would make a good starting point.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5D9AgFEhGZ3dzM3aUZMMWRvT00\" target=\"_blank\">Link here.</a><br /> <br /> It's definitely not finished, but it's a start.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T01:20:43-08:00","id":1016026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1012512#post1012512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's one aspect of Genius I wanted to discuss: Funding. Being a genius is expensive since they rely completely on technology to do their thing. I like how the game acknwoledges this, but as some people have pointed out in here a player shouldn't be worrying about balancing numbers and businesses. As such I have come with a system that I hope will balance both aspects. Please, feel free to share your opinions and suggestions on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Many many pages ago in this very same thread I had a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=966076#post966076\">post</a> suggesting a similar switch of Funding from a Resources derived merit into its own system. I've had more time and practice to come back to a Funding or Budget conversation.<br /> <br /> I'm of the philosophy is that if you try to create too many parameters for a single merit, it should instead become its own system. Although many do not want to factor a 'Budget' into how their Genius creates their Wonders, it ties back to one of the game themes of desperation and it is a fitting limiter to what a Genius can do at the start of a Chronicle versus the end. Reworked as a new system, it would have to tie back to other aspects of the game.<br /> <br /> So my revamped pro funding platform:<br /> <br /> <b>Get Some Perks from Funding</b><br /> Who doesn't like perks? If a Genius has a certain variety of Funding they also receive a small circumstantial boon, its bonus tied to the rating of that Funding.<br /> <br /> <b>Reduce Axiom Penalties</b><br /> Trying to create a Wonder beyond your current rating of Axiom? Now you can with the right Funding. The rating of applied Funding will reduce the penalty you get for Wonder creation tied to the rating of Wonder you are trying to create. However this caps all the other uses of Funding for the session, or maybe a story. Instead of requiring a Budget for everything, the Funding now instead smooths over the times you face too many penalties with your Wonder creation roll. Although it can only do so at select times.<br /> <br /> <b>Funding Upkeep as Story Hooks</b><br /> Each Funding would require some kind of upkeep, such as time or criteria or a dice roll. Even if these are not required, use Funding as a way to introduce or influence plots. Working your 9-5 job to get the cloning budget doesn't have to be only a time sink, you can use it as a storytelling medium for things that interest the Genius or for plots along that sphere of Funding.<br /> <br /> <b>Tie Funding to Obligation (2.0)</b><br /> This is the biggest point that could of had a lot of potential in the 1.1 edition of Genius yet it was a missed opportunity. As much as a Genius is a fount of ideas and a conduit of Mania, they cannot create in a vacuum. If Obligation was meant to relate how stable a Genius remains in relation to the society around them, Funding is where this should occur. Funding and its ratings would serve as an ideal 'Touchstone' for breaks of Obligation. Risking a drop on the meter yet you upheld a tenant of your Funding? Have it as a bonus to the roll. On the flip side, if you've spurned Funding on an Obligation lowering act the Funding becomes a penalty. Only a single source of Funding could affect Obligation breaking points at a time. Yet it can't be one you've already tapped out for other advantages.<br /> <br /> <b>Encourage Different Play Styles</b><br /> Does your Genius get involved with a lot of ventures, having a wealth of various 1 dot Fundings? Soak up the perks and incur few drawbacks when you invariably step away from some of them. However your bonus from any single Funding will never be that great and that's a lot of upkeep to keep spinning. Or you can be a Genius that defines and expresses themselves from a single Funding at a high rating. It gives a mighty bonus yet hurts all the more to step away from when its high rating becomes a penalty. Additionally, Funding types could be exchanged between stories and other such points between sessions in a Chronicle.<br /> <br /> <b>Fix Some Merits</b><br /> With Funding as a separate sub system, other Genius merits can be renovated with appropriate mechanics and themes. The Tenure Merit, besides mitigating Failures with Wonder creation, could also preventing a single type of Funding from dropping lower than 1 dot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T07:50:30-08:00","id":1016105,"title":"","content":"Since Orphaned Wonders are still a thing, I think it would be a good idea to make the original, always-becomes-a-monster Orphans their own thing; they become functionally antagonists only when they figure out how to upgrade themselves (perhaps they have their own term to distinguish them from &quot;glitchy but normal&quot; Orphans-perhaps something like Vital Orphans, because at that point they match the biological criteria for &quot;alive&quot;, minus maybe reproduction and only because of lack of motive, not ability). Which leads me into the intelligence scale, and fixing that quickly:<br /> <br /> <b>Zombie: </b>The Orphan is active, but it's still debatable whether it's actually alive or not; it evolves, it reacts to stimuli, it can even reproduce, but it's otherwise mindless in all other ways; it acts based on a predictable program, more video game NPC on a fixed loop and attack pattern than any actual thought. That makes it predictable and hacked easily enough by a Genius who figures out the internal logic gates, but that also makes it completely relentless; many Genii regard zombie Orphans as actually the worst kind of Vital if the Wonder that became it was powerful enough, as it doesn't comprehend stopping. Zombie Orphans cannot have an Intelligence or Manipulation higher than 1, nor do they have [Virtue] or [Vice]; they just don't have the proper emotions.<br /> <br /> <b>Animal: </b>The Orphan may not be able to talk, but it has a personality. An animal Orphan has well and truly developed a mature ability to think, if not precisely reason; on a raw intelligence scale, it's developed the brain power of a very smart dog or perhaps a dumb chimpanzee. It isn't capable of discussing philosophy, but it has an answer to the meaning of life; eat, remain safe, sleep, breed, repeat. Some Genii wonder what the difference between this and a zombie Wonder actually is, all of whom have never owned a pet; animals may not decide on much beyond where their next meal comes from, but they're quite capable of exercising judgement, gauging a situation for danger, or learning from experience; an animal Orphan who escapes Vital hunters will remember what they look like, and the tactics they used. The good (or perhaps awful, if one lacks Animal Ken) news is that Orphans are domesticated by default; as creations of humans, they do not inherently fear hominids and will react well to being treated nicely. Then again, wild dogs have been known to eat people precisely because they don't fear them. Animal Orphans cannot have an Intelligence greater than 2, but some Wonders originally meant for gauging social situations can have a Manipulation up to 4; instinct is a crafty thing in social animals.<br /> <br /> <b>Sentient: </b>Both the most and least dangerous of the Vital, sentient Orphans are capable of communicative cognizance and the full capacity for logical thought. That doesn't make them smart, but if every Intelligence 1 person was a complete moron, people would stop hiring them as muscle due to forgetting what they were doing in the middle of their jobs. No, sentient Orphans have that lethal combination of instinct plus the ability to have ideas that aren't bound by dumb instinct, one that is still largely motivated by finding food and shelter. Which is to say, they aren't inherently alien to humans, though a sentient ray gun is going to have rather different priorities than a domestic servant bot, simply because that's how it's built and what it can do. Thus, it's not actually that easy to communicate with the more alien Orphans (to some solitary Vital, it's quite possible they only understand language as &quot;big humanoid things make noises at each other, change behavior&quot; without getting <i>why</i>-they've never had to come up with a language of their own), but it's entirely possible to talk to one if one gets the concept of talking (insert sidebar for &quot;Teaching Language to the Speechless&quot; here), and from there come up with a deal that benefits all sides. Of course, that also means sentient Orphans can network with others not of their own &quot;species&quot;; anyone who's multilingual has pulled off a similar trick. There are no particular limits on the Attributes of sentient Orphans, though many of the less humanoid ones have bizarre Skills due to their nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T15:20:01-08:00","id":1034281,"title":"","content":"What if there were options for an endgame similar to finding/building your Hell in Demon, but with more mechanical guidance? As it is, I think Genius lacks purpose. You can't go back to the life of a regular scientist now that you are Inspired, so what do you do with the power you've been given? Just mope around and lash out when mere mortals break your toys?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T17:11:44-08:00","id":1034335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1034281#post1034281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if there were options for an endgame similar to finding/building your Hell in Demon, but with more mechanical guidance? As it is, I think Genius lacks purpose. You can't go back to the life of a regular scientist now that you are Inspired, so what do you do with the power you've been given? Just mope around and lash out when mere mortals break your toys?</div> </div> </div> </div>That was going to be what I wanted Magnum Opus to eventually be. The Genius's vision of the world made manifest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T17:24:06-08:00","id":1034343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1034335#post1034335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was going to be what I wanted Magnum Opus to eventually be. The Genius's vision of the world made manifest.</div> </div> </div> </div> It's an excellent idea, but we could use some rules for actually getting there. IIRC, Imperial Mysteries and the Demon Storyteller's Guide have rules for something like this. Perhaps we could use that as inspiration?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 01-18-2017, 08:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T18:35:25-08:00","id":1034382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1012271#post1012271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think we <i>need</i> Geniuses to be more powerful, though. They are on even or near-even footing with Mages as it stands.</div> </div> </div> </div>If anything they need to be less powerful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6783-notanautomaton","name":"notanautomaton","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T19:02:34-08:00","id":1034398,"title":"","content":"Sorry if this question has been answered somewhere else, but is there someplace where I can see all the compiled materials at the moment?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11554-fate-inker","name":"Fate Inker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T11:16:35-08:00","id":1034732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fate Inker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1034398#post1034398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry if this question has been answered somewhere else, but is there someplace where I can see all the compiled materials at the moment?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's not much actually compiled as of yet. <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B5D9AgFEhGZ3S1otbU13YlFoRlk/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Here is a link to the rough Wonder design rules</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T19:37:56-08:00","id":1035008,"title":"","content":"What would a typical game of Genius look like in 2ED? The sample Chronicles from the book are all over the place. In the official gamelines, you have mechanics which encourage a certain type of gameplay. Arcane Experiences motivate you to investigate Mysteries, Cover Experiences are earned when you make an effort to live according to your human identity, and so on. How would you earn Wondrous Experiences, and what type of gameplay are they meant to encourage?<br /> <br /> Also, I would rather let Geniuses keep using Virtue and Vice, and have the Magnum Opus and Delusion work as special Aspirations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T20:13:43-08:00","id":1035028,"title":"","content":"Vampire:<br /> Blood Bond and Ghouling encourages players to addict people to their blood and gain power from it. Additionally, each Clan has Disciplines that encourage them to play a certain kind of vampire, like Ventrue have Dominate, and so on. This encourages players to act like power-hungry vampires.<br /> <br /> This makes the basic game of Vampire easy to figure out; it's about trying to get and maintain power.<br /> <br /> Werewolf:<br /> Has extra mechanics for tracking someone by scent, hunting, and gives additional bonuses for pack formation. Additionally, maintaining loci health/altering loci is a thing, though it's not entirely mechanized. This encourages players to make a pack, hunt and control territory.<br /> <br /> This makes the base game for werewolf easy to figure out; you hunt and control territory.<br /> <br /> Mage:<br /> You get xp from finding out weird supernatural stuff, and have an additional Aspiration related to the supernatural. It also has an additional system for discovering more about weird supernatural stuff, and a larger, more dynamic system for spellcasting. This encourages players to run around trying to solve mysteries.<br /> <br /> This makes the base game of Mage easy to figure out; you run around solving mysteries and acting on obsessions.<br /> <br /> How does Genius encourage players to act like mad scientists? Does this make the base game easy to figure out? What is the base game, ie, if I'm ST'ing Genius, what's the first basic idea that pops into my head when it comes time to design a campaign, like politics for Vampire, control a territory and hunt shit for Werewolf, and investigate supernatural stuff for Mage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6783-notanautomaton","name":"notanautomaton","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T14:44:36-08:00","id":1035842,"title":"","content":"I say we nix buying Axioms for characters entirely, instead having Wonders buy Axioms in Wonder creation. So you don't buy Katastrofi and then get the ability to build ray-guns, you spend xp on one specific ray-gun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6783-notanautomaton","name":"notanautomaton","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T14:57:56-08:00","id":1035848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>notanautomaton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1035842#post1035842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I say we nix buying Axioms for characters entirely, instead having Wonders buy Axioms in Wonder creation. So you don't buy Katastrofi and then get the ability to build ray-guns, you spend xp on one specific ray-gun.</div> </div> </div> </div> If there are no Axioms, how do we establish limits for what characters can build?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T15:44:30-08:00","id":1035867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1035848#post1035848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If there are no Axioms, how do we establish limits for what characters can build?</div> </div> </div> </div>XP costs and... I'm not sure what to call them. Fractions? Paradigms? Properties? Fields of Study? Basically, make xp costs rather expensive for the high-tier stuff. Then you can gain additional things like 'cyrogenics' or 'weather control,' or whatever Then whenever you build something that takes advantage of that a Field, the xp is reduced.<br /> <br /> So then a Genius can build tech that's a little better than normal pretty easily, but when they want FTL or a death ray that can destroy a city, they have to pay through the nose. So either you can have a large number of weak Wonders, one great big wonder, or something in between, unless you're taking advantage of your Field, in which case you get the ability to have a greater number of devices.<br /> <br /> Also keep in mind that that one of the things that I have in mind is making the Havoc rules much harsher, so you can loose your great big Wonder more easily, especially if its effects can be noticed as abnormal by muggles.<br /> <br /> Additionally, I'm thinking about changing it so that Funding is the fuel stat rather than Mania, so that your great big Wonder is expensive and hurts to lose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6783-notanautomaton","name":"notanautomaton","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T21:29:18-08:00","id":1035946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>notanautomaton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1035867#post1035867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">XP costs and... I'm not sure what to call them. Fractions? Paradigms? Properties? Fields of Study?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been calling them &quot;Postulates,&quot; with &quot;Fields&quot; being the groups the Postulates are placed in. For example, a Field of Parachronics concerned with temporal stuff, that might include a Time Travel Postulate (Skafoi), a Time Control Postulate (Epikrato), a Time Window Postulate (Apokalypsi), etc. The Fields provide the subject being dealt with, and the Axioms act as the lens through which the subject is viewed, giving the Postulate as the resulting application.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Basically, make xp costs rather expensive for the high-tier stuff. Then you can gain additional things like 'cyrogenics' or 'weather control,' or whatever Then whenever you build something that takes advantage of that a Field, the xp is reduced. </div> </div> </div>Eh...I'm actually not a huge fan of Wonders costing XP directly anymore.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So then a Genius can build tech that's a little better than normal pretty easily, but when they want FTL or a death ray that can destroy a city, they have to pay through the nose. So either you can have a large number of weak Wonders, one great big wonder, or something in between, unless you're taking advantage of your Field, in which case you get the ability to have a greater number of devices. </div> </div> </div>Well, in the new structure, Axiomata work more like a Werewolf's Renown than like a Mage's Arcana. Raising an Axiom's rating makes your maximum effects more potent, but the actual capabilities of Wonders you make are all coming from the Postulates you know.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also keep in mind that that one of the things that I have in mind is making the Havoc rules much harsher, so you can loose your great big Wonder more easily, especially if its effects can be noticed as abnormal by muggles. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, more outlandish Wonders would be more prone to Havoc. Especially if you're Renegade or you decide to cheap out on the components.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Additionally, I'm thinking about changing it so that Funding is the fuel stat rather than Mania, so that your great big Wonder is expensive and hurts to lose. </div> </div> </div>No, I don't like that. One of the biggest annoyances in Genius (in my opinion) is the presence of a concrete concern of funding. I'd rather make the building of the Wonder an entirely (or almost entirely) roleplaying-based concern. You aren't spending 5 points of Money, you're knocking over material science labs for monoatomic filament wire and hunting the denizens of the Hidden Neanderthal Valley Bardo for their brains.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":4488,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","user":"malonkey1","date":". 01-22-2017, 12:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T22:58:34-08:00","id":1035968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1035946#post1035946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> No, I don't like that. One of the biggest annoyances in Genius (in my opinion) is the presence of a concrete concern of funding. I'd rather make the building of the Wonder an entirely (or almost entirely) roleplaying-based concern. You aren't spending 5 points of Money, you're knocking over material science labs for monoatomic filament wire and hunting the denizens of the Hidden Neanderthal Valley Bardo for their brains.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Funding wouldn't directly translate into Resources. So you could get Funding by building the tools to build the tools, knocking over a research lab, raiding a junkyard or Bardo, whatever. However, it all translates into how much Funding you can get, like how Mage doesn't care if you got Mana from an Artifact, a Hollow, or pattern scourging.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6783-notanautomaton","name":"notanautomaton","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T06:33:56-08:00","id":1036036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>notanautomaton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1035968#post1035968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, Funding wouldn't directly translate into Resources. So you could get Funding by building the tools to build the tools, knocking over a research lab, raiding a junkyard or Bardo, whatever. However, it all translates into how much Funding you can get, like how Mage doesn't care if you got Mana from an Artifact, a Hollow, or pattern scourging.</div> </div> </div> </div>But then that leaves the problem of having two separate systems that represent the same thing. Resources exist as the system to represent things like funding, we don't need to adapt the Fuel Stat to do that. Don't hammer nails with a wrench when you have a perfectly good hammer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T06:37:23-08:00","id":1036038,"title":"","content":"Been following this thread awhile. If you need a fuel stat for Geniuses then I might suggest &quot;Mania&quot; which is what allows them to burn the midnight oil building things while normal folks are taking naps.<br /> <br /> As malonkey mentions, money pretty well covered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T16:56:10-08:00","id":1036340,"title":"","content":"I think the Dresden Files RPG uses this, but: What about when you build a Wonder, you roll Resources (or Funding, or whatever) against some target. Succeed? Great, you were able to secure the necessary supplies, or already have them on hand in the lab/garage. Fail? You need to take story time to actually get them. Be they plutonium, or Albino Yeti brains or whatever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T18:40:46-08:00","id":1036392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1036340#post1036340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Dresden Files RPG uses this, but: What about when you build a Wonder, you roll Resources (or Funding, or whatever) against some target. Succeed? Great, you were able to secure the necessary supplies, or already have them on hand in the lab/garage. Fail? You need to take story time to actually get them. Be they plutonium, or Albino Yeti brains or whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I think that could be a perfectly valid alternate rule/hack, but I think I'd rather have the component gathering by default, at least in my own opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T04:00:54-08:00","id":1036527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1036392#post1036392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, I think that could be a perfectly valid alternate rule/hack, but I think I'd rather have the component gathering by default, at least in my own opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, the amount of time (or even the requirement) would vary by table. Still, I think there should be [ I]some[/I] kind of resource requiement (be it through Resources, Allies, skill checks like Computers to represent electronic fraud, etc.) simply because &quot;I needed the money&quot; seems important to some/many mad scientist stories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T06:58:22-08:00","id":1036590,"title":"","content":"Does anybody have the ideas in this thread tidied up nicely somewhere? Or at least their personal or favorite vision on the 2E update? We all could use a summary about now. There's quite a lot of ideas left simmering in the 34 pages here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T08:39:17-08:00","id":1036655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1036590#post1036590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anybody have the ideas in this thread tidied up nicely somewhere? Or at least their personal or favorite vision on the 2E update? We all could use a summary about now. There's quite a lot of ideas left simmering in the 34 pages here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll get to compiling all this stuff in a publicly visible document this evening after I'm done with classes. I needed to get this all put together anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T01:56:46-08:00","id":1037089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1036655#post1036655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'll get to compiling all this stuff in a publicly visible document this evening after I'm done with classes. I needed to get this all put together anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Much thanks in advance. Maybe I'll finally be able to contribute, after becoming able to compare my mental notes with that of others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T19:21:38-08:00","id":1038188,"title":"","content":"Many of my points from my previous <a href=\"http://\u200bhttp://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1016026#post1016026\" target=\"_blank\">post</a> about the matter of Funding still apply, although I'm going to revamp that into a new model I'll call Budgets. Instead of being a Merit-like subsystem Budgets could be represented by special Conditions, much like the Catalyst Conditions or Demon Agenda Conditions. For the system to be viable it will have to integrate with different mechanics but be simple to use.<br /> <br /> a) it should be optional for the player if they even need a Budget. They are not required for Wonder creation per sae, although Budgets can negate penalties and achieve a basic success in the result of failure in Wonder creation.<br /> b) as a special Condition, the Budget will have an always active minor boon and drawback whenever the Budget is active. You earn a Beat from meeting the struggles to maintain the Budget and can resolve it once per Story for potent effects.<br /> c) Budgets can be redefined between stories, indicative of setting and network changes in the Chronicle.<br /> d) Budgets are stackable for two key reasons; their effective rating increases the boon of their perk and also serve as a Touchstone for Breaking Point pluses and minuses along the Integrity/Obligation 2.0 meter<br /> <br /> A Budget could be gotten from role-play or a dice roll much like how Clues are generated in 2E Chronicles of Darkness. At the end of a sequence dedicated to showing how a Genius goes about gathering materials and requirements for their inventing, a special roll is designated. Much like the Elements of Clues, the effective stacks of the Budget are gotten from what played into the results of the roll. +1 for exceptional success, +1 for skill expertise (4+ rating), +1 for specialty, and +1 for meeting an Aspiration, amongst other criteria.<br /> <br /> To me it's fitting to have some kind of special system for how a Genius goes about setting a Budget. To answer the earlier question of &quot;<i>what does a Genius do?&quot; </i>in regards to gameplay and storytelling, I would say for Geniuses they are striving <b>for the means to work their Inspiration.</b> They are trying to establish livelihoods and do everything they can to get their invention, their great visions to work in spite of all the risks, Faults, Havoc and failures predisposed towards creations of Mania. I know one of the original themes of the game, the Mood of 'Bitter Disappoint' is not a popular one. When taken to the extreme it suggests that Genuises will always fail, which is not a desirable circumstance for any character let alone the player choosing to join a game of Genius. The bitterness is there to make the success all the more sweeter when it happens, when the Genius can look back at what it took them to accomplish.<br /> <br /> No one said creating a Wonder would be easy. Of course, you want your Wonder to do preciously what you anticipated but it's still going to be shackled with Faults, it will still be prone to Havoc. It caps your effective Mania unless you go the Kitbashing route and take the time to rebuild it every scene. And if having to navigate hoops to make your clone servitor or awesome gadget feels likes its too much, go ahead and commit the worst Transgression you can think of. You'll get a juicy Wonder empowering Larvae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T06:25:26-08:00","id":1038376,"title":"","content":"Thoughts on Wonders, Axioms, and fields. (might be duplicated - need to review)<br /> <br /> What about defining what a wonder is and can do by the intersection of Axiom (what something does) and Field (what something applies to). Examples:<ul><li>Say you have the Field of Necronics (Ghosts, basically).<ul><li>With Katastrofi, you can damage/destroy ghostly things, things about ghosts (Essence, Anchors, etc.), and/or damage things <i>with</i> ghosts (replicating a ghost Blast Numina, for example). Katastrofi Rank (and/or Postulates?) determine the degree of the effect, but the field limits it to Ghostly stuff - it can't affect Spirits or Goetia, and a Ghost Shield spell (or similar effect) would protect against attacks, just as if it came from ghosts.</li> </ul></li> <li>Field - Biotics<ul><li>With Exelixi, you can restore/improve biological things, but not mechanical. With Apokalypsi, you can scan lifeforms (and for lifeforms), but not other subject material.</li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> If you want broad, does/affects anything Wonders, you load up on fields. If you want powerful specialists, you take a few fields, but dive deep into the Axioms. The final results/effects can be negotiated with ST, given guidelines (if you can figure out how to make an Economics+Katastofi weapon work, good for you).<br /> <br /> It isn't quite the dramatic power increase Geist 1E gets out of a similar system, since you still have to actually build Wonders to exploit the options open to you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T09:17:31-08:00","id":1038444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1038376#post1038376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thoughts on Wonders, Axioms, and fields. (might be duplicated - need to review)<br /> <br /> What about defining what a wonder is and can do by the intersection of Axiom (what something does) and Field (what something applies to). Examples:<ul><li>Say you have the Field of Necronics (Ghosts, basically).<ul><li>With Katastrofi, you can damage/destroy ghostly things, things about ghosts (Essence, Anchors, etc.), and/or damage things <i>with</i> ghosts (replicating a ghost Blast Numina, for example). Katastrofi Rank (and/or Postulates?) determine the degree of the effect, but the field limits it to Ghostly stuff - it can't affect Spirits or Goetia, and a Ghost Shield spell (or similar effect) would protect against attacks, just as if it came from ghosts.</li> </ul></li> <li>Field - Biotics<ul><li>With Exelixi, you can restore/improve biological things, but not mechanical. With Apokalypsi, you can scan lifeforms (and for lifeforms), but not other subject material.</li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> <br /> If you want broad, does/affects anything Wonders, you load up on fields. If you want powerful specialists, you take a few fields, but dive deep into the Axioms. The final results/effects can be negotiated with ST, given guidelines (if you can figure out how to make an Economics+Katastofi weapon work, good for you).<br /> <br /> It isn't quite the dramatic power increase Geist 1E gets out of a similar system, since you still have to actually build Wonders to exploit the options open to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's sort of similar to the system I had in mind. Basically, there are the Fields, which are broken into Postulates keyed to Axiomata (sort of like Werewolf Gifts are broken up into Facets keyed to Renowns). So you could have your Necrotics Field, and it would have the (example) Postulates:<ul><li><b>Apokalypsi (Spectral Sensor):</b> You can create Wonders that can detect and analyze ghosts and ghostly phenomena.</li> <li><b>Epikrato (Ectoplasmic Manipulation):</b> You can create Wonders that can control ghosts and the flow of Essence.</li> <li><b>Exelixi (Plasmic Regenerator):</b> You can create Wonders that temporarily raise a Ghost's Rank.</li> <li><b>Katastrofi (Necro-Disentanglement):</b> You can create Wonders that can sever a Ghost from its Anchors and remove Possessing and Claiming ghosts.</li> <li><b>Prostasia (Ecto-Containment):</b> You can create Wonders that ward off or contain Ghosts.</li> <li><b>Skafoi (Keymaster):</b> You can create Wonders that open or close Avernian Gates.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T09:38:03-08:00","id":1038452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1038444#post1038444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's sort of similar to the system I had in mind. Basically, there are the Fields, which are broken into Postulates keyed to Axiomata (sort of like Werewolf Gifts are broken up into Facets keyed to Renowns). So you could have your Necrotics Field, and it would have the (example) Postulates:<ul><li><b>Apokalypsi (Spectral Sensor):</b> You can create Wonders that can detect and analyze ghosts and ghostly phenomena.</li> <li><b>Epikrato (Ectoplasmic Manipulation):</b> You can create Wonders that can control ghosts and the flow of Essence.</li> <li><b>Exelixi (Plasmic Regenerator):</b> You can create Wonders that temporarily raise a Ghost's Rank.</li> <li><b>Katastrofi (Necro-Disentanglement):</b> You can create Wonders that can sever a Ghost from its Anchors and remove Possessing and Claiming ghosts.</li> <li><b>Prostasia (Ecto-Containment):</b> You can create Wonders that ward off or contain Ghosts.</li> <li><b>Skafoi (Keymaster):</b> You can create Wonders that open or close Avernian Gates.</li> </ul><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, like that, but with more effects within each Axiom. For Example, with Katastofi, not just severing Ghost from Anchors (likely removing the Conditions), but also depleting Ghost Essence, or blasting people with raw ghost-stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T06:57:03-08:00","id":1038867,"title":"","content":"What are people's thoughts on this take for Wonders and Havoc:<br /> <br /> Wonders and their affects can be largely grouped into 3 categories - Advanced, Hyper-tech, and Paranatural [Terms subject to revision]<br /> <b>Advanced</b> Wonders are those like you might see existing in a few decades time, or in certain Hard Sci-Fi. It isn't possible now, but nothing indicates it might not eventually be. Though still subject to Havoc, it is only triggered under in depth analysis and manipulation by Uninspired. Just because Inspiration showed you how to build a compact plasma battery to power it, doesn't mean you labelled things properly or put in safeties. The effects of Havoc are usually limited to the Wonder falling apart, or at worst blowing up. These are very useful for Research, since they are mostly/entirely &quot;real&quot;, just poorly understood.<br /> <b>Hyper-tech</b> Wonders are those so advanced they can scarcely be comprehended. Their effects maybe, but how they work? You might see examples in Soft Sci-Fi. Still, more into the category of &quot;Well, physics doesn't say it is outright <i>impossible</i> yet...&quot;. These are vulnerable to Havoc even from someone Uninspired touching or performing basic analysis upon them. When even the Genius doesn't rightly know how their Accelerated Regeneration Serum works, X-Rays or an uncalibrated electromagnetic field (like another person's touch) might trigger odd behavior. The effects of Havoc <i>sometimes</i> render the Wonder inert, but most Genii aren't quite that lucky. These still have some Research value, as <i>something</i> in them is grounded in actual reality (even if in the more occult depth of the pool).<br /> <b>Paranatural</b> Wonders are those that make physicists/biologists/etc. cry. They flagrantly violate physical laws, and the Genius's best explanations of how they work fully earn them the &quot;Time-cube crackpot&quot; moniker. The best Inspired researchers have been able to explain their operation/existence is through some <i>extremely</i> loose interpretation of Many Worlds phenomenon and overlapping realities and their laws. These are <i>exceptionally</i> vulnerable to Havoc - even the slight effect of an Observer running the <i>correct</i> calculations of what should be going on can collapse the quantum BS waveform that enables it to work. Blowing up is often the best case scenario - extra-dimensional/temporal intelligences <i>have</i> been known to co-opt such Wonders before. Their research value is more &quot;well, <i>some</i> reality might work this way, but ours sure doesn't&quot;. NOTE to Paragons: Don't use these unless absolutely necessary - they break Integrity as casually as they do physics, and a passel of Beholden is the last thing the Peerage needs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 01-28-2017, 08:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T11:59:43-08:00","id":1046871,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4488_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4488\" data-vbnamecard=\"4488\">malonkey1</a> I could try writing up Biotics, but before, I need to ask what should the Potency of Automata Wonders determine? Rank of appropriate Horror? Rating of appropriate Retainer, as Golem and that Death Weaving spell that raises zombies?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum