e Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-11T08:46:49-08:00","id":1047240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tambov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1046871#post1046871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4488_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4488\" data-vbnamecard=\"4488\">malonkey1</a> I could try writing up Biotics, but before, I need to ask what should the Potency of Automata Wonders determine? Rank of appropriate Horror? Rating of appropriate Retainer, as Golem and that Death Weaving spell that raises zombies?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much, yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-11T09:21:47-08:00","id":1047261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1047240#post1047240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pretty much, yeah.</div> </div> </div> </div>Horror Rank or Retainer Rating?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-11T11:19:29-08:00","id":1047326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tambov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1047261#post1047261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Horror Rank or Retainer Rating?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably Horror Rank for anything intended to injure things, but otherwise Retainer Rank.<br /> <br /> So Death-Borg 8000 would be a Horror with Rank equal to Potency (and you could probably Reach for more), but C3PO would be a Retainer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T08:24:40-08:00","id":1047711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1047326#post1047326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Probably Horror Rank for anything intended to injure things, but otherwise Retainer Rank.<br /> <br /> So Death-Borg 8000 would be a Horror with Rank equal to Potency (and you could probably Reach for more), but C3PO would be a Retainer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh. I got it. How about this:<br /> Base: Potency=Retainer<br /> +2 Reach: Potency=Horror Rank?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T14:38:40-08:00","id":1047894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tambov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1047711#post1047711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh. I got it. How about this:<br /> Base: Potency=Retainer<br /> +2 Reach: Potency=Horror Rank?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it is more Potency(?) = Retainer dots/Horror Potency, but if you want (and are suicidally crazy) you can always add more power to your Death-bot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T19:45:16-08:00","id":1048040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1047894#post1047894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it is more Potency(?) = Retainer dots/Horror Potency, but if you want (and are suicidally crazy) you can always add more power to your Death-bot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct.<br /> <br /> Basically, you can make your Killbot with Rank up to your Automata rank, and you can Reach for Advanced Potency to add even more if you can make the extra Reach with Axiom Rank, or you're willing to take the extra Havoc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T09:27:25-08:00","id":1048277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1048040#post1048040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Correct.<br /> <br /> Basically, you can make your Killbot with Rank up to your Automata rank, and you can Reach for Advanced Potency to add even more if you can make the extra Reach with Axiom Rank, or you're willing to take the extra Havoc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. Havoc is triggered, though (and any mechanic for &quot;Reach&quot; hasn't been established). What about increasing the Core Modifier by adding additional Faults? And pre-existing Faults penalize Havoc rolls (as well as bringing the Wonder closer to Terminal Havoc by possessing too many Faults)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T10:33:28-08:00","id":1048309,"title":"","content":"Guys.<br /> <br /> Potency=Retainer means a Potency 1 Automaton's highest dice pool is 2 die.<br /> Potency=Rank means a Potency 1 Automaton has similar stats to a starting character.<br /> There's a big difference between the two. Horror Rank is much stronger.<br /> <br /> Also, if your Killbot 8000 requires Reach, you can spend less Reach on making it actually smart, unlike C-3PO.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T12:37:22-08:00","id":1048383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tambov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1048309#post1048309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guys.<br /> <br /> Potency=Retainer means a Potency 1 Automaton's highest dice pool is 2 die.<br /> Potency=Rank means a Potency 1 Automaton has similar stats to a starting character.<br /> There's a big difference between the two. Horror Rank is much stronger.<br /> <br /> Also, if your Killbot 8000 requires Reach, you can spend less Reach on making it actually smart, unlike C-3PO.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright, hang on, you're right, there.<br /> <br /> Okay. So with that in mind, it make make more sense to have all independent Automata be Retainers by default, and make Horror status require Reach. What do you guys think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T14:01:05-08:00","id":1048413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1048383#post1048383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Alright, hang on, you're right, there.<br /> <br /> Okay. So with that in mind, it make make more sense to have all independent Automata be Retainers by default, and make Horror status require Reach. What do you guys think?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd think it would depend on what you are making - an automaton to compile and analyze news feeds for interesting events is just a Retainer with something like Streetwise, while an attack drone/beast/plant should probably be modeled with actual combat stats.<br /> <br /> What about using the Brief Nightmares rules? Automata are mostly Minions, in numbers a Horde, and only &quot;Lone Terrors&quot; (or using full Horror rules) when a Genius sinks major time and effort into them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T17:22:00-08:00","id":1048491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1048413#post1048413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd think it would depend on what you are making - an automaton to compile and analyze news feeds for interesting events is just a Retainer with something like Streetwise, while an attack drone/beast/plant should probably be modeled with actual combat stats.<br /> <br /> What about using the Brief Nightmares rules? Automata are mostly Minions, in numbers a Horde, and only &quot;Lone Terrors&quot; (or using full Horror rules) when a Genius sinks major time and effort into them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright. As I was afraid of, Automaton rules are going to have to be (at least slightly) more complicated than other Wonders. I wanted to avoid that, but it doesn't seem possible.<br /> <br /> Still it's gonna be simpler than 1E Automata, though. I'll go and play around with some ideas and come back with something more solid to pick at.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T18:19:50-08:00","id":1048514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1048491#post1048491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Alright. As I was afraid of, Automaton rules are going to have to be (at least slightly) more complicated than other Wonders. I wanted to avoid that, but it doesn't seem possible.<br /> <br /> Still it's gonna be simpler than 1E Automata, though. I'll go and play around with some ideas and come back with something more solid to pick at.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, with grafting and Integrated Wonders, all Automata needs to do is provide the creature base to stick other Wonders on. If you are building a robo-dog, just take a dog, and modify from there - Automata is merely what lets you do so. Look at the Hellhounds Exploit - it slaps the Cryptid template on an animal. Automata could be like that, but in reverse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T19:51:42-08:00","id":1048545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1048514#post1048514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, with grafting and Integrated Wonders, all Automata needs to do is provide the creature base to stick other Wonders on. If you are building a robo-dog, just take a dog, and modify from there - Automata is merely what lets you do so. Look at the Hellhounds Exploit - it slaps the Cryptid template on an animal. Automata could be like that, but in reverse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's what I was thinking. I also thought there'd be three basic types of automata:<ul><li>Lares: Retainer-type Automata. Potency = Retainer Rating. Multi-purpose but not very good for murder.</li> <li>Legionarii: Minion or Horde-type Nightmares, only good for one task, but easy to mass-produce without too much extra cost.</li> <li>Miraculi: Horrors (Potency equals, uh, Potency). Powerful. Dangerous. Havoc = rebellion, probably patricide.</li> </ul><br /> Different Postulates could make different kinds of Automata (for example, you might have one that can create armies of shambling corpses, and a different one for making a sentient computer virus).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T18:07:21-08:00","id":1060715,"title":"","content":"This thread hasn't seen any activity in a while.<br /> <br /> I might as well bump with a question: have we reached any consensus on how 2ED will treat the various antagonists?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-10T05:44:27-08:00","id":1060831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1060715#post1060715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This thread hasn't seen any activity in a while.<br /> <br /> I might as well bump with a question: have we reached any consensus on how 2ED will treat the various antagonists?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think we have. I've been hit with a lot of projects for college lately.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-10T06:17:12-08:00","id":1060839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1038867#post1038867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are people's thoughts on this take for Wonders and Havoc:<br /> <br /> Wonders and their affects can be largely grouped into 3 categories - Advanced, Hyper-tech, and Paranatural [Terms subject to revision]<br /> <b>Advanced</b> Wonders are those like you might see existing in a few decades time, or in certain Hard Sci-Fi. It isn't possible now, but nothing indicates it might not eventually be. Though still subject to Havoc, it is only triggered under in depth analysis and manipulation by Uninspired. Just because Inspiration showed you how to build a compact plasma battery to power it, doesn't mean you labelled things properly or put in safeties. The effects of Havoc are usually limited to the Wonder falling apart, or at worst blowing up. These are very useful for Research, since they are mostly/entirely &quot;real&quot;, just poorly understood.<br /> <b>Hyper-tech</b> Wonders are those so advanced they can scarcely be comprehended. Their effects maybe, but how they work? You might see examples in Soft Sci-Fi. Still, more into the category of &quot;Well, physics doesn't say it is outright <i>impossible</i> yet...&quot;. These are vulnerable to Havoc even from someone Uninspired touching or performing basic analysis upon them. When even the Genius doesn't rightly know how their Accelerated Regeneration Serum works, X-Rays or an uncalibrated electromagnetic field (like another person's touch) might trigger odd behavior. The effects of Havoc <i>sometimes</i> render the Wonder inert, but most Genii aren't quite that lucky. These still have some Research value, as <i>something</i> in them is grounded in actual reality (even if in the more occult depth of the pool).<br /> <b>Paranatural</b> Wonders are those that make physicists/biologists/etc. cry. They flagrantly violate physical laws, and the Genius's best explanations of how they work fully earn them the &quot;Time-cube crackpot&quot; moniker. The best Inspired researchers have been able to explain their operation/existence is through some <i>extremely</i> loose interpretation of Many Worlds phenomenon and overlapping realities and their laws. These are <i>exceptionally</i> vulnerable to Havoc - even the slight effect of an Observer running the <i>correct</i> calculations of what should be going on can collapse the quantum BS waveform that enables it to work. Blowing up is often the best case scenario - extra-dimensional/temporal intelligences <i>have</i> been known to co-opt such Wonders before. Their research value is more &quot;well, <i>some</i> reality might work this way, but ours sure doesn't&quot;. NOTE to Paragons: Don't use these unless absolutely necessary - they break Integrity as casually as they do physics, and a passel of Beholden is the last thing the Peerage needs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never got the chance to say it but I love this idea. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-10T08:18:34-08:00","id":1060887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1060715#post1060715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This thread hasn't seen any activity in a while.<br /> <br /> I might as well bump with a question: have we reached any consensus on how 2ED will treat the various antagonists?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, let's see if we can identify them first:<ul><li>Other Genii<ul><li>Rogues (Rivals)</li> <li>Lemuria (Opposing Faction)</li> <li>Illuminated (<b><sup><sub>GRIMDARK</sub></sup></b> Mirrors)</li> </ul></li> <li>Manes (Wandering Monster)</li> <li>Clockstoppers (Anti-type Nemesis)</li> <li>Cold Ones (Eldritch Horror)</li> <li>Reality/Yourself (Sun to Icarus's Wings)</li> </ul>Any others people can thing of?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-10T11:52:46-08:00","id":1060964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1060887#post1060887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well, let's see if we can identify them first:<ul><li>Other Genii<ul><li>Rogues (Rivals)</li> <li>Lemuria (Opposing Faction)</li> <li>Illuminated (<b><sup><sub>GRIMDARK</sub></sup></b> Mirrors)</li> </ul></li> <li>Manes (Wandering Monster)</li> <li>Clockstoppers (Anti-type Nemesis)</li> <li>Cold Ones (Eldritch Horror)</li> <li>Reality/Yourself (Sun to Icarus's Wings)</li> </ul>Any others people can thing of?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been kicking around an idea I call &quot;Edisons.&quot;<br /> <br /> Basically, they're &quot;semi-inspired.&quot; They aren't Genii, but they can play with Mania and use Wonders without causing Havoc. But the thing that makes them dangerous is that they can reproduce Wonders they get their paws on without risking Havoc, and they don't have the social interaction problems of the Inspired. Some might kill Genii and steal their Wonders, but the more insidious ones might bankroll the Genius in their Wonder-Making, steal the Wonder, make millions, and leave the Inspired broke <i>at best</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-10T12:01:26-08:00","id":1060967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1060964#post1060964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been kicking around an idea I call &quot;Edisons.&quot;<br /> <br /> Basically, they're &quot;semi-inspired.&quot; They aren't Genii, but they can play with Mania and use Wonders without causing Havoc. But the thing that makes them dangerous is that they can reproduce Wonders they get their paws on without risking Havoc, and they don't have the social interaction problems of the Inspired. Some might kill Genii and steal their Wonders, but the more insidious ones might bankroll the Genius in their Wonder-Making, steal the Wonder, make millions, and leave the Inspired broke <i>at best</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sounds <i>almost</i> like Beholden with a bit of willpower and ambition. Maybe a variant?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-10T12:08:31-08:00","id":1060969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1060967#post1060967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Sounds <i>almost</i> like Beholden with a bit of willpower and ambition. Maybe a variant?</div> </div> </div> </div>Conceivably. The idea is that they seem like useful allies for Genii, and some genuinely are, but there's always that chance that they'll stab you in the back, and never even give you that $50 grand he promised you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-10T12:09:45-08:00","id":1060971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1060969#post1060969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Conceivably. The idea is that they seem like useful allies for Genii, and some genuinely are, but there's always that chance that they'll stab you in the back, and never even give you that $50 grand he promised you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bastards. First the time travelling Nigerian Prince, and then them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-10T12:25:08-08:00","id":1060975,"title":"","content":"Ideas on Lemuria (2.0):<br /> <br /> After the organizational collapse following the defeat of the 9 Unknown Men at the conclusion of the Invisible War, Lemurian Baramins have repurposed to become less &quot;factions of the Illuminati&quot; and more &quot;Take over the World Hobbyist Clubs&quot;. Still, the deals, procedures, favors, and pawns that they were in charge of prior still means they are (sadly) the best placed to regulate some of the odder corners of the hidden Inspired world. Their scramble for money and influence on the way to World Domination, also means they more often have the cash to blow on laser-shark security systems than paying this month's lab electricity bills (yes, crime <i>does</i> pay, as long as you are fine with unmarked bills and dodging the IRS). Without the overriding &quot;One World Order&quot; plot, the Baramins get along far less well than they used to.<br /> <br /> <i>Genii join Lemuria</i>: to gain allies and co-conspirators for Taking Over The World (or at least your corner of the city). The different Baramins are great for making sure you can find like-minded individuals whose utopian visions don't conflict (too much) with yours. <br /> <br /> <i>Peers use Lemuria</i>: to deal with threats they don't have the manpower or time to handle. No matter how unrealistic you find the Atomist's goals, at least they can be relied upon to try and prevent anyone else from blowing up or controlling the world. Better the devils you know (at least until they try to &quot;mass uplift&quot; everyone with a nano-reassembler).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T01:23:57-08:00","id":1061165,"title":"","content":"How does Etherite Tesla fit there? He just wanted to spread his inventions and snog birds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T07:00:50-08:00","id":1061229,"title":"","content":"Idea for new Condition: True Believer. Condition can occur naturally among mortals and Inspired but all Unmada automatically receive one upon becoming one and must always have one attached to them. Phenomenologist grand could allow them to apply new True Believer Conditions to themselves at will or change blief of their True Bliever condition.<br /> Upon character gaining this Condition Storyteller and player should construct a belief character has about working of the world and assign mental skill to it.<br /> Effects: True Believer gets +1 bonus to interaction with Wonders and Manes that have matching working principal or aesthetic. Mundane True Believers do not trigger havoc checks on Wonders they gain bonus on. Believer may substitute Subtefuge skill checks that would rely on their belief to predetermined Mental Skill (Phenomenelogist who's belief is that Lemuria Rules the World could use Politics instead of Subterfuge to Con their way into high security facility, while Etherite could fast talk a person about ether using Science, and so on).<br /> Beat: Whenever inaccuracy of belief puts True Believer or their allies in danger.<br /> Resolution: When belief is proven beyond shadow of doubt to be wrong. Roll a breaking point with penalty. If True Believer was an Unmada they receive new True Beliver Condition but can have different belief accosiated with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T09:39:40-08:00","id":1061271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tambov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1061165#post1061165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does Etherite Tesla fit there? He just wanted to spread his inventions and snog birds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Never quite understood why he'd ever be in Lemuria. If he was, probably when they were doing their &quot;we're in charge, and you have to join us or be crushed&quot; phase.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T11:15:51-08:00","id":1061292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1061271#post1061271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Never quite understood why he'd ever be in Lemuria. If he was, probably when they were doing their &quot;we're in charge, and you have to join us or be crushed&quot; phase.</div> </div> </div> </div>He was deeply opposed to the theory of relativity. Ironically, Einstein himself spent much of his later years attempting to disprove quantum mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T06:11:35-07:00","id":1061798,"title":"","content":"Suppose this may sit as the extension of Mane threats to some extent, but I always wanted to play more with the threats that Bardos presented. Besides the strange metaphysics and hazardous environments within, you had the various denizens of a particular Bardo. That are generally treated as Manes when outside of it, although it can serve as an exotic backstory for any particular Inspired.<br /> <br /> Bardos require Mania to sustain, although normally these are 'closed off' and able to sustain themselves off of both disproven theories and fantasies and raw chaotic Mania storms, since they are purely abstract at this point. However, when a point of entry is discovered into a Bardo (from a Genius's discovery, wonder or creation, as an example) this delicate protection is lost. Not only can outsiders and Bardo denizens cross over the entry point, the Bardo begins losing Mania as it begins to undo itself when it comes into contact with the reality that serves to be contrary to the paradigms and aesthetics the Bardo runs on.<br /> <br /> What's a local Bardo populace to do? If they don't just turn over and take the end of their existence, or work out some support deals with the local Genii, there's always a simple answer. Invade reality to take its riches and Mania by force.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T08:33:11-07:00","id":1061833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1061798#post1061798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Suppose this may sit as the extension of Mane threats to some extent, but I always wanted to play more with the threats that Bardos presented. Besides the strange metaphysics and hazardous environments within, you had the various denizens of a particular Bardo. That are generally treated as Manes when outside of it, although it can serve as an exotic backstory for any particular Inspired.<br /> <br /> Bardos require Mania to sustain, although normally these are 'closed off' and able to sustain themselves off of both disproven theories and fantasies and raw chaotic Mania storms, since they are purely abstract at this point. However, when a point of entry is discovered into a Bardo (from a Genius's discovery, wonder or creation, as an example) this delicate protection is lost. Not only can outsiders and Bardo denizens cross over the entry point, the Bardo begins losing Mania as it begins to undo itself when it comes into contact with the reality that serves to be contrary to the paradigms and aesthetics the Bardo runs on.<br /> <br /> What's a local Bardo populace to do? If they don't just turn over and take the end of their existence, or work out some support deals with the local Genii, there's always a simple answer. Invade reality to take its riches and Mania by force.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You mean like the Martian Invasion?<br /> <hr /><br /> Thinking about Manes, would it make sense to have categories like I proposed for Wonders?<br /> <br /> <b>Variant</b> Manes are those with entirely plausible and real biology (even when they don't fit into any terrestrial line of descent). They arguably aren't even really &quot;Manes&quot; in the proper sense and don't need Mania to function. Human and near-Human inhabitants of Bardos and the very best mimicry Automata are examples.<br /> <b>Deviant</b> Manes are those that are mostly understandable... excepting the integral &quot;Wonders&quot; that define their particular biology. These require Mania to function as they are, but some can &quot;survive&quot; without it, albeit at the cost of their abilities. Many of the more common &quot;Mane species&quot; and Automata designed for hibernation are examples.<br /> <b>Extra-rational</b> Manes are those who can't even exist without the strange fluctuations and energies of Mania to give them life. Tulpas born of the worst cases of Unmada-ism, extra-dimensional/temporal intelligences from discarded or alien universes and timelines, or Automata designed with no regard for physics or biology (or, often, sanity) are prime examples.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T19:26:56-07:00","id":1062133,"title":"","content":"A straight up martian invasion is just one way of doing it. Invaders, as a loose descriptor for any Bardo populace aggressively raiding reality and Mania for their needs, could come from any conceivable Bardo location. To use some other examples from the original finished document:<br /> <br /> Invaders from the Gray Plateau of Tsoska would be running straight up political espionage, party infiltration and economic turnover to support the 'every poorly run empire magnified ten-fold' back home. Counter to denizens of The Grid mainly investing computer banks and servers, very rarely if ever able to manifest in areas with enough electronics. The Hollow Earth cracks open just enough and long extinct dinosaurs and early taxa try to reestablish themselves in the food chain.<br /> <br /> &quot;Invader&quot; as a term, is more about the antagonistic motives of a Bardo populace and doesn't mean only select groups or common methods are used. Much like the Huntsmen in Changeling 2E, they have a variety of motives and ways of getting what they need. Invading earth (mainly Genius institutions, or even other Bardos...) is born primarily from their desperation to continue an impossible existence, different than the Huntsmen's aims to end the hunt so they can return to non-existence.<br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> I know I haven't been around for awhile. While I can see the point of your earlier Wonder/Field distinctions I'm unsure if Manes need that amount of mechanical difference? There is a great majority of functional, paradigm, aesthetic and origin difference (Bardo native or Genius creation) to categorize Manes, almost as numerous as Spirits.<br /> <br /> The basics of Manes (although this is presented as a Merit in the 1.1 guide, in case of a Genius having it) is that they require 1 Mania per day to function outside of their Bardos and Manes also cause Havoc. I could see the most 'human, but not' Manes not even needing Mania. Or perhaps if Manes had other ways of leeching Mania from the environment as fitting their paradigm than just the Calculus Vampire merit.<br /> <br /> Although since the majority of Manes are presumed to be substantial (with a minority as Ephemeral, or technically Ephemeral when viewing their Bardo from the outside) perhaps Variants have either little Mania needs or have a bonus to resist Havoc, and then you have standard ones and any aforementioned Ephemeral manes so bizarre can can't even exist or manifest without Mania.<br /> <br /> Speaking of, should Manes have a Rank? Or just broad categories of template that is stylized differently when considering form and origins. Whether its a class of Manes that use Attributes and Skills or trait categories and such. Besides needing it to survive (or power native Bardo Wonders) would a Mane use Mania for anything else? Unless they Catalyze Manes aren't considered Geniuses (and that would cancel out the daily Mania a Genius gets anyways).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T20:03:55-07:00","id":1062146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1062133#post1062133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know I haven't been around for awhile. While I can see the point of your earlier Wonder/Field distinctions I'm unsure if Manes need that amount of mechanical difference? There is a great majority of functional, paradigm, aesthetic and origin difference (Bardo native or Genius creation) to categorize Manes, almost as numerous as Spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I don't think the Manes really need to have too much categorization beyond what's there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The basics of Manes (although this is presented as a Merit in the 1.1 guide, in case of a Genius having it) is that they require 1 Mania per day to function outside of their Bardos and Manes also cause Havoc. I could see the most 'human, but not' Manes not even needing Mania. Or perhaps if Manes had other ways of leeching Mania from the environment as fitting their paradigm than just the Calculus Vampire merit. </div> </div> </div>I think the rules on how much Mania a Mane requires should be more of a suggestion. Maybe make it so Manes have a store of Mania, but it drains when they suffer Havoc? So a smarter Mane could avoid directly interacting with Mortals and persist without a huge amount of trouble, but more alien or unintelligent Manes would have to be Mania-drainers.<br /> <br /> I was also thinking of changing Calculus Vampire from a Merit to a Dread Power.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Speaking of, should Manes have a Rank? Or just broad categories of template that is stylized differently when considering form and origins. Whether its a class of Manes that use Attributes and Skills or trait categories and such. Besides needing it to survive (or power native Bardo Wonders) would a Mane use Mania for anything else? Unless they Catalyze Manes aren't considered Geniuses (and that would cancel out the daily Mania a Genius gets anyways). </div> </div> </div>I think Manes will probably just be Nightmares for the most part, with Inspired Manes being Horrors with Inspiration equivalent to Rank.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T20:15:36-07:00","id":1065565,"title":"","content":"So, i'm new here. Just got done reading through the thread.<br /> <br /> I made a couple of sample fields and Inferences (calling them that cause Postulates just doesn't seem right). Got Necronics and some of Parachronics from previous posters. Sort of gave up making them when i started writing Psionics, especially the naming. so here you go:<br /> <br /> <b>Field of Necronics</b><br /> This Field is the study and manipulation of spectral beings and the Underworld. (May need to be broadened to the Field of Spectrology if need to be combined with Spirits and the Shadow as well)<br /> <b>Required Skill:</b> Occult<br /> <b>Infarences:</b><ul><li><b>Spectral Sensor (Apokalypsi):</b> Allows your Wonders to detect Ghosts and various Ghostly Phenomena (Haunts, Numina, their Power stat, Possession, Claiming, how much Essence they have, etc.)</li> <li><b>Ectoplasmic Manipulation (Epikrato):</b> You can create Wonders that can control ghosts and the flow of Essence.</li> <li><b>Plasmic Regenerator (Exilixi):</b> You can create Wonders that temporarily raise a Ghost's Rank or heal Ghostly Beings.</li> <li><b>Necro-Disentanglement (Katastrofi):</b> You can create Wonders that can sever a Ghost from its Anchors and remove Possessing and Claiming ghosts.</li> <li><b>Ectoplasmic Disintegrator (Katastrofi):</b> You can create Wonders that can harm Ghostly beings and objects. (May also harm Spirits if we decide Ghosts and Spirits require different Fields. May or may not have a special effect on Sin-Eaters, who are half-ghosts)</li> <li><b>Specter Cannon (Katastrofi): </b>You can create Wonders that replicate Ghostly attacks, they are defended as if they come from a Ghost of Rank (either Katastrofi or a fraction of Inspiration)</li> <li><b>Phaseshift Manipulator (Metaptropi):</b> You can create Wonders that turns the target intangible (May turn Ghosts and Sin-Eaters tangible, if Ghosts can do that naturally and if Sin-Eaters can turn Intangible, don\u2019t know enough about Geist to know for sure.)</li> <li><b>Ecto-Containment (Prostasia):</b> You can create Wonders that ward off or contain Ghosts.</li> <li><b>Keymaster (Skafoi):</b> You can create Wonders that open or close Avernian Gates.</li> </ul><br /> <b>Note</b>: Katastrofi was separated into three Inferences because otherwise it would be way too broad, I guess some of them can be removed if deemed too OP or unthematic. Don\u2019t know enough about Geist to know for sure. Sorry if some of these ones are bad.<br /> <br /> <b>Field of Parachronics </b><br /> This Field covers Time as a subject of study, manipulation, and, ultimately, a method of travel. Though Time Travel is indeed possible, it is often times hindered by the sporadic existence of the Time Police. <br /> <b>Required Skill:</b> Academics<br /> <b>Inferances:</b><ul><li><b>Chronoscopic Sensor (Apokalypsi):</b> Allows your Wonders to detect things that happen in the past or future. However, due to the turbulent and ever shifting nature of the future, it is far easier to see into the past. Efforts to see into the future lead to ever more sporadic results the farther you try to see. By default, this Inference can only reveal what mundane senses can, however, other Apokalypsi Inferences can modify this to an extent.</li> <li><b>Accelerated Mending (Exilixi):</b> Allows you to build Wonders that reduce the time required to regenerate wounds or repair objects or structure. May only work on self-repairing system. May require a supply of sustenance/material to allow it to function properly.</li> <li><b>Temporal Stasis Fields (Exilixi): </b>Allows you to build Wonders that put targets in a state of stasis, preventing them from being damaged or from a deteriorating condition while simultaneously preventing them from healing or acting in anyway.</li> <li><b>Entropic Decay (Katastrofi):</b> Allows you to build Wonders that accelerates aging on the target.</li> <li><b>Timescale Accelerator (Skafoi):</b> Allows you to build Wonders that either speeds up or slows down targets actions.</li> </ul><br /> <b>Obscure Inferences:</b><ul><li><b>Time Travel (Skafoi):</b> Allows you to build Wonders that allows for travel through time and to change the past. Due to the often-destructive results of such meddling, this Inference has been outlawed by the Peerage, on the penalty of death. Now that the Peerage has broken, there is nothing stopping a Genius from trying to change the past.</li> <li><b>Timeshift Stabilizer (Prostasia):</b> Allows you to build Wonders that protects the target from changes to the past.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>Field of Psionics</b><br /> This Field covers psychic powers and mental manipulation caused by any source.<br /> <b>Required Skill:</b><br /> <b>Inferences:</b><ul><li><b>Psionic Sensor (Apokalypsi):</b> Allows your Wonders to detect mental interference caused by outside sources. Be it from a Mind Mage, a Vampire using Dominate, Disquet, Lunacy, or other, similar powers.</li> <li><b>Mind Reading (Apokalypsi):</b> Allows your Wonders to view the memories and minds of others.</li> <li><b>Mind Control (Epikrato):</b> Allows you to build Wonders that Control others thoughts.</li> <li><b>Mental Repair (Exilixi):</b> Allows you to build Wonders that repairs others Minds, curing Derangements.</li> <li><b>Mind Wipe (Katastrofi):</b> Allows you to build Wonders that damages the mind. Draining Mental Attributes and causing Amnesia in the target.</li> <li><b>Mental Barrier (Prostasia):</b> Allows you to build Wonders that protects your mind from outside influences.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T20:29:47-07:00","id":1067352,"title":"","content":"I looked at the Preliminary Wonder Rules, and noticed some things.<br /> <br /> 1) It does not say what Advanced Potency does.<br /> <br /> 2) It says under Incorporating Components that the dice pool is Inspiration + Skill, but under Beta Testing, Doc Awful uses Intelligence and Wits instead of Inspiration to Incorporate Components. Why isn't the dice pool Intelligence + Skill + Inspiration, like in 1ED? Can you use non Mental Skills? What about Laboratory Equipment, Beholden Ability, Cooperation, spending Mania/Willpower, taking extra time and Conditions? Do Professional Training and similar Merits apply to this dice pool? If not, I think they should at least apply to rolls for using the Wonders. We also need a list of results for Exceptional Success and Dramatic Failure.<br /> <br /> 3) What do Geniuses roll for Clashes Of Wills involving their Wonders that are not Havoc? I assume it's Inspiration + Resolve + Longer Durations, plus whatever bonuses they get by spending Mania and Willpower.<br /> <br /> 4) Are Wonders still more fragile than mundane equivalents and automatically dangerous to Implant? Or should these traits be Flaws?<br /> <br /> 5) I think the roll for finding alternate Components should be changed to Wits + a Skill relevant to the Component.<br /> <br /> 6) It does not say what happens if the user who triggered Havoc gets an Exceptional Success.<br /> <br /> 7) Can Geniuses still spend a Willpower point to Hold It Together (i.e. automaticaly prevent a Havoc roll from happening to a Wonder that is in their possession)?<br /> <br /> 8) Can Geniuses still willingly abandon their Wonders?<br /> <br /> 9) Do Wonders still start out with a Persistent Flaw?<br /> <br /> 10) Withstand ratings are mentioned. Do these work just like the ones in Mage? How does Supernatural Tolerance work with Withstanding?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 03-23-2017, 11:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T20:59:30-07:00","id":1067367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1067352#post1067352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I looked at the Preliminary Wonder Rules, and noticed some things.<br /> <br /> 1) It does not say what Advanced Potency does.<br /> <br /> 2) It says under Incorporating Components that the dice pool is Inspiration + Skill, but under Beta Testing, Doc Awful uses Intelligence and Wits instead of Inspiration to Incorporate Components. Why isn't the dice pool Intelligence + Skill + Inspiration, like in 1ED? Can you use non Mental Skills? What about Laboratory Equipment, Beholden Ability, Cooperation, spending Mania/Willpower, taking extra time and Conditions? Do Professional Training and similar Merits apply to this dice pool? If not, I think they should at least apply to rolls for using the Wonders. We also need a list of results for Exceptional Success and Dramatic Failure.<br /> <br /> 3) What do Geniuses roll for Clashes Of Wills involving their Wonders that are not Havoc? I assume it's Inspiration + Resolve + Longer Durations, plus whatever bonuses they get by spending Mania and Willpower.<br /> <br /> 4) Are Wonders still more fragile than mundane equivalents and automatically dangerous to Implant? Or should these traits be Flaws?<br /> <br /> 5) I think the roll for finding alternate Components should be changed to Wits + a Skill relevant to the Component.<br /> <br /> 6) It does not say what happens if the user who triggered Havoc gets an Exceptional Success.<br /> <br /> 7) Can Geniuses still spend a Willpower point to Hold It Together (i.e. automaticaly prevent a Havoc roll from happening to a Wonder that is in their possession)?<br /> <br /> 8) Can Geniuses still willingly abandon their Wonders?<br /> <br /> 9) Do Wonders still start out with a Persistent Flaw?<br /> <br /> 10) Withstand ratings are mentioned. Do these work just like the ones in Mage? How does Supernatural Tolerance work with Withstanding?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Where is this doc?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T21:17:55-07:00","id":1067379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1067367#post1067367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Where is this doc?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5D9AgFEhGZ3dzM3aUZMMWRvT00\" target=\"_blank\"><b>right here.</b></a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T17:42:21-07:00","id":1067866,"title":"","content":"So to wit; Here are some of the changers this thread has decided:<br /> <br /> Geniuses use actual science; some might only be theoretical or be the science of parallel worlds, but science nonetheless. Havoc is more the result of Genii not labeling things and having nonsensical control mechanisms than them forcing alien laws of physics on reality (Though that also comes into play).<br /> <br /> There is no one in charge; The Peerage and Lemuria are basically glorified Fellowships (Which are probably mechanically Fellowships as well?) that might have been major once but have fallen so far. In this case, the Y splats (Artificers, Directors, Navigators, etc) should probably be Approaches to Mad Sciences (Knowledges?) instead of factions of The Peerage. They might have been, once, but now Navigators is a catch all term for Mad Explorers/Adventurers/Iron Man wannabe. Similarly, Lemuria has been defeated long ago and so the Baramins should probably be a loose collection of Fellowships united only by common origin and pretty dang independent otherwise.<br /> <br /> Genii Integrity equivalent pushes them to be more careful of their changes; The higher on the scale they are, the more 'sane' they are and the more ineffective they become. Likewise, the lower they are on the scale, the more unstable they are but the more powerful and effective they are overall. We should put lots of incentive to be on the lower side of the scale, of course being made to be careful as fuck with higher Integrity would probably do it for some players. High Integrity would probably also lock the best Wonders away due to how dangerous they are while simultaneously lowering Havoc chances and effects (Probably), due to fail-safes and them labeling their shit. Low Integrity would grant the best Wonders and (Probably) enhance their effects while making Havoc and its effects worse. Social penalties and bonuses are also (Probably) spread around.<br /> <br /> Clockstoppers are Anti-Beholden instead of Anti-Geniuses to differentiate them from Banishers; They would probably still have Anti-Tech powers, but they are the result of some people having the opposite reactions than regular Beholden. Should probably determine Beholden/Clockstopper chances via the Integrity or Inspiration Stats. Either more careful Genii have less chance of making Clockstoppers but are less likely to attempt to make Beholden as well, or More powerful Genii (like Inspiration 6+) are less likely to make Clockstoppers (As their Wonders become more sublime and shit) but make stronger ones instead.<br /> <br /> Time Travel is easier but has more consequences; no Mania is needed to change the past, so someone who came along for a ride in your Time Machine can change the Present until you find out whats going on and fix it. Time police exists sometimes, maybe there the Guardians of Forever stopping you from killing Hitler in the name of their former masters, maybe the Terminals stop you, maybe a cult of Time Traveling Geniuses, maybe none of those ever existed in the first place. Whatever the case truly is, each trip through time, even by the same Genius, will yield differing results.<br /> <br /> Anything else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T06:07:28-07:00","id":1068269,"title":"","content":"Since we are entirely decentralizing Lemuria, it brings up a question of what happened to all their Bureaus and other maniacal smoke and mirror mechanisms. Here is my suggestion: Lemurians claim God-Machine stole it from them. The Nine Secret Men were perfectly aware of Its existence and included protocols and guides in their playbook to keep It from stealing Lemurian bureocractic and political mechanisms, but with them gone Lemurians found themselves looking helplessly as their power slipped between their fingers to the grinding gears. Lemurians hate the God-Machine, they love God-Machine, they seek to destroy It, while worshipping It, and trying to banter with It for the Infrastructure It stole from them.<br /> Peerage struggles to acknowledge existence of such Machine much in the very same way as Lemuria fails to acknowledge the Mages, as far as they are concerned Lemurians are awful at accounting and No One Is in Control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T07:02:45-07:00","id":1068281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1068269#post1068269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since we are entirely decentralizing Lemuria, it brings up a question of what happened to all their Bureaus and other maniacal smoke and mirror mechanisms. Here is my suggestion: Lemurians claim God-Machine stole it from them. The Nine Secret Men were perfectly aware of Its existence and included protocols and guides in their playbook to keep It from stealing Lemurian bureocractic and political mechanisms, but with them gone Lemurians found themselves looking helplessly as their power slipped between their fingers to the grinding gears. Lemurians hate the God-Machine, they love God-Machine, they seek to destroy It, while worshipping It, and trying to banter with It for the Infrastructure It stole from them.<br /> Peerage struggles to acknowledge existence of such Machine much in the very same way as Lemuria fails to acknowledge the Mages, as far as they are concerned Lemurians are awful at accounting and No One Is in Control.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hmm. Seems a little bit too Cross-over dependent (even if the G-M is in Core, it is still an optional component). Their existing infrastructure could also simply be just as headless and running on auto-pilot. Local Lemurian Collectives control what they can, others are coasting on stale orders, others have been so-opted by all manner of factions (the G-M being only one potential). Drives home more of the &quot;No one is in charge&quot; theme than having it mostly stolen by a single power.<br /> <br /> Also brings up options for moral ambiguity - the best outcome might actually be helping Lemurians regain control over some of their old power base, if only so someone is monitoring it and preventing it from becoming a worse danger left on its own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T05:39:21-07:00","id":1070582,"title":"","content":"2 thoughts:<br /> <br /> What about including something like Mummy's &quot;let Fate decide my next Affinity&quot; mechanic? At the cost of randomness/lack of control, if gives a discount (less XP, higher Core Modifier, more Reach, easier build, etc.)... and allows for Wonders outside of the Genius's current Axioms. They enter a Strange Mood, and build something even they don't understand - yet.<br /> <br /> Other idea: All* Inspired create an Unmada Field. It is just &quot;sane&quot; Genii realize or suspect what is happening and the effect mostly cancels itself out (mostly). Unmada don't realize what they are, so it runs unchecked.<br /> * Exceptions exist and while Genii in a compatible Bardo still technically have a Field, it may be undetectable against the Bardo's own physics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T12:13:52-07:00","id":1072128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1070582#post1070582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2 thoughts:What about including something like Mummy's &quot;let Fate decide my next Affinity&quot; mechanic? At the cost of randomness/lack of control, if gives a discount (less XP, higher Core Modifier, more Reach, easier build, etc.)... and allows for Wonders outside of the Genius's current Axioms. They enter a Strange Mood, and build something even they don't understand - yet.<br /> <br /> Other idea: All* Inspired create an Unmada Field. It is just &quot;sane&quot; Genii realize or suspect what is happening and the effect mostly cancels itself out (mostly). Unmada don't realize what they are, so it runs unchecked.<br /> * Exceptions exist and while Genii in a compatible Bardo still technically have a Field, it may be undetectable against the Bardo's own physics.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the first idea, what limits would there be to this Strange Mood? Would there be a list of suggested results that can be randomly selected and then combined by rolling xd10s?<br /> <br /> For the second idea, how exactly would the Unmada Field work? Does it come in degrees according to your Obligation? Maybe Geniuses with high Obligation emit a Field that attracts evidence and Manes that <b>oppose </b>or at least challenge their worldview. This would make them question themselves more frequently and approach the world more like an ideal scientist. This is certainly stressful and even dangerous, but could be a source of Wondrous Experiences. Geniuses with low Obligation emit the typical Field.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T12:43:16-07:00","id":1072136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1072128#post1072128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the first idea, what limits would there be to this Strange Mood? Would there be a list of suggested results that can be randomly selected and then combined by rolling xd10s?</div> </div> </div> </div>Could. I was thinking, you are limited by the normal [XP/whatever] cost for the Wonder (before discount). As for tables, I guess? Ideally, if the Player says &quot;I'm going to let Inspiration guide me on my next invention&quot;, the ST already has a goal in mind for whatever Wonder &quot;they&quot; come up with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1072128#post1072128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the second idea, how exactly would the Unmada Field work? Does it come in degrees according to your Obligation? Maybe Geniuses with high Obligation emit a Field that attracts evidence and Manes that <b>oppose </b>or at least challenge their worldview. This would make them question themselves more frequently and approach the world more like an ideal scientist. This is certainly stressful and even dangerous, but could be a source of Wondrous Experiences. Geniuses with low Obligation emit the typical Field.</div> </div> </div> </div>&lt;shrug&gt; I remember the old discussion about a Genius's &quot;Aura&quot;, and I was thinking the only thing close was the Unmada Field, but that only applied to Unmada. Or does it need to? After all, non-Unmada are really only distinguished by that they <i>known</i> (or at least suspect) they are crazy, while Unmada don't think they are. What if that &quot;these readings may be Inspiration generated BS&quot; acts as a check on the Field, and when one goes Unmada, they don't start generating a Field, the check is simply gone now.<br /> <br /> Could be a great excuse for how oddness finds Genii no matter what they do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T02:15:29-07:00","id":1072415,"title":"","content":"So, Fields. Should we have them just be their own thing that touches upon some parts of all Axioms, or should some (Like Biology) be gated behind Axioms (in this case Exelixi)?.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying all of them should be like that, but some like the aforementioned Biology, Robotics, Weather, Armor, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T06:22:22-07:00","id":1072483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DArchon5</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1072415#post1072415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, Fields. Should we have them just be their own thing that touches upon some parts of all Axioms, or should some (Like Biology) be gated behind Axioms (in this case Exelixi)?.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying all of them should be like that, but some like the aforementioned Biology, Robotics, Weather, Armor, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> See, Biology doesn't have to be tied to Exelixi - Katastrofi can destroy a target's cells, or assault with fast acting diseases; Skafoi organic wings; Apokalypsi life-scanners; Prostasia living armor or armored skin;<br /> <br /> Fields would be categories or subjects, Axiomata would be the how or what you are doing.<br /> <br /> I say, list a few Fields and examples, but leave it open for Genii to create/discover their own.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Which is not to say Fields are so broad that the delineation is pointless - your Biology Katastrofi weapon is going to have a hard time against inorganic targets like some machines and ephemerals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-03-2017, 12:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T14:59:15-07:00","id":1073381,"title":"","content":"Idea for new Genius Intergity 2.0: Denial. <br /> All Geniuses are no longer quite human. They have transgressed humanity in their breakthrough and in fact are more like monstrous Illuminated or True Fae. No morals, attachments, laws, or logic can bind them. What they are and what they do is fundamentally wrong.<br /> However the thin line that separates them from their breathen, from monsters that prey on humanity and heartless machines that stare at them with million eyes is spark of defience. Denial. Most Geniuses want to believe that they are still human. Most Geniuses want to fill comfort of their homes. Geniuses will deny that they are anything alike with monsters in the dark, for when they accept their state it will trully become permanent. Thus, Geniuses face breaking point whenever they are faced with painful truth that they live a lie.<br /> \u2022Humans treating them as &quot;other.&quot;<br /> \u2022Supernatural beings treating them as fellow supernatural beings.<br /> \u2022Using Wonders of clashing aesthetic and functional principle.<br /> \u2022Witnessing human's breaking point caused by Genius's own actions/creations.<br /> \u2022Seeing human fail to use Wonder properly.<br /> \u2022Talking and listening to being with Integrity score or its equivalent at 0.<br /> \u2022Drawing a line between themselves and humans<br /> \u2022Crossing the line between humans and supernatural or geniuses and supernatural.<br /> \u2022Acts of wanton cruely done for no reason beyond humilating or degrading another sentient being.<br /> <br /> Genius at Denial 10 is able to emulate normalcy like a chameleons, disturbing any observing supernatural or maniacal beings, but putting fellow humans at ease. Mania becomes harder to channel, reality breaking Wonders are incredibly inefficient, larvea and other supernatural ingredient and placebos are unusable.<br /> Genius at Denial 1, have come through all phases. They have wrathed against themselves, their peers, and everymen. They have bargained with maniacal and supernatural, trying to find an all encompasing explanation. There is very little left for them but accepting their state, letting Mania sement it or pretend and join ranks of fellow Geniuses playing make believes in their fake societies, hiding among humans they so desperately wish to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12082,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","user":"Weird","date":".  Fixed minor typo. Would this metric be too opposite to Peerage's worldview? This way Peers are fucking up by drawing the line while Lemurians are fucking up by exposing their Wonders to humans and bei 04-04-2017, 06:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T17:39:23-07:00","id":1074423,"title":"","content":"Going to dump more ideas before I forget them:<br /> <br /> <b>The Many Flavors of Havoc</b><br /> So, other than adding Faults, breaking/being destroyed, there are certain Catastrophic fates that may befall Wonders. Some examples include:<ul><li><u>Katastrofi</u> Wonders often explode, damaging their surroundings an operators. A few <u>Metatropi</u> Wonders behave similarly (turned to dust by an explosion, or transmuted into fine silica being academic to victims). <u>Protasia</u> Wonders are also sometimes know to overload and explode. And the forces manipulated by certain <u>Epikrato</u> Wonders can run away to disastrous effects.</li> <li><u>Automata</u> Wonders are the most likely to &quot;go Orphan&quot;, attaining independence (and sometimes motion). <u>Exelixi</u> Wonders follow behind, though they often grant something else the independence. Some <u>Metatropi</u> Wonders have similar results.</li> <li><u>Skafoi</u> Wonders can randomly displace things, or even open inter-dimension/temporal rifts (like Orphaning, in that there is a new &quot;Wandering Monster&quot;, but it may have no relation to the source Wonder). A few <u>Apokalypsi</u> Wonders have &quot;dialed&quot; a few entities better left undisturbed too.</li> <li><u>Epikrato</u> Wonders often warp or unhinge their victims, permanently scarring them. <u>Metatropi</u> Wonders are also known for this.</li> <li>etc.</li> </ul><br /> <b>Havoc and Consequences</b><br /> Maybe Havoc could be something like [Obligation] + Inspiration? - Faults + Wonder Rank or Category? + triggerer's applicable Skill. Failure means another Fault (making it more likely to go wrong next time), Dramatic Failure a Catastrophy. Success, nothing happens (maybe a temporary -1 to the next roll in a scene?). Ex Success... Yay? Immune to Havoc next time or for the Scene?<br /> <br /> Oh, and a Havoc Failure should probably be an [Obligation] Trigger - nothing tends to infuriate Mad Scientists more than &quot;cretins&quot; messing with their toys and breaking them.<br /> <br /> <b>Size Matters - Bigger is Better</b><br /> I think there should be some mechanical impact and incentive to have Wonders of larger Sizes. Bonus to effects, cheaper to produce, etc. Larger Wonders have their own inherent disadvantages (just where are you going to store your 20 meter War Mech? And how much notice is it going to attract?), in addition to...<br /> <br /> <b>Raw Materials</b><br /> I'm thinking part of Wonder creation involves coming up with <i>at least*</i> the Wonder's Size in materials. Clones and monsters require organic material to be composed of, super-computers need silicon and conductors, and if you are somehow generating energy fields or beings, that energy needs to come from somewhere. Bigger Wonders are stronger, but also more costly.<br /> <br /> * I said &quot;at least&quot;, because there may be room for a bonus (though not as big a one as permanent Size) for requiring Developmental Material - that Juggernaut Serum may only end up being Size 1 (for Consumable vials) or 0 (for an Internalize treatment), but it requires 200 liters of fluid to be refined, and the machinery to do so. You can even get creative - your Secret Kung Fu Technique (Internalized Wonder) may &quot;consume&quot; volumes of obscure Academics materials in perfecting it.<br /> <br /> <b>X and Y Splats</b><br /> Does anyone think either should give (an option of) a free Field, or are Fields too idiosyncratic for that to be an option to list? Should Foundations/Baramins grant &quot;in favored Axiom&quot; discounts for Wonder Creation, since they are mostly groups of like minded individuals sharing knowledge? Easier to build a Robot when you have the information and support of the Artificers Union on your side.<br /> <hr /><br /> I've got some comments on the &quot;Foundations and Baramins are mostly gone&quot; debate/idea, but I'll add that later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T02:17:28-07:00","id":1074563,"title":"","content":"Anothet possible replacement: Overlap/Mutuality. What aspects of Genius's personality and beliefs overlap with consensus/those closest to them. Genius with high Overlap have very little outside of being like the others, while those on low might barely pass Turing Test against their own creations. Breaking points of Mutuality/Overlap would be learning that something Genius thought they had in common with majority was just them projecting, break ups from friends, family, and acquaintances, and some from list of Denial.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T05:42:32-07:00","id":1075089,"title":"","content":"I just realized something. How are we going to scale Wonders?. Are we going to give broad descriptions on what each dot of Axiom can do and let Fields and Inferences further limit them or are we going to have to list what each Inference can do at certain levels of Axioms?. The former sounds better tome, less work for STs if were going to encourage active Field Homebrewing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T06:52:36-07:00","id":1075104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1074423#post1074423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going to dump more ideas before I forget them:<br /> <br /> <b>The Many Flavors of Havoc</b><br /> So, other than adding Faults, breaking/being destroyed, there are certain Catastrophic fates that may befall Wonders. Some examples include:<ul><li><u>Katastrofi</u> Wonders often explode, damaging their surroundings an operators. A few <u>Metatropi</u> Wonders behave similarly (turned to dust by an explosion, or transmuted into fine silica being academic to victims). <u>Protasia</u> Wonders are also sometimes know to overload and explode. And the forces manipulated by certain <u>Epikrato</u> Wonders can run away to disastrous effects.</li> <li><u>Automata</u> Wonders are the most likely to &quot;go Orphan&quot;, attaining independence (and sometimes motion). <u>Exelixi</u> Wonders follow behind, though they often grant something else the independence. Some <u>Metatropi</u> Wonders have similar results.</li> <li><u>Skafoi</u> Wonders can randomly displace things, or even open inter-dimension/temporal rifts (like Orphaning, in that there is a new &quot;Wandering Monster&quot;, but it may have no relation to the source Wonder). A few <u>Apokalypsi</u> Wonders have &quot;dialed&quot; a few entities better left undisturbed too.</li> <li><u>Epikrato</u> Wonders often warp or unhinge their victims, permanently scarring them. <u>Metatropi</u> Wonders are also known for this.</li> <li>etc.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the Wonders were going to suffer Havoc Conditions when they go haywire, and custom ones based on the Wonder are certainly within the realm of possibility.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Havoc and Consequences</b><br /> Maybe Havoc could be something like [Obligation] + Inspiration? - Faults + Wonder Rank or Category? + triggerer's applicable Skill. Failure means another Fault (making it more likely to go wrong next time), Dramatic Failure a Catastrophy. Success, nothing happens (maybe a temporary -1 to the next roll in a scene?). Ex Success... Yay? Immune to Havoc next time or for the Scene? </div> </div> </div>Havoc is a Clash of Wills between Genius and Wonder (Wits + appropriate Skill vs. Havoc Pool + Modifiers). Each Wonder's Havoc Pool is determined when it's made. Renegades have a higher base Havoc Pool, skipping Components also increases it, using Larvae deacreases it. A Havoc Pool can be Zero, in which case it will only risk Havoc when triggered under conditions that add dice, otherwise you risk Havoc any time you activate it. So a very safely-made Wonder will only go into Havoc when it's pushed to the breaking point or a normal person tries to open it up, while a slapdash Wonder made by some wildly irresponsible Genius risks immediately going into Havoc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oh, and a Havoc Failure should probably be an [Obligation] Trigger - nothing tends to infuriate Mad Scientists more than &quot;cretins&quot; messing with their toys and breaking them. </div> </div> </div>Definitely. Letting a Wonder go into Havoc is definitely a break toward Renegade. Intentionally causing Havoc is a <i>big</i> break.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Size Matters - Bigger is Better</b><br /> I think there should be some mechanical impact and incentive to have Wonders of larger Sizes. Bonus to effects, cheaper to produce, etc. Larger Wonders have their own inherent disadvantages (just where are you going to store your 20 meter War Mech? And how much notice is it going to attract?), in addition to... </div> </div> </div>I haven't really put much thought into the Size of the Wonders. I suppose it could be covered in the Wonder's Scale Factor, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Raw Materials</b><br /> I'm thinking part of Wonder creation involves coming up with <i>at least*</i> the Wonder's Size in materials. Clones and monsters require organic material to be composed of, super-computers need silicon and conductors, and if you are somehow generating energy fields or beings, that energy needs to come from somewhere. Bigger Wonders are stronger, but also more costly.<br /> <br /> * I said &quot;at least&quot;, because there may be room for a bonus (though not as big a one as permanent Size) for requiring Developmental Material - that Juggernaut Serum may only end up being Size 1 (for Consumable vials) or 0 (for an Internalize treatment), but it requires 200 liters of fluid to be refined, and the machinery to do so. You can even get creative - your Secret Kung Fu Technique (Internalized Wonder) may &quot;consume&quot; volumes of obscure Academics materials in perfecting it. </div> </div> </div>Well, materials are generally covered in Components. But I could see a giant war mech needing &quot;800 tons of plasma steel&quot; as one of its Components.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>X and Y Splats</b><br /> Does anyone think either should give (an option of) a free Field, or are Fields too idiosyncratic for that to be an option to list? Should Foundations/Baramins grant &quot;in favored Axiom&quot; discounts for Wonder Creation, since they are mostly groups of like minded individuals sharing knowledge? Easier to build a Robot when you have the information and support of the Artificers Union on your side. <hr /><br /> I've got some comments on the &quot;Foundations and Baramins are mostly gone&quot; debate/idea, but I'll add that later. </div> </div> </div>Each Foundation has a couple of commonly-available Fields (Artificers might have Electroengineering and Hyper-Robotics, for example).<br /> <br /> And I don't Foundations and Baramins will be gone, so much as downplayed and less relevant. The Peerage still exists as an academic community, but it isn't really organized anymore, and it still has collective resources, but Genius society cares more about Fellowships than Foundations at large. And Baramins in this structure are more like Fellowships with extremely hard-line anti-modern views.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T07:00:54-07:00","id":1075105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DArchon5</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1075089#post1075089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just realized something. How are we going to scale Wonders?. Are we going to give broad descriptions on what each dot of Axiom can do and let Fields and Inferences further limit them or are we going to have to list what each Inference can do at certain levels of Axioms?. The former sounds better tome, less work for STs if were going to encourage active Field Homebrewing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably a bad idea, but what about tying certain effects (Inferences) to a cost. Potency equivalent also costs, and various modifiers also cost (or add, if they are limiting or negative). A Genius pumps up this [Core Modifier?] up, then spends it in various things.<br /> <br /> Inspiration could add, as could Raw Materials, rare materials, Catalyst or Foundation bonus, extra Faults, etc. So even a novice Genius can make a powerful Wonder... given an enormous amount of bonuses. Expert Genii can do more with less.<br /> <br /> Probably shouldn't reply when tired.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T07:24:37-07:00","id":1075112,"title":"","content":"No, I meant where are mechanics going to go?, a general write up in Axioms or more specialized ones in each Inference like you said?.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T10:29:16-07:00","id":1075169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DArchon5</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1075112#post1075112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I meant where are mechanics going to go?, a general write up in Axioms or more specialized ones in each Inference like you said?.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the Inference, since that is what controls the effect? Axioms are general categories of intent. Inferences probably require a certain &quot;level&quot; of Axiom, though, or other prerequisites.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T02:47:02-07:00","id":1075418,"title":"","content":"Just realized that we should probably figure out what should be possible on each dot of Axiom. But here\u2019s an incomplete write up for Fields.<br /> <br /> <b>Fields</b><br /> [Fluff]<br /> <br /> <b>Gaining Fields and Inferences</b><br /> Each Genius can learn any Field he desires without training, though training will significantly reduce the required time, should he have its Skill and Axiom requirements. Once a Field is learnt, he gains one of it\u2019s Inferences for free, usually an Inference of one of his Favored Axioms. After that he may purchase Inferences either through spending experience or by raising Inspiration, which grants a free Inference in a known Field.<br /> <br /> <b>Favored Fields</b><br /> Favored Fields are determined by the character\u2019s Method (Artificer, Director, Scholastic, etc.), his Fellowship, and his own personal preference, with each granting one Favored Field. Rogue Geniuses (a steadily rising percentage of them) gain an extra Favored Field, this vanishes upon joining a Fellowship, replaced by one of said Fellowships Favored Field.<br /> <br /> <b>Obscure Inferences</b><br /> Obscure Inferences are quite different, they require either a teacher or up to twice the required training times.<br /> <br /> <b>Sidebar</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b><i>On the Precipice of Discovery</i></b><br /> Whether or not they are sane the Inspired are <i>scientists</i> they are able to, nay, obligated to pioneer new technology as never seen before, even by their own peers. The Inferences presented here are not an exhaustive list, there is nothing to prevent players from adding their own custom Inferences or wholesale Fields other than the approval of the Storyteller. As a general rule, each Field should have a minimum of six Inferences, from at least four different Axioms. When designing new Fields and its Inferences consult the examples presented here and how they progress.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Field of Astronomy</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Space, the final frontier. For as long as mankind has lived we have wondered what it was and lies within it, whether it was gods or aliens, this is undeniable. It is no wonder that this Field is fairly popular among the Inspired.<br /> <b>Required Skill: </b>Science<br /> <b>Inferences: </b><ul><li><b>Deep Space Scanner </b>(Apokaypsi \u25cf+): Wonders using this Inference can be used to detect and scan objects in outer space, such as asteroids and exoplanets. Apokalypsi \u25cf can be used to scan the entirety of our solar system for particularly large objects, large asteroids, planets, kilometer long space ships, etc. though it can only detect what regular high tech instruments can and even the most minor of stealth Wonders would hide things from it, and can remotely control any spaceborne Automata or Skafoi Wonders the character had set it to. Apokalypsi (\u25cf\u25cf) allows for a Clash of Wills to detect any cloaked objects and allows for the detection of extraterrestrial lifeforms and for it\u2019s scans to reach throughout the galaxy. Apokalypsi (\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf) allows for scans to reach all throughout the galactic cluster, Apokalypsi (\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf) scans reaches throughout the galactic supercluster, and Apokalypsi (\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf) allows for scans reaching all throughout the universe.</li> <li><b>Life Support </b>(Exilixi \u25cf): This Inference is meant to be used with the Space Station or Spaceship Inference below; This Inference allows for the spacecraft to support human life, with recycled atmosphere and artificial gravity. Exilixi (\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf) allows for <i>any</i> lifeform to survive in the Wonder,</li> <li><b>Orbital Destruction Cannon </b>(Katastrofi \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf): Wonders made using this Inference can fire from the surface to orbit and vice-versa, though they have a base Size of 6. Accuracy fluctuates wildly as the cannon is calibrated for surface-to-orbit fire and have a greater chance of missing the closer the target is and the smaller they are, though certain Apokaypsi Inferences may fix this issue.</li> <li><b>Terraforming </b>(Metaptropi \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf): Wonders created using this Inference can change the very surface of a planet, changing it\u2019s atmosphere and soil make up to allow for human (or stranger) life. Barren planets would remain devoid of life and Terraforming</li> <li><b>Cosmic Shielding </b>(Prostasia \u25cf): This Inference blocks all manner of natural cosmic radiation and debris. Shielding from the weapons of spacecraft or other weaponry require other Prostasia Inferences. Prostasia \u25cf\u25cf would also protect from collisions with spaceborne asteroids, Prostasia \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf would protect even crashes from orbit.</li> <li><b>Space Station </b>(Prostasia \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf): This Inference allows for the creation of spaceborne structures.</li> <li><b>Spaceship </b>(Skafoi \u25cf\u25cf+): Wonders built using this Inference can travel to space, Skafoi (\u25cf\u25cf) can move planet to planet in a matter of days and travel up to the limits of the solar system in a few months. Skafoi (\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf) can travel faster-than-light, and may reach several nearby (for outer space standards) solar systems in weeks, and intra-solar planets in hours. Skafoi (\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf) can go even farther, going from Earth to Neptune in minutes, reaching other solar systems in hours, and can even go to other galaxies in weeks. Skafoi (\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf) allows for casual intergalactic travel. Though without Prostasia cosmic radiation would kill any traveler on any trip lasting more than an hour.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Field of Dimensions</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">As each Genius learned during their Breakthrough, there are an infinite number of possible worlds, each with it\u2019s own unique laws of physics. Several have learned to tap into those possibilities.<br /> <b>Required Skill:</b><br /> <b>Inferences:</b><ul><li><b>Dimensional Scanner </b>(Apokalypsi \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf): Scanners built using this Inference can scan other worlds and can detect the nearest way into those worlds. It would also allow for communication between such worlds.</li> <li><b>Schr\u00f6dinger\u2019s Gun </b>(Katastrofi \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf): This Wonder is able to project it\u2019s attack through the dimensional barrier into alternate \u2018Mirror\u2019 universes or, when in a pinch, into the Twilight. Though it may be useful, some Geniuses find themselves under attack from other possible versions of themselves when feeling especially unsure of their own decisions, and many try to return the sentiment.</li> <li><b>Pocket Dimension</b> (Metaptropi \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf): This Wonder would allow for the creation of Personal Dimensions. This Dimension follows the physical laws of the Genius\u2019 home universe and has space within it equal to (Inspiration x Metatropi (5) x 5) square cube of space. Many use such devices to store their Wonders and materials, and at times, their labs. Though such Dimensions are Bardo by nature and thus may suffer from Havoc, its similarity to the Genius\u2019 home universe allow it to exist through only it\u2019s own bound Mania. Exposure to worlds with different enough physical laws would subject it to the Mania requirements of regular Bardo.</li> <li><b>Dimensional Shield </b>(Prostasia \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf): This Inference allows for shielding from extra-dimensional attacks and intrusion, calling for a contested roll between the Wonder\u2019s creator and the intruding being</li> <li><b>Dimensional Portals</b> (Skafoi \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf): This Inference allows Wonders to open gateways into alternate universes. A Skafoi (\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf) wonder built using this Inference can open ways into <i>any</i> other world, such as the Gauntlet, Supernal Realms, Hedge, and Arcadia. Though the denizens of such realms would rarely welcome such intrusion.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Edit: Well... How did I do?<br /> <br /> Please note that I'm a complete amature at this and have yet to complete High School","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12398,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","user":"DArchon5","date":".  Fixed Spoiler Tabs 04-09-2017, 07:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T05:58:02-07:00","id":1075443,"title":"","content":"So, in this model, Fields are prebaked with a number of Inferences (to start with?). Raising Inspiration (or Axiom) grants free Inferences. Some Inferences scale with Axiom, and some require a minimum Axiom.<br /> <br /> How much do Fields cost, and how much do Inferences cost? I'd make them fairly cheap, since they only enable Wonder Creation - Genii can still only build so many.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T08:15:18-07:00","id":1075486,"title":"","content":"Well, yeah. Unless we want to either cut out or really heavily nerf the Time and Dimensions stuff were going to have to gate some of these things behind Axiom dots.<br /> <br /> As for their costs, maybe one experience per Inference?, thats how much a dot of Merit and a Specialization cost but if we want them to be cheaper than that then we could make a rules Hack with Wonderous XP being three Wonderous Beats instead of five but can only be used to buy Inferences. Though such a specific rule may not be many players cup of tea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T10:30:19-07:00","id":1075522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DArchon5</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1075486#post1075486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, yeah. Unless we want to either cut out or really heavily nerf the Time and Dimensions stuff were going to have to gate some of these things behind Axiom dots.<br /> <br /> As for their costs, maybe one experience per Inference?, thats how much a dot of Merit and a Specialization cost but if we want them to be cheaper than that then we could make a rules Hack with Wonderous XP being three Wonderous Beats instead of five but can only be used to buy Inferences. Though such a specific rule may not be many players cup of tea.</div> </div> </div> </div>1xp is fine for an Inference. What about for a Field? 2 or 3xp? It includes a free Inference, I'd think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T17:08:00-07:00","id":1075635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1075522#post1075522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1xp is fine for an Inference. What about for a Field? 2 or 3xp? It includes a free Inference, I'd think.</div> </div> </div> </div>Two is fine, I think.<br /> <br /> I just realized that it might be a good idea to put all this down in Google Drive and make it's link and docs easily accessible","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12398,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","user":"DArchon5","date":". 04-09-2017, 08:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T20:34:40-07:00","id":1075698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DArchon5</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1075486#post1075486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, yeah. Unless we want to either cut out or really heavily nerf the Time and Dimensions stuff were going to have to gate some of these things behind Axiom dots.<br /> <br /> As for their costs, maybe one experience per Inference?, thats how much a dot of Merit and a Specialization cost but if we want them to be cheaper than that then we could make a rules Hack with Wonderous XP being three Wonderous Beats instead of five but can only be used to buy Inferences. Though such a specific rule may not be many players cup of tea.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see no reason to cut or nerf. Genii exist to break the world, let them break the world. Give them enough rope to hang themselves. Build a time machine? Better hope you don't make a paradox. Build a dimensional window? Lots of scary shit in the multiverse, let's hope it doesn't notice you.<br /> <br /> No point in having mad visionaries if we can't let their visions go horribly, horribly right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T00:56:07-07:00","id":1075776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1075698#post1075698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I see no reason to cut or nerf. Genii exist to break the world, let them break the world. Give them enough rope to hang themselves. Build a time machine? Better hope you don't make a paradox. Build a dimensional window? Lots of scary shit in the multiverse, let's hope it doesn't notice you.<br /> <br /> No point in having mad visionaries if we can't let their visions go horribly, horribly right.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yeah. But were probably still going to have to limit their options by how experienced they are if we dont want them to be completely unbalanced gameplay wise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T07:54:33-07:00","id":1080890,"title":"","content":"No any propositions just little bit of thinking what I would personally desire from Genius Integrity 2.0:<br /> \u2022Encourage Blue-Orange/&quot;alien -morality. While it would be good idea to keep mad scientists from becoming just conspiracy of serial killers, I think Geniuses should be encouraged to be Heels to stay sane, not just Faces.<br /> \u2022Create paradoxical interaction with Hunters. There should be something to reward Genius for joining and supporting Hunters, but if Hunters get sniff oft their resident Genius being more than just a eccentric geek they instantly jump to treat them like a Slasher. This may not mean end of cooperation, since some Hunter cells are known to give Slashers second chances, but Genius&amp;Hunter interaction could come in three flavors: Closeted Supernatural Ally, Stabbed in the Back with Torches and Pitchforks, and/or Not Quite Beholden and their Not Quite Slasher.<br /> \u2022Encourage Geniuses to stay away from The Lost. I really enjoy idea of Changelings being completely terrified by Inspired, while Geniuses risking breaking point from being compared to True Fae. However to add the sadistic choice Geniuses may also have a strong urge to help to protect the Lost (possibly encouraged mechanically with a stick).<br /> \u2022Make Illuminated scary not as threat to health but as extreme hazarrads to sanity. Just reading their notes or listening to babbling of their victims could mean risk of becoming like them. This could be expanded to all 0 Integrity monsters for Geniuses.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile here is another possible interpritations what the number could mean: How much &quot;life&quot; Genius has beyond their big Idea. Integrity 10 Genius can go on for days without even thinking about their grand scheme to throw over the Government for giving their grandchild cancer, while Madcap with measly 1 spends even their time sleeping to dream big about their nearly immortality formula. <br /> The difference between Illuminated and Genius becomes apparent: Genius is but a mortal obsessed (or possessed?) by an Idea, Inspired and driven by it, even if sometimes unable to express or contain it. Illuminated are Ideas wearing mortals like diving suits. Illuminated remember lives of their hosts, but are completely unable to relate to them or rest of humanity. Some may even find idea of other Illuminated completely repulsive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T17:23:18-07:00","id":1081193,"title":"","content":"So, Axioms and Inferences. How many do you think starting PCs should get and should Inferences scale with Inspiration or Axioms?<br /> <br /> Edit: So genii are driven by Obsession?, maybe not that word though, we want to move as far away from Mage parallels as we can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T19:07:05-07:00","id":1081230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DArchon5</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1081193#post1081193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, Axioms and Inferences. How many do you think starting PCs should get and should Inferences scale with Inspiration or Axioms?<br /> <br /> Edit: So genii are driven by Obsession?, maybe not that word though, we want to move as far away from Mage parallels as we can.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are driven by a singular obsession. While a Mage might &quot;obsess&quot; over a few things, a Genius is <i>consumed</i> with their obsession. Finding immortality, conquering the world, getting that Szechuan Chicken Sauce, it's all they want, and it constantly threatens to push them past the edge of morality in its pursuit. A Mage has obsessions, but a Genius is capital-&quot;O&quot; <b>Obsessed.</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T06:24:04-07:00","id":1081413,"title":"","content":"Just thought of something. What if we made the Integrity Stat upside down. So the lower it is the saner you are. As the stat grows higher the harder it is for anyone, or even the Genius himself else for that matter, to deter them from their Goal. This would mean high Integrity Genii would be quite Obsessed and very hard to control, even by supernatural means, and maybe have stronger Wonders as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T07:15:45-07:00","id":1081428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DArchon5</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1081413#post1081413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just thought of something. What if we made the Integrity Stat upside down. So the lower it is the saner you are. As the stat grows higher the harder it is for anyone, or even the Genius himself else for that matter, to deter them from their Goal. This would mean high Integrity Genii would be quite Obsessed and very hard to control, even by supernatural means, and maybe have stronger Wonders as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought we were going with a two-ended Restraint, with either end having its own advantages and drawbacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T07:31:56-07:00","id":1081432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1081428#post1081428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought we were going with a two-ended Restraint, with either end having its own advantages and drawbacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds familiar (The Fettered vs the Unfettered). What were the bonuses and penalties? High = less powerful, but Havoc is less likely; Low = the opposite?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T12:22:12-07:00","id":1081535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1081432#post1081432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sounds familiar (The Fettered vs the Unfettered). What were the bonuses and penalties? High = less powerful, but Havoc is less likely; Low = the opposite?</div> </div> </div> </div>Renegade/Low Restraint: Higher base Havoc, more Jabir penalties, less Mania costs, can more freely/publicly break social rules without hesitating<br /> <br /> Paragon/High Restraint: Lower base Havoc, lower Jabir penalties, higher Mannia costs, more likely to &quot;choke&quot; when taking decisive action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T00:06:24-07:00","id":1081734,"title":"","content":"Y'know, i should have realized that sooner. But what i mean is that, yes Paragon and Renegade are still the same, but at different ends of the meter. And now it sounds like a cheap way to make them seem alien. Fuck.<br /> <br /> In other news, Foundations, are they still the Y-Splat or are we just gonna assume all Genii are Rogues and the Foundations and Baramins are now just Fellowships that used to be hot stuff until X happened. In which case they would be the Prestige Class of Genii that provide special training and resources (Fields and Materials), to go with the whole No One Is In Charge theme. Because this way, literally no one is in charge. Just a bunch of Genii running around unchecked, most of which think no one else like them exists<br /> <br /> If were going with the latter. Then I would suggest that the Y-Splat be Method, the How to the Catalyst's Why and the Goal's What<br /> <br /> Artificer<br /> Favored Axioms: Automata or Prostasia<br /> Fields: ???, ???<br /> <br /> Director<br /> Favored Axioms: Automata or Epikrato<br /> Fields: Drones, ???<br /> <br /> Navigator<br /> Favored Axioms: Katastrofi or Skafoi<br /> Fields: Aeronotics, Oceanautic<br /> <br /> Progenitor<br /> Favored Axioms: Automata or Exelixi<br /> Fields: Biology, Cybernetics<br /> <br /> Scholastic<br /> Favored Axioms: Apokalypsi or Metatropi<br /> Fields: Chronotics, Dimensionics<br /> <br /> I lost my muse half way through. Sorry. If we do this, we might as well allow them to switch between them under certain circumstances, they might as well not get Grants either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T03:56:10-07:00","id":1081769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DArchon5</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1081734#post1081734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In other news, Foundations, are they still the Y-Splat or are we just gonna assume all Genii are Rogues and the Foundations and Baramins are now just Fellowships that used to be hot stuff until X happened. In which case they would be the Prestige Class of Genii that provide special training and resources (Fields and Materials), to go with the whole No One Is In Charge theme. Because this way, literally no one is in charge. Just a bunch of Genii running around unchecked, most of which think no one else like them exists</div> </div> </div> </div>I say: keep the Foundations. They simplify things (for now), even if most Genii are members in name only. It's convenient (both for us, for now, and the Inspired themselves) - they get some good information on areas of interest, and the Foundations don't really ask for anything in return other than occasional feedback (of which the Genius might give more than desired anyways). The Peerage still wouldn't be &quot;in charge&quot; anyways. What do they manage? Other Genii, at most, and them only with their compliance (baring... extreme outliers). Lemuria's back has been broken, and for all the different Baramin's claims at world domination, you can't get more than two Collaboratives <i>in the same Baramin</i> to agree on anything (and getting two is difficult). Each of the &quot;Inspired Superpowers&quot; are about as toothless as the Articles of Confederation<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DArchon5</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1081734#post1081734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I lost my muse half way through. Sorry. If we do this, we might as well allow them to switch between them under certain circumstances, they might as well not get Grants either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Meh. My muse is still gibbering in the corner.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T06:20:03-07:00","id":1081803,"title":"","content":"Anyway, would any of you mind if i go back and started to put all these notes in a Drive. I know someone else has done it, but I've lost the link and I would prefer to compile a more complete list of everthing we've discussed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T07:38:27-07:00","id":1081829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DArchon5</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1081803#post1081803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, would any of you mind if i go back and started to put all these notes in a Drive. I know someone else has done it, but I've lost the link and I would prefer to compile a more complete list of everthing we've discussed.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Feel free.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T09:29:36-07:00","id":1081878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DArchon5</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1081803#post1081803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, would any of you mind if i go back and started to put all these notes in a Drive. I know someone else has done it, but I've lost the link and I would prefer to compile a more complete list of everthing we've discussed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. I'll probably get back to writing more in between projects this week. 2 software development classes and a database class does not an empty semester make.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T02:06:14-07:00","id":1082186,"title":"","content":"So, Lemuria. Since no more than a Collaborative of Unmada can work together for long periods of time, how do they manage it. 'Cause the way I'm currently imagining it, Fellowships, Foundations, and Baramins are less groups of Genii with the same goals and more like Alliances of Convenience. They may help each other, but more often than not they just pretend that they are the only Genius to have ever existed. Lemurians are more cutthroat about this. Each thinking that they are using Lemuria for their own goals when everyone else does so as well.<br /> <br /> But if this is the case, how were they an actual threat?<br /> <br /> I mean, I could imagine that early Lemurians merely helped each other more to set up the illusion of being a coherent whole, when they are nothing of the sort. And when the Peerage showed up most of them were in too deep to back out so they Quintupled Down and pretended that everything was going according to plan when it was actually just a series of events that they have little to no control over. I could even imagine that, due to their division, whenever a Lemurian Collaborative went down two more took their place, casting the illusion that they have great numbers, when really all that was happening was that those Collaboratives were fighting over the resources of their fallen cohorts. Heck, the 'collapse' of Lemuria might have actually just been the point were their little Masquerade in a Masquerade fell and the Peerage figured out that the 'conspiracy' they were fighting are actually just a mass of squabbling Genii with the maturity of spoiled children.<br /> <br /> I just don't see how the Peerage couldn't have figured it out sooner without them holding the Idiot Ball due to the fact that mind reading and omnipotence tech is a thing. Not unless we make it so that Unmada cannot be mind read due to the interference of their reality warping and their maddness thus taking care of the former, and make omnipotence tech either incredibly hard to create or make it so that Peerage members can't make it for some reason. Or just make the whole, 'cloaked mind, even from omnipotence' thing either a Grant or a powerful Wonder made by an Unmada especially invested in the whole 'Lemuria' thing. With the threat of them seeming too much like VII, which isn't really a threat at all.<br /> <br /> Really, my muse must have died, cause I cannot think of any idea to make it fit.<br /> <br /> Edit: Should we make more Inferences available at Character Creation. I mean, I get that this system is based of of Werewolf, but we should probably make sure Geniuses at their beginning have more 'spells' to compensate for their relative squishiness and lack of ability to naturally transform into death machines. I don't know, like give them 6 Axiom dots (capped at 3) like mages. This way they probably start with about 7 Inferences. More if we allow them to allocate 'free' Inferences.<br /> <br /> Edit 2: Oh, and I'm currently compiling a dot-by-dot list of what each Axiom could do to help scale Inferences. Any suggestions?.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12398,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","user":"DArchon5","date":".  Seems like my muse is most effective at sarcasm. 04-22-2017, 06:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T03:40:06-07:00","id":1082207,"title":"","content":"Out of curiosity: are you planning to tone down the power level of this version of Genius? In the original version, an advanced character could build a Death Star given the resources.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T05:04:27-07:00","id":1082213,"title":"","content":"Probably not, but were sure as hell making building the Death Star more difficult using Inferences. Besides its not that bad, its actually worse. Starting Characters can build a CPU sized Universal Translator with a range of: Planet Earth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T09:05:41-07:00","id":1082284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1082207#post1082207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Out of curiosity: are you planning to tone down the power level of this version of Genius? In the original version, an advanced character could build a Death Star given the resources.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes...and no. We're making Genii a little more focused in what each one can build by constraining them to Fields and Postulate/Inferences (I was using the term Postulate, but other people here are saying Inferences, and both terms work.).<br /> <br /> In 1E, a Death Star just requires Katastrofi, Skafoi, Prostasia and maybe Automata, and then the Resources and time to match.<br /> <br /> In 2E, a Death Star requires you to have Fields that relate to space travel, lasers, and life support, and then you still need the Axiomata in order to use the Inferences, and then you need to find the material Components (Hypermatter cores ain't cheap, mate).<br /> <br /> So making big, complex Wonders is harder overall, but if you want to <i>really</i> hone in on <i>one specific thing</i>, then you can get some enormous results. And if you want to be a dabbler in a lot of fields, you can do that. But being a god-like omnidisciplinary Genius is very difficult, and requires and extreme amount of time and energy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T15:53:33-07:00","id":1082415,"title":"","content":"Well, not Omnidisciplinary as in having a bunch of un related Wonders, but applying skill in unusual ways (ie. Using skills for things they never tried before) is fair game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T16:46:26-07:00","id":1082433,"title":"","content":"Well, not Omnidisciplinary as in having a bunch of un related Wonders, but applying skill in unusual ways (ie. Using skills for things they never tried before) is fair game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T03:03:59-07:00","id":1082549,"title":"","content":"Hey, should Automata only get robots and AI and such, or should it also get creation stuff, like Hard-Light Constructs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T06:23:15-07:00","id":1082576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DArchon5</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1082549#post1082549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, should Automata only get robots and AI and such, or should it also get creation stuff, like Hard-Light Constructs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anything independent, I'd say. Automata should be for creating/modelling creatures as Wonders - AI, robots, bio-engineered monstrosities, zombies, sentient energy patterns, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T09:59:05-07:00","id":1082677,"title":"","content":"So, Green Lantern Rings arent Automata. Then what are they? Metatropi? Katastrofi?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T10:30:31-07:00","id":1082701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DArchon5</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1082677#post1082677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, Green Lantern Rings arent Automata. Then what are they? Metatropi? Katastrofi?</div> </div> </div> </div>Epikrato and Katastrofi, mostly. They mostly blast and make hard-light constructs.<br /> <br /> Sometimes they act on their own, including finding a new wearer, so there might be Automata in there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T15:40:07-07:00","id":1082796,"title":"","content":"Got it. Factories are still Automata though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T05:40:50-07:00","id":1082979,"title":"","content":"So is what you're doing there sorted and compiled in any sort of document anywhere for people to see? Did it yield any results so far? Or is it just 40 pages of intense brainstorming?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T06:03:29-07:00","id":1082987,"title":"","content":"Currently, its the latter. Some of the more recent ideas have been recorded in Drives but we're still in the brainstorming phase. If we get any farther than that the we might get a new thread and make the folder more accessable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T07:25:19-07:00","id":1083003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DArchon5</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1082987#post1082987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Currently, its the latter. Some of the more recent ideas have been recorded in Drives but we're still in the brainstorming phase. If we get any farther than that the we might get a new thread and make the folder more accessable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Establishing Consensus is Hard.<br /> <br /> I think we all agree upon a few points by now, however.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T08:00:06-07:00","id":1083017,"title":"","content":"Oh, I just remembered. I'm going to write some of these Fields in my spare time. They're going to have Axiom prerequisites determined by 1E. Is that alright or should we shift some of these powers around.<br /> <br /> Should each Axiom have a single Inference in a Field, even if that would mean an Inference with multiple powers, or should each power be an Inference, even if an Axiom would have more than one Inference per Field.<br /> <br /> Finaly, at what level of Metatropi do you think turning into a ghost would be. I'm thinking 4 or 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T08:14:03-07:00","id":1083020,"title":"","content":"One Postulate/Inference per power. Epikrato might have more, but since you have to purchase them individually (other than the freebies), that balances out its utility.<br /> <br /> Transformation into metaphysical energy (Ghost Ephemera), I'd place at 3 minimum, 4, more reasonably. Maybe 5 for permanent transformations (making previous versions temporary).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T14:51:03-07:00","id":1083193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DArchon5</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1082987#post1082987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Currently, its the latter. Some of the more recent ideas have been recorded in Drives but we're still in the brainstorming phase. If we get any farther than that the we might get a new thread and make the folder more accessable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. I have some docs and notes together in a Drive Folder, but things are hectic for me at the moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T02:54:41-07:00","id":1083391,"title":"","content":"Alright, I'll probably put the upgrade style powers (Healing Lethal and Aggravated) in the same Inference, though well see if upgrading them just requires more dots in Axiom or actually buying them again. As each Axiom can have multiple Inferences that puts standard Fields at up to 6-16+ Inferences, though we can probably just shuffle some into other Fields later. I'll try to make a few Inferences based on the stuff from 1E for now and see how that goes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T05:38:41-07:00","id":1083416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DArchon5</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1083391#post1083391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, I'll probably put the upgrade style powers (Healing Lethal and Aggravated) in the same Inference, though well see if upgrading them just requires more dots in Axiom or actually buying them again. As each Axiom can have multiple Inferences that puts standard Fields at up to 6-16+ Inferences, though we can probably just shuffle some into other Fields later. I'll try to make a few Inferences based on the stuff from 1E for now and see how that goes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Upgraded powers just require Reaching for them within the Inference in the first place in the notes I have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T06:13:51-07:00","id":1083428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1083416#post1083416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Upgraded powers just require Reaching for them within the Inference in the first place in the notes I have.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is Reaching?<br /> <br /> And it might not be the best idea for full Aggravated damage available from start, with minor cost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T08:20:17-07:00","id":1083465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1083428#post1083428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What is Reaching?<br /> <br /> And it might not be the best idea for full Aggravated damage available from start, with minor cost.</div> </div> </div> </div>'Course not. I'm basing all of these Inferences on 1E mechanics. Aggravated Healing requires Exelixi 4. As for Reach, its a Mage mechanic that effects their spells powers. I'm not sure whether we should use mechanics from mage, but this whole Field and Inference system is already a frankenstein of Werewolf Gifts and Renown, Sin-Eater Keys and Manefestations, and Changeling Contracts that adding mage mechanics would only make it more unrecodnizeable. However I have no idea how Reaching actually works so I'm just gonna let someone else implement it once I'm done cannibalizing 1E Genius.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T08:42:52-07:00","id":1083477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DArchon5</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1083465#post1083465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">'Course not. I'm basing all of these Inferences on 1E mechanics. Aggravated Healing requires Exelixi 4. As for Reach, its a Mage mechanic that effects their spells powers. I'm not sure whether we should use mechanics from mage, but this whole Field and Inference system is already a frankenstein of Werewolf Gifts and Renown, Sin-Eater Keys and Manefestations, and Changeling Contracts that adding mage mechanics would only make it more unrecodnizeable. However I have no idea how Reaching actually works so I'm just gonna let someone else implement it once I'm done cannibalizing 1E Genius.</div> </div> </div> </div>&lt;shrug&gt; The way I see the interactions of Axioms, Inferences, and Fields are:<br /> <b>Axiom:</b> Defines the category of effect (Healing or Improvement are Exelixi, Destruction is Katastrofi)<br /> <b>Axiom Rank:</b> Establishes the degree (Bashing vs Lethal damage, minor manipulation vs total Mind Control)<br /> <b>Inference:</b> Is the specific effect (Health damage vs reducing object Durability, or Healing vs Attribute Increase)<br /> <b>Field:</b> Defines the subject or method (Biology means it operates on or through living creatures, Mechanics means it operates on or through artificial constructions, Ectoplasmics means it operates on or through ectoplasm, etc.)<br /> <br /> I think Field shouldn't be locked down at &quot;This Field offers these Inferences/Effects&quot;. I see Field as more clarification, focus, and flavoring.<br /> <br /> <b>Wonder does </b><i>[Effect][to degree]</i><b> to/through </b><i>[subject]</i>. [Effect] is the Inference (grouped by Axiom), [to degree] is determined by Axiom Rank (possible the Inference itself, gate-locked behind a certain minimum Axiom rating), and [subject] is the Field.<br /> <br /> Field is there so a Genius specializing in Biology can't just make a fusion cannon. Not without hefty justification how something biological is able to generate nuclear fusion. Their Katastrofi weaponry is going to have to use bacteria, or organ-produced acid or something.<br /> <br /> That's just my thoughts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T08:56:49-07:00","id":1083484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1083477#post1083477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &lt;shrug&gt; The way I see the interactions of Axioms, Inferences, and Fields are:<br /> <b>Axiom:</b> Defines the category of effect (Healing or Improvement are Exelixi, Destruction is Katastrofi)<br /> <b>Axiom Rank:</b> Establishes the degree (Bashing vs Lethal damage, minor manipulation vs total Mind Control)<br /> <b>Inference:</b> Is the specific effect (Health damage vs reducing object Durability, or Healing vs Attribute Increase)<br /> <b>Field:</b> Defines the subject or method (Biology means it operates on or through living creatures, Mechanics means it operates on or through artificial constructions, Ectoplasmics means it operates on or through ectoplasm, etc.)<br /> <br /> I think Field shouldn't be locked down at &amp;quot;This Field offers these Inferences/Effects&amp;quot;. I see Field as more clarification, focus, and flavoring.<br /> <br /> <b>Wonder does </b><i>[Effect][to degree]</i><b> to/through </b><i>[subject]</i>. [Effect] is the Inference (grouped by Axiom), [to degree] is determined by Axiom Rank (possible the Inference itself, gate-locked behind a certain minimum Axiom rating), and [subject] is the Field.<br /> <br /> Field is there so a Genius specializing in Biology can't just make a fusion cannon. Not without hefty justification how something biological is able to generate nuclear fusion. Their Katastrofi weaponry is going to have to use bacteria, or organ-produced acid or something.<br /> <br /> That's just my thoughts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, thats just the 1E system with the effects being Axiom locked Variables and Fields being minor Aesthetics.<br /> <br /> Another thoughy, what if we made Unmadaness infectious with the infected genius gaining the same world view as the one who infected him?.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T11:23:41-07:00","id":1083565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DArchon5</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1083484#post1083484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, thats just the 1E system with the effects being Axiom locked Variables and Fields being minor Aesthetics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, somewhat - instead of getting all variable for free, they are picked up individually (with Axiom dots and Inspiration granting freebies, like with Renown granting free Gift Facets when increased). Locking things down into a matrix makes new abilities extremely hard to fit in.<br /> <br /> The idea was to address things like Epikrato giving telekinesis, economic manipulation, and mind control. This model would require someone to commit to generalization instead of getting it for free. Fields further define/specialize what the Genius can do and is about - its a bit more than Aesthetics, since it can actively limit what a Genius can do.<br /> <br /> Again, what I had in my mind. Seeing examples helps with Pro/Con analysis.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DArchon5</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1083484#post1083484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another thoughy, what if we made Unmadaness infectious with the infected genius gaining the same world view as the one who infected him?.</div> </div> </div> </div>How would that work, mechanically? Provoking [Breaking Point] checks, with failure granting the Unmada Condition and changing the worldview/model to match?<br /> <br /> Torture <i>can</i> turn you evil? (For Genii, and certain definitions of evil)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T15:12:56-07:00","id":1083712,"title":"","content":"Ok, yeah, doing something like that would make things much easier. I'll try to write that then.<br /> <br /> Edit: As for infectous unmadaness, the idea is that the Genius' worldview is twisted by the unmada field until it matches the Unmada's, just like it twists the 'Real World'. This is mostly to explain unmada working together when their madness makes them paint those with even slightly different worldviews as fools.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12398,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","user":"DArchon5","date":". 04-25-2017, 06:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T00:48:19-07:00","id":1083883,"title":"","content":"I just thought of something. Because reading the same Healing ability on three different Fields is boring, why don't we keep the powers under the description of each Axiom dot, each Inference would then reference a specific power on its Axiom and mention how it changes the targeting and the overall effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T05:10:00-07:00","id":1083923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DArchon5</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1083883#post1083883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just thought of something. Because reading the same Healing ability on three different Fields is boring, why don't we keep the powers under the description of each Axiom dot, each Inference would then reference a specific power on its Axiom and mention how it changes the targeting and the overall effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you write up a quick before and after comparison?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T05:33:30-07:00","id":1083925,"title":"","content":"I'll try but it might take a while. All my data is on docs and the Internet Connection in my house is broken. So working on my computer is out. I have the required stuff on a tablet though so ill at least try.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T05:52:01-07:00","id":1083930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DArchon5</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1083883#post1083883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just thought of something. Because reading the same Healing ability on three different Fields is boring, why don't we keep the powers under the description of each Axiom dot, each Inference would then reference a specific power on its Axiom and mention how it changes the targeting and the overall effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>So rather like the basic concepts sections of Mage Arcana, where they explain an effect that's common to numerous spells in the Arcanum so they don't have to re-explain it each time?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T06:20:50-07:00","id":1083937,"title":"","content":"Probably, havent actually read any iteration of Mage before but well see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T09:22:22-07:00","id":1084005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DArchon5</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1083937#post1083937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably, havent actually read any iteration of Mage before but well see.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mage 2E has sections for each Arcanum, and the sections note any common threads running through an Arcanum. For example, many Fate spells place Hexes or Boons, so they're explained in the introduction to Fate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T02:39:27-07:00","id":1084388,"title":"","content":"Ok, i got an example<br /> <br /> <b>Axioms</b><br /> Axioms are composed of multiple base [powers] that are available at each dot, some of which improve as the Inspired's mastery of the Axiom and Inspiration grows. These powers cannot be integrated into Wonders on their own, but must be molded and focused by Inferences. Most Inferences grant bonuses to the base power while constricting it's targets, some Inferences simply grant new powers wholesale, though these are inevitably narrow in focus.<br /> <br /> <b>Example Axioms<br /> Exelixi</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Autonomous Repair </b>(\u2022): Wonders made using this [Power] can heal itself as if they were human.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Mending</b> (\u2022, and \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022): This [Power] allows for the genius the mend both organic and inorganic matter. He rolls Dexterity + Medicine or Crafts. Each success repairs one point of Structure</span></span> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">or Lethal damage or two points of Bashing damage.</span></span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <b>Katastrofi</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Basic Damage </b>(\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022): The base effect of Katastrofi Wonders is dealing damage. At Katastrofi (\u2022) the Wonder can only deal Bashing damage. Katastrofi (\u2022\u2022) can deal Lethal damage and grants the 9-again quality to Bashing damage. Katastrofi (\u2022\u2022\u2022) Wonders can deal Aggravated damage, grants the 9-again quality to Lethal damage, and the 8-again quality to Bashing damage. Katastrofi (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) grants the 9-again quality to Aggravated damage and 8-again to both Lethal and Bashing damage. Katastrofi (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) grants 8-again on all damage.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Trait Reduction </b>(\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022): This [Power] allows the Wonder to remove dots in a Trait specified by the chosen Inference. This Trait is reduced by one dot per three Health Levels of damage that would have been dealt. At Katastrofi (\u2022) this Trait heals at the rate of Bashing damage, Lethal damage at Katastrofi (\u2022\u2022), and Aggravated damage at Katastrofi (\u2022\u2022\u2022).</span></span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <b>Skafoi</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Dimensional Travel</b> (<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022): This [Power] allows the Wonder to access other dimensions.</span></span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Example Fields</b><br /> <b>Necronics</b> [Ghosts]<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This Field is the study and manipulation of spectral beings and the Underworld.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Required Skill</b>:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Occult</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Inferences</b>:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Plasmic Regenerator</b> </span></span>(<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Exelixi \u2022):</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> This Inference uses the <b>Mending</b> [Power] of Exelixi, allowing it to heal the Corpus of ghosts, using Occult instead of Medicine in the roll. If it can only heal ghosts, add the higher of geniuses Exelixi or Inspiration to the Dexterity + Occult roll.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ectoplasmic-Disintegrator </span></span></b>(<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Katastrofi \u2022): This Inference uses the <b>Basic Damage</b> [Power] of Katastrofi, allowing it to harm ghosts. If it can only harm ghosts, they treat all attacks as coming from a being with an honorary Rank of the higher of the geniuses Katastrofi or Inspiration.<br /> <b>Plasmic Reductor </b>(Katastrofi \u2022): This Inference uses the <b>Trait Reduction </b>[Power] of Katastrofi, allowing it to reduce a ghost's Power, Finesse, or Resistance traits. If it can only reduce a ghosts Traits, it can reduce Rank as well, which is reduced by one dot per five Health Levels of damage that would have been dealt. Reducing Rank to 0 would permanently destroy the ghosts as nothing of it remains.</span></span><br /> <b>Keymaster </b>(<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Skafoi \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: This Inference uses the <b>Dimensional</b> [Power] of Skafoi, allowing it to open Avernian Gates. If it cannot create new gates, it gains a +5 bonus to open them.</span></span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Edit</b>: So basically, you can choose the regular option and effect the thing as you normally would, in addition to anything else it can do. Or, you can specialize and get bonuses to rolls or entirely new effects","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12398,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","user":"DArchon5","date":". 04-27-2017, 06:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T05:59:26-07:00","id":1084437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DArchon5</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1084388#post1084388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, i got an example<br /> <br /> <b>Axioms</b><br /> Axioms are composed of multiple base [powers] that are available at each dot, some of which improve as the Inspired's mastery of the Axiom and Inspiration grows. These powers cannot be integrated into Wonders on their own, but must be molded and focused by Inferences. Most Inferences grant bonuses to the base power while constricting it's targets, some Inferences simply grant new powers wholesale, though these are inevitably narrow in focus.<br /> <br /> <b>Example Axioms<br /> Exelixi</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Autonomous Repair </b>(\u2022): Wonders made using this [Power] can heal itself as if they were human.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Mending</b> (\u2022, and \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022): This [Power] allows for the genius the mend both organic and inorganic matter. He rolls Dexterity + Medicine or Crafts. Each success repairs one point of Structure</span></span> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">or Lethal damage or two points of Bashing damage.</span></span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <b>Katastrofi</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Basic Damage </b>(\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022): The base effect of Katastrofi Wonders is dealing damage. At Katastrofi (\u2022) the Wonder can only deal Bashing damage. Katastrofi (\u2022\u2022) can deal Lethal damage and grants the 9-again quality to Bashing damage. Katastrofi (\u2022\u2022\u2022) Wonders can deal Aggravated damage, grants the 9-again quality to Lethal damage, and the 8-again quality to Bashing damage. Katastrofi (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) grants the 9-again quality to Aggravated damage and 8-again to both Lethal and Bashing damage. Katastrofi (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) grants 8-again on all damage.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Trait Reduction </b>(\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022): This [Power] allows the Wonder to remove dots in a Trait specified by the chosen Inference. This Trait is reduced by one dot per three Health Levels of damage that would have been dealt. At Katastrofi (\u2022) this Trait heals at the rate of Bashing damage, Lethal damage at Katastrofi (\u2022\u2022), and Aggravated damage at Katastrofi (\u2022\u2022\u2022).</span></span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <b>Skafoi</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Dimensional Travel</b> (<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022): This [Power] allows the Wonder to access other dimensions.</span></span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Example Fields</b><br /> <b>Necronics</b> [Ghosts]<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This Field is the study and manipulation of spectral beings and the Underworld.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Required Skill</b>:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Occult</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Inferences</b>:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Plasmic Regenerator</b> </span></span>(<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Exelixi \u2022):</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> This Inference uses the <b>Mending</b> [Power] of Exelixi, allowing it to heal the Corpus of ghosts, using Occult instead of Medicine in the roll. If it can only heal ghosts, add the higher of geniuses Exelixi or Inspiration to the Dexterity + Occult roll.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ectoplasmic-Disintegrator </span></span></b>(<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Katastrofi \u2022): This Inference uses the <b>Basic Damage</b> [Power] of Katastrofi, allowing it to harm ghosts. If it can only harm ghosts, they treat all attacks as coming from a being with an honorary Rank of the higher of the geniuses Katastrofi or Inspiration.<br /> <b>Plasmic Reductor </b>(Katastrofi \u2022): This Inference uses the <b>Trait Reduction </b>[Power] of Katastrofi, allowing it to reduce a ghost's Power, Finesse, or Resistance traits. If it can only reduce a ghosts Traits, it can reduce Rank as well, which is reduced by one dot per five Health Levels of damage that would have been dealt. Reducing Rank to 0 would permanently destroy the ghosts as nothing of it remains.</span></span><br /> <b>Keymaster </b>(<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Skafoi \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: This Inference uses the <b>Dimensional</b> [Power] of Skafoi, allowing it to open Avernian Gates. If it cannot create new gates, it gains a +5 bonus to open them.</span></span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Edit</b>: So basically, you can choose the regular option and effect the thing as you normally would, in addition to anything else it can do. Or, you can specialize and get bonuses to rolls or entirely new effects</div> </div> </div> </div>I really don't think we need to gate things behind specific dot ratings, especially for Inferences/Postulates. For example, with Keymaster, you're waiting around until you get Skafoi 4 just to open Avernian gates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T06:20:54-07:00","id":1084448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1084437#post1084437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really don't think we need to gate things behind specific dot ratings, especially for Inferences/Postulates. For example, with Keymaster, you're waiting around until you get Skafoi 4 just to open Avernian gates.</div> </div> </div> </div>Opening existing Gates should be easier yeah. Like 2 dots, or maybe 3. Creating Gates ex nihilo would be higher, though, like 4. Total bypasses and rules breaks would be 5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-27-2017, 09:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T06:45:09-07:00","id":1084458,"title":"","content":"Well, all this is based on 1E stuff. And I'm not fammiliar enough with things that interact with the Underworld to really make good ways for it to interact with wonders. Other than that, and the whole Dimensions thing, what do you think about the current system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T20:01:01-07:00","id":1085296,"title":"","content":"Ok, how about this<br /> <br /> <b>Focused</b>: Focused effects are optional effects that come with each Inference. It would specify a drawback that would narrow down its effect but would in turn grant bonuses to the specified action itself.<br /> <br /> <b>Axioms</b><br /> Axioms are composed of multiple base [Powers] that are available at each dot, most of which improve as the Inspired mastery of the Axiom and Inspiration grows. These powers cannot be integrated into Wonders on their own, but must be molded and focused by Inferences. Most Inferences grant optional bonuses to the base power while constricting it's targets, some Inferences simply grant new powers wholesale, though these are inevitably narrow in focus.<br /> <br /> <b>Example Axioms<br /> <br /> Exelixi</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Autonomous Repair </b>(\u2022): Wonders made using this [Power] can heal itself as if they were human.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Mending</b> (\u2022, and \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022): This [Power] allows for the genius the mend both organic and inorganic matter. He rolls Dexterity + Medicine or Crafts. Each success repairs one point of Structure</span></span> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">or Lethal damage or two points of Bashing damage.</span></span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Katastrofi</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Basic Damage </b>(\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022): The base effect of Katastrofi Wonders is dealing damage.<br /> <br /> At Katastrofi (\u2022) the Wonder can only deal Bashing damage.<br /> <br /> Katastrofi (\u2022\u2022) can deal Lethal damage and grants the 9-again quality to Bashing damage.<br /> <br /> Katastrofi (\u2022\u2022\u2022) Wonders can deal Aggravated damage, grants the 9-again quality to Lethal damage, and the 8-again quality to Bashing damage.<br /> <br /> Katastrofi (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) grants the 9-again quality to Aggravated damage and 8-again to both Lethal and Bashing damage.<br /> <br /> Katastrofi (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) grants 8-again on all damage.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Trait Reduction </b>(\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022): This [Power] allows the Wonder to remove dots in a Trait specified by the chosen Inference. This Trait is reduced by one dot per three Health Levels of damage that would have been dealt.<br /> <br /> At Katastrofi (\u2022) this Trait heals at the rate of Bashing damage, Lethal damage at Katastrofi (\u2022\u2022), and Aggravated damage at Katastrofi (\u2022\u2022\u2022).<br /> <br /> <b>Drain</b> (\u2022\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022): This [Power] allows Wonders to drain and disperse Metanormal Energies from the target, be it inflicting an Ephemeral Entity with Essence Bleed, literally making hemophages bleed, or stranger things.<br /> <br /> At Katastrofi (\u2022\u2022) those targeted are involved in a Clash of Wills with the Genius, if the target loses, it gains the Mild Power Bleed Condition. They lose one point of Metanormal Energy (Such as Vitae, Essence, Mana, Glamour, and Pyros) every hour. Once per the Genius' Inspiration in hours, the target repeats the Clash of Wills until it finally wins. The target can also spend a point of Willpower to force a Clash once per hour.<br /> <br /> Katastrofi (\u2022\u2022\u2022) inflicts the Moderate Power Bleed Condition, the target loses a point of Metanormal Energy every <i>half</i>-hour.<br /> <br /> Katastrofi (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) inflicts the Serious Power Bleed Condition, the target loses a point of Metanormal Energy every <i>minute</i>.<br /> <br /> Katastrofi (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) inflicts the Fatal Power Bleed Condition, the target loses a point of Metanormanl Energy each <i>turn </i>(3 seconds). At this stage the target may spend Willpower to force a Clash once per turn.</span></span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Skafoi</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Dimensional Travel</b> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(\u2022\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022): This [Power] allows the Wonder to access other dimensions.<br /> <br /> At Skafoi (\u2022\u2022) the Wonder can only open preexisting portals for access.<br /> <br /> Skafoi (\u2022\u2022\u2022) allows the Wonder to open new Dimensional Gates in locations where the barriers between worlds are particularly thin, such as Loci or places particularly attuned to death, for the Shadow and the Underworld respectively.<br /> <br /> Skafoi (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) allows the Wonder to open Gates to any Dimension anywhere.<br /> <br /> Skafoi (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) allows the Wonder to simply transport the Genius to another Dimension as an instant action, bypassing the need for Gates entirely.</span></span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Example Fields</b><br /> <br /> <b>Necronics</b> [Ghosts]<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> This Field is the study and manipulation of spectral beings and the Underworld.</div></div> </div> </div></span></span><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Required Skill</b>:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Occult</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Inferences</b>:</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Plasmic Regenerator</b> </span></span>(<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Exelixi):</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> This Inference uses the <b>Mending</b> [Power] of Exelixi, allowing it to heal the Corpus of ghosts, using Occult instead of Medicine in the roll.<br /> <b>Focused</b>: The Wonder can only heal ghosts, add the higher of geniuses Exelixi or Inspiration to the Dexterity + Occult roll.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ectoplasmic-Disintegrator </span></span></b>(<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Katastrofi): This Inference uses the <b>Basic Damage</b> [Power] of Katastrofi, allowing it to harm ghosts.<br /> <b>Focused</b>: The Wonder can only harm ghosts, who treat all attacks as coming from a being with an honorary Rank of the higher of the geniuses Katastrofi or Inspiration.<br /> <br /> <b>Plasmic Reductor </b>(Katastrofi): This Inference uses the <b>Trait Reduction </b>[Power] of Katastrofi, allowing it to reduce a ghost's Power, Finesse, or Resistance traits.<br /> <b>Focused</b>: The Wonder can only reduce a ghosts Traits, it can reduce Rank as well, which is reduced by one dot per five Health Levels of damage that would have been dealt. Reducing a ghost Rank to 0 would permanently destroy it as nothing of it remains.<br /> <br /> <b>Ecto-Drain </b>(Katastrofi): This Inference uses the <b>Drain</b> [Power] of Katastrofi, allowing it to drain a ghosts Essence.<br /> <b>Focused</b>: The Wonder can only drain ghosts, not even other Ephemerals, the ghost loses two points of Essence every interval.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Keymaster </b>(<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Skafoi)</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: This Inference uses the <b>Dimensional</b> [Power] of Skafoi, allowing it to open travel to the Underworld.<br /> <b>Focused</b>: The Wonder can only travel to the Underworld, it gains a bonus to the roll equal to the higher of the Genius' Inspiration or Skafoi</span></span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Faeries </b>[Fae]<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This Field is the study and manipulation of Fae beings and the Hedge</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Required Skill</b>:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Occult</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Inferences</b>:<br /> <br /> <b>Goblin Healing</b> (Exelixi): This Inference uses the <b>Mending</b> [Power] of Exelixi, allowing it to heal the Fae creatures, using Occult instead of Medicine in the roll when appropriate.<br /> <b>Focused</b>: The Wonder can only heal Fae, add the higher of geniuses Exelixi or Inspiration to the Dexterity + Skill roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Wyrd Reduction </b>(Katastrofi): This Inference uses the <b>Trait Reduction </b>[Power] of Katastrofi, allowing it to reduce a Fae's Attributes.<br /> <b>Focused</b>: The Wonder can only reduce a Fae's Traits, it can reduce Wyrd as well, which is reduced by one dot per five Health Levels of damage that would have been dealt.<br /> <br /> <b>Banality </b>(Katastrofi): This Inference uses the <b>Drain</b> [Power] of Katastrofi, allowing it to drain Glamour.<br /> <b>Focused</b>: The Wonder can only drain Glamour, the target loses two points of Glamour every interval.<br /> <br /> <b>Hedge Key </b>(Skafoi): This Inference uses the <b>Dimensional</b> [Power] of Skafoi, allowing it to open travel to the Hedge.<br /> <b>Focused</b>: The Wonder can only travel to the Hedge, it gains a bonus to the roll equal to the higher of the Genius' Inspiration or Skafoi</span></span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Edit</b>: Kinda iffy on the Drain [Power], is it overpowered?, I mean it basically fucks anything over at Katastrofi 5 so it fits there but the lower levels might be OP. I have never got an eye for these things","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12398,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","user":"DArchon5","date":". 04-28-2017, 11:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T10:16:31-07:00","id":1085489,"title":"","content":"So, do you think this system is too complicated? Or is it fine but needs some fine tuning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T19:49:44-07:00","id":1085661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DArchon5</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1085489#post1085489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, do you think this system is too complicated? Or is it fine but needs some fine tuning.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a bad start, I think, and people could certainly do interesting things with it. My system was kind of a mix of Werewolf Gifts/Facets and Mage spells, your seems to skew a little closer to Changeling Contracts. I personally prefer mine, but if people prefer yours, I'd be fine with going in that direction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T22:32:05-07:00","id":1085704,"title":"","content":"Alright then, now to Unmada. Should we give their Wonders bonuses for working within their Unmada Field due to resonant physics?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T05:58:51-07:00","id":1085767,"title":"","content":"Maybe Ex!Success on 3 instead of 5? And opposing Wonders/Effects lose 10-again?<br /> <br /> Or custom Conditions, like Mage has Nimbus?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T12:22:50-07:00","id":1085847,"title":"","content":"I think the Unmada field could be broken into three parts:<ul><li>The &quot;Paradigm Field&quot;: This imposes an illusion of the Genius's Paradigm on those around them. A Genius might be able to identify the handiwork of another by the traces of the Paradigm field. Things get a little weird around the Genius, in a very specific way to the Genius, but it's mostly cosmetic.</li> <li>The Unmada Field: An Unmada's Paradigm Field actually bends reality around them. Their Wonders explicitly working by means that suit their Paradigm get exceptional success on rolls to use within the field. This may also extend to other paranormal effects (A Narrativist Genius might also bolster certain aspects of the Wyrd). The field also imposes a Tilt on the area to reflect its effects. The field doesn't <i>actually</i> change reality, and when it is removed, things snap back to normal. A Genius can also invoke Deep Inspiration to temporarily invoke this field, risking Unmada status as normal.</li> <li>Asserting the Paradigm: Genii with opposing Paradigms interact weirdly, and often violently. A Genius can purposely lash out at an Inspired phenomenon (a Mane, a Wonder, a Bardo, etc.) that directly opposes their Paradigm, invoking a Clash of Wills (Presence + Inspiration vs. target's Composure + Inspiration). If the Genius successfully lashes out, the target suffers Havoc. On failure, the Genius instead gains the Beaten Down Tilt. How the Genius might lash out may vary from simple intimidation, to a projection of psychic energy, to a simple effort to disprove the opponent in a puff of logic.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T16:48:55-07:00","id":1085946,"title":"","content":"Love it, though if the power of such Fields are so potent we should probably lessen its range. Though an Inspiration 7+ Unmada would still be some sort of god in his own domain, I'm a bit iffy if that domain should still be an entire city. I mean, non-unmada geniuses using their Unmada Field would probably have intensely limited range and actual unmada would have longer reach, but the whole city-god thing should probably be reserved for either Inspiration 10 or the use of a Wonder of Pankosmoi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T04:36:39-07:00","id":1086130,"title":"","content":"Okay! I've been thinking and I do think failure is key ingredient of what it means to be mad scientist. Geniuses are heavily tied into tropes of supervillains and morally questionable heroes, which is why I feel like their Integrity should give leeway for those kind of characters. But there should be reason for players to try to sabotage Genius's own work as if they were doing it subconsciously. Why would Genius need to fail? Do they need to be proved wrong about something? What could separate most self indulgent and basdardly, villainous Genius from cold disconnected Illuminated? Answer to all thesequestions would be Faith. Geniuses need to have Faith in Humanity. Even most misanthropic Neid or transhumanist Hoffnung need to believethat at the end of the day humanity will go on. In the lowest end of the scale this Faith might even lashout similarly to hatred and anger, but Geniuses would be spewing their insults towards mankind while wishing that someone would come by to prove them wrong. Illuminated don't hate humanity, they don't care about it in the slightest beyond as part of their big plan.<br /> Geniuses loose Faith when they see mortals (or even beholden) raise up to the challange, when they fail to preprogrammed pattern Genius has foreseen them to go. They restore Faith when they see acts of selflessness and genuine kindness (which may be rare in World of Darkness), but also when humans raise against great odds (like destroying wannabe overlord's domination scheme). Taking this in account Hunters would indeed make an amazing source of Faith, but eventually cause it to deplete.<br /> So, what do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T07:39:45-07:00","id":1086191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1086130#post1086130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay! I've been thinking and I do think failure is key ingredient of what it means to be mad scientist. Geniuses are heavily tied into tropes of supervillains and morally questionable heroes, which is why I feel like their Integrity should give leeway for those kind of characters. But there should be reason for players to try to sabotage Genius's own work as if they were doing it subconsciously. Why would Genius need to fail? Do they need to be proved wrong about something? What could separate most self indulgent and basdardly, villainous Genius from cold disconnected Illuminated? Answer to all thesequestions would be Faith. Geniuses need to have Faith in Humanity. Even most misanthropic Neid or transhumanist Hoffnung need to believethat at the end of the day humanity will go on. In the lowest end of the scale this Faith might even lashout similarly to hatred and anger, but Geniuses would be spewing their insults towards mankind while wishing that someone would come by to prove them wrong. Illuminated don't hate humanity, they don't care about it in the slightest beyond as part of their big plan.<br /> Geniuses loose Faith when they see mortals (or even beholden) raise up to the challange, when they fail to preprogrammed pattern Genius has foreseen them to go. They restore Faith when they see acts of selflessness and genuine kindness (which may be rare in World of Darkness), but also when humans raise against great odds (like destroying wannabe overlord's domination scheme). Taking this in account Hunters would indeed make an amazing source of Faith, but eventually cause it to deplete.<br /> So, what do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we may want to move away from failure in a direct sense. I think &quot;Gone Horribly Right&quot; is a much more interesting angle to take, and there are already plenty of ways for the Genii to screw themselves (Havoc and Jabir, for example).<br /> <br /> The Integrity replacement I've been working on is Restraint, representing how well the Genius can control themselves and their Inspiration, as well as their general ability to fit in. At low levels, you have your Dr. Venture and your Victor Von Dooms, at high levels, you have your Lex Luthor and your Elon Musk-types. Renegades at the low end are more proactive, but have a harder time fitting in and are more likely to Illuminate. Paragons at the high end are more restrained and can hide their Inspiration better, but tend to choke up when shit gets real, and at extremely high Restraint, become nearly suicidally (or Genius-cidally) aware of how dangerous Inspiration is.<br /> <br /> Guys in the middle are good at laying low (they're not blowing up banks with plasma cannons, but they're also not building utopic arcology projects in downtown Detroit).<br /> <br /> Being at any point on the bar can have advantages and drawbacks.<br /> <br /> <sup><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1St0PBLVPHrBTVq-k9oZJz7DsPOyA_V1DYLaryVs60_o/\" target=\"_blank\">Oh, look, who left this here?</a></sup>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T10:16:27-07:00","id":1086244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1086191#post1086191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think we may want to move away from failure in a direct sense. I think &amp;quot;Gone Horribly Right&amp;quot; is a much more interesting angle to take, and there are already plenty of ways for the Genii to screw themselves (Havoc and Jabir, for example).<br /> <br /> The Integrity replacement I've been working on is Restraint, representing how well the Genius can control themselves and their Inspiration, as well as their general ability to fit in. At low levels, you have your Dr. Venture and your Victor Von Dooms, at high levels, you have your Lex Luthor and your Elon Musk-types. Renegades at the low end are more proactive, but have a harder time fitting in and are more likely to Illuminate. Paragons at the high end are more restrained and can hide their Inspiration better, but tend to choke up when shit gets real, and at extremely high Restraint, become nearly suicidally (or Genius-cidally) aware of how dangerous Inspiration is.<br /> <br /> Guys in the middle are good at laying low (they're not blowing up banks with plasma cannons, but they're also not building utopic arcology projects in downtown Detroit).<br /> <br /> Being at any point on the bar can have advantages and drawbacks.<br /> <br /> <sup><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1St0PBLVPHrBTVq-k9oZJz7DsPOyA_V1DYLaryVs60_o/\" target=\"_blank\">Oh, look, who left this here?</a></sup></div> </div> </div> </div>I like it. More to comment later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T13:29:24-07:00","id":1086309,"title":"","content":"Just a thought,<br /> <br /> Wouldn't it be more engaging for the players to have a gauge going from 1 to 10 tracking how willing they are to break the laws of reality over their knee rather than a gauge from 10 to 1 tracking how much self-control they have? <br /> <br /> That way it more encourages players to invite trouble onto their doorstep through their actions rather than work to upkeep their societal standings. And, it allows the players themselves to decide just how &quot;mad&quot; their scientist is. Plus it can work to gauge the scope of the Chronicles the players want since a low (let's just call it...I don't know...Transgression) Genius would probably prefer more localized stories involving them trying to have a normal life, while a high Transgression Genius would want to be off dimension hopping and having space battles with the Lemurians, Outer Spirits, and God Machine Angels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T17:08:25-07:00","id":1086387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1086309#post1086309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a thought,<br /> <br /> Wouldn't it be more engaging for the players to have a gauge going from 1 to 10 tracking how willing they are to break the laws of reality over their knee rather than a gauge from 10 to 1 tracking how much self-control they have?<br /> <br /> That way it more encourages players to invite trouble onto their doorstep through their actions rather than work to upkeep their societal standings. And, it allows the players themselves to decide just how &quot;mad&quot; their scientist is. Plus it can work to gauge the scope of the Chronicles the players want since a low (let's just call it...I don't know...Transgression) Genius would probably prefer more localized stories involving them trying to have a normal life, while a high Transgression Genius would want to be off dimension hopping and having space battles with the Lemurians, Outer Spirits, and God Machine Angels.</div> </div> </div> </div>That might work as a hack for encouraging even pulpier play, but I think I prefer Restraint personally. Anyone else want to weigh in?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T19:26:25-07:00","id":1086433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1086387#post1086387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That might work as a hack for encouraging even pulpier play, but I think I prefer Restraint personally. Anyone else want to weigh in?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd second (or third?) Restraint. Inspiration kinda serves as the barometer for &quot;physics, shut up and do what I say&quot; already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T19:41:51-07:00","id":1086438,"title":"","content":"Restraint is good. Yeah, in other news. What about Unmada Fields?. Unmada is now a Condition but maybe we should make the Field part of the drawbacks of powerfull Inspiration? Like, even while not Unmada those of Inspiration 6+ have their beliefs reinforced in subtle but pervasive ways. The Narrativists life becomes more like fiction and the like. Not enough no warp reality in obvious ways but enough to risk detection from others who know what to look for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T19:52:39-07:00","id":1086441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DArchon5</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1086438#post1086438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Restraint is good. Yeah, in other news. What about Unmada Fields?. Unmada is now a Condition but maybe we should make the Field part of the drawbacks of powerfull Inspiration? Like, even while not Unmada those of Inspiration 6+ have their beliefs reinforced in subtle but pervasive ways. The Narrativists life becomes more like fiction and the like. Not enough no warp reality in obvious ways but enough to risk detection from others who know what to look for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds good. Intermediate Inspiration gives 9-again to recognize a <i>specific</i> Genius's field when you're present. High Inspiration gives 9-again to recognizes the traces of it, and makes recognizing it when you're actually present pretty much an automatic success?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":4488,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","user":"malonkey1","date":". 05-01-2017, 10:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T20:11:40-07:00","id":1086443,"title":"","content":"Fair enough, but before I slink back off to the Bolthole let me make one last sales pitch for Transgression. <br /> <br /> With Transgression, the player's actions and consiquences become the forefront of Genius' Integrity system. An Inspired's Transgression would rise without roll every time they cross a greater threshold between what is possible and shouldn't be possible, and all instances that the line is crossed accidentally or unintentionally would result in a threshold roll. Rising in Transgression would give scientific beats (if you folks are still incorporating something like arcane beats) and bestow conditions relative to the consiquences of the Genii's Transgression (becoming noticed by Hunters or the God Machine, creating time paradoxes, instilling a panic amongst the city's residents, even Unmada.) Which in turn generates more beats and incentivizes the Genii to Transgress further until they run the risk of Transgressing so far that they either make a powerful enough enemy to destroy themselves, have a large enough miscalculation to destroy themselves (and maybe erase a city from known history), or even most horrifying of all...actually succeed in their wildest dreams. <br /> <br /> If nothing else at least make certain actions and character decisions automatic Restraint decreases. That way it truly feels like the gauge is an honest representation of just how far a Genius is willing to go for their Vision.<br /> <br /> That is all I have for now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Spellcheck 05-01-2017, 11:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T20:19:55-07:00","id":1086444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1086443#post1086443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If nothing else at least make certain actions and character decisions automatic Restraint decreases. That way it truly feels like the gauge is an honest representation of just how far a Genius is willing to go for their Vision.<br /> <br /> That is all I have for now.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is something we may want to include, actually. Morality Chains for Renegades and Moral (or Social, I suppose) Event Horizons for Paragons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T01:40:53-07:00","id":1086522,"title":"","content":"Question as I haven't been keeping up with this thread super often. What is there to keep the masquerade? Is it still just mundane break wonders and geniuses are poor at explaining things?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T01:53:38-07:00","id":1086523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1086522#post1086522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question as I haven't been keeping up with this thread super often. What is there to keep the masquerade? Is it still just mundane break wonders and geniuses are poor at explaining things?</div> </div> </div> </div>Currently, Geniuses with Restraint 4-7 like to lay low and avoid attention, Havoc works with range if the mortal is smart enough, a possible copy of Syballis that drives people mad with Wonders, and the fact that Wonders would be dismissed as flukes 'cause there not replicable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T02:23:58-07:00","id":1086526,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure how people would consider a laser cannon which can be fired multiple times a fluke... Just because mortal science can't figureout what what x is in a formula doesn't mean they'll just give up. Especially when the genius can make multiple of the wonders.<br /> <br /> How would they think a giant mecha was &quot;just a fluke I'll pay no attention to it&quot; rather than &quot;holy crap that's a mecha I'm getting out my phone and filming this&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T04:12:10-07:00","id":1086543,"title":"","content":"The biggest elephant in the room when it comes to genius, at least for me, has always been how their superscience hasn't changed the world or how they manage to remain hidden from the rest of society.<br /> Restraint is a very good way to explain why they censor themselves and try not to draw attention, I love it, but even then I think we need more. It doesn't need to be one thing, it can be a combination of factors on top of restraint. Maybe society rejects their discoveries because it's no ready for them, maybe there are powerful people who don't want society to change, etc...<br /> Even if their wonders can't be reproduced or tend to be very unstable, just the fact that they're technological devices will make regular scientists try to reproduce their effects somehow, and that pushes technological development, even if it's just a little bit. A dedicated scientist doesn't need to understand it, just knowing that it's possible will make him try and push forward. In a certain way it's the whole point of being a genius, not only are they inspired, their mere existence inspires people around them.<br /> This are just some general observations, although I haven't had time to go through all the posts I like the changes that are being introduced, I just would like a bit more development in these two areas of the setting, that's all. Good luck with it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2964,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","user":"Firanai","date":". 05-02-2017, 07:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T05:36:52-07:00","id":1086564,"title":"","content":"Just thought of something. Reverse Engineering Wonders, not mortals doing it, but other geniuses. This would let them simply steal the knowledge of its Field rather than working to get it. It wouldn't be as quick as a teacher but it would be better than starting from scratch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T05:39:43-07:00","id":1086567,"title":"","content":"<b>Edit:</b> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12398\" data-vbnamecard=\"12398\">DArchon5</a> Yeah, we were going to have that. You can reverse-engineer Wonders, Manes, and paranormal phenomena to open up new Fields and act as Theses for increasing Inspiration or Axiom ratings.<br /> <br /> The &quot;masquerade&quot; is a combination of:<ul><li>Havoc breaking Wonders</li> <li>Many Wonders being impossible for most people to replicate, and those that <i>can</i> replicate it are either Edisons* or working with a Wonder that's within the realm of mortal theoretical knowledge anyway.</li> <li>The Peerage and Lemuria keeping things quiet for their respective reasons (&quot;mankind's not ready&quot; and &quot;We're called <i>secret masters</i> for a reason, guys!&quot;)</li> <li>the Restraint of many Genii</li> <li>People being willing to rationalize things away, like with a lot of the weird stuff</li> <li>The sheer expense of a lot of bigger projects makes them rare and slow-going</li> <li>and finally, Genii voluntarily hiding for their own benefit.</li> </ul><br /> There's not a lot <i>enforcing</i> the masquerade unless you want it to. I wouldn't be surprised to see a few Genii that have to act as cleaners, mopping up the nonsense other Genii leave and possibly removing Genii who get too loud or rowdy. If a person sees a giant mecha in the streets, that might out a specific mad scientist, who might have to answer to the Cleaners, the Peerage or Lemuria at large, their close colleagues who aren't interested in being outed, as well as Edisons* who might want to get their hands on a mech to sell to the military.<br /> <br /> *As a side note, Edisons are intended to be sort of semi-Inspired, analogous to Wolf-Blooded, Proximi or Fae-Touched. Their deal is that they have a limited capacity to store and use Mania, and can reproduce Wonders that they've analyzed, but they can't make their own and depend on Genii for what they do. On the flip side, they're much more magnetic and able to fit in socially, making them a tempting proxy for Genii who want to make a buck off their Wonders. However, if you know the story of Tesla and Edison, you'll probably know why working with an Edison might not be a great idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":4488,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","user":"malonkey1","date":". 05-02-2017, 08:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T11:41:30-07:00","id":1086723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1086567#post1086567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Edit:</b> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12398\" data-vbnamecard=\"12398\">DArchon5</a> Yeah, we were going to have that. You can reverse-engineer Wonders, Manes, and paranormal phenomena to open up new Fields and act as Theses for increasing Inspiration or Axiom ratings.<br /> <br /> The &quot;masquerade&quot; is a combination of:<ul><li>Havoc breaking Wonders</li> <li>Many Wonders being impossible for most people to replicate, and those that <i>can</i> replicate it are either Edisons* or working with a Wonder that's within the realm of mortal theoretical knowledge anyway.</li> <li>The Peerage and Lemuria keeping things quiet for their respective reasons (&quot;mankind's not ready&quot; and &quot;We're called <i>secret masters</i> for a reason, guys!&quot;)</li> <li>the Restraint of many Genii</li> <li>People being willing to rationalize things away, like with a lot of the weird stuff</li> <li>The sheer expense of a lot of bigger projects makes them rare and slow-going</li> <li>and finally, Genii voluntarily hiding for their own benefit.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> There's not a lot <i>enforcing</i> the masquerade unless you want it to. I wouldn't be surprised to see a few Genii that have to act as cleaners, mopping up the nonsense other Genii leave and possibly removing Genii who get too loud or rowdy. If a person sees a giant mecha in the streets, that might out a specific mad scientist, who might have to answer to the Cleaners, the Peerage or Lemuria at large, their close colleagues who aren't interested in being outed, as well as Edisons* who might want to get their hands on a mech to sell to the military.<br /> <br /> *As a side note, Edisons are intended to be sort of semi-Inspired, analogous to Wolf-Blooded, Proximi or Fae-Touched. Their deal is that they have a limited capacity to store and use Mania, and can reproduce Wonders that they've analyzed, but they can't make their own and depend on Genii for what they do. On the flip side, they're much more magnetic and able to fit in socially, making them a tempting proxy for Genii who want to make a buck off their Wonders. However, if you know the story of Tesla and Edison, you'll probably know why working with an Edison might not be a great idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome explanation, with all of that combined it seems more plausible. If you allow me I would like to one more. Keep the number of geniuses low, not just because few manage to become geniuses, but also due to the inherent dangers of their lives many end up dead, that makes exposure to their craziness even less likely.<br /> Keep doing an awesome job. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T13:27:56-07:00","id":1086759,"title":"","content":"*Bolthole door swings open*...<br /> <br /> Damnit, quite bringing up such good points that I'd like to talk about. :/<br /> <br /> I agree with Firanai that the Genii's masquerade needs to be a little more potent considering how there's of yet very little masquerade mechanics involved when dealing with Genius' Wonders. My suggestion is a little more proactive though, and draws upon the spirit of my earlier lobbying. <br /> <br /> Bring back the Secret War. It's one thing for the Peerage and Lemuria to police themselves, but making the danger of outside notice could be even more rewarding for Chronicles. Make the battle for the development of humankind a war that involves all kinds of mortal and supernatural conspiracies that range from purely local to cosmic in scope. The war can be a sort of cold-war due to the rapid development of technology during this century, but make it clear that bringing attention of your Wonders and Vision to the wrong people could be a death sentence...or worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T13:43:52-07:00","id":1086769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1086759#post1086759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Bolthole door swings open*...<br /> <br /> Damnit, quite bringing up such good points that I'd like to talk about. :/<br /> <br /> I agree with Firanai that the Genii's masquerade needs to be a little more potent considering how there's of yet very little masquerade mechanics involved when dealing with Genius' Wonders. My suggestion is a little more proactive though, and draws upon the spirit of my earlier lobbying.<br /> <br /> Bring back the Secret War. It's one thing for the Peerage and Lemuria to police themselves, but making the danger of outside notice could be even more rewarding for Chronicles. Make the battle for the development of humankind a war that involves all kinds of mortal and supernatural conspiracies that range from purely local to cosmic in scope. The war can be a sort of cold-war due to the rapid development of technology during this century, but make it clear that bringing attention of your Wonders and Vision to the wrong people could be a death sentence...or worse.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I could certainly see some plot hooks thrown in to support it as well - with the Guardians of Forever gone (for the moment - try back later), who is to say you don't have future Genii and other forces enforcing their own masquerade for whatever reasons? If their timeline isn't based on &quot;Fifty-foot robot destroys DC&quot;, then the erstwhile Genius building said contraption could quietly end up dead in their bathtub before the legs are completed.<br /> <br /> Queue investigation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T14:26:03-07:00","id":1086793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1086769#post1086769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I could certainly see some plot hooks thrown in to support it as well - with the Guardians of Forever gone (for the moment - try back later), who is to say you don't have future Genii and other forces enforcing their own masquerade for whatever reasons? If their timeline isn't based on &quot;Fifty-foot robot destroys DC&quot;, then the erstwhile Genius building said contraption could quietly end up dead in their bathtub before the legs are completed.<br /> <br /> Queue investigation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't even consider the &quot;temporal cold war&quot; angle. That's good!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T08:02:30-07:00","id":1087159,"title":"","content":"Guys, I think I found one of the the reasons geniouses don't change the world with their tech, they have other priorities..... <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://imgur.com/1kRIvC9\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://imgur.com/1kRIvC9\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://imgur.com/1kRIvC9\" target=\"_blank\"> http://imgur.com/1kRIvC9 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T09:15:31-07:00","id":1087196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1087159#post1087159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guys, I think I found one of the the reasons geniouses don't change the world with their tech, they have other priorities.....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://imgur.com/1kRIvC9\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://imgur.com/1kRIvC9\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://imgur.com/1kRIvC9\" target=\"_blank\"> http://imgur.com/1kRIvC9 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Strictly sepaking, yeah. Genii are pretty selfish jerks a lot of the time. &quot;Cut Lex Luthor a Check&quot; is the operating principle here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T15:26:03-07:00","id":1087356,"title":"","content":"Another issue is that changing the world with your tech requires gathering investors and writing up business plans, and people tend to frown upon world-wide Epikrato. Even if you went with something feasible for a starting character like building an Apokalypsi 2 Wonderthat allows all people of the world to communicate perfectly with one another, you are essentially building the Tower of Babel (with all the negative connotations that come with this, even if said Wonder fits in a large shopping bag). Oh, and you're still violating the physical integrity of the entire human race with the push of a button, but if you care about such things you're playing the wrong game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T19:12:09-07:00","id":1087461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1087356#post1087356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another issue is that changing the world with your tech requires gathering investors and writing up business plans, and people tend to frown upon world-wide Epikrato. Even if you went with something feasible for a starting character like building an Apokalypsi 2 Wonderthat allows all people of the world to communicate perfectly with one another, you are essentially building the Tower of Babel (with all the negative connotations that come with this, even if said Wonder fits in a large shopping bag). Oh, and you're still violating the physical integrity of the entire human race with the push of a button, but if you care about such things you're playing the wrong game.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm pretty sure that's another instance like Vent0 mentioned where if that Genii is 100% dead set on making their Tower of Babel then they'll quietly end up dead in their bathtub before the investor sales pitch is even drafted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T20:15:57-07:00","id":1087483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1087356#post1087356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">you are essentially building the Tower of Babel (with all the negative connotations that come with this, even if said Wonder fits in a large shopping bag).</div> </div> </div> </div>Popping in briefly after this reminded me to suggest that if there's still any incentive to make Huge Wonders it be as a prerequisite for large effects; in Mage terms, having Wonders with particularly extreme applications have infrastructural/logistical Scale requirements in dedicated personnel, space, and/or supernaturally-potent resources (with man-portable applications of those effects being a function of relays and similar traceable conveyances), and plot-device level effects like flying cities or nation-wide mind control are things that take legendary characters to accomplish within a mortal lifetime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 05-04-2017, 11:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T18:31:21-07:00","id":1094739,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1086759#post1086759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Bolthole door swings open*...</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1086759#post1086759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Damnit, quit bringing up such good points that I'd like to talk about. :/</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I agree with Firanai that the Genii's masquerade needs to be a little more potent considering how there's of yet very little masquerade mechanics involved when dealing with Genius' Wonders. My suggestion is a little more proactive though, and draws upon the spirit of my earlier lobbying.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Bring back the Secret War. It's one thing for the Peerage and Lemuria to police themselves, but making the danger of outside notice could be even more rewarding for Chronicles. Make the battle for the development of humankind a war that involves all kinds of mortal and supernatural conspiracies that range from purely local to cosmic in scope. The war can be a sort of cold-war due to the rapid development of technology during this century, but make it clear that bringing attention of your Wonders and Vision to the wrong people could be a death sentence...or worse.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1086769#post1086769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could certainly see some plot hooks thrown in to support it as well - with the Guardians of Forever gone (for the moment - try back later), who is to say you don't have future Genii and other forces enforcing their own masquerade for whatever reasons? If their timeline isn't based on &quot;Fifty-foot robot destroys DC&quot;, then the erstwhile Genius building said contraption could quietly end up dead in their bathtub before the legs are completed.<br /> <br /> Queue investigation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I support bringing back the Secret War, but I believe we should keep its history open for customization, in order to keep the 2ED in line with the toolbox nature of the CoD. Any ideas about &quot;historical figure X was Inspired!&quot; should be strictly in the realm of rumors, legends and propaganda. The Inspired tend to be outcasts, mavericks and freaks by nature, after all. The inclusion of time travel in the Secret War should be optional, hard to accomplish and largely experimental. If it was easy and reliable, it would be used to fix every little mistake and there would be no plot. In fact, some of the conflicts and lost information of the Secret War may have been caused by cumulative failed attempts at time travel, which were only partially fixed by disparate organizations and forces. Fix one thing, and you'll break another. The fall of one Genius' Magnum Opus gives rise to another. No One Is In Charge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T18:58:22-07:00","id":1094742,"title":"","content":"Another idea: since some of us have pointed out that there is too much focus on Mad Engineering and Mental Skills, which doesn't leave enough room for other types of Inspired, here's what we could do.<br /> <br /> The main dice pool for building Wonders can be Any Attribute + Any Skill + Inspiration.<br /> <br /> Let's imagine a Genius who is all about harnessing esoteric vital energies like chakra to go past his human limits. As a Navigator, he specializes in harnessing vital energy to improve his physical performance by constantly training in martial arts, meditating and such. When he wants to develop a new fighting technique (an Internalized Katastrofi Wonder), instead of rolling Intelligence + Medicine + Inspiration, he could roll Composure + Brawl + Inspiration. Composure represents discipline and mastery of the self, Brawl represents knowledge of the body's workings in combat, and the Inspiration is responsible for making the vital energies flow. The Components of such a Wonder might include: rare scrolls detailing the techniques of forgotten or legendary martial arts masters, herbs and incenses located in the Hedge or an Atlantean Temple, a duel with a supernatural warrior of great skill, solving an esoteric spiritual riddle given by a powerful Spirit, and so on.<br /> <br /> This could be applied to all sorts of Geniuses. As another example, an Inspired politician could roll Presence + Expression + Inspiration, with the Components being the various parts of the Wondrous political campaign.<br /> <br /> As a consequence, Kitbashing would be expanded. The aforementioned martial artist could improvise a fighting technique by rolling Wits + Brawl + Inspiration, or a defensive maneuver by rolling Dexterity + Athletics + Inspiration. The Havoc would be applied to his body and mind. In the case of the politician, he could improvise most of what they need in a pinch by rolling Manipulation + Subterfuge/Persuasion/Politics + Inspiration. The Havoc is applied to his reputation and everything linked to it, which may include objects and people if his campaign was supporting hospitals and people suddenly think they're corrupt.<br /> <br /> What do you guys think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 05-19-2017, 10:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T19:10:49-07:00","id":1094746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1094742#post1094742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another idea: since some of us have pointed out that there is too much focus on Mad Engineering and Mental Skills, which doesn't leave enough room for other types of Inspired, here's what we could do.<br /> <br /> The main dice pool for building Wonders can be Any Attribute + Any Skill + Inspiration.<br /> <br /> Let's imagine a Genius who is all about harnessing esoteric vital energies like chakra to go past his human limits. As a Navigator, he specializes in harnessing vital energy to improve his physical performance by constantly training in martial arts, meditating and such. When he wants to develop a new fighting technique (an Internalized Katastrofi Wonder), instead of rolling Intelligence + Medicine + Inspiration, he could roll Composure + Brawl + Inspiration. Composure represents discipline and mastery of the self, Brawl represents knowledge of the body's workings in combat, and the Inspiration is responsible for making the vital energies flow. The Components of such a Wonder might include: rare scrolls detailing the techniques of forgotten or legendary martial arts masters, herbs and incenses located in the Hedge or an Atlatean Temple, a duel with a supernatural warrior of great skill, solving an esoteric spiritual riddle given by a powerful Spirit, and so on.<br /> <br /> This could be applied to all sorts of Geniuses. As another example, an Inspired politician could roll Presence + Expression + Inspiration, with the Components being the various parts of the Wondrous political campaign.<br /> <br /> As a consequence, Kitbashing would be expanded. The aforementioned martial artist could improvise a fighting technique by rolling Wits + Brawl + Inspiration, or a defensive maneuver by rolling Dexterity + Athletics + Inspiration. The Havoc would be applied to his body and mind. In the case of the politician, he could improvise most of what they need in a pinch by rolling Manipulation + Subterfuge/Persuasion/Politics + Inspiration. The Havoc is applied to his reputation and everything linked to it, which may include objects and people if his campaign was supporting hospitals and people suddenly think they're corrupt.<br /> <br /> What do you guys think?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was gonna go with either Attribute + Skill + Primary Axiom (of the Wonder), but Attribute + Skill + Inspiration could also work. The dice pool would get a bit larger at higher-level play, and be more broadly applicable, but wouldn't grow as rapidly in the short term for specific kinds of Wonders.<br /> <br /> I think it will depend on what Wonders shape up to be. I might reorient them to be a tinge more like Hunter Endowments, but I'll have to wait and see. I should have time later this week to think on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T19:16:34-07:00","id":1094747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1094746#post1094746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was gonna go with either Attribute + Skill + Primary Axiom (of the Wonder), but Attribute + Skill + Inspiration could also work. The dice pool would get a bit larger at higher-level play, and be more broadly applicable, but wouldn't grow as rapidly in the short term for specific kinds of Wonders.<br /> <br /> I think it will depend on what Wonders shape up to be. I might reorient them to be a tinge more like Hunter Endowments, but I'll have to wait and see. I should have time later this week to think on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>In what sense would they be like Hunter Endowments? You could also use [highest between main Axiom and Inspiration] in the dice pool.<br /> <br /> Do you like my idea of changing the main dice pool for Wonder Creation to make playing alternative Geniuses easier? How about the expanded Kitbashing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 05-19-2017, 10:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T20:04:02-07:00","id":1094763,"title":"","content":"I'm always for more options. Especially when one considers how broad &quot;technology&quot; and science are.<br /> <br /> As for the 2E Endowment model... how so? Wonders as kinda-Conditions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-20T06:51:11-07:00","id":1094854,"title":"","content":"I think there should be no magic inspection i think and this is just me that instead of mad science it should be simply any skill but improved<br /> super science<br /> chakra<br /> meme making<br /> ans more<br /> but that my 2 cents","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-20T07:50:31-07:00","id":1094863,"title":"","content":"It has been brought to my attention that Skafoi is arguably a better combat Axiom than Katastrofi due to the vehicle collision rules. How can we limit the damage output of Skafoi in a way that makes sense?<br /> <br /> EDIT: In the words of Altasaire from Discord:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Regarding fleshing out Near-Earth space through Skafoi... Where Mage is very Mysteries-driven and there are a lot of Mysteries on the world (and there are no really fleshed out ways offworld except Space teleport, even if a canny player can flesh out some more of those), Genius is, in part, built on the raygun gothic aesthetic narratively, and on &quot;to boldly go&quot;.<br /> <br /> And when a starting character can build an offworld-capable thing by raiding the nearest dumpster and hardware store? You need to give at least some hints to what's there. And there you start to run into gribblies of the other splats, specifically proto-Idigam and other WtF gribblies beyond the Moon's orbit. </div> </div> </div>Maybe our solar system can be reached by starting characters, but going outside the galaxy is a Magnum Opus?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 05-20-2017, 10:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-20T11:35:35-07:00","id":1094900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1094863#post1094863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It has been brought to my attention that Skafoi is arguably a better combat Axiom than Katastrofi due to the vehicle collision rules. How can we limit the damage output of Skafoi in a way that makes sense?<br /> <br /> EDIT: In the words of Altasaire from Discord:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Maybe our solar system can be reached by starting characters, but going outside the galaxy is a Magnum Opus?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, what degree of &quot;Alt-Reality&quot; is FTL travel? Are Aliens subject to Mane!Havoc? Are there arguments that extra-terrestrial worlds are just a different kind of Bardo? Are interstellar powers another actor in the Secret/Invisible War(s)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-20T14:08:02-07:00","id":1094940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1094900#post1094900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, what degree of &quot;Alt-Reality&quot; is FTL travel? Are Aliens subject to Mane!Havoc? Are there arguments that extra-terrestrial worlds are just a different kind of Bardo? Are interstellar powers another actor in the Secret/Invisible War(s)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I'd say that aliens may or may not exist, and that most of them are very unfriendly and, well, <i>alien</i>. Some alien worlds might be Bardos, especially ones that have been disproved like the sundry kinds of Martians, but others might exist, far away.<br /> <br /> I don't think aliens will be a default part of the setting, human-level, comprehensible aliens even less so, but I won't rule them out. They'd probably skew more toward Xenomorphs and Body-Snatchers than Vulcans and Asari.<br /> <br /> I'm fine with providing for players who want to explore space, but it's hard to change society if you're parsecs away from it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-20T15:44:24-07:00","id":1094958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1094940#post1094940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, I'd say that aliens may or may not exist, and that most of them are very unfriendly and, well, <i>alien</i>. Some alien worlds might be Bardos, especially ones that have been disproved like the sundry kinds of Martians, but others might exist, far away.<br /> <br /> I don't think aliens will be a default part of the setting, human-level, comprehensible aliens even less so, but I won't rule them out. They'd probably skew more toward Xenomorphs and Body-Snatchers than Vulcans and Asari.<br /> <br /> I'm fine with providing for players who want to explore space, but it's hard to change society if you're parsecs away from it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if Aliens were handled similar to Manes and Bardos, then that explains why you can't just bring ET back home for revelation, or conquer the world with alien hyper-tech.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-20T17:30:54-07:00","id":1094974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1094958#post1094958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, if Aliens were handled similar to Manes and Bardos, then that explains why you can't just bring ET back home for revelation, or conquer the world with alien hyper-tech.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose, but then you have the fact that people have probably already tried this, and there are probably Genii who try to make sure it doesn't happen. Not to mention that aliens probably aren't too keen on being abducted, tipping their hand, or giving out their advanced tech, and may possibly have something like the Prime Directive.<br /> <br /> Though, you could probably make a whole campaign out of answering the Fermi Paradox, so as always, it can be left open to players and Storytellers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-20T23:25:54-07:00","id":1095032,"title":"","content":"I still find it odd Bardos are called Bardos. The term in genius has nothing to do with Bardos, and the term Bardos is a Buddhism term not a science or sci-fi term, so it's always seemed odd seeing it over and over.<br /> <br /> Anyone have any ideas for a different term which could be used which fits the aesthetics of the game more accurately?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-20T23:59:10-07:00","id":1095037,"title":"","content":"Shard or Splinter.<br /> <br /> Demon already uses those terms, why not adopt it too to follow that timeless CofD tradition of having multiple things that are similar be named the same? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T01:44:33-07:00","id":1095063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1095032#post1095032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still find it odd Bardos are called Bardos. The term in genius has nothing to do with Bardos, and the term Bardos is a Buddhism term not a science or sci-fi term, so it's always seemed odd seeing it over and over.<br /> <br /> Anyone have any ideas for a different term which could be used which fits the aesthetics of the game more accurately?</div> </div> </div> </div>Bardo, or antarabhava, is any liminal state or a thing (from tibetan bar+do &quot;divide in two&quot; and cognate to Old English bord &quot;a plank, flat surface,&quot; from Proto-Germanic *burdam (source also of Old Norse bor\u00f0 &quot;plank,&quot; Dutch bord &quot;board,&quot; German Brett &quot;plank&quot;), from PIE *bhrdh- &quot;board,&quot; from root *bherdh- &quot;to cut, divide&quot; and through &quot;board&quot; cognate to the modern word &quot;border&quot; ).<br /> <br /> Bardos, outside the general six bardos of death/sleep/etc, were also used in tibetan thought exercises of the nirmita, also known as tulpa, where the practitioner formed a figure of the mind, limited by the circle of their will (bardo, liminality, limit), learnt what he could from it of the illusory nature of the world, then banished it. Given that inhabitants of the Bardos in Genius do exhibit a lot of the qualities of being 'unreal', because they live in a disproven world, it is quite apropos that their worlds (or, probably, at first, the skins and borders of their worlds) would have been called such by ancient Geniuses.<br /> <br /> As to it being 'not sci-fi'... Why should it be? Geniuses are vastly older than the modern conception of sci-fi and exist in all parts of the world, why should their preferred terms not show a mish-mash of cultures?<br /> <br /> tl;dr -- it's a perfectly good word that does mean what it means, please do not change it for the sake of changing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10091-altasaire","name":"Altasaire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10091_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T02:35:27-07:00","id":1095070,"title":"","content":"can someone just sum up everything decused on this thread for someone new to this thread","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T03:19:47-07:00","id":1095074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ameraaaaaa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1095070#post1095070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">can someone just sum up everything decused on this thread for someone new to this thread</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Everything should be changed and while we all have ideas and a document containing said ideas we're still far from having something playable.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T05:53:15-07:00","id":1095100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Altasaire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1095063#post1095063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Bardo, or antarabhava, is any liminal state or a thing (from tibetan bar+do &quot;divide in two&quot; and cognate to Old English bord &quot;a plank, flat surface,&quot; from Proto-Germanic *burdam (source also of Old Norse bor\u00f0 &quot;plank,&quot; Dutch bord &quot;board,&quot; German Brett &quot;plank&quot;), from PIE *bhrdh- &quot;board,&quot; from root *bherdh- &quot;to cut, divide&quot; and through &quot;board&quot; cognate to the modern word &quot;border&quot; ).<br /> <br /> Bardos, outside the general six bardos of death/sleep/etc, were also used in tibetan thought exercises of the nirmita, also known as tulpa, where the practitioner formed a figure of the mind, limited by the circle of their will (bardo, liminality, limit), learnt what he could from it of the illusory nature of the world, then banished it. Given that inhabitants of the Bardos in Genius do exhibit a lot of the qualities of being 'unreal', because they live in a disproven world, it is quite apropos that their worlds (or, probably, at first, the skins and borders of their worlds) would have been called such by ancient Geniuses.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's... not an accurate description of what bardos are as far as I can tell. They're the states between life and death, and sometimes the stages of &quot;Life, Various levels of thought, Death, Truth, Transformation into new life&quot; depending on the faith. And yes, in such faiths &quot;reality&quot; is a illusion created by the limited awareness of reality, but bardos are not actually part of the maya/nirmita, one of the stages in the six bardos (the one which is between dying and being reborn and which the term bardo refers to most of the time) is even specifically defined by the truth of existence being laid bare. Bardos are not tulpa in any material I've read. They're not will manifest, they're not thoughtforms. They're they stages which separate life and death.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As to it being 'not sci-fi'... Why should it be? </div> </div> </div>I can see it being acceptable to use scientific terms for things in a game like genius. I'm not suggesting it needs to sound sci-fi, but since it doesn't really match what bardos are in the game AND it isn't sci-fi, it fails the two main criteria for making sense as a game term for Genius. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> tl;dr -- it's a perfectly good word that does mean what it means, please do not change it for the sake of changing it. </div> </div> </div>Not suggesting it be changed for the sake of changing it, I'm suggesting it be changed because it's a term about existence between life and reincarnating... not fantasy lands made from thoughts that went rogue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 05-21-2017, 08:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T06:18:00-07:00","id":1095106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1095100#post1095100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's... not an accurate description of what bardos are as far as I can tell. They're the states between life and death, and sometimes the stages of &quot;Life, Various levels of thought, Death, Truth, Transformation into new life&quot; depending on the faith. And yes, in such faiths &quot;reality&quot; is a illusion created by the limited awareness of reality, but bardos are not actually part of the maya/nirmita, one of the stages in the six bardos (the one which is between dying and being reborn and which the term bardo refers to most of the time) is even specifically defined by the truth of existence being laid bare. Bardos are not tulpa in any material I've read. They're not will manifest, they're not thoughtforms. They're they stages which separate life and death.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>States of mind, stages of life, and realms of existence are often not so separate in Buddhist and Hindu schools of thought. But yeah, Bardos are supposed to be transcendental, not illusory. Unless it's the Genii's madness warping their perspectives so that their illusions appear transcendental. Which, now that I think of it, is fitting for Genii in general.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> I can see it being acceptable to use scientific terms for things in a game like genius. I'm not suggesting it needs to sound sci-fi, but since it doesn't really match what bardos are in the game AND it isn't sci-fi, it fails the two main criteria for making sense as a game term for Genius.<br /> <br /> <br /> Not suggesting it be changed for the sake of changing it, I'm suggesting it be changed because it's a term about existence between life and reincarnating... not fantasy lands made from thoughts that went rogue. </div> </div> </div>I just hope that the Sci-Fi terms don't get <i>too </i>professional. The level of jargon in Demon and Mage is the right level I'd prefer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T06:24:17-07:00","id":1095107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1095106#post1095106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> States of mind, stages of life, and realms of existence are often not so separate in Buddhist and Hindu schools of thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh definitely, it's just more &quot;Supernal realm&quot; style place that is both a place and a state of existence rather than say &quot;Narnia&quot;. :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T06:34:04-07:00","id":1095108,"title":"","content":"If I may give my own opinion, I like the Bardos name just fine, and I am not sure it's needed to change it. But eh, that's just me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T06:45:34-07:00","id":1095113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1095108#post1095108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I may give my own opinion, I like the Bardos name just fine, and I am not sure it's needed to change it. But eh, that's just me.</div> </div> </div> </div>We can always, instead of getting rid of an ill-fitting name, slightly tweak the setting so that the name ends up fitting it.<br /> <br /> &quot;Bardo&quot; originally means states of liminality where your consciousness transcends its normal limits, and is etymologically related to &quot;boundary.&quot; Genii of ancient times who didn't quite get the &quot;Inspiration brings you madness&quot; note might have deceived themselves into thinking that the Mania-realms reveal transcendental reality and not their own delusions, and yet despite their madness have successfully perceived that Bardos are intimately related to the human state of consciousness. Hence the naming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T16:59:18-07:00","id":1095294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1095037#post1095037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shard or Splinter.<br /> <br /> Demon already uses those terms, why not adopt it too to follow that timeless CofD tradition of having multiple things that are similar be named the same? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I actually rather like &quot;shards&quot; in place of Bardos, especially since that's actually used for &quot;official&quot; alternate settings.<br /> <br /> I actually run it that Genii refer to anything that's not what the Mages call the Phenomenal as &quot;Bardo.&quot;<br /> <br /> A place where sentient morphic fields feed off each other and the symbolic resonance of the physical world? That's a bardo. Gestalt consciousness of mankind? Bardo. Hollow world filled with dinosaurs and Nazis? Bardo. Lightless world inhabited by smoke owls? Bardo. Dimension containing the psychic resonances of the dead? Bardo. Some Bardos might be Maniac Bardos, many are not, some are sort-of-Maniac-but-not-really. All of them are weird, and exactly as dangerous and useful as they need to be for Genii to get into serious trouble.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T07:02:14-07:00","id":1096707,"title":"","content":"We should probably agree on Theme before we could actually start making the new system though. Then we could pound it into the readers head with a jackhammer.<br /> <br /> I propose Obsession. Genii are all, to differing degrees, obsessed with their Magnum Opus. Bardo/Shard Worlds/Splinters are Obsessed with true existance. Inspiration is Obsessed with the advancement of humanity. Humanity is Obsessed with holding on in an increasingly chaotic world. Manes are Obsessed with getting Mania. And the proposed Edisons (probably should get different name though) are Obsessed with Wonders.<br /> <br /> Obsession can drive people to ever greater heights and, if left unchecked, can also lead to ever greater atrocities in pursuit of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T08:49:32-07:00","id":1096744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DArchon5</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1096707#post1096707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We should probably agree on Theme before we could actually start making the new system though. Then we could pound it into the readers head with a jackhammer.<br /> <br /> I propose Obsession. Genii are all, to differing degrees, obsessed with their Magnum Opus. Bardo/Shard Worlds/Splinters are Obsessed with true existance. Inspiration is Obsessed with the advancement of humanity. Humanity is Obsessed with holding on in an increasingly chaotic world. Manes are Obsessed with getting Mania. And the proposed Edisons (probably should get different name though) are Obsessed with Wonders.<br /> <br /> Obsession can drive people to ever greater heights and, if left unchecked, can also lead to ever greater atrocities in pursuit of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>We kind of already got into the themes. The idea of there not being anyone in charge, the tension between the future you want and the blood and tears that pave the road to it. Genii can see that the rules of society are only rules in so far as people are willing to follow them, and that being a Genius is about rejecting those rules, and maybe substituting your own if you can get around to it.<br /> <br /> Obsession is present, but it's not obsession with a mystery for its own sake, like Magi. Genii don't get obsessed with the Well of Souls, from which all life force flows, because it's an amazing mystery that could rewrite everything we understand. They get obsessed with it because they want to know how they can use it to build their perfect future where all mankind is connected to a collective consciousness. Their obsessions are practical, rather than academic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T15:27:54-07:00","id":1096883,"title":"","content":"Great!, well write that down and work on the next thing. Which should probably be Axioms and Wonders, then we get to Genii themselves, the Foundations and Fellowships, Lemuria, and finally all those other bits and pieces.<br /> <br /> Ill probably convert Genius 1E into a Word Gile, cut it up to a bunch of pieces and work on making a 2E version one at a time. That sound good?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T16:33:19-07:00","id":1096898,"title":"","content":"For me, the tragedy of the genius, and their main motivation is this: They're smart enough to see the glaring faults of society with greater clarity than the average person, while at the same time they see the amazing potential of what that society could be. It's the conflict between the vision of a utopia that their inspiration brings to their minds and the clash against the sad crushing reality of our world that their eyes see. A world populated by a majority of people that are too afraid of change and too trapped in their routines to dream.<br /> The irony is that the very same intelligence and inspiration that provides them with their amazing abilities and perspective also shows them just how impossibly difficult their task is. Their probabilities of success are really low, and even if they succeed their solution will surely have unforeseen, and probably disastrous, consequences. No matter how smart someone is, nobody can see all the variables or predict all the outcomes. This is of course without taking into account if their utopia is really that perfect, their arrogance blinds them to their imperfect vision, turning their idea of paradise into a hell for everybody else.<br /> However, the genii won't give up, oh no they won't. Despite everything, they still hope. It's a hope born out of the desperation, and the joy, of seeing pieces of that dream of utopia taking life in their lab.The genius keeps working while they murmur &quot;If only they could see...&quot;, and that's why they persist. Because if only the world could see people would believe in their vision of utopia, and no matter what they will make the world see because it's a dream worth fighting for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2964,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","user":"Firanai","date":". 05-25-2017, 07:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T17:08:23-07:00","id":1096909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1096898#post1096898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me, the tragedy of the genius, and their main motivation is this: They're smart enough to see the glaring faults of society with greater clarity than the average person, while at the same time they see the amazing potential of what that society could be. It's the conflict between the vision of a utopia that their inspiration brings to their minds and the clash against the sad crushing reality of our world that their eyes see. A world populated by a majority of people that are too afraid of change and too trapped in their routines to dream.<br /> The irony is that the very same intelligence and inspiration that provides them with their amazing abilities and perspective also shows them just how impossibly difficult their task is. Their probabilities of success are really low, and even if they succeed their solution will surely have unforeseen, and probably disastrous, consequences. No matter how smart someone is, nobody can see all the variables or predict all the outcomes. This is of course without taking into account if their utopia is really that perfect, their arrogance blinds them to their imperfect vision, turning their idea of paradise into a hell for everybody else.<br /> However, the genii won't give up, oh no they won't. Despite everything, they still hope. It's a hope born out of the desperation, and the joy, of seeing pieces of that dream of utopia taking life in their lab.The genius keeps working while they murmur &quot;If only they could see...&quot;, and that's why they persist. Because if only the world could see people would believe in their vision of utopia, and no matter what they will make the world see because it's a dream worth fighting for.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Good, but that only really encapsulates Hoffnungs, and perhaps Neids. Grimms, Staunen, and Klagen have different motivations (even if some may be similar).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T20:31:56-07:00","id":1096967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DArchon5</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1096883#post1096883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great!, well write that down and work on the next thing. Which should probably be Axioms and Wonders, then we get to Genii themselves, the Foundations and Fellowships, Lemuria, and finally all those other bits and pieces.<br /> <br /> Ill probably convert Genius 1E into a Word Gile, cut it up to a bunch of pieces and work on making a 2E version one at a time. That sound good?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm actually already working on Axioms and Wonders. Basically, you can build anything you want*, provided you have the Axiom to do it (and at a highe enough level), but working on things you don't understand, or doing things further outside what mankind in general understands, increases its complexity. The more complex it is, the more expensive it gets in terms of components, and you either have to run yourself ragged getting pieces for your more advanced Wonders, use Larvae, or skip some components and permanently increase the dice pool the Wonder has for Havoc.<br /> <br /> Working within a Field and having excessively high Axiom ratings can help alleviate it, but the they can only do so much. If I can find time after work this weekend, I'll write a more complete outline and share it with the class.<br /> <br /> <sup>*Provided you can fit it into your Paradigm in form and function</sup>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T23:18:06-07:00","id":1096995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1096967#post1096967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm actually already working on Axioms and Wonders. Basically, you can build anything you want*, provided you have the Axiom to do it (and at a highe enough level), but working on things you don't understand, or doing things further outside what mankind in general understands, increases its complexity. The more complex it is, the more expensive it gets in terms of components, and you either have to run yourself ragged getting pieces for your more advanced Wonders, use Larvae, or skip some components and permanently increase the dice pool the Wonder has for Havoc.<br /> <br /> Working within a Field and having excessively high Axiom ratings can help alleviate it, but the they can only do so much. If I can find time after work this weekend, I'll write a more complete outline and share it with the class.<br /> <br /> <sup>*Provided you can fit it into your Paradigm in form and function</sup></div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome, hopefully we can get something playable soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T03:31:22-07:00","id":1097065,"title":"","content":"2 things <br /> 1 after the playable demo we shoud include something like golconde from vampire or ascension from mage or the new dawn for Promethean or apotheosis for mummy or becoming incarnation in beasts <br /> for this i think it shoud get rid of havoc simple but changes everything but like the others it shoud be hard to do and most should fall<br /> 2 maybe some samples characters for the demo","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T03:47:32-07:00","id":1097069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ameraaaaaa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1097065#post1097065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2 things <br /> 1 after the playable demo we shoud include something like golconde from vampire or ascension from mage or the new dawn for Promethean or apotheosis for mummy or becoming incarnation in beasts <br /> for this i think it shoud get rid of havoc simple but changes everything but like the others it shoud be hard to do and most should fall<br /> 2 maybe some samples characters for the demo</div> </div> </div> </div>Bit early to think about play testing. But the Goal of Genii would be their Magnum Opus if anything. Still, we barely have Wonder Creation working, much less Genii Traits in general. So its a long ways away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T06:22:46-07:00","id":1097098,"title":"","content":"Given the theme of failure, I think that there shouldn't be some kind of &quot;win condition&quot; like the New Dawn. No matter how smart a Genius is or how well they master the Axioms, they will never make the world a better place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T06:36:37-07:00","id":1097101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1097098#post1097098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given the theme of failure, I think that there shouldn't be some kind of &amp;quot;win condition&amp;quot; like the New Dawn. No matter how smart a Genius is or how well they master the Axioms, they will never make the world a better place.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think &quot;Outright failure&quot; is being dropped in favor of &quot;Change is Hard&quot;. The &quot;Win Condition&quot; in this case would be actually succeeding in affecting a change, acceptably.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T07:16:29-07:00","id":1097115,"title":"","content":"Yeah i think outright failure should be dropped for change is hard","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T07:52:33-07:00","id":1097124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1097098#post1097098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given the theme of failure, I think that there shouldn't be some kind of &quot;win condition&quot; like the New Dawn. No matter how smart a Genius is or how well they master the Axioms, they will never make the world a better place.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, but that was one of the things that I hate the most about first edition genius, and I couldn't be happier that they're ditching it. What's the point of having those amazing skills if you can't do anything with them? Hell, what's the point of playing a game in which nothing I do matters? I already talked about this on my first posts.<br /> For me, genious is not about failing no matter what and dealing with the desperation that comes with the realization that you can't win. For me, genious is a game about leaving behind the arrogant attitude of the genius that makes him think that he, and he alone, can change the world for the better, solve all its problems, and create a perfect utopia.<br /> Change, the kind that truly benefits the world, takes a lot of time, hard work, teamwork, and it won't solve all the problems. The genious that reaches victory is the one that internalizes this truth and learns that to succed he must work with the world, not against it, to create a positive change.<br /> The amazing abilities of the genious are a beacon of light that ignites the spark of inspiration in the people around him, and with that he plants the seeds of belief in a better world. The people, fileld with that newfound faith in a better tomorrow, will work to make that vision a reality.<br /> The world won't become the amazing utopia that the genious has envisioned, but that's not the point. The point is to make the world a better place, one piece at a time, till one day utopia becomes real.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2964,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","user":"Firanai","date":". 05-26-2017, 02:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T08:46:26-07:00","id":1097142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1097124#post1097124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me, genious is a game about trascending the arrogant attitude of the genius that makes him think that he, and he alone, can change the world for the better, solve all its problems, and create a perfect utopia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure you just described Lemuria there.<br /> <br /> And the rest you described? Working with the world, inspiring the people around them, planting the seeds of a better world and making it better one change at a time? I've seen that before. Namely, in Changeling: The Dreaming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T09:03:24-07:00","id":1097150,"title":"","content":"I heard changling the dreaming sucks but i Haven't played it or even checked it out changling the lost i heard is a better game and i checked it out but Haven't read the rulebook yet but im waiting for 2e <br /> Now from what i heard changling the dreaming did not have much darkness in it and i think thats the problem <br /> but main point whats the point if everything leads to failure not just thats boring but since only 8 to 10 on the dice is a success every game line dos have failure as a main thing thanks for someones review of genius for telling me that and i agree <br /> but even then whats wrong with sharing themes if we can do it better","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T11:16:16-07:00","id":1097189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1097142#post1097142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty sure you just described Lemuria there.<br /> <br /> And the rest you described? Working with the world, inspiring the people around them, planting the seeds of a better world and making it better one change at a time? I've seen that before. Namely, in Changeling: The Dreaming.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll admit that perhaps my personal vision of genious may be a bit too optimistic and, like you pointed out, a bit too similar to changeling the dreaming, but I'm sure that we can find a middle ground between &quot;You can create the power armor from iron man but it doesn't matter because it will eventually fail and have no impact on the world&quot; and &quot;My etheric generator will give unlimited clean energy to the world, eliminating the necessity for any other source of power and therefore allowing us to create an utopia free from fossil fuels&quot; or between Rick Sanchez and Reed Richards. It's the chronicles of darkness, there should be tragedy, but not to the point that there's no hope.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T22:46:18-07:00","id":1097428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1097189#post1097189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'll admit that perhaps my personal vision of genious may be a bit too optimistic and, like you pointed out, a bit too similar to changeling the dreaming, but I'm sure that we can find a middle ground between &quot;You can create the power armor from iron man but it doesn't matter because it will eventually fail and have no impact on the world&quot; and &quot;My etheric generator will give unlimited clean energy to the world, eliminating the necessity for any other source of power and therefore allowing us to create an utopia free from fossil fuels&quot; or between Rick Sanchez and Reed Richards. It's the chronicles of darkness, there should be tragedy, but not to the point that there's no hope.</div> </div> </div> </div>even if you make that generator i dont think it should be able to have unlimited energy thats impossible i think so yeah you can give the would that but there will be flaws in the plan where is the energy coming from it might be a bad idea you know what i mean but thats just what i think","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T02:30:03-07:00","id":1097470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ameraaaaaa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1097428#post1097428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">even if you make that generator i dont think it should be able to have unlimited energy thats impossible i think so yeah you can give the would that but there will be flaws in the plan where is the energy coming from it might be a bad idea you know what i mean but thats just what i think</div> </div> </div> </div>Or make the problem more mundane. Your &quot;free energy for everyone forever&quot; engine will get a lot of leery faces from people who made their riches with more mundane sources and will get you into trouble from them.<br /> <br /> But going all CthulhuTech is an option as well (1: Harness extradimensional energies for free power. 2: After all debunking attempts fail the engines are adapted. 3: Cold War with the former oil-producing nations. 4: Aliens attack. 5: Aliens are revealed to be created by the Migou (they're Mi-Go) because they feel threatened by humanity and the fact it's about to escape its Earthen cage. 6: An interplanetary war.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T12:22:14-07:00","id":1097584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1097470#post1097470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or make the problem more mundane. Your &quot;free energy for everyone forever&quot; engine will get a lot of leery faces from people who made their riches with more mundane sources and will get you into trouble from them.<br /> <br /> But going all CthulhuTech is an option as well (1: Harness extradimensional energies for free power. 2: After all debunking attempts fail the engines are adapted. 3: Cold War with the former oil-producing nations. 4: Aliens attack. 5: Aliens are revealed to be created by the Migou (they're Mi-Go) because they feel threatened by humanity and the fact it's about to escape its Earthen cage. 6: An interplanetary war.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it'd be quite probable that a Genius who'd managed to make reliable free energy would be under the gun from people with money in oil, nuclear, thermal, solar, hydro, and wind power. Not to mention any Genii who have competing energy solutions, or those Genii who believe free energy would destabilize or prevent their own Opus.<br /> <br /> Not to mention, if free energy became a thing, the Mania Storm that results could cause some pretty nasty stuff, as it would then basically disprove not only thermodynamics as we understand them, but also undermine the concept of scarcity under which much of our economy still runs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T12:44:00-07:00","id":1097590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1097584#post1097584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to mention, if free energy became a thing, the Mania Storm that results could cause some pretty nasty stuff, as it would then basically disprove not only thermodynamics as we understand them, but also undermine the concept of scarcity under which much of our economy still runs.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know what that means, right? We'd get a Bardo where there is naught but scarcity.<br /> <br /> That's right. The Bardo of Thunderdome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T17:28:38-07:00","id":1097641,"title":"","content":"*Bolthole slowly creeks open, a whisper can be heard coming from the thin opening*<br /> <br /> <br /> Is everyone reeaaaaly married to the term &quot;Mania&quot; to describe the cosmic creative energy that Genii use to power and build their Wonders? Because the term is honestly kinda backwards.<br /> <br /> I know it's used to fit the whole &quot;mad science&quot; vibe, but at best it's comical and at worst it's sorta offensive. Since the name of the game is Genius wouldn't it be better to name the energy source after a more proper kind of hypothetical energy or matter that both exists and doesn't on some quantum level? <br /> <br /> Other than that great work on 2nd edition so far...<br /> <br /> *Bolthole closes just as slowly*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Spell Check 05-27-2017, 09:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T18:10:28-07:00","id":1097646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1097641#post1097641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Bolthole slowly creeks open, a whisper can be heard coming from the thin opening*<br /> <br /> <br /> Is everyone reeaaaaly married to the term &quot;Mania&quot; to describe the cosmic creative energy that Genii use to power and build their Wonders? Because the term is honestly kinda backwards.<br /> <br /> I know it's used to fit the whole &quot;mad science&quot; vibe, but at best it's comical and at worst it's sorta offensive. Since the name of the game is Genius wouldn't it be better to name the energy source after a more proper kind of hypothetical energy or matter that both exists and doesn't on some quantum level?<br /> <br /> Other than that great work on 2nd edition so far.....<br /> <br /> *Bolthole closes just as slowly*</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, but what term? What wouldn't skew things in another direction? Especially with Genii not being restricted to solely mad scientist/engineers (provided we are still doing that).<br /> <br /> I'm fine with Mania, personally. &quot;<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\">an excessive enthusiasm or desire; an obsession&quot; seems to fit just fine.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T18:39:38-07:00","id":1097654,"title":"","content":"If it were just that, then perhaps it wouldn't be that bad. But Mania also is a form of mental illness, or denotes a mental illness. There's no ignoring that. I fear most of all it would be in bad taste for 2nd edition to still use that term. That's why I suggested putting heads together to see if there's a better alternative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T18:46:20-07:00","id":1097657,"title":"","content":"How about Insight?, it would do for now. At least until I can either find a better word in English or use Google-Fu to find one in Latin.<br /> <br /> Genii still have that preoccupation with Latin right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T18:58:17-07:00","id":1097659,"title":"","content":"Perhaps the answer lies in other parallels in terminology. Bardo is a Tibetan Buddhism term, and I believe the Axioms use a lot of German. Latin can work too, heck Quantum is already Latin so we could just use the plural of that: Quanta.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T19:10:56-07:00","id":1097662,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3436_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3436\" data-vbnamecard=\"3436\">Dusksage</a> If you really think Mania might be an issue as a term, how about Impetus?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T19:14:14-07:00","id":1097663,"title":"","content":"Holy shit! <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4443_5.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4443\" data-vbnamecard=\"4443\">GibberingEloquence</a>, this is it! This is exactly what in game Mania is supposed to be. Impetus is perfect. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Heck, this could even help add some more elements to the Genius setting to. The collective force of Impetus could be called The Movement. It differentiates itself from the Principle by setting things into motion or generating movement of all forms rather than fostering change and transformation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Polish 05-27-2017, 10:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T19:34:20-07:00","id":1097667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1097663#post1097663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Holy shit! <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4443_5.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4443\" data-vbnamecard=\"4443\">GibberingEloquence</a>, this is it! This is exactly what in game Mania is supposed to be. Impetus is perfect. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Heck, this could even help add some more elements to the Genius setting to. The collective force of Impetus could be called The Movement. It differentiates itself from the Principle by setting things into motion or generating movement of all forms rather than fostering change and transformation.</div> </div> </div> </div>The distinction between Impetus/The Movement and the Principle might be academic in most scenarios, but I'm glad you liked my idea so much. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But would it be mechanically different from Mania? Maybe it could have new ways to be gathered/used?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T20:38:55-07:00","id":1097676,"title":"","content":"Probably not. Though maybe, instead of Binding Mania (Which is being thrown out anyway) Impetus can be used to Activate a Wonder for its Duration (Most commonly, a scene, otherwise less or greater).<br /> Edit: So more like Alembics with Pyros, but less innate, and each Wonder is charged separately.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T12:25:02-07:00","id":1097842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DArchon5</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1097676#post1097676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably not. Though maybe, instead of Binding Mania (Which is being thrown out anyway) Impetus can be used to Activate a Wonder for its Duration (Most commonly, a scene, otherwise less or greater).<br /> Edit: So more like Alembics with Pyros, but less innate, and each Wonder is charged separately.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't recall us deciding upon throwing out bound Mania, but if people would rather just charge Wonders rather than Bind Mania, that's still fairly workable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T13:11:51-07:00","id":1097854,"title":"","content":"Regarding Bound vs Charged (or Updated, or Recalibrated, or whatever other terms fits): this depends greatly upon the Mania (using that term until a new one is settled on, if any) economy.<br /> <br /> If Mania is easy to come by, Charging may be little different than Bound over time - 3 Bound Mania vs 1 Mania a Scene for 3 Scenes averages out to the same, assuming full or near full recharge. However, if Mania is harder to restore, than Charging will bleed a Genius's reserves dry, at least in comparison.<br /> <br /> <b>Bound</b><br /> <u>Pros</u>: Always on. There may be other effects with their own costs (even more Mania), but the core Wonder always functions once built. You never have to worry about not being able to power it when needed.<br /> <u>Cons</u>: It takes away your total flexibility by locking up some of your fuel resource. This hardly matters with a lower percentage Bound, but can easily add up. Additionally, this sets an upper cap on the number of active Wonders one can have, since once you've Bound all you Mania, that's it.<br /> <br /> <b>Charged</b><br /> <u>Pros</u>: More flexible in terms of what Wonders you want to use at any given moment - you might carry a small arsenal, but if you only use one or three, the other Wonders effectively don't matter in terms of cost. Also more flexible in terms of cost/benefit - since how long it remains active is now a variable, longer or shorter duration becomes a bargaining chip in Wonder creation math.<br /> <u>Cons</u>: Repeated usage, especially with more limited Mania recover will quickly render a Genius spent. Additionally, it may not even make sense for Wonders that &quot;should&quot; be always active, like armor or inherent improvements.<br /> <br /> Personally, since I like more options over less, why not have both? Maybe Bound Mania gives you a very nice bonus when it comes to mitigating powerful effects, at least compared to Charged, but at the cost of a &quot;permanent&quot; reduction in Mania. Like spending Willpower points, compared to Willpower <b>dots</b>. For Permanent things, or a Genius's signature Wonders, they'll probably Bind, while they use some mix of Charged for anything else they create, but might not need or use all the time. This also solves the Cave of Wonders issue - those found Wonders were simple another Genius's stockpile of Charged ones, no need to figure out why they didn't break down or go Orphan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 05-28-2017, 04:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T16:04:27-07:00","id":1097894,"title":"","content":"I'd suggest making it slightly tough to come by. That is, Impetus (I really like that name.) isn't especially rare, and Genii can generate small amounts of it on their own, or a decent amount for a single person with concerted effort (trading with Bardos, taking it from Generators, possibly extracting it by more specialized means), but the kind of juice needed to power anything big becomes prohibitive very quickly.<br /> <br /> For example, Tony can generate enough Impetus on his own to maintain his main power armor, just with the point of Impetus he gets each day. In order to use his Hulkbuster, he needs to tap into the Impetus generated by his research labs, and even then, he can't use it all the time. He could only use his <i>full</i> armory, all together, <i>once</i>. It basically wiped out his Impetus stores, and in order to avoid dealing with a bunch of Orphans down the line, blew them to pieces.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T19:31:36-07:00","id":1097937,"title":"","content":"A random thought about an alternate way of handling Mania/Impetus... what if it was more like an integrity stat than a fuel stat?<br /> <br /> The way I'm visualizing this is that, rather than costing Mania, axioms instead set three boundaries - the first one being &quot;You can make Wonders with this Axiom&quot;, the second being &quot;You can control Wonders made with this Axiom&quot;, and the third being &quot;Wonders made with this Axiom function&quot;. The first tends to be higher than the second, which tends to be higher than the third.<br /> <br /> As your Mania/Impulse builds, you start losing control - you get social penalties, as well as increasing compulsions which will eventually overwhelm your desire to eat and sleep. So you'll want to lower it and keep it under control... which stands a pretty good chance of orphaning your more powerful Wonders, as you drop below the threshold that lets you control them.<br /> <br /> Stuff like taking it slowly, working inside a paradigm, getting help, and having a plan can drive down the boundaries.<br /> <br /> Of course, this makes the most sense if Geniuses can forcibly raise their Mania but have a hard time lowering it.<br /> <br /> =---=<br /> <br /> Another thought - one of the inherent powers of Geniuses should be that nothing short of unconsciousness can stop them from thinking &quot;clearly&quot;. They're <i>inspired</i> - what's a little hunger, pain, or fatigue?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T19:40:56-07:00","id":1097941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1097937#post1097937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A random thought about an alternate way of handling Mania/Impetus... what if it was more like an integrity stat than a fuel stat?<br /> <br /> The way I'm visualizing this is that, rather than costing Mania, axioms instead set three boundaries - the first one being &quot;You can make Wonders with this Axiom&quot;, the second being &quot;You can control Wonders made with this Axiom&quot;, and the third being &quot;Wonders made with this Axiom function&quot;. The first tends to be higher than the second, which tends to be higher than the third.<br /> <br /> As your Mania/Impulse builds, you start losing control - you get social penalties, as well as increasing compulsions which will eventually overwhelm your desire to eat and sleep. So you'll want to lower it and keep it under control... which stands a pretty good chance of orphaning your more powerful Wonders, as you drop below the threshold that lets you control them.<br /> <br /> Stuff like taking it slowly, working inside a paradigm, getting help, and having a plan can drive down the boundaries.<br /> <br /> Of course, this makes the most sense if Geniuses can forcibly raise their Mania but have a hard time lowering it.<br /> <br /> =---=<br /> <br /> Another thought - one of the inherent powers of Geniuses should be that nothing short of unconsciousness can stop them from thinking &quot;clearly&quot;. They're <i>inspired</i> - what's a little hunger, pain, or fatigue?</div> </div> </div> </div>That could be incorporated into our rules for <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1St0PBLVPHrBTVq-k9oZJz7DsPOyA_V1DYLaryVs60_o/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Restraint.</b></a><br /> <br /> As for your suggested inherent power, perhaps it could be represented as an immunity to the Insensate Tilt, and a greater resistance against the Fatigue/Lethargic Condition?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 05-28-2017, 10:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T20:29:41-07:00","id":1097955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1097941#post1097941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That could be incorporated into our rules for <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1St0PBLVPHrBTVq-k9oZJz7DsPOyA_V1DYLaryVs60_o/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Restraint.</b></a><br /> <br /> As for your suggested inherent power, perhaps it could be represented as an immunity to the Insensate Tilt, and a greater resistance against the Fatigue/Lethargic Condition?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if that's really comptible with Restraint as it currently exists. It would make anyone who actually intends to use their Wonders pretty much required to slip down into Renegade.<br /> <br /> What I <i>could</i> see, however, might be switching to a Condition-based fuel, rather than a pool of points. <s>Give me a minute, and I'll write up and edit in a slap-dash example into this post.</s> Here it is:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <b>Impetus (Persistent)</b><br /> <br /> You feel the electric force of Inspiration in you, and you can\u2019t help but let it out.<br /> <b>Benefit:</b> You receive a number of Impetus Points equal to your Inspiration Rating upon gaining this Condition. You must expend these points first to maintain Wonders and other Impetus drains (any Manes under your employ, for example), and then can choose to spend the remainder at any time throughout the chapter. You regain this Condition at the beginning of each Chapter.<br /> As long as you have at least one point of Impetus unspent, you suffer no penalties due to fatigue or exhaustion, dehydration, or sleep deprivation (although you still risk any adverse health effects from being in such a state), and are immune to the Insensate Tilt from mundane sources.<br /> <b>Regaining Impetus:</b> You can replenish Impetus Points by draining Impetus from existing sources, such as Generators. Roll the source\u2019s Impetus Rating (usually 1 to 5), gaining 1 Impetus Point per Success. You can also attempt to force Impetus from within yourself once per Scene by spending a point of Willpower and rolling Inspiration, regaining 1 Impetus if you succeed. Other, more potent methods of acquiring Impetus, and even creating self-sufficient Impetus engines to fuel things without you, may exist, but they are usually obscenely dangerous or morally dubious.<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> You can Resolve this Condition to immediately gain additional Impetus Points equal to your Inspiration Dots until the end of the scene. After the scene ends, you lose this Condition and any unspent Impetus Points with it, and you must make an Unmada Check.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":4488,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","user":"malonkey1","date":". 05-29-2017, 12:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T22:39:55-07:00","id":1097989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1097955#post1097955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know if that's really comptible with Restraint as it currently exists. It would make anyone who actually intends to use their Wonders pretty much required to slip down into Renegade.<br /> <br /> What I <i>could</i> see, however, might be switching to a Condition-based fuel, rather than a pool of points. <s>Give me a minute, and I'll write up and edit in a slap-dash example into this post.</s> Here it is:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <b>Impetus (Persistent)</b><br /> <br /> You feel the electric force of Inspiration in you, and you can\u2019t help but let it out.<br /> <b>Benefit:</b> You receive a number of Impetus Points equal to your Inspiration Rating upon gaining this Condition. You must expend these points first to maintain Wonders and other Impetus drains (any Manes under your employ, for example), and then can choose to spend the remainder at any time throughout the chapter. You regain this Condition at the beginning of each Chapter.<br /> As long as you have at least one point of Impetus unspent, you suffer no penalties due to fatigue or exhaustion, dehydration, or sleep deprivation (although you still risk any adverse health effects from being in such a state), and are immune to the Insensate Tilt from mundane sources.<br /> <b>Regaining Impetus:</b> You can replenish Impetus Points by draining Impetus from existing sources, such as Generators. Roll the source\u2019s Impetus Rating (usually 1 to 5), gaining 1 Impetus Point per Success. You can also attempt to force Impetus from within yourself once per Scene by spending a point of Willpower and rolling Inspiration, regaining 1 Impetus if you succeed. Other, more potent methods of acquiring Impetus, and even creating self-sufficient Impetus engines to fuel things without you, may exist, but they are usually obscenely dangerous or morally dubious.<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> You can Resolve this Condition to immediately gain additional Impetus Points equal to your Inspiration Dots until the end of the scene. After the scene ends, you lose this Condition and any unspent Impetus Points with it, and you must make an Unmada Check.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, assuming we use this, then Wonders would cost a lot less. Probably one Impetus per Wonder, with each additional point after that granting a Focused Effect / Extra Reach. Some particularly powerful Wonders, the likes of Axiom 5, would probably require Resolving Impetus (Condition) to power it in addition to regular Impetus Cost to simulate how draining powering it is.<br /> <br /> Or maybe, we can make it so that there is an extra effect for some Wonders that can only be activated if the Impetus (Condition) is sacrificed (Do not gain Impetus Points). Like dramatically increased effects, the likes of which would befit a Magnum Opus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T04:22:22-07:00","id":1098057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1097955#post1097955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know if that's really comptible with Restraint as it currently exists. It would make anyone who actually intends to use their Wonders pretty much required to slip down into Renegade.<br /> <br /> What I <i>could</i> see, however, might be switching to a Condition-based fuel, rather than a pool of points. <s>Give me a minute, and I'll write up and edit in a slap-dash example into this post.</s> Here it is:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <b>Impetus (Persistent)</b><br /> <br /> You feel the electric force of Inspiration in you, and you can\u2019t help but let it out.<br /> <b>Benefit:</b> You receive a number of Impetus Points equal to your Inspiration Rating upon gaining this Condition. You must expend these points first to maintain Wonders and other Impetus drains (any Manes under your employ, for example), and then can choose to spend the remainder at any time throughout the chapter. You regain this Condition at the beginning of each Chapter.<br /> As long as you have at least one point of Impetus unspent, you suffer no penalties due to fatigue or exhaustion, dehydration, or sleep deprivation (although you still risk any adverse health effects from being in such a state), and are immune to the Insensate Tilt from mundane sources.<br /> <b>Regaining Impetus:</b> You can replenish Impetus Points by draining Impetus from existing sources, such as Generators. Roll the source\u2019s Impetus Rating (usually 1 to 5), gaining 1 Impetus Point per Success. You can also attempt to force Impetus from within yourself once per Scene by spending a point of Willpower and rolling Inspiration, regaining 1 Impetus if you succeed. Other, more potent methods of acquiring Impetus, and even creating self-sufficient Impetus engines to fuel things without you, may exist, but they are usually obscenely dangerous or morally dubious.<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> You can Resolve this Condition to immediately gain additional Impetus Points equal to your Inspiration Dots until the end of the scene. After the scene ends, you lose this Condition and any unspent Impetus Points with it, and you must make an Unmada Check.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So, it is still a pool, but based on a Condition? What about a cascading sequence of Conditions, like with Beast's Satiety Conditions (though those are based off a numeric trait) or a Demon-Blooded's Cipher? The later is probably a better example, since reaching the &quot;bottom/top&quot; of the Condition chain could trigger Unmada or even Illumination.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T15:03:41-07:00","id":1098575,"title":"","content":"The systems seems to loose the endearing touch of deconstructed Hollywood's and Pulp Fiction's capital S Science and becomes more and more painfully complicated with each proposed revision. Can I try to remind you that the game is about MAD Scientists, not ordinary or just insane ones? <br /> The current take lacks passionate self-destructiveness brought forth by arrogance and delusions of grandeur. Impetus is... Artifical. Didn't we complain about Genius feeling like it doesn't support Mad Artists (and Bakers, Musicians, and Poets)? Sure, Mania as a term is imperfect (even if it's fun pun of Mana), but I think you missed the point. <br /> <br /> Genii and their Wonders should run on Passion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12082,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","user":"Weird","date":".  I hope I didn't come off as attacking. This has just been bothering me for awhile and this discussion seems to be an excellent example of why. 05-30-2017, 06:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T15:19:17-07:00","id":1098578,"title":"","content":"Sure, did you have any suggestions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T16:03:29-07:00","id":1098598,"title":"","content":"Counter argument:<br /> <br /> It happens in an instant, like a flash of lightning. One moment you're exactly who you've always been, and the next changes everything. Inspiration sets something into motion. It cannot be simply ignored. That's how we always begin. Eureka! And we grab hold of Impetus and shape it towards our vision. Our Magnum Opus. Our Utopia. <br /> <br /> You can't stop the Movement.<br /> <br /> It spreads ever outwards in a wave. The train is already on the tracks and at speed. We all tend to it's course using all of our knowledge and skill, but there's no conductor. How could there be? It's a force of nature. It's cosmic. All we can do is nudge the Movement in the direction we want it. Just a little nudge here and there. Next stop, Utopia! That's how the War started after all. That's what keeps the War going still. Everyone's trying to steer the damn train...except there's a problem. There are no god damn breaks on this thing. <br /> <br /> You can't stop the Movement.<br /> <br /> Even if our dream is realized, world hunger solved, world peace achieved, immortality realized, the cosmos still turns. Events still unfold. Impetus sets things into motion. It's what it does. It never stops. Nobody ever warned us inspiration was a one way trip. Utopia is achieved but the train keeps on steaming along. Try to slow it down, even risk jumping off but it's too late. You missed your Utopia by miles, and now your neck is broken. <br /> <br /> So, why bother at all then? Why try to create something meaningful and lasting when you know it'll either inevitably collapse or change into something unrecognizable? Because, in those moments when Utopia is realized (be it a minute to a single lifetime) is when life can be better. Existence can be kinder, longer, or more prosperous. Don't think for a second those moments aren't without meaning. Those moments are what dreams are made of. And I think we all realize that somewhere deep down inside. Eureka, am I right? <br /> <br /> <br /> *Or in other words: I argue that passion is alive and well with the current revision. The game has shifted slightly away from MAD science, but in a tasteful manner that acknowledges it's forebearers but takes things in an interesting new direction. Science fiction can match pulp Science!'s drama and passion when given the chance and imagination of storytellers who love the genre. I argue we give it that chance without falling back on nostalgia for nostalgia's sake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T12:24:21-07:00","id":1099240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1098578#post1098578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, did you have any suggestions?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, forgive me if my last sentence wasn't quite clear. I think Passion is MUCH better name for Mania than Impetus, since it's intuitive and easier to change to from maniac terminology: storm of passion, blinded by passion, passionless citizens... You get the same idea Mania cowered in 1st edition, but it isn't ableistic like original (but remains intuitive, unlike Impetus).<br /> <br /> I will address the counrer argument later. I had to tap into all my creative juice reserves over past week, and I need to recharge.<br /> <br /> ...speaking of which, even &quot;Juice&quot; is more Mad Scientist sounding than Impetus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T16:53:45-07:00","id":1099332,"title":"","content":"Well honestly, Passion is leagues better than Mania in terms of being an inoffensive term. Hell, even Juice works as a common slang but only if the main issue of this discussion is addressed. <br /> <br /> That being what is the main genre of Genius 2E going to be? Specifically is it a Science Fiction storyteller game or a Pulp storyteller game. Both are legitimate directions to go in and both would make for some very interesting Chonicles, but with all that's been done it firmly looks like the game can't be both without sacrificing the essence of what each of these individual genres have to offer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Spellcheck 06-01-2017, 07:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T19:59:38-07:00","id":1099372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1099332#post1099332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well honestly, Passion is leagues better than Mania in terms of being an inoffensive term. Hell, even Juice works as a common slang but only if the main issue of this discussion is addressed.<br /> <br /> That being what is the main genre of Genius 2E going to be? Specifically is it a Science Fiction storyteller game or a Pulp storyteller game. Both are legitimate directions to go in and both would make for some very interesting Chonicles, but with all that's been done it firmly looks like the game can't be both without sacrificing the essence of what each of these individual genres have to offer.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess, if I had to say, I'm leaning more toward &quot;occult sci-fi&quot;? That is, it's got a very sci-fi bent in themes and a lot of the aesthetic trappings, but there's a lot of the occult underlying it? Like, demons being summoned through a carefully-determined mathematical formula, or a tortured geneticist who recreates his dead family, but then finds that they're displaying traits in common with the undead, or a man who cracks the secret to freeing the mind from the body with a special drug, but find that there are <i>others</i> in that space, with less-than-friendly intentions.<br /> <br /> So, definitely science fiction, but less Star Trek, more Re-Animator.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T20:59:08-07:00","id":1099383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1099372#post1099372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess, if I had to say, I'm leaning more toward &quot;occult sci-fi&quot;? That is, it's got a very sci-fi bent in themes and a lot of the aesthetic trappings, but there's a lot of the occult underlying it? Like, demons being summoned through a carefully-determined mathematical formula, or a tortured geneticist who recreates his dead family, but then finds that they're displaying traits in common with the undead, or a man who cracks the secret to freeing the mind from the body with a special drug, but find that there are <i>others</i> in that space, with less-than-friendly intentions.<br /> <br /> So, definitely science fiction, but less Star Trek, more Re-Animator.</div> </div> </div> </div>That'd get me into Genius for sure. We <i>are </i>making a fan gameline for a series of horror games, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T18:06:58-07:00","id":1099971,"title":"","content":"I took a digression from Wonder Rules for Impetus version 0.1<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5D9AgFEhGZ3ZEhNOGtub25wbDQ?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Have a look and tell me everythng you hate so I can make you hate it less on the next try.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T05:47:52-07:00","id":1100086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1099971#post1099971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I took a digression from Wonder Rules for Impetus version 0.1<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5D9AgFEhGZ3ZEhNOGtub25wbDQ?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Have a look and tell me everythng you hate so I can make you hate it less on the next try.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>So, to summarize, Impetus is handled via a chain of Conditions that control what you can support (in addition to other effects): Impetus (Inspiration) -&gt; Stressed (+Composure) -&gt; Deep Inspiration (infinite).<br /> <br /> In addition, some other sources can grant more &quot;slots&quot; - Generators, bountiful Bardos, and your Magnum Opus. Maybe add in Larvae here? Based on using your Touchstones in the production of said Wonder/whatever.<br /> <br /> So, in this model, there is no Impetus Binding (because, above). So how will traditional fuel stat expenditures be handled? Willpower?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T06:03:25-07:00","id":1100090,"title":"","content":"Hmm. Mechanically I can see a spot for favored designs when Kitbashing (negates some of the penalties when Kitbashing that specific Wonder). It would support certain signature Wonders that aren't always around, and especially the Alchemist or disposable gadgeteer Archetype. But is there any thematic justification?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T06:59:50-07:00","id":1100108,"title":"","content":"Okay, honestly I have a bone to pick not only with new Name for Mana, but with Restrain mechanic as well. <br /> Integrity needs to reflect the mood playstyle encourages, and Restrains feels like completely unintuitive system for non-werewolves. Werewolves are aboute delicate balance of human and spirit. Sure, you can say Genius is about delicate balance of Id and Superego, but those aren't concious element of decision making. <br /> No name yet, but here basic outline for another possible Integrity system that would be different from others seen so far: Mad Scientists are closely related to ancient Greek mythology of mortals, giants, and demigods angering gods by acts of hubris and being punished in nemesis. The original Obligation system was flawed that it often ended the story at Hubris, with Genius having to repent their sins right there and then or risk getting unhinged. Current Restraint is some crazy check book of &quot;good deeds &amp; bad deeds&quot;?<br /> In classic horror literature, the mad scientist are very slow to learn their lessons in responsibility and morality. They often think that they have figured out the game and supress the pangs of guilt as they commit crimes against humanity and nature. They think so for quite a while, up until their careless actions bring logical unforeseen consequences. <br /> Geniuses bend and stretch reality, but are often caught off guard when &quot;reality ensues&quot;. Geniuse's Integrity/Restraint/Obligation rating should go down as their illusion of control collapses around them. Genius can feel perfectly justified stealing and scamming at local pawnshop because of their great and just causes, but when the shop suddenly closes down they are met with unforeseen consequence of their action. <br /> In a way this makes it much easier for Geniuses' creations and grand schemes to go wrong; you can't make an omlette without breaking few eggs, but when your omlette proceeds to come to life and strangle your neighbor, you should probably reevaluate your life choices. <br /> If you decide to Take Over the World, you'll be met with transgressions commited on the way there whenever the new utopia fails to meet the expectations.<br /> <br /> New Breaking Point: <br /> Encountering destructive/tragic/unpleasant consequences of one's actions. <br /> Encountering similar consequences on behalf of actions of one's Wonders, Orphans, Beholden, Unmada field spawned Manes and people closest to you.<br /> <br /> Gameplay-wise this should encourage players to try to anticipate as many of possible outcomes of their actions and create backup plans to deal with them, which should be very close to the vibe a Genius story should have. Additional triggers may need to be added... For example I like the idea that person who knows of Genius's past transgressions can lavarage them against them; Anyone in mood for some &quot;We are quite alike, you and me.&quot; -breaking speeches or heroic mortals forcing Mad Scientist to take a close look at what they have become?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12082,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","user":"Weird","date":". 06-04-2017, 10:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T02:43:52-07:00","id":1100382,"title":"","content":"great idea for genius","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T03:34:22-07:00","id":1100388,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4488_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4488\" data-vbnamecard=\"4488\">malonkey1</a> For Impetus, the pool starts at 1, for starting Inspiration. Isn't that a little low? Starting Genius can only build and maintain 1 Wonder before Stressed? What about allowing an inherent Resolve for the pool (giving it a starting range from 1 to 5, typically 2 or 3), then add in Inspiration from Impetus? Or move +Inspiration to Stressed, making that state more attractive for higher powered Genii?<br /> <br /> As far as dealing with the &quot;No more fuel stat pool&quot;, what about traditional &quot;Costs X Mania to use/activate&quot; instead take up an Impetus Sink for the Scene?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T05:14:40-07:00","id":1100408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1100388#post1100388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4488_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4488\" data-vbnamecard=\"4488\">malonkey1</a> For Impetus, the pool starts at 1, for starting Inspiration. Isn't that a little low? Starting Genius can only build and maintain 1 Wonder before Stressed? What about allowing an inherent Resolve for the pool (giving it a starting range from 1 to 5, typically 2 or 3), then add in Inspiration from Impetus? Or move +Inspiration to Stressed, making that state more attractive for higher powered Genii?</div> </div> </div> </div>That could work. In fact it'd probably be better, yeah. The intent was that it would make low-power Genii stick to their single Wonder more often, so a Low-Inspiration Genius would be more like the single-focus creators of things like Frankenstein or Re-Animator, while those with higher Inspiration would be the &quot;purveyors of wonder&quot; types with numerous Wonders like Willy Wonka, but I could see an argument for making it Impetus = Resolve, Stressed = Inspiration. It would also make it a lot harder for new Genii to avoid dropping into Deep Inspiration, though, and I don't know if that's good or bad.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As far as dealing with the &quot;No more fuel stat pool&quot;, what about traditional &quot;Costs X Mania to use/activate&quot; instead take up an Impetus Sink for the Scene? </div> </div> </div>That was the intent, yeah. So if you're at your Impetus limit, and you Kitbash a Wonder or feed a Mane, you get Stressed for a Scene (or until you cut back down on Impetus some other way).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T05:55:57-07:00","id":1100415,"title":"","content":"Would other Merits and Conditions play with the total Impetus Limit? Like Unmada, or Paragon? Maybe rework Kitbasher to not count up to X kitbashed Wonders for a Scene (Kitbashing would still have the other inherent drawbacks)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 06-05-2017, 09:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T08:12:33-07:00","id":1100450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1100415#post1100415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would other Merits and Conditions play with the total Impetus Limit? Like Unmada, or Paragon? Maybe rework Kitbasher to not count up to X kitbashed Wonders for a Scene (Kitbashing would still have the other inherent drawbacks)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, those are probably going to be the case. It's the Renegades that get a cost break, though. Paragons have the benefit of less Havoc.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T08:41:32-07:00","id":1100456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1100450#post1100450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, those are probably going to be the case. It's the Renegades that get a cost break, though. Paragons have the benefit of less Havoc.</div> </div> </div> </div>So Paragons in this model wouldn't have a Impetus Limit (IL) penalty? Just they don't get the Renegade's bonus?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T08:49:10-07:00","id":1100459,"title":"","content":"Aside: my view/desire at this point is to see Wonder Creation rules similar to Demon's Pact rules (and Hunter 2E's Endowments?) - you total up pros and subtract cons, then try to equal 0. Either method (Mania, or Impetus, or something else) works, though each would have different &quot;cost break&quot; options.<br /> <br /> Addendum: not sure how the &quot;Reach&quot; mechanics in the current doc play into this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T10:14:40-07:00","id":1100487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1100459#post1100459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aside: my view/desire at this point is to see Wonder Creation rules similar to Demon's Pact rules (and Hunter 2E's Endowments?) - you total up pros and subtract cons, then try to equal 0. Either method (Mania, or Impetus, or something else) works, though each would have different &quot;cost break&quot; options.<br /> <br /> Addendum: not sure how the &quot;Reach&quot; mechanics in the current doc play into this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm going to be rewriting the wonders, and Reach is going to go. Basically, the less you know about the subject of the Wonder (lacking the right Field, or having the right Field but missing a specific Postulate), and the more you push beyond what human science or occultism (since that's still in the realm of mortal knowledge) can do, the more complex it is. You get a certain level of complexity based on your Axiom rating, and anything beyond that raises the Wonder's Havoc dice. The more complex the Wonder, the harder it is to build, and the more likely that you might have to skip a component and risk greater Havoc dice and more Wrinkles.<br /> <br /> So you could build a cloning machine, which is modarately complex (let's say 2, we might be able to do it in two or three generations).<ul><li>If you lacked knowledge in a Bio-Engineering Field, it would suffer a large increase in complexity (say, +3), while having Bio-Engineering but not having the Cloning Postulate would incur a smaller increase (only +1), since you have most of the base knowledge and are just applying it in a novel way. You can reach similar effects with wildly differing fields, but they'll work on fundamentally different principles. So you could have a cloner that grows a new person in a vat mad by a Mad Biologist, or a &quot;cloner&quot; that yanks a doppleganger from a similar alternate reality from a Mad Cosmologist, or a &quot;cloning procedure&quot; that surgically and hypnotically transforms a person into another person from a Mad Doctor, etc. The Field used depends on how you wish to achieve your intended Wonder, and whether you can fit that Field and that functionality into your Paradigm.</li> <li>You gather your components (1 per point of complexity). What the components are depends on your Paradigm and what your Wonder does.</li> <li>If your Complexity is higher than your Axiom rating, raise the Havoc by each point it goes over, and add 1 Havoc die for each skipped component. If you use a Larva, reduce Havoc for the wonder by 1 (or 2 if it's a truly obscene Larva).</li> <li>Then you choose (or your Storyteller assigns) a Wrinkle, a specific complication that makes the Wonder harder to use. If you skip any components, you roll Havoc dice, and add another Wrinkle on success (two on Exceptional Success).</li> <li>Then you just have to use it once without sending it into Havoc, and you've built your Wonder.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T10:33:21-07:00","id":1100494,"title":"","content":"Hmm. Just as commentary, I see Fields as basically Genius-specific Specialties (though they aren't tied to a specific Skill, necessarily, and don't give a +1 die to rolls... Unless they could?), that serve as justification for certain themed Wonders/powers. Like needing Neurosurgeon Specialty for Medicine to do brain surgery, you need Animologist to make Wonders dealing with the Spirits of the Shadow (at full effectiveness).<br /> <br /> Which diverges from the document, I know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T10:41:40-07:00","id":1100497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1100494#post1100494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. Just as commentary, I see Fields as basically Genius-specific Specialties (though they aren't tied to a specific Skill, necessarily, and don't give a +1 die to rolls... Unless they could?), that serve as justification for certain themed Wonders/powers. Like needing Neurosurgeon Specialty for Medicine to do brain surgery, you need Animologist to make Wonders dealing with the Spirits of the Shadow (at full effectiveness).<br /> <br /> Which diverges from the document, I know.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, that's pretty close to how I think they'll work. But instead of applying to a Skil, they're Specialties that just sort of &quot;float&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T00:42:09-07:00","id":1100745,"title":"","content":"i see i like the new wonder rules","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T19:07:57-07:00","id":1101074,"title":"","content":"Okay, so I should have gotten more sleep before I did it, but I did it anyway. I wrote newer Wonder rules. If it's not coherent, I'll go back through and make it more coherent after I sleep some.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1btESfH9pv061cZ9TUp_hWnY16nEXEfmKhMgQr5rJvH0/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Here is a link to the newer rules.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T19:48:22-07:00","id":1101089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1101074#post1101074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so I should have gotten more sleep before I did it, but I did it anyway. I wrote newer Wonder rules. If it's not coherent, I'll go back through and make it more coherent after I sleep some.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1btESfH9pv061cZ9TUp_hWnY16nEXEfmKhMgQr5rJvH0/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Here is a link to the newer rules.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>There's nothing there... Maybe a page.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T19:59:38-07:00","id":1101090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1101089#post1101089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's nothing there... Maybe a page.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's odd. Maybe the changes have yet to save? Because the version I'm looking at right now is 11 pages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T20:06:17-07:00","id":1101091,"title":"","content":"First of all, I thought we were going to use Inferences?, Postulates sound like a gross condition to me.<br /> <br /> Secondly, while the Axioms are more vague now, I am actually approving of that descision, but may I implore you to expand upon them in due time?, preferably make them a bit like Yozi Exellencies in EX2<br /> <br /> Thirdly, it appears that Wonder Creation is way too complex and tedious. I get making them more personalized but making it so that Components are definitively hard to find is just asking for the whole game to devolve into a large group of sidequests to try making a Wonder to progress the plot.<br /> <br /> Finally, it appears that the only difference between Low and High Inspiration Genii is that the latter has more stable Wonders and can support more at a time. They're Wonders powers might still be identical. Is this intentional?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T20:22:23-07:00","id":1101092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DArchon5</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1101091#post1101091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First of all, I thought we were going to use Inferences?, Postulates sound like a gross condition to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm fine iwth either. I just used &quot;Postulates&quot; because that's the word I'd been using.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Secondly, while the Axioms are more vague now, I am actually approving of that descision, but may I implore you to expand upon them in due time?, preferably make them a bit like Yozi Exellencies in EX2 </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'll be doing that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thirdly, it appears that Wonder Creation is way too complex and tedious. I get making them more personalized but making it so that Components are definitively hard to find is just asking for the whole game to devolve into a large group of sidequests to try making a Wonder to progress the plot. </div> </div> </div>I can kind of see that. My issue with Genius's Resourcs-based Wonder construction (other than the 1E Resources), was that it felt too simplistic, and it made the Wonders feel less personal as a result. I did leave the option in to just have components pop up as you go, but I can definitely see how it might bog down play, especially for hight-complexity Wonders. I'm not sure how I can fix that, though. It does kind of have the side benefit of forcing a Genius in a crunch to take extra Havoc, but it's debatable as to whether that's actually a benefit rather than a flaw.<br /> <br /> Maybe loosen the requirements, have one Core Component that holds it together and is hard to get, and the other components are just ones you can just pick up more easily? So you could have a raygun that requires a few mildy-rare gizmos that you can pull together with your contacts and favors in downtime (using Resources, Status, Contacts, having Retainers fetch them), but it also requires a massive diamond that you pretty much have to get yourself because the only available one is too well-guarded for anyone to want to help you?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Finally, it appears that the only difference between Low and High Inspiration Genii is that the latter has more stable Wonders and can support more at a time. They're Wonders powers might still be identical. Is this intentional? </div> </div> </div>Sort of. There's kind of been an issue of &quot;do-everything Genii&quot; in Genius, and I wanted to make it so you would be less able to to everything (for example, now you have to fit it into your Paradigm, and it's harder to make things you don't have a working knowledge of), but still able to play the Genius you want to play (Your character can start play with their weird psychic technique or whatnot, and they can develop more without having to progress super-far into things), without making advancing pointless.<br /> <br /> And while it's kind of only tangentially related, I'm considering the idea of making Inferences/Postulates/Whatever into a Condition you can get by working with a Field. So, in preparation for developing your formula for turning lead to gold, you can perform some studies with Alchemy to get the &quot;Transmutation&quot; Inference Condition, or you could study an open Avernian Gate you run across in order to store up a Condition in case you wanted to build a portal to the Underworld later. Resolving the Inference Condition reduces the complexity of a relevant Wonder, and offers an Inspired Beat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T00:51:36-07:00","id":1101142,"title":"","content":"can we test it <br /> i was thinking ray gun but also revival so lets do both","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T03:21:26-07:00","id":1101162,"title":"","content":"Sure!, I've got nothing to do right now anyway.<br /> <br /> Inspiration 2 (Around apprentice level, not fresh out of Breakthrough nut not a newb either)<br /> Exelixi 3 (Spent most points here)<br /> Field of Biology, Healing Inference gained as part of the package<br /> Medicine 3, Computer 2 (Above average healer and average programmer)<br /> Neutral<br /> <br /> <i>Step 1: Concept</i> - Healing Bangle<br /> <br /> <i>Step 2: Function</i> - Heal Exelixi point of Bashing Damage.<br /> Range: Touch.<br /> Duration: One Scene<br /> Skill: Medicine.<br /> Activation: Instant, allows Impetus to be spent Reflexively to heal Exelixi points of Damage. (+1 Complexity) Automated once active<br /> <br /> <i>Step 3: Determine Axiom, Field, and Inference</i> - Axiom: Exelixi, Field of Human Bodies, Inference (Healing)<br /> <br /> <i>Step 4: Complexity</i> - Base Complexity (3) (Not Plausible, but not disproven), Expertise (+0), Other (+2 Easy to Use, +1 Effectiveness)<br /> Total: 6<br /> <br /> <i>Step 5: Determine Components</i> - Experimental Regeneration Medicine, Heart Monitor, Organ Printer<br /> <br /> <i>Step 6: Acquiring and Incorporating Components</i> - After three mini adventures, a wasted Chapter spent finding them, the Genius incorporates the Components.<br /> Experimental Regeneration (Roll Inspiration + Medicine) (5) (2 Successes)<br /> Heart Monitor (Roll Inspiration + Computer) (4) (2 Successes)<br /> Organ Printer (Roll Inspiration + Medicine) (5) (2 Successes)<br /> <br /> <i>Step 7: Determine Wrinkle</i> - Catastrophic Failure (Exceptional Havoc at 3 Successes)<br /> <br /> <i>Step 8: Determine Havoc</i> - (Complexity - Axiom) (6 - 3) 3 dice<br /> <br /> <i>Step 9: Beta Testing</i> - Clash of Wills: Wonder (Havoc + Inspiration) (5) Vs. Genius (Axiom + Skill) (6)<br /> <br /> <i>Round One:</i><br /> Wonder (5 dice): 10, 2, 6, 8, 10 [3, 5] (3 Successes) Catastrophic Failure!, the Wonder takes a Persistent Havoc Condition<br /> Genius (6 dice): 4, 9, 8, 10, 6, 7 [6] (3 Successes) Its a tie!<br /> Still Apply Persistent Condition? Y/N<br /> <br /> <i>Round Two:</i><br /> Wonder (4 dice): 10, 4, 3, 6 [10] [4] (2 Successes) Slightly less dangerousLess Dangerous!<br /> Genius (6 dice): 2, 1, 3, 7, 9, 6 (1 Success) Failure!<br /> Havoc Condition Applied<br /> <br /> <i>One Chapter of Fighting off Orphan Healing Bangle later...</i><br /> <br /> <i>Round Three:</i><br /> Wonder (3 dice): 6, 2, 2 (Failure!) Tamed<br /> Genius (6 dice): 4, 6, 9, 1, 3, 10 [5] (2 Successes) Finally!<br /> <br /> Wonder Creation Successful!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12398,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","user":"DArchon5","date":". 06-07-2017, 06:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T04:03:25-07:00","id":1101167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1101092#post1101092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can kind of see that. My issue with Genius's Resourcs-based Wonder construction (other than the 1E Resources), was that it felt too simplistic, and it made the Wonders feel less personal as a result. I did leave the option in to just have components pop up as you go, but I can definitely see how it might bog down play, especially for hight-complexity Wonders. I'm not sure how I can fix that, though. It does kind of have the side benefit of forcing a Genius in a crunch to take extra Havoc, but it's debatable as to whether that's actually a benefit rather than a flaw.<br /> <br /> Maybe loosen the requirements, have one Core Component that holds it together and is hard to get, and the other components are just ones you can just pick up more easily? So you could have a raygun that requires a few mildy-rare gizmos that you can pull together with your contacts and favors in downtime (using Resources, Status, Contacts, having Retainers fetch them), but it also requires a massive diamond that you pretty much have to get yourself because the only available one is too well-guarded for anyone to want to help you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, we could always just provide some ST advice stating that Players can state they were able to easily acquire the Components in the same downtime they build the Wonder... with the option of the consequences of that acquisition coming up later. Say you instead picked up the Quantum Ruby at a pawn shop for cheap, no Scene necessary. Muto-Ray Complete! Only later, it turns out the Ruby was stolen (and pawned) from another Genius. Who wants it back. Components = Plot Hooks, but they can be optional ones.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1101092#post1101092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sort of. There's kind of been an issue of &quot;do-everything Genii&quot; in Genius, and I wanted to make it so you would be less able to to everything (for example, now you have to fit it into your Paradigm, and it's harder to make things you don't have a working knowledge of), but still able to play the Genius you want to play (Your character can start play with their weird psychic technique or whatnot, and they can develop more without having to progress super-far into things), without making advancing pointless.<br /> <br /> And while it's kind of only tangentially related, I'm considering the idea of making Inferences/Postulates/Whatever into a Condition you can get by working with a Field. So, in preparation for developing your formula for turning lead to gold, you can perform some studies with Alchemy to get the &quot;Transmutation&quot; Inference Condition, or you could study an open Avernian Gate you run across in order to store up a Condition in case you wanted to build a portal to the Underworld later. Resolving the Inference Condition reduces the complexity of a relevant Wonder, and offers an Inspired Beat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems clunky, at that point.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T04:04:20-07:00","id":1101168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1101090#post1101090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's odd. Maybe the changes have yet to save? Because the version I'm looking at right now is 11 pages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just checked on my desktop, and it shows - it was my mobile's fault, somehow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T06:15:42-07:00","id":1101194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DArchon5</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1101162#post1101162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Round One:</i><br /> Wonder (5 dice): 10, 2, 6, 8, 10 [3, 5] (3 Successes) Catastrophic Failure!, the Wonder takes a Persistent Havoc Condition<br /> Genius (6 dice): 4, 9, 8, 10, 6, 7 [6] (3 Successes) Its a tie!<br /> Still Apply Persistent Condition? Y/N</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm. Away from books right now, don't both parties roll again for ties in a Clash of Wills?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T06:43:22-07:00","id":1101200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1101194#post1101194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hm. Away from books right now, don't both parties roll again for ties in a Clash of Wills?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably, but the Wonder has Catastrophic Failure as a Wrinkle, which unfortunately makes it so that it receives Exceptional Success on 3 Successes instead of 5. I assumed it only applied to the Wonder and not the Genius ('Cause then it wouldn't be much of a Wrinkle would it?). So while numerically they tied, conceptually, the Wonder got an Exceptional Success while the Genius got a regular Success.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T07:02:53-07:00","id":1101204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DArchon5</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1101162#post1101162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure!, I've got nothing to do right now anyway.<br /> SNIP</div> </div> </div> </div>That actually sounds like it's functioning pretty much to how I imagine Genius &quot;should be&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T07:12:27-07:00","id":1101207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1101204#post1101204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That actually sounds like it's functioning pretty much to how I imagine Genius &amp;quot;should be&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean the fact that the Wrinkle came and bit them in the ass pretty much immediately?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T08:12:50-07:00","id":1101224,"title":"","content":"Kinda. Wrinkles are supposed ot bite the Genius in the ass at some point, even if not immediately. And if you're worried that a specific Wrinkle is too much, you can always work with your ST to find one that's more appropriate. Like maybe instead of catastrophic failure, your &quot;healing bangle&quot; is addictive to its subjects, or it becomes toxic if used too frequently, or its subject build up a resistance if it's used too often, or so on. Whatever fits the Wonder.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Here's the new text for Step 6, &quot;Acquiring Components.&quot;<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Step 6: Acquiring and Incorporating Components</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Now that you\u2019ve designed your Wonder, the hunt is on! You need to somehow get ahold of the Components. You can do this through trade, calling in favors, skullduggery, heroics, or simply taking it, and while you might be able to get them through favors, Allies, Contacts, Status, or sending a Retainer to retrieve it, there will always be at least one Linchpin component, one that\u2019s integral to your Wonder and is too rare or difficult to acquire to simply buy it or send somebody else to get it. </span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">System: Minor and Major Components</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Most of the components for a Wonder are not <i>too</i> terribly difficult to get. Usually, they can be gotten by buying them, getting a Grant from status in your Fellowship, calling in a favor, or sending a Retainer to go get it (often an Igor, or occasionally a more intelligent Mane or Automaton.). These a Minor Components. Funtionally, they are goods with an Availability rating of 2 to 4 dots, and you can use Resources, Status or Contacts in a relevant group, Allies, or the rating of your Retainer to get it (and you may have to roll for it if you can\u2019t get it). These are still necessary, but they\u2019re easier to acquire. If you can\u2019t get the Component this way, you can choose to acquire it like a Major Component (</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>below</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">), or you can try to redesign your Wonder to use a different component.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Alternately, there are also Major Components. These Components are rare enough, dangerous enough, or just difficult enough to get hold of that you can\u2019t just call it in. You\u2019re going to have to get it yourself. Every Wonder has at least one Major Component (called a Lynchpin). A Larva is also automatically a Major Component (you can\u2019t just call up your biology professor and ask him to steal people\u2019s eyes, now, can you?), and you can make a single Component a Major Component to apply 9-again to incorporating any Minor Components, as you\u2019ve specificaly found the perfect part to tie the Wonder together. These aren\u2019t more difficult to Incorporate, but they\u2019re immensely more difficult to find. Getting a Major Component should be a miniature adventure in itself. Breaking into a government lab to steal their experimental processor, hunting through a dense jungle Bardo for an ancient Diamond, chasing down a damaged UFO to take its power core, and so on.</span></span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":4488,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","user":"malonkey1","date":".  Double-posting is for weiners and druggos. 06-07-2017, 01:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T17:10:45-07:00","id":1101414,"title":"","content":"Alright lest test this thing!<br /> Using a Starting Genius I never actually got to play before:<br /> <br /> <b>Nathan Victor Graham</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <i>Catalyst: </i>Staunten<br /> <i>Foundation: </i>Scholastics <i>(Rogue until we figure out how Foundations work)<br /> Magnum Opus:</i> Omniscience<i> (Knowing All The Things)<br /> Musterbleistift:</i> The Universe Is A Living Being, And We're It's Reproductive Organs<i> (Using Musterbleistift because Paradigm is way too obviously Mage for me, It's German for Paradigm anyway or maybe Erkenntnis, which is German for Cognition, Realization, and Insight</i><i>)</i><br /> <br /> <b>Attributes</b><br /> Intelligence 3, Wits 4, Resolve 2<br /> Strength 3, Dexterity 3, Stamina 1<br /> Presence 1, Manipulation 3, Composure 2<br /> <br /> <b>Skills </b><br /> Computer 3, Investigation 2, Occult 3, Science 3<br /> Athletics 2, Firearms 3, Stealth 2<br /> Persuasion 2, Subterfuge 2<br /> <br /> <b>Merits</b><br /> Resources (3), Energy Channeler (1), Kitbasher (2), Utility Belt (Computers, Science) [It's a Phone] (1), Eidetic Memory (2), Eidetic Memory (Advanced, 1) <i>(Because obviously Genii are going to have access to Advanced Mental Merits)</i><br /> <br /> <b>Advantages</b><br /> Inspiration 1<br /> Impetus Sinks: 3 [Normal, Inspiration + Resolve], +2 (Stressed)<br /> Axioms: Apokalypsi 3<br /> Fields: Fae (Mien Visualizer), Lycanthropy (Lycanthrope Detection, Lunacy Immunization), Thaumaturgy (Spell Analysis, Paradox Detection)<br /> <br /> Defense 5<br /> Initiative Mod 5<br /> Size 5<br /> Speed 11<br /> Health Boxes: 6<br /> Willpower 4<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <i>Step 1: Concept</i><br /> Metanormal Detector (Detects Lifeforms or Phenomena harmful to the Universe, i.e. triggers it's immune systems in some way)<br /> <br /> <i>Step 2: Function</i><br /> Effect: Detects Metanormal Phenomena that causes reactions in the Universe, such as Vampires ('cause they're basically cancer), Werewolves (who might be White Blood Cells but still causes Lunacy, so it counts), Mages (Paradox), Changeling (Their Contract Shenanigans), Prometheans (Disquiet and Wastelands), and Mummies (Syballis)<br /> Range: A (Apokalypsi) Kilometer radius<br /> Duration: One Scene<br /> Skill: Occult (3)<br /> Activation: Instant<br /> <br /> <i>Step 3: Determine Axiom, Field, and Inference</i> - Axiom: Apokalypsi, Field of Lycanthropy (Or any Supernatural really), Inference (Lycanthrope Detection)<br /> <br /> <i>Step 4: Complexity</i> - Base Complexity (1) (Possible for decently informed Occultists), Expertise (+0/+3 if just detecting Werewolves doesn't slide), Other (+1 Broadness), (-1 Serving the Opus [Omniscience gotta start somewhere right?])<br /> Total Complexity: 1/4 if detecting all Supernatural requires more than just Werewolf Mastery (Not terribly complex)<br /> <br /> <i>Step 5: Determine Components</i> - Lycanthrope Genetic Sample (Linchpin), a Radar, X-Ray Machine, (Optional) Hemophage Blood Sample (Major)<br /> <br /> <i>Step 6: Acquiring and Incorporating Components</i> - After a Chapter spent negotiating with/fighting a Werewolf, Nate has acquired a hair sample, he has procured the remaining components when he was conveniently attacked by a Hemophage, probably 'cause he stole that guy's Radar thing. He barely escaped, though he has acquired a Blood sample, so it wasn't a total waste of time.<br /> <br /> Lycanthrope Genetic Sample (Roll Inspiration + Occult) (4) [3, 9, 4, 8] (2 Successes)<br /> <br /> Hemophage Blood (Roll Inspiration + Occult) (4) [6, 10, 8, 8] [1] (3 Successes)<br /> <br /> X-Ray Machine (Roll Inspiration + Computer) (4) [5, 4, 7, 4] (Failed!)<br /> Try Again<br /> X-Ray Machine (Roll Inspiration + Computer) (3) [6, 10, 5] [4] (1 Success)<br /> <br /> Radar (Roll Inspiration + Computer) (4) [10, 1, 5, 1] [5] (1 Success)<br /> <br /> <i>Step 7: Determine Wrinkle</i> - <i>Blind Spots (Certain Metanormal Creatures Can Hide Their Presence Exceptionally Well, The Wonder Can Only Detect Active Metanormal Phenomena, Lycanthropes in Human Form, Masked Fae, Hemophages with Blush of Life, or Thaumaturges Not Casting Spells Cannot Be Detected)</i><br /> <br /> <i>Step 8: Determine Havoc</i> - (Complexity - Axiom) (1 - 3) 1 dice / (4 - 3) 1 dice<br /> <br /> <i>Step 9: Beta Testing</i> - Clash of Wills: Wonder (Havoc + Inspiration) (1) Vs. Genius (Axiom + Skill) (4)<br /> <br /> <i>Round One:</i><br /> Wonder (2 dice): 8, 8 (2 Successes) Surprisingly Dangerous!<br /> Genius (4 dice): 8, 10, 7, 1 [4] (2 Successes) Nate Matches its Ferocity!<br /> Tied!<br /> <br /> <i>Round One-Two:<br /> Nate Spends A Willpower Point!</i><br /> Wonder (2 dice): 8, 9 (2 Successes) Surprisingly Dangerous!, the Dice love the Wonder<br /> Genius (7 dice): 10, 7, 2, 5, 3, 5, 9 [6] (2 Successes) Nate Matches its Ferocity!, The Dice Hate Nate!<br /> <br /> <i>Round One-Three:<br /> Nate Spends A Willpower Point!</i><br /> Wonder (2 dice): 10, 9 [5] (2 Successes) Surprisingly Dangerous!, It keeps getting luckier and more ferocious the longer this keeps up!<br /> Genius (7 dice): 10, 9, 5, 8, 4, 6, 2 [9] (4 Successes) Nate Has Tamed The Wonder!<br /> It is Now A Fully Fledged Wonder!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Metanormal Detector</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Complexity:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 1/4</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Havoc:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dice Pool:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Apokalypsi + Occult</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Scene</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Effect:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> This Device Detects all active Metanotmal Phenomena within an (Apokalypsi) Kilometer Radius</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Wrinkles:</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Blind Spot:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The Detector can only detect active Metanormal Phenomena, such as Firestorms, Distillations, Disciplines, Contracts, Spells, and Werewolf Rites/Werewolves in other forms. They Elude the detector once their powers wear off.</span></span></li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T18:55:45-07:00","id":1101451,"title":"","content":"Now this kind of borders on the edge of the &quot;everything detector.&quot; I would make it +2 complexity for its sheer breadth. If you cut it down to just things that played with the fabric of reality itself (so, dimensional breaches and Paradox), I'd be more accepting of it.<br /> <br /> The components you've chose wouldn't fit that terribly well, and it'd make more sense to have the Linchpin be the means of detection (for example, an Atlantean Spyglass, or a tuning fork made from Thaumium that emits a very specific frequency), and the other components just supporting that. The Radar makes sense, and arguably the X-Ray does, too, but the werewolf and vampire samples would only really fit if it were to detect just them.<br /> <br /> It also might help if you elaborated on the means by which the Wonder detects the incursions. Does it work by detecting cosmological antibodies in the area? Or by detecting fluctuations in the fabric of spacetime? Or does it pick up disturbances in ambient morphic fields? What principles are we working on, here?<br /> <br /> Otherwise, you appear to understand this pretty well. Is there anything you feel I need to clarify in the doc?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T19:02:43-07:00","id":1101454,"title":"","content":"Yes, how broad can a Field be (In specific) and probably some examples of Complexity values","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T19:17:23-07:00","id":1101459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DArchon5</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1101454#post1101454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, how broad can a Field be (In specific) and probably some examples of Complexity values</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. Well, a Field is, roughly, something that's specific enough you could get an advanced degree in it. So you can't have biology as a field, but you could have genetic engineering, microbiology, or biomechanics as a field. The Fields your Genius had are decent examples, although I might pare &quot;Fae&quot; down just slightly (maybe splitting it into Hedge Studies, Fairy Biology, and Wyrd), since there's so much stuff in that. Otherwise, the Fields you have seem to have the right breadth of scope.*<br /> <br /> As for Complexity, when it comes to breadth, here's a rule of thumb:<br /> <br /> If it's very specific in its intent (&quot;You pass butter.&quot;), then it's a +0. Most Wonders should have a single, specific function that it doesn't deviate from.<br /> If it's a little vague, but it's still limited enough not to be always or nearly-always useful, then it's +1. A literally all-terrain vehicle that can do land, air and sea might fall here. It's pretty damn versatile, but it's still got one clear function.<br /> If it's really broad or vague, but it still has firm limits, then it's a +2. Something that could, say, detect pretty much any type of supernatural phenomenon, or is pretty much always going to come in handy, will fall in here.<br /> If it has nearly unlimited applications, or its uses are so varied that it's easier to list what it can't accomplish, then it's +3, and I'd be very leery of even allowing it at my tables. A device that can change anything into anything else, a machine that can arbitrarily relocate objects across the multiverse, etc.<br /> <br /> The Complexity increase for breadth of function is kind of there to act as a deterrent for making anything scanners and do-anything robots, which were kind of an issue in 1e Genius. I'm not sure if this is the way to go about it, though, so if anyone has any thoughts, I'd appreciate it.<br /> <br /> <sup>*I'd also call Lycanthropy &quot;Lycanthropology&quot;, partly for the pun value, but that's not really relevant.</sup>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T22:32:47-07:00","id":1101502,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the Help!<br /> Now lets see..<br /> <br /> Nate:<br /> Axiom: Epikrato 2 Get!<br /> Field: Cosmological Defense Mechanisms, Inferences (Cosmological Antibodies, Cosmological Reactions, Symbiotic Forces)<br /> <br /> <i>Step 1: Concept</i><br /> Macrocosm Pathogen Neutralizer (Controls Cosmological Antibodies To Destroy Metanormal Creatures)<br /> <br /> <i>Step 2: Function</i><br /> Effect: Deal (Epikrato)L to a nearby Metanormal Creatures by Manipulating Cosmological Antibodies, Only Creatures are Affected, Phenomena, such as Loci, and Inanimate Objects, such as Fetishes and most Wonders, are unaffected. Mobile Constructs, such as Wonders of Skafoi and Automata, are still affected. Bypasses passive downgrade damage shenanigans, useless on Normals. It does not have to be aimed but it can only target one at a time, once per turn Reflexive target switch, target has to be in range.<br /> Range: Pistol Ranges as AoE<br /> Duration: One Scene<br /> Skill: Firearms (3)<br /> Activation: Instant<br /> <br /> <i>Step 3: Determine Axiom, Field, and Inference</i> - Axiom: Epikrato, Field of Cosmological Defense Mechanisms, Inference (Cosmological Antibodies)<br /> <br /> <i>Step 4: Complexity</i> - Base Complexity (0) (Its basically a gun that only works on Supernaturals), Expertise (+0), Other (+1 Only works on Supernaturals, Useless on Mortals, +1 No Aiming)<br /> Total Complexity: 2 (Simple)<br /> <br /> <i>Step 5: Determine Components</i> - Cosmological Bacteria (Linchpin, Mane), A Pistol<br /> <br /> <i>Step 6: Acquiring and Incorporating Components</i> - After a Chapter spent negotiating fighting a Cosmological Bacteria, the Components are ready to be integrated<br /> <br /> Cosmological Bacteria (Roll Inspiration + Occult) (4) [5, 1, 3, 5] (Failed!)<br /> Try again<br /> Cosmological Bacteria (Roll Inspiration + Occult) (3) [7, 6, 4] (Failed!)<br /> Try again<br /> Cosmological Bacteria (Roll Inspiration + Occult) (2) [5, 9] (1 Success)<br /> <br /> Pistol (Roll Inspiration + Firearms) (4) [8, 5, 6, 10] [2] (2 Successes)<br /> <br /> <i>Step 7: Determine Wrinkle</i><br /> <i>Specific Targeting: Only Harms Metanormal Beings</i><br /> <br /> <i>Step 8: Determine Havoc</i> - (Complexity - Axiom) (2 - 2) 1 dice<br /> <br /> <i>Step 9: Beta Testing</i> - Clash of Wills: Wonder (Havoc + Inspiration) (2) Vs. Genius (Axiom + Skill) (5)<br /> <i>Round One:</i><br /> Wonder (2 dice): 10, 4 [2] (1 Success)<br /> Genius (5 dice): 3, 8, 1, 1, 5 (1 Success)<br /> <i>Round One-Two:</i><br /> Wonder (2 dice): 6, 9 (1 Success)<br /> Genius (5 dice): 4, 2, 9, 7, 3 (1 Success)<br /> <i>Round One-Three:</i><br /> Wonder (2 dice): 2, 4 (Failed!)<br /> Genius (5 dice): 2, 1, 2, 7, 2 (Failed!)<br /> <i>Round One-Four:</i><br /> Wonder (2 dice): 3, 5 (Failed!)<br /> Genius (5 dice): 8, 5, 2, 10, 5 [3] (2 Successes)<br /> Success!<br /> <br /> <b>Macrocosm Pathogen Neutralizer </b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Complexity:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Havoc:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dice Pool:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Apokalypsi + Firearms</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Scene</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Effect: </span></span>Deal (Epikrato)L to a nearby Metanormal Creatures by Manipulating Cosmological Antibodies, Only Creatures are Affected, Phenomena, such as Loci, and Inanimate Objects, such as Fetishes and most Wonders, are unaffected. Mobile Constructs, such as Wonders of Skafoi and Automata, are still affected. Bypasses passive downgrade damage shenanigans, useless on Normals. It does not have to be aimed but it can only target and damage one per Turn. Reflexive target change at the start of the Turn.<br /> Range: (50 x Epikrato) yards<br /> Wrinkle:<ul><li><i>Specific Targeting: Only Harms Metanormal Beings</i></li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T06:35:24-07:00","id":1101612,"title":"","content":"Hmm. What about an inherent Wonder as a background? IE, lab accident or event happens, altering or tying the new Genius to it. Mechanically, they start with a Wonder, usually Internalized, which triggered their Breakthrough (based on how they responded). So, how to support starting with a Wonder the Character technically (or outright) can't build yet? Like a starting Mage and the Artifact Merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 06-08-2017, 09:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T06:59:59-07:00","id":1101627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DArchon5</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1101502#post1101502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the Help!<br /> Now lets see..<br /> <br /> Nate:<br /> Axiom: Epikrato 2 Get!<br /> Field: Cosmological Defense Mechanisms, Inferences (Cosmological Antibodies, Cosmological Reactions, Symbiotic Forces)<br /> <br /> <i>Step 1: Concept</i><br /> Macrocosm Pathogen Neutralizer (Controls Cosmological Antibodies To Destroy Metanormal Creatures)<br /> <br /> <i>Step 2: Function</i><br /> Effect: Deal (Epikrato)L to a nearby Metanormal Creatures by Manipulating Cosmological Antibodies, Only Creatures are Affected, Phenomena, such as Loci, and Inanimate Objects, such as Fetishes and most Wonders, are unaffected. Mobile Constructs, such as Wonders of Skafoi and Automata, are still affected. Bypasses passive downgrade damage shenanigans, useless on Normals. It does not have to be aimed but it can only target one at a time, once per turn Reflexive target switch, target has to be in range.<br /> Range: Pistol Ranges as AoE<br /> Duration: One Scene<br /> Skill: Firearms (3)<br /> Activation: Instant<br /> <br /> <i>Step 3: Determine Axiom, Field, and Inference</i> - Axiom: Epikrato, Field of Cosmological Defense Mechanisms, Inference (Cosmological Antibodies)<br /> <br /> <i>Step 4: Complexity</i> - Base Complexity (0) (Its basically a gun that only works on Supernaturals), Expertise (+0), Other (+1 Only works on Supernaturals, Useless on Mortals, +1 No Aiming)<br /> Total Complexity: 2 (Simple)<br /> <br /> <i>Step 5: Determine Components</i> - Cosmological Bacteria (Linchpin, Mane), A Pistol<br /> <br /> <i>Step 6: Acquiring and Incorporating Components</i> - After a Chapter spent negotiating fighting a Cosmological Bacteria, the Components are ready to be integrated<br /> <br /> Cosmological Bacteria (Roll Inspiration + Occult) (4) [5, 1, 3, 5] (Failed!)<br /> Try again<br /> Cosmological Bacteria (Roll Inspiration + Occult) (3) [7, 6, 4] (Failed!)<br /> Try again<br /> Cosmological Bacteria (Roll Inspiration + Occult) (2) [5, 9] (1 Success)<br /> <br /> Pistol (Roll Inspiration + Firearms) (4) [8, 5, 6, 10] [2] (2 Successes)<br /> <br /> <i>Step 7: Determine Wrinkle</i><br /> <i>Specific Targeting: Only Harms Metanormal Beings</i><br /> <br /> <i>Step 8: Determine Havoc</i> - (Complexity - Axiom) (2 - 2) 1 dice<br /> <br /> <i>Step 9: Beta Testing</i> - Clash of Wills: Wonder (Havoc + Inspiration) (2) Vs. Genius (Axiom + Skill) (5)<br /> <i>Round One:</i><br /> Wonder (2 dice): 10, 4 [2] (1 Success)<br /> Genius (5 dice): 3, 8, 1, 1, 5 (1 Success)<br /> <i>Round One-Two:</i><br /> Wonder (2 dice): 6, 9 (1 Success)<br /> Genius (5 dice): 4, 2, 9, 7, 3 (1 Success)<br /> <i>Round One-Three:</i><br /> Wonder (2 dice): 2, 4 (Failed!)<br /> Genius (5 dice): 2, 1, 2, 7, 2 (Failed!)<br /> <i>Round One-Four:</i><br /> Wonder (2 dice): 3, 5 (Failed!)<br /> Genius (5 dice): 8, 5, 2, 10, 5 [3] (2 Successes)<br /> Success!<br /> <br /> <b>Macrocosm Pathogen Neutralizer </b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Complexity:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Havoc:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dice Pool:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Apokalypsi + Firearms</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Scene</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Effect: </span></span>Deal (Epikrato)L to a nearby Metanormal Creatures by Manipulating Cosmological Antibodies, Only Creatures are Affected, Phenomena, such as Loci, and Inanimate Objects, such as Fetishes and most Wonders, are unaffected. Mobile Constructs, such as Wonders of Skafoi and Automata, are still affected. Bypasses passive downgrade damage shenanigans, useless on Normals. It does not have to be aimed but it can only target and damage one per Turn. Reflexive target change at the start of the Turn.<br /> Range: (50 x Epikrato) yards<br /> Wrinkle:<ul><li><i>Specific Targeting: Only Harms Metanormal Beings</i></li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Direct damage seems wrong with Epikrato. Maybe instead have it provoke specific systems (such as Paradox), or manipulate a Tilt?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T08:49:46-07:00","id":1102277,"title":"","content":"Quick question: Is this actually simpler/easier than original Wonder creation rules?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T09:47:38-07:00","id":1112163,"title":"","content":"Should we wait until Hunter 2ED comes out so we can borrow ideas from the Endowment rules for Wonders, or do we continue brainstorming right now?<br /> <br /> The Illuminated were mentioned as the possible Strix/Idigam/Huntsmen equivalent for Genius 2ED, but they are closer to Mad Mages. Is there any chance <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4488_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4488\" data-vbnamecard=\"4488\">malonkey1</a> and others could expand on his idea for the Beyonders in the Google Doc as the Strix/Idigam/Huntsmen of 2ED?<br /> <br /> Will Seattle still be the signature city of Genius in 2ED? Will there be optional plot hooks for crossover with Demon, since they share that city? What other cities could fit the themes of Genius, and what would their overall situation look like?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T10:01:12-07:00","id":1112170,"title":"","content":"I still think Illuminated hold a bigger role than the Mad do in Mage.<br /> <br /> As for focus city, what about Silicon Valley, Pittsburgh (see Tesla and Edison), or Bolder Colorado?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T10:26:36-07:00","id":1112188,"title":"","content":"First off, sorry I've been so quiet. I just got a new job at a call center (farewell Subway, I shan't miss you), and I'm getting settled into that, and things have been chaotic at my place in general.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1112163#post1112163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should we wait until Hunter 2ED comes out so we can borrow ideas from the Endowment rules for Wonders, or do we continue brainstorming right now?</div> </div> </div> </div>It might be a good idea to look at those when they're available, yeah. I think there was an Open Dev about it. I'll see if I can find it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Illuminated were mentioned as the possible Strix/Idigam/Huntsmen equivalent for Genius 2ED, but they are closer to Mad Mages. Is there any chance malonkey1 and others could expand on his idea for the Beyonders in the Google Doc as the Strix/Idigam/Huntsmen of 2ED? </div> </div> </div><ul><li>Illuminated: These are probably the headlining &quot;Chronicles&quot; antagonists right now. If a Genius drops too far into Renegade, they might get Illuminated. I think it might be more interesting if they had a sort of &quot;mad lucidity.&quot; Give them a sense that they're clearly seeing <i>something</i> that the rest of the Inspired can't, something they may actually want to know about. They reflect how a Genius can go too far in the search of knowledge, but it's pretty clear that nobody <i>wants</i> to be Illuminated, unless they're already almost there. The Illuminated should be terrifying, but have access to such a deep level of knowledge that it's tempting anyway. Maybe trick some more arrogant Genii into thinking they can dip into that well without losing control.</li> <li>Edisons: The Proximus/Wolf-Blooded analog. They are as much ally as antagonist to Genii. They can still interact with normal humanity, but they also have a very limited form of Inspiration that allows them to duplicate Wonders they've been allowed to analyze. Genii might want them around, since they can help communicate his ideals and theories, but Edisons are often in it for their own gain, often stabbing Genii in the back, playing them against each other, and sometimes just outright stealing from them.</li> <li>Beyonders: These are kind of a broad group. Basically, they are thing that interact with Inspiration, but aren't necessarily Genii nor Manes. You might find interdimensional monsters that get agitated upon seeing Wonders, like they know something you don't, or aliens that demand test subjects in exchange for favors (such favors including &quot;not making you a test subject&quot;), or transhuman invaders from a possible future where Inspiration has spread to all of humanity, and so on.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Will Seattle still be the signature city of Genius in 2ED? Will there be optional plot hooks for crossover with Demon, since they share that city? What other cities could fit the themes of Genius, and what would their overall situation look like? </div> </div> </div>I haven't really thought about the signature city, actually. It'd probably be a good idea not to share a signature city with an existing gameline for simplicity's sake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T11:00:58-07:00","id":1112219,"title":"","content":"Other city options might be those that have hosted a world fair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T14:27:22-07:00","id":1112341,"title":"","content":"Hello! I've been a bit sidetracked from watching this project, but I want to know what your progress is compared to Dragon, and if there's anything we should throw in for crossover stuff... Can anyone give me an overview of what you've got in this book so far?<br /> <br /> Edit: Heh, both the Leviathan 2 and Genius 2 threads are 51 pages...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T20:47:45-07:00","id":1112484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1112341#post1112341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello! I've been a bit sidetracked from watching this project, but I want to know what your progress is compared to Dragon, and if there's anything we should throw in for crossover stuff... Can anyone give me an overview of what you've got in this book so far?<br /> <br /> Edit: Heh, both the Leviathan 2 and Genius 2 threads are 51 pages...</div> </div> </div> </div>You still have access to the Drive folder, right? I can send you the link if you want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T00:01:49-07:00","id":1112533,"title":"","content":"You're right, I should... Please send me the link again so I can re-find it. Also, if you want to chatter at length, you guys should send me your Skype names...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T23:45:33-07:00","id":1118094,"title":"","content":"Idle thought: I think Genii should have the following as a inherent template power. Whenever another supernatural uses a power to affect a Wonder in an unwanted way (such as Epikrato, the Matter Arcanum or Gifts Of Technology), you must roll a Clash Of Wills against the Genius' Resolve + Inspiration + Duration Bonus Of The Wonder + Mania Expenditure. Wonders aren't just held together by nuts and bolts, after all. If a Genius wants to protect a Wonder against direct damage, they can invest in Prostasia.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, why not have the Illuminated + Edisons + Beyonders + whatever else we come up with as the story catalysts of 2ED?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 07-19-2017, 02:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T23:24:54-07:00","id":1119784,"title":"","content":"Been away for awhile but nice to see that there's been activity in this thread!<br /> <br /> Amazing work that's been going into Genius thus far. I find when looking at any Chronicles/2E project it helps to be able to summarize game mechanics and features down to their core points in order to be able to understand the fundamentals, and then build the lore and characters and fluff to Storyteller and players' delight around that. Cheat-sheets if you will. So after looking at some updates in the drive folder I wanted to ask for clarifications here:<br /> <br /> With the change to Impetus, which is condition based and tied to Inspiration values, is there no more Mania point fuel? With Impetus being more like Beast Sateity, rather than the common variations of Vitae/Glamour/Mana/Pyros etc.<br /> <br /> Point of clarification on the Axiom definitions in the Wonder creation rules. I've understood Apokalypsi to be 'information, revelation &amp; <b><i>communication</i></b>' with <u><i>illusion</i></u> being in the purview of Metaptropi with 'transformation &amp; transmutation'<br /> <br /> Wrinkles appears to be the new name for Faults. Any reason for the name change or just personal preference? I like how succinct example Wrinkles are defined, would there be general and Axiom specific Wrinkles again?<br /> <br /> Do Edisons replace Beholden entirely or are they some parallel/tangential/unrelated minor template? I much like the idea of Beholden as acclimatized mortals to a Genius's Wonders and worldview, slowly losing their ambitions and grasp on reality until they are dependent on their relationship/assistance with a Genius (or teeter out in some explosive fashion). I've considered Marty McFly a prime example of a modern Beholden, with his own life but largely defined by is association with Doc, able to (barely) operate his Wonders with the same aptitude as Doc. Doctor Who companions are another example.<br /> <br /> (I'm curious on the use of Edison as the term as per the 'who x in history was really/not a Genius' arguments but there have been people-derived nicknames amongst the Genius tropes before)<br /> <br /> This may sound strange but if the Peerage and Lemuria have the same broad characteristics/factions, which are going to have some Field affinities, what is really the difference with a Field and a Fellowship? A more niche, cross-departmental Field? Esoteric Paradigms? If the character's knowledge of various Fields is going to be the primary means of determining function and flavor, what use from a game development perspective would there be for Fellowships as a 'z-splat' style faction? Unless it could provide something outside of the options available from character creation and the current Wonder &amp; Field mechanics.<br /> <br /> There's a few other things I wanted to address but getting up to speed is more important for now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T11:07:56-07:00","id":1119958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1119784#post1119784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Been away for awhile but nice to see that there's been activity in this thread!<br /> <br /> Amazing work that's been going into Genius thus far. I find when looking at any Chronicles/2E project it helps to be able to summarize game mechanics and features down to their core points in order to be able to understand the fundamentals, and then build the lore and characters and fluff to Storyteller and players' delight around that. Cheat-sheets if you will. So after looking at some updates in the drive folder I wanted to ask for clarifications here:<br /> <br /> With the change to Impetus, which is condition based and tied to Inspiration values, is there no more Mania point fuel? With Impetus being more like Beast Sateity, rather than the common variations of Vitae/Glamour/Mana/Pyros etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, there's no Mania points anymore. If you do something that would Bind Mania, then it just counts as an Impetus sink long-term. If you're doing something that involves spending Mania (e.g. Kitbashing), then you just have an extra Impetus sink for the scene.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Point of clarification on the Axiom definitions in the Wonder creation rules. I've understood Apokalypsi to be 'information, revelation &amp; <b><i>communication</i></b>' with <u><i>illusion</i></u> being in the purview of Metaptropi with 'transformation &amp; transmutation' </div> </div> </div>That was a change mostly because I feelt it made more sense to me. Apokalypsi is the Axiom of information, and I would describe an illusion as a person receiving false information. Again, you can achieve similar effects with differnt Axiomata depending on how exactly you do it, Apokalypsi is just the most direct path to that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wrinkles appears to be the new name for Faults. Any reason for the name change or just personal preference? I like how succinct example Wrinkles are defined, would there be general and Axiom specific Wrinkles again? </div> </div> </div>It was just personal preference on the naming. Genii are arrogant jerks, so I doubt many would feel comfortable referring to the problems in their Wonders as &quot;faults&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do Edisons replace Beholden entirely or are they some parallel/tangential/unrelated minor template? I much like the idea of Beholden as acclimatized mortals to a Genius's Wonders and worldview, slowly losing their ambitions and grasp on reality until they are dependent on their relationship/assistance with a Genius (or teeter out in some explosive fashion). I've considered Marty McFly a prime example of a modern Beholden, with his own life but largely defined by is association with Doc, able to (barely) operate his Wonders with the same aptitude as Doc. Doctor Who companions are another example.<br /> <br /> (I'm curious on the use of Edison as the term as per the 'who x in history was really/not a Genius' arguments but there have been people-derived nicknames amongst the Genius tropes before) </div> </div> </div>Beholden and Edisons are separate phenomena. A Beholden is like Morty Smith, Marty McFly, and the like. Edisons a related, but separate thing. They have a faint glimmer of Inspiration that allows them to remain their own people in the face of the Genius's Inspiration, and they can even build Wonders that they've learned to understand. As their name implies, they often have a relationship to Genii similar to Edison and Tesla. Edisons can be extremely valuable assets for communicating their worldview to the outside world, but they also have a tendency to backstab and steal from Genii.<br /> <br /> Thomas Edison himself is <i>rumoured</i> to still be kicking around under a variety of false identities, trying to run tech startups off of stolen software Wonders. I kind of want to get away from &quot;X was a Genius/Beholden/Whatever&quot;, in favor of &quot;There are some rumors X was a Genius/Beholden/Whatever.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This may sound strange but if the Peerage and Lemuria have the same broad characteristics/factions, which are going to have some Field affinities, what is really the difference with a Field and a Fellowship? A more niche, cross-departmental Field? Esoteric Paradigms? If the character's knowledge of various Fields is going to be the primary means of determining function and flavor, what use from a game development perspective would there be for Fellowships as a 'z-splat' style faction? Unless it could provide something outside of the options available from character creation and the current Wonder &amp; Field mechanics.<br /> <br /> There's a few other things I wanted to address but getting up to speed is more important for now. </div> </div> </div>Fellowships are somewhere between an academic organization and a mystery cult. They have a Field Affinity, but they also have organizational traits that would distinguish them from each other. For example, you might have a Ghost-Busters-type Fellowship and a Fellowship of ecstatic mediums, and while they would both have a Field that dealt in ghosts, they'd have very different aesthetics, entry requirements, grants, and organizational perks. While the Ghostbusters might offer access to their facility and workshops, and might be willing to lend a proton pack-wielding Beholden in a pinch, while the Ecstatics would be able to provide spiritual allies and relatively reliable means of astral projection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":4488,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","user":"malonkey1","date":". 07-24-2017, 02:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T16:59:26-07:00","id":1120143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1119958#post1119958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was a change mostly because I feelt it made more sense to me. Apokalypsi is the Axiom of information, and I would describe an illusion as a person receiving false information. Again, you can achieve similar effects with differnt Axiomata depending on how exactly you do it, Apokalypsi is just the most direct path to that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm thinking more along the lines of appearance changing projections, holograms, false smells and the like whenever your Metatropi Wonders create <i>Illusions</i> without creating a permanent change (in most cases). Deceptions or miscommunication along your bedrock transceiver is fine, of course, but that sounds like a case of user input as to whether the information is factual or false. Apokalypsi as the Axiom of Discovery is about the revelation and sending of information. My Apokalypsi wonder would be the best way to leave a convincing paper trail, but I'm not going to use it to throw up a fake wall to cover my escape. Metaptropi is the more fitting Axiom to include 'conjuration tricks' where it looks like you just created something out of nothing, and then everyone finds out the construct wasn't even substantial to begin with.<br /> <br /> Basically it boils down to one's definition of illusion. The rest of the changes make sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T17:13:25-07:00","id":1120151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1119958#post1119958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, there's no Mania points anymore. If you do something that would Bind Mania, then it just counts as an Impetus sink long-term. If you're doing something that involves spending Mania (e.g. Kitbashing), then you just have an extra Impetus sink for the scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>Has that actually been finalized, or is it still being tested out? I'm somewhat fine either way (I think), but Mania seems like it allows for smaller units of comparison than Impetus Sinks (which really needs a better, one-word name).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1119958#post1119958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was a change mostly because I felt it made more sense to me. Apokalypsi is the Axiom of information, and I would describe an illusion as a person receiving false information. Again, you can achieve similar effects with differnt Axiomata depending on how exactly you do it, Apokalypsi is just the most direct path to that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. I think Metatropi still works a bit better as Transforming sensory input. I could see Faults/Wrinkles in Apokalypsi Wonders having illusionary effects, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1119958#post1119958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was just personal preference on the naming. Genii are arrogant jerks, so I doubt many would feel comfortable referring to the problems in their Wonders as &quot;faults&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes sense, though &quot;wrinkle&quot; still doesn't sound right somehow. I'll need to look at a Thesaurus...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1119958#post1119958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beholden and Edisons are separate phenomena. A Beholden is like Morty Smith, Marty McFly, and the like. Edisons a related, but separate thing. They have a faint glimmer of Inspiration that allows them to remain their own people in the face of the Genius's Inspiration, and they can even build Wonders that they've learned to understand. As their name implies, they often have a relationship to Genii similar to Edison and Tesla. Edisons can be extremely valuable assets for communicating their worldview to the outside world, but they also have a tendency to backstab and steal from Genii.<br /> <br /> Thomas Edison himself is <i>rumoured</i> to still be kicking around under a variety of false identities, trying to run tech startups off of stolen software Wonders. I kind of want to get away from &quot;X was a Genius/Beholden/Whatever&quot;, in favor of &quot;There are some rumors X was a Genius/Beholden/Whatever.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Better call. So Edisons have an Impetus/Mania pool, and can recreate (but not Invent) Wonders? But the don't suffer from Jabir?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1119958#post1119958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fellowships are somewhere between an academic organization and a mystery cult. They have a Field Affinity, but they also have organizational traits that would distinguish them from each other. For example, you might have a Ghost-Busters-type Fellowship and a Fellowship of ecstatic mediums, and while they would both have a Field that dealt in ghosts, they'd have very different aesthetics, entry requirements, grants, and organizational perks. While the Ghostbusters might offer access to their facility and workshops, and might be willing to lend a proton pack-wielding Beholden in a pinch, while the Ecstatics would be able to provide spiritual allies and relatively reliable means of astral projection.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always saw it as a matter of focus and degree - Foundations are communities of interest to entire Axioms, while Fellowships focus on specific applications or Fields.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T19:05:11-07:00","id":1120181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1120151#post1120151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has that actually been finalized, or is it still being tested out? I'm somewhat fine either way (I think), but Mania seems like it allows for smaller units of comparison than Impetus Sinks (which really needs a better, one-word name).</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing here is really finalized. If we come up with something that works better, we could certainly go with that instead. Mania is definitely more granular, which has its own advantages, but I like Impetus because it's not granular. It's flexible and approximate. If you're a Genius who maintains their psychic powers with intense daily meditation and potent psychoactive drugs, then you do that, and you can maintain X number of distinct powers at a time, instead of having one that Binds 2 Mania, another that binds 5, still another that binds 3 but also costs 1 to use. It's kind of a tradeoff between granularity and simplicity to me, and I prefer to err on the side of simplicity and ease in this case.<br /> <br /> I may also be looking back at Wonder creation later, as I can't say that it's objectively simpler (although I think it's at least a little more grokable) than 1E Wonders. Except for Automata. Switching to Retainer and Horror rules for Automata makes it so much easier that the whole Automation Points subsystem, to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Better call. So Edisons have an Impetus/Mania pool, and can recreate (but not Invent) Wonders? But the don't suffer from Jabir? </div> </div> </div>Pretty much, yeah. Edisons are sort of, I guess Half-Inspired? They can't make new Wonders, because they don't have that kind of spark behind them, but that means their souls are still intact enough to function in human society without too much trouble. They are the script kiddies and asset flippers to the Genius's deep-level hackers and developers. The main reason they haven't managed to totally infiltrate the Peerage and Lemuria is a mixture of Genius paranoia, and the fact that Edisons can also steal from each other, and do so quite frequently. If a Storyteller wanted to, they could add a whole layer of Inspired society made of corporate espionage and revenge with the Edisons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I always saw it as a matter of focus and degree - Foundations are communities of interest to entire Axioms, while Fellowships focus on specific applications or Fields. </div> </div> </div>It's a bit of that, too. Fellowships are more specific in their interests and how they work. Some are more worried about the subject, and might have members from a variety of Foundations (or even Baramins!), others are strictly following under one specific worldview, but they all have a specific field of study that they focus on heavily. You can be a member of one of more Fellowships, provided you can maintain Dues (Fellowship Dues vary widely, from research data, to material or personnel resources, or even an Impetus Sink), but you don't want to join too many Fellowships in case of a conflict, and though you can enter and leave them freely and keep access to the Field (provided you've taken the time to learn it), you might get a reputation for disloyalty or opportunism if you leave and enter a lot of Fellowships too often.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T23:26:33-07:00","id":1120247,"title":"","content":"I think there should be no axioms instead it's about the flavor like do you make lazer gun or freeze ray that would alow players more combos but give your genie a theme fiting them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T06:00:03-07:00","id":1120331,"title":"","content":"Hmm, I'm guessing reputation means a lot to the Genii. As for Impetus, we should probably increase the amount Genii gain, but yeah, simplicity is better. As for Apokalypsi Illusions... better make them more limited than Metatropi Illusions, like how you differed Automata and Epikrato Control","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T16:10:29-07:00","id":1122828,"title":"","content":"malonkey1, Is there any more to this new version of Genius than you have written down? Are you Kyle Marquis, aka Moochava, and are you coming out with a CoD compatible Genius? I hope so. I really hope so. There's so much that can be done with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T22:01:06-07:00","id":1122909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpectacularTentacular</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1122828#post1122828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">malonkey1, Is there any more to this new version of Genius than you have written down? Are you Kyle Marquis, aka Moochava, and are you coming out with a CoD compatible Genius? I hope so. I really hope so. There's so much that can be done with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>In order: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Yes, I do have more stuff written down, in a Google Drive folder, although I have shared most of it with you guys.</li> <li>I am not Kyle Maquis. I e-mailed him, and asked him if he had any plans for 2E Genius, and he said he did not, but did not object to others making it.</li> <li>Yes, I do intend to come out with a CoD compatible Genius. I won't have a lot of time to work on it, though, as I have a full-time job and am also returning to school (my last year before I get my degree in being Dilbert!). I'll try to keep up, though.</li> </ol><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T10:04:19-07:00","id":1123054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1122909#post1122909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In order:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Yes, I do have more stuff written down, in a Google Drive folder, although I have shared most of it with you guys.</li> <li>I am not Kyle Maquis. I e-mailed him, and asked him if he had any plans for 2E Genius, and he said he did not, but did not object to others making it.</li> <li>Yes, I do intend to come out with a CoD compatible Genius. I won't have a lot of time to work on it, though, as I have a full-time job and am also returning to school (my last year before I get my degree in being Dilbert!). I'll try to keep up, though.</li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I wasn't sure, but I appreciate the effort you're making on updating Genius. So far, looks good!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T05:50:23-07:00","id":1124716,"title":"","content":"Hmm. How &quot;Mental&quot; are Genii? Might a &quot;Mental Intensity&quot; mechanic similar to Vampire's Physical Intensity be suited for the template?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T07:09:04-07:00","id":1124746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1124716#post1124716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. How &quot;Mental&quot; are Genii? Might a &quot;Mental Intensity&quot; mechanic similar to Vampire's Physical Intensity be suited for the template?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they are pretty mental.<br /> <br /> They're also really intellectually capable, too. <sup>rimshot</sup><br /> <br /> Thus far they can perform &quot;Bat Deductions&quot; to skip past Clues in investigations, and they can Overclock mundane technology, using an extremely broad definition of technology that basically means &quot;Any practical application of mortal knowledge founded on sound, self-consistent observations of the real world,&quot; meaning it includes things like psychoanalysis, exorcisms, and mathematics. So they could turn a normal form of psychoanalysis into a freakishly-accurate &quot;Sherlock Scan,&quot; or they could turbo-charge an old Cadillac into a super-racer for a scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":4488,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","user":"malonkey1","date":". 08-04-2017, 10:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T21:23:15-07:00","id":1125786,"title":"","content":"So with the change from Mania to Impetus, I wanted to address what changes that would bring to the minor templates and features converted from 1E to 2E.<br /> <br /> A Genius gained 1 Mania each day, along with other methods of gaining it. Most Manes and certain types of Wonder required 1 Mania each day, and any Inspired Manes or similar basically canceled out their daily Mania gain/spent. Thus far, easy to see how that works with Impetus.<br /> <br /> So then you get to the ways Mania was stored. At the core, Beholden were useful not only for physical assistance and servitude, they could be supplied with Mania as limited by their Intelligence + Resolve. That Mania could be used to empower other Wonders independently.<br /> <br /> So if the Genius must still transfer Impetus to a Beholden, making that character a &quot;sink&quot; is it always required for the Beholden to have Impetus to be a Beholden? And if Impetus is more limited in scope, like Satiety, might it instead be the Genius could extend their own Impetus with the Beholden's traits provided they maintain their loyalty? I always figured more was at work than just being Mania/Impetus batteries, as Beholden have their worldview dominated by their Genius's perspective that even their characteristics like Virtue and Vice work differently.<br /> <br /> And for the distinction with Edisons, they can generate Impetus but not use it? What is their limit of Impetus without becoming a full blown Genius (or worse)?<br /> <br /> Although in contrast, this change of system may better explain the Hollow Men/Clockstoppers, the enemies of the Inspired that become walking Banes to all Wondrous and mundane technology, innovation and development. They just suck the Impetus out of things like avatars of entropy. Which could also be used for invading Manes and stranger things to crop up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T22:46:10-07:00","id":1125801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1125786#post1125786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So with the change from Mania to Impetus, I wanted to address what changes that would bring to the minor templates and features converted from 1E to 2E.<br /> <br /> A Genius gained 1 Mania each day, along with other methods of gaining it. Most Manes and certain types of Wonder required 1 Mania each day, and any Inspired Manes or similar basically canceled out their daily Mania gain/spent. Thus far, easy to see how that works with Impetus.<br /> <br /> So then you get to the ways Mania was stored. At the core, Beholden were useful not only for physical assistance and servitude, they could be supplied with Mania as limited by their Intelligence + Resolve. That Mania could be used to empower other Wonders independently.<br /> <br /> So if the Genius must still transfer Impetus to a Beholden, making that character a &quot;sink&quot; is it always required for the Beholden to have Impetus to be a Beholden? And if Impetus is more limited in scope, like Satiety, might it instead be the Genius could extend their own Impetus with the Beholden's traits provided they maintain their loyalty? I always figured more was at work than just being Mania/Impetus batteries, as Beholden have their worldview dominated by their Genius's perspective that even their characteristics like Virtue and Vice work differently.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm thinking that Beholden will indeed be Impetus Sinks. Basically, you can place 1 Impetus into a Beholden, and that Beholden can use it as they see fit, possibly maintain a Wonder (or building one to your specifications), using certain Genius abilities like the Bat Deduction, or just holding onto it for safe keeping. A Beholden without an Impetus suffers the effects of the Soulless condition (although it doesn't progress unless they actually lose their soul).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And for the distinction with Edisons, they can generate Impetus but not use it? What is their limit of Impetus without becoming a full blown Genius (or worse)? </div> </div> </div>They can generate Impetus, and they can use it in limited fashion. Basically, they have Inspiration 0, so they need to get a Generator, sponsorship from a Genius, or go into Stressed if they want to use it. They can make Wonders they have been allowed to analyze, but they cannot produce Wonders of their own invention. I think I've previously compared them to &quot;script kiddies,&quot; and it's still the most apt comparison I can think of.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Although in contrast, this change of system may better explain the Hollow Men/Clockstoppers, the enemies of the Inspired that become walking Banes to all Wondrous and mundane technology, innovation and development. They just suck the Impetus out of things like avatars of entropy. Which could also be used for invading Manes and stranger things to crop up. </div> </div> </div>That's certainly one way that it could work. If Clockstoppers are a force of anti-Inspiration, they would definitely be sucking Impetus out of things. Manes could also conceivably take over a Generator appropriate to their Paradigms, as could Beyonders with a specific goal. For example, there are rumours of a Mane based on the idea of a future of genetically-perfect supermen hanging around Genentech and occasionally sneaking in to taste the genetic samples. But that's just crazy. My buddy, the six-foot-five, athletically-built, unusually well-educated security guard says he hasn't seen anything like that. Nice guy. He'll flip his shit if you try to touch him, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":4488,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","user":"malonkey1","date":". 08-07-2017, 01:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T02:11:17-07:00","id":1126225,"title":"","content":"Speaking of Impetus and Clockstoppers, I had a though about both very recently thanks to some lovely videos I've recently viewed regarding actual science! <br /> <br /> An interesting angle to look at how Impetus is shaping up is very similar to the concept of Dark Energy, the theoretic forces that set the universe into motion and will inevitable lead to the heat death of the universe itself. In this take the Genii are able to channel that Dark Energy, the Prima Impetus, in order to accelerate physical and metaphysical phenomena into new shapes and forms that would otherwise be impossible with humanity's current level of technology. The Clockstoppers by contrast in this theory would be the unknowing avatars for the counterpart to Dark Energy: Dark Matter, the matter that binds the known universe together into something even capable of sustaining form and structure, let alone the potential for sentient life. Rather than an anti-Impetus force they would be more akin to a counter-Impetus force that act as Stasis' agents to negate strong outputs of Impetus in order to prevent reality from being irrevocably changed by the Genii's vision. But then again that's just some sci-fi musing I had. More than anything I'm just amazed that Impetus ended up sharing such similarities with an actual theoretical energy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T03:59:43-07:00","id":1126247,"title":"","content":"Great idea sage","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T09:11:25-07:00","id":1126328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1126225#post1126225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of Impetus and Clockstoppers, I had a though about both very recently thanks to some lovely videos I've recently viewed regarding actual science!<br /> <br /> An interesting angle to look at how Impetus is shaping up is very similar to the concept of Dark Energy, the theoretic forces that set the universe into motion and will inevitable lead to the heat death of the universe itself. In this take the Genii are able to channel that Dark Energy, the Prima Impetus, in order to accelerate physical and metaphysical phenomena into new shapes and forms that would otherwise be impossible with humanity's current level of technology. The Clockstoppers by contrast in this theory would be the unknowing avatars for the counterpart to Dark Energy: Dark Matter, the matter that binds the known universe together into something even capable of sustaining form and structure, let alone the potential for sentient life. Rather than an anti-Impetus force they would be more akin to a counter-Impetus force that act as Stasis' agents to negate strong outputs of Impetus in order to prevent reality from being irrevocably changed by the Genii's vision. But then again that's just some sci-fi musing I had. More than anything I'm just amazed that Impetus ended up sharing such similarities with an actual theoretical energy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That is definitely how a Genius with an astrophysicist bent might explain Impetus. It wasn't on my mind at the time, but it's neat. I might use that at some point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T10:43:13-07:00","id":1126362,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4488_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4488\" data-vbnamecard=\"4488\">malonkey1</a> Where is the main drive location? Worth adding it to your sig, you think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T10:48:41-07:00","id":1126367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1126362#post1126362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4488_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4488\" data-vbnamecard=\"4488\">malonkey1</a> Where is the main drive location? Worth adding it to your sig, you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably a good idea, yeah.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=13snxZhcaNzrOdVX35TVJPO4aMsqIN3gzHRV8ePCNfiU\" target=\"_blank\">Also, here's Beholden and Edisons.</a><br /> <br /> Morty Smith is what I consider the best example of a Beholden.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Alright, so apprently, it shortened the text. Eh, it still gets the point across.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":4488,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","user":"malonkey1","date":". 08-08-2017, 01:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T10:59:03-07:00","id":1126374,"title"