angression-2th-edition?p=1126374#post1126374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also broke the link.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hang on, I figured out what I did wrong. Should be fixed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T11:23:18-07:00","id":1126386,"title":"","content":"Haven't been keeping up recently -- are Beholden still intended to be unable to hold coherent worldviews or perspectives unless said are transmitted to them by Genii?<br /> <br /> Also, I feel like &quot;all persuasion rolls are rote actions&quot; is way too powerful for an innate ability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5757-calvaryketer","user":"CalvaryKeter","date":". 08-08-2017, 02:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5757-calvaryketer","name":"CalvaryKeter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5757_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T11:51:09-07:00","id":1126396,"title":"","content":"Glad the Sci-Fi musings were enjoyed. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I have a couple more ideas based around the whole Dark Matter &amp; Dark Energy thought, use them as you will or not at all if it please you. <br /> <br /> \u2022 Impetus &amp; Stasis as energy sources for Genii: In this scenario the Inspired have two power sources instead of one. Impetus functions as normal without any changes, Stasis on the other hand functions as a stabilizing energy to Impetus' creative/destructive energy. Wonders then would be created with a certain number of Links, the more one has the more advanced it is. Linking Impetus to a Wonder does exactly what was talked about earlier. It powers the Wonder and allows it unleash more power at the cost of potential Havoc. Linking Stasis to a Wonder however still powers it, but at the cost of loosing some of the more potent functions of the Wonder at the cost of eliminating the chances for Havoc and adding greater longevity and durability to the Wonder. Also, in this system Impetus would be far more readily come by since Stasis is rarer and potentially more dangerous to acquire since harvesting it is more likely to attract entities that are devoted to keeping the status quo. With this system Stasis would be needed to build the most advance Wonders, and balancing which Links are filled with which energy could potentially make for an excellent puzzle for player characters. <br /> <br /> \u2022 Stasis and Banisher Equivalencies: In this scenario we introduce the Genii Clockstoppers. Or, more accurately, Genii who's vision is filled with all the possibilities for everything to go wrong. Instead of seeing Utopia they see 1984 or Mad Max potential in the labors of the other Inspired, so they instead work to prevent such futures from ever happening by working against their fellows. Like Banishers many might join together to form their own Stasis Foundations, some more terrifying still might become Unmada. But the two things they all have in common is a deep fear for what the future may bring with Genii behind the wheel and the ability to create Clockstoppers in the same way Genii create Beholden. <br /> <br /> And that's all I've got for now. As mentioned these are just personal ideas I've had based around the work done so far. Great work is being done here, can't wait to see more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T12:05:26-07:00","id":1126401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1126396#post1126396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Glad the Sci-Fi musings were enjoyed. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I have a couple more ideas based around the whole Dark Matter &amp; Dark Energy thought, use them as you will or not at all if it please you.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Impetus &amp; Stasis as energy sources for Genii: In this scenario the Inspired have two power sources instead of one. Impetus functions as normal without any changes, Stasis on the other hand functions as a stabilizing energy to Impetus' creative/destructive energy. Wonders then would be created with a certain number of Links, the more one has the more advanced it is. Linking Impetus to a Wonder does exactly what was talked about earlier. It powers the Wonder and allows it unleash more power at the cost of potential Havoc. Linking Stasis to a Wonder however still powers it, but at the cost of loosing some of the more potent functions of the Wonder at the cost of eliminating the chances for Havoc and adding greater longevity and durability to the Wonder. Also, in this system Impetus would be far more readily come by since Stasis is rarer and potentially more dangerous to acquire since harvesting it is more likely to attract entities that are devoted to keeping the status quo. With this system Stasis would be needed to build the most advance Wonders, and balancing which Links are filled with which energy could potentially make for an excellent puzzle for player characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds even more complicated, sadly. High Restraint accomplishes similarly, in that Wonders are more enduring/stable, but more costly (which I'd like to be interchangeable with power).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1126396#post1126396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 Stasis and Banisher Equivalencies: In this scenario we introduce the Genii Clockstoppers. Or, more accurately, Genii who's vision is filled with all the possibilities for everything to go wrong. Instead of seeing Utopia they see 1984 or Mad Max potential in the labors of the other Inspired, so they instead work to prevent such futures from ever happening by working against their fellows. Like Banishers many might join together to form their own Stasis Foundations, some more terrifying still might become Unmada. But the two things they all have in common is a deep fear for what the future may bring with Genii behind the wheel and the ability to create Clockstoppers in the same way Genii create Beholden.<br /> <br /> And that's all I've got for now. As mentioned these are just personal ideas I've had based around the work done so far. Great work is being done here, can't wait to see more.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Genii who's vision is filled with all the possibilities for everything to go wrong.&quot; Isn't this basically Klagen?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 08-08-2017, 03:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T12:35:14-07:00","id":1126411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1126367#post1126367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Probably a good idea, yeah.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=13snxZhcaNzrOdVX35TVJPO4aMsqIN3gzHRV8ePCNfiU\" target=\"_blank\">Also, here's Beholden and Edisons.</a><br /> <br /> Morty Smith is what I consider the best example of a Beholden.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd generalize the Beholden's loyalty to whatever is supplying them with Impetus. This is mostly how it is, but doesn't need to call out Genii and Edisons specifically all the time. Plus it allows for Beholden to be influenced by Generators with an agenda of their own, or other forces.<br /> <br /> Also, maybe make it so they aren't &quot;Spineless&quot; - their worldview is bent toward whatever their Impetus source's is. This will naturally make them amenable to whatever the source wants (same vision and all), but still allows for Beholden to stand up to their sources if the source deviates from their original goal. And, of course, Renegades would probably be incentivized to browbeat their Beholden to make them more compliant.<br /> <br /> Additionally, I still think the baseline for Impetus should be something other than straight Inspiration (like Resolve, or flip it with Stress and make it Composure to start with, then Inspiration).<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5757-calvaryketer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5757_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5757\" data-vbnamecard=\"5757\">CalvaryKeter</a> that Rote actions to persuasion (no limits or conditions) is too strong. I mean, they already have a leg up by not needing to worry about Jabir.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T13:42:40-07:00","id":1126437,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a> <br /> <br /> You're going to have to remind me which Catalyst the Klagen was again exactly. Because there is a good chance I just subconsciously drew upon that idea. It has happened many times before. - . -'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T13:57:19-07:00","id":1126440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1126437#post1126437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a><br /> <br /> You're going to have to remind me which Catalyst the Klagen was again exactly. Because there is a good chance I just subconsciously drew upon that idea. It has happened many times before. - . -'</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Catalyst of sorrow. They are the ones with the quote about &quot;put down the syringe so we don't have to fight zombies. Again.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T14:04:43-07:00","id":1126442,"title":"","content":"Ah, well not as close as I was fearing but I do see your point. In that case they would be a zero sum sort of Klagen. Less reason with the transgressor and more destroy them, their prototype, their research, anyone who witnessed their research, and anyone who witnessed them destroying the above mentioned. Sorta like regular Clockstoppers except with Genius level abilities and their own Wonders at their disposal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T15:56:08-07:00","id":1126485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CalvaryKeter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1126386#post1126386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Haven't been keeping up recently -- are Beholden still intended to be unable to hold coherent worldviews or perspectives unless said are transmitted to them by Genii?<br /> <br /> Also, I feel like &quot;all persuasion rolls are rote actions&quot; is way too powerful for an innate ability.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that is probably too powerful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1126411#post1126411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd generalize the Beholden's loyalty to whatever is supplying them with Impetus. This is mostly how it is, but doesn't need to call out Genii and Edisons specifically all the time. Plus it allows for Beholden to be influenced by Generators with an agenda of their own, or other forces.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would probably work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, maybe make it so they aren't &quot;Spineless&quot; - their worldview is bent toward whatever their Impetus source's is. This will naturally make them amenable to whatever the source wants (same vision and all), but still allows for Beholden to stand up to their sources if the source deviates from their original goal. And, of course, Renegades would probably be incentivized to browbeat their Beholden to make them more compliant. </div> </div> </div>Makes sense. That actually would make it more interesting, when your Beholden seems to be more focused on the goal than the Genius sometimes.<br /> <br /> Now, Beholden have &quot;The Mission,&quot; which makes protecting their Impetus Source's long-term goals an aspiration.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Additionally, I still think the baseline for Impetus should be something other than straight Inspiration (like Resolve, or flip it with Stress and make it Composure to start with, then Inspiration). </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I thought I had actually already done that. Fixed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T16:50:02-07:00","id":1126503,"title":"","content":"Hmm. Idea after rereading Impetus: What about making Foundation, instead of granting XP discounts to Axioms (as in 1E), instead offer bonus Impetus specifically for Wonders of those Axioms? Such that, if you an Artificer (for instance), you can support an Automata or Prostasia Wonder (IS = 1?) without counting against your normal limit? Possibly in addition to some Grant ability which the bonus Impetus might also be spent for.<br /> <br /> Or maybe do similar with Catalysts. Or something. Just an idea.<br /> <hr /><br /> Also, regarding Larvae, I'd like to re-push tying them into Touchstones. Namely, they don't just arise from Transgressions, but specifically Transgression against/with/using your Touchstones. They cost you the Touchstone, but offer <i>power</i>.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, I'm thinking a benefit equivalent to 3XP, 1 for the Touchstone merit dot, 2 for the no-doubt lost Restraint.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 08-08-2017, 08:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T18:53:03-07:00","id":1126547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1126503#post1126503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. Idea after rereading Impetus: What about making Foundation, instead of granting XP discounts to Axioms (as in 1E), instead offer bonus Impetus specifically for Wonders of those Axioms? Such that, if you an Artificer (for instance), you can support an Automata or Prostasia Wonder (IS = 1?) without counting against your normal limit? Possibly in addition to some Grant ability which the bonus Impetus might also be spent for.<br /> <br /> Or maybe do similar with Catalysts. Or something. Just an idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an interesting idea, actually. For example, Progenitors might get extra Impetus for Wonders that further the whole &quot;transhuman&quot; aspect of their ideals, while Artificers could get extra Impetus for industrial Wonders. I think we might actually want to go with that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, regarding Larvae, I'd like to re-push tying them into Touchstones. Namely, they don't just arise from Transgressions, but specifically Transgression against/with/using your Touchstones. They cost you the Touchstone, but offer <i>power</i>.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, I'm thinking a benefit equivalent to 3XP, 1 for the Touchstone merit dot, 2 for the no-doubt lost Restraint. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm not opposed. Making Larvae about a more personal severance from humanity. Larvae being used in a Wonder, or being used as an easy path to a Thesis. For example, it's a lot easier to study the effects of soul loss if you rip the soul out of somebody, rather than waiting for somebody to lose their soul.<br /> <br /> As for Theses, I wasn't sure where to go with them, or if we should even keep them. The idea was that in order to learn a new Field, gain Inspiration, or gain a rank in a non-favored Axiom, you had to acquire the Thesis Persistent Condition from studying a phenomenon relating to the Field, Axiom, or your Paradigm, and then once you earned 4 Inspired Beats (1 Inspired Experience), you would then resolve the Condition and be able to gain the Field/Axiom Dot/Inspiration Dot. Using a Larva under this paradigm* would basically be equivalent to taking moral shortcuts, letting you learn a lot quickly, but at a terrible moral cost, immediately Resolving it and giving you the Inspired Experience on the spot, similarly to Diablerie being an easy way to get Experiences for Blood Potency at the cost of messing up what remains of their soul.<br /> <br /> <b>Off-the-cuff, rough idea for the Thesis Condition:</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Thesis (Persistent)</b><br /> In order to advance in their work, a Genius needs to perform studies to understand their subjects. This takes the form of a Thesis, a collection of observations and experiments that are intended to lay a subject bare to the Genius's Inspired knowledge.<br /> <b>Acquiring the Condition:</b> A Genius can choose to acquire this condition upon encountering a new Inspired or otherwise Paranormal phenomenon, keying it to a relevant Field or Axiom, or keying it to their Paradigm (and thus Inspiration). What qualifies as &quot;new&quot; is vague, but there has to be a real qulaitative difference from anything they've yet studied. For example, a Genius could study a Mane capable of manipulating Orgone energy to get this Condition, and later study a different Mane that accesses Gestalt consciousness to get a different version of this Condition, but they can't try and study an Orgone Mane, and then another Orgone Mane. A Genius can have up to three versions of this Condition, one for a Field, one for a non-favored Axiom, and one for their Paradigm.<br /> <b>Beat:</b> Each time the Genius further studies an Inspired or paranormal phenomenon relating to the subject of this Condition, they gain an Inspired Beat.<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> This Condition Resolves when the Genius has gained 4 Inspired Beats from it. Upon Resolving the Condition, the Genius can now gain the Field, Axiom Dot, or Inspiration Dot they were working toward. The Genius can also use a Larva to immediately Resolve the Condition, gaining an Inspired Experience in the process.<br /> <b>Ending the Condition:</b> A Genius can voluntarily end this Condition without Resolving it, effectively giving up on the avenue of study it represents.<br /> <br /> <b>Example Thesis: &quot;A Dissertation</b><b> on the Speciation of Non-Material Entities&quot;</b><br /> Doctor Astral has noted that, despite being the most important part of human reality, astral beings are emphatically the <i>least</i> common form of non-material beings in the universe. Seeing as that is the case, he's decided to study how the various ephemerals differ in order to better understand and control the Gestalt. This is keyed to Doctor Astral's Paradigm of Gestalt consciousness, and resolving it will allow him to increase his Inspiration.<br /> <b>Beat: </b>Gain an Inspired Beat each time you learn the properties of a new ephemeral being, or find a new interaction between differing ephemera. Thus far, he has gained 2 such Beats, and is working on his third.<ul><li>Thus far, Doctor Astral has been able to study a being that called itself &quot;Begotten&quot; which appears to be some kind of human fear dredged up from the Gestalt and placed in a human body. Studying how its Lair connects the Astral to the physical world was quite edifying.</li> <li>Doctor Astral has also been able to analyze a ghost, and determined the symbolic significance of Anchors as they relate to the ghost's experiences, and has determined the ghost to be a psychic imprint of its former self upon those Anchors.</li> <li>Presently, Doctor Astral has been attempting to determine how Spirits are able to cross the Gauntlet, and what separates their animistic spiritual Gestalt from the human Gestalt, but has not yet made any breakthroughs.</li> </ul><br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Upon gaining his fourth Inspired Beat from this Condition, it will Resolve. Doctor Astral's player, Roger, has also determined that he could make a Larva if he were to purposely cause his Touchstone, a kindly old neighbor named Lucille, to become possessed or Claimed in order to study its effects.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> *<sup>Pun totally intended</sup><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T18:20:58-07:00","id":1126911,"title":"","content":"That's a good look at the Thesis, glad to see it still exists in the mechanics somewhere and has also expanded to include Axioms and Fields beyond Inspiration. Does that include all Axiom dots, or would it be waived for the Catalyst's core Axiom?<br /> <br /> <br /> As for what the Foundation provides in terms of Impetus boosts, are the Foundations still granting further starting Axioms? Or might they work better offering starting Fields? While not limiting Fields to only certain Foundations, there's a few 'career' ideas around each Foundation that could serve as initial Field examples.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T22:25:20-07:00","id":1126980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1126911#post1126911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a good look at the Thesis, glad to see it still exists in the mechanics somewhere and has also expanded to include Axioms and Fields beyond Inspiration. Does that include all Axiom dots, or would it be waived for the Catalyst's core Axiom?</div> </div> </div> </div>It only includes non-Favored Axiomata. Favored Axiomata don't require a thesis, since they come more naturally to the Genius.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for what the Foundation provides in terms of Impetus boosts, are the Foundations still granting further starting Axioms? Or might they work better offering starting Fields? While not limiting Fields to only certain Foundations, there's a few 'career' ideas around each Foundation that could serve as initial Field examples. </div> </div> </div>My thinking is that Foundations (and Baramins) have favored Fields, with each Genius getting a second Favored Axiom of their choice to make up. With how Axiomata tend to be so broad, it felt odd to tie a specific Axiom to what was originally a specific scientific discipline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T03:46:12-07:00","id":1127035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1126980#post1126980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My thinking is that Foundations (and Baramins) have favored Fields, with each Genius getting a second Favored Axiom of their choice to make up. With how Axiomata tend to be so broad, it felt odd to tie a specific Axiom to what was originally a specific scientific discipline.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except they Axiomata are more ways (more accurately ends) of doing things. Fields are so broad, that for the Foundations to be comprehensive, they'd have huge lists.<br /> <br /> Fellowships are usually more specialized and would fit particular Fields better, I think. Plus, if they have similar benefits (Bonus Impetus for things in theme), then they could stack, so the Malcom T. Washington Fellowship could have a Field of Arthropods which an Artificer could use to make many or a single powerful Anthropod Automata without adversely affecting their normal limits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T07:52:13-07:00","id":1127116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1127035#post1127035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except they Axiomata are more ways (more accurately ends) of doing things. Fields are so broad, that for the Foundations to be comprehensive, they'd have huge lists.<br /> <br /> Fellowships are usually more specialized and would fit particular Fields better, I think. Plus, if they have similar benefits (Bonus Impetus for things in theme), then they could stack, so the Malcom T. Washington Fellowship could have a Field of Arthropods which an Artificer could use to make many or a single powerful Anthropod Automata without adversely affecting their normal limits.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's valid. My thinking was that it was odd to tie specific Axiomata to specific Foundations. An Artificer could be just as capable with Skafoi as a Navigator. Just look at Henry Ford.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T08:15:11-07:00","id":1127133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1127116#post1127116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's valid. My thinking was that it was odd to tie specific Axiomata to specific Foundations. An Artificer could be just as capable with Skafoi as a Navigator. Just look at Henry Ford.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't Ford more an Edison, though? He didn't invent either the car or the assembly line, but rather commercialized the concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T09:18:47-07:00","id":1127164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1127133#post1127133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isn't Ford more an Edison, though? He didn't invent either the car or the assembly line, but rather commercialized the concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe so, but I was just trying to illustrate a point.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T09:48:11-07:00","id":1127178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1127164#post1127164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe so, but I was just trying to illustrate a point.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I understand. But in 1E's context, <i>all</i> Genii are artificers/engineers to some extent, simply due to Wonder creation.<br /> <br /> Additionally, Foundations have to draw the line somewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T15:36:08-07:00","id":1127370,"title":"","content":"In 1E the Foundations followed an academic/Mad Science trope to a T, so that's were the 'engineering' emphasis comes strongly even if they weren't Artificers. There's a lot more occupations and interests to apply the Mad Arts &amp; Sciences (and beyond) to, so broadening the Foundations a little bit more would be key. Which could be done with their initial Fields, perhaps a few Fellowships that have ties to the Foundations. At character creation the player selects the first most applicable Field for their Genius.<br /> <br /> For example, as a foil to a graffiti artist character in a game I run on Sundays I introduced a Neid Artificer with a bizarre take on color theory for a paradigm, if you will, and they've been butting heads ever since. The Genius, Spectra Heliotrope, does have an automated paint factory and some walking paint missiles, but she also insists she is an artist first, even with the chemical and gun running she does on the side.<br /> <br /> Taking another look at the 1.1 edition, here's some Field ideas for each of the Foundations. I trust others could come up with some more 'Inspired' titles for each. Obviously some could work across multiple Foundations.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Artificers</b></u><br /> The Union of Artifice is suggested to be a slurry of various interests, enthusiasts and rejects of all walks of life and clashing aesthetics, bound together by the common driving to create, create and create with numerous ideas each day.<br /> - Robotics<br /> - Engineering<br /> - Architecture and Construction<br /> - Computational Programming<br /> - Painting, sculpture and visual arts<br /> - Chemical proliferation and potioneering, alchemy<br /> - Toymaking<br /> - Smithing<br /> - Mechanics, Craftsmen and Tradespeople<br /> - Gadgetry<br /> <br /> <u><b>Directors</b></u><br /> The Fellowship of Manifest Direction (which needs a new title to separate from Fellowships, even if the 1E backstory wants to be cute) are the schemers and conspiracies that plot world domination and new governments alongside poaching each other's staff, conceptualizing new projects.<br /> - Psychology and hypnotism<br /> - Business and Economics<br /> - Ariguture<br /> - Performance arts<br /> - Cinematopgrapy<br /> - Political Science<br /> - Law and leagalese<br /> - Anthropology and sociology<br /> - Brand marketing<br /> - Social media<br /> - Intelligence networking, Espionage<br /> - Industrialization<br /> - Fashion<br /> - Occult rituals<br /> <br /> <u><b>Navigators</b></u><br /> The Center for Circumferential Navigation includes explorers and trailblazers, daredevils that would rather test their gear in the field than be coped up all day in the lab. They tend to survive the risks as they quickly discern how to improve Wonders at the testing phase.<br /> - Partical physics<br /> - Archeology and paleontology<br /> - Geography and geophysics<br /> - Astrophysics<br /> - Pan-Dimensional theory<br /> - Oceanic studies<br /> - Environmental science<br /> - Temporal distortion &amp; travel<br /> - Military tech<br /> - Paranormal debunking and documentation<br /> - Stunt performance<br /> - Field medic and warfare<br /> - Animal control<br /> - Law Enforcement<br /> - Kineticthesiology and sports science<br /> <br /> <u><b>Progenitors</b></u><br /> The Reformed Society of Progenitors contains transhumanists, demiurges and classical mad scientists keen on legacy as they improve upon generations of their wonders. They shape their lives and environments unlike any other, deeply passionate about having their projects exceed and continue where they can not.<br /> - Biology<br /> - Zoology &amp; veterinary science<br /> - Cybernetics and biometrics<br /> - Death and undertaking<br /> - Botany and landscaping<br /> - Medical sciences<br /> - Nutrition and culinary arts<br /> - Ecology<br /> - Cloning<br /> - Extraterristrial specices<br /> - Genetics and anatomy<br /> - Pharmacology and quackery<br /> - Necromancy<br /> - Diseases, viral and microbiology<br /> <br /> <u><b>Scholastics</b></u><br /> The College of Scholastic Theory does its best to document, label and rationalize everything unexplainable in Inspiration. By which most of the modern terminology has come from their lexicon but they are no more experts of the Mad Arts &amp; Sciences than the rest of them. Still, the collegiate tries to explain and understanding everything of new wonders and mysteries before hand, attempting to finding stability in the uncertainty of Inspiration.<br /> - Philosophy<br /> - Literary arts<br /> - Advanced mathematics<br /> - Journalism<br /> - Education<br /> - Taxonomy<br /> - Linguistics<br /> - Astronomy<br /> - Historical archeology<br /> - Cryptographers<br /> - Software development<br /> - Forensics<br /> - Lorekeepers<br /> - Music theory<br /> - Religio","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12284,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","user":"-metablender","date":". 08-10-2017, 06:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T16:27:44-07:00","id":1129010,"title":"","content":"Regarding Impetus, should the initial Attribute be changed to something other than Composure? I mean, Mad Scientists aren't really known for being in control of their emotions very well (who can resist a nice Mwahahahahaha!, after all?). Maybe Intelligence, or Resolve instead?<br /> <br /> And should Deep Inspiration really grant infinite Impetus, or merely large amounts? Going over could inflict the Lethal burnout penalty. Or just risk outright Illumination.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T11:06:13-07:00","id":1129304,"title":"","content":"In regards to Fields, perhaps another approach would be to fully embrace the broad nature of the concept and not clearly define what they are and simply have the player character simply gain a favored field of their choice or own creation from their Foundations. Instead of a concrete list of options there would be an example list of what popular choices are amongst the Foundation, so that way if a Artificer player reeeealy wants to buck type and chose Biology as their Field then that would be possible but also make them a black sheep to their own Foundation. Which, of course would lead to more drama and if successful a moment of supreme vindication when that Artificer creates a plant that grows ray-guns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Spellcheck 08-15-2017, 02:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T14:42:18-07:00","id":1129438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1129304#post1129304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In regards to Fields, perhaps another approach would be to fully embrace the broad nature of the concept and not clearly define what they are and simply have the player character simply gain a favored field of their choice or own creation from their Foundations. Instead of a concrete list of options there would be an example list of what popular choices are amongst the Foundation, so that way if a Artificer player reeeealy wants to buck type and chose Biology as their Field then that would be possible but also make them a black sheep to their own Foundation. Which, of course would lead to more drama and if successful a moment of supreme vindication when that Artificer creates a plant that grows ray-guns.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that was the idea. There'd be a few Fields that are more commonly known, but the sky isn't even the limit. You can have a Field, and it can be totally outside the stereotype of your Foundation. There are plenty of Bio-Engineer Artificers, Machinist Demiurges, and Meditative Navigators. 2E Foundations are divided philosophically, not by discipline.<ul><li><b>Artificers:</b> They are materialists that believe that <i>stuff</i> can make the society they want. They <i>make</i> things, like machines, organisms, software, etc. They are defined by a worldview that places the concrete and &quot;real&quot; over the abstract and theoretical.</li> <li><b>Directors:</b> They are manipulators and administrators that believe that social hierarchies are the best tool to make their Opus real. The <i>control</i> things, seeking to manipulate societies into what they want, or make a new society in their image. They are defined by a wordlview that places the power of society above the power of individuals over the long term.</li> <li><b>Navigators:</b> They are mavericks and men of action that believe that the Opus can come only by force of will. They prefer action over planning, and decisive action and aggression is more appealing than hedging, hemming and hawing. They are defined by a worldview that places individual greatness above the fears and rules placed by society.</li> <li><b>Progenitors:</b> They are the creators and teachers of the Peerage. They believe that the only way to change the world is to change the <i>people</i>. Whether it's by education or... more invasive means. They have a worldview defined by both humanism and <i>trans</i>-humanism, where people are the most important element.</li> <li><b>Scholastics:</b> They are the philsophers, theoreticians and &quot;idea guys.&quot; To a Scholastic, it's that ideas that change society. Machines and societies are great and all, but they were ideas first, and it's ideas that bring real change. They are defined by a worldview that places theory over practice, and emphasizes the power of knowledge.</li> </ul><br /> As a result, you could conceivably deal in any Field, and still be a part of any Foundation. It just depends on how you choose to apply yourself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T19:51:03-07:00","id":1129582,"title":"","content":"I like the way the Foundations are shaping up! Do we have any similar ideas for the Baramins? Are they like dark reflections of the Foundations, or do they have more separate philosophies?<br /> <br /> As a side note, are Inspired Manes and Orphan Wonders transforming into Genii still a thing? I really liked those, and I see no reason to remove them. It would be especially cool if you could play as them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T20:36:07-07:00","id":1129619,"title":"","content":"I figure they keep on being foils, but only the Peerage notices a lot of the time. It fits with how insular and hostile to outside influence Lemurians can be, to suffer repeated empathy failures with their archrivals.<br /> <br /> <b>Atomists:</b> Foils to the Artificers; they're what happens when an Artificer is <i>not </i>conflicted about progress, or assumes it is a good in-and-of-itself. Not only do they place the concrete over the abstract, they are <i>openly dismissive</i> of the idea of an abstract mattering. Their disconnect with humanity is that they never factor in the fact that people will be <i>using </i>their devices, or if so that they will simply learn as they go along.<br /> <br /> <b>Etherites: </b>Foils to the Navigators; they're the Great Man theory of history applied to the present. A lot of that is their universal pet Grand Unified Theories, but that's ultimately secondary to the idea that one man (and it's usually a man) can tame and understand the universe singlehandedly. Their disconnect is their tendency to see humanity as a bunch of bit players to a One-Genius(-And-His-Pals) Show.<br /> <br /> <b>Mechanists: </b>Foils to the Directors: all the focus on society, complete disregard for the components. It's not that they don't believe in free will, it's that they believe it to be a net negative in the hands of too many people. Their disconnect is obvious, not seeing the trees for the forest...and yet it's often subtle enough to the point where they have the highest amount of Paragons among them minus the Oracles, since they do care very deeply about human welfare, it's just that <i>how </i>they care tends to be horrific (see; Borg).<br /> <br /> <b>Oracles: </b>Foils to the Progenitors; coming from the opposite angle from most of their misanthropic peers, Oracles are outright human supremacists. They feel humanity is the <i>only </i>creature that matters in the long term, with certain stipulations for transhumans who &quot;retain their souls&quot;, whatever the hell that means for a particular Oracle. Their disconnect is with context; while they do have enough genuine compassion for mortals to frequently be Paragons (hence why Illuminated are not associated with Oracle &quot;crystal-tech&quot;; most Illuminated were never Oracles), it's all too frequent for them to exclude certain subgroups from the Humanity Club, and they do not consider the effects their works often have on the environment around them.<br /> <br /> <b>Phenomenologists: </b>Foils to Scholastics, they change the evidence to suit the theory. It's simple, but ironic; for a group that claims to be the embodiments of postmodern ideals, they sure like to cling to their pet theories of the mind in the face of all reasonable evidence. Their disconnect is always assuming the idea is objectively right, and if a person disagrees, they are an enemy to be convinced otherwise or destroyed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T21:58:04-07:00","id":1129670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1129619#post1129619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I figure they keep on being foils, but only the Peerage notices a lot of the time. It fits with how insular and hostile to outside influence Lemurians can be, to suffer repeated empathy failures with their archrivals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that sounds right. The Peerage are uncomfortably aware of how similar the Lemurians are to them, while the Lemurians look at the Peerage as poseurs, wimps and cowards.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Atomists:</b> Foils to the Artificers; they're what happens when an Artificer is <i>not </i>conflicted about progress, or assumes it is a good in-and-of-itself. Not only do they place the concrete over the abstract, they are <i>openly dismissive</i> of the idea of an abstract mattering. Their disconnect with humanity is that they never factor in the fact that people will be <i>using </i>their devices, or if so that they will simply learn as they go along. </div> </div> </div>Sounds good. Definitely the kind of people who would create Cybermen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Etherites: </b>Foils to the Navigators; they're the Great Man theory of history applied to the present. A lot of that is their universal pet Grand Unified Theories, but that's ultimately secondary to the idea that one man (and it's usually a man) can tame and understand the universe singlehandedly. Their disconnect is their tendency to see humanity as a bunch of bit players to a One-Genius(-And-His-Pals) Show. </div> </div> </div>Sounds like Rick Sanchez to me. I didn't think of Rick as Lemurian, but with that description, Rick would definitely fit there, considering his utter disregard for anyone's opinion but his own.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Mechanists: </b>Foils to the Directors: all the focus on society, complete disregard for the components. It's not that they don't believe in free will, it's that they believe it to be a net negative in the hands of too many people. Their disconnect is obvious, not seeing the trees for the forest...and yet it's often subtle enough to the point where they have the highest amount of Paragons among them minus the Oracles, since they do care very deeply about human welfare, it's just that <i>how </i>they care tends to be horrific (see; Borg). </div> </div> </div>No, wait, <i>these guys</i> would make Cybermen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Oracles: </b>Foils to the Progenitors; coming from the opposite angle from most of their misanthropic peers, Oracles are outright human supremacists. They feel humanity is the <i>only </i>creature that matters in the long term, with certain stipulations for transhumans who &quot;retain their souls&quot;, whatever the hell that means for a particular Oracle. Their disconnect is with context; while they do have enough genuine compassion for mortals to frequently be Paragons (hence why Illuminated are not associated with Oracle &quot;crystal-tech&quot;; most Illuminated were never Oracles), it's all too frequent for them to exclude certain subgroups from the Humanity Club, and they do not consider the effects their works often have on the environment around them. </div> </div> </div>And these are the guys who would build mutant-hunting Sentinels. These are people like Cerberus from Mass Effect, or Zarus if you want to make mildly obscure D&amp;D references.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Phenomenologists: </b>Foils to Scholastics, they change the evidence to suit the theory. It's simple, but ironic; for a group that claims to be the embodiments of postmodern ideals, they sure like to cling to their pet theories of the mind in the face of all reasonable evidence. Their disconnect is always assuming the idea is objectively right, and if a person disagrees, they are an enemy to be convinced otherwise or destroyed. </div> </div> </div>This is definitely the Scholastics gone wrong. Ideas at the expense of reality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T11:06:00-07:00","id":1129884,"title":"","content":"Are the Lemurians still strictly Unmada? Because the most horrifying things about the above mentioned Baramins is that rational people still choose to champion those concepts even to this day. Making it so that any Genii can shift to a Batamin regardless of how close they are to Unmada might be a fresh way to inject life into the Lemurians. <br /> <br /> In addition, has the in world reason for why the Baramins work together been flushed out yet for 2nd Edition. Because a pet theory of mine is that the Lemurians of each Baramin keep discovering ruins and technology of the &quot;Third Race&quot; that shows evidence that their Baramin was once a key scientific or philosophical cornerstone of the &quot;Third Race's&quot; society, and that this supposed united origin helps keep tensions from boiling over often amongst the Lemurians. For added effect, one could also put evidence of a great doom that came to lost Lemuria and that utilizing all of their scientific might the &quot;Third Race&quot; found a way to project their worldly consciousness across time and space. This theory postulated that the Lemurians of today are also the reincarnations of the &quot;Third Race&quot; and thus the true inheritors of the world. <br /> <br /> Again though, just some thoughts. Because man, that write up for the Baramins was really good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Polish 08-16-2017, 02:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T12:43:30-07:00","id":1129930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1129884#post1129884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are the Lemurians still strictly Unmada? Because the most horrifying things about the above mentioned Baramins is that rational people still choose to champion those concepts even to this day. Making it so that any Genii can shift to a Batamin regardless of how close they are to Unmada might be a fresh way to inject life into the Lemurians. <br /> <br /> In addition, has the in world reason for why the Baramins work together been flushed out yet for 2nd Edition. Because a pet theory of mine is that the Lemurians of each Baramin keep discovering ruins and technology of the &amp;quot;Third Race&amp;quot; that shows evidence that their Baramin was once a key scientific or philosophical cornerstone of the &amp;quot;Third Race's&amp;quot; society, and that this supposed united origin helps keep tensions from boiling over often amongst the Lemurians. For added effect, one could also put evidence of a great doom that came to lost Lemuria and that utilizing all of their scientific might the &amp;quot;Third Race&amp;quot; found a way to project their worldly consciousness across time and space. This theory postulated that the Lemurians of today are also the reincarnations of the &amp;quot;Third Race&amp;quot; and thus the true inheritors of the world. <br /> <br /> Again though, just some thoughts. Because man, that write up for the Baramins was really good.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought that we had said we were dropping that fairly early in this thread? Because I figure that &quot;all being Unmada&quot; was a pretty minor part of Lemurians anyway.<br /> <br /> I figure they're a lot more accepting of Unmada, but still recognize that going Unmada for too long can provoke Illumination. They treat it like nuclear power-dangerous, but very useful. <br /> <br /> Though, actually, if the Foundations still have full official titles, I figure the Baramins should too, that ties into their history and core ideas.<br /> <br /> For example, the Oracles' full name is the Enlightened Conclave of Pythian Oracles and Sybils. If we are still going by the idea that each Baramin crystalized around a disproven theory, their core maxim is that a world without concrete forces of good and evil is one fundamentally hostile to humanity, and thus they formed to ensure that the species did not lose faith in the face of an amoral universe. A most noble aspiration that also happens to be founded in extreme anthropocentricism and paranoia (many Oracles are fans of Lovecraft...and grow upset when people call out his xenophobia). They've drifted a bit, but their core is still a bunch of priests terrified of a world without easy answers to moral questions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T15:48:40-07:00","id":1130017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1129930#post1129930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought that we had said we were dropping that fairly early in this thread? Because I figure that &amp;quot;all being Unmada&amp;quot; was a pretty minor part of Lemurians anyway.<br /> <br /> I figure they're a lot more accepting of Unmada, but still recognize that going Unmada for too long can provoke Illumination. They treat it like nuclear power-dangerous, but very useful. <br /> <br /> Though, actually, if the Foundations still have full official titles, I figure the Baramins should too, that ties into their history and core ideas.<br /> <br /> For example, the Oracles' full name is the Enlightened Conclave of Pythian Oracles and Sybils. If we are still going by the idea that each Baramin crystalized around a disproven theory, their core maxim is that a world without concrete forces of good and evil is one fundamentally hostile to humanity, and thus they formed to ensure that the species did not lose faith in the face of an amoral universe. A most noble aspiration that also happens to be founded in extreme anthropocentricism and paranoia (many Oracles are fans of Lovecraft...and grow upset when people call out his xenophobia). They've drifted a bit, but their core is still a bunch of priests terrified of a world without easy answers to moral questions.</div> </div> </div> </div>^ That. So much that. <br /> <br /> That is a concept that I would happily build a character around. Damn fine work. Damn fine work everyone. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T17:04:17-07:00","id":1130051,"title":"","content":"<b>New Ephemeral: Achronals</b><br /> <br /> As any Genius skilled enough in the Axioms and well traveled knows, time is less an arrow, or even stream, and more like an ocean. Sure, everyone you can name is caught in the same current, but one can swim against the flow - or jump currents and depths.<br /> <br /> The entity type known generally as &quot;Achronals&quot; (named for their causal approach to linear time) are beings foreign not so much to this spatial dimension (though they can be as well), but are alien to this temporal epoch. Coming either from the far past, far future, a wildly divergent timeline, or some combination of the three, these being exist partially out of phase with the material universe. At least, initially. They often influence events to bring the relative &quot;present&quot; into resonant harmony with their own native environment, allowing them to manifest more fully in this time-space point.<br /> <br /> While some are simple cross-temporal tourist and scholars, curious about &quot;alien&quot; time-spaces, the Inspired have unfortunately found far more are more malicious (or perhaps simply negligent, as the common person is of the microbes upon their skin). Some of these beings crave resources plentiful in our time, but scarce-to-novel in their own, others are monsters locked out of coherent time by forces that may no longer exist, and more are stranger things besides. <hr /><br /> I don't have anything really new mechanics-wise yet, merely different interpretations on existing Ephemeral mechanics. Achronals exist &quot;out of phase&quot; with normal reality, occupying their own band of Twilight (showing up to Time Mage-Sight, for those curious).<br /> <br /> Their Resonant Condition is more aligned to &quot;moments&quot; that mirror something native or familiar to them. For travelers from the future, this may be when past events are more on track to lead to their eventual existence.<br /> <br /> When circumstances are strengthened (leading to the Open Condition), they can do the usual Materialize, etc. Manifestations. Your ersatz-Great-Old-Ones can even Possess and Claim, should they wish.<br /> <br /> Numina are things natural to the being (whether from allowable physics, or advanced technology), and Influences are those &quot;tweaks&quot; they can make to the time-stream from their own weird position in it (flavor-wise, they resemble more &quot;strange circumstance&quot; the kind of &quot;just so&quot; coincidences that Demonic Embeds are cable of - keyword: subtle).<br /> <br /> Essence, is whatever meta-justification they have for manipulating this temporal point to begin with (used for shenanigans, and if you drop it to 0, <i>then</i> destroy them, they are &quot;banished from local causality&quot;).<br /> <br /> The simplified Ephemeral Attributes are justified in that a sufficiently powerful Achronal doesn't really have recognizable Skills, and any Mental/Physical/Social tasks are more &quot;brute forced&quot; (They aren't smooth-talkers or understanding, so much as they can simulate your responses thousands of times, then pick the interaction that is most favorable to them).<br /> <br /> They probably have a Virtue and Vice (though strange ones), so they are more closely related to Ghosts and Goetia than Spirits, mechanics wise.<br /> <br /> Thoughts? I'll try to create an example or two to illustrate, when I have time. (heh) <br /> <br /> Stubs:<br /> Blue-and-Orange scholar from beyond.<br /> Creature from outside of time.<br /> Cold One emissary.<br /> Skynet.<br /> <hr /><br /> Oh, and I was also thinking about a more general &quot;Outsider/Beyonder&quot; Condition that can be applied to alien (be it from time, reality, or reason) entities. More of a tag to say &quot;this here does not belong&quot;. Resolution would, of course, lead to it no longer being &quot;here&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 08-17-2017, 11:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T22:29:43-07:00","id":1130148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1129884#post1129884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are the Lemurians still strictly Unmada? Because the most horrifying things about the above mentioned Baramins is that rational people still choose to champion those concepts even to this day. Making it so that any Genii can shift to a Batamin regardless of how close they are to Unmada might be a fresh way to inject life into the Lemurians.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you can be Unmada and a Paragon (which is a terrifying thought). All that's necessary is going into Deep Inspiration or Exceptionally Failing a Break toward Renegade. Lemurians are more prone to being Unmada, just because they willingly and pruposefully shut out other worldviews more than the Peerage. I don't think we need Lemurians to be Unmada automatically.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In addition, has the in world reason for why the Baramins work together been flushed out yet for 2nd Edition. Because a pet theory of mine is that the Lemurians of each Baramin keep discovering ruins and technology of the &quot;Third Race&quot; that shows evidence that their Baramin was once a key scientific or philosophical cornerstone of the &quot;Third Race's&quot; society, and that this supposed united origin helps keep tensions from boiling over often amongst the Lemurians. For added effect, one could also put evidence of a great doom that came to lost Lemuria and that utilizing all of their scientific might the &quot;Third Race&quot; found a way to project their worldly consciousness across time and space. This theory postulated that the Lemurians of today are also the reincarnations of the &quot;Third Race&quot; and thus the true inheritors of the world. </div> </div> </div>Well...The Baramins hold together for mostly practical reasons, much like the Peerage, but it's often more outwardly transactionary. With Lemurians, you're not among your peers, you're among your betters and your lessers. Powerful, influential Lemurians are in charge, usually disastrously, and new, younger, less important Lemurians are flunkies, interns and servants until they prove themselves, usually humiliating their masters in the process. They're the worst stereotypes of academia as arrogant, Ivory-Tower jerks that either don't care about life in the real world, or are actively hostile to the laity.<br /> <br /> In some chapters, Baramins are downright feudal, with a literal Science Lord. This is especially common among Etherites, where their &quot;Great Man&quot; philosophy easily morphs into the Divine Right of Kings.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again though, just some thoughts. Because man, that write up for the Baramins was really good. </div> </div> </div>Agreed. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar180_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"180\" data-vbnamecard=\"180\">Leliel</a> did a good job, and I'll definitely be using that stuff.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1130051#post1130051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>New Ephemeral: Achronals</b><br /> <br /> As any Genius skilled enough in the Axioms and well traveled knows, time is less an arrow, or even stream, and more like an ocean. Sure, everyone you can name is caught in the same current, but one can swim against the flow - or jump currents and depths.<br /> <br /> The entity type known generally as &quot;Achronals&quot; (named for their causal approach to linear time) are beings foreign not so much to this spatial dimension (though they can be as well), but are alien to this temporal epoch. Coming either from the far past, far future, a wildly divergent timeline, or some combination of the three, these being exist partially out of phase with the material universe. At least, initially. They often influence events to bring the relative &quot;present&quot; into resonant harmony with their own native environment, allowing them to manifest more fully in this time-space point.<br /> <br /> While some are simple cross-temporal tourist and scholars, curious about &quot;alien&quot; time-spaces, the Inspired have unfortunately found far more are more malicious (or perhaps simply negligent, as the common person is of the microbes upon their skin). Some of these beings crave resources plentiful in our time, but scarce-to-novel in their own, others are monsters locked out of coherent time by forces that may no longer exist, and more are stranger things besides.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is certainly an interesting idea. I could certainly see Achronals making for an interesting opponent for a time travel-related adventures. Sounds like the Cold Ones would fit as these. Very high-ranking ones that need something pretty nasty to show up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't have anything really new mechanics-wise yet, merely different interpretations on existing Ephemeral mechanics. Achronals exist &quot;out of phase&quot; with normal reality, occupying their own band of Twilight (showing up to Time Mage-Sight, for those curious). </div> </div> </div>Makes sense. It'd make it the first ephemeral to show up on a Mage's Sight for a Gross Arcanum.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Their Resonant Condition is more aligned to &quot;moments&quot; that mirror something native or familiar to them. For travelers from the future, this may be when past events are more on track to lead to their eventual existence.<br /> <br /> When circumstances are strengthened (leading to the Open Condition), they can do the usual Materialize, etc. Manifestations. Your ersatz-Great-Old-Ones can even Possess and Claim, should they wish. </div> </div> </div>We could do some neat stuff with this. Plenty of room for Event Horizon-style stuff.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Numina are things natural to the being (whether from allowable physics, or advanced technology), and Influences are those &quot;tweaks&quot; they can make to the time-stream from their own weird position in it (flavor-wise, they resemble more &quot;strange circumstance&quot; the kind of &quot;just so&quot; coincidences that Demonic Embeds are cable of - keyword: subtle). </div> </div> </div>Hm...That implies that there may be a connection between the God-Machine and Achronals. That's a neat thread to leave for players and STs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The simplified Ephemeral Attributes are justified in that a sufficiently powerful Achronal doesn't really have recognizable Skills, and any Mental/Physical/Social tasks are more &quot;brute forced&quot; (They aren't smooth-talkers or understanding, so much as they can simulate your responses thousands of times, then pick the interaction that is most favorable to them). </div> </div> </div>Or, they simply are too alien to have things that could be defined under a human understanding of &quot;skills.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They probably have a Virtue and Vice (though strange ones), so they are more closely related to Ghosts and Goetia than Spirits, mechanics wise. </div> </div> </div>Possibly. Maybe replace it with Purpose (what they're doing here) and Causation (The timeline they come from). Indulging their Purpose or protecting their Timeline gives them back Willpower, but messing with either can disrupt them. (preventing them from fulfilling their purpose in our time, or preventing their timeline from coming to be).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...when I have time. (heh) </div> </div> </div>Now see here!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oh, and I was also thinking about a more general &quot;Outsider/Beyonder&quot; Condition that can be applied to alien (be it from time, reality, or reason) entities. More of a tag to say &quot;this here does not belong&quot;. Resolution would, of course, lead to it no longer being &quot;here&quot;. </div> </div> </div>I don't know if we need a condition. Beyonders are really kind of Night Horror fodder. Theoretically, any kind of Horror could be a Beyonder with tweaking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":4488,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","user":"malonkey1","date":". 08-17-2017, 01:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T23:01:22-07:00","id":1130153,"title":"","content":"When I think Ivy League snots the first thing that comes to mind is sadly the entire Peerage. Could very well be a throwback to 1st Edition *shiver* but a lasting impression none the less (they do have the stones to call themselves the Peerage after all.)<br /> <br /> I would argue a better way to design the Lemurians is for them to be far more like a Cult of Personality. Rather than a Master/Student relationship it would be far more creepier to have a Master/Disciple approach to the Baramins. That way you can draw upon real world cult indoctrination methods for the Baramins, and you can play up the insular and isolationist nature of their beliefs since most cults already work very much like that. <br /> <br /> That's not to say you can't have masonic style leagues where the elite of the elite gather and explore the esoteric principles of reality at the expense of their lessers. Honestly it would be a crying shame not to. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T23:24:04-07:00","id":1130158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1130153#post1130153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I think Ivy League snots the first thing that comes to mind is sadly the entire Peerage. Could very well be a throwback to 1st Edition *shiver* but a lasting impression none the less (they do have the stones to call themselves the Peerage after all.)<br /> <br /> I would argue a better way to design the Lemurians is for them to be far more like a Cult of Personality. Rather than a Master/Student relationship it would be far more creepier to have a Master/Disciple approach to the Baramins. That way you can draw upon real world cult indoctrination methods for the Baramins, and you can play up the insular and isolationist nature of their beliefs since most cults already work very much like that.<br /> <br /> That's not to say you can't have masonic style leagues where the elite of the elite gather and explore the esoteric principles of reality at the expense of their lessers. Honestly it would be a crying shame not to. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the Peerage and Baramins are both really fractured in 2E, so it might really depend on the specific chapter and its history. And there's certainly Peerage who fit the Ivy League Snots mold, though the fact that Foundations are more ideological and less disciplinary now should serve to make that the exception, rather than the rule. The Peerage certainly has their own baggage to work out, and arrogance and runaway scientism certainly number among them. Baramins just tend to be worse in that regard because their ideals require a more explicit rejection of criticism, while the Peerage nominally welcomes open discussion, even as some voices try to manipulate the discussion in their favor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T09:16:01-07:00","id":1130304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1130148#post1130148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is certainly an interesting idea. I could certainly see Achronals making for an interesting opponent for a time travel-related adventures. Sounds like the Cold Ones would fit as these. Very high-ranking ones that need something pretty nasty to show up.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1130148#post1130148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or, they simply are too alien to have things that could be defined under a human understanding of &quot;skills.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically, yeah.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1130148#post1130148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Possibly. Maybe replace it with Purpose (what they're doing here) and Causation (The timeline they come from). Indulging their Purpose or protecting their Timeline gives them back Willpower, but messing with either can disrupt them. (preventing them from fulfilling their purpose in our time, or preventing their timeline from coming to be).</div> </div> </div> </div>That sound closer to Aspirations, really. No need to rebrand and invent new Anchors just because, I'd think.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1130148#post1130148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now see here!</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1130148#post1130148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if we need a condition. Beyonders are really kind of Night Horror fodder. Theoretically, any kind of Horror could be a Beyonder with tweaking.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, this was more &quot;Dimension-Hopping or Time-Traveling? This Condition is your Visa - keep it safe, because you <i>will</i> go home without it.&quot;. Just to serve as an umbrella tag for things out of place. Other effects can then simply key off the Condition, rather than specify what they do affect in text.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T19:30:39-07:00","id":1130652,"title":"","content":"Now that we have a pitch for Deviant, can I say that the obvious Crossover is a Lemurian figuring out how to make one? And then doing it again?<br /> <br /> I figure going Progenitor counts as using a Larvae, since you're literally cracking open some poor schmuck's soul and seeing what tumbles out. And that's a <i>willing </i>Deviant, abducting someone off the street is an automatic slide towards Renegade. On the plus side (for the Inspired) watching how the Deviant soul regulates its own internal Wonders without Havoc is probably grounds for a Thesis...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T23:23:29-07:00","id":1130731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1130652#post1130652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now that we have a pitch for Deviant, can I say that the obvious Crossover is a Lemurian figuring out how to make one? And then doing it again?<br /> <br /> I figure going Progenitor counts as using a Larvae, since you're literally cracking open some poor schmuck's soul and seeing what tumbles out. And that's a <i>willing </i>Deviant, abducting someone off the street is an automatic slide towards Renegade. On the plus side (for the Inspired) watching how the Deviant soul regulates its own internal Wonders without Havoc is probably grounds for a Thesis...</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, definitely. Deviant/Genius interaction may be enough to warrant its own supplement down the line. There is a lot of stuff that can go on between them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T03:22:26-07:00","id":1130758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1130158#post1130158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, the Peerage and Baramins are both really fractured in 2E, so it might really depend on the specific chapter and its history. And there's certainly Peerage who fit the Ivy League Snots mold, though the fact that Foundations are more ideological and less disciplinary now should serve to make that the exception, rather than the rule. The Peerage certainly has their own baggage to work out, and arrogance and runaway scientism certainly number among them. Baramins just tend to be worse in that regard because their ideals require a more explicit rejection of criticism, while the Peerage nominally welcomes open discussion, even as some voices try to manipulate the discussion in their favor.</div> </div> </div> </div>That actually gives me a great idea. I don't know how much of the origins for Lemuria you're keeping, but a wonderful alternate origin that's more grounded in reality (or at least compared to the original) might be a great way to explain the similarities between the Foundations and Baramin. And that being: The Peerage and Lemuria were once the same organization. <br /> <br /> During the height of colonialism the Genii found themselves more interconnected than ever before. With the colonial powers at the time strongly supporting academia and the growth of scientific exploration, the most wealthy and prominent Genii of their fields gather together and formed the first &quot;official&quot; Inspired Institution. Taking inspiration from scientific and spiritual movements of the age, specifically Theosophy since it resonated with many Western Inspired beliefs, the institution named itself &quot;The Theosophic Foundation for the Enlightened Sciences.&quot; <br /> <br /> The organization's goals was to use colonialism as a vector to spread their theories and practices across the world, helping civilization progress towards a enlightened utopia free of sickness, poverty, and barbarism. What actually happened was that the Genii of the time got into bed with the rich and elite, reinforcing philosophies that legitimized the aristocracy's dreams of conquest and empire in exchange for a measure of wealth and influence that very few Inspired could ever hope to acquire on their own. This is where the belief of Inspired Masters carefully paving the way for an enlightened society stems from, where the common masses were better off following the ambitions and vision of great men and women of science (with the expected level of misogyny thrown in of course.) Some even bought into this rhetoric, taking command of the future for the betterment of all. That was, until the War To End All Wars.<br /> <br /> With World War I came not just the destruction of the Aristocracy as the Genii knew it, but also the end to the belief that society and progress could solely be a positive force. The Foundation watched as their theories and inventions were turned into weapons so horrible that they changed the very nature of war itself. Philosophers and Theologians alike were left wondering if there was a God, and if so how could it be a just and loving being to allow such death and destruction. For all it's idealism the Foundation fractured as the world took a collective sign and began treating it's wounds, and in this fracture the Peerage and Lemurians as we know them were born. <br /> <br /> Those who saw the Genii's hand in the war, not as architects or fire starters but as enablers and sycophants, tried to bring the organization back to it's roots. They banded together with those who had similar scholastic interests and returned to experimentation and theory rather than trying to directly influence society. They all took different names, but collectively referred to themselves as the Foundations (after the original experiment and it's intended purpose.) <br /> <br /> The other side saw the war as a call to arms, that not enough was done on the Genii's part to prevent the Uninspired from nearly bringing an end to civilization. The loss of their power base and the drastic changes that occurred after the war seemed like the Genii had lost something irreplaceable, and that if nothing was done soon then the Uninspired would continue to plunge the world into chaos. The image of Lemuria, the lost civilization of the Third Race, became an icon amongst these Genii. It became an icon of the end of a glorious era, and the hope that such glory and bounty could be restored. It became a warning to the dangers of the Uninspired, and why the Genii must protect humanity from both themselves and the horrors that lurk beyond sight. Like the nascent Foundations these Baramins (a term that might have been used originally to designate a Genii's field of expertise in the past due to it's pseudoscientific Christian roots) gathered together like minded Inspired and galvanized them toward the cause of saving the known world. <br /> <br /> And the rest is history, although in a world with time travel and alternate dimensions such a story may be entirely fabricated. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Spellcheck 08-18-2017, 06:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T08:37:03-07:00","id":1130833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1130758#post1130758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That actually gives me a great idea. I don't know how much of the origins for Lemuria you're keeping, but a wonderful alternate origin that's more grounded in reality (or at 