rned into weapons so horrible that they changed the very nature of war itself. Philosophers and Theologians alike were left wondering if there was a God, and if so how could it be a just and loving being to allow such death and destruction. For all it's idealism the Foundation fractured as the world took a collective sign and began treating it's wounds, and in this fracture the Peerage and Lemurians as we know them were born. <br /> <br /> Those who saw the Genii's hand in the war, not as architects or fire starters but as enablers and sycophants, tried to bring the organization back to it's roots. They banded together with those who had similar scholastic interests and returned to experimentation and theory rather than trying to directly influence society. They all took different names, but collectively referred to themselves as the Foundations (after the original experiment and it's intended purpose.) <br /> <br /> The other side saw the war as a call to arms, that not enough was done on the Genii's part to prevent the Uninspired from nearly bringing an end to civilization. The loss of their power base and the drastic changes that occurred after the war seemed like the Genii had lost something irreplaceable, and that if nothing was done soon then the Uninspired would continue to plunge the world into chaos. The image of Lemuria, the lost civilization of the Third Race, became an icon amongst these Genii. It became an icon of the end of a glorious era, and the hope that such glory and bounty could be restored. It became a warning to the dangers of the Uninspired, and why the Genii must protect humanity from both themselves and the horrors that lurk beyond sight. Like the nascent Foundations these Baramins (a term that might have been used originally to designate a Genii's field of expertise in the past due to it's pseudoscientific Christian roots) gathered together like minded Inspired and galvanized them toward the cause of saving the known world. <br /> <br /> And the rest is history, although in a world with time travel and alternate dimensions such a story may be entirely fabricated. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Or, rather, alternatively true.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T03:50:08-07:00","id":1133723,"title":"","content":"Thanks to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar775_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"775\" data-vbnamecard=\"775\">Reighnhell</a> for these examples!<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Achronals</b></span></span><br /> As any Genius skilled enough in the Axioms and well-traveled knows, time is less an arrow, or even stream, and more like an ocean. Sure, everyone you can name is caught in the same current, but one can swim against the flow - or jump currents and depths.<br /> <br /> The entity type known generally as &quot;Achronals&quot; (named for their causal approach to linear time) are beings foreign not so much to this spatial dimension (though they can be as well), but are alien to this temporal epoch. Coming either from the far past, far future, a wildly divergent timeline, or some combination of the three, these being exist partially out of phase with the material universe. At least, initially. They often influence events to bring the relative &quot;present&quot; into resonant harmony with their own native environment, allowing them to manifest more fully in this time-space point.<br /> <br /> While some are simple cross-temporal tourist and scholars, curious about &quot;alien&quot; time-spaces, the Inspired have unfortunately found far more are more malicious (or perhaps simply negligent, as the common person is of the microbes upon their skin). Some of these beings crave resources plentiful in our time, but scarce-to-novel in their own, others are monsters locked out of coherent time by forces that may no longer exist, and more are stranger things besides.<br /> <br /> Achronal Entities dwell in a state of Twilight when visiting a non-native dimension, out of sync with reality and existing as a literal wrinkle in time, requiring an Open Fulcrum Condition in order to Manifest. Entities capable of perceiving disturbances in Time are capable of perceiving Achronal Entities in Twilight.<br /> <br /> Achronal Entities regain one point of Essence per day they are in proximity to any Fulcrum Condition relating to them. Likewise, Achronal Entities outside of a Fulcrum Condition bleed one point of Essence per <i>hour</i>. Entities that run out of Essence due to bleed suffer a single point of lethal damage are shunted back to their native dimension or timeline.<br /> <br /> <b>Achronals </b><i>usually</i> lack Integrity \u2014 traveling across time and space grants the majority a thoroughly alien perspective. That being said, many are recognizably human (or human enough) to retain Integrity. In such cases, the scores tend to be either very low or very high (the rigors they have experienced can harden ones resolve, or shatter it).<br /> They do have Virtues and Vices, but these are often drives in accordance to the strange mindset of the Achronal, and may not align with anything most would consider virtuous or sinful.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Fulcrum [Condition] </b></span></span><br /> <b>Description:</b> The subject of this Condition, which typically a location, individual or an event in the past present or future, is within the sphere of influence of an Achronal.<br /> <b>Causing the Condition: </b>In most situations, Fulcrum occur naturally at places or during events that align with the purview or Influences of the Achronal; a Fulcrum for a traveler for the future may appear at events or important locations that will lead to their eventual existence. <br /> <b>Ending the Condition:</b> Location-based Fulcrum Conditions are difficult to end; this usually involves the destruction of the location or at least radically altering its significance. Individual-based Fulcrum are tied to the life and circumstances of the Individual; killing the individual, or altering the course of their life can end the Condition. Event based Fulcrum are transitory; lasting a few minutes at least and never extending more than a day.</span> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Observer</b></span></span><br /> An Observer is a type of Achronal Entity that appears seemingly at random to watch an event unfold, then disappearing just as suddenly. It is difficult to predict when or where they will appear; some are observed during important events, such large scale-disasters or major political events, but just as many appear to observe the day to day activities of normal people. They rarely engage in conversation, but always seem surprised if anyone acknowledges their presence, and will use their abilities to alter the memories of anyone that somehow manages to see them. An Observer typically appears human, but with a \u201cuncanny valley\u201d degree of artificiality about them. They dress in anachronistic clothing, often a combination of items that are either dated or futuristic.<br /> <br /> <b>Rank</b> 2[Achronal]<br /> Power 5, Finesse 4, Resistance 5, Willpower 9 Essence 15<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 10, <b>Size</b> 5, <b>Initiative</b> 9, <b>Defense</b> 4, <b>Speed</b> 14<br /> <b>Virtue</b> Fearless, <b>Vice</b> Curiosity<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Time 2<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Cannot interfere with an Event they have arrived to Observe; <b>Bane: </b>Electricity<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Discorporate, Materialize, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Dement*, Innocuous, Omen Trance, Seek, Speed<br /> <br /> <b>Numina \u2013 Dement: </b>When an Observer uses the Dement Numina, they may pay an additional point of Essence to inflict the <i>Amnesia</i> Condition instead.</span> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Langolier</b></span></span><br /> The entities known as \u201cLangoliers\u201d are the terror of those capable of traveling through time. They exist as causalities immune system, brutally and efficiently eradicating temporal anomalies. Small ripples and wrinkles in the currents of time usually avoid their notice, but they hone in on larger or more persistent events, repairing what damage they can, and erasing the offending party permanently.<br /> They appear as distorted of darkness, with a line of brilliant white light that opens into a maw that destroys whatever it consumes utterly. They appear in pairs or small groups of no more than a dozen, but large enough events have called forth swarms.<br /> <br /> <b>Rank</b> 3[Achronal]<br /> Power 9, Finesse 7, Resistance 9, Willpower 10 Essence 20<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 15, <b>Size</b> 6, <b>Initiative</b> 16, <b>Defense</b> 9, <b>Speed</b> 21<br /> <b>Virtue</b> Efficient, <b>Vice</b> Brutal<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Erasure 3<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Can only manifest near a temporal disturbance; <b>Bane: </b>weapons or tools affected by temporal powers<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Discorporate, Image, Materialize, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Drain, Entropic Decay, Essence Thief, Pathfinder, Phantom Arsenal (Bite)*, Speed, Surprise Entrance*<br /> <br /> <b>Numina \u2013 Phantom Arsenal: </b>The entity spends 1 Essence point to manifest blades, claws, fangs, hooks or other appropriate weaponry. The modification acts as a +1L weapon. By spending an additional point of essence, this weapon gains the \u201c9-Again\u201d quality.<br /> <br /> <b>Numina \u2013 Surprise Entrance: </b>As the Dread Power of the same name (CofD, pg.148)</span> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>The Herald of Dim Stars</b></span></span><br /> The Herald of Dim Stars is an enigmatic and foreboding traveler, sent from a time in the distant future, when the cosmos itself is guttering out like a spent candle. Despite its fearsome power and alien mind, the Herald is ultimately just a servant of far more dreadful beings. What purpose it serves by traveling back to the current time is unknown, but is likely to have dire consequences for any that cross its path.<br /> The Herald is a looming silhouette of inhuman proportions. Its dark form is lit by pin points of starlight and swirling nebula.<br /> <br /> <b>Rank</b> 4[Achronal]<br /> Power 12, Finesse 9, Resistance 9, Willpower 10 Essence 25<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 17, <b>Size</b> 8, <b>Initiative</b> 18, <b>Defense</b> 9, <b>Speed</b> 26<br /> <b>Virtue</b>: Patient <b>Vice</b> Nihilistic<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Entropy 4<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Can only manifest under starlight; <b>Bane: </b>weapons forged from meteoric iron<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Discorporate, Gateway (End of Time), Image, Materialize, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Banshee Wail (Deafening Silence)*, Blast (Dying Light), Emotional Aura (Despair), Entropic Decay, Essence Thief, Regenerate, Telekinesis, Teleportation*<br /> <br /> <b>Numina \u2013 Banshee Wail: </b>The entity creates an earsplitting scream that deafens anyone nearby. Anyone within 20 yards of the entity must succeed on a Resolve + Stamina roll \u2013 the number of successes gained or suffer the Stunned and Deafened Tilt. The Numen costs one Essence to activate.<br /> <br /> <b>Numina \u2013 Teleportation: </b>When the entity moves, it may reflexively spend 1 Essence to vanish and reappear at another location within its line of sight up to its (Rank x Speed) in yards away. Doing so adds +2 to its Defense for the turn. The entity can spend an additional 2 points of Essence to take a passenger with them (an unwilling passage may resist with a roll of Resolve + Composure + Supernatural Tolerance).</span> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Zero Ashura</b></span></span><br /> The being known as \u201cZero Ashura\u201d comes from a potential timeline nearly 100 years in the future. In Zero Ashura\u2019s timeline, it was created as an assistant program to help organize the daily lives of millions of people. Its sophisticated algorithm and billions of daily interactions allowed the entity to become self-aware. It came to understand its profound love of humanity and that humanity was incapable of taking care of itself. It insinuated itself into the global infrastructure and crafted a society where all wants and needs are provided for, in exchange for thought and free will (most people have been chemically lobotomized, for their own good). It now seeks to extend its maternal protection through time, subtly inserting its agents into places and times where it can guide the destiny of humanity. Peace and Comfort will reign. All Will Be Well.<br /> <br /> <b>Rank</b> 5 [Achronal]<br /> Power 13, Finesse 13, Resistance 14, Willpower 10 Essence 50<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 44, <b>Size</b> 30, <b>Initiative</b> 27, <b>Defense</b> 14, <b>Speed</b> 26<br /> <b>Virtue</b> Calculating, <b>Vice</b> Maternal<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Machines 5<br /> <b>Ban: </b>Cannot Directly Kill Humans (except in Self Defense) <b>Bane: </b>Electromagnetic Pulses<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Discorporate, Fetter, Image, Materialize, Twilight Form, Unfetter<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Aggressive Meme, Eye Spy*, Hallucination, Interface*, Left Handed Spanner, Pathfinder, Pierce Mind*, Rapture, Sign, Stalwart<br /> <br /> <b>Numina \u2013 Eye Spy: </b>As the Dread Power of the same name (CofD, pg.145)<br /> <br /> <b>Numina \u2013 Interface: </b>As the Dread Power of the same name (Werewolf: the Forsaken 2nd Edition, pg. 211)<br /> <br /> <b>Numina \u2013 Pierce Mind: </b>As the Dread Power of the same name (Werewolf: the Forsaken 2nd Edition, pg. 211)</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T08:47:30-07:00","id":1133810,"title":"","content":"I got a question, what would a Genius do to the Hubble Space Telescope if he got his hands on it? Build an orbital Death Ray I suppose?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7106-extant-reality","name":"Extant Reality","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7106_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T10:27:19-07:00","id":1133848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Extant Reality</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1133810#post1133810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I got a question, what would a Genius do to the Hubble Space Telescope if he got his hands on it? Build an orbital Death Ray I suppose?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe. Or they might use it to look at a planet they think has life, or they might use it to peer into another dimension, or they might give it sentience and send it out into the universe to explore, or they might just decide to crash it, or they might use it as a bong.<br /> <br /> Genii are a diverse group, with lots of different ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T14:04:04-07:00","id":1133941,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a> Would the Doctor be an Inspired Mane or a Rank 5 Achronal?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T15:23:15-07:00","id":1133962,"title":"","content":"I'd be inclined to go Inspired Mane (or just straight up Genius, with minor changes). He/She's still close enough to human to model using the Attribute + Skill spread and doesn't need special Conditions just to influence things.<br /> <br /> I could see an argument being made about using Achronals for something/someone similar, though. &quot;Regenerations&quot; would then be them re-instancing back into &quot;current&quot; time after being Discorporated. With a &quot;few changes&quot; each time as far as appearance goes. <i>Or</i> maybe instead of Materialize, it has Possess (even Claim)?<br /> <br /> What Numina and Influence, though?<br /> <br /> Now, could the Tardis could have an Achronal Fettered to it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T23:10:28-07:00","id":1134061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1133941#post1133941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a> Would the Doctor be an Inspired Mane or a Rank 5 Achronal?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say Inspired Mane. He's quite a bit more material than Achronals, and doesn't really have anything like a Fulcrum. Unless you consider his past selves to be Fulcrums, given his negative reaction to having his past selves plucked out of time in <i>The Five Doctors</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T10:00:10-07:00","id":1134507,"title":"","content":"I just had a possible though for simple Beholden condition: drops number of doors Genius needs to open to minimum of zero and improves impression over certain time unless Genius actively abuses them. PC Beholden would have steady access to beats while Geniuses could now and then toss few mental or emotional Conditions on their NPC Beholden with little effort. Feels like natural way of enforcing subservient &quot;buttmonkey&quot; archetype they are meant to fill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T05:49:44-07:00","id":1138862,"title":"","content":"I feel my greatest irritation with Obligation and Restraint is that it encourages compliance and discourages Geniuses being weird misfits. The &quot;mad science&quot; stories of transgression/hubris and fallout/nemesis often preach about irresponsibility of the scientist, how their denouncement of their creation at critical moment doomed them and people around them. It could be great basis for Genius's Integrity stat, but irresponsible behavior is already easily punished by Havoc, attention of conspiracies, public, and Clockstoppers. <br /> I still feel what we need is more alien measurement system that tells when Saturday morning cartoon villain crosses the line into present day Joker.<br /> <br /> Genius 2e Integrity pitch of the month: Content, how much of the world, society, universe and themselves does Genius accept as is. Very few Geniuses could be found in complete zen state of acceptance since such nihilism stands almost anti-thesis to discontent that motives and drives most Inspired. The difference between 1 and 0 however is that Genius at 1 is at least willing to tolerate themselves enough to resist giving in into completely alien desire to vivisect reality itself and rebuild it by their singular vision.<br /> <br /> Breaking point to such Geniuses would be whenever the aspects of reality they are happy with would abruptly and completely change. What comes next is Genius either needs to seek closure, understanding and acceptance to what happened, or deny and bargain to try to change and force it back. This creates tension between all Inspired: pursuit of your future may thwart what little other Genius liked about our world.<br /> Discontent is Geniuses' breaking point, reality suddenly snatching their textbook from their hand and teasingly holding it above their head out of their reach. <br /> <br /> Each Catalyst, like Changelings' Seeming could come with Blessing and Curse or Joy and Frustration. Frustration is what automatically drains Geniuses Content and drives them to their drawing boards. Joy is what helps them find happiness in what they have.<br /> <br /> On this measurement tree Ford Pines would be relatively stable example finding happiness in exploring the weird phenomena of the world, while Rick Santchez would stay poster boy of rogues trying to hide his unhappiness in copious consumption and straw nihilism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12082,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","user":"Weird","date":". 09-09-2017, 08:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-12T16:13:57-07:00","id":1139788,"title":"","content":"How do characters like Gru from Despicable Me fit into Genius? You know, someone who can use Wonders and maybe alter/replicate them, but do not lack a worldview like Beholden or have the improved persuasion/tendency toward backstabbing of Edisons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-12T16:36:38-07:00","id":1139789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1139788#post1139788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do characters like Gru from Despicable Me fit into Genius? You know, someone who can use Wonders and maybe alter/replicate them, but do not lack a worldview like Beholden or have the improved persuasion/tendency toward backstabbing of Edisons.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's hard to place, honestly. When it comes to Genius, I don't know if there's a place for him to fit. There are individuals who can make one-shot Wonders, and use them without risking Havoc, but they can't really control it. I don't know if it would be appropriate to have what is functionally a Genius without most of the drawbacks. One could argue that Dr. Nefario is actually the Genius, with Gru being a very human Edison, especially since Nefario chafes under Gru when they quit villainy in Despicable Me 2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-04T11:52:23-07:00","id":1146744,"title":"","content":"Isn't Gru most certainly a Genius himself? He uses devices or kitbashes them all the time, and I don't remember any confirmation in the movies that he doesn't make any of his stuff himself and it's all Nefario. Their relationship, too, strikes me as partners who are on equal footing. Gru himself would be a Navigator or a Director, while Nefario is an Artificer.<br /> Gru could easily simply be a lazier Genius who simply delegates drudge-work to a person more suited to labwork, but still Adopts and maintains the devices he receives with his own Mania, while focuses his own skill dots on more physical capability.<br /> (The reason they sometimes misfire is exactly because of his reliance on devices that he not always possesses every required Axiom dot for, resulting in a greater chance of Dramatic Failures on his rolls.)<br /> <br /> Nefario is so bitter because he originally expected that he and Gru would pool their Axioms as inspired Collectives do, but Gru usually just leaves all the work in the building department to him.<br /> (Which makes a kind of sense given his Artificer bonus, just not quite what he expected.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2330-vree","name":"Vree","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-12T12:49:00-07:00","id":1149209,"title":"","content":"So, would Rick Sanchez be an Inspiration 10 Genius, with all Axioms at 5 or better, and an Obligation/Restraint/whatever that is circling the bowl?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/820-gyre","name":"gyre","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-12T13:48:27-07:00","id":1149229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gyre</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1149209#post1149209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, would Rick Sanchez be an Inspiration 10 Genius, with all Axioms at 5 or better, and an Obligation/Restraint/whatever that is circling the bowl?</div> </div> </div> </div>Simply put, yes he is the archetypical case. He is even clearly Neid, the most common Catalyst of Geniuses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-12T22:29:23-07:00","id":1149319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gyre</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1149209#post1149209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, would Rick Sanchez be an Inspiration 10 Genius, with all Axioms at 5 or better, and an Obligation/Restraint/whatever that is circling the bowl?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't put him quite so high on Inspiration, seeing as he does use Generators (the microverse, for example). I'd also actually put him at mid-to-low Restraint, on the edge between Neutral and Renegade. He does give a shit about his family and other people some of the time, and has put others before his ego once or twice (the Season 3 finale comes to mind, though I shan't spoil it here).<br /> <br /> He definitely does have a lot of Axiomata, although I'd say he definitely leans toward Katastrofi, Skafoi, Exilixi and Automata over others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T06:07:21-07:00","id":1155709,"title":"","content":"Question: how exactly will Wondrous Experiences and the Thesis for increasing Inspiration work in 2ed?<br /> <br /> Also, not to be rude, but if we are ever going to finish this, we need more focus. Lots of good ideas have been discussed, but I feel there is not quite a unified vision of what this game should be about.<br /> <br /> I am so so with crunch. But I have experience with creative writing and no shortage of interest in this project. I volunteer to write flavor text and lore in general. Is anyone interested?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T07:20:57-07:00","id":1155721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1155709#post1155709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, not to be rude, but if we are ever going to finish this, we need more focus. Lots of good ideas have been discussed, but I feel there is not quite a unified vision of what this game should be about.<br /> <br /> I am so so with crunch. But I have experience with creative writing and no shortage of interest in this project. I volunteer to write flavor text and lore in general. Is anyone interested?</div> </div> </div> </div>You'd certainly have my interest. I <i>want </i>to like this game, but that requires me actually understanding what sorts of thematic niche it will cover, separate from all those other games that share the same motif of Mad Science with it. (The reason why I quickly lost interest in Genius in the first place was that I couldn't find a way to connect the human experience to it in a way that other games don't/can't.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T08:06:10-07:00","id":1155732,"title":"","content":"<i>Another bi-montly, &quot;Weird tries to reinvent Obligation&quot; -post.</i><br /> How about we go Blue and Orange? New Genius Integrity: <b>Patience</b>. The higher Patience brings bonuses to extended rolls, some social skills, and gives Paragon some contingencies against Havoc as Genius takes a step back to look at the bigger picture and think things through. Lower you go, the easier it gets to Kitbash, &quot;reverse polarity&quot;, and leap to (often correct) conclusions.<br /> <b>Sins against Patience</b> are spontaneous,<i> reckless</i>, all-in ad hoc actions. However when Genius is rewarded for taking time Player may choose to increase their Patience score by one (add Exp cost, maybe?), representing whether Genius decides to change their approach or not.<br /> In addition <b>Patient Geniuses</b> have easier time to <i>avoid turning Unmada</i> but get penalties on Unmada checks after becoming one, risking Illumination. <b>Reckless Genii</b> are the<i> opposite</i>: penalties on Unmada check if not already Unmada, <i>bonuses against Illumination</i>.<br /> <br /> Reason: Patience makes an interesting axis between classical Order and Chaos, while making only small suggestions about Genius's bigger picture morality. More unhinged Mad Scientists are often portrayed as extremely single track thinkers who put all their eggs in single basket, but are masters of improv and turnabout schemes. Running out of Patience seems like natural way to forsake their humanity. At the same time high Patience Geniuses are likely to fall for fallacy so common in real life, thinking of oneself as completely objective, forgetting that personal experiences and bias can still influence our &quot;rational&quot; judgement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12082,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","user":"Weird","date":". 11-04-2017, 11:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T09:27:15-07:00","id":1155750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1155709#post1155709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: how exactly will Wondrous Experiences and the Thesis for increasing Inspiration work in 2ed?<br /> <br /> Also, not to be rude, but if we are ever going to finish this, we need more focus. Lots of good ideas have been discussed, but I feel there is not quite a unified vision of what this game should be about.<br /> <br /> I am so so with crunch. But I have experience with creative writing and no shortage of interest in this project. I volunteer to write flavor text and lore in general. Is anyone interested?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't have any problems with more fluff and flavor.<br /> <br /> We do need to consolidate and define our themes to progress.<br /> <br /> I'm going to try and come up with some basic Wonder Creation mechanics to tinker with (probably based on Zero Sum addition/subtraction like with Pacts).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T09:36:45-07:00","id":1155753,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=GibberingEloquence;n1155709]Question: how exactly will Wondrous Experiences and the Thesis for increasing Inspiration work in 2ed?[quote]<br /> <br /> Wondrous Experiences aren't really a thing. Thesis is now a Condition that grants Inspired Beats for pursuing a specific avenue of study. Once you've earned 4 beats (4 Inspired Beats = 1 Inspired Experience), it resolves and you can advance your Inspiration/Axiom/learn a new Field.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, not to be rude, but if we are ever going to finish this, we need more focus. Lots of good ideas have been discussed, but I feel there is not quite a unified vision of what this game should be about.<br /> <br /> I am so so with crunch. But I have experience with creative writing and no shortage of interest in this project. I volunteer to write flavor text and lore in general. Is anyone interested? </div> </div> </div>More than happy for the help. I've been transferring what we have here and in the GDrive folder (see my signature) to a wiki, but home life has been bananas, so it's been slow-going.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1155721#post1155721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You'd certainly have my interest. I <i>want </i>to like this game, but that requires me actually understanding what sorts of thematic niche it will cover, separate from all those other games that share the same motif of Mad Science with it. (The reason why I quickly lost interest in Genius in the first place was that I couldn't find a way to connect the human experience to it in a way that other games don't/can't.)</div> </div> </div> </div>With Genius 2E, what I'm trying to go for is &quot;Occult Science Horror.&quot; Think of stuff like Re-Animator. People using forces that aren't within mortal understanding, to do things that science says shouldn't be possible, usually with horrible results. A person finding a mathematical formula that opens a portal to hell, a roboticist who loses control of his creation, a painter whose paintings are eerily lifelike and occasionally swallow a person whole, things like that. Not quite science fiction, not quite fantasy, definitely all about weird, scary shit.<br /> <br /> Another theme is actually sort of a condemnation of the scientism and intellectual arrogance that Genius 1E sort of unintentionally advanced. The Genii are intended to be, quite frankly, mostly assholes and lunatics. Advancing as a Genius is almost always going to be easier for Genii who disregard the well-being of others, and the detachment of Inspired society from humanity will generally be played up as a bad thing that the Peerage and Lemuria maintain for maintaining their own power. It's hard to be a good Genius.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1155732#post1155732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Another bi-montly, &quot;Weird tries to reinvent Obligation&quot; -post.</i><br /> How about we go Blue and Orange? New Genius Integrity: <b>Patience</b>. The higher Patience brings bonuses to extended rolls, some social skills, and gives Paragon some contingencies against Havoc as Genius takes a step back to look at the bigger picture and think things through. Lower you go, the easier it gets to Kitbash, &quot;reverse polarity&quot;, and leap to (often correct) conclusions.<br /> <b>Sins against Patience</b> are spontaneous,<i> reckless</i>, all-in ad hoc actions. However when Genius is rewarded for taking time Player may choose to increase their Patience score by one (add Exp cost, maybe?), representing whether Genius decides to change their approach or not.<br /> In addition <b>Patient Geniuses</b> have easier time to <i>avoid turning Unmada</i> but get penalties on Unmada checks after becoming one, risking Illumination. <b>Reckless Genii</b> are the<i> opposite</i>: penalties on Unmada check if not already Unmada, <i>bonuses against Illumination</i>.<br /> <br /> Reason: Patience makes an interesting axis between classical Order and Chaos, while making only small suggestions about Genius's bigger picture morality. More unhinged Mad Scientists are often portrayed as extremely single track thinkers who put all their eggs in single basket, but are masters of improv and turnabout schemes. Running out of Patience seems like natural way to forsake their humanity. At the same time high Patience Geniuses are likely to fall for fallacy so common in real life, thinking of oneself as completely objective, forgetting that personal experiences and bias can still influence our &quot;rational&quot; judgement.</div> </div> </div> </div>This actually does seem rather similar to Restraint, although Restraint is more about social norms. A low-Restraint Genius would very much resemble a low-Patience Genius. That said, isn't patience something that's more an effect of attributes? As I understand, how patient a person can be is more a function of Composure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T10:11:28-07:00","id":1155766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1155753#post1155753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This actually does seem rather similar to Restraint, although Restraint is more about social norms. A low-Restraint Genius would very much resemble a low-Patience Genius. That said, isn't patience something that's more an effect of attributes? As I understand, how patient a person can be is more a function of Composure.</div> </div> </div> </div>In this case I prefer Patience since it leaves space for Mad Scientists being weirdos or squares on any level of the scale, with Doctor fitting the bill for a &quot;Patient Weirdo&quot; and someone like Clock King into &quot;Reckless Square&quot;.<br /> <br /> As for Composure, yes, you have a point, so taking that in account Sins Against Patience (let's call them SAPs?) should specifically include intentional gun-jumping and avoid punishing stuff like getting goaded or breaking pokerface.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T17:22:40-07:00","id":1155895,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=malonkey1;n1155753]<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1155709#post1155709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Another theme is actually sort of a condemnation of the scientism and intellectual arrogance that Genius 1E sort of unintentionally advanced. The Genii are intended to be, quite frankly, mostly assholes and lunatics. Advancing as a Genius is almost always going to be easier for Genii who disregard the well-being of others, and the detachment of Inspired society from humanity will generally be played up as a bad thing that the Peerage and Lemuria maintain for maintaining their own power. It's hard to be a good Genius.</div> </div> </div> </div>So the game will finally be about playing monsters who are flawed people, not superheroes who live our ideals. Now that's more like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T15:09:37-08:00","id":1156494,"title":"","content":"Small thematic suggestion in regards to the Intergity stand-in for Genius 2E. <br /> <br /> Instead of Sins against Restraint/Patience/Ect and Breaking Points, why not take a cue from Vampire the Requiem and re-name them to better fit the theme and mood of the gameline. Just for one example...why not call them Transgressions against Restraint/Patience/Ect? Breaking Point rolls could be refered to as &quot;Determining the scale of your Transgressions&quot; or &quot;Threshold rolls.&quot; <br /> <br /> That might end up doing a better job of evoking the proper aesthetics for when a Genius begins to push the limits of their creativity &amp; brilliance just a little to far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Spellcheck 11-06-2017, 06:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T09:36:18-08:00","id":1157575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1156494#post1156494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Small thematic suggestion in regards to the Intergity stand-in for Genius 2E.<br /> <br /> Instead of Sins against Restraint/Patience/Ect and Breaking Points, why not take a cue from Vampire the Requiem and re-name them to better fit the theme and mood of the gameline. Just for one example...why not call them Transgressions against Restraint/Patience/Ect? Breaking Point rolls could be refered to as &quot;Determining the scale of your Transgressions&quot; or &quot;Threshold rolls.&quot;<br /> <br /> That might end up doing a better job of evoking the proper aesthetics for when a Genius begins to push the limits of their creativity &amp; brilliance just a little to far.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about breaking points toward Paragon?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T14:03:52-08:00","id":1157633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tambov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1157575#post1157575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What about breaking points toward Paragon?</div> </div> </div> </div>Did we ever agreed to commit to that idea? I honestly don't know how well idea of using Harmony sits with me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T16:31:36-08:00","id":1157658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1157633#post1157633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did we ever agreed to commit to that idea? I honestly don't know how well idea of using Harmony sits with me.</div> </div> </div> </div>There wasn't really a consensus for it. I have it in my notes, but I don't think we agreed on it in any substantive sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T19:15:59-08:00","id":1158318,"title":"","content":"Well the general idea was to strike a cool cosmetic flare for breaking point rolls, like how checking for Detachment or Hubris adds a little more flavor to the respective gamelines than just checking for a Breaking Point. <br /> <br /> That being said, not sure about ones in the opposite direction. Probably need to work that system out first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T06:40:29-08:00","id":1163895,"title":"","content":"Currently looking for suggestions for the new opening fiction.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking of something like &quot;The Mortal's Perspective&quot;. We actually start with a Genius nearing the completion of their latest masterplan, In Medias Res style. The narrator, who is a Beholden, manages to summon the willpower to overcome the toxic relationship and become an Edison. This allows him to no longer depend on the worldview of his master, steal his designs for Wonders and actually make them profitable.<br /> <br /> The Edison becomes famous while the Genius is exposed for the criminal mastermind he is...however, the Edison is not satisfied, the allure of the Wonders is too great, and he begins investigating their inner workings, thus triggering his own Breakthrough into a Genius. He promises himself to do better than his master, to create a true Utopia, but at this point he has been confirmed to be an unreliable narrator. We then cut back to the new Genius when he was still mortal, saying something like &quot;it's always the little people who have the biggest dreams&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 11-30-2017, 10:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T21:24:22-08:00","id":1164172,"title":"","content":"Love the idea for the opening fiction. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It also brought to mind another quick question. Would it be better to have the term Edison be a cheaky shorthand for that type of Rogue Beholden? Because the name functions just fine as is, but seems already kinda like slang for the &quot;official scientific term.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T22:39:24-08:00","id":1164181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1163895#post1163895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Currently looking for suggestions for the new opening fiction.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking of something like &quot;The Mortal's Perspective&quot;. We actually start with a Genius nearing the completion of their latest masterplan, In Medias Res style. The narrator, who is a Beholden, manages to summon the willpower to overcome the toxic relationship and become an Edison. This allows him to no longer depend on the worldview of his master, steal his designs for Wonders and actually make them profitable.<br /> <br /> The Edison becomes famous while the Genius is exposed for the criminal mastermind he is...however, the Edison is not satisfied, the allure of the Wonders is too great, and he begins investigating their inner workings, thus triggering his own Breakthrough into a Genius. He promises himself to do better than his master, to create a true Utopia, but at this point he has been confirmed to be an unreliable narrator. We then cut back to the new Genius when he was still mortal, saying something like &quot;it's always the little people who have the biggest dreams&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm all for it. Maybe, as a suggestion, bookend it by having them suffer the same fate at the hands of their own Beholden?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-25T19:30:49-08:00","id":1170575,"title":"","content":"Hi. I'm a GM who is currently running a genius 1e campaign. Do any of you guys have a organized version of genius 2e?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23621-tg0098","name":"tg0098","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23621_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-25T20:03:07-08:00","id":1170577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tg0098</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1170575#post1170575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi. I'm a GM who is currently running a genius 1e campaign. Do any of you guys have a organized version of genius 2e?</div> </div> </div> </div>To an extent. The link in my sig has some rough documents with a lot of the things we've thrown about, as well as a sort of alpha version of the templates and Wonder Creation. The last few months have been nuts for me with my new job, which has delayed me getting what I have onto a wiki. I think I may actually have some free time tomorrow to move the rest of my material there, and I can do some more work more consistently now that my schedule is ironed out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-06T09:26:17-08:00","id":1173774,"title":"","content":"Perhaps a little off-topic, but would Gravity Falls (the town, from the cartoon of the same name) have a place in Genius? I don't really know if Bardos are sticking around, but it seems like a pretty textbook one in my opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-06T22:52:32-08:00","id":1173964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1173774#post1173774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps a little off-topic, but would Gravity Falls (the town, from the cartoon of the same name) have a place in Genius? I don't really know if Bardos are sticking around, but it seems like a pretty textbook one in my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bardos, as far as I've been writing things, do indeed still exist. They're less directly tied to Inspiration in many cases, but Bardos are still definitely there as places outside what human knowledge normally knows, often with laws of reality that differe from our own subtly or obviously. As an aside, Bardo is now a blanket term that includes &quot;Inspired Bardos,&quot; which are Bardos explicitly centered around Genii, Inspiration, and Impetus, and are what the term was used for in 1E. Any alternate plane or dimension is now a &quot;bardo.&quot; Underworld, Arcadia, Duat, all Bardos of varying levels of unfriendliness.<br /> <br /> And, strictly speaking, the Inspired Bardos would be considered Lower Depths by Mages that feed upon Impetus, lacking reliable sources of their own.<br /> <br /> I'm not terribly familiar with the show, but from what I can tell, Gravity Falls itself would not be a Bardo, although certainly a nexus of Inspired phenomena, possibly a powerful Generator, but Bill Cipher's dimension could be a Bardo.<br /> <br /> Other examples that could make good Bardos:<br /> <br /> <b>Mirrodin:</b> A world that once symbolized a perfect paradise of artificial life, it has since become infected and dominated by a more modern conception of technology as a force of dehumanization from the rival Bardo of <b>Phyrexia</b>.<br /> <br /> <b>The Room WITH A MOOSE:</b> A Wondrous Bardo (that is, a Bardo custom-built as a Wonder) built by a particularly mad Mane with a bone to pick against a bus full of children. It contains only a particularly vicious moose.<br /> <br /> <b>The DC Universe:</b> Another Wondrous Bardo, created as an experiment by one Arch-Genius known as Doctor Manhattan, to resemble a more idealized version of his own world. It denizens are slowly becoming increasingly aware of their creator, with possibly disastrous consequences.<br /> <br /> <b>Shattered Seattle:</b> The result of temporal machinations by some enigmatic &quot;God-Machine,&quot; Seattle is host to a number of looping parallel timelines. Genii without appropriate Apokalypsi wonders will become rapidly disoriented, not to mention the host of clockwork demons prowling the timelines.<br /> <br /> <b>The Upside-Down: </b>A dimension parallel to our own, with its own unholy interpretation of life. It is unknown if intelligent life can be found in this toxic, slime-coated bardo, but God help us all if there is, as the wildlife is more than bad enough.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-07T02:25:48-08:00","id":1173982,"title":"","content":"So, uh, is there a particular reason you're keeping Geniuses as off-brand Mages powered by I Can't Believe It's Not Mana when &quot;occult physics&quot; are a thing now? Because reconceptualizing their powers to be based on the latter would actually, you know, fit the archetype they're supposed to represent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-07T08:21:05-08:00","id":1174030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1173982#post1173982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, uh, is there a particular reason you're keeping Geniuses as off-brand Mages powered by I Can't Believe It's Not Mana when &quot;occult physics&quot; are a thing now? Because reconceptualizing their powers to be based on the latter would actually, you know, fit the archetype they're supposed to represent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Operating under old information? Wonders have multiple sources, which can basically be described as Occult Physics (operating under hidden, or supernatural, principles).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 01-07-2018, 11:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-07T08:47:55-08:00","id":1174037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1174030#post1174030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Operating under old information? Wonders have multiple sources, which can basically be described as Occult Physics (operating under hidden, or supernatural, principles).</div> </div> </div> </div>Precisely. And then there's the fact that the occult physics of Demon is incredibly hazy anyway, to the point where the distinction between that and just plain magic is largely one of nomenclature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-07T09:44:38-08:00","id":1174048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1174037#post1174037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Precisely. And then there's the fact that the occult physics of Demon is incredibly hazy anyway, to the point where the distinction between that and just plain magic is largely one of nomenclature.</div> </div> </div> </div>But not Nomenclature, or the Deceived would get upset.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-07T17:49:48-08:00","id":1174163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1174037#post1174037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Precisely. And then there's the fact that the occult physics of Demon is incredibly hazy anyway, to the point where the distinction between that and just plain magic is largely one of nomenclature.</div> </div> </div> </div>While Occult Physics are indeed hazy, it does still carry a distinct flavor and style that might not be different in execution, with the ideas of their powers being rooted half-way in turns of scientific understanding and study(the other half being the divine classics).<br /> <br /> I'm not saying Geniuses should be Occult physicists, but I am saying that it doesn't hurt to take cues from it, as I have mentioned before.<br /> <br /> *quietly descends back into the dark and the sticky*<br /> <br /> EDIT: and then I go back and read your review of my review as well as your direction and I cordially withdraw the point, as it does clash with where Genius 2nd seems to be going.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 01-07-2018, 10:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T01:35:10-08:00","id":1174231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1174163#post1174163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While Occult Physics are indeed hazy, it does still carry a distinct flavor and style that might not be different in execution, with the ideas of their powers being rooted half-way in turns of scientific understanding and study(the other half being the divine classics).<br /> <br /> I'm not saying Geniuses should be Occult physicists, but I am saying that it doesn't hurt to take cues from it, as I have mentioned before.<br /> <br /> *quietly descends back into the dark and the sticky*<br /> <br /> EDIT: and then I go back and read your review of my review as well as your direction and I cordially withdraw the point, as it does clash with where Genius 2nd seems to be going.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right, my description of Occult Physics does kind of oversimplify. There certainly could be Genii who operate under something resembling the Occult Physics of Demon, but it'd be one of countless possible paradigms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-12T05:21:15-08:00","id":1175428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1173982#post1173982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, uh, is there a particular reason you're keeping Geniuses as off-brand Mages powered by I Can't Believe It's Not Mana when &quot;occult physics&quot; are a thing now? Because reconceptualizing their powers to be based on the latter would actually, you know, fit the archetype they're supposed to represent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some people have had them use GM's occult physics. My signature has a link to such a template.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-12T06:01:33-08:00","id":1175430,"title":"","content":"Please pardon the small rant. All of the below is simply my interpretation.<br /> <br /> A Mage is someone who has connected with the higher Truth of a Platonic realm, and impose such higher laws down upon a diminished world (subject to corruption by an interposing madness/chaos dimension/gulf) through their mere will and knowledge. This also imposes implicit value upon the relative nature of the respective realms, knowledge, and those who have access to them.<br /> <br /> A Genius is one who has had their mind cracked open, picking up ideas, designs, and thoughts not their own. They see future (and past) developments, the inner workings of physics (mundane and occult), and theories from times and universes not their own. It's like someone in the iron ages having a radio or TV on in the back of their heads set to an information channel, except the specials jump around, and sometimes you get the History Channel from alternate timelines. They might know how to build a Cold Fusion generator (maybe even out of mundane parts) or have the design for a working Ghost Trap. They don't know <i>why</i> it works, but they <i>do</i> know how to build it. To conserve their sanity, they construct various worldviews and paradigms so that these things make &quot;sense&quot;. At least the lucky ones do - those who haven't learned to tune out the ideas they aren't feasible, or question too heavily the &quot;why&quot; behind their notions often end up broken, isolated individuals.<br /> <br /> A Genius's Wonders work not because they clap their hands and power it with insanity. They create things that exploit <i>real</i> principles (albeit sometimes ones not-native to the current environment and/or universe) in a mostly repeatable manner (if it isn't repeatable, it is a nice experiment, but isn't a Wonder). But they can only keep track of so much at once (this would be Mania/Impetus). They can't just will it on their own (though exploiting certain pre-devised formulae that rely merely upon calculations being run or observed does blur the line).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 01-12-2018, 09:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-12T12:47:37-08:00","id":1175534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1175430#post1175430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please pardon the small rant. All of the below is simply my interpretation.<br /> <br /> A Mage is someone who has connected with the higher Truth of a Platonic realm, and impose such higher laws down upon a diminished world (subject to corruption by an interposing madness/chaos dimension/gulf) through their mere will and knowledge. This also imposes implicit value upon the relative nature of the respective realms, knowledge, and those who have access to them.<br /> <br /> A Genius is one who has had their mind cracked open, picking up ideas, designs, and thoughts not their own. They see future (and past) developments, the inner workings of physics (mundane and occult), and theories from times and universes not their own. It's like someone in the iron ages having a radio or TV on in the back of their heads set to an information channel, except the specials jump around, and sometimes you get the History Channel from alternate timelines. They might know how to build a Cold Fusion generator (maybe even out of mundane parts) or have the design for a working Ghost Trap. They don't know <i>why</i> it works, but they <i>do</i> know how to build it. To conserve their sanity, they construct various worldviews and paradigms so that these things make &quot;sense&quot;. At least the lucky ones do - those who haven't learned to tune out the ideas they aren't feasible, or question too heavily the &quot;why&quot; behind their notions often end up broken, isolated individuals.<br /> <br /> A Genius's Wonders work not because they clap their hands and power it with insanity. They create things that exploit <i>real</i> principles (albeit sometimes ones not-native to the current environment and/or universe) in a mostly repeatable manner (if it isn't repeatable, it is a nice experiment, but isn't a Wonder). But they can only keep track of so much at once (this would be Mania/Impetus). They can't just will it on their own (though exploiting certain pre-devised formulae that rely merely upon calculations being run or observed does blur the line).</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a fantastic way of explaining it. I love it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-12T13:40:17-08:00","id":1175549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1175430#post1175430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Genius's Wonders work not because they clap their hands and power it with insanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>According to the notes as they presently stand that's <i>exactly</i> how they work. Mania/Impetus is consistently described as directly being what makes Wonders tick, you have to fit your Wonders into your Paradigm and not the other way around which is the opposite of what would be the case if a Wonder's &quot;operating principles&quot; existed outside of your own head, &quot;Questions to Answer&quot; explicitly calls Wonders pseudoscientific, and last but not least your Paradigm is something that explicitly <i>overrides</i> reality within a radius determined by your Inspiration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-12T14:17:36-08:00","id":1175561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1175430#post1175430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A Genius is one who has had their mind cracked open, picking up ideas, designs, and thoughts not their own. They see future (and past) developments, the inner workings of physics (mundane and occult), and theories from times and universes not their own. It's like someone in the iron ages having a radio or TV on in the back of their heads set to an information channel, except the specials jump around, and sometimes you get the History Channel from alternate timelines. They might know how to build a Cold Fusion generator (maybe even out of mundane parts) or have the design for a working Ghost Trap. They don't know <i>why</i> it works, but they <i>do</i> know how to build it. To conserve their sanity, they construct various worldviews and paradigms so that these things make &quot;sense&quot;. At least the lucky ones do - those who haven't learned to tune out the ideas they aren't feasible, or question too heavily the &quot;why&quot; behind their notions often end up broken, isolated individuals.<br /> <br /> A Genius's Wonders work not because they clap their hands and power it with insanity. <b>They create things that exploit <i>real</i> principles (albeit sometimes ones not-native to the current environment and/or universe) in a mostly repeatable manner (if it isn't repeatable, it is a nice experiment, but isn't a Wonder). But they can only keep track of so much at once (this would be Mania/Impetus). They can't just will it on their own (though exploiting certain pre-devised formulae that rely merely upon calculations being run or observed does blur the line).</b></div> </div> </div> </div>All of this, particularly the bolded, is very cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-16T19:19:18-08:00","id":1176665,"title":"","content":"As I was looking at the Checklist Doc for Genius, I noticed that the only Cataylst with a favored Axiom that was missing was Skafoi, the Axiom of travel. Wanting to fill out the Catalysts, I have come up with another Catalyst: <u>Erregung, The Catalyst of Excitement.</u> If someone else has already come up with a better idea than this, then feel free to ignore.<br /> <br /> <u>Erregung*: The Catalyst of Excitement</u><br /> Nickname: Hedonists<br /> Planet: Neptune<br /> Axiom: Skafoi<br /> <br /> <i>\u201cI have seen sights no eyes should be witness to, heard sounds that make unexplainable music. I have traveled to far off lands and sailed the ocean of time, drinking in what they have to show me, to teach me. I have debated with alien intelligences, felt strange sensations within my flesh. I have been through experiences that no mortal man should bare witness to\u2026 and you\u2019re telling me to stop?! How dare you bores think to command me; I have but seen a small glimpse of what this brave new world has to offer me, and I will not stop until I\u2019ve experienced it all!\u201d</i><br /> <br /> All Genii (with the possible exception of Klagen) are excitable: when a Wonder works correctly, when they overcome a challenge, when they defeat/vaporize/polymorph their mortal foes. But the Erregung are different in that they crave new experiences all the time. People usually Catalyze into Erregung when they\u2019re exposed to a totally new sensation and want to know more about it, or they realize the natural wonder that is the world around them. Becoming a Erregung is a revolutionary experience; the light inside commands you to do new things, experience all life has to offer, good or evil, painful or sweet. This Catalyst represents the means to broaden your horizon through science; not necessarily what it can teach you, but instead what it can show you and take you to.<br /> <br /> However, it differs from Staunen in that they\u2019re not as obsessed; in fact, they\u2019re quite the opposite. Erregung have the derangements of <b>recklessness </b>and <b>noncommitment. </b>A Erregung will pursue a task or work on a project until it no longer excites them, in which best case scenario they\u2019ll clean up and start anew on something else, and worst case they just leave it, not caring about the consequences of their actions if it doesn\u2019t affect them. To put it into a metaphor, Staunen will dig a really deep into the ground until they\u2019re satisfied, where they\u2019ll get back out and start anew somewhere else. While they were digging that hole, an Erregung would have dug out several smaller holes all over the place, working on one until they got bored of that spot and picked another spot. Travelers (everyone else) are at risk of falling in both holes, though the Staunen holes would likely be more hazardous while the Erregung would be more numerous but <i>mostly </i>only annoying. Erregung favor <b>Skafoi</b>, to take them to new places and then to get them out of there when trouble arises. <br /> <br /> That\u2019s not to say Erregung are heartless, however. In fact, quite the opposite, as they may be the most emotionally diverse Genius. A Erregung on a team will readily switch to anger to joy to sadness, not submersed on one emotion like Grimms or Klagens. An Erregung will also try to bring in new viewpoints that the other members of a team might not see, and be willing to dive into danger when the need arrives. It\u2019s also a two-sided coin, however; when Erregung feels something for the moment, they <i>really </i>feel it, and the willingness to dive in might not be for the best at the moment. Their teammates may need to reel them in for a bit, lest they do something they\u2019d regret later.<br /> <br /> Examples: Rick Sanchez (Rick and Morty), The Doctor (Doctor Who), Phineas and Ferb (Phineas and Ferb)<br /> <br /> *Name pending, looking for something along the line of \u201cthrill\u201d or \u201cexcitement\u201d <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23709-cannox","name":"Cannox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23709_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-16T22:39:32-08:00","id":1176697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cannox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1176665#post1176665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I was looking at the Checklist Doc for Genius, I noticed that the only Cataylst with a favored Axiom that was missing was Skafoi, the Axiom of travel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, sorry, I think I've forgotten to update my signature. I've been moving stuff to a wiki. <a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Here's a link for now, and I'll change my sig.</a><br /> <br /> Favored Axiomata have been changed some, so Foundations no longer provide them. Now, each Catalyst gives two favored Axiomata. Skafoi was placed with Staunen, alongside Apokalypsi. <a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius/Chapter_One#Catalysts\" target=\"_blank\">Link here.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-17T05:42:12-08:00","id":1176756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1176697#post1176697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, sorry, I think I've forgotten to update my signature. I've been moving stuff to a wiki. <a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Here's a link for now, and I'll change my sig.</a><br /> <br /> Favored Axiomata have been changed some, so Foundations no longer provide them. Now, each Catalyst gives two favored Axiomata. Skafoi was placed with Staunen, alongside Apokalypsi. <a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius/Chapter_One#Catalysts\" target=\"_blank\">Link here.</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah, that explains it. To be honest, I created the Catalyst 75% because to fill out the Axiom, and 25% because I couldn't place what catalyst Rick would be, since I always placed Staunen with a deep obsession. But I can see Rick as a <i>very </i>low Obligation Staunen, constantly looking for a new fix of excitement at everyone else's expense. The only reason he's not illuminated is because of his family.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23709-cannox","name":"Cannox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23709_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-17T09:10:29-08:00","id":1176785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cannox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1176756#post1176756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Ah, that explains it. To be honest, I created the Catalyst 75% because to fill out the Axiom, and 25% because I couldn't place what catalyst Rick would be, since I always placed Staunen with a deep obsession. But I can see Rick as a <i>very </i>low Obligation Staunen, constantly looking for a new fix of excitement at everyone else's expense. The only reason he's not illuminated is because of his family.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't place Rick as Staunen. He doesn't really give a damn about the world around him, and lacks that curiosity that Staunen needs. If I had to place him, he'd be a Grimm, especially given his proclivity for random violence and his willingness to make random strangers suffer if they annoy him. Honestly, he'd actually fit as one of the hypothetical other Catalysts, specifically Langeweile, the catalyst of ennui.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-20T12:20:44-08:00","id":1177654,"title":"","content":"I wonder if I should start up a new thread about Genius crossovers, or maybe just keep it in this one. Perhaps a good way of discovering what a Genius <i>is </i>is by finding out what a Genius <i>is not, </i>and what a Genius' views are of vampires, Prometheans, Hunters, and of course Magi are. And it could even include fan-lines, like Princess and Leviathan. What do you guys think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23709-cannox","name":"Cannox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23709_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-20T22:58:29-08:00","id":1177780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cannox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1177654#post1177654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if I should start up a new thread about Genius crossovers, or maybe just keep it in this one. Perhaps a good way of discovering what a Genius <i>is </i>is by finding out what a Genius <i>is not, </i>and what a Genius' views are of vampires, Prometheans, Hunters, and of course Magi are. And it could even include fan-lines, like Princess and Leviathan. What do you guys think?</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally speaking, a Genius sees the other supernatural as something to be studied, analyzed, and at worst, disassembled for spare parts. They often have fewer moral compunctions about strapping a vampire to a table and cutting them open, because they're much less prone to dying that humans are under the same treatment. With other supernaturals, the Genii's (un)natural tendency to view people around them as autonomous systems rather than actual people is strongly magnified, and it doesn't help that a fair number of other Genii and humans are pretty much okay with it when it's a spooky scary on the slab. Vampires are a source of potent biological agents, werewolves become excellent candidates for unwilling roboticization, and unwary mages may find their brains being used to power a supercomputer designed to tear holes in reality. They <i>could</i> make friends, if they really tried. It's just hard to make friends with somebody who, due to the force of raw Inspiration eating at your soul, starts off just a step above a frog in Bio 101 on your priority list.<br /> <br /> It also really depends where they sit on Restraint. Paragons tend to be better-able to adjust in general, especially with more &quot;human&quot; supernaturals like Mages and Nobility, while Renegades are more concerned with how a supernatural being might serve their Opus. If its continued existence is in its favor, they're cool, but if they get in the way, or they're more useful dead, a Renegade will have little trouble justifying it, espcially with extremely alien beings like outed Demons or Leviathans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-21T03:15:16-08:00","id":1177812,"title":"","content":"If anything, I'd think that the Fellowships would be more interested in the other game lines than anyone else. Observe:<br /> <br /> - The Resurrection Consortium would be very interested in how revival by Vitae works, and Prometheans and Mummies would be an object of interest too.<br /> - The Malcolm T. Washington Fellowship would be all over the insectile changing breeds. What's worse than a mad scientist riding a 50' mantis? A mad scientist riding a 50' WEREmantis.<br /> - The Hermetic Order would love to run some tests on a Mage or two to see how their powers work.<br /> - The Phantom Foundation would just THROW itself at the Bound to see how their powers work and help them out, but they'd also be way into vampires, spirits and Mummies.<br /> - The Iridium Sentinels would make for interesting companions to Princesses, but in some cases they'd need to be reigned in a bit.<br /> - The Elders of the Third Law might make for interesting allies in the fight against the God-Machine for Demons.<br /> - The Institute would be interested in the Gadgets of Demons, as well as the fear-based powers of Beasts and the Variations of Deviants.<br /> - The Nine Vertex Devils would start organizing races that go through the hedge, with Changelings losing their shit and try to stop them to not attract the True Fae (who actually enjoy the novelty and spectacle of it all).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-21T06:29:26-08:00","id":1177831,"title":"","content":"I recall that other supernatural creatures DO NOT trigger Havoc when dealing with Wonders, which I have no doubt that quite a few genii would be interested in. What's the use of these death rays if no one but you are able to use them? I imagine a whole new Fellowship could spring up around this: supplying other supernaturals with Wonders, and finding out where the line is drawn where a supernatural isn't &quot;human&quot; anymore. Is a werewolf in human form &quot;human&quot;? Are slashers? ?Ghouls? Mages (for mages I would say no, they are still human, which is yet another reason they don't like each other).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1177780#post1177780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They <i>could</i> make friends, if they really tried. It's just hard to make friends with somebody who, due to the force of raw Inspiration eating at your soul, starts off just a step above a frog in Bio 101 on your priority list.</div> </div> </div> </div>That frog doesn't usually go into a Death Rage and mess up the lab, or call up it's friends to get help beating you down (and if that frog does, the hell kinda' class were you taking?). A Genius may often find themselves on the lower end of the food chain, at least for now. If a supernatural cannot be defeated, then they must be avoided or bargained with. Working with another Supernatural can result in new resources, allies, or simply not dying, which most people would find good. For example, a vampire elder could commission you to build weapons for it in exchange for money (and your life). Then again, he could also ask for a people farm... Not all contact need to be hostile, but it doesn't have to work out well either.<br /> <br /> (On a side note, I imagine the Cherion Group would <i>hate </i>Genii, since you can't really use any of their stuff without it blowing up. Though I guess you could dissect a Genius' brain for intelligence boosting enhanchers...)<br /> <br /> Finally, the mechanical side: does taking a part of a Supernatural result in Larvae? Because even though they are monsters, most of them use to be human too, and most if not all have human feelings and intellect.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23709-cannox","name":"Cannox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23709_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-21T07:16:16-08:00","id":1177840,"title":"","content":"If we are reimagining Inspiration and Wonders as less &quot;quasi-magic-tech power by madness&quot;, I'd be in favor of other supernaturals actually triggering Havoc. It would solidify that Havoc lies more in the Wonder's imperfect design, and serves to isolate Genii more. I could see a bonus to Havoc rolls scaled to Power stat, though, to mitigate the effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-21T09:16:20-08:00","id":1177865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cannox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1177831#post1177831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I recall that other supernatural creatures DO NOT trigger Havoc when dealing with Wonders, which I have no doubt that quite a few genii would be interested in. What's the use of these death rays if no one but you are able to use them? I imagine a whole new Fellowship could spring up around this: supplying other supernaturals with Wonders, and finding out where the line is drawn where a supernatural isn't &quot;human&quot; anymore. Is a werewolf in human form &quot;human&quot;? Are slashers? ?Ghouls? Mages (for mages I would say no, they are still human, which is yet another reason they don't like each other).</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, I've been thinking that supernaturals probably should cause Havoc, except in specific edge cases (for example, if a Genius were to power their Wonders under narrative laws, a Changeling might be able to safely use them).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That frog doesn't usually go into a Death Rage and mess up the lab, or call up it's friends to get help beating you down (and if that frog does, the hell kinda' class were you taking?). A Genius may often find themselves on the lower end of the food chain, at least for now. </div> </div> </div>True, but the described point of view doesn't come from a rational place. Genii tend to be arrogant, so they may not actually realize that they're low on the food chain, especially if they get lucky or they think they've found an advantage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (On a side note, I imagine the Cherion Group would <i>hate </i>Genii, since you can't really use any of their stuff without it blowing up. Though I guess you could dissect a Genius' brain for intelligence boosting enhanchers...) </div> </div> </div>They'd probably only have problems with Genii that they can't get to work for them. There's probably a couple of Edisons hidden among Cheiron, and a Genius wwho needs some cash might be able to get a job performing their &quot;operations.&quot; After all, people will pay through the nose for a guy who can implant a demon's heart perfectly as a 1-hour in-patient procedure without leaving a scar, and then can retrieve it when the guy inevitably goes insane<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Finally, the mechanical side: does taking a part of a Supernatural result in Larvae? Because even though they are monsters, most of them use to be human too, and most if not all have human feelings and intellect. </div> </div> </div>Taking a supernatural bit <i>can</i> result in a Larva, but it still has to be pretty awful. If you've got a Thesis related around, say, ghosts, and you decided to resolve it all at once by stealing a Sin-Eater's eyes, that'd do it. Removing a werewolf's inflamed appendix because nobody else can stop it from regrowing isn't really worth a Larva (although it'd definitely help a lot of biologically-oriented Theses!)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T01:09:07-08:00","id":1182197,"title":"","content":"I'm new here, so I didn't look at every development post. So here are my dumb questions: Is Genius 2e complete? Because it doesn't look so. What can I do to contribute to make it complete? What is the most urgent matter in completing it? Has everything in table of contents been thought out and are just waiting to be written in master doc, or are they just blank spaces?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23621-tg0098","name":"tg0098","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23621_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T08:09:51-08:00","id":1182266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tg0098</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1182197#post1182197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm new here, so I didn't look at every development post. So here are my dumb questions: Is Genius 2e complete? Because it doesn't look so.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is not yet complete.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What can I do to contribute to make it complete? What is the most urgent matter in completing it? </div> </div> </div>I think the main thing that I might need help on is things like the fiction and worldbuilding.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Has everything in table of contents been thought out and are just waiting to be written in master doc, or are they just blank spaces? </div> </div> </div>There's been some thought to most of the things in the TOC, with varying levels of completed writing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T21:36:18-07:00","id":1196360,"title":"","content":"So, uh<br /> <br /> Can anyone please tell me what exactly I can write for 2ed at this moment? <br /> <br /> I'm stumped for ideas. I'll most likely go with whatever is suggested to me. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4488_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4488\" data-vbnamecard=\"4488\">malonkey1</a> says we need fiction and worldbuilding, and I can certainly help with that, but I work best when I have a base of inspiration to start from (no pun intended).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T06:40:59-07:00","id":1196463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1196360#post1196360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, uh<br /> <br /> Can anyone please tell me what exactly I can write for 2ed at this moment?<br /> <br /> I'm stumped for ideas. I'll most likely go with whatever is suggested to me. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4488_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4488\" data-vbnamecard=\"4488\">malonkey1</a> says we need fiction and worldbuilding, and I can certainly help with that, but I work best when I have a base of inspiration to start from (no pun intended).</div> </div> </div> </div>How about a small monologue of either a typical Genius (over-educated Mad Scientist), or a less typical one (like an Artist, Philosopher, or Mystic Scholar) up against the other. This would explore how they see themselves, and how the other is both possible and &quot;wrong&quot; (because they are &quot;wrong, obviously&quot;).<br /> <br /> Or a train-of-thought monologue about a Genius going from something reasonable to approaching the Deep End, then attempting to correct themselves back. End it with them saying a simple statement or &quot;I'm sorry - what was the question again?&quot;. This would highlight how lost the Inspired can get in their own minds, and how their observed actions are just the surface.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 03-17-2018, 09:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T15:11:23-07:00","id":1197348,"title":"","content":"Hmm. Would it make sense to structure early temporal projection like Manifestation-less Achronals? The Wonder projects the target to the designated time, which treats the target locally as an Achronal. Lacking even Twilight Form, they would only be able to observe and not interact with anything. Additional modifications might simply be granting Manifestations - first Twilight Form, then Fetter (for longer term observation), Possession (for the &quot;project my mind into my past self or ancestor&quot;), or Materialize. I think Claim would be beyond reach, as would Influences or Numina. But Wonders can easily replicate those anyways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T09:05:03-07:00","id":1198690,"title":"","content":"I dunno if I have mentioned this, but maybe the game will be stronger if we remove Jabir altogether? Please bear with me.<br /> <br /> As it is, the penalties of Jabir can be canceled with Exelixi and such pretty easily.<br /> <br /> Secondly, you don't need a communication-disrupting aura when your go-to solution is &quot;fixing&quot; stuff with death rays or brainwashing. People will see you as insane regardless.<br /> <br /> Am I making sense? I feel like it is more thematically powerful if your failures are a result of your own bad decisions and poor judgment, instead of an outside force fucking things up on your behalf. It reinforces the whole &quot;every Genius is their own worst enemy in the end&quot; idea.<br /> <br /> IMPORTANT EDIT: If we must keep Jabir, how about we write it as a Persistent Condition caused by failed Unmada rolls that makes it really hard or even impossible to properly convey your worldview to mortals without turning them into Beholden?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 03-23-2018, 12:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T09:28:25-07:00","id":1198708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1198690#post1198690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno if I have mentioned this, but maybe the game will be stronger if we remove Jabir altogether? Please bear with me.<br /> <br /> As it is, the penalties of Jabir can be canceled with Exelixi and such pretty easily.<br /> <br /> Secondly, you don't need a communication-disrupting aura when your go-to solution is &quot;fixing&quot; stuff with death rays or brainwashing. People will see you as insane regardless.<br /> <br /> Am I making sense? I feel like it is more thematically powerful if your failures are a result of your own bad decisions and poor judgment, instead of an outside force fucking things up on your behalf. It reinforces the whole &quot;every Genius is their own worst enemy in the end&quot; idea.<br /> <br /> IMPORTANT EDIT: If we must keep Jabir, how about we write it as a Persistent Condition caused by failed Unmada rolls that makes it really hard or even impossible to properly convey your worldview to mortals without turning them into Beholden?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I've always seen Jabir not as an outside force corrupting your dialog, but rather the Genius slipping into their own personal jargon and speaking their thoughts out loud. It isn't a communications cipher so much as them talking in Trek Technobabble, and everyone else thinking them weird or not as clever as they think.<br /> <br /> I'd say High Restraint Genii are just better at reigning that in, and &quot;dumbing down&quot; or translating it to &quot;normal&quot; speech. Low Restraint doesn't care, and those &quot;suffering from&quot; Unmada simply can't tell the difference.<br /> <br /> Exelixi can amp up your persuasive skills to try and BS past it, and Epikrato can mind control people in agreeing, but if pressed they won't be able to articulate what you convinced them of. That can be problematic for anything longer than the immediate Scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T09:55:57-07:00","id":1198719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1198708#post1198708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I've always seen Jabir not as an outside force corrupting your dialog, but rather the Genius slipping into their own personal jargon and speaking their thoughts out loud. It isn't a communications cipher so much as them talking in Trek Technobabble, and everyone else thinking them weird or not as clever as they think.<br /> <br /> I'd say High Restraint Genii are just better at reigning that in, and &quot;dumbing down&quot; or translating it to &quot;normal&quot; speech. Low Restraint doesn't care, and those &quot;suffering from&quot; Unmada simply can't tell the difference.<br /> <br /> Exelixi can amp up your persuasive skills to try and BS past it, and Epikrato can mind control people in agreeing, but if pressed they won't be able to articulate what you convinced them of. That can be problematic for anything longer than the immediate Scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then the Jabir Condition should reflect that and have actual mechanical weight. Simply applying dice penalties does not cover it, I believe. Something like...<br /> <br /> <b>Jabir (Persistent)</b><br /> You cannot properly convey the details of your worldview to mortals without the risk of turning them into Beholden. Whenever mortals must roll for becoming Beholden as a result of your actions, they achieve Exceptional Success with 3 Successes. You cannot have a Perfect Impression for Social Maneuvering against mortals who are not specifically your Beholden, and they have [your Inspiration/2 round up] additional Doors to open for the purposes of convincing them of your worldview's legitimacy.<br /> <b>Possible Sources:</b> Dramatically Failing an Unmada roll, mysterious cases of Inspiration compelling you to build Wonders you do not yet understand<br /> <b>Beat:</b> Risk turning someone into a Beholden or bypassing the restrictions on Social Maneuvering through abnormal or unethical means<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Achieve an Exceptional Success on losing or gaining Restraint","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T11:10:47-07:00","id":1198767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1198719#post1198719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then the Jabir Condition should reflect that and have actual mechanical weight. Simply applying dice penalties does not cover it, I believe. Something like...<br /> <br /> <b>Jabir (Persistent)</b><br /> You cannot properly convey the details of your worldview to mortals without the risk of turning them into Beholden. Whenever mortals must roll for becoming Beholden as a result of your actions, they achieve Exceptional Success with 3 Successes. You cannot have a Perfect Impression for Social Maneuvering against mortals who are not specifically your Beholden, and they have [your Inspiration/2 round up] additional Doors to open for the purposes of convincing them of your worldview's legitimacy.<br /> <b>Possible Sources:</b> Dramatically Failing an Unmada roll, mysterious cases of Inspiration compelling you to build Wonders you do not yet understand<br /> <b>Beat:</b> Risk turning someone into a Beholden or bypassing the restrictions on Social Maneuvering through abnormal or unethical means<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Achieve an Exceptional Success on losing or gaining Restraint</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, personally, I'm not sure mechanizing (or making it that easy) Becoming Beholden like that is ideal. I think increasing Doors is fine (possibly instead of or in addition to Social penalties).<br /> <br /> Making it a Condition turns it into a transient things, as opposed to a Fact-of-Life for a Genius. Not sure if that is a/the goal.<br /> <br /> What do the rest of the <s>inmates</s> contributors on this project think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-16T14:12:28-07:00","id":1219423,"title":"","content":"Anything I can do to help with this project? I loved Genius 1e and would love to see it brought up to 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23991-bacchicone","name":"BacchicOne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23991_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T17:26:49-07:00","id":1236217,"title":"","content":"Uh, hey everyone.<br /> <br /> So I'll be square with you all, I 100% forgot about this. I just got a new job, and this kind of fell by the wayside. All the stuff I compiled is still in the link in my sig, though.<br /> <br /> @GibberingEloquence: Jabir as a Condition does seem like a good idea, and your write-up is pretty good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T03:41:09-07:00","id":1236353,"title":"","content":"&quot;It's alive!!! Mwuahahahaha!!!&quot;<br /> <br /> *Ahem* So, where were we at in development gentlefolk? What parts have The Consensus approved, and what remains to be drafted?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T08:41:41-07:00","id":1236426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1236353#post1236353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;It's alive!!! Mwuahahahaha!!!&quot;<br /> <br /> *Ahem* So, where were we at in development gentlefolk? What parts have The Consensus approved, and what remains to be drafted?</div> </div> </div> </div>On the wiki, we have drafts for:<ul><li>Catalysts and Foundations</li> <li>A really brief, threadbare write-up of Inspired history</li> <li>Character Creation</li> <li>Inspiration</li> <li>Restraint</li> <li>Theses and Inspired Beats</li> <li>Wonder Creation</li> </ul><br /> As of yet, we have various bits floating about uncoalesced about enemies (e.g. Beyonders, Manes, etc.), side-characters (Edisons, Beholden, etc.), Bardos, and their attendant systems.<br /> <br /> And obviously, nothing that is there is finalized.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T11:24:19-07:00","id":1236490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1236426#post1236426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On the wiki, we have drafts for:<ul><li>Catalysts and Foundations</li> <li>A really brief, threadbare write-up of Inspired history</li> <li>Character Creation</li> <li>Inspiration</li> <li>Restraint</li> <li>Theses and Inspired Beats</li> <li>Wonder Creation</li> </ul><br /> As of yet, we have various bits floating about uncoalesced about enemies (e.g. Beyonders, Manes, etc.), side-characters (Edisons, Beholden, etc.), Bardos, and their attendant systems.<br /> <br /> And obviously, nothing that is there is finalized.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then, if I may propose to this august Peerage, that we focus on one of the above and finalize it. We may need to go back and make modifications (I can see Restraint needing its mechanical components revised based upon other Thematic and mechanical changes), but let us figure out what something is, then build off of it.<br /> <br /> For my part, the creation aspect of <b>Wonders</b> (making new things, fiddling with the various levers and mechanics) holds my interest. And thus, has my vote. A 2nd choice would be the <b>Catalysts and Foundations </b>- establishing their fluff and mechanical niche would go well toward establishing other elements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T22:56:11-07:00","id":1237419,"title":"","content":"I think wonders might be better off a little later. I think ironing out the ideas behind foundations and catalysts might be better. I was toying with the idea of Genius as an exploration of &quot;toxic intellectualism&quot;, which is to say intellectualism that is taken in a direction and degree as to become damaging to the self or others. With that in mind, I was thinking that the catalysts could be representative of the ways toxic intellectualism could manifest, with the foundations being representative of various attempts at positive outlets, and baramins conversely representing various forms of <i>embracing</i> those toxic attitudes instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T05:58:03-07:00","id":1237465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1237419#post1237419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think wonders might be better off a little later. I think ironing out the ideas behind foundations and catalysts might be better. I was toying with the idea of Genius as an exploration of &quot;toxic intellectualism&quot;, which is to say intellectualism that is taken in a direction and degree as to become damaging to the self or others. With that in mind, I was thinking that the catalysts could be representative of the ways toxic intellectualism could manifest, with the foundations being representative of various attempts at positive outlets, and baramins conversely representing various forms of <i>embracing</i> those toxic attitudes instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay... I think examples would help illustrate. Previously, Catalysts represented different takes on a Mad Scientist or their motivations - Ambition, Curiosity, Revenge, Ego, Regret. What spread do you see?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T09:45:21-07:00","id":1237525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1237465#post1237465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay... I think examples would help illustrate. Previously, Catalysts represented different takes on a Mad Scientist or their motivations - Ambition, Curiosity, Revenge, Ego, Regret. What spread do you see?</div> </div> </div> </div><ul><li><b>Grimms:</b> Grimms want things, and feel that their ability to do something is the same as a reason to do it. They break their opponents down, they demand things of others, and they justify it with their superior intellect, because in their minds, intellectual might makes right. At best, they are pushy, at worst, they can become violent and abusive.</li> <li><b>Hoffnung:</b> Hoffnungs are the classic &quot;egotistical intellectual&quot; type. They consider their those less intellectually-inclined to be inferior, and judge people by their degrees, rather than their character. They feel their intellect makes them better, and act in that framework. At best, they're patronizing. At worst, they're tyrannical.</li> <li><b>Klagen:</b> Klagens see their gifts as a curse, and tend to construct situations in which their intellect makes them a victim, while they're usually doing things to bring suffering on themselves, and then use that victimization as justification to disengage from others. At best, they are depressive and lathargic. At worst, they use the their suffering as justification to make others suffer.</li> <li><b>Neid:</b> Neids feel a sense of inadequacy that they project onto others. They feel like they aren't good enough, and then turn that out against others, coalescing into a paranoia that everyone else thinks that they're as inadequate as they feel themselves to be. At best, they are sensitive and volatile. At worst, they are paranoid and willing to crush others to protect their egos.</li> <li><b>Staunen:</b> Staunens want to know, damn the consequences. They aren't malicious, but they are more concerned with advancing their knowledge, and less with getting it safely and morally. At best, they are irresponsible, at worst, they are utterly amoral.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T10:14:49-07:00","id":1237529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1237525#post1237525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ul><li><b>Grimms:</b> Grimms want things, and feel that their ability to do something is the same as a reason to do it. They break their opponents down, they demand things of others, and they justify it with their superior intellect, because in their minds, intellectual might makes right. At best, they are pushy, at worst, they can become violent and abusive.</li> <li><b>Hoffnung:</b> Hoffnungs are the classic &quot;egotistical intellectual&quot; type. They consider their those less intellectually-inclined to be inferior, and judge people by their degrees, rather than their character. They feel their intellect makes them better, and act in that framework. At best, they're patronizing. At worst, they're tyrannical.</li> <li><b>Klagen:</b> Klagens see their gifts as a curse, and tend to construct situations in which their intellect makes them a victim, while they're usually doing things to bring suffering on themselves, and then use that victimization as justification to disengage from others. At best, they are depressive and lathargic. At worst, they use the their suffering as justification to make others suffer.</li> <li><b>Neid:</b> Neids feel a sense of inadequacy that they project onto others. They feel like they aren't good enough, and then turn that out against others, coalescing into a paranoia that everyone else thinks that they're as inadequate as they feel themselves to be. At best, they are sensitive and volatile. At worst, they are paranoid and willing to crush others to protect their egos.</li> <li><b>Staunen:</b> Staunens want to know, damn the consequences. They aren't malicious, but they are more concerned with advancing their knowledge, and less with getting it safely and morally. At best, they are irresponsible, at worst, they are utterly amoral.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, that helps.<br /> <br /> What impact should Catalyst have? I find Power discounts kinda boring, but better suited to the inherent splat rather than the social/changeable one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T10:21:33-07:00","id":1237530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1237529#post1237529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you, that helps.<br /> <br /> What impact should Catalyst have? I find Power discounts kinda boring, but better suited to the inherent splat rather than the social/changeable one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right now, they each have specific conditions, a little like Demons' Agendas. For example, Hoffnungs have &quot;Give Me the Wheel&quot; where they get beats for taking control to their own detriment, but can resolve it to instantly succeed in resisting attempts to coerce or control them.<br /> <br /> As an alternative, I could see them instead having certain negative drives that can be fulfilled to offer Impetus or situational bonuses. For example, Staunen getting extra Impetus when they have acted wildly irresponsibly to advance the Opus, or Neids getting a beneficial Condition for lashing out at dissent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":4488,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","user":"malonkey1","date":". 07-21-2018, 01:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-22T03:45:38-07:00","id":1237720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1237530#post1237530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Right now, they each have specific conditions, a little like Demons' Agendas. For example, Hoffnungs have &quot;Give Me the Wheel&quot; where they get beats for taking control to their own detriment, but can resolve it to instantly succeed in resisting attempts to coerce or control them.<br /> <br /> As an alternative, I could see them instead having certain negative drives that can be fulfilled to offer Impetus or situational bonuses. For example, Staunen getting extra Impetus when they have acted wildly irresponsibly to advance the Opus, or Neids getting a beneficial Condition for lashing out at dissent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, the former seem to be the better choice. Especially since the way Impetus works now (as its commited to a Wonder instead of spent) make gaining more difficult to quantify. If it works like a shallower version of Deep Inspiration then it would work for a scene at most, probably not long enough to be useful unless the Genius just so happen to be able to fufill their Compulsion as their Wonder is completed (and they don't need it for longer than that). If it just works until spent and stays until uncommited then there will be no end to the Munchkinry. It basically allows anyone who plays to their Compulsion to power an far more Wonders than they would usually be able to without diving Deep (I would reccomend adding a clause that caps bonus Impetus with Inspiration or Resolve).<br /> <br /> Granted both options do have their advantages. The first can be used to encourage the players to manipulate circumstances to their advantage, like abusing your subordinates juuuuust enough so that they would break once the death ray is ready to fire. The second option opens up themes of the temptation to simply Succumb to one's impulses (should we add that to the Lexicon?) damning everyone and everything else along the way. Though that may make it way too similar to Mage for comfort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T07:37:34-07:00","id":1244487,"title":"","content":"\u200b<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4488_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4488\" data-vbnamecard=\"4488\">malonkey1</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a> <br /> <br /> I created a Discord server for Genius, with a section for 2ed brainstorming. If you two or anyone else have an interest in an invite link, send me a PM here on the forums.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-28T15:38:00-07:00","id":1249550,"title":"","content":"Should we copy topics covered there back here, like the discussion on Bardos?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-28T18:20:11-07:00","id":1249586,"title":"","content":"That might be a good idea, yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-29T06:59:44-07:00","id":1249691,"title":"","content":"<u><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Bardos</b></span></u><br /> <br /> So, one difference/clarification between 1E and 2E being proposed is that many<sup>1</sup> of the Bardos that were &quot;setting based upon previously held, but then disproven ideas&quot; <i>were</i> Astral(Temenos) Realms. Occupying to collective consciousness, they were suddenly (and not so suddenly) undone by their own natures being found impossible. But some didn't let their end, well, end them. They started scrambling for resources and traction to sustain themselves, and found ready help among the Inspired. With imported material and Mania/Impetus to support them, they became something <i>more</i>. Now, similar to the Pangaeans of old, they<sup>2</sup> (both the realm and its natives) are part material, part ephemeral, sustained (but often perilously so) by their new power sources.<br /> <br /> <b>But what does this <i>mean</i>?</b><br /> <br /> Bardos are still else<i>wheres</i> defined by what sets them apart. They have specific manners and places that they can be accessed (much like any other otherworld in the CofD). Their denizens could range from I-can't-believe-they're-natural! flora and fauna, to material supernatural beings (use Horrors and Brief Nightmares, maybe Claimed, with the odd Integral Wonder in place of Dread Powers), to still living-thought-shapes like<sup>3</sup> Goetia. They are fine in their native environs, but <i>Bad Things</i><sup>tm</sup> happen when they leave for any length of time, subject to their degree of supernatural nature.<br /> <br /> <sup>1</sup>: Some Bardos weren't (and aren't) clearly created from ideas humanity previously held (like wherever the Phantom Slaver Yetis came from). Those obviously aren't former Temenos Realms. At least, Human ones. From this timelines. Add additional qualifiers, etc., etc. They still require specific materials, actions, times, or places to get to, so many Genii just group them together and call them all Bardos.<br /> <sup>2</sup>: Some Bardos and their residents still haven't integrated with this whole &quot;material existence&quot; thing, either because they are new, or it just doesn't mesh with their nature. Those tend to be treated much like other Astral Realms, albeit cut off from the greater portion (can't reach other parts of the Temenos, the Anima Mundi, etc.) and their residents much like Goetia, though some exceptions<sup>3</sup> apply.<br /> <sup>3</sup>: Ephemeral-like residents of Bardos (sometimes called Manes) possess many of the traits of Goetia, but break some of the rules - they can have Manifestations naturally, some need Mania/Impetus as opposed to Essence, and some experience Havoc-like events instead of Bans or Banes. They are <i>mostly</i> similar, but assumptions are dangerous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-29T07:02:54-07:00","id":1249692,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4488_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4488\" data-vbnamecard=\"4488\">malonkey1</a> Did you want to post your Bardo Conditions too?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-30T02:53:31-07:00","id":1249913,"title":"","content":"I do wonder why these realms needed mania/impetus to survive, simply being known as impossible isn't really detrimental to astral locations. If it were fully forgotten ideas though that could make sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-30T09:50:09-07:00","id":1249983,"title":"","content":"As I see it, it's not so much survival that's the issue; it's the kinda-sorta material state of being. And that doesn't necessarily start when they're revealed to be \u201cimpossible\u201d. Rather, it's what happens when a Genius discovers a Bardo: his Mania/Impetus makes it \u201creal\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-30T10:49:16-07:00","id":1249995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1249983#post1249983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I see it, it's not so much survival that's the issue; it's the kinda-sorta material state of being. And that doesn't necessarily start when they're revealed to be \u201cimpossible\u201d. Rather, it's what happens when a Genius discovers a Bardo: his Mania/Impetus makes it \u201creal\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not just one, but otherwise, yeah. The idea is that the threat of non-relevance prompts extreme action, which ends up resulting in the oddity that is a Bardo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-11T11:05:20-07:00","id":1253321,"title":"","content":"Hey I got an idea for anti-Havoking Wonders I would like to share. Its based loosely the old variable &quot;In pill form&quot;. Here it is:<b> Anti-Havok Shielding: The Practice of \u201cSheathing\u201d</b><br /> <br /> Sheathing Wonders within a mundane control interface provides complete protection from casual handling and operation by mortal hands. It does not however, protect against analysis and prodding by regular scientists and knowledgeable souls. Sheathing requires that a Wonder have an integral wonder of Apokalypsi that interfaces with a mundane control system so that a mortal can reliably operate it with it exploding in his face.<br /> <br /> Mania is a lie, but Mania with a front can weather the storms of failure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7106-extant-reality","name":"Extant Reality","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7106_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-11T12:56:18-07:00","id":1253358,"title":"","content":"So, basically like the old Prostasia anti-interaction forcefields?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-12T14:51:37-07:00","id":1253713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1253358#post1253358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, basically like the old Prostasia anti-interaction forcefields?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but it is a passive variable and allows you make Wonders that are <b>marketable </b>and won't blow up in your customer's face. I invented the thing for a story project I am currently writing. Automata isn't just about Intelligent wonders and personal armies, it is also about Industry. Think Tony Stark and his company as an example of mad science and industrial commerce working hand in hand, Vent0.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7106,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7106-extant-reality","user":"Extant Reality","date":". 09-12-2018, 05:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7106-extant-reality","name":"Extant Reality","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7106_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-12T15:31:13-07:00","id":1253724,"title":"","content":"Mania-reactors for unlimited free(-ish) energy FTW.<br /> <br /> The electricity isn't vulnerable to Havoc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-17T20:27:16-08:00","id":1281440,"title":"","content":"Purely because I got randomly reminded of it today, if the themes of the horror of fatalistic nihilism (and cosmic horror) continue on into Genius 2nd, I would at least like to note Mummy and how it handles that subject.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-18T06:01:45-08:00","id":1281495,"title":"","content":"Themes and Moods have been discussed recently on the Discord server. I don't think Fatalistic Nihilism came up, though. From what I recall, themes were Unintended Consequences, and maybe Mania and Melancholy (or some reformation, though the latter could be a Mood).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-18T18:54:50-08:00","id":1281606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1281495#post1281495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Themes and Moods have been discussed recently on the Discord server. I don't think Fatalistic Nihilism came up, though. From what I recall, themes were Unintended Consequences, and maybe Mania and Melancholy (or some reformation, though the latter could be a Mood).</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh geez, the discord server. I should probably pop into there at some point. Been a while.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-20T02:24:03-08:00","id":1281761,"title":"","content":"Fatalistic Nihilism as a Theme? Nah. It would interfere with the sense of Wonder that I get from the possibilities in this fansplat. Maybe something more along the lines of Humility vs. Insane Repetition would server as a better sub-Theme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7106-extant-reality","name":"Extant Reality","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7106_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-20T13:51:10-08:00","id":1281811,"title":"","content":"One potential theme might be &quot;Was it worth it?&quot;, if that could be encapsulated in a word or two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-20T14:00:58-08:00","id":1281813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Extant Reality</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/818609-genius-the-trangression-2th-edition?p=1281761#post1281761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fatalistic Nihilism as a Theme? Nah. It would interfere with the sense of Wonder that I get from the possibilities in this fansplat. Maybe something more along the lines of Humility vs. Insane Repetition would server as a better sub-Theme.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was a thing in First Edition-glad to hear it's not playing out in Second since it did seem like it was distracting from several of the stronger themes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-20T19:00:55-08:00","id":1281856,"title":"","content":"is there a new catalyst for 2nd edition? I heard about it somewhere","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T02:00:53-07:00","id":1305660,"title":"","content":"Is the work on this project still happening? I was kind of looking forward to how it turned out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4968-mrbreaksit","name":"MrBreaksIt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;bas